ragraph': ' The American Orthotic & Prosthetic Association, a national trade group, has promised to provide artificial limbs to any people who lost a leg in the Boston Marathon bombings if they are uninsured or their insurance fails to cover the cost. \xa0More than a dozen people lost limbs in the blasts; it is not yet known how many will need help paying for prostheses. The cost of an initial prosthesis could be $8,000 to $30,000, said Tom Fise, the group’s executive director. Many insurance plans sharply limit coverage, he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Aid Promised for Victims Who Lost Limbs', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Aid Promised For Victims Who Lost Limbs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostheses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMPUTATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T00:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc09db93-34c6-51a3-9b23-a3cf86ab0f46', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc09db93-34c6-51a3-9b23-a3cf86ab0f46'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry called a new initiative “a very big step forward,” but initial reactions suggested that the plan might have difficulty penetrating a years-long impasse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/world/middleeast/kerry-welcomes-arab-plan-for-israeli-palestinian-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry called a new initiative “a very big step forward,” but initial reactions suggested that the plan might have difficulty penetrating a years-long impasse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Secretary of State John Kerry on Tuesday embraced a proposal by the Arab League to revive peace talks between Israel and the Palestinians as “a very big step forward,” but initial reactions suggested that the new initiative might have difficulty penetrating the years-long impasse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Calls Arab League Plan to Revive Talks With Israel a ‘Big Step’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Calls Arab League Plan to Revive Talks With Israel a ‘Big Step’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on Foreign Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T00:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers and Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'l