: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f3d99c-36f5-5419-8aef-9b3215cd5bf3', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f3d99c-36f5-5419-8aef-9b3215cd5bf3'}, {'abstract': 'Former Mayor Rudolph Giuliani is actually hurting, not helping, the Lhota campaign with all his talk of trampling the Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/opinion/mayor-giuliani-is-hurting-not-helping-the-lhota-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Former Mayor Rudolph Giuliani is actually hurting, not helping, the Lhota campaign with all his talk of trampling the Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Mayor Rudolph Giuliani went to a fund-raiser on Staten Island on Monday for Joseph Lhota, his former deputy who is running for Mr. Giuliani’s old job. Thanks to a blogging reporter, Jacob Kornbluh, there is video of Mr. Giuliani reprising his role as the Mayor of 9/11.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Friend Like Rudy ...', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With a Friend Like Rudy ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T01:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cfdad47-567f-5af7-a764-db12df6e5943', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cfdad47-567f-5af7-a764-db12df6e5943'}, {'abstract': 'Americans need an accounting of the C.I.A.’s astounding cash payments to President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/opinion/ghost-money-and-lots-of-it-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Americans need an accounting of the C.I.A.’s astounding cash payments to President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news that the Central Intelligence Agency has been spending lavishly in Afghanistan should come as no surprise. The agency went to work in the country right after Sept. 11, 2001, and has played a dominant covert role hunting down Al Qaeda and the Taliban ever since, while the Pentagon and other agencies have pursued more transparent military and development operations costing many billions of dollars. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Ghost Money,’ and Lots of It', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Ghost Money,’ and Lots of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T01:08:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f38814-bb63-5a49-af3f-2ec7978c581a', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f38814-bb63-5a49-af3f-2ec7978c581a'}, {'abstract': 'Six months after Hurricane Sandy, IceStone, a Brooklyn factory specializing in making hard surfaces like tables, is back in operation because its employees made what had seemed impossible possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/nyregion/empowered-workers-help-revive-a-brooklyn-factory-hit-by-hurricane.html', 'snippet': 'Six months after Hurricane Sandy, IceStone, a Brooklyn factory specializing in making hard surfaces like tables, is back in operation because its employees made what had seemed impossible possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day after Hurricane Sandy, Dal LaMagna drove to his factory in Building 12 at the Brooklyn Navy Yard. His company, IceStone, had been making hard surfaces, like countertops and tables, using recycled glass and cement. As he pulled into the yard, his first sight was of the factory’s new garage door, which cost $21,000, peeled back like the lid of a sardine tin. Inside were six destroyed forklifts. The entire place was drowned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/nyregion/01ABOUT1-span/01ABOUT1-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flooded Factory Is Brought Back by Its Workers', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flooded Factory Is Brought Back By Its Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Navy Yard (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vargas, Manuel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IceStone LLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T01:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/946ea4fb-2699-5b61-a252-fb06f15806be', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/946ea4fb-2699-5b61-a252-fb06f15806be'}, {'abstract': 'Despite 2012 setbacks, Charles and David Koch have rejected any notion of stepping back from electoral politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/us/politics/koch-brothers-plan-more-political-involvement-for-their-conservative-network.html', 'snippet': 'Despite 2012 setbacks, Charles and David Koch have rejected any notion of stepping back from electoral politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the country’s leading conservative donors finished off plates of roast lamb and spaetzle in a Palm Springs, Calif., hotel ballroom on Monday, Charles G. Koch delivered a pep talk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Koch Brothers Plan More Political Involvement for Their Conservative Network', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Koch Brothers Plan More Political Involvement for Their Conservative Network', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Charles G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Confessore, Nicholas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans for Prosperity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch Industries Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T01:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c64b531-1bb0-504d-a00f-ac685115879f', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c64b531-1bb0-504d-a00f-ac685115879f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Obama promised, yet again, to close the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba. He has failed to keep that promise for five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/opinion/president-obama-and-the-hunger-strike-at-guantanamo.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Obama promised, yet again, to close the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba. He has failed to keep that promise for five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama said a lot of important things on Tuesday about the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba. It is a blight on the nation’s reputation. It mocks American standards of justice by keeping people imprisoned without charges. It has actually hindered the prosecution and imprisonment of dangerous terrorists. Even if Guantánamo seemed justified to some people in the immediate aftermath of the attacks on Sept. 11, 2001, those justifications are wearing thin. It is unsustainable and should be closed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President and the Hunger Strike', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The President and the Hunger Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T01:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2af6c5-5aee-57e7-9c6e-c34c0dc007bd', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2af6c5-5aee-57e7-9c6e-c34c0dc007bd'}, {'abstract': 'In today’s hyperconnected world, we all have to learn much more about investing in ourselves in order to succeed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/opinion/friedman-its-a-401k-world.html', 'snippet': 'In today’s hyperconnected world, we all have to learn much more about investing in ourselves in order to succeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to have a conversation today with any worker, teacher, student or boss who doesn’t tell you some version of this: More things seem to be changing in my world than ever before, but I can’t quite put my finger on it, let alone know how to adapt. So let me try to put my finger on it: We now live in a 401(k) world — a world of defined contributions, not defined benefits — where everyone needs to pass the bar exam and no one can escape the most e-mailed list.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', '