his lovely Wednesday puzzle. Her challenge to me is to figure out how to discuss this without getting fired. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fun Holiday to Celebrate', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e57e292f-1a5b-5372-939e-b339b6d6ee32', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e57e292f-1a5b-5372-939e-b339b6d6ee32'}, {'abstract': 'The genocide trial of a former dictator of Guatemala, Gen. Efraín Ríos Montt, resumed Tuesday, 12 days after a judge ruled to annul the court proceedings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/world/americas/guatemala-former-dictators-genocide-trial-resumes.html', 'snippet': 'The genocide trial of a former dictator of Guatemala, Gen. Efraín Ríos Montt, resumed Tuesday, 12 days after a judge ruled to annul the court proceedings.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The genocide trial of a former dictator of Guatemala, Gen. Efraín Ríos Montt, resumed Tuesday, 12 days after a judge ruled to annul the court proceedings. Guatemala’s highest court has yet to issue a clear statement on the legality of that decision, but it made several rulings last week that sent the case back to the chief trial judge, Jasmín Barrios, to restart proceedings. Testimony is almost complete, but Guatemala’s highest court must still consider several more motions related to the trial, and experts say more delays are possible. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guatemala: Former Dictator’s Genocide Trial Resumes', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemala: Former Dictator’s Genocide Trial Resumes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rios Montt, Efrain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:06:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e390802d-8fb2-5179-b3a3-e0149d683046', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e390802d-8fb2-5179-b3a3-e0149d683046'}, {'abstract': 'A federal prosecutor told the jury that John C. Liu, a Democratic candidate for New York City mayor, had to have been aware of a scheme to use straw donors for Mr. Liu’s campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/nyregion/liu-is-prominent-figure-in-prosecutors-closing-arguments-at-ex-aides-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A federal prosecutor told the jury that John C. Liu, a Democratic candidate for New York City mayor, had to have been aware of a scheme to use straw donors for Mr. Liu’s campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As closing arguments began on Tuesday in a widely watched political corruption trial in Manhattan, a federal prosecutor asked a jury to convict two former associates of John C. Liu, the New York City comptroller and a Democratic candidate for mayor, of conspiring to funnel money to his campaign through an illegal fund-raising scheme.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liu Is Prominent Figure in Closing Argument at Ex-Aides’ Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liu Is Prominent Figure in Closing Argument at Ex-Aides’ Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hou, Jia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pan, Xing Wu', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Sharon', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Comptrollers', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1537762-6199-5a0e-932d-6ed2264b0802', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1537762-6199-5a0e-932d-6ed2264b0802'}, {'abstract': 'Collins had been filled with fear at the prospect of openly acknowledging he is gay, but the response to his announcement has been overwhelmingly positive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/sports/jason-collins-took-personal-steps-before-coming-out-publicly.html', 'snippet': 'Collins had been filled with fear at the prospect of openly acknowledging he is gay, but the response to his announcement has been overwhelmingly positive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — When Jason Collins signed with Boston Celtics last year, he was a player in search of a number. His number for years — 34 — was taken, and 35, which he had with the Nets at the start of his career, had been retired by his new team.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 846}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1453, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/COLLINS/COLLINS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Collins Took Personal Steps Before Coming Out Publicly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Collins Took a Series of Personal Steps Before Coming Out Publicly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b950c262-6c6d-5abc-a56f-2bbaf483ad3a', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b950c262-6c6d-5abc-a56f-2bbaf483ad3a'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department will allow President Raúl Castro’s daughter to travel to Philadelphia to receive a gay civil rights award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/world/americas/cuba-us-allows-presidents-daughter-to-travel.html', 'snippet': 'The State Department will allow President Raúl Castro’s daughter to travel to Philadelphia to receive a gay civil rights award.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The State Department will allow President Raúl Castro’s daughter to travel to Philadelphia to receive a gay civil rights award. Mariela Castro, director of Cuba’s National Center for Sex Education, was granted a diplomatic visa to attend United Nations meetings in April, but the State Department did not issue a second visa she requested to attend the Equality Forum 2013 Summit this weekend. Cuban diplomats cannot travel more than 25 miles without prior authorization. Ms. Castro is considered an international leader in the issue of rights for gay and transgender people. The Equality Forum received word on Monday that the State Department decided to lift the 25-mile restriction. “Better judgment prevailed,” said the group’s director, Malcolm Lazin. The State Department did not explain the reversal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: U.S. Allows President’s Daughter to Travel', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuba: U.S. Allows President’s Daughter to Travel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robles, Frances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Education', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Raul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frances Robles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frances', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6725836c-f8af-5b08-9d3f-c6d87842d87b', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6725836c-f8af-5b08-9d3f-c6d87842d87b'}, {'abstract': 'One week after a lawsuit by livery and black-car operators challenging the use of such apps was dismissed, the Uber company said its service was available.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/nyregion/uber-companys-app-for-hailing-yellow-taxis-is-available-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'One week after a lawsuit by livery and black-car operators challenging the use of such apps was dismissed, the Uber company said its service was available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a series of court hearings and false starts, New York City’s yellow taxi riders can now, for the first time, legally hail a cab with a smartphone app.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Company’s App Can Now Be Used to Hail Yellow Cabs in City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Company’s App Can Now Be Used to Hail Cabs in City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T02:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81172303-a62c-5b85-8988-c5e158fa073d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81172303-a62c-5b85-8988-c5e158fa073d'}, {'abstract': 'Republican sponsors of the immigration bill say that an amendment to allow immigran