erdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Sajjan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T05:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betwa Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betwa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288d67fb-d089-5bb9-bf59-c06c3727b76b', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288d67fb-d089-5bb9-bf59-c06c3727b76b'}, {'abstract': 'Arrest in Bangladesh; Obama recommits to closing Guantánamo; cash in China; Berlin names streets for women; and Oslo runs out of trash.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/iht-quick-read-may-1/', 'snippet': 'Arrest in Bangladesh; Obama recommits to closing Guantánamo; cash in China; Berlin names streets for women; and Oslo runs out of trash.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The most reviled man in Bangladesh, Sohel Rana, 35, is under arrest. Mr. Rana owned the Rana Plaza, which collapsed last week, killing nearly 400 people. Many others are still missing. On Tuesday, a top Bangladeshi court seized his assets, as the public called for his execution, especially as it appears that the tragedy could have been averted if the frantic warnings of an engineer who examined the building the day before had been heeded. Jim Yardley reports from Savar, Bangladesh. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 's