rah Cox, who plays the prostitute Lucy, sings her character’s signature song, the power ballad “Someone Like You.” The show runs through June 30 at the Marquis Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Deborah Cox of ‘Jekyll & Hyde’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Deborah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildhorn, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T12:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82873698-653a-5672-9bc7-95281a8276bd', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82873698-653a-5672-9bc7-95281a8276bd'}, {'abstract': 'Vyjack, a gelding running in Saturday’s Kentucky Derby, was uncooperative as a young horse, but a hackamore bridle helped him settle down.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/vyjack-has-learned-to-behave-and-to-win/', 'snippet': 'Vyjack, a gelding running in Saturday’s Kentucky Derby, was uncooperative as a young horse, but a hackamore bridle helped him settle down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve seen only one Kentucky Derby starter up close this year. The starter, Vyjack, came to Fair Hill for two weeks or so in April, and he struck me as a lively personality during several visits over a few days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vyjack Has Learned to Behave, and to Win', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None