?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Wolf has a very good piece on the attempts to put the Baltic states, Latvia especially, on a pedestal and claim that they prove that austerity works. Mainly he makes points I have made previously: first, that output is still well below the previous peak, and unemployment still very high despite drastic out-migration:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baltic Brouhaha', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T14:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44640dad-1cb0-57f6-9bda-79979b6476fc', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44640dad-1cb0-57f6-9bda-79979b6476fc'}, {'abstract': 'To be an “eyeshine” expert you might need to spend a lot of time in a dark forest, feeling your way around with a flashlight.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/telling-eyes-in-the-dark/', 'snippet': 'To be an “eyeshine” expert you might need to spend a lot of time in a dark forest, feeling your way around with a flashlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary E. Blair is a postdoctoral researcher at the American Museum of Natural History’s Center for Biodiversity and Conservation, where she coordinates the Enhancing Diversity in Conservation Science Initiative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/science/saw-blair-3-1/saw-blair-3-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i