 Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T14:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8430edc0-6193-51b5-9026-45cf4e9995bb', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8430edc0-6193-51b5-9026-45cf4e9995bb'}, {'abstract': 'One of the consequences of an expatriate life is separation from family and friends, and from the major life events that define families. How do you deal with the loss of a loved one when you’re on the other side of an ocean?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/dying-long-distance/', 'snippet': 'One of the consequences of an expatriate life is separation from family and friends, and from the major life events that define families. How do you deal with the loss of a loved one when you’re on the other side of an ocean?', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The last conversation I had with my father was by Skype. He was in a sunny room in southeastern Pennsylvania; I was in Paris, where I live and work. He was surrounded by my siblings and their spouses; my mother had visited earlier that day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/rdv-jan/rdv-jan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dying Long Distance', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skype Technologies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T14:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Benzel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benzel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a541131d-0ce0-5107-9e59-6bb4b51e0662', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a541131d-0ce0-5107-9e59-6bb4b51e0662'}, {'abstract': 'Purchases of movies and TV shows rose about 5 percent in the first quarter, according to an industry group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/business/media/home-spending-on-entertainment-rises.html', 'snippet': 'Purchases of movies and TV shows rose about 5 percent in the first quarter, according to an industry group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Home entertainment spending on movies and television shows rose about 5 percent in the first quarter, to $4.69 billion, compared with the same period a year ago, as some strong titles including “Skyfall” and “Argo” hit the market, according to figures released Wednesday by the Digital Entertainment Group, an industry consortium.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Spending on Entertainment Rises', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spending Increases For Home Entertainment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Entertainment Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T14:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d957a59f-16c2-55a3-9ad6-1a202e5d16ea', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d957a59f-16c2-55a3-9ad6-1a202e5d16ea'}, {'abstract': 'International Labor Day o