 Branson, Virgin’s founder, right, introduced the service last month in a video billed as his “guide to getting lucky at 35,000 feet.” Try it, he said, and your chances of “deplaning with a plus one are at least 50 percent.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friendly, Maybe Lucky, Skies', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airlines: Friendly, Maybe Lucky, Skies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branson, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T15:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9149007a-cc18-5751-90e9-2b40ff142825', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9149007a-cc18-5751-90e9-2b40ff142825'}, {'abstract': 'If you are audited by the I.R.S. and found to owe money, there are multiple steps you can take to appeal.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/what-if-you-are-audited-by-the-i-r-s/', 'snippet': 'If you are audited by the I.R.S. and found to owe money, there are multiple steps you can take to appeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The April 15 tax deadline is now receding in our collective rear view mirror. Nothing to do now, but to start collecting records for next year. Right?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if You Are Audited by the I.R.S.', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.R.S. Audits: What to Know', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T15:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f1da7eb-ce23-5304-8769-3dfaeb576cd4', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f1da7eb-ce23-5304-8769-3dfaeb576cd4'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Loren Fishman, a specialist in rehabilitative medicine who has long incorporated yoga into patient treatment, is taking questions about yoga.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/booming/yoga-for-the-middle-aged-questions.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Loren Fishman, a specialist in rehabilitative medicine who has long incorporated yoga into patient treatment, is taking questions about yoga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Ask an Expert features Dr. Loren Fishman, who will answer questions about practicing yoga in your middle years. In 1972, before applying to medical school, he studied yoga with B.K.S. Iyengar for a year in Pune, India. Dr. Fishman, 72, has now been a practicing back-pain and rehabilitative medicine specialist for 33 years. From the start he incorporated yoga in patient care, and he teaches seminars in yoga nationally and internationally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 209,