We were cut off from the outside world for quite a while, just looking at nature. One of our guides showed us a wild dog who had wandered into the area a few years before, apparently lost from her pack. So she stole some jackal pups and raised them. Now they’re a team — the dog does the hunting and the jackals keep a lookout for lions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Days of the Jackals', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Botswana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T16:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e257e0-7c0e-5718-96b7-759ad887200e', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e257e0-7c0e-5718-96b7-759ad887200e'}, {'abstract': 'The season will feature Cloud Gate 2, the Houston Ballet, Pam Tanowitz Dance and the Lar Lubovitch Dance Company, among others.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/the-joyce-announces-its-2013-2014-season/', 'snippet': 'The season will feature Cloud Gate 2, the Houston Ballet, Pam Tanowitz Dance and the Lar Lubovitch Dance Company, among others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur Pita’s award-winning interpretation of Kafka’s “Metamorphosis,” originally staged by the Royal Ballet in London, will open the fall dance season at the Joyce Theater on Sept. 17, with the Royal Ballet principal Edward Watson dancing the role of Gregor Samsa, and Frank Moon performing his own score live. The production, which runs through Sept. 29, is the first of 16 that the theater has scheduled through February 2014. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joyce Announces Its 2013-2014 Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T16:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c7ddc4-6bd4-5867-99c1-aaf564f1451a', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c7ddc4-6bd4-5867-99c1-aaf564f1451a'}, {'abstract': 'The “Car Free LA” program offers seven itineraries for tourists up for biking, walking or taking the Metro transit system in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/leaving-cars-behind-in-l-a/', 'snippet': 'The “Car Free LA” program offers seven itineraries for tourists up for biking, walking or taking the Metro transit system in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Los Angeles’s tourism agency is hoping to entice visitors to find new ways to explore the city. Its “Car Free LA” program offers seven itineraries for tourists up for biking, walking or taking the Metro transit system. Trips include the bike route from Venice to Santa Monica and a walking tour of Hollywood, though you may have to take a taxi to the starting point.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaving Cars Behind in L.A.', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tourism: Leaving Cars Behind in L.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25446908-9279-5474-9e7f-281694891a22', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25446908-9279-5474-9e7f-281694891a22'}, {'abstract': 'If you have determined that none of your retailers are interested in a business, don’t you have every right to do it yourself?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/a-wholesaler-decides-to-abandon-his-most-profitable-sales-channel/', 'snippet': 'If you have determined that none of your retailers are interested in a business, don’t you have every right to do it yourself?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, we published a case study about an entrepreneur, new to the furniture business, who had expanded his business selling patio and deck furniture to $7 million in annual sales. Instead of selling through sales representatives, Gerald Shvartsman, founder and chief executive of Source Outdoor, which is based in Miami, employed a multichannel sales strategy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'