e': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T18:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf49232a-fa4b-513b-90b4-f7dd0835e0b6', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf49232a-fa4b-513b-90b4-f7dd0835e0b6'}, {'abstract': 'On beauty-focused social networks, amateurs and professionals can see which products are new and popular, and offer reviews of their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/fashion/online-everyones-a-makeup-critic-skin-deep.html', 'snippet': 'On beauty-focused social networks, amateurs and professionals can see which products are new and popular, and offer reviews of their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matin Maulawizada, a makeup artist based in New York, used to spend hours prowling department stores’ beauty floors to find out what was new and noteworthy. Now, Mr. Maulawizada, the global artistry director for Laura Mercier, likes to log on to Pampadour.com, a sleek new beauty-focused social network, to see what products colleagues are using — or, in the company’s parlance, “pamping.” “It really saves me time,” Mr. Maulawizada said.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SKINDEEP_SPAN/02zSKIN-DEEP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Online, Everyone Can Be a Makeup Critic', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online, Everyone Can Be a Makeup Critic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boncompagni, Tatiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T18:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tatiana Boncompagni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tatiana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boncompagni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cefb9ce-4cc1-533b-ba81-c594626a6755', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cefb9ce-4cc1-533b-ba81-c594626a6755'}, {'abstract': 'The Paris-based Japanese designer will make a rare New York appearance tomorrow evening at Kisan boutique in SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/window-dressing-tsumori-chisato/', 'snippet': 'The Paris-based Japanese designer will make a rare New York appearance tomorrow evening at Kisan boutique in SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attention, Tsumori Chisato devotees: The Paris-based Japanese designer, who’s earned a dedicated following for her whimsical prints and graceful use of manga, is making a rare New York appearance tomorrow evening. She’ll be hosting a cocktail party at Kisan, the SoHo boutique owned by the Icelandic-French couple Thorunn Anspach and Olivier Bremond. In honor of Tsumori’s visit, the two have created a special window display that showcases her Arizona-themed spring collection, pictured above, which was inspired by a visit to Sedona and includes references to the work of the artist Georgia O’Keefe. Tsumori, a tireless traveler who just returned from Italy, says that she is always on the lookout for fresh ideas for her designs. In New York, she’ll be “walking the streets and feeling the very unique atmosphere,” though she’s mainly looking forward to meeting her fans. “That makes my day!” she says. “Every time I meet a woman wearing my clothes I can tell she feels good in them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Window Dressing | Tsumori Chisato', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T19:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name