type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f952824c-3c8e-5f45-8a16-550ac4d962f9', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f952824c-3c8e-5f45-8a16-550ac4d962f9'}, {'abstract': 'A new study adds to evidence of a link between late-life depression and dementia.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/does-depression-contribute-to-dementia/', 'snippet': 'A new study adds to evidence of a link between late-life depression and dementia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large body of research has linked late-life depression to social isolation, poorer health and an increased risk of death. Now, a new study finds that depression is associated with subsequent vascular dementia and Alzheimer’s disease, conditions poised to expand dramatically with the aging population.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Depression Contribute to Dementia?', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T19:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c265279e-4156-5b51-9ad6-8fe423ca2b4a', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c265279e-4156-5b51-9ad6-8fe423ca2b4a'}, {'abstract': 'Who needs to wait another three years to choose America’s second-in-command? Not HBO, that’s for sure.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/hbo-orders-third-season-of-veep/', 'snippet': 'Who needs to wait another three years to choose America’s second-in-command? Not HBO, that’s for sure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who needs to wait another three years to choose America’s second-in-command? Not HBO, that’s for sure: on Wednesday, that cable network announced it was ordering a third season of “Veep,” its comedy series starring Julia Louis-Dreyfus as the vice president of the United States. In its first season in 2012, “Veep,” created by Armando Iannucci (the author of the political satires “The Thick of It” and “In the Loop”) was an Emmy nominee for outstanding comedy; Ms. Louis-Dreyfus, an Emmy winner for her performances on “Seinfeld” and “The New Adventures of Old Christine,” earned her third such award for portraying the “Veep” title character, Selina Meyer. “Veep” was just three episodes into its second season (which started on April 14) when HBO announced its latest renewal. The network said a third season of 10 episodes will be shown next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/veep/veep-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/veep/veep-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/veep/veep-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/veep/veep-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum