between real-life politicians and the Hollywood stars who portray them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, it seems, someone makes a big to-do over the White House Correspondents’ Association dinner and how it has been overrun with celebrities. (This year, Tom Brokaw and Barbara Walters criticized the event’s star turn.) It’s safe to say they didn’t make it to the annual after-party hosted by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg and Vanity Fair magazine.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02SCENE_SPAN/02SCENE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150,