: 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua David Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a3b657-0213-5363-bf1f-943d5c25e737', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a3b657-0213-5363-bf1f-943d5c25e737'}, {'abstract': 'Fortune cookies, a band or a flash mob might be a better approach than simply requesting a date.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/fashion/the-prom-ask-becomes-a-big-production.html', 'snippet': 'Fortune cookies, a band or a flash mob might be a better approach than simply requesting a date.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was almost midnight, and I was perched next to my teenage son at his computer. He was frantically searching the Internet for a Web site that could produce custom Chinese fortune cookies — in 48 hours. Finally he hit upon a company called Tankinz Inc., and his fingers flew over the keys, “Lizzie, will you go to the prom with me?”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02NOTED/02zNOTED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02NOTED/02zNOTED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02NOTED/02zNOTED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/fashion/02NOTED/02zNOTED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'cr