Creator', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T21:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0704b981-5708-5e83-b3c1-07543a3657aa', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0704b981-5708-5e83-b3c1-07543a3657aa'}, {'abstract': 'For Steven Soderbergh, a far-reaching speech and a Twitter novella indicate a retirement that is anything but idle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/books/soderbergh-explores-a-new-medium.html', 'snippet': 'For Steven Soderbergh, a far-reaching speech and a Twitter novella indicate a retirement that is anything but idle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the release of “Side Effects” earlier this year, Steven Soderbergh’s retirement from filmmaking (at least for the big screen), announced in 2011, finally took effect. Liberation might be a better word, since his recent activities seem to belong to a restless person newly freed from the constraints of his profession, rather than a used-up man at rest.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/arts/jpsoderbergh1/jpsoderbergh1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/arts/jpsoderberg