that includes the International Contemporary Furniture Fair and satellite shows. Steven Learner, 52, the architect and designer who started Collective (known as Collective.1 in its first iteration), made a trip uptown to discuss it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02QNA1_SPAN/02QNA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Creative Season, a New Design Fair', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Creative Season, A New Design Fair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Learner, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T22:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf0c3b1-7d77-5703-9991-239879e2b478', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf0c3b1-7d77-5703-9991-239879e2b478'}, {'abstract': 'A light festooned with crystals takes up residence near the palace of Versailles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/garden/bespoke-chandeliers-inspired-by-bees.html', 'snippet': 'A light festooned with crystals takes up residence near the palace of Versailles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Guerlain, the French perfume company, opened a boutique and learning center in La Cour des Senteurs on the Rue de la Chancellerie in Versailles, a hundred yards from the main entrance of the royal chateau. Suspended from the shop’s 22-foot-high arched entrance is a frothy chandelier by Marie Christophe, a sculptor in Toulouse. Ms. Christophe said the light was inspired by the chandeliers of the palace and by the gilded bees on vintage Guerlain bottles. Its wire frame is hung with crystals, some from flea markets and some made by contemporary artisans and embedded with gold paper. The LED chandelier is 7 feet high and 4 feet in diameter and sells for $60,000 through the design retailer Lisa Fontanarosa. Custom sizes are available. Information: (505) 872-1929 or lisafontanarosa.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 911, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LIGHTING/02CURR2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bespoke Chandeliers Inspired by Bees', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bespoke Chandeliers Inspired by Bees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T22:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90116af7-6093-5029-9dde-8534607d7d9b', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90116af7-6093-5029-9dde-8534607d7d9b'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Hardy, a 20-something designer, talked his way into the opportunity to make furniture for Design Within Reach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/garden/helix-tables-by-chris-hardy-for-design-within-reach.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Hardy, a 20-something designer, talked his way into the opportunity to make furniture for Design Within Reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the last day of the Hospitality Design show in Las Vegas three years ago when Chris Hardy ventured into the Design Within Reach booth with his portfolio in hand. There, he stumbled on John Edelman, the company’s chief executive. As a result, Mr. Hardy, a designer in Atlanta, found himself on a short list of hopefuls asked to submit ideas for small tables. He was among those who prevailed, and now his Helix side tables and coffee tables are ready for market. They feature asymmetrical walnut- and cast-bronze bases topped by glass. “The brass not only stabilizes the base but creates a nice movement out from the center, with a layered effect,” said Mr. Hardy, 29. The side table comes with a round top ($1,400), while the coffee table is available with a round or square top ($2,200) or an oval one ($2,400). The tables are at DWR Studios nationwide. Information: (800) 944-2233 or dwr.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02FURNITURE/02CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge'