ok on the formidable task of building a business, a house and a life in a foreign country. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/garden/02LOCATION_SPAN/02LOCATION2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Coconuts Come Calling', 'kicker': 'On Location | Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Coconuts Come Calling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mala, Elisa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ho Chi Minh City (Vietnam)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-01T22:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisa Mala', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mala', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa069b2-8a30-5faa-9b10-64954b4f2daf', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa069b2-8a30-5faa-9b10-64954b4f2daf'}, {'abstract': 'Angela Adams’s new Landscape collection was inspired by woodlands, harbors, gardens and dunes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/garden/angela-adamss-new-landscape-collection.html', 'snippet': 'Angela Adams’s new Landscape collection was inspired by woodlands, harbors, gardens and dunes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, Angela Adams, a rug designer in Portland, Me., began using scissors and sheep shears to carve shapes into tufted wool. The second generation of this experiment, a collection called Landscape, is being introduced this week. Ms. Adams described the sculptural rugs as “literal translations of nature,” inspired by her favorite places: “open areas in the woods; a garden in July with big bold bursts of color everywhere; a nice beach I like; and what it feels like to be on the water at night.” The rugs are made in Thailand of hand-tufted New Zealand wool. They are available in four designs (Woodland, Garden, Harbor and Dune) and three sizes (9 by 11 feet for $12,000, 3 by 8 feet for $2,200 and 8-feet round for $8,000). Information: (800) 255-9454 or angelaadams.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York T