b_date': '2013-05-02T01:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f987dade-11e8-5cb3-9771-208a79e6c658', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f987dade-11e8-5cb3-9771-208a79e6c658'}, {'abstract': 'The revolt against unjustifiably high prices of cancer medications has been joined by more than 100 leukemia experts from more than 15 countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/opinion/exorbitant-prices-for-cancer-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'The revolt against unjustifiably high prices of cancer medications has been joined by more than 100 leukemia experts from more than 15 countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year we were heartened when doctors at the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center in New York refused to use an outrageously overpriced drug for treating advanced colorectal cancer because it was no better than a cheaper (but still costly) alternative. Neither did much to extend a patient’s life. Now the revolt against unjustifiably high cancer drug prices has been joined by more than 100 leukemia experts from more than 15 countries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exorbitant Prices for Leukemia Drugs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exorbitant Prices for Leukemia Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leukemia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T01:13:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/051252e1-2fcc-5235-abd0-f2e4a1481e64', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/051252e1-2fcc-5235-abd0-f2e4a1481e64'}, {'abstract': 'State and federal regulators need to get a handle on the lack of disclosure in tactics used by companies that specialize in separating retirees from their pensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/opinion/preying-on-pensioners.html', 'snippet': 'State and federal regulators need to get a handle on the lack of disclosure in tactics used by companies that specialize in separating retirees from their pensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the run-up to the mortgage crisis, elderly people were often duped into taking out subprime loans that earned a fortune for the lenders while leaving the borrowers with little or no home equity and headed for foreclosure. A similar brand of wealth stripping is alive and well in a new crop of companies that specialize in separating retirees from their pensions. Unless state and federal regulators get a handle on this problem, ever larger numbers of elderly people who are already battered by the recession will end up even worse off. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preying on Pensioners', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preying on Pensioners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T01:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d52328-122a-543d-8f6b-ba7c21f6fa67', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d52328-122a-543d-8f6b-ba7c21f6fa67'}, {'abstract': 'Confirming Prime Minister Enrico Letta is an essential first step on the road to political and economic recovery, but tough challenges are ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/opinion/italys-new-government-led-by-prime-minister-letta.html', 'snippet': 'Confirming Prime Minister Enrico Letta is an essential first step on the road to political and economic recovery, but tough challenges are ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than two months after an inconclusive election, Italy at last has a new government, an essential first step on the road to political and economic recovery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy’s New Government', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy’s New Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letta, Enrico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T01:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/154c29ab-05c3-51b4-a94a-c27ec54716bf', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/154c29ab-05c3-51b4-a94a-c27ec54716bf'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate is finally about to pass a bill to let states collect sales taxes on purchases made on the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/opinion/fairness-on-sales-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate is finally about to pass a bill to let states collect sales taxes on purchases made on the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-one years is a long time to wait. But that is how long local retailers have waited for Congress to undo a 1992 Supreme Court decision that exempted many online retailers, like Amazon.com, from collecting most state sales taxes. The exemption has given online sellers a 5 percent to 10 percent price advantage over Main Street stores. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairness on Sales Taxes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fairness on Sales Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T01:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff81e361-926d-5683-91f5-c8e6d4e2cc71', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff81e361-926d-5683-91f5-c8e6d4e2cc71'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s second term is just beginning. Let’s let him have it before skipping ahead to 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/opinion/blow-the-juice-the-jousting-and-the-job.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s second term is just beginning. Let’s let him have it before skipping ahead to 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During Tuesday’s presidential news conference, Jonathan Karl of ABC News asked the president if he still had “the juice” to get the rest of his agenda through Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS