'The leader of Turkmenistan learned this week just how difficult it can be to maintain a cult of personality in the Internet era, when the official account of his dashing triumph in a horse race on Sunday was undermined by video footage posted on foreign Web sites, showing what state television had failed to mention — the president’s spectacular fall to the track seconds after his horse crossed the finish line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Turkmen Leader’s Spectacular Fall Foils Effort to Cover Up Accident', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdymukhammedov, Gurbanguly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkmenistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T01:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e69c7d-a10c-55ea-a52a-7b524c7d9a82', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e69c7d-a10c-55ea-a52a-7b524c7d9a82'}, {'abstract': 'Directional advice from Josh Knapp.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/crossed-by-a-center-line/', 'snippet': 'Directional advice from Josh Knapp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — I really enjoyed this crunchy, word drop puzzle by Josh Knapp, although it took me a while to tumble to the theme. Thankfully, there’s a very clever reveal in the center of his 15-by-16 grid, and I especially liked the fact that the entry NEITHER/NOR is kind of a whole phrase unto itself even though the complete reveal is NEITHER [HERE] NOR [THERE]. That’s an elegant theme concept right THERE.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crossed by a Center Line', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T02:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4975ad7-9800-5e73-b711-d16649ec4b0e', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4975ad7-9800-5e73-b711-d16649ec4b0e'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans rejected a State Senate plans as well as the G.O.P. governor’s wishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/us/florida-runs-out-of-time-on-medicaid.html', 'snippet': 'House Republicans rejected a State Senate plans as well as the G.O.P. governor’s wishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Prospects for Medicaid expansion in Florida, which was embraced, improbably, by the state’s Republican governor in February, are all but dead this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 