os of three men wanted in connection with the attacks on an American diplomatic mission and C.I.A. outpost in Benghazi, Libya, in September.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The F.B.I. on Wednesday released photos of three men whom investigators want to question in connection with the attacks on a United States diplomatic mission and C.I.A. outpost in Benghazi, Libya, last September. A statement by the bureau said the three “were on the grounds of the United States Special Mission when it was attacked.” Four people — including the United States ambassador to Libya — died in the attacks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya: 3 Sought for Questioning in Benghazi Attack', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya: 3 Sought for Questioning in Benghazi Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T02:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab48fdc2-7bb0-5f10-b42d-c1548364427f', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab48fdc2-7bb0-5f10-b42d-c1548364427f'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptian authorities jailed an anti-Islamist activist late Tuesday on charges that included insulting President Mohamed Morsi, state news media said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/world/middleeast/egypt-critic-of-morsi-is-jailed.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptian authorities jailed an anti-Islamist activist late Tuesday on charges that included insulting President Mohamed Morsi, state news media said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Egyptian authorities jailed an anti-Islamist activist late Tuesday on charges that included insulting President Mohamed Morsi, state news media said. After turning himself in to prosecutors, the activist, Ahmed Douma, was transferred to a prison to be held for four days. Mr. Douma has been a vocal critic of Mr. Morsi and his allies in the Muslim Brotherhood, using social media and joining anti-Islamist protests. Human rights groups have accused Mr. Morsi and his allies of targeting their critics in politically motivated prosecutions — a charge Mr. Morsi’s aides deny. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Critic of Morsi Is Jailed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Anti-Islamist Activist, a Critic of Morsi, Is Jailed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douma, Ahmed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T02:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/87e94591-3e3b-51c2-b79c-8158755a0b36', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87e94591-3e3b-51c2-b79c-8158755a0b36'}, {'abstract': 'In a case against three foreign men charged with supporting a Somali terrorist group, documents offer a glimpse of the government’s rationale for bringing such cases into the federal courts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/nyregion/court-papers-offer-glimpse-of-government-rationale-in-federal-terror-cases.html', 'snippet': 'In a case against three foreign men charged with supporting a Somali terrorist group, documents offer a glimpse of the government’s rationale for bringing such cases into the federal courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The terrorism case landed on the public docket in Federal District Court in Brooklyn last year like a riddle. Prosecutors charged three foreign men arrested overseas with supporting a Somali terrorist group. They did not reveal details of the allegations against the men, their nationalities or even their connections to the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Papers Offer Details in Terror Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Papers Offer Details In Terror Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Secret, Mosi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 4, 'majo