, Doc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Paul (1977- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T04:49:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f37f1114-bc66-5218-880f-d7abcc121d83', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f37f1114-bc66-5218-880f-d7abcc121d83'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:30 P.M. (HBO2) THE IRON GIANT (1999) In this animated tale set during the height of cold-war nuclear anxiety, a young boy named Hogarth (voiced by Eli Marienthal) discovers and befriends a 50-foot-tall robot (Vin Diesel) from outer space that has crash-landed in his small town. Hogarth must hide the robot from his mother (Jennifer Aniston) and protect it from an overzealous government agent (Christopher McDonald) who wants it destroyed. “Directed by Brad Bird, ‘The Iron Giant’ is a smooth, skilled example of animated filmmaking,” Lawrence Van Gelder said in The New York Times, adding, “Many adults, including parents eager to have their children absorb lessons about the perils of guns and the merits of peace and tolerance, will doubtless approve of the film’s messages while they ponder how the passing years have smoothed the jagged edges of history.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "What's On Today", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T05:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae6eb33-1f68-59b8-8fb8-93388893588c', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae6eb33-1f68-59b8-8fb8-93388893588c'}, {'abstract': 'The fate of Sarabjit Singh, on death row for espionage, had long been a source of contention between India and Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/world/asia/indian-prisoner-in-pakistan-dies-after-beating.html', 'snippet': 'The fate of Sarabjit Singh, on death row for espionage, had long been a source of contention between India and Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MULTAN, Pakistan — An Indian man on death row in Pakistan for espionage has died after being attacked by fellow inmates, Pakistan’s state television said early Thursday, prompting an angry response from India.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Prisoner in Pakistan Dies After Beating, Prompting Angry Reply From India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Prisoner in Pakistan Dies After Beating, Prompting Angry Reply From India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Sarabjit', 'rank': 5, 'major'