when in reality, this is not the case.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Partnering for Peace and International Security', 'kicker': 'Forum for New Diplomacy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T13:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d303fe78-c553-5b19-9345-b2e3432cd42c', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d303fe78-c553-5b19-9345-b2e3432cd42c'}, {'abstract': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration said it would investigate the cars for safety matters ranging from rear suspension failure to large coolant leaks.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/n-h-t-s-a-investigates-dodge-viper-ford-crown-victoria-and-porsche-911/', 'snippet': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration said it would investigate the cars for safety matters ranging from rear suspension failure to large coolant leaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A pit of vipers sounds like trouble, which may be what the Chrysler Group is in concerning its 2005-6 Dodge Vipers. Citing a concern about rear suspension failures, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration opened an investigation covering about 2,500 of the sports cars, according to a report posted on the agency’s Web site.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.T.S.A. Investigates Dodge Viper, Ford Crown Victoria and Porsche 911', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agency Investigates The Dodge Viper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dodge Division of Chrysler Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porsche AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T14:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen and Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b59fbaf5-23c9-5575-9115-965d888fd84a', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b59fbaf5-23c9-5575-9115-965d888fd84a'}, {'abstract': 'For one horse racing fan, none of the recent long shots to win the Kentucky Derby compare to Exterminator, the 1918 victor that went off at 30-1.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/exterminator-a-long-shot-to-remember/', 'snippet': 'For one horse racing fan, none of the recent long shots to win the Kentucky Derby compare to Exterminator, the 1918 victor that went off at 30-1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A long shot will seize your attention during the Kentucky Derby television coverage. Among the biopics of sure things and heartwarming stories about trainers and owners will appear a brief moment with that horse who should not win the race. The announcer might mention Mine That Bird (2009 winner; odds of 50-1) or Giacomo (2005, also 50-1) to prove that sometimes the seemingly impossible happens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exterminator, a Long Shot to Remember', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T14:05:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliza McGraw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGraw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f535eb7b-5f92-585b-b3ab-18c99175c59f', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f535eb7b-5f92-585b-b3ab-18c99175c59f'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks and the Thunder won their first three playoff games, but not Games 4 and 5. The rumblings have begun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/in-the-playoffs-there-is-room-for-panic.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks and the Thunder won their first three playoff games, but not Games 4 and 5. The rumblings have begun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rumblings always start when an expected sweep turns into a 3-1 series. It grows into a howl when the series reaches 3-2 and everyone starts wondering if this is the year, finally, for the ultimate comeback. Maybe the favorite did not just nap through a game or two, people start to wonder, maybe they are just not as good as advertised. And then, almost always before things become really interesting, the favorite wins and everybody remembers this is the N.B.A., not hockey or baseball, and N.B.A. does not do upsets, at least not big ones. They are so unstylish. Celebrity fans find them so inconvenient.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/sports/basketball/03leadingpic/03leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Playoffs, There Is Room for Panic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj