'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f4327c7-a411-5ba8-9f3e-ad518355ad83', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f4327c7-a411-5ba8-9f3e-ad518355ad83'}, {'abstract': 'The departure of Mark King after just four months at the head of the company’s most prestigious division was a surprise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/business/global/rolls-royce-aerospace-chief-mark-king-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'The departure of Mark King after just four months at the head of the company’s most prestigious division was a surprise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Rolls-Royce, the British engineering group, on Thursday announced the surprise resignation of Mark King as chief of its aerospace business, barely four months after the 27-year company veteran had been appointed to run the group’s most prestigious division, which builds engines for commercial and military aircraft.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rolls-Royce Aerospace Chief Resigns Unexpectedly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolls-Royce PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T14:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/491d33cd-523c-50c4-871f-95730a3ee105', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/491d33cd-523c-50c4-871f-95730a3ee105'}, {'abstract': 'Demands by Turkey’s religious right that former churches and mosques that have been turned into museums be converted back into mosques are producing architectural disasters.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/the-cost-of-turning-turkeys-old-churches-and-museums-back-into-mosques/', 'snippet': 'Demands by Turkey’s religious right that former churches and mosques that have been turned into museums be converted back into mosques are producing architectural disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — In 1921 an ecumenical service was held in six languages at St. John the Divine, New York City’s Episcopal cathedral, to call for the return of Byzantium’s most important monument to the Orthodox Church. Days after his 1453 conquest of Constantinople, today’s Istanbul, Mehmet II decided to turn the 6th century basilica of St. Sophia into a mosque. Some 500 years later, with the city under Allied occupation, Christendom wanted the building back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Church to Mosque to Museum Back to Mosque', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T14:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e316bd5-92c9-52b2-b48a-27f1894e7d03', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e316bd5-92c9-52b2-b48a-27f1894e7d03'}, {'abstract': 'You can easily find out the type of processor the computer uses, the amount of memory installed and other details of your PC or Mac with menu commands or keyboard shortcuts.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/tip-of-the-week-find-your-system-information-quickly/', 'snippet': 'You can easily find out the type of processor the computer uses, the amount of memory installed and other details of your PC or Mac with menu commands or keyboard shortcuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Want to buy that cool new video game but are unsure how much memory or what kind of processor your computer uses so you can make sure the software will work? Both Windows and Mac OS X keep these details, along with other hardware information, in a convenient place.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Find Your System Information Quickly', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tip Of The Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T14:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89850e33-2cca-50a7-9