hina, said the first day’s take on Wednesday for Marvel Entertainment’s action film was almost $21 million, beating the previous one-day record set by “Transformers: Dark of the Moon” in 2011.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Opening for ‘Iron Man 3’ in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Victory for Hollywood\r\nWith ‘Iron Man 3’ in China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Iron Man 3 (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T15:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7100326b-d3cb-59ae-ac9a-c94fe7a33ea8', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7100326b-d3cb-59ae-ac9a-c94fe7a33ea8'}, {'abstract': 'A backlog of vacancies in top posts throughout the Obama administration, especially in the State Department, has slowed policy making in a capital already known for inaction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/us/politics/top-posts-remain-vacant-throughout-obama-administration.html', 'snippet': 'A backlog of vacancies in top posts throughout the Obama administration, especially in the State Department, has slowed policy making in a capital already known for inaction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — John Kerry is practically home alone at the State Department, toiling without permanent assistant secretaries of state for the Middle East, Asia, Europe and Africa. At the Pentagon, a temporary personnel chief is managing furloughs for 800,000 civilian employees. There has not been a director of the Internal Revenue Service since last November, and it was only on Thursday that President Obama announced a nomination for commerce secretary after the job was open for nearly a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/JP-VACANCY/JP-VACANCY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics and Vetting Leave Key U.S. Posts Long Unfilled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trading Blame As U.S. Posts Stay Unfilled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T15:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8576b292-4afb-57b5-8dd6-63083797bda9', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8576b292-4afb-57b5-8dd6-63083797bda9'}, {'abstract': 'Just because Republicans are dysfunctional on health policy doesn’t mean that conservatives are wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/the-oregon-data-and-the-health-care-debate/', 'snippet': 'Just because Republicans are dysfunctional on health policy doesn’t mean that conservatives are wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The big news in health care today is the latest data from an ongoing study of Medicaid recipients in Oregon, which finds that while being on Medicaid improves people’s financial situation and boosts their mental well-being, in the interval studied the program seemed to have little or no statistically significant impact on their actual physical health. I’ll try to have more to say about this over the weekend \xa0—\xa0for now, I recommend reading\xa0Megan McArdle and Jonathan Cohn for a sense of the debate\xa0— but since I’ve been writing about the Republican Party’s health policy problem this week I was struck by this line from Matt Yglesias, in a post mostly dismissing the significance of the new data:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Oregon Data and the Health Care Debate', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T15:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32421642-d568-529e-9f4b-de205021b7bc', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32421642-d568-529e-9f4b-de205021b7bc'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/the-gun-report-may-2-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend, my new friend Jessica Mindich held a gun buyback in New Jersey. She really did. The company she runs, Jewelry For a Cause—which melts down guns and turns them into very cool-looking bracelets—put up $33,000 in proceeds from bracelet sales, allowing the city of Newark to offer cash for guns. More than 200 guns were turned in, including a number of assault weapons. The city touted the success of the buyback with a press conference on Tuesday. Indeed, Mindich and Newark view the buyback as so successful they are planning to hold another one later this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 2, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrisburg (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Paul (Minn)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T15:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a14d09-95de-5138-9f79-cb16e14ed170', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a14d09-95de-5138-9f79-cb1