-ups that take venture capital and even fewer chances for the founders of companies to earn anything in an exit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my previous Deal Professor column, I wrote about a Delaware lawsuit involving a venture capital company, Bloodhound Technologies, and how it exposed venture capital’s dirty little secret: in a sale, the founders are often left with nothing even if the venture capitalists profit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venture Capital’s Rocky Road for Entrepreneurs', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodward, Susan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbe122de-acff-5cfe-9011-060812b0938e', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbe122de-acff-5cfe-9011-060812b0938e'}, {'abstract': 'Glencore International, the Swiss commodities trader, announced on Thursday that its merger with the mining giant Xstrata was complete and that shares in the newly combined company, called Glencore Xstrata, will start trading in London on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/glencore-completes-deal-for-xstrata/', 'snippet': 'Glencore International, the Swiss commodities trader, announced on Thursday that its merger with the mining giant Xstrata was complete and that shares in the newly combined company, called Glencore Xstrata, will start trading in London on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – One of the world’s largest deals in recent years has finally reached the finishing line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore Completes Deal for Xstrata', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Mick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glasenberg, Ivan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xstrata', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d67854c0-022f-5cc4-9c4c-a46f49b98a64', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d67854c0-022f-5cc4-9c4c-a46f49b98a64'}, {'abstract': 'Children born outside the United States were 48 percent less likely to suffer from allergic diseases like asthma, eczema, hay fever and food allergies than those born in America, a study found.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/american-born-children-are-at-higher-risk-of-allergies/', 'snippet': 'Children born outside the United States were 48 percent less likely to suffer from allergic diseases like asthma, eczema, hay fever and food allergies than those born in America, a study found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American children born outside the United States may have a significant advantage over the native-born: They are less likely to have allergies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American-Born Children Are at Higher Risk of Allergies', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eczema', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca29f7c-b005-55c8-a83a-dbcba617f8db', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca29f7c-b005-55c8-a83a-dbcba617f8db'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of the upcoming exhibit at Metropolitan Museum of Art, “Punk: Chaos to Couture,” T seeks out the rock legacy in today’s market.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/market-report-punk-pieces/', 'snippet': 'In honor of the upcoming exhibit at Metropolitan Museum of Art, “Punk: Chaos to Couture,” T seeks out the rock legacy in today’s market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art pays homage to the style influence of iconic enfants terribles like Joe Strummer and Sid Vicious in the new exhibit “Punk: Chaos to Couture,” which will open to the public on May 9. T chimes in on the fashion conversation with a roundup of the chic counterculture legacy in today’s market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Punk Pieces', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2343180-64f1-52f9-8792-83d94fe1ccef', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2343180-64f1-52f9-8792-83d94fe1ccef'}, {'abstract': 'The acquisition of Instagram by Facebook a year ago was risky, and Instagram is still not profitable. But the potential payout is increasing, the author contends.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/instagram-deal-is-looking-better-and-better/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of Instagram by Facebook a year ago was risky, and Instagram is still not profitable. But the potential payout is increasing, the author contends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook’s Instagram option is looking like a better bet than it was a year ago. The social network agreed to shell out $1 billion for the revenue-free photo-sharing app. Even paid for partially in overvalued stock, the deal looked pricey. Instagram’s growth spurt – it passed 100 million monthly users in the first quarter – suggests Facebook is turning a defensive move to its advantage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Instagram Deal Is Looking Better and Better', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:38:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6227860-37a4-58fc-8676-1becbb8ddf54', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6227860-37a4-58fc-8676-1becbb8ddf54'}, {'abstract': 'A Twitter account called Did the Mets Lose? answers the question and, usually, no more.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/for-mets-fans-even-140-characters-can-be-too-many/', 'snippet': 'A Twitter account called Did the Mets Lose? answers the question and, usually, no more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who use Twitter to comment about the Mets – from @MetsMerized and @kranepool to @TheHappyRecap and @metspolice — usually have plenty to say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Mets Fans, Even 140 Characters Can Be Too Many', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francesa, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T16:43:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/620c0282-6968-5e67-861c-7a7934ddd9b5', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/620c0282-6968-5e67-861c-7a7934ddd9b5'}, {'abstract': 'The protagonist of Claire Messud’s new novel is an elementary schoolteacher in need of a fantasy. She finds one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/books/the-woman-upstairs-by-claire-messud.html', 'snippet': 'The protagonist of Claire Messud’s new novel is an elementary schoolteacher in need of a fantasy. She finds one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Claire Messud’s latest novel, “The Woman Upstairs,” is an incongruous mashup of a very self-consciously literary novel (invoking the likes of Chekhov) and one of those psychological horror films like “Single White Female” or “The Hand That Rocks the Cradle,” in which someone, ominously, is not who she appears to be. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03BOOK_SPAN/03BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 15