 the level of air pollution, the greater the thickening of the carotid artery, a known risk for heart attack and stroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Air pollution has been linked to cardiovascular disease, and now researchers may be closer to understanding why: it increases atherosclerosis, or hardening of the arteries, a known risk for heart attack and stroke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/health/well_safety/well_safety-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 213, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/health/well_safety/well_safety-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 213, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/health/well_safety/well_safety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/health/well_safety/well_safety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/health/well_safety/well_safety-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Air Pollution’s Role in Heart Disease', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARTERIOSCLEROSIS AND ATHEROSCLEROSIS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carotid Arteries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T17:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9f969f9-7b42-5277-b2e9-7c31dab98a01', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9f969f9-7b42-5277-b2e9-7c31dab98a01'}, {'abstract': 'It isn’t possible to tell the story of the Civil War without recourse to the million photographic images that were created, some of the best of which are part of a new museum exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/cameristas/', 'snippet': 'It isn’t possible to tell the story of the Civil War without recourse to the million photographic images that were created, some of the best of which are part of a new museum exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roughly 150 years ago, in March or April 1863, a shocking photograph was taken in Louisiana. Unlike most photos, it was given a title, “The Scourged Back,” as if it were a painting hanging in an art museum. Indeed, it fit inside a recognizable painter’s category — the nude — but this was a nude from hell. The sitter, an African-American male named Gordon, had been whipped so many times that a mountainous ridge of scar tissue was climbing out of his back. It was detailed, like a military map, and resulted from so many whippings that the scars had to form on top of one another. Gordon had escaped from a nearby Mississippi plantation to a camp of federal soldiers, supporting the great Vicksburg campaign of the spring. Medical officers examined him, and after seeing his back, asked a local photography firm, McPherson and Oliver, to document the scar tissue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cameristas', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T17:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Widmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Widmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab42d977-bc76-58a2-a6ea-fff604422c23', 'word_count': 1467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab42d977-bc76-58a2-a6ea-fff604422c23'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Moss and Michael Pollan on weeknight cooking on a tight schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/a-nutritious-meal-even-faster/', 'snippet': 'Michael Moss and Michael Pollan on weeknight cooking on a tight schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An hour just to make lunch? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nutritious Meal, Even Faster', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T17:27:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Weinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/783d65d9-ab3d-59ae-b0e5-bfb04fe36171', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/783d65d9-ab3d-59ae-b0e5-bfb04fe36171'}, {'abstract': 'The theater critics for The New York Times answer readers’ questions about musical adaptations, their biggest disappointments of the season and what awards season means.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/brantley-isherwood-answer-readers-questions-about-the-theater-season/', 'snippet': 'The theater critics for The New York Times answer readers’ questions about musical adaptations, their biggest disappointments of the season and what awards season means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood, theater critics for The New York Times, took readers’ questions about the Broadway season and this week’s announcement of the Tony Award nominations. Below are their answers to selected questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brantley, Isherwood Answer Readers’ Questions About the Theater Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T17:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356ad55f-87c4-56da-a3d1-f244e4972b97', 'word_count': 1980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356ad55f-87c4-56da-a3d1-f244e4972b97'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of the Swiss banking giant, the author says, should see Knight Vinke’s intervention as a warning — stick with the program and don’t stop cutting risk.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/why-a-ubs-split-would-not-be-the-best-move/', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of the Swiss banking giant, the author says, should see Knight Vinke’s intervention as a warning — stick with the program and don’t stop cutting risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UBS is the wrong target for an activist-led breakup. Knight Vinke has called on the Swiss bank to separate its risky investment banking business from the core wealth-management arm. The investment firm is right that no one would create a bank modeled on UBS as it is today. But it doesn’t automatically follow that a breakup is the best strategy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why a UBS Split Would Not Be the Best Move', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARNOLD, LUQMAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ermotti, Sergio P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T17:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominic Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominic', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad8f917-e305-5e8a-a6d0-0319e19549a2', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad8f917-e305-5e8a-a6d0-0319e19549a2'}, {'abstract': 'Quirks of the game: With 3-pointers harder to come by for the Knicks, analysts Steve Kerr and Shaquille O’Neal differ on whether the Knicks should adjust their long-range game.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/quirks-of-the-game-shooting-gets-tougher-in-the-playoffs/', 'snippet': 'Quirks of the game: With 3-pointers harder to come by for the Knicks, analysts Steve Kerr and Shaquille O’Neal differ on whether the Knicks should adjust their long-range game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quirks of the Game is a regular feature on 