ld-trade-center/', 'snippet': 'The spire of 1 World Trade Center was hoisted aloft on Thursday and set atop a temporary platform. It will be bolted into place at a later date.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking a bit like a rocket taking flight, the spire of 1 World Trade Center was hoisted aloft on Thursday and set on a temporary platform atop the nearly completed building. When it is bolted into place at a later date, the spire will bring the building to a height of 1,776 feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-wtc1a/02cityroom-wtc1a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crowning 1 World Trade Center', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acacbe30-1c97-5a33-89ad-f0c250fec82c', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acacbe30-1c97-5a33-89ad-f0c250fec82c'}, {'abstract': 'Works by the photographer Garry Winogrand — more than any museum has mounted at once — are the focus of a retrospective at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/arts/design/garry-winogrand-retrospective-in-san-francisco.html', 'snippet': 'Works by the photographer Garry Winogrand — more than any museum has mounted at once — are the focus of a retrospective at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Garry Winogrand refreshed classic street photography in the 1960s and ’70s, influenced by (and influencing) the increasingly warped sensibility that had started to shape the broader culture. Using a snapshot style, he captured the nation’s unseemly nervous breakdown in stark black and white.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN/05WINOGRAND1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Some Well-Eyed Streets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revisiting Some Well-Eyed Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loos, Ted', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winogrand, Garry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Loos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Loos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ece0274-8016-5978-84e3-7091909dee97', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ece0274-8016-5978-84e3-7091909dee97'}, {'abstract': 'A chat with Wrenn Schmidt, who will play the young muse Hilde in a production of Ibsen’s “Master Builder” at the Harvey Theater at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/theater/wrenn-schmidt-in-the-master-builder.html', 'snippet': 'A chat with Wrenn Schmidt, who will play the young muse Hilde in a production of Ibsen’s “Master Builder” at the Harvey Theater at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With her flowing red curls and the spray of freckles dusting her porcelain skin, Wrenn Schmidt looks like a Dante Gabriel Rossetti painting that has swanned off the canvas. She wears 1920s chiffons and cloches on the HBO series “Boardwalk Empire,” on which she plays Julia Sagorsky, the sympathetic girlfriend of the masked and disfigured tough guy Richard Harrow (Jack Huston), like a second skin. (HBO confirms that her character will return in the fourth season.) And the Mint Theater, which traffics exclusively in the curiosities of yesteryear, has drawn on Ms. Schmidt’s talents more than once, most recently in the title role of “Katie Roche.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1618, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1618}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 380, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05SNAPSHOT/05SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Period Look, Ringlets and All', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Wrenn Schmidt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Period Look, Ringlets and All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grode, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibsen, Henrik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Wrenn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Grode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/43e164b4-4de5-5532-9312-bf79a1e4006f', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43e164b4-4de5-5532-9312-bf79a1e4006f'}, {'abstract': 'Following on its five Tony nominations, the Douglas Carter Beane play starring Nathan Lane will be extended eight weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/the-nance-extends-its-run/', 'snippet': 'Following on its five Tony nominations, the Douglas Carter Beane play starring Nathan Lane will be extended eight weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performances of the Broadway play “The Nance” will be extended by eight weeks through August 11, Lincoln Center Theater announced on Thursday, aiming to capitalize on the Tony Award nomination this week for lead actor Nathan Lane. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Nance’ Extends Its Run', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Nance (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lane, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:21:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c073a0f5-470d-51c8-a963-8e0a9aa09bb0', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c073a0f5-470d-51c8-a963-8e0a9aa09bb0'}, {'abstract': 'Normandy Invasion, a 12-1 shot at the Kentucky Derby, ran off with his exercise rider for three-eighths of a mile, but he appeared to be unhurt.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/normandy-invasion-too-keen-during-workout/', 'snippet': 'Normandy Invasion, a 12-1 shot at the Kentucky Derby, ran off with his exercise rider for three-eighths of a mile, but he appeared to be unhurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The draw for post positions is complete, and the morning-line odds for the 139th running of the Kentucky Derby have been set. None of the key contenders appeared to be compromised by their post-position draw, so the Churchill Downs oddsmaker, Mike Battaglia, did not have to adjust the preliminary line he made before the draw. The favorites are Orb (7-2, Post 16) and Verrazano (4-1, Post 14).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Normandy Invasion Too Keen During Workout', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36e8c09f-9d8d-5a0e-a0dc-4d5463d35876', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36e8c09f-9d8d-5a0e-a0dc-4d5463d35876'}, {'abstract': 'A refund service from Citi has some caveats.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/my-tryout-of-citis-price-protection-service/', 'snippet': 'A refund service from Citi has some caveats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Awhile back, I wrote about a new service that Citigroup offers on its credit cards called Price Rewind. It lets cardholders register purchases, and then searches for the same items at lower prices. If it finds one, it refunds you the difference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Tryout of Citi’s Price Protection Service', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc4fc3d-2472-5ee0-af19-3c03bdd247fe', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc4fc3d-2472-5ee0-af19-3c03bdd247fe'}, {'abstract': 'A technology boom that once created middle-class jobs and lifted the overall economy now fuels a growing gap between the very rich and everyone else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/us/airport-project-reflects-a-changing-silicon-valley.html', 'snippet': 'A technology boom that once created middle-class jobs and lifted the overall economy now fuels a growing gap between the very rich and everyone else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN JOSE, Calif. — The approval of a new corporate jet center at this city’s struggling airport might have been just another losing skirmish in the battle between Silicon Valley billionaires and middle-class neighborhoods worried about noise pollution. Instead, it is becoming the latest symbol for the rapidly growing gap between the region’s haves, with their private jets and untold wealth, and the have-nots, clinging to more modest lives in the dwindling number of communities they can afford.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 466, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 466}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1590, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/us/SILICON/SILICON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Jet Center Exposes Silicon Valley’s Class Divide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corporate Jet Center Exposes Silicon Valley’s Class Divide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mineta San Jose International Airport (San Jose, Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Aircraft', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fe87b1c-aed9-5127-81a3-13df4974ad59', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fe87b1c-aed9-5127-81a3-13df4974ad59'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration’s compromise on reproductive rights will hurt girls and women and is bound to undermine the president’s credibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/opinion/putting-politics-ahead-of-womens-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration’s compromise on reproductive rights will hurt girls and women and is bound to undermine the president’s credibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Appearing before Planned Parenthood’s annual convention last Friday, President Obama pledged his continuing support for women’s reproductive rights. In a speech before the National Academy of Sciences on Monday, Mr. Obama promised to keep science a sphere “not subject to politics” or “skewed by an agenda.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Politics Ahead of Science', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting Politics Ahead of Science', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plan B (Contraceptive)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebelius, Kathleen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korman, Edward R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a60ab0ef-d303-5c24-a917-71928f2bcccb', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a60ab0ef-d303-5c24-a917-71928f2bcccb'}, {'abstract': 'Edward Albee’s play “Laying an Egg” was to have been the centerpiece of the new season at the Signature Theater, which scheduled and postponed the work once before, in the 2011-12 season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/albees-new-play-laying-an-egg-postponed-again/', 'snippet': 'Edward Albee’s play “Laying an Egg” was to have been the centerpiece of the new season at the Signature Theater, which scheduled and postponed the work once before, in the 2011-12 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edward Albee’s “Laying an Egg,” announced six weeks ago as a centerpiece of the Signature Theater’s 2013-14 season, has been postponed for the second time, the company announced on Thursday. Mr. Albee’s work was originally to have had its world premiere as part of the Off Broadway company’s 2011-12 season – its first at the Pershing Square Signature Center, its new Midtown space – but was postponed when the famously self-critical playwright, now 85, decided that it needed revamping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albee’s New Play, ‘Laying an Egg,’ Postponed Again', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:39:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b12eaff7-c70a-53eb-9e1b-ebf5b406be1e', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b12eaff7-c70a-53eb-9e1b-ebf5b406be1e'}, {'abstract': 'A primer on how to cook it.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/notes-from-the-recipe-tester-a-short-season-for-white-asparagus/', 'snippet': 'A primer on how to cook it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Denise Landis has been testing recipes for The New York Times for more than 20 years. She is also the author of “Dinner for Eight: 40 Great Dinner Party Menus for Friends and Family.” She is @TheCooksCook on Twitter. Here, she explains how to prepare white asparagus, available only for a short time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Recipe Tester: A Short Season for White Asparagus', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', '