s'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3a503e-5705-5205-b886-9dd1131d707f', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3a503e-5705-5205-b886-9dd1131d707f'}, {'abstract': 'The producers of “I’ll Eat You Last” and “Macbeth,” both of which were blanked in the Tony nomination derby, have decided not to offer free tickets to Tony voters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/ill-seat-you-last-tony-snubbed-shows-take-back-free-tickets/', 'snippet': 'The producers of “I’ll Eat You Last” and “Macbeth,” both of which were blanked in the Tony nomination derby, have decided not to offer free tickets to Tony voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday the Tony Award big shots had their say, spreading around nominations to 26 Broadway plays and musicals – and shutting out several others. Now some of the scorned are striking back: The producers of Bette Midler’s hit play “I’ll Eat You Last” and Alan Cumming’s mostly-one-man version of “Macbeth” are pulling back free tickets for many of the 868 Tony voters, and instead offering to sell them at standard prices of about $135 each.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I’ll Seat You Last: Tony-Snubbed Shows Take Back Free Tickets', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shut-Out Shows Strike Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davenport, Ken', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Midler, Bette', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T18:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23644643-5591-5c5c-a5e8-c97fa1b2d564', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23644643-5591-5c5c-a5e8-c97fa1b2d564'}, {'abstract': 'In a letter written on behalf of the co-op, a letter was written calling on Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to “take a leadership role” to save Long Island College Hospital, or LICH.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/park-slope-food-co-op-takes-up-new-cause-saving-a-hospital/', 'snippet': 'In a letter written on behalf of the co-op, a letter was written calling on Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to “take a leadership role” to save Long Island College Hospital, or LICH.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Park Slope Food Co-op, which fought a veritable civil war over whether to boycott Israeli products, has taken on a new cause célèbre: the fight to save Long Island College Hospital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-coop/02cityroom-coop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-coop/02cityroom-coop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-coop/02cityroom-coop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/nyregion/02cityroom-coop/02cityroom-coop-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype