ail': 'images/2013/05/02/movies/first_span/first_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/02/movies/first_span/first_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Tough to Keep a Tune, but Easy to Fall in Love', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Tough to Keep a Tune, But Easy to Fall in Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menaul, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maestro, Mia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Richard E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brightman, Sarah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovenden, Julian', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T22:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f99f89cc-db2d-5b9d-bb98-831dde3a3231', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f99f89cc-db2d-5b9d-bb98-831dde3a3231'}, {'abstract': 'Reinhart and Rogoff disappoint again.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/more-straw/', 'snippet': 'Reinhart and Rogoff disappoint again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Reinhart-Rogoff rehabilitation tour has been really depressing. There are a number of routes they could have gone; unfortunately, they seem addicted to the notion that they can end the discussion by arguing with straw men. I noted one example in their Times piece, in which they tried to rebut the reverse-causation argument by associating it with a claim — that it’s all about the business cycle — that, as far as I know, nobody has made. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Straw', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T22:24:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa3309b2-301d-531b-aeb4-bcf483bdfaef', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa3309b2-301d-531b-aeb4-bcf483bdfaef'}, {'abstract': 'This white Spanish wine goes well with cheese and asparagus, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/dining/matching-albarinos-with-more-than-just-seafood.html', 'snippet': 'This white Spanish wine goes well with cheese and asparagus, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People say that no wine pairs well with asparagus. I beg to differ. And Eric Asimov wondered whether anything other than seafood should be put with the albariños we tasted. Again, I beg to differ. Seafood is an obvious choice, but there is a long list of cheeses that would work well. Satiny, funky Torta del Casar and rich Mahón come to mind, though there are many other options from beyond Spain. Perhaps cheese with asparagus; these wines, with their persistent citric notes and occasional herbal allure, easily tame that springtime\xa0wine challenger. I chose asparagus barely cooked, to dress pasta in pastel green.\xa0I kept the tips whole and used the stems to make a finely ground pestolike mixture with garlic, olive oil and cheese, this time Grana Padano. Asparagus done this way also could\xa0enrich a risotto, fill an omelet or garnish a fillet of salmon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/dining/08PAIR/08PAIR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Matching Albariños With More Than Just Seafood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asparagus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'