. Events will take place both at the institute and at sites around the city.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for May 3-May 9', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Higgins DeSmet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': 'Higgins', 'lastname': 'DeSmet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aebc760-7cea-501e-b7b1-9351999a994c', 'word_count': 3117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aebc760-7cea-501e-b7b1-9351999a994c'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times critics on “Iron Man 3,” “What Maisie Knew” and “Something in the Air.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002204908/this-weeks-movies.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Times critics on “Iron Man 3,” “What Maisie Knew” and “Something in the Air.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times critics on “Iron Man 3,” “What Maisie Knew” and “Something in the Air.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/video-movies-05032013/video-movies-05032013-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Movies | May 3, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Iron Man 3 (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What Maisie Knew (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Something in the Air (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/56e06b54-a63f-55a4-af1f-ed48ca4edc62', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/56e06b54-a63f-55a4-af1f-ed48ca4edc62'}, {'abstract': 'Soren Kierkegaard’s strategy of “indirect communication” is not too far removed from the “dog-whistling” of modern political campaigns.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/rogue-philosopher-great-communicator/', 'snippet': 'Soren Kierkegaard’s strategy of “indirect communication” is not too far removed from the “dog-whistling” of modern political campaigns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, visitors to the Copenhagen City Museum wandered into a modest room that contains a few artifacts from the Danish philosopher Soren Kierkegaard’s life: portraits, meerschaum pipes, first editions and, best of all, the desk where he stood and produced with preternatural speed a series of original and difficult works, many of them written pseudonymously and published in editions that numbered in the hundreds — among them “Either-Or,” “Fear and Trembling,” “The Concept of Dread” and “Repetition.” The exhibit has been refreshed to mark Kierkegaard’s 200th birthday on May 5th. His belongings — a large library, furniture, paintings, and knickknacks —were pretty well dispersed after his death in 1855, but the expanded version will add an “outer circle” of relevant material. Manuscripts and papers from the Kierkegaard archives will be on display at the Royal Library.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rogue Philosopher, Great Communicator', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kierkegaard, Soren', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Copenhagen (Denmark)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9de5807-bec6-5f84-b350-246ac2ab8cda', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9de5807-bec6-5f84-b350-246ac2ab8cda'}, {'abstract': 'At Vietnamese restaurants in America, all kinds of foods are served together — noodles, soups, stir-frys, spring rolls. But in Vietnam, restaurants are often devoted to a single dish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/travel/learning-to-love-the-peoples-food-in-ho-chi-minh-city-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'At Vietnamese restaurants in America, all kinds of foods are served together — noodles, soups, stir-frys, spring rolls. But in Vietnam, restaurants are often devoted to a single dish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 1996, fresh out of college, I moved to Ho Chi Minh City for one simple reason: I loved Vietnamese food. At restaurants in Virginia, Maryland and Washington, I’d grown fond of the staples of the cuisine — grilled meats, startling herbs, crunchy vegetables — and particularly of pho, the aromatic beef noodle soup that is Vietnam’s national dish. As graduation approached, I knew I wanted to live overseas, and Communist Vietnam, which had just opened its doors to the West, was the obvious choice. In fact, it didn’t even feel like a choice at all — it felt like destiny.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05PERSONALJOURNEYS_SPAN/05PERSONALJOURNEYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05PERSONALJOURNEYS_SPAN/05PERSONALJOURNEYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub