ivier Assayas’s “Something in the Air” looks at the aftermath of a promising revolutionary energy that surged through France in 1968.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baby-boomer coming-of-age stories are about as rare as superhero movies or career-girl romantic comedies, and no less bound by conventions. A sensitive child, growing up amid social and political turmoil, feels misunderstood by parents and the universe and discovers what a character in “A Serious Man” memorably called “the new freedoms.” Sex, drugs and heartbreak line the path to a sadder, wiser understanding of life, in which youthful rage and idealism are blunted but not entirely abandoned. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex and Sadness After a Failed Revolt', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sex and Sadness After a Failed Revolt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assayas, Olivier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Something in the Air (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2486718-2d47-5e01-979a-cf15bd14425a', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2486718-2d47-5e01-979a-cf15bd14425a'}, {'abstract': 'Zach Johnson hadn’t planned on playing at the Wells Fargo Championship. But then North Korea began saber rattling …', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/seoul-out-charlotte-in/', 'snippet': 'Zach Johnson hadn’t planned on playing at the Wells Fargo Championship. But then North Korea began saber rattling …', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — The Wells Fargo Championship was not originally on Zach Johnson’s schedule. He added it after pulling out of last week’s Ballantine’s Championship, an event outside Seoul, South Korea, that was co-sanctioned by the European and Asian tours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seoul Out, Charlotte In', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Zach', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0cdc4a-941f-5a05-bda5-52ddeb3e8b7c', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0cdc4a-941f-5a05-bda5-52ddeb3e8b7c'}, {'abstract': 'Eat, shop and squeeze through the crowds in the giant Japanese city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO.html', 'snippet': 'Eat, shop and squeeze through the crowds in the giant Japanese city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eat, shop and squeeze through the crowds in the giant Japanese city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK/05TOKOYO-slide-ZTYK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do in Tokyo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5dd3a4d9-a17b-5421-b4c9-9157194eb0da', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5dd3a4d9-a17b-5421-b4c9-9157194eb0da'}, {'abstract': 'Besides joining the crowds on Tokyo’s shopper-clogged streets, you can take a cruise, see a Buddhist temple or partake of a kaiseki dinner on the 45th floor of a luxury hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/travel/36-hours-in-tokyo.html', 'snippet': 'Besides joining the crowds on Tokyo’s shopper-clogged streets, you can take a cruise, see a Buddhist temple or partake of a kaiseki dinner on the 45th floor of a luxury hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan’s population may be skewing older, leading the global march to demographic gridlock, but Tokyo feels like a city powered by the young. Sophisticated and sprawling, with half a dozen city centers that long ago grew together, it combines the life force of a national capital of everything — politics, finance, culture, style — with a talent for change and renewal that it earned the hard way, bouncing back after repeated flattening by earthquakes, fires and war over its 400 years of existence. The skyscraper race of the ’90s has slowed down, but a new romance with the city’s waterfront is flourishing, spots for sushi and pâté de foie gras are always being added to its 160,000 restaurants, and the teenagers jamming anime-inspired shopping districts update the outlandish costume of the moment every few months.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/travel/05HOURS1_SPAN/05HOURS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Tokyo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Tokyo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-02T23:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Ireland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ireland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be05b395-cf2c-52ab-b118-95fa1c76ddbe', 'word_count': 1572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be05b395-cf2c-52ab-b118-95fa1c76ddbe'}, {'abstract': 'This Republican House is almost like a parallel government, sitting in for some fantasy nation created in talk-radio land.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/house-of-un-representatives/', 'snippet': 'This Republican House is almost like a parallel government, sitting in for some fantasy nation created in talk-radio land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, the congressman from northeast Texas, Louie Gohmert, was talking about how the trans-Alaska oil pipeline improved the sex lives of certain wild animals — in his mind, the big tube was an industrial-strength aphrodisiac. “When the caribou want to go on a date,” he told a House hearing, “they invite each other to head over to the pipeline.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House of Un-Representatives', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gohmert, Louis B Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T00:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa4763f0-7555-569e-8bde-a06d50604837', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa4763f0-7555-569e-8bde-a06d50604837'}, {'abstract': '“Once Upon a Time in Brooklyn,” directed by Paul Borghese, enlists some familiar faces for a tale about a parolee who rejoins his old gang of thugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/movies/once-upon-a-time-in-brooklyn-directed-by-paul-borghese.html', 'snippet': '“Once Upon a Time in Brooklyn,” directed by Paul Borghese, enlists some familiar faces for a tale about a parolee who rejoins his old gang of thugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a rule of thumb, the thicker a film’s publicity notes, the slimmer its rewards. So if I tell you that the notes for “Once Upon a Time in Brooklyn” (previously titled “Goat”) could probably choke a medium-size anaconda, you may not need to read further.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1215, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN/03RDP_ONCE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'leg