6, 'uri': 'nyt://article/884264c4-e78f-5196-8c8d-7e410b2470c3'}, {'abstract': 'A Twitter campaign inspired by a documentary about the 1989 Central Park jogger case designates a prosecutor as the only villain in a collective failure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/nyregion/central-park-five-petition-oversimplifies-blame-in-a-collective-failure.html', 'snippet': 'A Twitter campaign inspired by a documentary about the 1989 Central Park jogger case designates a prosecutor as the only villain in a collective failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night of April 16, Frank Chi, watching television, became upset by the documentary “The Central Park Five,” about an attack on a jogger in 1989 and how the world responded to it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/about/about-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 487, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/about/about-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/about/about-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/about/about-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/about/about-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From ‘Central Park Five’ Case, a Lesson in Assigning Blame', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From ‘Central Park Five’ Case, a Lesson in Assigning Blame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Jogger Case (1989)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lederer, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chi, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Central Park Five (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Ken', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Sarah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairstein, Linda', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T00:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/129ca978-b69e-5d27-807d-210f53010d83', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129ca978-b69e-5d27-807d-210f53010d83'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for the opposition candidate in the recent presidential election, Henrique Capriles Radonski, on Thursday submitted papers to the Supreme Court challenging the result.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/world/americas/venezuela-legal-challenge-to-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for the opposition candidate in the recent presidential election, Henrique Capriles Radonski, on Thursday submitted papers to the Supreme Court challenging the result.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lawyers for the opposition candidate in the recent presidential election, Henrique Capriles Radonski, on Thursday submitted papers to the Supreme Court challenging the result. Mr. Capriles lost to Nicolás Maduro, the handpicked heir of former President Hugo Chávez, by less than two percentage points. Arguing that the voting was marred by irregularities, the lawyers said the goal was to force a new election. Mr. Capriles said this week that he did not expect a favorable ruling from the court, which many say is packed with government loyalists. But he said he hoped that international pressure would impel a change in Venezuela. He has refused to take part in a partial review of digital voting records planned by electoral authorities, calling it a sham. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Legal Challenge to Vote', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Legal Challenge to Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capriles Radonski, Henrique', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T00:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/274be2e6-f65c-5c7e-a7c7-aa2b74f12218', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/274be2e6-f65c-5c7e-a7c7-aa2b74f12218'}, {'abstract': 'The United States should not intervene unilaterally in Syria. It needs to have Russia and the Arab League on board.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/opinion/obama-cant-go-it-alone-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The United States should not intervene unilaterally in Syria. It needs to have Russia and the Arab League on board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Obama administration is awash in advice about what to do in Syria. With the administration’s having declared chemical weapons use by the government of Bashar al-Assad a “game changer,” many are advising the president to intervene militarily. The stakes are high: every day that Mr. Assad remains in power brings death and destruction to more Syrians; but after more than a decade of war in Iraq and Afghanistan, the prospect of American military intervention is daunting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Can’t Go It Alone in Syria', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Can’t Go It Alone in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'r