b_date': '2013-05-03T02:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b37714b3-bffc-5b3a-be09-b343912c5dd3', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b37714b3-bffc-5b3a-be09-b343912c5dd3'}, {'abstract': 'A crispy, twisty puzzle from David Kwong.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/02/crispy-twister/', 'snippet': 'A crispy, twisty puzzle from David Kwong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Here’s how you make an outstanding Friday puzzle: spend an inordinate amount of time listening and looking for terrific words and phrases that are fun to say, write and think about. Stash those nuggets of brilliance in your crossword database and wait patiently for the day when you can spring them on an unsuspecting public. Salt your blank grid with some of them, at least one in each sector to spread the love around. Eliminate all junk as you go. Resist the common temptation when feeling fill fatigue to add too many partials, obscurities and abbreviations. Rip those sections out when they appear. Harden your heart and rip again. When the grid is filled to within an inch of its life with awesomeness, clue that baby up (make it tough, now: it’s Friday) and then stand back as Will Shortz polishes it to a gleam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crispy Twister', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T02:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/738ffbc0-5d83-552c-8094-b29fe8d862e4', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/738ffbc0-5d83-552c-8094-b29fe8d862e4'}, {'abstract': 'Small-business owners in New York said a City Council package of antismoking legislation would drive customers into the arms of bootleg distributors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/nyregion/business-owners-take-aim-at-proposed-antismoking-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Small-business owners in New York said a City Council package of antismoking legislation would drive customers into the arms of bootleg distributors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Small-business owners took aim on Thursday at the New York City Council’s package of antismoking legislation, including a proposal to raise the minimum age to purchase cigarettes to 21.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Owners Take Aim at Proposed Smoking Laws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Business Owners Take Aim At Proposed Smoking Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farley, Thomas A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convenience Stores', 'rank': 9, 'major':