ada Leo Smith’s “Ten Freedom Summers,” a monumental jazz work presented at Roulette in Brooklyn, conjures the spirit and struggles of the civil rights movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/arts/music/ten-freedom-summers-by-wadada-leo-smith.html', 'snippet': 'Wadada Leo Smith’s “Ten Freedom Summers,” a monumental jazz work presented at Roulette in Brooklyn, conjures the spirit and struggles of the civil rights movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trumpeter and composer Wadada Leo Smith talked to the audience and took questions for a little while after performing the first third of his five-and-a-half-hour work “Ten Freedom Summers” on Wednesday night at Roulette, and it was good that he did. The music had been heavy on elegy: alternately noble or mournful, sometimes formal, sometimes severe and agitated. But Mr. Smith was playful, open and demystifying. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03WADADA_SPAN/WADADA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03WADADA_SPAN/WADADA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03WADADA_SPAN/WADADA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03WADADA_SPAN/WADADA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/03WADADA_SPAN/WADADA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'widt