cle/0144e2b2-365e-551f-80d2-fd7c0755e9c4'}, {'abstract': 'Despite fiscal austerity in Washington, the private sector is helping create jobs and force the overall unemployment rate in April down to its lowest level since the end of 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/business/economy/us-adds-165000-jobs-in-april.html', 'snippet': 'Despite fiscal austerity in Washington, the private sector is helping create jobs and force the overall unemployment rate in April down to its lowest level since the end of 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington may be hitting the brakes, but the private sector is still rolling ahead, helping create nearly 200,000 jobs a month, on average, since the beginning of the year and forcing the overall unemployment rate in April down to its lowest level since the end of 2008. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Data Eases Fears of Economic Slowdown in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs Data Eases Fears Of a Sharp Slowdown; Joblessness Dips to 7.5%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T12:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd724c3-1e53-54d6-9445-1031f759f5fb', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd724c3-1e53-54d6-9445-1031f759f5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Valery Gergiev leads a two-and-a-half-hour performance at the Mariinsky II in St. Petersburg, Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/furs-putin-and-music-and-ballet-too-at-new-mariinsky-theater-gala/', 'snippet': 'Valery Gergiev leads a two-and-a-half-hour performance at the Mariinsky II in St. Petersburg, Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Russia — At the gala concert on Thursday evening that formally opened Mariinsky II, the $700 million companion to the opulent 19th-century Mariinsky Theater here, the theme was the union of old and new. The point was to show off the technical capabilities of the limestone-and-glass house while assuring the well-heeled, well-furred audience, which included President Vladimir V. Putin, that the Mariinsky’s traditions would be upheld.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/music/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/music/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/music/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/music/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/arts/music/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'i