 '2013-05-03T14:48:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve McPherson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McPherson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c2be5e-d372-5647-8301-1e829ccc671c', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c2be5e-d372-5647-8301-1e829ccc671c'}, {'abstract': 'In a report published late on Thursday, Institutional Shareholder Services backed virtually every argument that Elliott has made for its five director nominees since beginning its fight earlier this year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/i-s-s-backs-elliott-in-fight-over-hess-board/', 'snippet': 'In a report published late on Thursday, Institutional Shareholder Services backed virtually every argument that Elliott has made for its five director nominees since beginning its fight earlier this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An influential adviser to shareholders sided with Elliott Management in the fight over Hess Corporation‘s board, recommending that investors support the hedge fund’s slate of five directors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.S.S. Backs Elliott in Fight Over Hess’s Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hess Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Shareholder Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T14:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb180919-5d2b-5695-bdd1-94bf479139cf', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb180919-5d2b-5695-bdd1-94bf479139cf'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not always about the money.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/varieties-of-academic-temptation/', 'snippet': 'It’s not always about the money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These aren’t good times for austerian economics; and, to be honest, they aren’t too good for economics in general. Even if some economists have come out of the Reinhart/Rogoff/Alesina/Ardagna business looking pretty good, the reputation of the intellectual enterprise as a whole has clearly suffered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Varieties of Academic Temptation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T14:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83b657c3-7cdc-5a6b-8f54-2dd33d9b6b5b', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83b657c3-7cdc-5a6b-8f54-2dd33d9b6b5b'}, {'abstract': 'The Warriors eliminated the Nuggets in an exciting series on Thursday night. Making it through the Bulls-Nets series was harder work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/sports/in-the-nba-a-late-show-worth-watching.html', 'snippet': 'The Warriors eliminated the Nuggets in an exciting series on Thursday night. Making it through the Bulls-Nets series was harder work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The good news for N.B.A. fans is that they got to witness a quirky and truly terrific first-round series in which a spunky, overlooked team charged into the second round while its rabid fans created a spectacular racket. The bad news for N.B.A. fans is that it happened in Oakland. For a good half of the country, watching the plucky Golden State Warriors topple the Nuggets required superhuman stamina or gallons of coffee — particularly if you spent the intervening prime-time hours watching the Nets and Bulls claw at each other in a desperate attempt to be the team that does not completely implode.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/sports/baseball/04leadingpic/04leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/04/sports/baseball/04leadingpic/04leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/sports/baseball/04leadingpic/04leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/sports/baseball/04leadingpic/04leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/sports/baseball/04leadingpic/04leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',