 Dylan quotes).', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05sedaris-img/05sedaris-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 457, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05sedaris-img/05sedaris-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 457, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05sedaris-img/05sedaris-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05sedaris-img/05sedaris-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05sedaris-img/05sedaris-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TBR: Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T15:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7deb449-ecb9-5380-b9a0-84c6e02de9dd', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7deb449-ecb9-5380-b9a0-84c6e02de9dd'}, {'abstract': 'Fiction meets history in Ismail Kadare’s novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/books/review/ismail-kadares-fall-of-the-stone-city.html', 'snippet': 'Fiction meets history in Ismail Kadare’s novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every city offers residents a way to chart the well-being of their surroundings. For the Albanian city of Gjirokaster, as depicted in Ismail Kadare’s tragicomic novel “The Fall of the Stone City,” a misperceived rivalry between doctors becomes a barometer to assess the political gales that battered Eastern Europe during World War II and the cold war.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Against Tyranny', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Against Tyranny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadare, Ismail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T15:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Byrd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Byrd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c667be0-0752-5860-9f46-f0b151de59bc', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c667be0-0752-5860-9f46-f0b151de59bc'}, {'abstract': 'The Polish singer Vera Gran survived World War II, but at a heavy price.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/books/review/vera-gran-the-accused-by-agata-tuszynska.html', 'snippet': 'The Polish singer Vera Gran survived World War II, but at a heavy price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring of 1941 the Jewish cabaret singer Vera Gran began performing at the Sztuka, a cafe in the Warsaw ghetto frequented by intellectuals and remnants of Jewish high society. The place was also popular with collaborators, including the so-called Jewish Gestapo who selected and rounded up their fellow Jews for transportation to Treblinka. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05LASDUN/05LASDUN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05LASDUN/05LASDUN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05LASDUN/05LASDUN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05LASDUN/05LASDUN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05LASDUN/05LASDUN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Suspicion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Suspicion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gran, Vera (1916-2007)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuszynska, Agata', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T15:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Lasdun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasdun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2972e9f2-5394-54c7-9aa4-870379bbac53', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2972e9f2-5394-54c7-9aa4-870379bbac53'}, {'abstract': 'In André Aciman’s novel, an alienated immigrant grad student befriends a volatile immigrant hack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/books/review/harvard-square-by-andre-aciman.html', 'snippet': 'In André Aciman’s novel, an alienated immigrant grad student befriends a volatile immigrant hack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing like a college campus in summer. It’s peaceful. You feel as if you finally own the place, as if you belong. The classrooms are empty, and you can wander the hallways alone. The undergraduates are gone, the professors traveling or holed up in their offices; a handful of shy grad students, the trees and grass, the fountains and libraries take over. It’s like the vanished gardens of Córdoba.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1211, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/05MARTIN/05MARTIN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxi Driver', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taxi Driver', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ACIMAN, ANDRE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T15:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clancy Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/07b3c551-d4fb-5306-a955-5f22599e2601', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07b3c551-d4fb-5306-a955-5f22599e2601'}, {'abstract': 'The theoretical physicist Lee Smolin examines the role of time in the universe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/books/review/time-reborn-by-lee-smolin.html', 'snippet': 'The theoretical physicist Lee Smolin examines the role of time in the universe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of the more fanciful conceptions of nature, the British physicist and philosopher Julian Barbour proposed that the world is just a “heap of moments,” each an instant of frozen time. There is no order to the moments, no sequence, no cause-and-effect relationship. We exist only from moment to moment. If we experience time passing, it’s because this particular moment has memories of another moment woven into it. Some moments are interesting: they contain complexity, stars and planets, life. Others are boring: they contain only energy, or perhaps nothing at all.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 664}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1559, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN/0505-bks-LIGHTMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/books/review/0505-bks