.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/world/europe/irish-catholic-church-condemns-abortion-legislation.html', 'snippet': 'Irish bishops called the legislation, which would permit abortions in cases where a threat existed to a woman’s life, morally unacceptable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — The Catholic Church in Ireland on Friday condemned the government’s abortion legislation, which would permit abortions in cases where a threat existed to a woman’s life, including from suicide. The church called the legislation “a dramatically and morally unacceptable change to Irish law.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irish Catholic Church Condemns Abortion Legislation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ireland: Catholic Bishops Condemn an Abortion Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalby, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T16:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1f68b96-51a9-5523-948d-f9afa15a85bf', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1f68b96-51a9-5523-948d-f9afa15a85bf'}, {'abstract': 'The Liberty Bell received a visit on Friday from Cuba’s premier sexologist, who is also the daughter of President Raúl Castro.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/liberty-bell-visit-by-fidel-castros-sexologist-niece-angers-cuban-americans/', 'snippet': 'The Liberty Bell received a visit on Friday from Cuba’s premier sexologist, who is also the daughter of President Raúl Castro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 4:55 p.m. Much to the chagrin of conservative Cuban-American exiles, a senior Cuban official was permitted to visit the iconic Liberty Bell in Philadelphia on Friday afternoon. The visitor was Mariela Castro, the daughter of President Raúl Castro and Cuba’s premier sexologist, currently visiting Philadelphia as a guest of the Equality Forum, a gay rights organization that is holding its annual conference there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/03/world/americas/03lede_castro/03lede_castro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnai