ian Flynn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lehane’s ‘Live by Night’ Wins Edgar Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mystery Writers of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T16:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9164531e-71b6-5774-8714-574a89f8b846', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9164531e-71b6-5774-8714-574a89f8b846'}, {'abstract': 'The clarinet, dominant in jazz’s early years, faded into obscurity as the saxophone became the reed of choice. But in the hands of Anat Cohen, the clarinet is cool again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/arts/music/anat-cohen-and-her-jazz-clarinet.html', 'snippet': 'The clarinet, dominant in jazz’s early years, faded into obscurity as the saxophone became the reed of choice. But in the hands of Anat Cohen, the clarinet is cool again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In search of some live Brazilian music a few months ago, I found my way to Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola, in the Time Warner Center, where the Brazilian percussionist Duduka Da Fonseca was leading a quintet. I can’t say I knew much about Mr. Da Fonseca before I heard his band that night, and among the things I didn’t know was that his quintet’s regular reed player was a 38-year-old Israeli woman named Anat Cohen, who has lived in New York since 1999.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05ANAT1_SPAN/05ANAT1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz’s Skinny Stepchild', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jazz&#8217;s Skinny Stepchild ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Anat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', '