 Ventura County, northwest of Los Angeles, damaging more than a dozen buildings and motor homes, fire officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Wildfire Jumps Pacific Coast Highway', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ventura County (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T18:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f83d64-ca26-5a7a-919d-9df3869140ce', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f83d64-ca26-5a7a-919d-9df3869140ce'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers discuss whether taxes are now at the top of their investing concerns, or whether taxes are a nonissue because the investments are all in retirement accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/investing-with-taxes-in-mind/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers discuss whether taxes are now at the top of their investing concerns, or whether taxes are a nonissue because the investments are all in retirement accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, looks at the role that higher taxes on investment gains are playing in investing decisions, especially in the wake of years of low tax rates. Indeed, financial advisers say more of their customers are asking about the tax implications of their buying and selling decisions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investing With Taxes in Mind', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T18:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d175ee0-9397-5066-a07b-ac9699edbc05', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d175ee0-9397-5066-a07b-ac9699edbc05'}, {'abstract': 'Palmetto Playground in Brooklyn Heights has been renamed “Adam Yauch Park” in commemoration of Mr. Yauch’s accomplishments as rapper, film director and activist, as well as his devotion to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/playground-named-for-a-beastie-boy/', 'snippet': 'Palmetto Playground in Brooklyn Heights has been renamed “Adam Yauch Park” in commemoration of Mr. Yauch’s accomplishments as rapper, film director and activist, as well as his devotion to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The name’s MCA – made in Downtown Brooklyn,” Adam Yauch sings on “Oh Word?,” the eighth track on the Beastie Boys’ 2004 album “To the 5 Boroughs.’’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/nyregion/03-yauch/03-yauch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/04/nyregion/03-yauch/03-yauch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't