o-hosts the celebrity-packed Barnstable Brown Gala with her twin sister, Priscilla Barnstable, on the eve of the Derby. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Party’s On With Our 2013 Kentucky Derby Picks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T19:23:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e86eab-0a57-59a2-9049-367f8849262d', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e86eab-0a57-59a2-9049-367f8849262d'}, {'abstract': 'A new four-part PBS series, “Constitution USA,” lets the NPR host Peter Sagal roam the nation on a motorcycle, investigating varied angles of one of America’s founding documents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/arts/television/scenic-views-of-the-constitution.html', 'snippet': 'A new four-part PBS series, “Constitution USA,” lets the NPR host Peter Sagal roam the nation on a motorcycle, investigating varied angles of one of America’s founding documents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To entice viewers who might be daunted by four hours of television devoted to the Constitution, PBS chose a host known for his comic touch with current events. Producers even put him on a specially decorated Harley-Davidson for jaunts around the country.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05CONSTITUTION1_SPAN/05CONSTITUTION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/arts/05CONSTITUTION1_SPAN/05CONST