o much to ask (listen to the lyrics); Win (lead singer) and Regine (drums in this video) just had a baby boy. But congrats — and there’s a new album reportedly coming!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: The Suburbs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T19:51:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f558ba9-efec-50ab-b0d5-7a5895666943', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f558ba9-efec-50ab-b0d5-7a5895666943'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway revival is the latest in a long line of flops with music by Frank Wildhorn.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/that-old-wildhorn-magic-jekyll-hyde-to-close/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway revival is the latest in a long line of flops with music by Frank Wildhorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The producers of the Broadway revival of the musical “Jekyll & Hyde” announced on Friday that the show would come to a premature end, with its final performance on Sunday, May 12, after only 15 previews and 30 regular performances at the Marquis Theater. It was scheduled to run until June 30.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Old Wildhorn Magic: ‘Jekyll & Hyde’ to Close', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Wildhorn Magic: ‘Jekyll & Hyde’ to Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildhorn, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T19:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/941c70eb-21f5-546a-b526-67a688a048e7', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/941c70eb-21f5-546a-b526-67a688a048e7'}, {'abstract': 'Rose to Gold was purchased for $1.400 but she has shown the heart of a champion heading into the Kentucky Oaks on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/rose-to-gold-makes-for-an-appealing-underdog-story/', 'snippet': 'Rose to Gold was purchased for $1.400 but she has shown the heart of a champion heading into the Kentucky Oaks on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — Fans searching for an endearing long shot when the $1 million Kentucky Oaks is run at Churchill Downs Friday may not have to look beyond 15-1 Rose to Gold and jockey Calvin Borel. She was a $1,400 purchase as a yearling who has won 5 of 7 career starts for earnings of $717,889.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rose to Gold Makes for an Appealing Underdog Story', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Oaks Horse Race', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T19:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a0db88f-5c2e-55e6-a12d-92658d1fb1a6', 'word_count': 23