for De Beers wrote a line that is now famous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peggy Olson, that emblem of the pioneering ad woman in a man’s world on the television show “Mad Men,” would have been all of 8 years old on the night in 1947 when the real-life copywriter Frances Gerety coined the phrase “A Diamond Is Forever.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1066, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05DIAMONDS_SPAN/05DIAMOND1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Diamonds Became Forever', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Diamonds Became Forever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T20:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Courtney Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'Courtney', 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72484c18-15ae-5362-88fc-603beed84142', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72484c18-15ae-5362-88fc-603beed84142'}, {'abstract': 'Should parents make emergency contraception available to teenagers?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/is-there-emergency-contraception-in-your-medicine-cabinet/', 'snippet': 'Should parents make emergency contraception available to teenagers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, a judge ordered that emergency contraception be available over-the-counter to girls and women of all ages, and the Obama administration announced its intention to appeal that order with respect to girls under 15. The Food and Drug Administration announced that the most widely known morning-after pill, Plan B One-Step, would be available to girls and women ages 15 and older, and that it would be stocked on drugstore shelves, rather than behind the counter. Purchasers will have to show ID to buy the drug.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There Emergency Contraception in Your Medicine Cabinet?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plan B (Contraceptive)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF PEDIATRICS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T20:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cb8d82f-f79f-57e2-9341-a94cbc6f2759', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cb8d82f-f79f-57e2-9341-a94cbc6f2759'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Nadler’s “I’m a Stranger Here Myself: Musik From the Weimar and Beyond,” at the York Theater Company, broadens his cabaret show about Germany before the Nazi crackdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/theater/reviews/mark-nadlers-im-a-stranger-here-myself-at-york-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Nadler’s “I’m a Stranger Here Myself: Musik From the Weimar and Beyond,” at the York Theater Company, broadens his cabaret show about Germany before the Nazi crackdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s evident that Mark Nadler’s “I’m a Stranger Here Myself: Musik From the Weimar and Beyond” has cabaret DNA, but Mr. Nadler has done a thoughtful job of expanding and deepening the piece for its theatrical run at the York Theater Company.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '