cb2d35f-957a-5982-9575-245947571523', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cb2d35f-957a-5982-9575-245947571523'}, {'abstract': 'A biography explains how the poet neglected to mention her thirst for glamour and fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/fashion/seeing-sylvia-plath-with-new-eyes-cultural-studies.html', 'snippet': 'A biography explains how the poet neglected to mention her thirst for glamour and fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, as anyone of a poetic temperament cannot fail to have noticed, is the 50th anniversary of Sylvia Plath’s suicide. Her death occurred a month after the publication of her autobiographical novel, “The Bell Jar,” and not long after she completed a manuscript of her influential poetry collection, “Ariel.” Plath’s estranged husband, the poet Ted Hughes, published a version of “Ariel” in 1965, ordering and choosing its poems as he saw fit, assuring her posthumous fame — and directing the shape that fame would assume.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05CULTURAL_SPAN/05CULTURAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05CULTURAL_SPAN/05CULTURAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05CULTURAL_SPAN/05CULTURAL_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05CULTURAL_SPAN/05CULTURAL_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's