 attempt to keep their children safe, access social media, but at the end of the day, is it really too much information?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be a timeless curse of parenthood to know simultaneously too much about one’s teenager and yet never access the information one actually wants. But the unruly morass of today’s social media and cellphone-infested landscape seems to have made both aspects of the curse worse. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05BIGMOTHER_SPAN/05BIGMOTHER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyberparenting and the Risk of T.M.I.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cyberparenting and the Risk of T.M.I.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Pamela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T22:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c4db98e-5386-5979-8df8-c17787ef3070', 'word_count': 1884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c4db98e-5386-5979-8df8-c17787ef3070'}, {'abstract': 'At Wild Rocket, the “rocket” in the 12-seat storefront cafe’s name refers to arugula, which is featured in most of the salads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/nyregion/sandwiches-rocket-fast-in-huntington.html', 'snippet': 'At Wild Rocket, the “rocket” in the 12-seat storefront cafe’s name refers to arugula, which is featured in most of the salads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wild Rocket, a new sandwich shop in Huntington, is the first fast-food venture from the Reststar Hospitality Group, which also owns Bistro Citron in Roslyn and Bistro Cassis and Café Buenos Aires in Huntington, among others. Wild Rocket, which opened in March, is run by Jason Machado, 34, of Huntington, and his brother, Eric, 41, two of the partners in Reststar. They hired Marc Anthony Bynum, a consultant and chef, to create a menu of sandwiches, salads and smoothies that took inspiration from the company’s restaurants.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandwiches, Rocket-Fast', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Huntington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sandwiches, Rocket-Fast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Huntington (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wild Rocket (Huntington, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T22:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan M. Novick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c9c458-2a1c-506e-a815-3a3e88dfcdf3', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c9c458-2a1c-506e-a815-3a3e88dfcdf3'}, {'abstract': 'Watch a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include a five-alarm fire in the Bronx, a motorcycle club in Queens and the cherry blossoms blooming in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/the-week-in-pictures-for-may-3/', 'snippet': 'Watch a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include a five-alarm fire in the Bronx, a motorcycle club in Queens and the cherry blossoms blooming in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects inclu