e_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5a2e3e-3d5d-50e3-8ddc-0ebee819025a', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5a2e3e-3d5d-50e3-8ddc-0ebee819025a'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include a suit against Warner Brothers by the developers of two sites based on cat memes, what Google is up to with game development, and a text service aimed at fans of “Arrested Development.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/todays-scuttlebot-internet-cats-sue-and-google-games/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include a suit against Warner Brothers by the developers of two sites based on cat memes, what Google is up to with g...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Internet Cats Sue, and Google Games', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-03T23:09:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b09d3d-ef90-5dcb-8be2-714c53eb036c', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b09d3d-ef90-5dcb-8be2-714c53eb036c'}, {'abstract': 'Gone are the days when “conformist” was a slur. Now, if you’re not following the crowd of five-star dispensers, you are a tasteless, undiscriminating shlub.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/fashion/seeking-out-peer-pressure.html', 'snippet': 'Gone are the days when “conformist” was a slur. Now, if you’re not following the crowd of five-star dispensers, you are a tasteless, undiscriminating shlub.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, a friend of mine, a dear man with exquisite taste, took me to dinner at Momofuku Má Pêche in Midtown Manhattan. I point out his taste because, being from out of town, he chose the restaurant on the fly, based on some reviews he had read on Yelp, the social networking site that rates everything from eating establishments to vacuum cleaners to gastroenterologists. The supertrendy place had gotten some raves.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05LONELY-SPAN/05LONELY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/fashion/05LONELY-SPAN/05LONELY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag