6-57d6-8276-d36ac5f7c1df'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet is presenting a Richard Rodgers program at the David H. Koch Theater as part of its American Music Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-in-an-all-rodgers-program.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet is presenting a Richard Rodgers program at the David H. Koch Theater as part of its American Music Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Igor Stravinsky is a composer synonymous with New York City Ballet and its co-founder George Balanchine, but what about Richard Rodgers? On Thursday, as part of the company’s American Music Festival at the David H. Koch Theater, City Ballet unveiled an all-Rodgers evening that opened a door to ballet’s jazzy, sensuous side. As the three-week festival continues, others, from Philip Glass to Nico Muhly, will be heard, revealing ways that music gains — or loses — flavor through ballet. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/arts/04RODGERS/04RODGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/04/arts/04RODGERS/04RODGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 607}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/arts/04RODGERS/04RODGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1014, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/arts/04RODGERS/04RODGERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2027, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/arts/04RODGERS/