the battlefield, as Sherman and his army took the conflict to the farmland and cities of the South.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning the Field, but Not the War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T00:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Q. Whitman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Whitman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a62931c8-f40e-5cf7-8f8e-95dfc539c4ff', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a62931c8-f40e-5cf7-8f8e-95dfc539c4ff'}, {'abstract': 'The legislation is a response to hours-long waits for voters in several counties and a deeply flawed early voting program in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/us/florida-lawmakers-approve-overhaul-of-states-problem-ridden-voting-process.html', 'snippet': 'The legislation is a response to hours-long waits for voters in several counties and a deeply flawed early voting program in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Six months after Florida became the butt of late-night jokes for a chaotic voting process that bedeviled the 2012 presidential election, the State Legislature passed a bill on Friday to remedy many of those problems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Lawmakers Approve Overhaul of State’s Problem-Ridden Voting Process', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida Lawmakers Approve Overhaul of State’s Problem-Ridden Voting Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Latvala, Jack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T00:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a1846d3-683d-545b-96bb-d5df572dfb73', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a1846d3-683d-545b-96bb-d5df572dfb73'}, {'abstract': 'The April employment report suggests the distressing shape of things to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/opinion/jobs-wages-and-the-sequester.html', 'snippet': 'The April employment report suggests the distressing shape of things to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The employment report released on Friday showed some economic resilience. Job growth for March was revised upward to 138,000 new jobs, while the tally for April, at 165,000 jobs, was stronger still. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs, Wages and the Sequester', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs, Wages and the Sequester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T01:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/521141f1-7434-5fc1-858b-b9f8efe91205', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/521141f1-7434-5fc1-858b-b9f8efe91205'}, {'abstract': 'For more than seven hours, a sinkhole in the West Village captivated the neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/small-cute-sinkhole-swallows-menu-and-soda-bottle/', 'snippet': 'For more than seven hours, a sinkhole in the West Village captivated the neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re like us, you’ve probably read more than enough stories about horrible nightmare sinkholes that swallow up trucks and kill people. Join us, then, in praise of the Little Sinkhole of West Tenth Street. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/03cityroom-sinkhole2/03cityroom-sinkhole2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/03cityroom-sin