], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/886986fa-228f-5d62-8a54-58410fca8bd0', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886986fa-228f-5d62-8a54-58410fca8bd0'}, {'abstract': 'In “New York and Los Angeles: The Uncertain Future,” two sociology professors examine the demographic, political, economic and cultural forces shaping the country’s two biggest metropolitan areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/nyregion/books-examine-outlook-for-new-york-and-la-and-lorcas-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'In “New York and Los Angeles: The Uncertain Future,” two sociology professors examine the demographic, political, economic and cultural forces shaping the country’s two biggest metropolitan areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One in eight Americans lives in metropolitan New York or Los Angeles, so exploring and comparing the regions is an instructive exercise in where the nation is heading. And in “New York and Los Angeles: The Uncertain Future” (Oxford University Press, $34.95), Andrew A. Beveridge and David Halle, sociology professors at Queens College and the University of California, Los Angeles, enlist experts from the social sciences to do just that.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Futures, a Poet’s Past', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Futures, a Poet’s Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Lorca, Federico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beveridge, Andrew A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T01:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ea9da9-7560-5ff1-bb00-8e5911ca31bb', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ea9da9-7560-5ff1-bb00-8e5911ca31bb'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, May 3, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/03/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-may-3-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, May 3, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It is the baby boomer group where we see the highest rates of suicide. There may be something about that group, and how they think about life issues and their life choices that may make a difference.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, May 3, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation Of The Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T01:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/991a3234-fa38-59b3-a323-495e7bfd6d13', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/991a3234-fa38-59b3-a323-495e7bfd6d13'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg fails to persuade in his defense of a troubled police program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/opinion/mayor-bloomberg-on-stop-and-frisk.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg fails to persuade in his defense of a troubled police program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg trotted out shopworn, discredited arguments this week while defending the constitutionally suspect police program under which hundreds of thousands of innocent New Yorkers have been detained and questioned on the streets every year. His speech, at 1 Police Plaza, castigated civil rights lawyers who oppose what they say is the practice of stopping people based on race instead of reasonable suspicion; Democratic mayoral candidates who want to rein in the stop-and-frisk program; and the City Council, which is considering a perfectly reasonable bill that would create the position of Police Department inspector general, with broad powers to review department policies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mayor on Stop-and-Frisk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mayor on Stop-and-Frisk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T01:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaec53bc-7b64-553d-ae79-5b7eea4c4fd0', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaec53bc-7b64-553d-ae79-5b7eea4c4fd0'}, {'abstract': 'In agreeing to bury the bombing suspect Tamerlan Tsarnaev, a Worcester, Mass., funeral director had to answer an official’s questions as he struggled to find a cemetery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/us/funeral-home-accepts-tsarnaevs-body-and-with-it-problems.html', 'snippet': 'In agreeing to bury the bombing suspect Tamerlan Tsarnaev, a Worcester, Mass., funeral director had to answer an official’s questions as he struggled to find a cemetery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WORCESTER, Mass. — Peter A. Stefan sat straight up in a leather chair in the funeral home he owns and looked purposefully at the city councilor who had come to ask him why he of all people was storing the body of Tamerlan Tsarnaev.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/us/BODY/BODY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 485, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/us/BODY/BODY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 485, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/us/BODY/BODY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/04/us/BODY/BODY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/04/us/BODY/BODY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Funeral Home Accepts Suspect’s Body, and Problems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Funeral Home Accepts Body, And With It, Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stefan, Peter A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2,