ne Sandy, would double the number of zones to six and include an additional 640,000 New York City residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/04/nyregion/new-york-city-to-double-number-of-storm-evacuation-zones.html', 'snippet': 'The expansion, outlined in a report on the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, would double the number of zones to six and include an additional 640,000 New York City residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bloomberg administration announced on Friday that it would double to six the number of evacuation zones along New York City’s coast and expand them to include an additional 640,000 residents, saying that the new map would provide more flexibility when major storms hit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Evacuation Zones in Response to Hurricane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adding Evacuation Zones In Response to Hurricane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halbfinger, David M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holloway, Caswell F IV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbs, Linda I', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T02:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger and Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/900dcb3c-037f-54b9-9de8-8bfaa509eb4a', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/900dcb3c-037f-54b9-9de8-8bfaa509eb4a'}, {'abstract': 'David S. Yassky, commissioner of the city’s Taxi and Limousine Commission, spends Sundays with his wife and daughter, walking the dog, going to spin class, cooking and watching classic television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/nyregion/on-sundays-david-yassky-trades-handshakes-for-home-cooking.html', 'snippet': 'David S. Yassky, commissioner of the city’s Taxi and Limousine Commission, spends Sundays with his wife and daughter, walking the dog, going to spin class, cooking and watching classic television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his former life as a city councilman and candidate for city comptroller, David S. Yassky, 49, saw many weekend hours sacrificed to political events; handshaking, crowd stirring, park-cleaning. But though his current job, as commissioner of the city’s Taxi and Limousine Commission, can intrude on any given weekend, he seems to have recaptured his Sundays. Now they begin with a trip to the dog run near his Brooklyn Heights home and an exercise outing with his wife, Diana Fortuna, the chief financial officer of the Metropolitan Opera. They typically end with a dose of classic television. In between, Mr. Yassky strives to prove his culinary chops to the couple’s 14-year-old daughter, Margaret, a Food Network fan with a discerning palate. Their other daughter, Susan, 19, is finishing her freshman year at Yale.  ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 