ss Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8be206d0-e474-5ed4-88d3-75febbd3451c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8be206d0-e474-5ed4-88d3-75febbd3451c'}, {'abstract': 'Alex and Jamie Schneider, autistic 22-year-old identical twins from Long Island, have completed more than 120 races, including five marathons, over the past seven years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/sports/autistic-twins-find-a-release-in-running.html', 'snippet': 'Alex and Jamie Schneider, autistic 22-year-old identical twins from Long Island, have completed more than 120 races, including five marathons, over the past seven years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHPAGE, N.Y. — Alex and Jamie Schneider run seemingly on instinct, saying nothing and drifting into a cone of concentration. They are autistic 22-year-old identical twins from Long Island whose passion is to run for miles at a time. The twins, who are nonverbal and can exhibit severe behaviors like self-injury and tantrums, have completed more than 120 races, including five marathons and eight half-marathons, over the past seven years. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/sports/DOGmarathon1/DOGmarathon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/sports/DOGmarathon1/DOGmarathon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/sports/DOGmarathon1/DOGmarathon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':