ls or incinerators in 2006-10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electronics Dump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T18:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c7af0cb2-2b7b-5c11-87a4-21f20693d823', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c7af0cb2-2b7b-5c11-87a4-21f20693d823'}, {'abstract': 'The most recent of many financial conflicts in the 83-year history of the Empire State Building seems to be inching toward a resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/business/empire-state-building-has-a-tangled-history.html', 'snippet': 'The most recent of many financial conflicts in the 83-year history of the Empire State Building seems to be inching toward a resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Empire State Building stands as an enduring symbol of New York City — and of the mayhem and legal conflict to which New York City real estate titans are prone. The most recent conflict, however, seems to be inching toward a resolution.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/business/05-EMPIRE/05-EMPIRE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 207, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/business/05-EMPIRE/05-EMPIRE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1814, 'width': 366, 'subType': 'superJumb