nd a way to win despite his lack of experience on a wet track, trudging to victory Saturday at Churchill Downs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/sports/orb-wins-the-kentucky-derby.html', 'snippet': 'Orb, ridden by Joel Rosario, found a way to win despite his lack of experience on a wet track, trudging to victory Saturday at Churchill Downs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — The revelers were sloppy, the grounds were sloppy and the racetrack was sloppy, but Orb apparently did not mind much, and afterward his owners and trainer could not have been happier with the way the day played out.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orb Finds Joy in Mudville', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Orb Finds Joy in Mudville', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoppert, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGaughey, Shug', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phipps, Ogden Mills', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T23:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3721ced8-430d-5667-91f5-0ef0b13ec793', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3721ced8-430d-5667-91f5-0ef0b13ec793'}, {'abstract': 'State Representative Charles Anderson has filed a bill to bar Texas Parks and Wildlife from further reducing the Big Bend herd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/us/texas-sale-of-100-longhorns-stirs-debate-on-breeds-future.html', 'snippet': 'State Representative Charles Anderson has filed a bill to bar Texas Parks and Wildlife from further reducing the Big Bend herd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resilient longhorn, able to survive on sparse foliage and water, has endured in Texas for more than 100 years. But the recent sale of about 100 longhorns by the Texas Parks and Wildlife Department has spurred debate about the breed’s future in the state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTLonghorn/05TTLonghorn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTLonghorn/05TTLonghorn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTLonghorn/05TTLonghorn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTLonghorn/05TTLonghorn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTLonghorn/05TTLonghorn-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'State Sale of 100 Longhorns Stirs Debate, and Proposed Law, on the Breed’s Future', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Sale of 100 Longhorns Stirs Debate, and Proposed Law, on the Breed’s Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cattle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Parks and Wildlife Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-04T23:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cody Permenter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cody', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Permenter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53cdf26c-36fb-5f37-b977-bf85ffa37a18', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53cdf26c-36fb-5f37-b977-bf85ffa37a18'}, {'abstract': 'Legislators are quietly restoring financing for women’s health services. The last lingering battlefield is abortion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/us/texas-lawmakers-set-to-restore-womens-health-financing.html', 'snippet': 'Legislators are quietly restoring financing for women’s health services. The last lingering battlefield is abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The political fireworks and high-octane drama that accompanied lawmakers’ 2011 fight over women’s health care and abortion have been absent this legislative session. They have been replaced with some semblance of concession, as legislators on both sides of the aisle work quietly to restore financing for women’s health services. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTHealth/05TTHealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/us/05TTHealth/05TTHealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60