ge fund manager knew he had a lot of work to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berkshire’s Bear on Tangling With a Master of Question-Dodging', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kass, Douglas A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munger, Charles T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seabreeze Partners Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-05T01:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39480f1d-5d44-503e-8a45-ec95a5837d97', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39480f1d-5d44-503e-8a45-ec95a5837d97'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Karlsson moved into a tie for fourth at the Wells Fargo Championship, two shots behind the co-leaders Phil Mickelson and Nick Watney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/sports/golf/robert-karlsson-in-tie-for-fourth-at-wells-fargo-championship.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Karlsson moved into a tie for fourth at the Wells Fargo Championship, two shots behind the co-leaders Phil Mickelson and Nick Watney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Robert Karlsson’s round of three-under-par 69 Saturday at the Wells Fargo Championship began with a single swing, which is not as simple as it sounds. Karlsson, who moved into a tie for fourth at Quail