ith bright red statements like “Done is better than perfect” and “Move fast and break things.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1219, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/technology/06disrupt-pic/06disrupt-pic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: New Motto for Silicon Valley: First Security, Then Innovation', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Security Needs Take a Back Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-05T15:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d49e81cf-cba3-505f-bf2a-8120811439d9', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d49e81cf-cba3-505f-bf2a-8120811439d9'}, {'abstract': 'Many lawyers have discovered that if you have a legal complaint against the city’s school system, you have to sue the department or, better yet, the Board of Education, which many New Yorkers thought was abolished.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/a-surprise-in-court-a-school-board-thought-to-be-obsolete-still-exists/', 'snippet': 'Many lawyers have discovered that if you have a legal complaint against the city’s school system, you have to sue the department or, better yet, the Board of Education, which many New Yorkers thought was abolished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 9, 2003, Jamie Perez was slashed by two fellow students at Evander Childs High School in the Bronx. He recovered, and his mother, Nancy Torres, sued the City of New York for negligence, claiming lax security. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/03boardofed-cityroom/03boardofed-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 285, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/03/nyregion/03boardofed-cityroom/03boardofed-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 285, 'subType':