: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/us/wrongfully-convicted-find-their-record-haunts-them.html', 'snippet': 'Across much of the country, sealing or clearing a criminal record after a wrongful conviction is a tangled and expensive process, advocates and former prisoners say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Wisconsin, Audrey Edmunds served 11 years in prison in the shaking death of an infant girl for whom she had been baby-sitting. In 2008, a mountain of new medical evidence cast so much doubt on the case that a higher court overturned her conviction and set her free. Leaving prison, Ms. Edmunds hoped that would be the end of it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/us/EXPUNGE-1/EXPUNGE-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrongfully Convicted Often Find Their Record, Unexpunged, Haunts Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrongfully Convicted Often Find Their Record, Unexpunged, Haunts Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-05T22:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/594cbde0-c6c8-5c88-bc98-15a1c78f8988', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/594cbde0-c6c8-5c88-bc98-15a1c78f8988'}, {'abstract': 'The case for austerity is now a complete muddle.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/george-osbornes-fear-of-ghosts/', 'snippet': 'The case for austerity is now a complete muddle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Truly, we live in bizarro world. The stern taskmasters of the IMF are coming to Britain, to demand that the government live it up and spend more; the government, defiantly, will insist on continuing to impose suffering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Osborne’s Fear of Ghosts', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-05T22:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e66c706-9cb0-516f-8a8e-e9a36c0306a9', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e66c706-9cb0-516f-8a8e-e9a36c0306a9'}, {'abstract': 'The Danish philosopher’s revisionist take on an ancient Greek tragedy grappled with the way acts of love, guilt and redemption are intertwined.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/05/kierkegaards-antigone/', 'snippet': 'The Danish philosopher’s revisionist take on an ancient Greek tragedy grappled with the way acts of love, guilt and redemption are intertwined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the most central theme in Soren Kierkegaard’s religious thought is the doctrine of original sin: the idea that we share in some essential human guilt simply by being born. But guilt is an important concept also in Kierkegaard’s secular writings. He thought that the modern era was defined by its concept of guilt. Kierkegaard’s 200th birthday gives us an occasion to assess the modern relevance of his legacy and the viability of his own view of modernity. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kierkegaard’s ‘Antigone’', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kierkegaard, Soren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sophocles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-05T23:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ulrika Carlsson', 'person'