ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa9ea2cc-2c75-551f-b1e8-302814ed4d43', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa9ea2cc-2c75-551f-b1e8-302814ed4d43'}, {'abstract': 'George T. McDonald, a Republican mayoral candidate, said that the city’s laws disadvantaged first-time candidates without a longtime base of supporters or a personal fortune.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/nyregion/judge-upholds-new-yorks-campaign-contribution-limits.html', 'snippet': 'George T. McDonald, a Republican mayoral candidate, said that the city’s laws disadvantaged first-time candidates without a longtime base of supporters or a personal fortune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge on Friday rebuffed an attempt by George T. McDonald, a first-time Republican mayoral candidate, to overturn New York City’s strict limits on campaign contributions, ruling that the city had the right to try to reduce the influence of money in politics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strict Limits on Giving in City Races Are Upheld', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strict Limits On Giving In City Races Are Upheld', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, George T', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T00:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0086bdfd-cdac-5f24-9af7-8fcc8bfb9a66', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0086bdfd-cdac-5f24-9af7-8fcc8bfb9a66'}, {'abstract': '“The Center Holds: Obama and His Enemies,” by Jonathan Alter, includes a chapter on Fox’s influence on the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/business/media/book-looks-behind-the-scenes-at-fox.html', 'snippet': '“The Center Holds: Obama and His Enemies,” by Jonathan Alter, includes a chapter on Fox’s influence on the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days before the presidential election last November, Roger Ailes, the chief executive of Fox News, ordered that Geraldo Rivera’s microphone be cut off after Mr. Rivera angrily defended the Obama administration against charges levied by others on Fox. So says a forthcoming book about the 2012 campaign by Jonathan Alter, a columnist for Bloomberg View and a contributor to MSNBC, a Fox competitor. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Scenes at Fox', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind the Scenes at Fox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alter, Jonathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T00:27:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'mi