). “The Whale,” by Samuel D. Hunter, won for outstanding play and lead actor for Shuler Hensley, who played a morbidly obese man coming to terms with his mistakes and fears. Jessica Pabst also won for her costumes for “The Whale.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Piano Lesson’ and ‘The Whale’ Win Lortel Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Whale’ Wins Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T01:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a648c9fb-300e-54e2-9b25-0111d23b78fd', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a648c9fb-300e-54e2-9b25-0111d23b78fd'}, {'abstract': 'For as much as $20,000, Worldwide Motion Picture Group compares the story structure and genre of a script with those of released movies, looking for clues to box-office success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/business/media/solving-equation-of-a-hit-film-script-with-data.html', 'snippet': 'For as much as $20,000, Worldwide Motion Picture Group compares the story structure and genre of a script with those of released movies, looking for clues to box-office success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Forget zombies. The data crunchers are invading Hollywood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05