of Herzog and De Meuron, the local architecture firm best known for creating the “Bird’s Nest” Stadium for the 2008 Beijing Olympics and converting a London power station into the Tate Modern in 2000; the firm completed its three-year transformation of the vast exhibition space just in time for the show, which concluded last week. The building’s exterior is now clad in a woven skin of undulating, interconnected bands of aluminum, while its interior is more open and easily maneuverable. Many exhibitors got in the spirit, hiring star designers to redesign their booths. Above, six of the best.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baselworld Watch Fair Gets an Extreme Makeover', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aed5d35-6a22-53a6-9892-032497c1602e', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aed5d35-6a22-53a6-9892-032497c1602e'}, {'abstract': "The artist Joshua Abelow creates a drawing inspired by Gabrielle Calvocoressi's poetic encounter with a deer in the twilight.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/t-magazine/a-picture-and-a-poem-gabrielle-calvocoressi-joshua-abelow.html', 'snippet': "The artist Joshua Abelow creates a drawing inspired by Gabrielle Calvocoressi's poetic encounter with a deer in the twilight.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Joshua Abelow creates a drawing inspired by Gabrielle Calvocoressi’s poetic encounter with a deer in the twilight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', '