hether it got better or worse.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/how-colonoscopies-are-like-home-renovations/', 'snippet': 'People don’t evaluate the pain of an experience by summing up the overall total. Instead, they remember the pain at the very end — and whether it got better or worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S a law of nature: Everyone who undertakes major home renovations ends up loathing their contractor. When I was recently redoing my kitchen and bathroom, I finally figured out why. It has nothing to do with the contractor’s honesty, quality of work, punctuality or the mess they make. It’s about behavioral economics and human psychology — in particular, the unusual way that we assess pain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Colonoscopies Are Like Home Renovations', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colonoscopy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahneman, Daniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T04:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15f1fbc7-071f-5be2-8a8f-71e96b67512c', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15f1fbc7-071f-5be2-8a8f-71e96b67512c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Lifetime) DEAR MOM, LOVE CHER In what started as an 86th birthday gift, Cher chronicles the life of her mother, Georgia Holt, (above right, with Cher) from her childhood in rural Arkansas through her eight tumultuous marriages (to six men) as she pursued a career in Hollywood as a singer and actress. Among those interviewed are Cher’s sister, Georganne LaPiere Bartylak, and her children, Chaz Bono and Elijah Blue Allman. Ms. Holt has just released her first album, “Honky Tonk Woman,” featuring tracks she recorded in the 1980s with Elvis Presley’s band as well as a duet with Cher.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T04:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/97b63ba8-44b0-55f4-bded-ef14b86ac2cf', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97b63ba8-44b0-55f4-bded-ef14b86ac2cf'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 6, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/pageoneplus/corrections-may-6-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 6, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 6, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'pri