 abused its dominance in wireless patents by seeking an injunction against Apple in Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Commission on Monday made a preliminary antitrust finding against Google’s mobile communications unit, Motorola Mobility, for seeking and enforcing an injunction against Apple in Germany over patents essential to smartphones and tablets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Rules Against Patent Move by Google’s Motorola Unit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Rules Against Patent Play by Google Unit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanter, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motorola Mobility LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T10:36:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c1b5a4-2423-5496-b27f-63df909c3f82', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c1b5a4-2423-5496-b27f-63df909c3f82'}, {'abstract': 'Given all the recent pre-election violence in Pakistan, any voter who even dares make it to the polls on Saturday will be casting a vote against the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/simply-voting-in-pakistans-election-will-be-an-of-defiance-against-the-taliban/', 'snippet': 'Given all the recent pre-election violence in Pakistan, any voter who even dares make it to the polls on Saturday will be casting a vote against the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARACHI, Pakistan — At the start of last week I was in the nation’s capital, Islamabad, which adjoins the country’s most populous and most powerful province, Punjab. Almost all the political talk there was about Punjab, the home province of former Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif, where he and his Pakistan Muslim League-N\xa0(P.M.L.-N) have been holding rallies, urging supporters to vote them into power. Most analysts believe that is exactly what will happen, even though Sharif won’t have the easy ride that he might once have expected: The cricketer-turned-politician Imran Khan and his Pakistan Tehrik-e-Insaf (P.T.I.) party have strong support in Punjab, and Khan has been traveling the length and breadth of the province to prove the pundits wrong. This is as it should be in a democracy the week before an election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ballot Against the Bullet', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T10:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kamila Shamsie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamila', 'middlename': 