35-53de-8bf8-6eedf71babcf'}, {'abstract': 'A set of six geometry challenges from the Julia Robinson Mathematics Festival. Can you solve them all?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/area-attack/', 'snippet': 'A set of six geometry challenges from the Julia Robinson Mathematics Festival. Can you solve them all?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week we’ll be featuring a set of geometry challenges regularly featured at the Julia Robinson Mathematics Festival, a half-day math event held throughout the year at various locations. The festival is designed for sixth- through 12th-graders who are interested in math, games and puzzles; participants include students who enjoy exploring problems collaboratively as well as math contest competitors looking for a more relaxed setting. (The next festival will be held this Saturday at Stanford University. Check the bottom of this post for details.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-articleLarge.png', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-jumbo.png', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-superJumbo.png', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/crosswords/JRMF-Berkeley-2013/JRMF-Berkeley-2013-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Area Attack!', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d126eacb-5749-5041-9d6d-9a7a51c99497', 'word_count': 1836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d126eacb-5749-5041-9d6d-9a7a51c99497'}, {'abstract': 'Jennifer Meyer’s flapper-inspired jewelry concept emerged from her time on the set of “The Great Gatsby” with husband Tobey Maguire.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/feeling-for-jennifer-meyers-bejeweled-bobby-pins/', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Meyer’s flapper-inspired jewelry concept emerged from her time on the set of “The Great Gatsby” with husband Tobey Maguire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles jewelry designer Jennifer Meyer makes her first foray into hair accessories next month with an elegant trio of flapper-inspired, 18-karat gold bobby pins adorned with diamonds, rubies and turquoise. “I had just spent six months in Australia on ‘The Great Gatsby’ set immersed in the most beautiful Tiffany jewelry imaginable,” says the Malibu-reared mother of two, whose husband, Tobey Maguire, stars in the forthcoming Baz Luhrmann film that has already inspired a Jazz Age revival in fashion. “The arrow shape was often featured in that period, and I wanted to bring it back with a contemporary spin,” says the 2013 CFDA Fashion Award nominee, adding that she plans to roll out new styles in the coming months. “I’ve always loved hair jewelry but haven’t challenged myself until now.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Jennifer Meyer’s Bejeweled Bobby Pins', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T16:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Cagney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cagney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e9893f-4bb5-5ec3-941b-1717c380a097', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e9893f-4bb5-5ec3-941b-1717c380a097'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you are living in Pakistan or abroad, join a discussion of what the most important issues are in the country’s general election this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/what-pakistans-election-means-to-its-people/', 'snippet': 'Whether you are living in Pakistan or abroad, join a discussion of what the most important issues are in the country’s general election this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times is interested in hearing from Pakistanis as the general election campaign comes to an end this week, promising the first democratic transfer of power from one civilian government to another in the country’s history. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/middleeast/pakistanelection2/pakistanelection2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 's