ry run of Harold Pinter’s “No Man’s Land” and Samuel Beckett’s “Waiting for Godot” this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/two-actors-to-join-pinter-and-beckett-repertory-run-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Billy Crudup and Shuler Hensley will join Ian McKellen and Patrick Stewart for the repertory run of Harold Pinter’s “No Man’s Land” and Samuel Beckett’s “Waiting for Godot” this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Billy Crudup (“The Coast of Utopia”) and Shuler Hensley (“The Whale”) have been added to the cast for the two-play repertory of Harold Pinter’s “No Man’s Land” and Samuel Beckett’s “Waiting for Godot” coming to Broadway this fall, the producers said Monday. Mr. Crudup will play Foster in “No Man’s Land” and Lucky in “Waiting for Godot,” while Mr. Hensley will take on Briggs in “No Man’s Land” and Pozzo in “Godot.” They will join the previously announced cast members Ian McKellen and Patrick Stewart for a 14-week run at the Cort Theater that is scheduled to begin with previews on Oct. 26 and an opening night set for Nov. 24. Both works will be directed by Sean Mathias. The specific schedule and performance dates for each play have not been announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Actors Join Repertory Pairing of Pinter and Beckett on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crudup, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hensley, Shuler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T16:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49075398-c442-5839-9ba7-7c916eef1a9b', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49075398-c442-5839-9ba7-7c916eef1a9b'}, {'abstract': 'Because Orb wowed Saturday, many of those who raced with him in the Derby will likely pass on the Preakness Stakes. As of now, only five other Derby starters are considering the Preakness.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/taking-stock-of-the-emerging-preakness-field/', 'snippet': 'Because Orb wowed Saturday, many of those who raced with him in the Derby will likely pass on the Preakness Stakes. As of now, only five other Derby starters are considering the Preakness.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:21 p.m. | Update The Derby contenders Vyjack and Normandy Invasion are also being considered for the Preakness. Fear the Kitten is no longer in the mix.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Stock of the Emerging Preakness Field', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napravnik, Rosie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T16:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b005be1-ba98-57d9-b679-fb082850cc25', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b005be1-ba98-57d9-b679-fb082850cc25'},