16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg and Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41581b21-f6fe-5d26-921e-52beadcfa429', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41581b21-f6fe-5d26-921e-52beadcfa429'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s “red line” statement on chemical weapons was unscripted.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/governing-by-random-comment/', 'snippet': 'The president’s “red line” statement on chemical weapons was unscripted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator John McCain was at it again on Sunday, attacking President Obama for not taking military action in Syria, especially after Israel struck Syrian missile sites. “We need to have a game changing action,” Mr. McCain said on Fox News. “And that is no American boots on the ground, establish a safe zone, and to\xa0protect\xa0it and to supply weapons to the right people in Syria who are fighting for obviously, the things we believe in.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government by Random Comment', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T17:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48fb6d25-6f46-5508-9ca9-303e11e35011', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48fb6d25-6f46-5508-9ca9-303e11e35011'}, {'abstract': 'Despite political action committees and awareness campaigns, half of Bangalore’s eligible voters didn’t go to the polls this election.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/why-angalores-young-educated-and-wealthy-dont-vote/', 'snippet': 'Despite political action committees and awareness campaigns, half of Bangalore’s eligible voters didn’t go to the polls this election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGALORE– On an unusually warm Sunday, a large number of young, first-time Bangalore voters stood in line at voting booths around the city. Later they laughed as they showed off their ink-marked fingers, proof that they did their civic duty, for cellphone camera pictures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young, Urban, Educated…and Choosing Not to Vote', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karnataka (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T17:36:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saritha Rai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e394b70-2f1a-51d2-8760-a94fae656c99', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e394b70-2f1a-51d2-8760-a94fae656c99'}, {'abstract': 'Rangers Coach John Tortorella insisted his team has been playing well against Washington, but it won’t matter unless they can win Game 3 and get back in the series.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/the-rangers-are-close-but-does-it-matter/', 'snippet': 'Rangers Coach John Tortorella insisted his team has been playing well against Washington, but it won’t matter unless they can win Game 3 and get back in the series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Tortorella addressed a philosophical quandary Monday morning before Game 3 of the Rangers-Capitals playoff series: should a coach judge his team on how it played, or on the result? He weighed that perplexity in light of two narrow losses that have left the Rangers desperately needing a win Monday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rangers Are Close, but Does it Matter?', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T17:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a322867-ce2e-573b-a56b-5c73846107fb', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a322867-ce2e-573b-a56b-5c73846107fb'}, {'abstract': 'Finlandia adopts a broad, tongue-in-cheek approach to selling cheese in a new campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/business/ads-proclaim-hail-finlandia.html', 'snippet': 'Finlandia adopts a broad, tongue-in-cheek approach to selling cheese in a new campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A common approach in advertising is called “product as hero,” which celebrates the sponsor’s soup, soap or soda as the be-all, end-all, cure-all and whatever-all-else. But in an era when skeptical consumers dismiss straightforward chest-thumping as hopelessly outdated, what’s a marketer to do?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 911}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1349, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/business/06ad-news1-SF/06ad-news1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ads Proclaim, ‘Hail, Finlandia’', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ads Proclaim, &#8216;Hail, Finlandia&#8217;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T17:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34310c04-0e94-5556-a27c-1aa061cfd069', 'word_count': 1558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34310c04-0e94-5556-a27c-1aa061cfd069'}, {'abstract': 'At the Frederick Law Olmsted awards luncheon of the Women’s Committee of the Central Park Conservancy, a favorite hat shape was the satellite dish, defying gravity on the side of the head.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/video-bill-cunningham-on-the-street-hats-off/', 'snippet': 'At the Frederick Law Olmsted awards luncheon of the Women’s Committee of the Central Park Conservancy, a favorite hat shape was the satellite dish, defying gravity on the side of the head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louisville has its Kentucky Derby. England has its Royal Ascot. And New York has its Frederick Law Olmsted awards luncheon of the Women’s Committee of the Central Park Conservancy. The luncheon drew more than 1,200 elaborately hatted guests, and all of the garden flowers were in tiptop bloom. A favorite hat shape was the satellite dish, defying gravity on the side of the head — a look that in the late ’30s was called the profile brim. The most amusing headdress was one of veiling that covered the face and had an appliquéd eye and lips, evoking a Dadaist mood. The most interesting fashion silhouettes were the revival of Dior’s New Look of 1947 and the Chanel nipped waists, full skirts and flyaway boleros.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Bill Cunningham On the Street, Hats Off', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Park Conservancy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T17:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf59c04-6cce-5c55-81ff-cb01b3922417', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf59c04-6cce-5c55-81ff-cb01b3922417'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from Leopold Blaschka’s description in 1853 of his first encounter with bioluminescent sea creatures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/science/inspiration-for-art-in-the-glowing-seas.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from Leopold Blaschka’s description in 1853 of his first encounter with bioluminescent sea creatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an 1853 letter, the glass sculptor Leopold Blaschka described the first time he was mesmerized by what is known today as bioluminescence. The letter was translated from Old German by Henri Reiling, a scholar at Utrecht University in the Netherlands:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/science/07glass-2/07glass-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inspiration for Art in the Glowing Seas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Glimpses of ‘a Realm of Fairies’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 