 standards, N.H.T.S.A. is asking for public comment to guide its development of new rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an effort to improve its New Car Assessment Program, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is seeking comments from the public on several areas of vehicle safety, including new rules to protect pedestrians and children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.T.S.A. Solicits Public Comment on Vehicle Safety Evaluations', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T18:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/594081f8-6c13-5d0c-aa99-df5b52b03c06', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/594081f8-6c13-5d0c-aa99-df5b52b03c06'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/walkabout-56-sungnyemun-gate-reopens-in-seoul-stockholm-welcomes-back-abba/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Restoration Celebration The 600-year-old Sungnyemun Gate in Seoul, which was destroyed in an arson attack in 2008, reopened this weekend\xa0with great fanfare, including a visit from President Park Geun-hye of South Korea. (Gadling)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout – 5/6: Sungnyemun Gate Reopens in Seoul; Stockholm Welcomes Back ABBA', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T18:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d84d9570-4fe3-5006-9dcd-f8485a7c4006', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d84d9570-4fe3-5006-9dcd-f8485a7c4006'}, {'abstract': 'SAC Capital is one of several firms that are seeking to insert provisions in employment contracts allowing them to recover compensation from employees who violate the law.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/on-wall-street-recovering-money-from-rogue-employees/', 'snippet': 'SAC Capital is one of several firms that are seeking to insert provisions in employment contracts allowing them to recover compensation from employees who violate the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems it should be a fairly intuitive policy: employees who violate the law should not be entitled to keep big bonuses earned based on illegal behavior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Wall Street, Recovering Money From Rogue Employees', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations and Restitution', 'rank': 4