2424f0'}, {'abstract': "The complaint alleges that the agent “engaged in a scheme to dupe’' the author into assigning the copyright to his company.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/business/media/harper-lee-sues-agent-over-copyright-on-mockingbird.html', 'snippet': "The complaint alleges that the agent “engaged in a scheme to dupe’' the author into assigning the copyright to his company.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Harper Lee, who skillfully chronicled courtroom drama in “To Kill a Mockingbird,” is tangled in a legal drama of her own. Ms. Lee, 87, filed a lawsuit last week accusing her literary agent, Samuel Pinkus, of improperly collecting royalties from “Mockingbird” since 2007. According to the complaint, filed in federal court in New York, Mr. Pinkus “engaged in a scheme to dupe Harper Lee, then 80 years old with declining hearing and eyesight,” into assigning the book’s copyright to his company. Ms. Lee does not recall signing the document or discussing it with Mr. Pinkus, the complaint said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harper Lee Sues Agent Over Copyright on ‘Mockingbird’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Mockingbird’ Author Sues Agent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Harper', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'To Kill a Mockingbird (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T18:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f24f61e2-9433-5e64-87ad-662e48c071ba', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f24f61e2-9433-5e64-87ad-662e48c071ba'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/dining-calendar-16/', 'snippet': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wandering Cheese Truck', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dining Calendar', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T18:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49207d30-4097-56af-aade-77269faed61a', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49207d30-4097-56af-aade-77269faed61a'}, {'abstract': 'In 26 meticulous pen drawings on view at the Paris boutique, the Irish artist tells the story of a young boy who is afraid of the dark.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/on-view-nigel-peake/', 'snippet': 'In 26 meticulous pen drawings on view at the Paris boutique, the Irish artist tells the story of a young boy who is afraid of the dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nigel Peake’s rural Irish roots were the muse for his 2011 book of drawings, “In the Wilds.” This year, the artist moved to Lausanne, the Swiss city on the shores of Lake Geneva, to teach architecture. The new setting influenced a series of 26 pen drawings that will be on view for a month starting today at the Paris boutique Colette. Peake’s “story of drawings,” as he calls it, tells the tale of a young boy who is afraid of the dark and takes solace in building boats. As with his other work, there is no visible human presence—the boy is only implied through images that hint at a larger narrative. For those who can’t make it to Paris to see the originals, Peake has self-published a limited-edition compilation of the images, called “In the Dark.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illustrator Nigel Peake Brings His Mysterious World to Colette', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View: A Sea of Ink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T19:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d6796f3-8da6-5649-908e-176fff655c17', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d6796f3-8da6-5649-908e-176fff655c17'}, {'abstract': 'Americans, mostly black, who live near large-scale farms say they are illegally discouraged from applying for work and treated badly by employers who prefer foreigners’ malleability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/us/suit-cites-race-bias-in-farms-use-of-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'Americans, mostly black, who live near large-scale farms say they are illegally discouraged from applying for work and treated badly by employers who prefer foreigners’ malleability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIDALIA, Ga. — For years, labor unions and immigrant rights activists have accused large-scale farmers, like those harvesting sweet Vidalia onions here this month, of exploiting Mexican guest workers. Working for hours on end under a punishing sun, the pickers are said to be crowded into squalid camps, driven without a break and even cheated of wages.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Workers Claim Race Bias as Farms Rely on Immigrants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Workers Sue As Big Farms Rely On Immigrants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronner, Ethan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant Labor (Agriculture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanley Farms (Vidalia, Ga)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T19:02:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c5f2181-0395-5c8f-af67-c696fd9741dd', 'word_count': 1414, 'uri': 'nyt: