life populations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/science/drones-offer-a-safer-clearer-look-at-the-natural-world.html', 'snippet': 'Technology developed for warfare finds surprising civilian applications, including surveys of wildlife populations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monte Vista National Wildlife Refuge, Colo. — An electric whir filled the air of this high desert valley as Jeff Sloan, a cartographer for the United States Geological Survey, hurled a small remote-controlled airplane into the sky. The plane, a four-and-a-half-pound AeroVironment Raven, dipped; then its plastic propeller whined and pulled it into the sky.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Drone’s-Eye View of Nature', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Drone’s-Eye View of Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farrell, Sean Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AeroVironment Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T19:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'Patrick', 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6839560b-0080-5a60-b646-df4cc8e48690', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6839560b-0080-5a60-b646-df4cc8e48690'}, {'abstract': 'In this first novel by Helene Wecker, set in immigrant-thronged New York in 1899, two mythical creatures, a golem and a jinni, arrive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/books/the-golem-and-the-jinni-a-novel-by-helene-wecker.html', 'snippet': 'In this first novel by Helene Wecker, set in immigrant-thronged New York in 1899, two mythical creatures, a golem and a jinni, arrive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title characters of Helene Wecker’s inventive novel, “The Golem and the Jinni,” are only slightly more bewildered than the thousands of other immigrants who end up in the teeming tenements of New York in 1899. Despite a handful of unusual powers, these two mythic creatures are still strangers in a strange land, caught between the folk traditions from which they spring and the modern world. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/arts/07BOOK/07BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/arts/07BOOK/07BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/arts/07BOOK/07BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/arts/07BOOK/07BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/arts/07BOOK/07BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub