: 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/d83097b5-3e28-5cdd-9b1e-f3955bea287e'}, {'abstract': 'A conversation with RuPaul Charles, the host of “RuPaul’s Drag Race,” on his show and the pendulum of social acceptance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/another-side-of-rupaul/', 'snippet': 'A conversation with RuPaul Charles, the host of “RuPaul’s Drag Race,” on his show and the pendulum of social acceptance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — “Have you ever worn a wig or done drag?” RuPaul Charles, the host of “RuPaul’s Drag Race,” asked me recently as he shopped for wigs on Hollywood Boulevard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Side of RuPaul', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charles, RuPaul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T20:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Mabry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mabry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb140e3c-08a8-51b9-ab06-8ca2c9582f39', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb140e3c-08a8-51b9-ab06-8ca2c9582f39'}, {'abstract': 'The horrible Battle of Chancellorsville also saw countless stories of mercy by each side.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/kindness-amid-the-slaughter/', 'snippet': 'The horrible Battle of Chancellorsville also saw countless stories of mercy by each side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the afternoon of May 2, 1863, Cpl. Rice Bull looked out over the position that his newly formed regiment, the 123rd New York Infantry, was assigned to defend, just south of the Chancellorsville crossroads. He and his fellow upstaters had not yet “seen the elephant” – the soldiers’ expression for experiencing combat – and he was reassured to see that they were supported by more veteran units, including the Second Massachusetts and the 27th Indiana. He noted the striking contrast between those units’ faded, bullet-ridden battle flags and the crisp, spotless condition of his regiment’s colors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kindness Amid the Slaughter', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-06T20:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Leonard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56d1c23-5633-5ac8-8e6d-16bcf49d7c91', 'word_count': 1985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56d1c23-5633-5ac8-8e6d-16bcf49d7c91'}, {'abstract': 'One of the original reality shows of TV, “Cops” will be shown in the same Saturday night time slot on Spike, which sees the program as perfect for its audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/business/media/cops-is-moving-to-spike-tv.html', 'snippet': 'One of the original reality shows of TV, “Cops” will be shown in the same Saturday night time slot on Spike, which sees the program as perfect for its audience.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Cops,” one of the original reality shows on television, is moving to cable after 24 years on network television.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3