', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e66b33-70c4-5f8c-9a28-35b33bf17f57', 'word_count': 1534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e66b33-70c4-5f8c-9a28-35b33bf17f57'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a history of strained relations, the United States and Russia have been working effectively to investigate the marathon bombings, American officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/us/politics/us-says-russia-is-aiding-inquiry-into-boston-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a history of strained relations, the United States and Russia have been working effectively to investigate the marathon bombings, American officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Despite years of differences on how to approach the terrorist threat, Obama administration officials said Monday that the American authorities investigating the Boston Marathon bombings were working effectively with their Russian counterparts and that they hoped the experience would usher in a new era of cooperation on counterterrorism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Hopes Russian Aid in Inquiry on Boston Bombings Signals Future Collaboration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Hopes Russian Aid in Inquiry on Boston Bombings Signals Future Collaboration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'ran