': 'In Manhattan Real Estate, Wealth and Power Are Relative', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Manhattan Real Estate, Wealth and Power Are Relatives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Extell Development Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derricks and Cranes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T00:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fe44b49-ffb9-5a0e-a03c-0897778c9207', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fe44b49-ffb9-5a0e-a03c-0897778c9207'}, {'abstract': 'Biographies do not commonly lurk in stuffy academic journals, but there was mine, in the latest issue of Basic and Applied Social Psychology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/opinion/the-best-little-boy-in-the-world-thats-me.html', 'snippet': 'Biographies do not commonly lurk in stuffy academic journals, but there was mine, in the latest issue of Basic and Applied Social Psychology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/o