lue': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pachankis, John E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatzenbuehler, Mark L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam D. Chandler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/042b97c3-2617-574f-947e-43f41ab9228a', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042b97c3-2617-574f-947e-43f41ab9228a'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Monday proposed new regulations for tanning beds that would require their makers to affix labels warning young people not to use them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/us/new-rules-proposed-for-tanning-beds.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Monday proposed new regulations for tanning beds that would require their makers to affix labels warning young people not to use them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Monday proposed new regulations for tanning beds that would require their makers to affix labels warning young people not to use them. Nearly 28 million Americans use tanning beds every year, according to the American Academy of Dermatology. The agency said the proposal was its first step toward potentially restricting access to the beds altogether for minors. Manufacturers would have to apply to the F.D.A. to get approval for their tanning bed products before selling them,\xa0“The science is clear,” said Dr. Mary Maloney, vice president of regulator policy at American Academy of Dermatology. “The risk of developing melanoma increases by 75 percent for individuals who’ve been exposed to ultraviolet radiation from indoor tanning.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rules Proposed for Tanning Beds', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rules Proposed For Tanning Beds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suntan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Melanomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF DERMATOLOGY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/85fecd64-dead-5766-8d46-6c2e370266ff', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85fecd64-dead-5766-8d46-6c2e370266ff'}, {'abstract': 'The California Supreme Court on Monday upheld the right of local governments to ban medical marijuana dispensaries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/us/california-court-upholds-ban-on-marijuana-dispensaries.html', 'snippet': 'The California Supreme Court on Monday upheld the right of local governments to ban medical marijuana dispensaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The California Supreme Court on Monday upheld the right of local governments to ban medical marijuana dispensaries. As dispensaries have proliferated since 1996, when California became the first state to allow medical marijuana, many municipalities across the state have used zoning laws to prohibits dispensaries from opening inside city limits. Patients and dispensary owners have argued that these local laws violate the state medical marijuana statutes by reducing patients’ access to the drug. But the court unanimously upheld a ban in the City of Riverside, paving the way for more municipalities to prohibit marijuana dispensaries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Court Upholds Ban on Marijuana Dispensaries', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Court Upholds Ban On Marijuana Dispensaries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e64c59-cd78-5949-8b64-c821a13e17bb', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e64c59-cd78-5949-8b64-c821a13e17bb'}, {'abstract': 'A filmmaker searches for a mysterious vandal who has been correcting grammar on placards in the sculpture garden of the Pratt Institute in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000002210649/vigilante-copy-editor.html', 'snippet': 'A filmmaker searches for a mysterious vandal who has been correcting g