ring to exploit every problem and complaint that arises as it is carried out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/us/politics/gop-is-readying-a-new-offensive-over-health-law.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans are trying to turn President Obama’s health care law into an election weapon and are preparing to exploit every problem and complaint that arises as it is carried out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As the administration struggles to put in place the final, complex piece of President Obama’s signature health care law, an endeavor on a scale not seen since Medicare’s creation nearly a half-century ago, Democrats are worried that major snags will be exploited by Republicans in next year’s midterm elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Midterms Loom, Democrats Worry About Health Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Worries For Democrats On Health Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a25e10d-cad3-5e1e-9c27-cdd2ef934def', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a25e10d-cad3-5e1e-9c27-cdd2ef934def'}, {'abstract': 'A sharp fall in the price of emissions in Europe has highlighted the need for reforms to an important program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/opinion/europes-carbon-trading-system.html', 'snippet': 'A sharp fall in the price of emissions in Europe has highlighted the need for reforms to an important program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Union became a pioneer in tackling climate change by starting the first major cap-and-trade system designed to reduce carbon-dioxide emissions by putting a price on them. But analysts are increasingly worried that technical mistakes, Europe’s prolonged recession and the failure of policy makers to strengthen the system is undermining its effectiveness.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Carbon Trading System Worth Saving', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Carbon Trading System Worth Saving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:16:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd3f1936-5715-5eed-9f97-b1cd9316a9ea', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd3f1936-5715-5eed-9f97-b1cd9316a9ea'}, {'abstract': 'The attack along the border with Afghanistan was the deadliest so far in the campaign for next Saturday’s national election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/world/asia/taliban-bomb-kills-at-least-20-at-a-pakistan-political-rally.html', 'snippet': 'The attack along the border with Afghanistan was the deadliest so far in the campaign for next Saturday’s national election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — A Taliban bomb ripped through a crowded political rally in Pakistan’s tribal belt on Monday, killing at least 20 people and wounding 45 in the deadliest attack so far of the campaign for next Saturday’s national election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Bomb Kills at Least 20 at a Pakistan Political Rally', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Bomb Kills at Least 20 At a Pakistan Political Rally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Ismail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:16:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh and Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9791c61-0ebf-5f1d-9416-81a9685fbfc8', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9791c61-0ebf-5f1d-9416-81a9685fbfc8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s nomination of Representative Melvin Watt to oversee the mortgage companies is a solid choice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/opinion/melvin-watt-fannie-mae-and-freddie-mac.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s nomination of Representative Melvin Watt to oversee the mortgage companies is a solid choice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many reasons to be bullish on housing. Valuations, affordability and supply and demand are moving in the right direction. But there are also causes for concern. Home sales and home prices can rise only so far given today’s high level of unemployment and low level of wage gains. And millions of homeowners are still in financial distress. At the end of 2012, some 11.3 million homeowners — nearly one-fourth of all those with a mortgage — still owed more on their mortgages than their homes were worth, according to Moody’s Analytics. Of those, three million are currently in or near foreclosure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Watt, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Watt, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watt, Melvin L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Finance Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:16:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed2529c-e15e-5edb-bd37-129da267cff9', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed2529c-e15e-5edb-bd37-129da267cff9'}, {'abstract': 'The indictment of yet another politician by federal investigators is one way to clean up New York’s rancid state government. Public financing of campaigns is another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/opinion/corruption-in-albany.html', 'snippet': 'The indictment of yet another politician by federal investigators is one way to clean up New York’s rancid state government. Public financing of campaigns is another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the talk among Gov. Andrew Cuomo and other leaders about cleaning up New York’s rancid state government, it is the F.B.I. that is doing the cleaning — indictment by indictment. State Senator John Sampson is the latest Albany politician to face corruption charges. On Monday, he was taken into custody by federal agents on charges of embezzling about $440,000 from the sale of foreclosed properties, obstruction of justice and witness tampering.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corruption in Albany', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corruption in Albany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sampson, John L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T01:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64c60aa-3368-5950-be3b-f5b6fa4930f0', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64c60aa-3368-5950-be3b-f5b6fa4930f0'}, {'abstract': 'Danny Bowien, who owns Mission Chinese Food in New York and San Francisco, won the rising star chef of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/several-in-new-york-take-top-beard-awards/', 'snippet': 'Danny Bowien, who owns Mission Chinese Food in New York and San Francisco, won the rising star chef of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Danny Bowien, who owns Mission Chinese Food in New York and San Francisco, was named the Rising Star Chef for 2013 at the annual James Beard Foundation awards ceremony Monday night. It’s one of the most significant of the many awards and medals handed out by the foundation for achievement in the world of restaurants and their chefs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Several in New York Take Top Beard Awards', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': N