rticle', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdcc64cb-6bc7-5de5-9416-c32f2ccf2b5c', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdcc64cb-6bc7-5de5-9416-c32f2ccf2b5c'}, {'abstract': 'Nate Robinson scored 27 points, including the game’s final 7 points, as injury-ravaged Chicago withstood LeBron James and defending champion Miami in their opener.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/sports/basketball/heat-may-have-mvp-in-lebron-james-but-bulls-have-series-lead.html', 'snippet': 'Nate Robinson scored 27 points, including the game’s final 7 points, as injury-ravaged Chicago withstood LeBron James and defending champion Miami in their opener.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — When Nate Robinson chased after a loose ball in the second quarter of Monday’s second-round playoff game, he quickly discovered that he had company in the form of the 6-foot-8, 250-pound LeBron James. At 5-8, Robinson paid the price. He retreated to the locker room to receive 10 stitches on his upper lip, and the Bulls pressed on without him.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heat May Have M.V.P., but Bulls Have Series Lead', 'kicker': 'Bulls 93, Heat 86', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robinson (27 Points, 10 Stitches) Lifts Bulls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Nate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T02:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/650342a9-d5a5-5bfc-9936-ce18fe23fb2e', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/650342a9-d5a5-5bfc-9936-ce18fe23fb2e'}, {'abstract': 'According to the report, most teachers in the nation’s largest school districts took pay cuts or had their pay frozen at least one year between 2008 and 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/education/teacher-pay-hurt-by-recession-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'According to the report, most teachers in the nation’s largest school districts took pay cuts or had their pay frozen at least one year between 2008 and 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the recession and its aftermath, public schools took a hit as both state coffers and local property taxes shriveled. That showed up in shrinking employment, but also in teacher salaries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teacher Pay Hurt by Recession, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teacher Pay Hurt by Recession, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Council on Teacher Quality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Center for Education Statistics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T03:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d530046-0506-5d41-bd59-758eb570b93e', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d530046-0506-5d41-bd59-758eb570b93e'}, {'abstract': 'An official fund created after the bombings has raised $28 million, but that will not be enough to cover the daunting medical costs for all the victims, so many are looking elsewhere to close the gap.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/06/victims-in-boston-marathon-bombings-turn-to-crowdfunding-for-support/', 'snippet': 'An official fund created after the bombings has raised $28 million, but that will not be enough to cover the daunting medical costs for all the victims, so many are looking elsewhere to close the gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was Brittany Loring’s 29th birthday. She and a fellow graduate student at Boston College, Liza Cherney, were making their way to the finish line of the Boston Marathon to meet a runner when the two bombs exploded. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victims in Boston Marathon Bombings Turn to Crowdfunding for Support', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'One Fund Boston', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T03:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ede2464a-f789-5571-a747-d72e11ccd0fc', 'word_count': 1555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ede2464a-f789-5571-a747-d72e11ccd0fc'}, {'abstract': 'Knicks fans haven’t forgotten Game 1 of the Knicks-Pacers playoff series in 1995 when Reggie Miller scored 8 points in 18.7 seconds for the Pacers. Miller returns to the Garden as a TV analyst for Game 2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/sports/basketball/knicks-fans-remember-reggie-millers-8-points-for-pacers-in-1995.html', 'snippet': 'Knicks fans haven’t forgotten Game 1 of the Knicks-Pacers playoff series in 1995 when Reggie Miller scored 8 points in 18.7 seconds for the Pacers. Miller returns to the Garden as a TV analyst for Game 2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reggie Miller still hears about the game whenever he comes to New York. Fans recognize him and want to talk about that Game 1 of the Knicks-Pacers playoff series in 1995, the one that became Page 1 of his New York legend. They all want to know how he scored 8 points in 18.7 seconds, flipping a 6-point Knicks lead into a preposterous Pacers victory.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/REGGIE/REGGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/REGGIE/REGGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 882}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/REGGIE/REGGIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/sports/REGGIE/REGGIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo