ami” made the vote closer than usual.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/some-silent-protest-in-malaysian-malls-after-disputed-election/', 'snippet': 'Some Malaysians took to the mall to protest silently against a Sunday electoral win by the ruling government coalition, now in power for 56 years; others denounced a charge that a “Chinese tsunami” made the vote closer than usual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — After the Malaysian opposition parties failed to win in Sunday’s election, some Malaysians staged “silent protests” in the country’s malls, dressed in black with their mouths taped shut, according to photographs posted online and #TheSilentWalk, a Twitter feed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 901, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 901, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/07/world/asia/07MalaysiaRDV2/07MalaysiaRDV2-thumbS