y,” in which he co-stars with his former girlfriend Deepika Padukone. Directed by Ayan Mukherjee, the movie follows the lives of four young college graduates and the evolution of their relationships over nearly a decade. Bunny (Ranbir Kapoor) and Naina (Deepika Padukone) meet at two separate points in their lives in the film, first when they are just out of college and then as 30-year-olds, holding on to certain unfulfilled dreams. (Spoiler alert: Somewhere along the line, they also fall in love.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 917}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/06/world/asia/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk/06-ranbir-kapoor-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r