itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a98259c-fdf9-5ae7-9e31-8e231d646091', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a98259c-fdf9-5ae7-9e31-8e231d646091'}, {'abstract': 'The iPad and iPad Mini have a switch on the side that can be used to either mute the tablet or prevent the screen from rotating, but you need to pick the function you want to use in the system settings.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/qa-setting-the-ipads-side-switch/', 'snippet': 'The iPad and iPad Mini have a switch on the side that can be used to either mute the tablet or prevent the screen from rotating, but you need to pick the function you want to use in the system settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q.& A.: Setting the iPad’s Side Switch', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping iPad Mini\r\nOn the Horizontal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T10:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c164523-e730-571e-ab83-a724535df1f2', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c164523-e730-571e-ab83-a724535df1f2'}, {'abstract': 'It’s important to understand the difference between Human Resources Happy and High Performance Happy.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/where-the-happy-talk-about-corporate-culture-is-wrong/', 'snippet': 'It’s important to understand the difference between Human Resources Happy and High Performance Happy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Tell me something I don’t know,” is what I think every time I see another article, blog post or book on the value of happy employees. And here is what I find disturbing about these happy-employee propagandists. They are mostly off about what it takes to motivate employees and keep them happy in a fast-growth culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Happy Talk About Corporate Culture Is Wrong', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T11:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7179c621-c758-5397-a680-1fc6ef299a58', 'word_count': 1675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7179c621-c758-5397-a680-1fc6ef299a58'}, {'abstract': 'Forecasting, not modeling.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/keyness-not-so-big-mistake/', 'snippet': 'Forecasting, not modeling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett, unusually, gets one wrong, although not in too bad a way. In his post Keynes’s Biggest Mistake, he misconstrues what Keynes meant by calling his book the “General Theory” of employment etc., and seems to imply something untrue about Keynes’s views on the liquidity trap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keynes’s Not So Big Mistake', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T11:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bf155d2-c8d4-584d-9640-6ab5918b5a28', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bf155d2-c8d4-584d-9640-6ab5918b5a28'}, {'abstract': 'Not all political, still.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/the-stimulus-debate-revisited/', 'snippet': 'Not all political, still.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong finds Clive Crook making some easily refuted claims about the nature of the stimulus debate in the winter of 2008-2009, and my role in particular. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stimulus Debate, Revisited', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T11:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f869f2d2-8ee0-5981-a9a2-328c1314c4f7', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f869f2d2-8ee0-5981-a9a2-328c1314c4f7'}, {'abstract': 'At the latest protest rally in Moscow, the mood was anything but uplifting.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/gloom-at-a-moscow-protest/', 'snippet': 'At the latest protest rally in Moscow, the mood was anything but uplifting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Under a menacing gray sky, people walked across the Great Stone Bridge, which spans the Moscow River at one end of the Kremlin. Dressed mostly in dark clothing, they walked purposefully, with somber faces, almost as in a funeral procession.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Standoff on Bolotnaya Square', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T11:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aae8b7a4-28b9-5798-af0a-f71fff18746e', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae8b7a4-28b9-5798-af0a-f71fff18746e'}, {'abstract': '“Little Red Riding Hood,” a maze of fairy tale stories and a music-making app may all provide delight for the younger people in your household.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/three-noteworthy-apps-for-children/', 'snippet': '“Little Red Riding Hood,” a maze of fairy tale stories and a music-making app may all provide delight for the younger people in your household.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are