nce-alan-cumming-of-macbeth/', 'snippet': 'The actor plays Lady Macbeth in a scene from this new version of Shakespeare’s tragedy on Broadway at the Ethel Barrymore Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Cumming is on Broadway playing the title role — and every other major one — in “Macbeth,” a reimagined version of Shakespeare’s tragedy set in a mental institution. In this scene Mr. Cumming plays the ruthless Lady Macbeth asking the spirits to “unsex me here.” Directed by John Tiffany and Andrew Goldberg, “Macbeth” continues through June 30 at the Ethel Barrymore Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Alan Cumming of ‘Macbeth’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barrymore, Ethel, Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T12:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0c26e02-8b87-5728-ac6d-90376d505f72', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0c26e02-8b87-5728-ac6d-90376d505f72'}, {'abstract': 'The United States has pressed China to rein in the North’s nuclear program, and the decision appeared to be its strongest move yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/world/asia/china-cuts-ties-with-north-korean-bank.html', 'snippet': 'The United States has pressed China to rein in the North’s nuclear program, and the decision appeared to be its strongest move yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The state-controlled Bank of China said on Tuesday that it had ended all dealings with a key North Korean bank in what appeared to be the strongest public Chinese response yet to North Korea’s willingness to brush aside warnings from Beijing and push ahead with its nuclear and ballistic missile programs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Cuts Ties With Key North Korean Bank', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Cuts Ties With Key North Korean Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T12:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher and Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78a8abfc-cc2d-5f3e-8ca1-d73b906952d0', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78a8abfc-cc2d-5f3e-8ca1-d73b906952d0'}, {'abstract': 'Also, two big banks face suits on mortgage pact abuses, Pfizer begins selling Viagra online and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/tuesday-reading-a-new-