rborne lap of plush-leather luxury, hopscotched around the country over the past few days, breezing into Chicago; Orlando, Fla.; and Little Rock, Ark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayoral Candidate Says Clintons Have Used His Private Jet', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T13:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5e5b610-27b6-5e8f-81b1-5720ee546862', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5e5b610-27b6-5e8f-81b1-5720ee546862'}, {'abstract': 'The success of Mauritania’s counterterrorism campaign means the defeat of efforts to curb torture.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/fighting-terrorism-in-mauritania-even-it-means-torture/', 'snippet': 'The success of Mauritania’s counterterrorism campaign means the defeat of efforts to curb torture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOUAKCHOTT, Mauritania — Outside our tent on a beach about 100 miles north of the capital, the Atlantic Ocean was glittering under the midday sun and a fresh tuna was searing on a grill. Inside, the conversation with my Mauritanian friends turned to torture and detention. One described how he’d been chained up naked for weeks; another talked about his brother who had a pin inserted under his fingernails. Both victims had been arrested during a crackdown on political dissidents in 2003, in the twilight of the 21-year dictatorship of Maaouya Sid’Ahmed\xa0Ould Taya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Torture Against Terrorism', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aziz, Mohamed Ould Abdel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mauritania', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T13:44:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Armstrong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Armstrong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59ee2b33-6dbe-5125-9f52-12b3316bc43b', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59ee2b33-6dbe-5125-9f52-12b3316bc43b'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities had been called two times to a house in Cleveland, Ohio, where three young women who disappeared about a decade ago were found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/us/cleveland-kidnapping.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities had been called two times to a house in Cleveland, Ohio, where three young women who disappeared about a decade ago were found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — One neighbor remembered occasional late-ni