idence (and noted amateur “American Idol”-ologist) ranks the five most-talented “Idol” contestants ever. Not necessarily the winners: Just the best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last weekend’s Riff, Heather Havrilesky examined what the difference between Mariah Carey and Nicki Minaj (hint: think anodyne glamor versus outsize freakiness) can tell us about our changing notions of musical talent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rank Something! The Top 5 Most Talented ‘American Idol’ Contestants Ever', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T15:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Reid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6796c54-5bd4-5821-b1d8-651d8928548d', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6796c54-5bd4-5821-b1d8-651d8928548d'}, {'abstract': 'Baxter International said that the immunoglobulin therapy did not significantly arrest the decline in either cognition or daily functioning when compared with a placebo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/business/baxter-says-its-new-alzheimers-treatment-has-failed.html', 'snippet': 'Baxter International said that the immunoglobulin therapy did not significantly arrest the decline in either cognition or daily functioning when compared with a placebo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In yet another setback for the treatment of Alzheimer’s disease, Baxter International said Tuesday that its drug, Gammagard, had failed to halt the mental decline caused by the disease in a late-stage clinical trial. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline'