call affecting about 3.3 million Japanese vehicles last month has apparently spread to BMW as well. BMW says it will recall about 42,000 of its 2002-3 3 Series models because a passenger side air bag defect could send shards of metal into the passenger compartment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Air Bag Recall Spreads to BMW; G.M. Recalls Some eAssist Models', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25547f76-71c6-55e9-92ff-7d937babd52b', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25547f76-71c6-55e9-92ff-7d937babd52b'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry and Foreign Minister Sergey V. Lavrov of Russia jointly intensified pressure on Syria to settle a conflict that has killed more than 70,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/world/middleeast/syria-golan-heights-united-nations.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry and Foreign Minister Sergey V. Lavrov of Russia jointly intensified pressure on Syria to settle a conflict that has killed more than 70,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia and the United States announced on Tuesday that they would seek to convene an international conference within weeks aimed at ending the civil war in Syria, jointly intensifying their diplomatic pressure on the combatants to peacefully settle a conflict that has taken more than 70,000 lives and left millions displaced and desperate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Russia Plan Conference Aimed at Ending Syrian War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and Russia Plan Conference Aimed at Ending Syrian War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Golan Heights', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavrov, Sergey V', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martyrs of Yarmouk (Syria)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:05:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/346cff40-e5a4-5c6f-95b6-dca45dca01d0', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/346cff40-e5a4-5c6f-95b6-dca45dca01d0'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/the-gun-report-may-7-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve written several times about an anti-gun violence organization called Evolve, which aims to change the culture around gun violence by reframing it as a public safety issue. A big part of these efforts is enlisting responsible gun owners in the movement to reduce gun deaths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 7, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e2d608-90ed-5be0-8f04-2f30bfc12a54', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e2d608-90ed-5be0-8f04-2f30bfc12a54'}, {'abstract': 'The rising star Lucien Smith evokes Giuliani-era New York—so recent, and yet, so long ago—with a new exhibition and a film made with Glenn O’Brien.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/on-view-a-wunderkind-artist-summons-a-barely-bygone-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The rising star Lucien Smith evokes Giuliani-era New York—so recent, and yet, so long ago—with a new exhibition and a film made with Glenn O’Brien.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He’s just 24, but Lucien Smith has arrived. In the past two years the assemblage artist, known for canvases that mix paint with found objects, has shown in prestigious galleries from L.A. to Milan, including Half Gallery, OHWOW and Brand New. Smith’s new solo show at the Suzanne Geiss Company, “A Clean Sweep,” which opens tomorrow, is an homage to Giuliani-era New York in three parts. The first is a group of free-standing brooms, “collected” off New York City streets by Smith and his friends, that are meant to signify the city’s gentrification. The second is a series of Polaroid grids featuring relics of the city’s urban landscape, including trash cans, crosswalks and playground signs. The third is a film (seen here) made in collaboration with a New York institution: Glenn O’Brien.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wunderkind Artist Summons a Barely Bygone New York', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806e6502-2c8e-5d6b-8808-9483c47bb31e', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806e6502-2c8e-5d6b-8808-9483c47bb31e'}, {'abstract': 'Crucial bills that would provide food to the poor and cement land acquisition rules held up by political fight.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/indias-parliament-descends-into-chaos-threatening-landmark-bills/', 'snippet': 'Crucial bills that would provide food to the poor and cement land acquisition rules held up by political fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI— India’s lower house of Parliament, under pressure to pass two pieces of legislation this week deemed crucial to the poor, farmers and development projects, descended into a shouting match Tuesday before adjourning.', 'source': 'The New 