ill skip this year’s meeting of the heads of the Commonwealth governments, the first time she has failed to attend since 1973, Buckingham Palace said on Tuesday. She will be represented at the biennial meeting, which this year is to be held in November in Sri Lanka, by her son Prince Charles, 64, the heir to the throne.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queen Elizabeth to Skip Commonwealth Meeting', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buckingham Palace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charles, Prince of Wales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d504fded-c30f-5bd4-ae40-c99ce5fbc26d', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d504fded-c30f-5bd4-ae40-c99ce5fbc26d'}, {'abstract': 'An American soldier was shipped out of Kunar Province after he was spotted expressing an unusual form of disrespect against President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/world/asia/us-soldier-targets-a-karzai-portrait-with-rocks.html', 'snippet': 'An American soldier was shipped out of Kunar Province after he was spotted expressing an unusual form of disrespect against President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — An American soldier would have been well served to remember the childhood adage about sticks and stones before he threw rocks at a wall-size portrait of President Hamid Karzai that graces a town square in northeastern Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.I. Stones a Portrait of Karzai, Causing a Stir', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.I. Stones A Portrait Of Karzai, Causing a Stir', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahidi, Said Fazlullah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65e169c7-4f62-5d78-9765-9c582a80660f', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65e169c7-4f62-5d78-9765-9c582a80660f'}, {'abstract': 'Youssou N’Dour and Kaija Saariaho will each be awarded about $150,000.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/senegalese-singer-and-finnish-composer-share-the-polar-prize/', 'snippet': 'Youssou N’Dour and Kaija Saariaho will each be awarded about $150,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senegalese singer Youssou N’Dour and the Finnish composer Kaija Saariaho were named the winners Tuesday of the 2013 Polar Music Prize. Each will be awarded one million Swedish kronor, or about $150,000, and will be invited to a ceremony in Stockholm on Aug. 27.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senegalese Singer and Finnish Composer Share the Polar Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Stig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "N'Dour, Youssou", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saariaho, Kaija', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/950deedd-959f-510a-8735-cff6940cfa0d', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/950deedd-959f-510a-8735-cff6940cfa0d'}, {'abstract': 'Even though there are more Democratic than Republican state senators in New York, a spate of indictments makes Democratic control seem unlikely soon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/nyregion/sampsons-arrest-further-hurts-albany-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'Even though there are more Democratic than Republican state senators in New York, a spate of indictments makes Democratic control seem unlikely soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — There are many more Democrats than Republicans in New York State. There are even more Democrats than Republicans in the State Senate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], '