vanced in-memory computing product, HANA, as a cloud service, and says everything else will go there. No word on prices, or on what Oracle and AWS will do.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/sap-takes-it-all-to-the-cloud/', 'snippet': 'The timeline isn’t clear, but the German software giant SAP thinks it’s time to get out of selling on-premise software. SAP is offering its advanced in-memory computing product, HANA, as a cloud service, and says everything else will go there. No ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAP, the German software giant, is making one of the largest pushes into cloud computing yet seen from a large incumbent company. It may even be destroying its own business, in order to build for a new one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/technology/07bits-sikka/07bits-sikka-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'SAP Takes It All to the Cloud', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T16:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cb40558-416f-5bf9-9724-d6e7cddaeb54', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cb40558-416f-5bf9-9724-d6e7cddaeb54'}, {'abstract': 'Two months after 14-year-old Gina DeJesus vanished in 2004, the son of the suspect in her kidnapping interviewed her mother while a college journalism student for a local community newspaper.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/son-of-cleveland-kidnapping-suspect-wrote-about-missing-girl-in-2004/', 'snippet': 'Two months after 14-year-old Gina DeJesus vanished in 2004, the son of the suspect in her kidnapping interviewed her mother while a college journalism student for a local community newspaper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The son of Ariel Castro, the Cleveland man suspected of abducting three women and keeping them hidden in his home for years, wrote about the disappearance of one of the victims, Gina DeJesus, for a local newspaper in 2004.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Son of Cleveland Kidnapping Suspect Wrote About Missing Girl in 2004', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': N