person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc70b595-b050-53ac-be94-6819961a922c', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc70b595-b050-53ac-be94-6819961a922c'}, {'abstract': 'Ruben Diaz Jr.’s endorsement was not much of a surprise, given that he had been a vocal supporter of William C. Thompson Jr. in 2009, but his endorsement had been coveted by all the major Democratic candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/thompson-gets-key-endorsement-from-bronx-borough-president/', 'snippet': 'Ruben Diaz Jr.’s endorsement was not much of a surprise, given that he had been a vocal supporter of William C. Thompson Jr. in 2009, but his endorsement had been coveted by all the major Democratic candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another sign of his deep ties to established leaders in minority communities, William C. Thompson Jr. collected a key endorsement in his bid for mayor Tuesday from Ruben Diaz Jr., the Bronx borough president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thompson Gets Key Endorsement From Bronx Borough President', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Ruben Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T17:36:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d66f3a75-2ea2-51d2-996e-c073474a93fe', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d66f3a75-2ea2-51d2-996e-c073474a93fe'}, {'abstract': 'The party has not been a big factor in recent elections, but if it can gain a spot on the general election ballot, John A. Catsimatidis could remain in the race for mayor even if he loses the Republican nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/liberal-party-endorses-catsimatidis/', 'snippet': 'The party has not been a big factor in recent elections, but if it can gain a spot on the general election ballot, John A. Catsimatidis could remain in the race for mayor even if he loses the Republican nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John A. Catsimatidis, the billionaire businessman and Gristedes supermarket owner running for mayor of New York City, picked up the endorsement of an obscure but potentially influential political group on Tuesday, adding another wrinkle to the Republican primary. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberal Party Backs Catsimatidis', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T17:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4764565-fa84-52e8-b53b-ba0cc3a07f97', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4764565-fa84-52e8-b53b-ba0cc3a07f97'}, {'abstract': 'An angry President Obama and Congress demanded action after a Pentagon survey estimated 26,000 people in the armed forces were assaulted last year, up from 19,000 in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/us/politics/pentagon-study-sees-sharp-rise-in-sexual-assaults.html', 'snippet': 'An angry President Obama and Congress demanded action after a Pentagon survey estimated 26,000 people in the armed forces were assaulted last year, up from 19,000 in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The problem of sexual assault in the military leapt to the forefront in Washington on Tuesday as the Pentagon released a survey estimating that 26,000 people in the armed forces were sexually assaulted last year, up from 19,000 in 2010, and an angry President Obama and Congress demanded action.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Assaults in Military Raise Alarm in Washington', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sexual Assaults in Military Raise Alarm in Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krusinski, Jeffrey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helms, Susan J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T17:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dad8d888-d141-5514-a02e-d4ae96284449', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dad8d888-d141-5514-a02e-d4ae96284449'}, {'abstract': 'CBS will continue to carry the championship game in 2014 and 2015, and the two networks will also start splitting Round of 8 games in 2014, rather than in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/sports/ncaabasketball/ncaa-tournament-final-four-is-moving-to-tbs.html', 'snippet': 'CBS will continue to carry the championship game in 2014 and 2015, and the two networks will also start splitting Round of 8 games in 2014, rather than in 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TBS will start televising the Final Four of the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament in 2014 and 2015, advancing the schedule contemplated in its 14-year, $10.8 billion contract with CBS that went into effect three years ago. In those two years, CBS will continue to carry the championship game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Men’s Final Four Is Moving to TBS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.C.A.A. Semifinals on TBS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TBS Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McManus, Sean', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T17:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', '