l operatives at taxpayer expense as they readied their own campaigns for mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/albanese-criticizes-2-elected-rivals-over-office-staff-hiring/', 'snippet': 'Sal F. Albanese accused Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, and Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, of having hired political operatives at taxpayer expense as they readied their own campaigns for mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sal F. Albanese, a former city councilman and a Democratic candidate for mayor, on Tuesday accused two of his rivals, Christine C. Quinn, the Council speaker, and Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, of having hired political operatives at taxpayer expense as they readied their own campaigns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albanese Criticizes 2 Elected Rivals Over Office Staff Hiring', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBANESE, SAL F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T18:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74d5a556-dcac-5994-a8bb-839e9d0b18bc', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74d5a556-dcac-5994-a8bb-839e9d0b18bc'}, {'abstract': 'The list of cities and towns across the nation that have their own poets laureate is rapidly growing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/us/poets-laureate-proliferate-across-us.html', 'snippet': 'The list of cities and towns across the nation that have their own poets laureate is rapidly growing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRESNO, Calif. — This city has long been an object of ridicule. Even seemingly innocuous details like the flatness of the land, reinforced by the sea of ranch-style houses, take on a pejorative hue. Midway between San Francisco and Los Angeles, the western gateway on Highway 99 to Yosemite National Park, Fresno is not a destination but “a bathroom stop,” in the words of its poet laureate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/08POET/08POET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recognition Grows for Poets of Streets, Main or Otherwise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recognition Grows for Poets Of Streets, Main Or Otherwise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poets Laureate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fresno County (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyner, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Philip (1928- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrera, Juan Felipe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T18:05:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/972ad1be-b31e-5291-9f3d-9e2c1aa3e396', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/972ad1be-b31e-5291-9f3d-9e2c1aa3e396'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s top banking regulator has begun an investigation into pension-advance firms, the lenders that woo retirees to sign over their monthly pension checks in return for cash.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/new-york-state-investigating-pension-advance-firms/', 'snippet': 'New York’s top banking regulator has begun an investigation into pension-advance firms, the lenders that woo retirees to sign over their monthly pension checks in return for cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s top banki