rennan, John O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T18:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/516eb05c-949a-5d4c-885b-52a0953b0a29', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/516eb05c-949a-5d4c-885b-52a0953b0a29'}, {'abstract': 'Derrick Rose’s absence has bewildered N.B.A. fans who are used to seeing injured players attempt to return, especially in the playoffs, especially this season in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/sports/basketball/bulls-derrick-rose-stands-out-for-not-toughing-it-out.html', 'snippet': 'Derrick Rose’s absence has bewildered N.B.A. fans who are used to seeing injured players attempt to return, especially in the playoffs, especially this season in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Los Angeles, Kobe Bryant tore his Achilles’ and limped out to shoot free throws in a valiant effort to make the playoffs. In Oakland, after being injured in his first postseason game after an eight-season wait, David Lee suited up with a torn hip flexor and took a minute to rise up for a rebound.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/sports/08araton/08araton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/sports/08araton/08araton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 948}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/sports/08araton/08araton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 6