it of Party for the Home', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-07T21:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35987e05-7458-50c6-ae35-a6ab6ba9c9e1', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35987e05-7458-50c6-ae35-a6ab6ba9c9e1'}, {'abstract': 'I devoured the details that came from an annotated version of Pamela Colloff’s 28,000-word article.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/07/marginalia-added-by-the-author/', 'snippet': 'I devoured the details that came from an annotated version of Pamela Colloff’s 28,000-word article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here at the magazine, you might say we have a thing about marginalia. So perhaps it’s not a surprise that I’m mildly infatuated with Nieman Storyboard’s Annotation Tuesday! (That’s not an unwarranted exclamation mark.) It’s a series produced every other week in which authors answer questions about their reporting and writing, which is obviously cool. (Who doesn’t want to know how a reporter got a witness to talk? Or where that detail about the marigolds came from?) But Annotation Tuesday! serves up the answers in the body of the story itself — kind of like the obsessive highlights and notes I tend to make with my Kindle, but in this case with actual answers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/07/magazine/07-texas-monthly-spread/07-texas-monthly-spread-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 364,