itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1508808-1626-558e-8d6f-24f2d6a24352', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1508808-1626-558e-8d6f-24f2d6a24352'}, {'abstract': 'God’s Love We Deliver, a provider of meals to sick people, sold its air rights for a condominium development to finance an expansion of its building. But some residents object to the plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/realestate/commercial/sohos-gods-love-we-deliver-faces-obstacle-to-expansion.html', 'snippet': 'God’s Love We Deliver, a provider of meals to sick people, sold its air rights for a condominium development to finance an expansion of its building. But some residents object to the plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After spending several years searching for a larger home, God’s Love We Deliver, a charity that prepares and delivers meals to the sick and homebound, decided that the best place for it to grow was in the building it already owned. To help pay for the major expansion, the group plans to sell about $4 million of its development rights to a developer to build a 14-story condo next door.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/business/God-Love1/God-Love1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/business/God-Love1/God-Love1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/business/God-Love1/God-Love1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1