: None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc0c80a-fa74-51bd-ad85-889cd52a1ab7', 'word_count': 1332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc0c80a-fa74-51bd-ad85-889cd52a1ab7'}, {'abstract': 'Five candidates running for New York City’s mayoral race try to outdo one another in compassion at a forum on animal rights. Who loves pets the most?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/opinion/mayoral-candidates-profess-love-of-four-legged-creatures.html', 'snippet': 'Five candidates running for New York City’s mayoral race try to outdo one another in compassion at a forum on animal rights. Who loves pets the most?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mayoral forum on animal rights, held at the Union Theological Seminary on Monday, offered the strange sight of New York politicians trying to outdo one another in gentleness and compassion. Five candidates sat beneath organ pipes, professing their love of four-legged creatures and easily eliciting cheers, claps, woos and hoots from an audience that seemed neither to know nor care how expertly it was being played. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Legs Are Good', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Four Legs Are Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major':