'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dominion Resources Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T01:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82add22f-86ed-5f5d-b254-b140073099e1', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82add22f-86ed-5f5d-b254-b140073099e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department announced sanctions against eight Mexicans on Tuesday whom it identified as the main bosses for the Sinaloa Cartel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/world/americas/mexico-us-penalizes-drug-traffickers.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department announced sanctions against eight Mexicans on Tuesday whom it identified as the main bosses for the Sinaloa Cartel.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Treasury Department announced sanctions against eight Mexicans on Tuesday whom it identified as the main bosses for the Sinaloa Cartel just south of Arizona and Mexicali, Calif. A joint investigation including the Drug Enforcement Agency and United States Customs and Border Protection identified the cartel leaders, and law enforcement officials said they expected additional penalties to follow, including the freezing of assets and bank accounts. “We rely on these types of enforcement actions to really lower the hammer,” said Adam Szubin, director of the Office of Foreign Assets Control at the Treasury Department. He added, “These are some pretty serious players.” Several other Sinaloa operatives have already been penalized, including Joaquin Guzmán, also known as El Chapo, the cartel’s leader. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: U.S. Penalizes Drug Traffickers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: U.S. Penalizes Drug Suspects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinaloa Cartel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guzman Loera, Joaquin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T01:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a2a07aa-fc5b-5d2b-89aa-32db8c724fc2', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a2a07aa-fc5b-5d2b-89aa-32db8c724fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Marco Rubio disputed a Heritage Foundation analysis released Monday that found the legislation offering a pathway to citizenship would produce a “lifetime fiscal deficit” of at least $6.3 trillion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/us/politics/rubio-says-heritage-foundation-analysis-on-immigration-is-flawed.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Marco Rubio disputed a Heritage Foundation analysis released Monday that found the legislation offering a pathway to citizenship would produce a “lifetime fiscal deficit” of at least $6.3 trillion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senator Marco Rubio, Republican of Florida, aggressively pushed back Tuesday against a Heritage Foundation report that estimated new immigration legislation would cost taxpayers $6.3 trillion by using the foundation’s longstanding support for dynamic scoring — which takes into account projected economic growth when determining the cost of legislation — as a cudgel against it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/us/IMMIG/IMMIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarg