eld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ed8fda0-a060-538d-9024-77fd35116b22', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ed8fda0-a060-538d-9024-77fd35116b22'}, {'abstract': 'The F.B.I. director Robert S. Mueller III met with Russian officials in Moscow on Tuesday to discuss the  the Boston bombings, according to American officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/world/europe/russia-fbi-director-in-moscow-to-discuss-boston-bombings.html', 'snippet': 'The F.B.I. director Robert S. Mueller III met with Russian officials in Moscow on Tuesday to discuss the  the Boston bombings, according to American officials.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The F.B.I. director Robert S. Mueller III met with Russian law enforcement and intelligence officials in Moscow on Tuesday to discuss the bureau’s investigation of the Boston Marathon bombings, according to American officials. The investigation has focused in part on intelligence the Russian government provided the F.B.I. in 2011 that one of the bombing suspects was a Muslim extremist. Since the attacks, President Obama and President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia have pledged to work closely together as law enforcement officials in both countries have tried to determine how they could have thwarted the attacks. In 2011, the F.B.I. investigated the Russian warning about one of the suspects, Tamerlan Tsarnaev, but ultimately told the Russians that it had not found any information to back their assertions. In response to several follow-up requests from the F.B.I., the Russians declined to provide more information about the intelligence. In recent weeks, however, the Russians have provided F.B.I. agents with that additional information. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: F.B.I. Director in Moscow to Discuss Boston Bombings', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: F.B.I. Director in Moscow to Discuss Boston Bombings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T01:36:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d04e9f08-0951-521b-ae82-b21ba6c89f06', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d04e9f08-0951-521b-ae82-b21ba6c89f06'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Wednesday, May 8, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-wednesday-may-8-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Wednesday, May 8, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Yesterday they came in and just threw five corpses on the ground.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, May 8, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_d