eren’t strong enough to pull the nation out of its economic quagmire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/business/global/china-trade-figures-rise-slightly-but-weaknesses-persist.html', 'snippet': 'The Chinese government said trade figures for April showed some improvement, but weren’t strong enough to pull the nation out of its economic quagmire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Trade figures for April released by the Chinese government on Wednesday morning were slightly better than economists expected, but still indicated that demand was fairly weak in foreign markets and in China itself.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Trade Figures Rise, but Weaknesses Persist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Trade Figures Rise Slightly, but Weaknesses Persist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T03:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02756f27-1e75-56c5-8dbb-eed982785d87', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02756f27-1e75-56c5-8dbb-eed982785d87'}, {'abstract': 'Four people will share the $1 million reward for the capture of Christopher Dorner, the former Los Angeles police officer became the subject of a manhunt across Southern California this year, the police said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/us/california-4-will-share-reward-in-manhunt.html', 'snippet': 'Four people will share the $1 million reward for the capture of Christopher Dorner, the former Los Angeles police officer became the subject of a manhunt across Southern California this year, the police said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four people will share the $1 million reward for the capture of Christopher Dorner, the former Los Angeles police officer who is suspected in four murders and became the subject of a manhunt across Southern California this year, the police said Tuesday. Karen and Jim Reynolds will receive 80 percent of the reward. Mr. Dorner tied them up and stole their car, after they found him hiding in their Big Bear Lake condominium. They freed themselves and called the police. He killed himself hours later, surrounded by law enforcement officers. Daniel McGowan, who reported seeing Mr. Dorner’s burning truck, will receive 15 percent of the reward. Lee McDaniel, who spotted Mr. Dorner and his truck in Corona, Calif., will receive 5 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: 4 Will Share Reward in Manhunt', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: 4 Will Share Reward In Manhunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorner, Christopher Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T03:50:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6fcd9ce-16f2-55f9-9eff-df57e041c323', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6fcd9ce-16f2-55f9-9eff-df57e041c323'}, {'abstract': 'At the Hôtel Americano in Chelsea, a visually stunning installation by the German artist Tobias Rehberger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/t-magazine/a-bar-thats-also-a-piece-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'At the Hôtel Americano in Chelsea, a visually stunning installation by the German artist Tobias Rehberger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most exciting installations in New York City the week of the Frieze Art Faircan be found not on Randall’s Island but in Chelsea, in the basement of the Hôtel Americano. There, the German artist Tobias Rehberger has constructed Bar Oppenheimer, a facsimile of his favorite Frankfurt watering hole, which he describes as both a sculptural artwork and a utilitarian space. The space, which opens May 10 and will remain open until July 14, dazzles the senses with its salonlike atmosphere, tight dimensions and prismatic black-and-white stripes; it’s also a functional bar where anyone can stop in for a drink during the life of the project.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/t-magazine/08rehberger-casale/08rehberger-casale-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/t-magazine/08rehberger-casale/08rehberger-casale-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/t-magazine/08rehberger-casale/08rehberger-casale-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 