'abstract': 'For employers, there are benefits and costs to replacing full-time employees with part-time ones, and the Affordable Care Act will provide an interesting case study in how this plays out, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/what-job-sharing-brings/', 'snippet': 'For employers, there are benefits and costs to replacing full-time employees with part-time ones, and the Affordable Care Act will provide an interesting case study in how this plays out, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Job-Sharing Brings', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T04:01:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4261c05e-b107-50d4-8127-64c8cb47ed40', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4261c05e-b107-50d4-8127-64c8cb47ed40'}, {'abstract': 'The Hall of Fame coach Phil Jackson has indicated that he is not interested in returning to the sideline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/s