 [{'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeacb59e-f8aa-50d8-ba50-60989c9c2200', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeacb59e-f8aa-50d8-ba50-60989c9c2200'}, {'abstract': 'An obscure London firm may decide whether Jamie Dimon remains both C.E.O. and chairman of JPMorgan Chase. | Kleiner Perkins is adjusting its strategy after hitting a rough patch. | Chrysler provides a lesson in how deals struck in haste can come back to haunt. | Yahoo has met with executives of Hulu, according to a report.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/deciding-on-dimons-dual-role/', 'snippet': 'An obscure London firm may decide whether Jamie Dimon remains both C.E.O. and chairman of JPMorgan Chase. | Kleiner Perkins is adjusting its strategy after hitting a rough patch. | Chrysler provides a lesson in how deals struck in haste can come b...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little-known firm in London could play a crucial role in determining the fate of Jamie Dimon, the chief executive of JPMorgan Chase. The firm, Governance for Owners, has been tasked with voting the shares of BlackRock, the bank’s largest shareholder, on the question of whether to strip Mr. Dimon of his role as chairman, Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deciding on Dimon’s Dual Role', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T12:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcf35d58-9582-5ff6-bccf-fe0a82aa4c40', 'word_count': 1728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcf35d58-9582-5ff6-bccf-fe0a82aa4c40'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A cabdriver named Bernie did the unexpected when a soldier on leave asked to be dropped at the nearest subway station.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/a-corporals-taxi-ride/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A cabdriver named Bernie did the unexpected when a soldier on leave asked to be dropped at the nearest subway station.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Corporal’s Taxi Ride', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LaGuardia Airport (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T12:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Washkevich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Washkevich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ad2ed2-491b-5023-a43c-9e3058ddb76f', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ad2ed2-491b-5023-a43c-9e3058ddb76f'}, {'abstract': 'The online home marketplace commissioned eight limited-edition collections to benefit different charities this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/objects-towel-off-with-designer-pieces-for-one-kings-lane/', 'snippet': 'The online home marketplace commissioned eight limited-edition collections to benefit different charities this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing its series of philanthropic collaborations with fashion and interior designers, the online home marketplace One Kings Lane tapped eight talents to create limited-edition prints for its inaugural Designer Series Beach Towels sale. The prints range from kitschy silhouettes of beach gear and diamonds (by Robert Verdi) to floral motifs (by Tracy Reese and Nanette Lepore) to geometric patterns (by Rebecca Minkoff, Celerie Kemble, Steven Alan and Jenni Kayne). Because they’re produced in the same basic colors, they can be mixed and matched easily. Beginning Monday, each designer will take a turn having a sale on OneKingsLane.com, offering several prints each for a few days at a time, with the proceeds benefiting a charity of the maker’s choosing. The first is Tracy Reese’s collection in support of AIDS Fund-New York Community Trust on May 13; the last is Jenni Kayne’s set to benefit Baby 2 Baby on June 18.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Objects | Towel Off With Designer Pieces for One Kings Lane', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Objects: Towel Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alan, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'One Kings Lane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T12:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c186ecec-df63-5521-a7f4-9f8ebe81e835', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c186ecec-df63-5521-a7f4-9f8ebe81e835'}, {'abstract': 'Two cloud-based software companies, GoodData, which does business analytics, and Box, which stores data, have announced a joint product. The move reflects the change in thinking about information, from a static fact to a potential source of insight.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/datas-transformation/', 'snippet': 'Two cloud-based software companies, GoodData, which does business analytics, and Box, which stores data, have announced a joint product. The move reflects the change in thinking about information, from a static fact to a potential source of insigh...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someday you’ll tell your grandchildren you remember the old days when data just sat there, like some list of information for people to look at.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-sub-levie/08bits-sub-levie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-sub-levie/08bits-sub-levie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-sub-levie/08bits-sub-levie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-sub-levie/08bits-sub-levie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-sub-levie/08bi