and aging, back pain, sciatica and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 100 readers submitted questions about aging and yoga to Dr. Loren Fishman, a back-pain and rehabilitative medicine specialist who has long incorporated yoga into patient care. In 1972, before applying to medical school, he studied yoga with B.K.S. Iyengar for a year in Pune, India. Dr. Fishman is medical director of Manhattan Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation in New York City, an assistant clinical professor at Columbia Medical School and an associate editor of the journal Topics in Geriatric Rehabilitation. He is also an author of eight books, including “Yoga for Osteoporosis: the Complete Guide.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 209, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 209, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice on Practicing Yoga in Middle Age, Part 1', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Back (Human Body Part)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sciatica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fishman, Loren', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T14:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/7433a33e-8372-5fe3-8c59-bbfa8d9bd99e', 'word_count': 2342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7433a33e-8372-5fe3-8c59-bbfa8d9bd99e'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Sanford, as the newly elected congressman from South Carolina’s First District, has become a symbol of political rehabilitation few thought could happen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/us/politics/mark-sanford-takes-spotlight-with-political-comeback.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Sanford, as the newly elected congressman from South Carolina’s First District, has become a symbol of political rehabilitation few thought could happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — After getting a few hours’ sleep, Mark Sanford made a victory lap Wednesday morning. He showed up on several national television news programs not only as the newly elected congressman from South Carolina’s First District, but also as a symbol of a political comeback many here and across the country thought could never happen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comeback Achieved, Sanford Takes Spotlight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanford, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T14:49:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea4a0c7b-f85e-51fc-979f-cccb1e719278', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea4a0c7b-f85e-51fc-979f-cccb1e719278'}, {'abstract': 'Some unemployed parents and their children, who have an entrepreneurial spirit but lack the experience or capital to start a business alone, are deciding to join forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/business/smallbusiness/with-bleak-job-prospects-parents-and-children-buy-into-franchises.html', 'snippet': 'Some unemployed parents and their children, who have an entrepreneurial spirit but lack the experience or capital to start a business alone, are deciding to join forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late one night in January 2012, Paige Palmer called her mother at home, crying. She was entering her final semester as a communications major at St. Mary’s College of California in Moraga, and neither she nor her friends were finding work. The job market was terrifying. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/09sb