mes, Gen. Joseph F. Dunford Jr., the supreme military commander in Afghanistan, discussed the readiness of the Afghan security forces, his optimism that the Afghan Army will be a unifying force for the country, the Taliban’s tactics this summer and winning over the Afghan people. Following are extended excerpts from the interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commander’s View of the Afghan Endgame', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunford, Joseph F Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T15:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cdb62f9-4344-58a8-9c78-db3e61163c02', 'word_count': 1470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cdb62f9-4344-58a8-9c78-db3e61163c02'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/the-gun-report-may-8-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This just in: two and a half months after California’s state pension funds voted to sell off their gun stocks, New York has followed suit. This morning, Comptroller John Liu announced that the New York City Employees’ Retirement System has sold $16.3 million worth of gun stocks. In his press release, Liu noted that another New York retirement fund, the Teachers’ Retirement System, had also dumped its gun stocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 8, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corpus Christi (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisville (Ky)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pensacola (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Raleigh (NC)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockford (Ill)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia Beach (Va)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T15:24:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/708a6922-ce28-565e-8a1a-a6a6ca7d0f14', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708a6922-ce28-565e-8a1a-a6a6ca7d0f14'}, {'abstract': 'The person doesn’t matter.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/south-carolina-voters-get-it/', 'snippet': 'The person doesn’t matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So they just convincingly voted for Mark Sanford, a man who cheated on his wife, tried to cover his actions with an absurd story about hiking the Appalachian Trail, and trespassed on his ex-wife’s property, over an exemplary Democratic candidate. And you know what? Given their preferences, this was the right thing to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina Voters Get It', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T15:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/337ac90d-2ebc-5321-9837-58a3d8d81d77', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/337ac90d-2ebc-5321-9837-58a3d8d81d77'}, {'abstract': 'Should President Obama approve the 1,700-mile Keystone XL pipeline, some foes of the project say he ought to  address climate policy at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/a-call-for-quid-pro-quo-on-keystone-pipeline-approval.html', 'snippet': 'Should President Obama approve the 1,700-mile Keystone XL pipeline, some foes of the project say he ought to  address climate policy at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama’s first major environmental decision of his second term could be to approve the Keystone XL pipeline, profoundly disappointing environmental advocates who have made the project a symbolic test of the president’s seriousness on climate change.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/business/energy-environment/09pipeline/09pipeline