her’s Day Gift', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Father's Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T15:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By David J. Ekerdt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Ekerdt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71909f64-b7f2-5dd3-a991-a15ee0b90170', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71909f64-b7f2-5dd3-a991-a15ee0b90170'}, {'abstract': 'Greta Gerwig stars in Noah Baumbach’s “Frances Ha,” a tribute to life in your 20s and to New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/movies/greta-gerwig-in-noah-baumbachs-frances-ha.html', 'snippet': 'Greta Gerwig stars in Noah Baumbach’s “Frances Ha,” a tribute to life in your 20s and to New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An address on Vanderbilt Avenue in Brooklyn. An F train that never comes. Unfinished on-spec scripts for “Saturday Night Live.” The artistically inclined friend of yours who, incongruously, is dating a man who works at Goldman Sachs. That exorbitant $3 fee at the Bank of America A.T.M. — and the long unpalatable walk to the next deli, to find a cheaper option. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12FRANCES-HA1_SPAN/12FRANCES-HA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge',