e', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Baron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3e3591a-626e-5271-bcce-9006b4304ae0', 'word_count': 1522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3e3591a-626e-5271-bcce-9006b4304ae0'}, {'abstract': 'This time on campuses.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/the-fix-the-debt-fix-is-still-in/', 'snippet': 'This time on campuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, Bill Clinton says that I’m right in the short run while Simpson-Bowles are right in the long run; he’s half right. But what’s interesting is to see the Peterson juggernaut still rolling along despite the enormous intellectual hit the cause has received.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fix the Debt Fix Is Still In', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T16:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40243dd5-7eef-5ff4-8db7-57533f95f2ec', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40243dd5-7eef-5ff4-8db7-57533f95f2ec'}, {'abstract': '“Let It Be,” which was created to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the Fab Four, will begin preview performances at the St. James Theater on July 16, with its opening night scheduled for July 24.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/beatles-concert-show-let-it-be-coming-to-broadway/', 'snippet': '“Let It Be,” which was created to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the Fab Four, will begin preview performances at the St. James Theater on July 16, with its opening night scheduled for July 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a group that split up more than four decades ago and never reunited, the Beatles are certainly finding plenty of opportunities to appear on Broadway. “Let It Be,” a popular British concert show based around the band’s music, will make its mop-topped way from the West End to Broadway this summer, press representatives for the production said on Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/arts/letitbe/letitbe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumb