': 'nyt://article/673f08f9-def7-5220-96f8-c9f1450ee39e'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln and the controversial decision to exile the dissident politician Clement L. Vallandigham.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/the-fire-in-the-rear/', 'snippet': 'Lincoln and the controversial decision to exile the dissident politician Clement L. Vallandigham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the Civil War’s most unusual surrenders took place on May 25, 1863. Accompanied by two Union officers, a former Ohio congressman named Clement L. Vallandigham approached a Confederate soldier on picket duty outside Murfreesboro, Tenn., and recited a short speech: “I am a citizen of Ohio, and of the United States. I am here within your lines by force and against my will. I therefore surrender myself to you as a prisoner of war.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fire in the Rear', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba2a7cb7-ab73-59df-82f1-765a187fb8dc', 'word_count': 1830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba2a7cb7-ab73-59df-82f1-765a187fb8dc'}, {'abstract': 'Baz Luhrmann, the director of “The Great Gatsby,” narrates a scene from his film.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/anatomy-of-a-scene-the-great-gatsby/', 'snippet': 'Baz Luhrmann, the director of “The Great Gatsby,” narrates a scene from his film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this video, the director Baz Lurhmann narrates a scene from “The Great Gatsby,” featuring a conversation between Jay Gatsby (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Nick Carraway (Tobey Maguire). Mr. Lurhmann discusses the location of the shoot (an area of Sydney, Australia, made up to look like Long Island) and how a rainstorm almost prevented the scene from happening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: ‘The Great Gatsby’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaprio, Leonardo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luhrmann, Baz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maguire, Tobey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f25f9721-f4de-5b70-ae5c-f264b26f6dc7', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f25f9721-f4de-5b70-ae5c-f264b26f6dc7'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Wagner, a senior executive at K.K.R.’s Capstone arm who had served as Go Daddy’s interim chief executive, will leave the private equity firm to to join Go Daddy full time as its chief operating officer and chief financial officer, he told DealBook in an interview.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/go-daddy-poaches-an-executive-from-k-k-r-as-company-eyes-growth/', 'snippet': 'Scott Wagner, a senior executive at K.K.R.’s Capstone arm who had served as Go Daddy’s interim chief executive, will leave the private equity firm to to join Go Daddy full time as its chief operating officer and chief financial officer, he told De...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Scott Wagner stepped up as the Go Daddy Group’s interim chief executive last summer, he viewed the move as temporary. He already had a day job, as a senior executive at an arm of Kohlberg Kravis Roberts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Go Daddy Lures an Executive From K.K.R.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irving, Blake', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Go Daddy Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b19ba454-d2b6-51c2-8fb6-5ebac55bf017', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b19ba454-d2b6-51c2-8fb6-5ebac55bf017'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students learn about the mysterious malady that has been killing honeybees across the country, discuss possible causes and potential solutions, and participate in a citizen science project to census honeybees in their neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/trouble-in-the-hive-researching-the-decimation-of-honeybee-colonies/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students learn about the mysterious malady that has been killing honeybees across the country, discuss possible causes and potential solutions, and participate in a citizen science project to census honeybees in their neighborhoods...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is colony collapse disorder, and why is it a growing concern to farmers and beekeepers? In this lesson, students learn about the ongoing decimation of honeybee colonies across the country, discuss its possible causes and potential solutions, and participate in a citizen science project to census honeybees in their neighborhoods.Materials | Computers with Internet connections, a variety of fruits', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trouble in the Hive: Researching the Decimation of Honeybee Colonies', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a96831-5eca-500d-bfff-187d1350fff4', 'word_count': 1659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a96831-5eca-500d-bfff-187d1350fff4'}, {'abstract': 'No previous Congressional effort to change immigration law has offered such a broad, swift reprieve to people expelled from the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/us/politics/in-immigration-bill-deportees-see-hope-for-second-chance.html', 'snippet': 'No previous Congressional effort to change immigration law has offered such a broad, swift reprieve to people expelled from the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIJUANA, Mexico — Erik García arrived at the metal gate of a migrant shelter here, deported from Los Angeles just hours earlier. After 23 years in the United States illegally, he suddenly found himself separated from the country where he had moved as a boy, and from his two teenage daughters, both American citizens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/us/09DEPORTEE/09DEPORTEE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Immigration Bill, Deportees See Hope for Second Chance in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Immigration Bill, Deportees See Hope for Second Chance in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cave, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tijuana (Mexico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d2a7cbe-f2b1-5e67-b8f5-69e1c44293c0', 'word_count': 1436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d2a7cbe-f2b1-5e67-b8f5-69e1c44293c0'}, {'abstract': 'We chart the success of the 75-year-old businessman Chris Blackwell, who has made a fortune betting on the charms of his beloved Jamaica.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/the-man-with-the-golden-ear/', 'snippet': 'We chart the success of the 75-year-old businessman Chris Blackwell, who has made a fortune betting on the charms of his beloved Jamaica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 75-year-old businessman Chris Blackwell has made a fortune betting on the charms of his beloved Jamaica. In 1959, Blackwell started Island Records, which brought reggae and Bob Marley to a worldwide audience. (He also signed U2, Cat Stevens, Grace Jones, Nick Drake and Roxy Music.) When Blackwell sold Island 30 years later, he turned his attention to hotels: both in Miami’s South Beach, which he helped put on the map when he transformed blighted Art Deco properties into luxury destinations; and, more enduringly, at home, where his current holdings include GoldenEye, the former home of the James Bond author Ian Fleming (a longtime lover of Blackwell’s mother, Blanche), which attracts the likes of Kate Moss and Naomi Campbell. His latest venture? Jamaican rum, naturally.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man With the Golden Ear', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man With the Golden Ear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:29:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef3410e-0173-5287-808d-31aad87903ed', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef3410e-0173-5287-808d-31aad87903ed'}, {'abstract': 'The Open Compute Project, a Facebook-led, open-source effort to build big data centers better and cheaper, is going after networking hardware. The project could prod competition among networking gear makers. It could also be a blow to Google, which runs proprietary equipment in its clouds.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/opening-up-networkings-black-box/', 'snippet': 'The Open Compute Project, a Facebook-led, open-source effort to build big data centers better and cheaper, is going after networking hardware. The project could prod competition among networking gear makers. It could also be a blow to Google, whic...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Open Compute Project, a Facebook-led effort to remake the computer servers and data storage of the biggest computing centers, is broadening its aims to include networking as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-open-compute/08bits-open-compute-jumbo.png', 'height': 138, 'width': 259, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-open-compute/08bits-open-compute-superJumbo.png', 'height': 138, 'width': 259, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-open-compute/08bits-open-compute-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/08/technology/08bits-open-compute/08bits-open-compute-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opening Up Networking’s Black Box', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Centers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Open-Source Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T17:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'rol