alue': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AARP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T18:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aa0f0ef-73ce-5633-9947-a6dfab21b127', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aa0f0ef-73ce-5633-9947-a6dfab21b127'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Chris Murphy said that, before deciding to run for office, you should ask yourself if you’re willing to beg absolute strangers for money.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/the-politician-as-telemarketer/', 'snippet': 'Senator Chris Murphy said that, before deciding to run for office, you should ask yourself if you’re willing to beg absolute strangers for money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal elected officials spend only a fraction of their time engaged in what might loosely be called the business of governing — even when they belong to the party that believes in government. Oh, sure, they write the occasional bill, and talk with their constituents, and go out to dinner with lobbyists, and yell at other politicians on Sunday talk shows. Mostly, though, they beg for cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Politician as Telemarketer', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Christopher Scott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T18:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8f40a4f-a3d0-5e40-9326-d061634edde6', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8f40a4f-a3d0-5e40-9326-d061634edde6'}, {'abstract': 'In the latest Intersection video, we head to Dumbo, Brooklyn and met people that work in the area, who draw their style inspiration from music festivals and furniture design.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/video-intersection-dumbos-style-mash-up/', 'snippet': 'In the latest Intersection video, we head to Dumbo, Brooklyn and met people that work in the area, who draw their style inspiration from music festivals and furniture design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest Intersection video, we headed to Dumbo, Brooklyn, and met people who work in the area and draw style inspiration from music festivals and furniture design. Martin Medina, a visual designer, draws fashion inspiration from his youth in the Lower East Side and bright colors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Intersection, Dumbo’s Style Mash-Up', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T18:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Nikas, Simone S. Oliver, Fritzie Andrade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Fritzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrade', 'qualifier': No