.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/todays-scuttlebot-inside-google-glass-and-a-cyberattack-report/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Wednesday, selections include a big price cut for the Facebook phone, Google Glass for dogs and Yahoo talking with Hulu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Inside Google Glass, and a Cyberattack Report', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T20:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4237650-9996-55a3-acb4-8127c36b930e', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4237650-9996-55a3-acb4-8127c36b930e'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Cheng, a Chinese-American author who has never visited Mississippi, has written what many are calling a convincing novel set in that state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/books/bill-chengs-novel-is-southern-cross-the-dog.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Cheng, a Chinese-American author who has never visited Mississippi, has written what many are calling a convincing novel set in that state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From its opening pages, “Southern Cross the Dog” has all the markers of a novel written in the finest Southern gothic tradition. The Great Mississippi Flood of 1927 sweeps in, taking a few unlucky characters with it. There are references aplenty to race, poverty, the blues, voodoo and an ill-fated brothel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/09CHENG1/09CHENG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 526, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/09CHENG1/09CHENG1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 526, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/09CHENG1/09CHENG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/09CHENG1/09CHENG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/09CHENG1/09CHENG1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Mississippi Sight Unseen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing Mississippi Sight Unseen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheng, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T20:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf3e6c0-4e60-5265-be99-ac475d876d38', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf3e6c0-4e60-5265-be99-ac475d876d38'}, {'abstract': 'On the Amalfi Coast, a family’s bid to keep its small business going mirrors Italy’s debate about keeping local traditions alive in a global economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/world/europe/fragrant-lemon-groves-retain-their-allure-in-italy-but-for-how-long.html', 'snippet': 'On the Amalfi Coast, a family’s bid to keep its small business going mirrors Italy’s debate about keeping local traditions alive in a global economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMALFI, Italy — On a recent spring morning, Luigi Aceto, a hale 78, climbed a ladder in a terraced lemon grove that stretched up the hillside in one of Italy’s most picturesque towns and expertly began snipping lemons into a wicker basket. The sun was shining. The lemons were ripe and as big as fists. The scent of blossoms was intoxicating.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur