York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Sanford and the Future of Marriage', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T20:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c668c1c-1ede-5985-8c6e-729f7d11e0d3', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c668c1c-1ede-5985-8c6e-729f7d11e0d3'}, {'abstract': 'The musicians of the Minnesota Orchestra have been locked out since October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/labor-dispute-effectively-ends-minnesota-orchestras-season/', 'snippet': 'The musicians of the Minnesota Orchestra have been locked out since October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Minnesota Orchestra, where musicians have been locked out in a labor dispute since October, announced on Wednesday that it had canceled its concerts through June 2 – effectively, the rest of its season. At the same time, Michael Henson, the orchestra’s president and chief executive, announced a series of concerts for late July and early August, with repertory drawn from this season’s unperformed programs, saying in a statement that the concerts were added because “we are not willing to give up on our entire season.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Labor Dispute Effectively Ends Minnesota Orchestra’s Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanska, Osmo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T20:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18f23728-5918-5d7a-a419-88f2f161ca6a', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18f23728-5918-5d7a-a419-88f2f161ca6a'}, {'abstract': 'With dexterity and insights, the pianist Maurizio Pollini performed four Beethoven sonatas in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/arts/music/maurizio-pollini-plays-beethoven-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'With dexterity and insights, the pianist Maurizio Pollini performed four Beethoven sonatas in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Admirers of the Italian pianist Maurizio Pollini are set in their lionization of this singular artist; his detractors, likewise, are steadfast. Were you not an aficionado of his methods before the recital he gave at Carnegie Hall on Sunday afternoon, nothing that he played during the all-Beethoven program was likely to change your mind. Equally, were you a devotee, nothing Mr. Pollini did on Sunday changed that condition. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/pollini/pollini-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 970, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/arts/pollini/pollini-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargew