nyt://article/cab477b1-11c5-5e8e-ab48-d4638ddc7bda'}, {'abstract': 'A furniture collection by Roman and Williams for the SoHo design shop Matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/garden/roman-and-williams-furniture-for-the-soho-design-shop-matter.html', 'snippet': 'A furniture collection by Roman and Williams for the SoHo design shop Matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robin Standefer and Stephen Alesch, of the design firm Roman and Williams, have created interiors for such era-defining buildings as the Ace and Standard hotels in New York. But their new furniture collection doesn’t stray from tradition. The couple have worked with the SoHo design store Matter in creating a chair, a side table, a coffee table and a series of lights, all in alluring woods like walnut, teak and reclaimed oak. Ms. Standefer described the style as American vernacular. “We’re embracing simple structures,” Mr. Alesch added. This leaves room for laserlike attention to details. The chair, shown, with its custom brass hardware and fine leather ($6,500), makes that point. Information: (212) 343-2600 or mattermatters.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/garden/09FURNITURE/09CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/garden/09FURNITURE/09CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/garden/09FURNITURE/09CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/garden/09FURNITURE/09CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1365, 'subTy