 today at the Collective.1 Design Fair at Pier 57 in Chelsea. Watch our exclusive video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the cavernous entrance to Pier 57 in Chelsea, an ancient loading dock has become a makeshift stage for the work of Gaetano Pesce, the 74-year-old Italian design legend who moved to New York 32 years ago because the city “was the capital of the 20th century.” He arrived with a splash, one of a who’s who of modern Italian designers included in MoMA’s groundbreaking 1972 show “Italy: The New Domestic Landscape.” But Pesce hasn’t had a comprehensive solo show in his adopted hometown since a 1999 exhibit tucked away at Columbia University’s School of Architecture. “He’s a legend and a New Yorker, so that tragedy needed to be corrected,” said Steven Learner, the creative director of the new Collective.1 Design Fair, where Pesce’s retrospective opened today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Legendary Gaetano Pesce on Work and Life', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-08T22:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Perry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e97eec7-7d1b-50a0-8be4-7c0e15812c23', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e97eec7-7d1b-50a0-8be4-7c0e15812c23'}, {'abstract': 'The 74-year-old Italian design legend discusses his highly personal career retrospective at the inaugural Collective.1 Design Fair in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/t-magazine/100000002214791/collective1-design-fair-gaetano-pesce.html', 'snippet': 'The 74-year-old Italian design legend discusses his highly personal career ret