tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1dce1d-1080-58c3-9f92-6cf00bb8f7b9', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1dce1d-1080-58c3-9f92-6cf00bb8f7b9'}, {'abstract': 'In an industry known for reclusive traders and math geeks, Wall Street’s Anthony Scaramucci is a P.T. Barnum in a Ferragamo tie.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/08/hedge-fund-impresario-plays-host-in-las-vegas/', 'snippet': 'In an industry known for reclusive traders and math geeks, Wall Street’s Anthony Scaramucci is a P.T. Barnum in a Ferragamo tie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Just outside the grand ballroom at the Bellagio hotel early Wednesday morning, Anthony Scaramucci, the backslapping host of the country’s largest hedge fund conference, spotted Gregory J. Fleming, president of Morgan Stanley Investment Management and one of Mr. Scaramucci’s most important business relationships.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Impresario Plays Host in Las Vegas', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hedge Fund Impresario Plays Host In Las Vegas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scaramucci, Anthony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T00:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99c3b57c-b674-518f-aa52-870ab43b7b75', 'word_count': 1432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99c3b57c-b674-518f-aa52-870ab43b7b75'}, {'abstract': 'After a series of horrifying injuries to pitchers, most recently to J. A. Happ of the Blue Jays, baseball is considering ways to better protect those on the mound from sizzling line drives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/sports/baseball/on-the-mound-60-feet-6-inches-from-disaster.html', 'snippet': 'After a series of horrifying injuries to pitchers, most recently to J. A. Happ of the Blue Jays, baseball is considering ways to better protect those on the mound from sizzling line drives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday night, hours after a line drive in St. Petersburg, Fla., crashed off the head of Toronto Blue Jays pitcher J. A. Happ, Brandon McCarthy took the mound in Los Angeles and made his best start of the season for the Arizona Diamondbacks. McCarthy fractured his skull last September at Oakland, a victim of another line drive. He earned a two-year, $15 million contract before pitching his next game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/KEPNER1/KEPNER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/KEPNER1/KEPNER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/KEPNER1/KEPNER1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/KEPNER1/KEPNER1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1239, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}},