hich passed with a large enough majority to override an expected veto, will initially require New York businesses with at least 20 employees to pay for five sick days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/nyregion/new-york-council-approves-paid-sick-leave-measure.html', 'snippet': 'The bill, which passed with a large enough majority to override an expected veto, will initially require New York businesses with at least 20 employees to pay for five sick days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Council, after years of impassioned debate, approved a bill on Wednesday that will require many businesses to offer paid time off to sick employees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Council Approves Bill Mandating Sick-Day Pay ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Council Approves Bill Mandating Sick-Day Pay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T00:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b484ec-26c7-5ce5-b9d6-da629619ab7d', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b484ec-26c7-5ce5-b9d6-da629619ab7d'}, {'abstract': 'Ahmed Khalfan Ghailani, the only terrorist detainee to be held at the Guantánamo Bay prison and then tried in the civilian court system, is seeking to have his conviction overturned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/nyregion/argument-to-overturn-detainees-conviction-cites-years-in-custody-without-a-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Ahmed Khalfan Ghailani, the only terrorist detainee to be held at the Guantánamo Bay prison and then tried in the civilian court system, is seeking to have his conviction overturned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawyer for the only terrorist detainee to be held at the military prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, and then tried in the civilian court system asked a federal appeals court on Wednesday to overturn his conviction, on the grounds that his long detention violated his right to a speedy trial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Detainee’s Appeal Cites Long Wait for a Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detainee’s Appeal Cites Long Wait for a Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghailani, Ahmed Khalfan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T00:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16b7008a-f708-57a9-a203-7037ee936ea0', 'word_co