killing of her onetime boyfriend, Travis Alexander, in a trial marked by months of salacious evidence and testimony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jodi Arias was found guilty of first-degree murder on Wednesday for the killing of her onetime boyfriend, Travis Alexander, in a trial marked by months of salacious evidence and testimony depicting the couple’s tumultuous relationship. Ms. Arias was accused of stabbing Mr. Alexander almost 30 times, shooting him in the head and slashing his throat from ear to ear during a fit of jealous rage in 2008. Her lawyers argued he had been abusive to her, and that she killed him in self-defense. Jurors, who reached their verdict after roughly three days of deliberations in Phoenix, will next decide whether Ms. Arias, 32, receives the death penalty. There are currently three other women on Arizona’s death row. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Conviction in Murder', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Conviction In Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arias, Jodi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T04:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/795f8d50-713f-591c-bb4e-f4565de2fe4d', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795f8d50-713f-591c-bb4e-f4565de2fe4d'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers blew a 2-0 lead, but they neutralized Alex Ovechkin and held on to even their opening-round playoff series against the Capitals at 2-2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/sports/hockey/rangers-beat-capitals-to-even-series-at-2-2.html', 'snippet': 'The Rangers blew a 2-0 lead, but they neutralized Alex Ovechkin and held on to even their opening-round playoff series against the Capitals at 2-2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rangers hit every Capital in sight Wednesday night. They fearlessly blocked 33 shots. They won almost twice as many face-offs as Washington. They made Alex Ovechkin irrelevant. And with the outcome in doubt late, again, the defense and goaltending were stout.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/RANGERS-1/RANGERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/RANGERS-1/RANGERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/RANGERS-1/RANGERS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/RANGERS-1/RANGERS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 1991, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/sports/RANGERS-1/RANGERS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail