 of cicadas, the red-eyed insects renowned for their shrill mating call, are beginning to crawl out of the earth, an emergence 17 years in the making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/science/marvels-and-a-few-mysteries-in-cicadas-17-years.html', 'snippet': 'Billions of cicadas, the red-eyed insects renowned for their shrill mating call, are beginning to crawl out of the earth, an emergence 17 years in the making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From North Carolina to Connecticut, billions of creatures with eyes the color of blood and bodies the color of coal are crawling out of the earth. Periodical cicadas are emerging en masse, clambering into trees and singing a shivering chorus that can be heard for miles.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/science/14zimmer-span/14zimmer-span-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/science/14zimmer-span/14zimmer-span-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/science/14zimmer-span/14zimmer-span-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/science/14zimmer-span/14zimmer-span-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1144, 'width': 1960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/science/14zimmer-span/14zimmer-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201