aba'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with Essence magazine, Chirlane McCray speaks about the intersection of her personal and political lives, describing herself and Mr. de Blasio as “a very conventional, unconventional couple.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/de-blasios-wife-gives-candid-interview/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with Essence magazine, Chirlane McCray speaks about the intersection of her personal and political lives, describing herself and Mr. de Blasio as “a very conventional, unconventional couple.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City mayor’s race has failed to attract much attention in the glossy world of national magazines, save for a handful of soft-focus features about Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, who would be the first woman and first openly gay person to run City Hall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/nyregion/09cityroom-deblasio/09cityroom-deblasio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 594, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/nyregion/09cityroom-deblasio/09cityroom-deblasio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 594, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/nyregion/09cityroom-deblasio/09cityroom-deblasio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/nyregion/09cityroom-deblasio/09cityroom-deblasio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/nyregion/09cityroom-deblasio/09cityroom-deblasio-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio’s Wife Gives Candid Interview', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Interview, De Blasio’s Wife Describes Life Changes and an Unconventional Couple ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Essence (Magazine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T13:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92bb477a-7c8a-5574-8900-45e669ff462e', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92bb477a-7c8a-5574-8900-45e669ff462e'}, {'abstract': 'Books to give and to get for Mother’s Day.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/books-to-give-your-mother-and-yourself/', 'snippet': 'Books to give and to get for Mother’s Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Memoirs. Cookbooks. Novels. Memoir-cookbook-novels. (O.K., I haven’t actually seen one of those. Yet.) Grabby nonfiction for those passionate about everything from eating to Jane Austen. Summer book season is nearly upon us, and that means if you’re book-shopping for your mother, your partner or yourself, your problem won’t be finding something good, but choosing among the options. Here are a few (a very few) of the books I’m sharing with my mom and friends this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Books to Give Your Mother (and Yourself)', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dab66391-8962-5fe7-9215-f39467943cc4', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dab66391-8962-5fe7-9215-f39467943cc4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Missoni’s easily recognizable multicolored knits became an insider status symbol for the ultra-wealthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/fashion/ottavio-missoni-is-dead-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Missoni’s easily recognizable multicolored knits became an insider status symbol for the ultra-wealthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ottavio Missoni, the patriarch of an esteemed Italian fashion house whose outré, multicolored knits and zigzag stitches became an insider status symbol for the ultra-wealthy, died on Thursday at the family’s home in Sumirago, Italy. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/MISSIONI2-obit/MISSIONI2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/world/M