ord_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3dbb0c-fd89-52f5-b53e-224189cedd3c'}, {'abstract': 'Having just returned from a visit to refugee camps in Iraq and Turkey, Marc Hanson, a senior advocate for Refugees International, talks to The Times about what he saw on the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000002216154/syrian-refugee-crisis-growing-.html', 'snippet': 'Having just returned from a visit to refugee camps in Iraq and Turkey, Marc Hanson, a senior advocate for Refugees International, talks to The Times about what he saw on the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having just returned from a visit to refugee camps in Iraq and Turkey, Marc Hanson, a senior advocate for Refugees International, talks to The Times about what he saw on the ground.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/world/video-tc-130509-syria/video-tc-130509-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/world/video-tc-130509-syria/video-tc-130509-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/world/video-tc-130509-syria/video-tc-130509-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/world/video-tc-130509-syria/video-tc-130509-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/world/video-tc-130509-syria/video-tc-130509-syria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Refugee Crisis Growing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Erica Berenstein, Channon Hodge, Pedro Rafael Rosado and Alyssa Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': 'Rafael', 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Alyssa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4a4ec81e-3eea-5887-9e63-f8edbd63f8e4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4a4ec81e-3eea-5887-9e63-f8edbd63f8e4'}, {'abstract': 'A bill pending before the City Council would require co-op board members to sign a statement saying that they did not discriminate on the basis of race and other criteria when turning down an applicant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/nyregion/new-bill-seeks-to-curb-discrimination-by-co-op-boards.html', 'snippet': 'A bill pending before the City Council would require co-op board members to sign a statement saying that they did not discriminate on the basis of race and other criteria when turning down an applicant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Real estate agents in New York City have long complained that co-op boards mistreat potential buyers they do not like. The boards sit on applications and never make a decision. If they turn down an applicant, they never explain why. And sometimes, the agents suspect, rejections are based on an applicant’s race or national origin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposals Seek to Curb Bias by Co-op Boards ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposals Seek to Curb Bias by Co-op Boards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navarro, Mireya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooperatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8902979f-f113-514f-ac6b-af74f72fd9e7', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8902979f-f113-514f-ac6b-af74f72fd9e7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Harris, a star of the CBS comedy “How I Met Your Mother,” first hosted the Tonys in 2009 and has won two Emmy Awards for his Tony work.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/neil-patrick-harris-to-host-tony-awards-for-a-fourth-time/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Harris, a star of the CBS comedy “How I Met Your Mother,” first hosted the Tonys in 2009 and has won two Emmy Awards for his Tony work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It doesn’t actually say this in the official announcement that the organizers of the Tony Awards sent around on Thursday morning, but you can almost hear them telling it to their industry colleagues at the Oscars: find a host who works, and stick with him. While the choosing of an Academy Awards host is an annual cycle of wondering who’s available to do it; wondering if the person or people chosen are up to the task; and then wondering what went wrong the morning after, the Tonys have dispensed with such uncertainty by naming Neil Patrick Harris to host the awards program for a fourth year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neil Patrick Harris to Host Tony Awards for a Fourth Time', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Neil Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/647f8d0a-be40-5d37-ae36-03c3f38f5e6b', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/647f8d0a-be40-5d37-ae36-03c3f38f5e6b'}, {'abstract': 'Why there’s no poster in your workplace pantry summarizing labor law, including the ability to join a union.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/no-right-to-know-your-rights/', 'snippet': 'Why there’s no poster in your workplace pantry summarizing labor law, including the ability to join a union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a big poster in the pantry on the floor where I work about federal laws in the workplace. There’s information on equal opportunity, health and safety, as well as a notice that my employer can’t require me to take a lie-detector test.\xa0 It would be disturbing if the powers that be at the Times wanted to hook me up to a polygraph, and it’s good to know they would be out of line if they tried.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Right to Know Your Rights', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab46b55-6522-5539-b2b3-87e7b06d876e', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab46b55-6522-5539-b2b3-87e7b06d876e'}, {'abstract': 'While Broadway plays seemed moribund this season, some of the work presented Off Broadway was terrific.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/theater/theaterspecial/charles-isherwood-on-off-broadway-playwriting.html', 'snippet': 'While Broadway plays seemed moribund this season, some of the work presented Off Broadway was terrific.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season just concluded was a terrific, even inspiring one for new American playwriting. But if you confined your theatergoing to Broadway, you really wouldn’t know it. Actually if you only ventured north of 42nd Street come curtain time, you would be more likely to draw precisely the opposite conclusion: that American playwriting was moribund, consisting primarily of empty vessels that had somehow been floated onto the city’s big stages by the presence of name-brand actors. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12Isherwood3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12Isherwood3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12Isherwood3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12Isherwood3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1630, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12ISHERWOOD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12ISHERWOOD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/arts/12ISHERWOOD3/12ISHERWOOD3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Year, Off Broadway Dug Deeper', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Year, Off Broadway Dug Deeper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5be3928c-1e5b-57aa-986c-fc15c74cd4ea', 'word_count': 1234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5be3928c-1e5b-57aa-986c-fc15c74cd4ea'}, {'abstract': 'Mother’s Day is increasingly an anachronism, in one mother’s opinion.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/why-im-sort-of-ignoring-mothers-day/', 'snippet': 'Mother’s Day is increasingly an anachronism, in one mother’s opinion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About this time, many spouses and children, including those who are grown, are hurrying to buy or create a gift for Mother’s Day.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I’m (Sort of) Ignoring Mother’s Day', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ignoring Mother’s Day, Sort Of', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T14:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc7f86af-2e3d-5af0-be8a-a1ab88e717f6', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc7f86af-2e3d-5af0-be8a-a1ab88e717f6'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/the-gun-report-may-9-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of today’s shootings involve men who allegedly gunned down their wives and other family members. In fact, many shootings covered in our daily report are domestic. This sad fact has apparently not gone unnoticed by Zombie Industries, an N.R.A. convention vendor famous for marketing a target that resembles President Obama. The company is under fire this week for marketing a mannequin shooting target in the likeness of a bleeding woman. Dubbed “The Ex,” the blond mannequin is clad in a tight white shirt and violet bra and actually bleeds fake blood when shot. After an outcry, Amazon just yesterday stopped selling it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 9, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank'