 think to charge for next, Frontier Airlines has an answer that is threefold: nonalcoholic drinks, carry-ons and using Expedia.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/bottled-water-its-not-free/', 'snippet': 'For airline passengers who wonder what carriers will think to charge for next, Frontier Airlines has an answer that is threefold: nonalcoholic drinks, carry-ons and using Expedia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For airline passengers who wonder what carriers will think to charge for next, Frontier Airlines has an answer that is threefold: nonalcoholic drinks, carry-ons and using Expedia. Soda, coffee, tea and juice will soon cost $1.99 for basic- and economy-fare ticket holders. Water in a glass will be free, but not bottled water. Some members of Frontier’s frequent-flier program are exempt from the fee, which was announced in conjunction with a $25 to $100 fee to stow carry-ons for basic passengers who booked their ticket through a third-party site. The fees are expected to take effect this summer.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bottled Water? It’s Not Free', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airlines: Bottled Water? It’s Not Free', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frontier Airlines Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T17:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5758513-9f3e-5d8f-acb7-93f3a5826b81', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5758513-9f3e-5d8f-acb7-93f3