 on Thursday show why the company covets Sprint. But the poor earnings — net income dropped 40 percent — also show why Sprint shareholders should be skeptical of Dish’s offer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dish’s Results Hint at Trouble for Sprint Bid', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dish Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SOFTBANK Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:16:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00bc9071-46bf-5b26-9fb7-29de5bd5884f', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00bc9071-46bf-5b26-9fb7-29de5bd5884f'}, {'abstract': 'A mother-in-law’s odd request; tattoo etiquette; peacemaker dos and don’ts; and pleading the vanity defense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/fashion/social-qs-what-gives.html', 'snippet': 'A mother-in-law’s odd request; tattoo etiquette; peacemaker dos and don’ts; and pleading the vanity defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years ago, my mother-in-law gave me a large stainless steel roasting pan at my bridal shower. I thanked her in person and wrote her a note. I like having it. It’s much nicer than my other kitchenware, but I’ve hardly used it because I rarely cook for a crowd. Over the years, she has asked about it frequently: Am I using it? How often? Last year, she asked for it back. I told her she could borrow it. Now she’s sent me a text message asking if she can buy it back. But it was a gift. What should I do? Should I stop accepting gifts from her? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Gives, Mom?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Gives, Mom?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:24:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/da345ca1-6b1b-51dd-90ec-a7e3f7cc52f7', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da345ca1-6b1b-51dd-90ec-a7e3f7cc52f7'}, {'abstract': 'Sir Harold Evans (otherwise known as Harry) has spent his life around words — reporting, editing and writing books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/books/review/up-front.html', 'snippet': 'Sir Harold Evans (otherwise known as Harry) has spent his life around words — reporting, editing and writing books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sir Harold Evans (otherwise known as Harry) has spent his life around words — reporting, editing and writing books. Born in Manchester, England, in 1928, he began his career as a journalist when he was only 16, rising rapidly through the years and accumulating honors as he went. He was the editor of The Sunday Times of London from 1967 to 1981, moved to the United States in 1984 and became — to mention only a few of his positions — editorial director of U.S. News and World Report, president of Random House and founding editor of Condé Nast Traveler. In 2001, British journalists voted him the all-time greatest British newspaper editor. He was knighted in 2004.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-Upfront/0512-bks-Upfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 569, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-Upfront/0512-bks-Upfront-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-Upfront/0512-bks-Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-Upfront/0512-bks-Upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-Upfront/0512-bks-Upfront-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Front', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Up Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Harold M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80480ab2-cfff-5f72-a4b1-910b8f8c13e9', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80480ab2-cfff-5f72-a4b1-910b8f8c13e9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Khan’s speech took advantage of a final opportunity to campaign before Pakistan’s general elections on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/imran-khan-gives-speech-from-hospital-as-pakistan-vote-nears/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Khan’s speech took advantage of a final opportunity to campaign before Pakistan’s general elections on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imran Khan, who was rushed to the hospital this week after falling from a forklift during an election event, addressed supporters of his party at a rally on Thursday via video link from his hospital bed, taking advantage of a final opportunity to campaign before Pakistan’s general elections on Saturday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imran Khan Gives Speech From Hospital as Pakistan Vote Nears', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilani, Yousaf Raza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Imran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rafiq, Arif', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:29:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261cf04e-84a7-5baa-baa8-1f2fd2d6d1ef', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261cf04e-84a7-5baa-baa8-1f2fd2d6d1ef'}, {'abstract': 'Two new books take the reader back to the complicated web of events leading up to World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/books/review/the-sleepwalkers-and-july-1914.html', 'snippet': 'Two new books take the reader back to the complicated web of events leading up to World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody at the time called the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo on June 28, 1914, “a shot heard round the world.” The phrase, filched from Ralph Waldo Emerson’s “Concord Hymn,” epitomizes a judgment that crystallized only as the horrendous sequels played out. Some parts of the international community weren’t listening at all. America was serene in its isolation and prosperity. “To the world, or to a nation,” The Grand Forks Herald in North Dakota declared, “an archduke more or less makes little difference.” President Wilson, pacing the lonely corridors of the White House, was distraught over the first lady’s failing struggle for life. Paris was engrossed in a murder trial brimming with sex and political scandal. London was too obsessed with Irish home rule to sustain attention until closer to midnight.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/books/review/0512-bks-EVANS/0512-bks-EVANS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Brink', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Brink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMeekin, Sean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harold Evans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harold', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Evans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b17b839-4a72-59ad-b9b9-3c8ca6887140', 'word_count': 1702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b17b839-4a72-59ad-b9b9-3c8ca6887140'}, {'abstract': 'These last-minute Mother’s Day gifts will have mom patting herself on the back for raising you so well.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/market-report-things-mom-wants-but-doesnt-know-it-yet/', 'snippet': 'These last-minute Mother’s Day gifts will have mom patting herself on the back for raising you so well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still in search of a memorable Mother’s Day gift? Keep it personal with customized and indulgent presents that are just for her. From a bespoke jewelry box to monthly floral deliveries, these thoughtful treasures will have Mom patting herself on the back for raising you so well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Things Mom Wants But Doesn’t Know It Yet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T19:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f410df3-f435-55fa-b63c-d83c54bd1426', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f410df3-f435-55fa-b63c-d83c54bd1426'}, {'abstract': 'Ottavio Missoni, an Italian track star, and his young bride, Rosita, created the Missoni label in the 1950s. Here are some archival runway looks throughout the years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/09/fashion/missonilegacy.html', 'snippet': 'Ottavio Missoni, an Italian track star, and his young bride, Rosita, created the Missoni label in the 1950s. Here are some archival runway looks throughout the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ottavio Missoni, an Italian track star, and his young bride, Rosita, created the Missoni label in the 1950s. Here are some archival runway looks throughout the years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/fashion/missonilegacy-slide-O0RP/missonileg