 6, with arrangements by Mark Kibble, has been known for its rare harmonic sophistication, crisp rhythmic brio and richly emulsified vocal mixture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/take-6-at-the-blue-note.html', 'snippet': 'Take 6, with arrangements by Mark Kibble, has been known for its rare harmonic sophistication, crisp rhythmic brio and richly emulsified vocal mixture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are three main reasons Take 6, the pop-gospel a cappella group, has thrived as long as it has, and they all factored in an encore at the Blue Note on Wednesday night. That song, capping off a sold-out first set, was the spiritual “Mary Don’t You Weep,” performed in a near facsimile of the version that first appeared (as the track “Mary”) on the group’s self-titled debut album 25 years ago. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10TAKE_SPAN/TAKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10TAKE_SPAN/TAKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10TAKE_SPAN/TAKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10TAKE_SPAN/TAKE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10TAKE_SPAN/TAKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbn