Library’s flagship Fifth Avenue building on Wednesday, protesting the library’s renovation plans, the library’s trustees were inside deciding to make the first public expenditure on that plan: $9 million for the project’s architect, Norman Foster. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Public Library to Begin Spending City Funds on Renovation', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Library Moves Ahead With Its Renovation Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Norman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T21:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/843990b2-3f05-5a09-a629-19992291db7f', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/843990b2-3f05-5a09-a629-19992291db7f'}, {'abstract': 'Led by JoAnn Falletta, the Buffalo Philharmonic Orchestra paired two works at Carnegie Hall that showed contrasting facets of life and art in the Soviet Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/buffalo-philharmonic-orchestra-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Led by JoAnn Falletta, the Buffalo Philharmonic Orchestra paired two works at Carnegie Hall that showed contrasting facets of life and art in the Soviet Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any politician or public figure who ever cited elitism as a reason to brush off supporting the local orchestra would have done well to attend a concert by the Buffalo Philharmonic Orchestra at Carnegie Hall on Wednesday night. The event was part of Spring for Music, a laudable series that has brought some of America’s most ambitious regional orchestras to New York City with their most inventive programs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUFFALT_SPAN/10BUFFALT_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Lands of Soviets, Exploring the Mystic', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 