th artificial light everywhere, “we do not have any night in our modern life,” he said in an interview in 2011. “But I think our body and our souls desire night, and I give this in my art.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Darkness, With Enlightenment in Mind', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using Darkness, With Enlightenment in Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haas, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sympho Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f426f063-fdcb-5e4c-9109-7437f7ec35c5', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f426f063-fdcb-5e4c-9109-7437f7ec35c5'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to indie rock, pop, R&B, folk and hip-hop performances in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/pop-and-rock-listings-for-may-10-16.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to indie rock, pop, R&B, folk and hip-hop performances in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pop', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop and Rock Listings for May 10-16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e2b99e-1ce1-5a8d-86cc-076258bd218e', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94e2b99e-1ce1-5a8d-86cc-076258bd218e'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamin Beilman, a rising 21-year-old, performed chamber works from several masters at Merkin Concert Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/benjamin-beilman-at-merkin-concert-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Benjamin Beilman, a rising 21-year-old, performed chamber works from several masters at Merkin Concert Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In college I used to drive a matchbox-size Volkswagen Polo with, according to the manual, a maximum speed of 142 kilometers (about 88 miles) per hour. But on empty stretches of a speed-limit-free German autobahn, I would floor the gas pedal until the needle climbed past 160 kilometers, and the car shook so hard that the keys jingled in the ignition, and the cassette threatened to pop out of the stereo. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Youthful Charisma Unleashed, Violin in Hand', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Youthful Charisma Unleashed, Violin in Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beilman, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:09:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/494f8620-d65d-544c-b560-27e66bbdce3c', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/494f8620-d65d-544c-b560-27e66bbdce3c'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibition by Los Carpinteros centers on a remarkable installation in which a traditional dance processional is performed entirely backwards.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/on-view-a-cuban-art-collectives-revelations-in-reverse/', 'snippet': 'A new exhibition by Los Carpinteros centers on a remarkable installation in which a traditional dance processional is performed entirely backwards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the early 1990s, the Cuban art collective Los Carpinteros has been creating elegant sculptures, drawings and installations that engage the public with a mix of wry humor and political resonance. For last year’s Havana Biennial, the artists directed a film called “Conga Irreversible,” in which 100 performers enacted a traditional Cuban comparsa — a ceremonial procession — down Havana’s historic Paseo del Prado, entirely in reverse. Marco Castillo, one of the group’s founders, compared the experience to directing an opera. “An original score was composed,” he recalled. “All of the costumes were custom designed.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cuban Art Collective’s Revelations in Reverse', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Bellman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8764262-44ae-54ec-ab86-aca328626ca2', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8764262-44ae-54ec-ab86-aca328626ca2'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/jazz-listings-for-may-10-16.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jazz', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Listings for May 10-16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/11e295f5-5a24-589b-b6e8-8bc533e826e9', 'word_count': 2590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11e295f5-5a24-589b-b6e8-8bc533e826e9'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to performances of classical music in New York and the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/music/opera-and-classical-music-listings-for-may-10-16.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to performances of classical music in New York and the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classical', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opera and Classical Music Listings for May 10-16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cc5f0f4-9445-5764-8b12-26fe56177128', '