'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/television/merrill-brockway-producer-of-tvs-dance-in-america-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Brockway, who was also a director, brought high art to millions of Americans though the PBS series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Merrill Brockway, a director and producer who brought high art to millions of Americans by presenting many of the 20th century’s greatest dancers and choreographers on the PBS television series “Dance in America,” died on May 2 in Santa Fe, N.M. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 954, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 954, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit/SUB-BROCKWAY-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merrill Brockway, Producer of TV’s ‘Dance in America,’ Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merrill Brockway, 90, PBS Producer, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brockway, Merrill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Julie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dance in America (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9f0d334-4899-507d-bbeb-f6290d191155', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9f0d334-4899-507d-bbeb-f6290d191155'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McKissack, with his wife, Patricia, wrote over 100 children’s books about African-American history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/books/fredrick-l-mckissack-childrens-book-author-dies-at-73.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. McKissack, with his wife, Patricia, wrote over 100 children’s books about African-American history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fredrick L. McKissack, who quit a career in construction to join his wife in writing more than 100 children’s books about African-American history, a piece of which his family owned as distinguished builders and architects, died on April 28 in Chesterfield, Mo., a St. Louis suburb. He was 73.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 868}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/MCKISSACK-obit/MCKISSACK-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fredrick L. McKissack, 73, Children’s Book Author, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fredrick L. McKissack, 73, Author of Children’s Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKissack, Fredrick L (1939-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKissack, Patricia C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e9d6f1a-1f9b-59e9-8f86-ffb85be79450', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e9d6f1a-1f9b-59e9-8f86-ffb85be79450'}, {'abstract': 'Like modern-day photo booths, cartes de visites in the mid-1800s allowed people to be playful with the camera.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/back-to-the-future-portraiture/', 'snippet': 'Like modern-day photo booths, cartes de visites in the mid-1800s allowed people to be playful with the camera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, I came across a very old photograph on Facebook that seemed to be a formal portrait . . . of someone’s back. Intrigued, I tracked down the owner of the image, Paul Frecker, who runs a Web site called the Library of Nineteenth-Century Photography. A Londoner, Frecker is a former fashion stylist who used to work for magazines like The Face and i-D in the 1980s, and then on music videos and commercials in the 1990s. In 2001, he stumbled on an album of carte de visites in an antiques store, and soon after that he gave up styling for collecting and trading photographs from that era. Some of his favorite images in his collection, he says, are his 60 or so “back to camera” carte de visites, small, mounted photographs — mostly portraits — that became popular in the second half of the 19th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to the Future Portraiture', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T22:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacey Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92d589a0-ac37-5392-838c-57ffc3bb15c6', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92d589a0-ac37-5392-838c-57ffc3bb15c6'}, {'abstract': 'A new lawsuit was filed last week that challenges the authenticity of a painting sold by the former Knoedler & Company gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/sixth-suit-filed-by-client-against-former-knoedler-gallery/', 'snippet': 'A new lawsuit was filed last week that challenges the authenticity of a painting sold by the former Knoedler & Company gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The once-celebrated Knoedler & Company gallery has been closed for more than a year and a half but the lawsuits keep coming. Last week, the philanthropist and former ambassador to Romania, Nicholas F. Taubman, became the sixth former client to sue the gallery in federal court in Manhattan, charging that Knoedler’s former director Ann Freedman duped him into buying a fake painting by Clyfford Still for $4.3 million in 2005. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sixth Suit Filed by Client Against Former Knoedler Gallery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knoedler & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T23:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f04536-3b6e-54c6-9c97-424a7b334461', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f04536-3b6e-54c6-9c97-424a7b334461'}, {'abstract': 'Trend-obsessed Montrealers are now strolling Saint-Henri’s once-sleepy sidewalks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/12/travel/20130512-SURFACING.html', 'snippet': 'Trend-obsessed Montrealers are now strolling Saint-Henri’s once-sleepy sidewalks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trend-obsessed Montrealers are now strolling Saint-Henri’s once-sleepy sidewalks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/travel/20130512-SURFACING-slide-C5P3/20130512-SURFACING-slide-C5P3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/travel/20130512-SURFACING-slide-C5P3/20130512-SURFACING-slide-C5P3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/tr