ject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-09T23:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/071e5820-1f47-50b8-aa3e-9847d49abf81', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/071e5820-1f47-50b8-aa3e-9847d49abf81'}, {'abstract': 'Laurie Anderson is the curator for an installment of Synth Nights at the Kitchen, featuring Yuka C. Honda, late of Cibo Matto, and Nels Cline of Wilco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/nyregion/electronic-music-at-the-kitchen-and-art-in-the-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'Laurie Anderson is the curator for an installment of Synth Nights at the Kitchen, featuring Yuka C. Honda, late of Cibo Matto, and Nels Cline of Wilco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser can’t leave home these days without encountering the AutoTuned pipes of one pop star or another. But while AutoTune’s vocal effect may seem like just the latest pop music craze, historians of electronic music point out its distinguished antecedents, in, say, Elvis Presley’s slapback echo, Peter Frampton’s talk box, or the vocoder used by Laurie Anderson in her unlikely 1981 pop hit, “O Superman.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electronic Music in Chelsea', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kitchen, The (Manhattan, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, LAURIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major'