t': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9388ce50-0476-5e46-b9ff-0d6daac5a68f'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court dominated by conservative judges rules against a requirement that employers post notices about union rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/opinion/the-nlrbs-contested-poster.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court dominated by conservative judges rules against a requirement that employers post notices about union rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subject of the latest outrageous ruling by the United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit is an 11-by-17-inch poster. The National Labor Relations Board requires nearly six million private employers to display the poster, which informs employees of their right to join or form a union or to take action together to improve their working conditions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The N.L.R.B.’s Contested Poster', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The N.L.R.B.&#8217;s Contested Poster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T01:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/55d29840-60f7-59d1-8bce-43614b3c3e01', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55d29840-60f7-59d1-8bce-43614b3c3e01'}, {'abstract': 'While they focus on the attack that killed four Americans in September, Libya is unraveling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/opinion/the-republicans-benghazi-obsession.html', 'snippet': 'While they focus on the attack that killed four Americans in September, Libya is unraveling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Wednesday’s hearing on the attack in Benghazi, Libya, Republicans in Congress promised explosive new details about the administration’s mishandling of the episode. Instead, the hearing showed, yet again, that sober fact-finding is not their mission. Common sense and good judgment have long given way to conspiracy-mongering and a relentless effort to discredit President Obama and former Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republicans’ Benghazi Obsession', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Republicans&#8217; Benghazi Obsession', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, Gregory N', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}