ore at the tournament since 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — Tiger Woods had not hit a shot and he was nine strokes behind the first-round leader at the Players Championship. Roberto Castro finished his round of nine-under 63, which tied the course record, before Woods recorded a stroke in his round of 67, his lowest score here since the final day in 2007.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woods Was Behind Before He Even Started', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Players Championship (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T02:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b50c5199-dbce-54eb-8fb6-133cc6023bcb', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b50c5199-dbce-54eb-8fb6-133cc6023bcb'}, {'abstract': '“Bunty Berman Presents ...,” about a financially beleaguered Bombay movie producer trying to scrape together the money and momentum for a comeback, provides one of the immortal lessons of showbiz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/theater/reviews/bunty-berman-presents-at-acorn-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Bunty Berman Presents ...,” about a financially beleaguered Bombay movie producer trying to scrape together the money and momentum for a comeback, provides one of the immortal lessons of showbiz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though it sounds as if it should be a hoot, “Bunty Berman Presents ...” is mostly only a whimper. Watching the New Group’s amiable but listless musical sendup of Indian moviemaking, which opened on Thursday night at the Acorn Theater, you can discern the reproachful outlines of the bigger, brasher and more satisfyingly outrageous show it might have been.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10BUNTY_SPAN/BUNTY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bollywood Without the Happy Ending', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bollywood Without The Happy Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 