 of musical theater, centers on a washed-up, alcoholic Broadway producer and a Mafia don to whom he owes money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/movies/how-sweet-it-is-directed-by-brian-herzlinger.html', 'snippet': '“How Sweet It Is,” an ode to the healing powers of musical theater, centers on a washed-up, alcoholic Broadway producer and a Mafia don to whom he owes money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Herzlinger’s “How Sweet It Is,” an ode to the healing powers of musical theater, misfires so badly at the beginning that it takes a while to notice when it goes from godawful to sweetly awful. Mr. Herzlinger, who wrote the script with Jay Black, comes out swinging, with cut-rate gags and unpleasant clichés, not to mention the treacly number that plays over the opening credits. (Sample lyric: “We still have a song to sing.”) It all but announces: Adjust your credibility meter and expectations way down.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN/10RDP_HOWSWEET_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N