': 'A Tunisian man has been accused of seeking to develop a terrorist network in the United States and of proposing to poison the water or air to kill up to 100,000 people, federal prosecutors said in court papers unsealed on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisian Is Accused of Proposing Contamination of Water or Air in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisian Is Accused of Proposing Contamination of Water or Air in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abassi, Ahmed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T02:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dbcacca-80d0-531e-9b2c-1ae96aa178cf', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dbcacca-80d0-531e-9b2c-1ae96aa178cf'}, {'abstract': 'In “No One Lives,” a gang of hillbillies attacks a stranger, who proves not to be an easy mark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/movies/no-one-lives-by-ryuhei-kitamura.html', 'snippet': 'In “No One Lives,” a gang of hillbillies attacks a stranger, who proves not to be an easy mark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Utterly mad yet improbably fascinating, Ryuhei Kitamura’s “No One Lives” camouflages an oddly compelling central idea with the trashy trappings of the low-budget slasher movie. The expectations raised by the first 20 minutes, however, make it a