cle/93a5bde9-564b-59aa-bee6-4fbd752d291e'}, {'abstract': 'As many as one third of all airline passengers say they have accidentally failed to turn off an electronic device during takeoff and landing, despite the admonition to do so, according to a study released on Thursday by two industry groups.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/09/30-percent-of-passengers-accidentally-leave-a-device-on-during-flight/', 'snippet': 'As many as one third of all airline passengers say they have accidentally failed to turn off an electronic device during takeoff and landing, despite the admonition to do so, according to a study released on Thursday by two industry groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take a guess at how many people actually fail to turn off their gadgets during takeoff and landing of a flight. Ten percent? No, that’s too low. Twenty percent? Still too low.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/technology/bits-flight/bits-flight-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/technology/bits-flight/bits-flight-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/technology/bits-flight/bits-flight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/technology/bits-flight/bits-flight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/technology/bits-flight/bits-flight-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Air Passengers Never Turn Off Electronics, Survey Finds', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foxx, Anthony R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huerta, Michael P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airline Passenger Experience Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Electronics Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T03:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f3dfba-9382-5f3d-b88f-0c197477fe99', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f3dfba-9382-5f3d-b88f-0c197477fe99'}, {'abstract': 'Downloadable files that can be used to make a gun with a 3-D printer were removed after the State Department said that posting the files may violate arms-exporting regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/us/texas-web-site-removes-do-it-yourself-gun-plans.html', 'snippet': 'Downloadable files that can be used to make a gun with a 3-D printer were removed after the State Department said that posting the files may violate arms-exporting regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Web site run by a Texas law student has removed downloadable design files that can be used to make a gun with a 3-D printer after the State Department said that posting the files may violate arms-exporting regulations. In a letter to the student, Cody Wilson, a department official wrote that by posting the files, the site, defcad.org, may have released “technical data” without authorization. The files, for a simple gun called the Liberator, were posted this week along with a video showing the weapon, which is largely made of plastic, being fired. Mr. Wilson, who had earlier used 3-D printers to make parts of assault rifles, said that he would try to claim an exemption for the regulations because on the Internet the files would be in the public domain. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Web Site Removes Do-It-Yourself Gun Plans', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Web Site Removes Do-It-Yourself Gun Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Cody Rutledge (1988- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T03:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cb8aa08-6b5f-5104-92ab-4e8b737fe545', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cb8