': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75257046-f97e-5c60-b73e-9f3b9b936898', 'word_count': 2374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75257046-f97e-5c60-b73e-9f3b9b936898'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:45 P.M. (MoreMax) RUBY SPARKS (2012) Zoe Kazan wrote and stars in this variation on the Pygmalion myth as Ruby, a smart, saucy, 26-year-old redhead from Dayton, Ohio, who magically appears in Los Angeles seemingly without much control over her emotions. Paul Dano (above, with Ms. Kazan), Ms. Kazan’s real-life partner, is Calvin, a literary whiz kid turned blocked writer who breathes life into this figment of his imagination, and then directs her every move. The cast is filled out by Chris Messina as Calvin’s worried older brother, Harry, who finally confirms to Calvin — now concerned that he has gone crazy — that Ruby is not a hallucination. Annette Bening is the brothers’ mother, living a hippie life in Big Sur, Calif., with her lover (Antonio Banderas) and intent on seeing her youngest son happy, however odd the arrangement. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T05:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_o