subject', 'value': 'Eyeglasses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/cba3290e-5b1c-56c1-91f1-0e0ed7fc549a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/cba3290e-5b1c-56c1-91f1-0e0ed7fc549a'}, {'abstract': 'The president of Planned Parenthood says that some members of Congress “forget that women are part of the equation.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/magazine/what-cecile-richards-has-learned-from-todd-akin.html', 'snippet': 'The president of Planned Parenthood says that some members of Congress “forget that women are part of the equation.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, for only the second time in history, Planned Parenthood endorsed a presidential candidate in Barack Obama. Do you think this resulted in Congress’s efforts in 2011 to defund the organization?  Not at all. In 2010, the Tea Party came after everything — Roe, birth control, they tried to overturn the family-planning law that Nixon signed into law and Planned Parenthood too. We were just part of a much bigger effort to repeal decades of progress on women’s health and rights.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12talk/mag-12Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 397, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12talk/mag-12Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 519, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url