untouchable cultural icons the way we do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Out in Malibu, the billionaire’s gardener has nicked a bronze with his weed whacker. In Echo Park, the Lady of the Lake is missing her benediction hand. Somewhere in Pasadena, a stone female nude has mysteriously sprouted pubic hair, accomplished with what appears to be hide glue and combings from an auburn Irish setter. Who knows how long it was there? No matter. A few brush strokes with warm distilled water, and she is returned to immodesty once more.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12lives/mag-12Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 510, 'width': 229, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12lives/mag-12Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 510, 'width': 229, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12lives/mag-12Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12lives/mag-12Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12lives/mag-12Lives-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of an Art Conservator’s Sidekick', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Object Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae5e1d1-61a2-59d8-b44c-16b99a993b6b', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae5e1d1-61a2-59d8-b44c-16b99a993b6b'}, {'abstract': 'The premiere of a new music video by Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/magazine/100000002216681/exclusive-preview-omds-dresden.html', 'snippet': 'The premiere of a new music video by Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The premiere of a new music video by Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/video-omd-dresden/video-omd-dresden-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/video-omd-dresden/video-omd-dresden-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/video-omd-dresden/video-omd-dresden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/video-omd-dresden/video-omd-dresden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/video-omd-dresden/video-omd-dresden-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exclusive Premiere: O.M.D.’s ‘Dresden’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark (Music Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'BMG Rights Management (UK) Ltd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bmg', 'middlename': 'Rights', 'lastname': 'Management', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5bf4b785-6057-5233-9316-09517a7714c7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5bf4b785-6057-5233-9316-09517a7714c7'}, {'abstract': 'From suitcase-size splotches of green and brown to a “Harry Potter” cloak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/magazine/who-made-that-digital-camouflage.html', 'snippet': 'From suitcase-size splotches of green and brown to a “Harry Potter” cloak.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I was basically designated the weird-projects officer,” says Timothy O’Neill, who worked with an Army team to improve the camouflage painted on tanks in the early 1970s. At the time, the military covered its vehicles with suitcase-size splotches of green and brown. The pattern could trick the eye at a distance, but it didn’t work well at close range. O’Neill set out to find a better solution. At the Aberdeen Proving Ground, a test site in Maryland, he and his team put an armored personnel carrier out in a field and painted it with two-inch squares in woodland colors. From far away, the flecks seemed to coalesce into a large pattern, so that the vehicle blended with the trees behind it. The tiny squares also mimicked close-up details: individual leaves, tufts of grass and shadows on a branch. O’Neill’s tests showed that this digital camouflage — as it would later be called — fooled the eye into seeing tank and landscape as one.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 241, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 241}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 241, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 241, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12wmt/12wmt-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Digital Camouflage?', 'kicker': 'Innovation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Digital Camouflage)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Pagan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camouflage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b516862f-00fe-5727-95c5-ec2db0c2bc7f', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b516862f-00fe-5727-95c5-ec2db0c2bc7f'}, {'abstract': 'Thirty-five years ago, Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark was certain that the overthrow of the electric guitar was imminent. They still haven’t given up hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/magazine/omds-plot-against-rock.html', 'snippet': 'Thirty-five years ago, Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark was certain that the overthrow of the electric guitar was imminent. They still haven’t given up hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy McCluskey and Paul Humphreys have devoted much of their artistic lives to a war on rock nostalgia, but when you’re showing a first-time visitor around Liverpool, what can you do? You’re obliged to end up at the Cavern Club, a not-completely-uncharming replica of the vaulted, subterranean bar where the pre-Fab Four honed their fabulousness.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/magazine/12omd/mag-12OMD-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'le