 to improve your fitness levels.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/app-smart-extra-more-ways-to-stay-fit/', 'snippet': 'With summer approaching, it’s the perfect time to improve your fitness levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week I wrote about apps that can take the place, at least in part, of a personal trainer. These fitness apps can coach and provide encouragement as you try to get fit. With summer fast approaching, now may be a great moment to take advantage of these apps to improve your overall fitness, lose some weight or tone your muscles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: More Ways to Stay Fit', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physical Education and Training', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9369830-a4d5-5d39-9a6b-7c445ed0d1b7', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9369830-a4d5-5d39-9a6b-7c445ed0d1b7'}, {'abstract': 'An introduction to Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/the-omg-who-is-o-m-d-playlist/', 'snippet': 'An introduction to Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a teenager, there was nothing in the world I liked half as much as my Walkman. I listened to it compulsively, like an addict, blasting music into my head and causing major damage to my ears. As mind-blowingly wonderful as it is to now carry 25,000 songs in my pocket, the Walkman forced a deeper engagement with the music you loved. Nobody carried around lots of cassettes. Maybe one or two extra. And if you were like me, you often kept the same one in there for weeks at a time, creating an intimacy that seems quaint now. Fast-forwarding and rewinding were a drag, so you tended to listen through entire albums, sometimes falling in love with songs you hated on first listen. This was commitment. The melodies and lyrics on these albums in particular — “Hatful of Hollow,” by the Smiths; “Murmur,” by R.E.M.; “Let It Be,” by the Replacements; “Head on the Door,” by the Cure; and “Architecture & Morality,” by Orchestral Manoeuvres in the Dark — are practically etched on the inside of my skull.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1025, 'width': 1464, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/09/magazine/09-omd/09-omd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The “OMG, Who Is O.M.D.?” Playlist', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc1234d6-e13b-55c0-af6a-dcee4cb515d3', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc1234d6-e13b-55c0-af6a-dcee4cb515d3'}, {'abstract': 'Carl C. Icahn and Southeastern Asset Management are preparing a rival bid for Dell. | California’s attorney general has accused JPMorgan Chase of debt collection abuses. | SAC Capital Advisors has extended a deadline for investors to decide whether to withdraw money. | The Securities and Exchange Commission appears to have softened its tone in a settlement with Philip A. Falcone.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/a-fresh-challenge-to-dell-buyout/', 'snippet': 'Carl C. Icahn and Southeastern Asset Management are preparing a rival bid for Dell. | California’s attorney general has accused JPMorgan Chase of debt collection abuses. | SAC Capital Advisors has extended a deadline for investors to decide whethe...', 'lead_paragraph': 'ICAHN AND SOUTHEASTERN READY RIVAL BID FOR DELL \xa0|\xa0 The billionaire Carl C. Icahn and Southeastern Asset Management, two of the biggest shareholders of Dell, plan to bid for the computer maker in a last-ditch effort to stop what they call “the great giveaway,” the $24.4 billion management buyout led by Michael S. Dell, the company’s founder, and the private equity firm Silver Lake, Andrew Ross Sorkin and Michael J. de la Merced report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Challenge to Dell Buyout', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T11:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b59ec746-c8d6-5e5d-9f92-912045e42508', 'word_count': 1645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b59ec746-c8d6-5e5d-9f92-912045e42508'}, {'abstract': 'If its slate of directors is approved next week, Hess will appoint John Krenicki, a former vice chairman of General Electric, as its nonexecutive chairman, while John B. Hess will remain chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/hess-to-split-chairman-and-c-e-o-jobs/', 'snippet': 'If its slate of directors is approved next week, Hess will appoint John Krenicki, a former vice chairman of General Electric, as its nonexecutive chairman, while John B. Hess will remain chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hess Corporation said on Friday that it planned to separate its chairman and chief executive roles, hoping to blunt a campaign by an activist investor and assuage restive shareholders.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hess to Split Chairman and C.E.O. Jobs',