s from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Owning a Dog Linked to Lower Heart Risk', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T12:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f098e2e-fc9a-5138-b60b-8e6da94b5f84', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f098e2e-fc9a-5138-b60b-8e6da94b5f84'}, {'abstract': '“Andy and His Grandmother,” a new collection from the independent record label Drag City, is culled from more than 82 hours of recordings that Kaufman made in the late 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/album-of-unreleased-andy-kaufman-material-coming-in-july/', 'snippet': '“Andy and His Grandmother,” a new collection from the independent record label Drag City, is culled from more than 82 hours of recordings that Kaufman made in the late 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be just like Andy Kaufman to find a way to keep releasing records long after his death. The pioneering comedian and “Taxi” co-star’s reputation for pranks and provocations was such that, even when he died of lung cancer at age 35 in 1984, some fans believed that this, too, was one of his outrageous acts of fakery. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/arts/kaufman/kaufman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,