}, {'abstract': 'In a question-and-answer exchange, the author of a new report on financial aid describes problems in making college affordable for low-income students, and potential solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/q-a-on-the-shell-game-of-college-aid/', 'snippet': 'In a question-and-answer exchange, the author of a new report on financial aid describes problems in making college affordable for low-income students, and potential solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': '“With their relentless pursuit of prestige and revenue, the nation’s public and private four-year colleges and universities are in danger of shutting down what has long been a pathway to the middle class for low-income and working-class students,” writes Stephen Burd, a senior policy analyst at the New America Foundation, in a new report that’s getting considerable attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. on the ‘Shell Game’ of College Aid', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New America Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T13:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': '