grew from about 19,000 last year to 26,000 this year. Obviously something must be done to reverse that trend but, in the meantime, the federal government could do more to help the victims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does the Pentagon Take Sexual Assault Seriously?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Ruth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pingree, Chellie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T13:03:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fd6685c-2fee-5c88-9be1-f9783f0ba5fb', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fd6685c-2fee-5c88-9be1-f9783f0ba5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Swale possessed the undeniable appeal of the underdog; he was Claiborne’s stand-in for their star, Devil’s Bag, and he shocked many fans with his Kentucky Derby upset over horses like Althea. Swale’s most famous moment, however, was not that Derby win, but his death.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/love-affair-with-swale-extends-well-beyond-his-death/', 'snippet': 'Swale possessed the undeniable appeal of the underdog; he was Claiborne’s stand-in for their star, Devil’s Bag, and he shocked many fans with his Kentucky Derby upset over horses like Althea. Swale’s most famous moment, however, was not that Derby...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1984, I was in the seventh grade, and I fell in love with Swale, who looked very much, I thought, like the picture of the Black Stallion on my copies of those books. I read everything Andrew Beyer and Tony Kornheiser wrote about him in The Washington Post. I cut out photographs from the sports section: Swale standing regally, chin raised, wind ruffling his mane; Swale and his assistant trainer, Mike Griffin, regarding each other with affection over a Pimlico stall door, a list of Preakness winners posted above them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Affair With Swale Extends Well Beyond His Death', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T13:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliza McGraw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGraw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21801062-8616-55f1-baea-e232a6383231', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21801062-8616-55f1-baea-e232a6383231'}, {'abstract': 'And nothing to do with austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/all-about-the-ecb/', 'snippet': 'And nothing to do with austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Weisenthal has a good post going after Roger Altman’s assertion that European austerity was necessary to satisfy the markets. As Paul De Grauwe has been arguing for a while, what has been needed all along to calm the markets isn’t austerity — which doesn’t seem to help at all — but a liquidity backstop from the ECB, which works wonders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All About the ECB', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T13:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bc5c349-e62a-54de-8186-e6e3a2220066', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bc5c349-e62a-54de-8186-e6e3a2220066'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of art collectors in Belgium — especially those favoring Contemporary works — are finding ways to share their collections with the public.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/in-brussels-private-art-collections-with-open-doors/', 'snippet': 'A growing number of art collectors in Belgium — especially those favoring Contemporary works — are finding ways to share their collections with the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you walk into the 1920s-era converted warehouse in central Brussels, you’re confronted with an out-of-the-ordinary greeting: a five-meter-wide red sign stabbed through with knives whose handles spell out “Run Like Hell.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/blogs/10rdv-belgiumart10a/10rdv-belgiumart10a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/blogs/10rdv-belgiumart10a/10rdv-belgiumart10a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption