ion_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1496a37-d412-5d3d-9daf-446c3ae9eac4', 'word_count': 1712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1496a37-d412-5d3d-9daf-446c3ae9eac4'}, {'abstract': 'The new movie of the Fitzgerald book shows Jay Gatsby driving a Duesenberg. Good luck finding a mention of that car in the book.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/gatsby-in-a-duesenberg-more-fiction/', 'snippet': 'The new movie of the Fitzgerald book shows Jay Gatsby driving a Duesenberg. Good luck finding a mention of that car in the book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jay Gatsby, the mysterious title character of F. Scott Fitzgerald’s “The Great Gatsby,” fancied luxury cars, but he would not have been driving a 1929 Duesenberg Model J.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gatsby in a Duesenberg? More Fiction', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gatsby in a Duesenberg? More Fiction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaprio, Leonardo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, F Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luhrmann, Baz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T15:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4add50-bb30-5860-aab4-97966c015bbe', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4add50-bb30-5860-aab4-97966c015bbe'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSE OF STONE: A Memoir of Home, Family, and a Lost Middle East,  by Anthony Shadid. (Mariner/Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $15.95.) In 2006, after years spent covering the Iraq war, Shadid began renovating the abandoned house of his great-grandfather in the Lebanese town of Marjayoun. (A correspondent for The New York Times, Shadid died last year while reporting from Syria.) This elegiac memoir combines stories of Shadid’s struggles with workmen, tales of his ancestors and their world, and reflections on his family’s journey to America.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T15:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f745a07-512c-579e-ae3f-23f8c982432d', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f745a07-512c-579e-ae3f-23f8c982432d'}, {'abstract': 'In its 34th year, the Texas Star Party drew more than 500 amateur astronomers from across the United States and Canada to gaze together into the vast open skies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/us/in-west-texas-a-gathering-to-consider-the-universe.html', 'snippet': 'In its 34th year, the Texas Star Party drew more than 500 amateur astronomers from across the United States and Canada to gaze together into the vast open skies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT DAVIS, Tex. — With a lime-green fleece blanket over his shoulders, Samuel David, 10, of Houston, bounced on his toes as dusk raced over the mountains. Attending his first Texas Star Party this week with his family, Samuel could not wait for a rare phenomenon in a lighted-up, night-denying world — a sky full of nothing but stars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/11/us/11stars-web/11stars-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '