': 'Bucks readers discuss their experience in buying life insurance or annuities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column this week is about the marketing of two straightforward financial products — life insurance and annuities — for their tax benefits. As Paul has written before, the increase in taxes this year is prompting many people to make taxes their priority — it’s determining what to invest in or how to set up their estate or buying life insurance — when taxes should be only one factor in the decision.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Taxes Aren’t the Only Consideration', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANNUITIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T15:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38286222-40ff-53b8-90b8-0f3fa87bd25a', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38286222-40ff-53b8-90b8-0f3fa87bd25a'}, {'abstract': 'James Levine returns to the podium after an extended break caused by back injuries, but questions remain about his role at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/arts/music/james-levine-is-returning-to-lead-the-met-orchestra.html', 'snippet': 'James Levine returns to the podium after an extended break caused by back injuries, but questions remain about his role at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s one week and counting until James Levine’s return to the podium.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 's