istory’s annual spoiler fest at which scientists and anthropologists examine your mysterious objects and tell you what it might be.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/own-a-mysterious-artifact-go-show-it-to-a-scientist/', 'snippet': 'Tomorrow is Identification Day, the American Museum of Natural History’s annual spoiler fest at which scientists and anthropologists examine your mysterious objects and tell you what it might be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life is full of mysteries. Some lives are full of mysterious objects. The necklace-looking thing you found on the beach that looks as if it probably came from an animal or maybe a plant. That rock your grandfather always told you was a meteorite. The dead turtle in a box on your desk — bog turtle or box turtle?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-idday/10cityroom-idday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-idday/10cityroom-idday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 572}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-idday/10cityroom-idday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 977, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-idday/10cityroom-idday-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 977, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-idday/10cityroom-idday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSt