 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wattenberg, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b95f0a1a-40e8-5743-8113-d56540385127', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b95f0a1a-40e8-5743-8113-d56540385127'}, {'abstract': 'Sixteen vintage cars were pulled through Harlem to Grand Central Terminal by two separate locomotives, late Thursday night and into Friday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains.html', 'snippet': 'Sixteen vintage cars were pulled through Harlem to Grand Central Terminal by two separate locomotives, late Thursday night and into Friday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixteen vintage cars were pulled through Harlem to Grand Central Terminal by two separate locomotives, late Thursday night and into Friday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/11trains-slide-4NAX/11trains-slide-4NAX-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Darkness, a Parade on the Rails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:48:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/86dfeda9-9142-5446-8b46-82599ac315b3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/86dfeda9-9142-5446-8b46-82599ac315b3'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark’s recipe can be doubled to feed more.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/pulled-pork-for-crowds-large-or-small/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark’s recipe can be doubled to feed more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s column and video, I give a recipe for a small batch of pulled pork. Instead of the usual 7-pound bone-in hunk of meat, I use a 3-pound chunk. That said, if you want to use the same recipe with the larger cut, you certainly can. Double the spice rub and barbecue sauce, and if you love coleslaw, consider making one and a half times that recipe. You will very likely need to cook the meat longer. Just check it every 30 minutes or so after the four-hour mark, and when it reaches an internal temperature of 200 degrees, it’s done. The recipe for pulled pork is here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pulled Pork, for Crowds Large or Small', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:49:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/134669f5-59a3-5171-9074-82ab11e45099', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/134669f5-59a3-5171-9074-82ab11e45099'}, {'abstract': 'David Hare’s adaptation of Ms. Boo’s award-winning book will be produced by London’s National Theater in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/katherine-boos-beautiful-forevers-headed-to-the-stage/', 'snippet': 'David Hare’s adaptation of Ms. Boo’s award-winning book will be produced by London’s National Theater in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katherine Boo brought the Annawadi slum to vivid life in “Behind the Beautiful Forevers: Life, Death, and Hope in a Mumbai Undercity,” one of the most acclaimed books of 2012. The National Theater in London hopes to do the same in a stage version of the book next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/books/10beautiful-forevers/10beautiful-forevers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 317, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/books/10beautiful-forevers/10beautiful-forevers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 317, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/books/10beautiful-forevers/10beautiful-forevers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/books/10beautiful-forevers/10beautiful-forevers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Katherine Boo’s ‘Beautiful Forevers’ Headed to the Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boo, Katherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hare, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norris, Rufus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Theater Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:50:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebaebc9d-d202-534d-be14-f46c7bf26aad', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebaebc9d-d202-534d-be14-f46c7bf26aad'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of privately owned train cars made their way to Grand Central late Thursday night, though Harlem appeared unmoved.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/a-parade-of-vintage-trains-unnoticed-in-the-harlem-night/', 'snippet': 'A collection of privately owned train cars made their way to Grand Central late Thursday night, though Harlem appeared unmoved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trains lurched through the Harlem darkness, rattling above an all-night pawnshop, a swell of reggaetón music and a man in a headdress, squawking from his bicycle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parade of Vintage Trains, Unnoticed in the Harlem Night', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:52:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5d943a2-6891-5d04-aa16-50af204a53bf', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5d943a2-6891-5d04-aa16-50af204a53bf'}, {'abstract': 'The box numbers from Thursday’s late night screenings indicate a first weekend that could be the most successful in Baz Luhrmann’s directing career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/business/media/great-gatsby-is-poised-for-a-strong-opening-no-thanks-to-critics.html', 'snippet': 'The box numbers from Thursday’s late night screenings indicate a first weekend that could be the most successful in Baz Luhrmann’s directing career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — As very early box-office numbers for “The Great Gatsby” rolled in — a strong $3.25 million from the Thursday late-night shows, Warner Brothers said on Friday morning — it was already becoming clear that the audience has a mind of its own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/business/gatsby-media/gatsby-media-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Great Gatsby’  Is Poised for a  Strong Opening, No Thanks to Critics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luhrmann, Baz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Gatsby (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Media', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454f7faf-2498-5cc2-86c6-faac0f1b6e0f', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454f7faf-2498-5cc2-86c6-faac0f1b6e0f'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/weekend-fare-141/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santa Teresa, a Venezuelan rum producer, will conduct four free tastings of its flagship rum, Santa Teresa 1796, at Union Square Wines and Spirits, 140 Fourth Avenue. The rum will be served neat, on the rocks and in cocktails. The first session is on Friday from 6 to 9 p.m., paired with chocolates for Mother’s Day. The three other sessions are on May 17, 24 and 31.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T18:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10f6b443-8f18-56bd-882b-b262f0feb46e', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10f6b443-8f18-56bd-882b-b262f0feb46e'}, {'abstract': 'If you’ve seen History’s “Counting Cars,” you may be surprised by the list of cars Danny Koker said he would like to have.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/an-eclectic-automotive-wish-list-from-counting-cars/', 'snippet': 'If you’ve seen History’s “Counting Cars,” you may be surprised by the list of cars Danny Koker said he would like to have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve seen “Counting Cars,” the reality show on the A&E Network’s History, you’re used to the sight of Danny Koker, known as the Count, and his best buddy, Kevin Mack, cruising the streets of Las Vegas in search of restoration projects for their Count’s Kustoms shop. They spot old cars and trucks in parking lots, peeking out of garages and sometimes even cruising in the next lane. Some they restore and pass on to new owners whose smiling faces are displayed prominently on the show. Other cars Mr. Koker keeps; he owns at least 58 cars and 10 motorcycles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eclectic Automotive Wish List From ‘Counting Cars’', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Dean', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Presley, Elvis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07bcabc9-8d27-574e-8ac9-1614a1388695', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07bcabc9-8d27-574e-8ac9-1614a1388695'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama told consumers not to be fooled by misinformation and said access to care was a right he would defend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/us/politics/obama-to-makes-new-pitch-on-health-care-law.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama told consumers not to be fooled by misinformation and said access to care was a right he would defend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama came out fighting in defense of his health care law on Friday, saying that he was “110 percent committed” to delivering its benefits on schedule, and that consumers should not be bamboozled by critics spreading misinformation about the law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 