ws, ‘Rock Center’ Is Canceled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rock Center (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T21:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dec63a22-0fd4-515b-a640-5853309aa383', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dec63a22-0fd4-515b-a640-5853309aa383'}, {'abstract': 'The issue of appropriate clothing for girls has been the subject of increasing academic and popular scrutiny, fed by panties printed with “wink wink” or leggings that say “cute butt sweat pants.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/fashion/clothing-straddles-the-line-between-sweet-and-skimpy.html', 'snippet': 'The issue of appropriate clothing for girls has been the subject of increasing academic and popular scrutiny, fed by panties printed with “wink wink” or leggings that say “cute butt sweat pants.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It first happened to me this spring. My daughters, who had just turned 8, came bounding into the room to show off new outfits they were wearing to an extended-family gathering. My eyes bulged. The dresses drooped provocatively off the shoulder and offered other peekaboos of their bodies. Sure, as a parent, I figured I would one day face clothing battles with my children. Politicians aren’t the only ones who draw red lines. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 188}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/fashion/12THISLIFE_SPAN/12THISLIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Line Between Sweet and Skimpy', 'kicker': 'This Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Line Between Sweet and Skimpy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiler, Bruce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T21:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Feiler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/343f46bc-f76c-5123-83d5-d4b54033094d', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/343f46bc-f76c-5123-83d5-d4b54033094d'}, {'abstract': '“The Good Boy,” Michael Bonnabel’s solo show about his experience as a hearing son with deaf parents, is at Abingdon Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/theater/reviews/the-good-boy-from-abingdon-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Good Boy,” Michael Bonnabel’s solo show about his experience as a hearing son with deaf parents, is at Abingdon Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man looks like an aging bachelor bank teller in a 1962 episode of “The Twilight Zone.” Or like the hopelessly square dad in a midcentury sitcom. But Michael Bonnabel — in his suit, narrow tie and eyeglasses — is the son in the Abingdon Theater Company’s production of his autobiographical solo show, “The Good Boy.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/theater/11good/11good-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/theater/11good/11good-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/