ch chanteuse Yvonne Constant, accompanied on piano by Russ Kassoff, sang “Comme d’habitude” in an autobiographical program titled “One of a Kind.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not many people know that the grandiose Sinatra anthem “My Way,” had an earlier life in France under the title “Comme d’habitude” (“As Usual”) whose morose narrator describes a deteriorating relationship that has settled into a chilly routine. Juiced up with new lyrics by Paul Anka, it became the triumphal ego trip we all know and have learned to tolerate. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling Chimps and Brel, in Her Own Way', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recalling Chimps and Brel, in Her Own Trans-Atlantic Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Constant, Yvonne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T22:10:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1b42f98-414b-5dec-82a1-6da7d47df57b', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1b42f98-414b-5dec-82a1-6da7d47df57b'}, {'abstract': 'A class assignment led to Kyle Abrahams’s winning entry in the Worldwide Plays Festival Competition, and it will be performed by professional actors on Saturday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/13-year-old-playwright-awaits-his-big-night/', 'snippet': 'A class assignment led to Kyle Abrahams’s winning entry in the Worldwide Plays Festival Competition, and it will be performed by professional actors on Saturday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kyle Abrahams had never tried to write a play before his drama teacher, John McEneny, required him to try for a middle school class in Brooklyn. Kyle had always liked acting – he recently performed in a production of “Frankenstein.” Now, though, he’d be the one giving other actors instructions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 803}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 968, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/10cityroom-kyle/10cityroom-kyle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '13-Year-Old Playwright Awaits His Big Night', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-10T22:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Hammill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hammill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/177b1441-a8ed-5c17-b987-171dce76b828', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/177b1441-a8ed-5c17-b987-171dce76b828'}, {'abstract': 'A court filing earlier this week detailing Bryant’s prized high school memorabilia is kind of humanizing.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/kobe-bryants-sentimental-shot/', 'snippet': 'A court filing earlier this week detailing Bryant’s prized high school memorabilia is kind of humanizing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday a friend and fan of all Philadelphia sports directed me to a Philly.com story about the former Notre Dame football player Manti Te’o’s “girlfriend” making the Maxim Hot 100; his reaction was basically “Phew, glad the Iggles didn’t draft this guy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156,