 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93fb07a9-6816-54dd-8cdd-c45d0f7dbd2d', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93fb07a9-6816-54dd-8cdd-c45d0f7dbd2d'}, {'abstract': 'More recollections of the late comedian Jonathan Winters.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/missing-jonathan-winters-badly/', 'snippet': 'More recollections of the late comedian Jonathan Winters.', 'lead_paragraph': '(This is the second part of a two-part article.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing: Jonathan Winters. Badly.', 'kicker': 'Dick Cavett', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winters, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T00:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dick Cavett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26b57ef2-2219-5da9-a4ca-8c9bd4aaec61', 'word_count': 1886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26b57ef2-2219-5da9-a4ca-8c9bd4aaec61'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptian activist Ahmed Maher was arrested on accusations of inciting protests in front of the Interior Ministry in March and was transferred to a high-security prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/world/middleeast/prominent-egyptian-activist-ahmed-maher-jailed.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptian activist Ahmed Maher was arrested on accusations of inciting protests in front of the Interior Ministry in March and was transferred to a high-security prison.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A prominent Egyptian activist was jailed Friday on accusations of inciting protests in front of the Interior Ministry in March, state news media said. The activist, Ahmed Maher, was arrested at the Cairo airport upon arriving from abroad and transferred to a high-security prison where he will be held for four days while the accusations are investigated. Mr. Maher is a leader in the April 6 Youth Group that help organize the protests that ousted President Hosni Mubarak in February 2011. He has recently spoken out against President Mohamed Morsi and his allies in the Muslim Brotherhood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Prominent Activist Jailed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Prominent Activist Jailed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Ahmed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T00:35:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bdf47d9-0b14-5a59-8ba2-b648e3aac2ee', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bdf47d9-0b14-5a59-8ba2-b648e3aac2ee'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition under way at Purchase College features four contemporary artists who make use of early images and motifs from Mesoamerica.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/nyregion/a-review-of-pre-columbian-remix-exhibition-at-the-neuberger-museum.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition under way at Purchase College features four contemporary artists who make use of early images and motifs from Mesoamerica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If modern art was characterized by the shock of the new, recent decades have seen an obsession with recycling. History is treated like an archive from which images and objects can be borrowed, appropriated, and repurposed — just like in popular music, where sampling was born, and which is alluded to in the title of “Pre-Columbian Remix: The Art of Enrique Chagoya, Demián Flores, Rubén Ortiz-Torres, and Nadín Ospina” at the Neuberger Museum of Art, Purchase College.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ARTSWE2-SPAN/12ARTSWE2-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ARTSWE2-SPAN/12ARTSWE2-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ARTSWE2-SPAN/12ARTSWE2-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima