in of the unit’s nickname.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samuel Noyes, Mountaineer', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1a101eb-3afe-5903-bf7f-60a5c2493c71', 'word_count': 1423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1a101eb-3afe-5903-bf7f-60a5c2493c71'}, {'abstract': 'Bloomberg News confirmed that reporters for its news service used the the company’s terminals to monitor subscribers’ usage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/business/media/privacy-breach-on-bloombergs-data-terminals.html', 'snippet': 'Bloomberg News confirmed that reporters for its news service used the the company’s terminals to monitor subscribers’ usage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A shudder went through Wall Street on Friday after the revelation that Bloomberg News reporters had extracted subscribers’ private information through the company’s ubiquitous data terminals to break news. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Privacy Breach on Bloomberg’s Data Terminals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privacy Breach On Bloomberg’s Data Terminals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'ra