ited States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yammer', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed38bec-2a88-5095-a68d-efc49569555f', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed38bec-2a88-5095-a68d-efc49569555f'}, {'abstract': 'Five years, five boroughs and five restaurants: A couple’s unusual dining tour is capped with dinner at Alder, the chef Wylie Dufresne’s newest restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/nyregion/at-alder-a-meal-in-borough-no-5-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'Five years, five boroughs and five restaurants: A couple’s unusual dining tour is capped with dinner at Alder, the chef Wylie Dufresne’s newest restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consider the crush of publicity and the lines that have formed on Second Avenue outside Wylie Dufresne’s newest restaurant. Note that Mr. Dufresne and his muttonchops are television celebrities. Add that last week Mr. Dufresne won the James Beard Award for New York’s Best Chef. So how refreshing it was that not everybody in Alder’s rustic-chic dining room on Wednesday was caught up on the place’s reputation. One food-loving couple transplanted from San Diego and Venice (Italy) came for their own adventure: the end of a five-borough birthday tour. They were delightfully unaware of WD-50, Mr. Dufresne’s celebrated flagship. And instead of debating the hype, they reveled in the whimsy of the evening and Alder’s modernist spin on comfort food, savoring their journey as much as the dehydrated pastrami.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12TABLE_SPAN/12TABLE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Meal in Borough No. 5: Manhattan', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Alder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Meal in Borough No. 5: Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Second Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dufresne, Wylie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alder (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41de2d4f-e8cd-5157-bc37-eafd00ef81f1', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41de2d4f-e8cd-5157-bc37-eafd00ef81f1'}, {'abstract': 'While Mark Brooks provided tough love and instruction to a pro who missed the cut at the Players Championship, Sergio Garcia and Tiger Woods took over the tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/sports/golf/former-pga-champion-mark-brooks-caddies-for-j-j-henry.html', 'snippet': 'While Mark Brooks provided tough love and instruction to a pro who missed the cut at the Players Championship, Sergio Garcia and Tiger Woods took over the tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — A seven-time PGA Tour winner missed the Players Championship cut by two strokes without even hitting a shot. Mark Brooks, whose tour victories include one major, the 1996 P.G.A. Championship, caddied for J. J. Henry, who finished at two over, 13 strokes higher than the 36-hole leader, Sergio García. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xl