grams.html', 'snippet': 'The Education Department said Friday that roughly 300 additional students had been wrongly excluded from eligibility in public school gifted programs because of another mistake by the testing company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three weeks after New York City disclosed that thousands of students had been wrongly excluded from eligibility in public school gifted programs, the Education Department said that roughly 300 additional students received incorrect scores because of another mistake by the testing company.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Error Found in Scoring of Test for Gifted Programs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Error Found in Scoring of Test for Gifted Programs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifted Students', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:27:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1174c54f-1130-5589-a01c-08092c9658c5', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1174c54f-1130-5589-a01c-08092c9658c5'}, {'abstract': 'Dennis Rodman told TMZ that he planned to return to North Korea on Aug. 1 to try to free Kenneth Bae, a Korean-American sentenced to 15 years of hard labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/world/asia/rodman-plans-new-north-korea-trip-to-free-american.html', 'snippet': 'Dennis Rodman told TMZ that he planned to return to North Korea on Aug. 1 to try to free Kenneth Bae, a Korean-American sentenced to 15 years of hard labor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis Rodman, the flamboyant former basketball player who has managed to engage with North Korea’s leader — something United States officials have been unable to do — said he planned to return to the North to try to gain the release of an imprisoned American citizen, according to a video posted Friday on the celebrity news Web site TMZ.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodman Says He’ll Ask North Korea to Free American', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodman to Ask North Korea to Free American', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Otis, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodman, Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bae, Kenneth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TMZ.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4869ec1c-ad12-5a50-b545-be96b38db885', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4869ec1c-ad12-5a50-b545-be96b38db885'}, {'abstract': 'Give families the time and money they need for better eating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/opinion/pay-people-to-cook-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'Give families the time and money they need for better eating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE home-cooked family meal is often lauded as the solution for problems ranging from obesity to deteriorating health to a decline in civility and morals. Using whole foods to prepare meals without additives and chemicals is the holy grail for today’s advocates of better eating. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pay People to Cook at Home', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pay People to Cook at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wartman, Kristin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:33:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristin Wartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7930274c-6404-5706-a4d1-abec7bc2c4da', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7930274c-6404-5706-a4d1-abec7bc2c4da'}, {'abstract': 'New York City violated federal law because its emergency management plans failed to address the needs of the disabled during Tropical Storm Irene, the government said on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/nyregion/storm-plans-for-disabled-inadequate-us-says.html', 'snippet': 'New York City violated federal law because its emergency management plans failed to address the needs of the disabled during Tropical Storm Irene, the government said on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City is in violation of federal law because its emergency management plans “do not adequately protect the rights of individuals with disabilities,” federal authorities said in a court filing on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Plans for Disabled Are Inadequate, U.S. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storm Plans For Disabled Inadequate, U.S. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Irene (2011)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T01:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27842be5-1698-5318-be26-63a7e809886d', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27842be5-1698-5318-be26-63a7e809886d'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Gaffigan, comedian, actor and author, spends Sundays with his wife and five children, at home, in church and at the park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/nyregion/comedian-jim-gaffigan-takes-sundays-off-from-stand-up.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Gaffigan, comedian, actor and author, spends Sundays with his wife and five children, at home, in church and at the park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sundays, the comedian and actor Jim Gaffigan, 46, takes a day off from stand-up. Instead of performing, he collects new fodder during family outings with his wife, Jeannie Noth Gaffigan, and their five children, Marre, 9; Jack, 7; Katie, 4; Michael, 22 months; and Patrick, 7 months, and time spent at their home, a fifth-floor walk-up on the Bowery. Some of this material can be seen and heard in Mr. Gaffigan’s Grammy-nominated, downloadable comedy special, “Mr. Universe,” and on his national tour. It also fills the pages of his new book, “Dad Is Fat,” which was released last week.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo