'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac03c193-47e3-57f5-80ca-15f7ab60274a', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac03c193-47e3-57f5-80ca-15f7ab60274a'}, {'abstract': 'Jill Sigman’s “Last Days/First Field” includes apocalyptic dance and a ritual planting of seedlings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/arts/dance/last-days-first-field-by-jill-sigman.html', 'snippet': 'Jill Sigman’s “Last Days/First Field” includes apocalyptic dance and a ritual planting of seedlings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a vigorous dance component in “Last Days/First Field,” but its choreographer, Jill Sigman, has even bigger ambitions in mind. The two-hour work, as she explains in program notes, “is a movement ritual for our time.” In the first half, “Last Days,” the focus is on dancing: there’s an apocalyptic feel as performers move frantically in packs or alone, gesticulating wildly as their feet slap soundly onto the floor. The ritual part comes to light in the second half, “First Field.” Ms. Sigman attempts to alter the landscape, both physically and spiritually, by bringing nature inside.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before You Can Plant, Dance Through the End of the World', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before You Can Plant, Dance Through the End of the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sigman, Jill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:06:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9534e0f6-51c4-5cf9-94a8-26ffd4d8406c', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9534e0f6-51c4-5cf9-94a8-26ffd4d8406c'}, {'abstract': 'Islamabad should expand news coverage, not restrict it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/opinion/times-reporter-expelled-by-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Islamabad should expand news coverage, not restrict it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pakistan is facing daunting challenges, including a violent insurgency that threatens the state and a critically important general election on Saturday. Yet its Interior Ministry this week had nothing better to do than to expel Declan Walsh, The Times’s bureau chief in Pakistan. The move was unjustified and should be reversed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expelled by Pakistan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expelled by Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Declan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c548a98-efc0-5fb2-b912-f67d3fe36091', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c548a98-efc0-5fb2-b912-f67d3fe36091'}, {'abstract': 'A resentencing fight reflects a wide and disturbing pattern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/opinion/racism-in-a-texas-death-case.html', 'snippet': 'A resentencing fight reflects a wide and disturbing pattern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the annals of racism in the Texas criminal justice system, seven death penalty cases are in a class by themselves. In 2000, after the Supreme Court ordered a new sentencing hearing in one of them, Senator John Cornyn, who was then the state attorney general, called for new sentencing hearings in the other cases for the same reason: because race was improperly and explicitly considered as a factor in determining the sentence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racism in a Texas Death Case', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racism in a Texas Death Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buck, Duane E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c96e42d-7752-5a3e-adbb-cb70c4d7ef76', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c96e42d-7752-5a3e-adbb-cb70c4d7ef76'}, {'abstract': 'It’s past time to address a profound impediment to real equality: workplace discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/opinion/beyond-basketball-and-bigotry-workplace-discrimination-based-on-sexual-orientation.html', 'snippet': 'It’s past time to address a profound impediment to real equality: workplace discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The overwhelmingly supportive response to Jason Collins, who came out last week as the first openly gay male athlete playing in a major American team sport, is an encouraging measure of the nation’s civil rights progress. But his barrier-breaking announcement a dozen years into his N.B.A. career also carries a reminder of a reality millions of gay people live with every day: being open about their sexual orientation could put their job and career at risk. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Basketball and Bigotry', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Basketball and Bigotry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Jason', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/515099ed-8a7c-53c9-9c84-12838b9eb962', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/515099ed-8a7c-53c9-9c84-12838b9eb962'}, {'abstract': 'The recovering marine mammal still needs all the protection it can get.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/opinion/ceaseless-pressure-on-whales.html', 'snippet': 'The recovering marine mammal still needs all the protection it can get.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 1986, when the International Whaling Commission imposed a moratorium on whaling, there has been a steady resurgence in whale populations. The recovery of several species pushed to the brink of extinction by commercial whaling is a reminder of the resilience of nature. Even so, there is a nearly constant push to ease the restrictions that have protected the whales and, in some cases, to resume hunting. There are two cases in point: fin whales near Iceland, a nation that has never accepted the I.W.C. moratorium, and humpback whales near Hawaii.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ceaseless Pressure on Whales', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ceaseless Pressure on Whales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:08:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5223c806-3b35-57a3-bf79-f82cb67fa96c', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5223c806-3b35-57a3-bf79-f82cb67fa96c'}, {'abstract': 'French officials said Friday that they are examining three people who came into contact with a man hospitalized with a new respiratory coronavirus related to SARS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/world/europe/concern-over-new-virus-in-france.html', 'snippet': 'French officials said Friday that they are examining three people who came into contact with a man hospitalized with a new respiratory coronavirus related to SARS.', 'lead_paragraph': ' French officials said Friday that they are examining three people who came into contact with a man hospitalized with a new respiratory coronavirus related to SARS, to see if they have also contracted the disease. The man, 65, hospitalized in late April, got the disease on a package tour to Dubai. Officials are now examining a nurse at the hospital, a doctor and a former roommate of the man, all of whom are being monitored\xa0 by doctors. The concern is how easily the new virus might spread from one person to another. Since the virus emerged last year, 18 people have died worldwide, but the man is so far the only confirmed case in France. He is in serious but stable condition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Concern Over New Virus', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Concern Over New Virus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SARS (Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4047c766-9ab5-54fe-b7fc-f5453835668e', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4047c766-9ab5-54fe-b7fc-f5453835668e'}, {'abstract': 'Back in Kansas City for the first time since his season-ending injury last May, a healthy Mariano Rivera was able to joke about what happened.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/rivera-is-able-to-laugh-it-off/', 'snippet': 'Back in Kansas City for the first time since his season-ending injury last May, a healthy Mariano Rivera was able to joke about what happened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — About two hours before the first pitch of the Yankees’ game against the Kansas City Royals, and nearly 53 weeks after Mariano Rivera suffered the worst injury of his career, two men carried a 12-foot sign out to the spot where Rivera went down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rivera Is Able to Laugh It Off', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d93f06a3-931a-54bf-bd90-e1530c89b3bc', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d93f06a3-931a-54bf-bd90-e1530c89b3bc'}, {'abstract': 'European countries need to make bold moves toward full integration of their economic policies.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/10/europes-careless-dithering/', 'snippet': 'European countries need to make bold moves toward full integration of their economic policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUROPE’S economic problems are growing steadily worse, with unemployment in parts of the Continent now above the level reached in the United States during the Great Depression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Careless Dithering', 'kicker': 'Steven Rattner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54ff7e11-fa77-5b6b-836e-535250e55c55', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54ff7e11-fa77-5b6b-836e-535250e55c55'}, {'abstract': 'A disclosure of e-mails showed the White House was more involved in revising talking points about the attack in Benghazi, Libya, than officials have previously acknowledged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/us/politics/benghazi-e-mails-put-white-house-on-the-defensive.html', 'snippet': 'A disclosure of e-mails showed the White House was more involved in revising talking points about the attack in Benghazi, Libya, than officials have previously acknowledged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A long-simmering dispute over the White House’s account of the deadly assault on the American diplomatic compound in Benghazi, Libya, flared up on Friday, with a disclosure of e-mails that show the White House was more deeply involved in revising talking points about the attack than officials have previously acknowledged.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Benghazi E-Mails Put White House on the Defensive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Benghazi E-Mails Put White House on the Defensive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Susan E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ansar al-Shariah', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Jay', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nuland, Victoria J', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:19:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a9325a8-885a-5a17-bb80-03df046e7fc1', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a9325a8-885a-5a17-bb80-03df046e7fc1'}, {'abstract': 'After battling Britain’s courts to avoid deportation, a militant Islamist preacher said he will fly home to Jordan if a treaty regarding torture is ratified.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/world/europe/militant-cleric-may-head-to-jordan.html', 'snippet': 'After battling Britain’s courts to avoid deportation, a militant Islamist preacher said he will fly home to Jordan if a treaty regarding torture is ratified.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After years of battling in Britain’s courts to avoid deportation to Jordan and a retrial there on terrorist bombing charges, a militant Islamist preacher of Palestinian descent known as Abu Qatada told an immigration court through his lawyer on Friday that he will fly home voluntarily if Britain and Jordan ratify a treaty concluded last month that will ensure that no evidence obtained by torture will be used in the case. The two countries have said they expect the ratification process to be completed within months. The 52-year-old cleric, whose real name is Omar Mahmoud Mohammed Othman was sentenced in absentia to life imprisonment on the bombing charges by a Jordanian court in 1990. In Britain, where he sought refugee status, he has become a symbol for many in Britain of the exploitation of the country’s immigration, welfare and justice systems by migrants seeking to use Britain as a haven for terrorist activities. Mr. Othman’s new pledge was met with widespread skepticism, with some legal experts saying he might be seeking to pre-empt a move favored by some in the government who have urged that Mr. Othman, currently held in prison for breaking bail conditions forbidding his use of cellphones and computers, be flown back to Jordan peremptorily, in defiance of British and European court rulings in his favor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Cleric May Head to Jordan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Cleric May Head to Jordan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Othman, Omar Mahmoud Mohammed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T02:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb040cb-ce3d-5b78-a64e-afc5393eb96b', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb040cb-ce3d-5b78-a64e-afc5393eb96b'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a rare player who pays such close attention while being stuck on the bench. But Mike Baxter does. This season, he is 5 for 9 as a pinch-hitter.', 'web_url'