l': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5f078308-53b9-5e3a-b467-943a66211f55', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5f078308-53b9-5e3a-b467-943a66211f55'}, {'abstract': 'The quirky comedy “Community” seemed to find new legs late this season, but for “Smash” and “The New Normal” the race is over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/business/media/nbc-saves-community-but-drops-two-other-series.html', 'snippet': 'The quirky comedy “Community” seemed to find new legs late this season, but for “Smash” and “The New Normal” the race is over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Against all expectations, NBC renewed its quirky comedy “Community” on Friday night, at the same time that it quietly pulled the plug on the eventually ill-named “Smash.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Saves ‘Community,’ but Drops Two Other Series', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NBC Saves ‘Community,’ but Drops Two Other Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyers, Jonathan Rhys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Michael J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spader, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T04:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c0d9329-209e-5c7d-876b-8e141b51a213', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c0d9329-209e-5c7d-876b-8e141b51a213'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) MADAGASCAR 3: EUROPE’S MOST WANTED (2012) Those escapees from the Central Park Zoo — Alex the lion (Ben Stiller), Marty the zebra (Chris Rock), Gloria the gorilla (Jada Pinkett Smith) and Melman the giraffe (David Schwimmer) — depart Africa to join a European circus, the better to evade a French animal-control officer (Frances McDormand) literally after Alex’s head, in this franchise’s latest installment. They also try to play nice with their new friends Vitaly (Bryan Cranston), a tiger; Gia (Jessica Chastain), a jaguar; and Stefano (Martin Short), a sea lion. “Life lessons in the script (partly by Noah Baumbach, Mr. Stiller’s ‘Greenberg’ director) are desultory, but a late twist is surprising,” Andy Webster wrote in The New York Times about this film directed by Eric Darnell, Tom McGrath and Conrad Vernon, and styled after Miroslav Sasek’s illustrations. “Where ‘Madagascar 3’ soars is in its visuals: A Monte Carlo chase is vertiginously madcap; a Cirque du Soleil-style spectacle dazzles with rich pastels; the 3-D effects have wit and invention,” Mr. Webster added. “Kids will be stimulated. And, parents, you’ll enjoy the sights.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef159798-5808-55ef-9f82-a5a990155a84', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef159798-5808-55ef-9f82-a5a990155a84'}, {'abstract': 'Survivor pulled from factory collapse; desegregating the Roma; Athens museum confronts crisis; and sailing death clouds America’s Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/iht-quick-read-may-11/', 'snippet': 'Survivor pulled from factory collapse; desegregating the Roma; Athens museum confronts crisis; and sailing death clouds America’s Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Day after day, the grim drudgery of digging for bodies had progressed at Rana Plaza. Talk of rescuing survivors had faded. This was the recovery phase, and what was being recovered were corpses, the numbers spinning remorselessly forward: 700 dead became 800, then 900, with no end in sight. By Friday morning, the number had pushed above 1,000. And then, late in the afternoon, a soldier from the Bangladeshi Army, standing atop the rubble of the wrecked building, noticed an iron rod that seemed to be moving. There was a noise, a voice. Rescuers hurriedly carved a hole through a concrete pillar. Television stations in Bangladesh cut to the scene: a woman, gasping, was alive in the wreckage, nearly 17 full days after Rana Plaza had collapsed. A new number was announced: One. A female garment worker named Reshma. A survivor. A miracle. “Save me!” rescuers heard her shout, before they pulled her into the afternoon light, her face powdered in dust as she was placed on a stretcher. Julfikar Ali Manik reports from Dhaka, Bangladesh and Jim Yardley reports from New Delhi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/world/bangladesh_span/bangladesh_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: May 11', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T05:06:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c34fd1c9-2a0f-57b7-9ca4-4c40dd60c5b0', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c34fd1c9-2a0f-57b7-9ca4-4c40dd60c5b0'}, {'abstract': 'Russian analysts say Washington is kidding itself if it believes Mr. Putin can orchestrate a quick and easy Assad exit. But the crisis has increased Vladimir Putin’s standing at home and Russia’s abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/why-putin-cant-solve-syria/', 'snippet': 'Russian analysts say Washington is kidding itself if it believes Mr. Putin can orchestrate a quick and easy Assad exit. But the crisis has increased Vladimir Putin’s standing at home and Russia’s abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW – After marathon meetings with Secretary of State John Kerry here this week, the Russian foreign minister, Sergey Lavrov, hinted that Moscow might finally pressure President Bashir al-Assad of Syria to leave office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1064, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/blogs/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria/11rdv-kerry-putin-syria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Putin Can’t Solve Syria', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T05:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rohde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3d0335-0df5-5b23-968a-5bd9ac86e2e4', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3d0335-0df5-5b23-968a-5bd9ac86e2e4'}, {'abstract': 'A former spokesman for President Park Geun-hye of South Korea said his behavior with a young woman during a state visit to Washington was misinterpreted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/world/asia/fired-aide-to-south-korean-leader-denies-improper-conduct.html', 'snippet': 'A former spokesman for President Park Geun-hye of South Korea said his behavior with a young woman during a state visit to Washington was misinterpreted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — A spokesman for President Park Geun-hye who was fired while on a recent state visit to the United States denied Saturday that he had groped a young woman in a Washington hotel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'su