', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95d23aa4-2bf8-532a-bddc-b7c4e25c44c7'}, {'abstract': 'Not so crazy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/11/inflation-madness/', 'snippet': 'Not so crazy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing I gather from various economic discussions as well as some of the trolls on this blog is that there’s a widespread view that the kind of monetary policy I advocate — which includes a higher inflation target — isn’t just wrong; it’s madness. It is, I am told in no uncertain terms, proof that I am no longer a real economist, if I ever was.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation Madness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-11T16:37:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3a7a643-0d92-59f1-9219-c10e91450719', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3a7a643-0d92-59f1-9219-c10e91450719'}, {'abstract': 'The new handbook of diagnoses won’t matter much to practicing psychiatrists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/opinion/sunday/why-the-fuss-over-the-dsm-5.html', 'snippet': 'The new handbook of diagnoses won’t matter much to practicing psychiatrists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LATER this month, the American Psychiatric Association will unveil the fifth edition of its handbook of diagnoses, the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders. Fourteen years in the making, the D.S.M.-5 has been the subject of seemingly endless discussion.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'su