: 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/01d2fb12-ed9e-51d8-9112-039f9c0178c2', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01d2fb12-ed9e-51d8-9112-039f9c0178c2'}, {'abstract': 'The salmon fly hatch is a bucket-list experience that attracts anglers to Oregon’s Lower Deschutes River from late May through mid-June.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/sports/when-rainbow-trout-go-bug-hunting-anglers-are-waiting.html', 'snippet': 'The salmon fly hatch is a bucket-list experience that attracts anglers to Oregon’s Lower Deschutes River from late May through mid-June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARM SPRINGS, Ore. — The sky was not exactly dark in a blotting-out-the-sun sense, but the salmon flies were certainly thick above central Oregon’s Lower Deschutes River. Thousands of female specimens circled 30 feet above the water’s surface, preparing to descend and drop their eggs. Occasionally, a bug would spiral slowly down to the river, flutter awkwardly on the surface, then disappear in a sudden splash.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/sports/dog-salmonfly-1/dog-salmonfly-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/11/sports/dog-salmonfly-1/dog-salmonfly-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/sports/dog-salmonfly-1/dog-salmonfly-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/11/sports/dog-salmonfly-1/dog-salmonfly-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r