r.html', 'snippet': 'With its “grit and grind” style, Memphis managed to hold off a persistent Oklahoma City team to take a 2-1 lead in their second-round N.B.A. playoff series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMPHIS — Zach Randolph screamed at Lionel Hollins. Marc Gasol screamed at the officials. Tony Allen screamed at himself. No one will ever accuse the Grizzlies of being a quiet, understated team. They like to share their feelings. Hollins, the team’s coach, prefers it that way.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/sports/city-grizzlies/city-grizzlies-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gritty Grizzlies, Their Kind of Win', 'kicker': 'Game 3: Grizzlies 87, Thunder 81', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Gritty Grizzlies, Their Kind Of Win', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Grizzlies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Marc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-12T00:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f137b19-2481-5dfc-a77b-f7baaee65455', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f137b19-2481-5dfc-a77b-f7baaee65455'}, {'abstract': 'Sergio García began the day with a one-stroke lead over Tiger Woods, but David Lingmerth emerged as the leader in the third round, which was suspended after a rain delay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/sports/golf/garcia-loses-his-concentration-and-the-lead-at-the-players-championship.html', 'snippet': 'Sergio García began the day with a one-stroke lead over Tiger Woods, but David Lingmerth emerged as the leader in the third round, which was suspended after a rain delay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — Nineteen other times Sergio García had been paired with Tiger Woods, and on most of those occasions García staggered off the course at the