nomic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-12T20:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6428c027-8175-5677-b9ac-94bf9f9a704b', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6428c027-8175-5677-b9ac-94bf9f9a704b'}, {'abstract': 'A program encompassing works by Dvorak, Brahms and Franck was performed at a lunchtime chamber-music concert on Thursday at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/arts/music/jaime-laredo-gives-violin-concert-at-the-92nd-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'A program encompassing works by Dvorak, Brahms and Franck was performed at a lunchtime chamber-music concert on Thursday at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was raining cats and dogs last Thursday at noon when audience members filed into the Kaufmann Concert Hall at the 92nd Street Y, spreading the odor of wet coats and umbrellas. It was the lunchtime performance of the final run of chamber-music concerts presented and, in part, performed by the violinist Jaime Laredo with a program encompassing works by Dvorak, Brahms and Franck. The auditorium was divided into two camps. In the front half, the musically literate, as evidenced by the significant number of musical scores spread out on laps. In the back, 150 high school students. For the former, chamber music was a necessity on par with a well-brewed cup of coffee; for the latter, a novelty.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Card Game at Lunchtime', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Card Game At Lunchtime', 'name': None, 'seo': 