ows that the Devil has the best tunes. And we also know what he plays them on: a fiddle. From Tartini’s “Devil’s Trill” Violin Sonata of 1713 to the Charlie Daniels Band’s 1979 country music ballad “The Devil Went Down to Georgia,” the instrument most readily associated with the Crafty One is a violin. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 890, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 890}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 691, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1219, 'width': 822, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/arts/miranda/miranda-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Music for Violin, With Faustian Strings Attached', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Music for Violin, With 