es from Princeton and Harvard Law, and a stint clerking at the Supreme Court. After a few months in Congress promoting Ted Cruz, smartest guy in the room, it looks as if he now wants to be Ted Cruz, extremely obnoxious president. But he keeps saying things that make no sense.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E Pluribus Me', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E Pluribus Me', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ff450ca-d372-589e-bdaa-f64ad07cf4a8', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ff450ca-d372-589e-bdaa-f64ad07cf4a8'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman will seek the cooperation of Apple, Google, Microsoft and Samsung to find ways of improving the security of the devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/nyregion/new-york-to-ask-smartphone-makers-to-help-prevent-thefts.html', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman will seek the cooperation of Apple, Google, Microsoft and Samsung to find ways of improving the security of the devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Co