ze East Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pilotless Planes, Pacific Tensions', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pilotless Planes, Pacific Tensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fcb59b7-6345-5f46-b037-3962fecd6f12', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fcb59b7-6345-5f46-b037-3962fecd6f12'}, {'abstract': 'People do not inevitably get sick or die because the economy has faltered. Fiscal policy can be a matter of life or death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/opinion/how-austerity-kills.html', 'snippet': 'People do not inevitably get sick or die because the economy has faltered. Fiscal policy can be a matter of life or death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY last month, a triple suicide was reported in the seaside town of Civitanova Marche, Italy. A married couple, Anna Maria Sopranzi, 68, and Romeo Dionisi, 62, had been struggling to live on her monthly pension of around 500 euros (about $650), and had fallen behind on rent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 762}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/opinion/0513OPEDgreig/0513OPEDgreig-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Austerity Kills', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Austerity Kills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stuckler, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basu, Sanjay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Stuckler and Sanjay Basu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuckler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sanjay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Basu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/092c5226-2168-5253-8c46-2d2b45885919', 'word_count': 1635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092c5226-2168-5253-8c46-2d2b45885919'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s proposal is a good start, but policy makers must remain watchful so Google does not abuse its power and limit competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/opinion/googles-offer-to-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s proposal is a good start, but policy makers must remain watchful so Google does not abuse its power and limit competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google’s competitors, like Microsoft, Expedia and Yelp, have long complained that the company uses its dominant search engine — it has more than 90 percent market share in Europe and about 70 percent in the United States — to promote its own services, like YouTube, Google Maps and others, at the expense of rivals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google’s Offer to Europe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google’s Offer to Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:07:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f425cc4e-e5fd-5e91-a8f6-9ec74d68c362', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f425cc4e-e5fd-5e91-a8f6-9ec74d68c362'}, {'abstract': 'Tiger Woods shot a final-round of 70 for a 13-under 275 to overtake Sergio García and win the Players Championship for his 78th career victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/sports/golf/tiger-woods-wins-players-championship-as-sergio-garcia-collapses.html', 'snippet': 'Tiger Woods shot a final-round of 70 for a 13-under 275 to overtake Sergio García and win the Players Championship for his 78th career victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — As the Players Championship wound down Sunday, there were as many compelling stories on the leader board as there were golf balls in the water surrounding the tournament’s signature hole, the par-3 17th.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1465, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Word to Woods as García’s Game Sinks on Last 2 Holes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Word to Woods as García’s Game Sinks on Last 2 Holes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Players Championship (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Sergio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13052b83-c76d-5c46-a59d-deca0c54f068', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13052b83-c76d-5c46-a59d-deca0c54f068'}, {'abstract': 'With soaring costs, stagnating incomes and little help from the government, there is only one way to pay for higher education: debt.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/student-debt-and-the-crushing-of-the-american-dream/', 'snippet': 'With soaring costs, stagnating incomes and little help from the government, there is only one way to pay for higher education: debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A CERTAIN drama has become familiar in the United States (and some other advanced industrialized countries): Bankers encourage people to borrow beyond their means, preying especially on those who are financially unsophisticated. They use their political influence to get favorable treatment of one form or another. Debts mount. Journalists record the human toll. Then comes bewilderment: How could we let this happen again? Officials promise to fix things. Something is done about the most egregious abuses. People move on, reassured that the crisis has abated, but suspecting that it will recur soon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Debt and the Crushing of the American Dream', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a54e7d-7c5f-5a23-adc1-94c1773122f6', 'word_count': 1877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a54e7d-7c5f-5a23-adc1-94c1773122f6'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bob Filner sees the border as a potential economic engine for the region, a remarkable shift in a city once viewed as a hotbed for illegal immigration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/us/san-diego-mayor-building-economic-bridges-to-tijuana.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bob Filner sees the border as a potential economic engine for the region, a remarkable shift in a city once viewed as a hotbed for illegal immigration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Opening a satellite city office in a far-flung neighborhood is not unusual in sprawling cities like this one. But one thing sets apart Mayor Bob Filner’s newest outpost: it is in another country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/us/Border/Border-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/us/Border/Border-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/us/Border/Border-jumbo.j