 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b350ca6-3651-5e55-adba-5c639e0c4df6', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b350ca6-3651-5e55-adba-5c639e0c4df6'}, {'abstract': 'Nathaniel Frank, a visiting scholar at Columbia Law School, responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/opinion/sublimating-gayness.html', 'snippet': 'Nathaniel Frank, a visiting scholar at Columbia Law School, responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sublimating Gayness', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sublimating Gayness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0fe35b6-90cf-5eef-ac27-d27515ec6b2f', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0fe35b6-90cf-5eef-ac27-d27515ec6b2f'}, {'abstract': 'After the recent scandals, there is growing pressure on lawmakers, especially recalcitrant Senate Republicans, to pass electoral reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/opinion/alarm-bells-in-albany.html', 'snippet': 'After the recent scandals, there is growing pressure on lawmakers, especially recalcitrant Senate Republicans, to pass electoral reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo, who promised to clean up state government in his 2010 campaign, has now become so alarmed by the latest scandals in Albany that he has issued a threat lawmakers ought to take seriously. If the Legislature does not pass a package of electoral reforms, including public financing, before the session ends in June, he says he will consider appointing a Moreland Act Commission that can investigate and subpoena government officials suspected of misconduct. The commission would be able to make public its findings and pass those findings on to local or federal investigators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alarm Bells in Albany', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alarm Bells in Albany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T01:26:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/57ca8a8c-6571-5259-9c0c-baa4b997bfc2', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57ca8a8c-6571-5259-9c0c-baa4b997bfc2'}, {'abstract': 'What we can learn from a think tank’s over-the-top attack on immigration reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/opinion/keller-dark-heritage.html', 'snippet': 'What we can learn from a think tank’s over-the-top attack on immigration reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week the Heritage Foundation delivered a report claiming that legalizing undocumented immigrants will create a more-or-less permanent underclass of benefit-sucking, wage-lowering, economy-crippling parasites, with a cost to American taxpayers of — megaphone, please — SIX POINT THREE TRILLION DOLLARS! The report was promptly denounced, not least by reputable conservative economists, for example here and here and here. Then one of the report’s co-authors resigned from Heritage after The Washington Post discovered that he had once proposed blocking immigrants with low I.Q. scores. (More on that later.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Heritage', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content