gazine/travel-essentials-marin-county-calif.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s where to eat, sleep and shop in San Francisco’s neighbor to the north.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our Summer Travel issue, which hit newsstands on Sunday, Adam Sachs professes his love for Marin County, a place he calls “the most beautiful, bucolic, privileged, liberal, hippie-dippie place on the earth.” Here’s where to eat, sleep and shop in San Francisco’s neighbor to the north.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/12/t-magazine/12extra-marin1/12extra-marin1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Essentials | Marin County, Calif.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d151a98-638f-54f4-9a73-23be30af63e8', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d151a98-638f-54f4-9a73-23be30af63e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Japanese skincare line Tatcha has created oils and balms using camellia and gold leaf created to protect and enhance skin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/t-magazine/tatcha-skincare.html', 'snippet': 'The Japanese skincare line Tatcha has created oils and balms using camellia and gold leaf created to protect and enhance skin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Francisco-based skin care expert Victoria Tsai has built her business by studying the beauty secrets, passed down over generations, of the traditional Japanese entertainers known as geisha. After many trips east and countless hours studying makeup regimens, Tsai founded Tatcha, a line of 95-percent-natural products made and formulated in Japan. One of her first discoveries was aburatorigami, the traditional handmade blotting papers used in ancient Japan to protect gold as it is hammered into delicate gold leaf. Several centuries ago, geisha realized that the papers could also absorb facial oil, without disturbing their signature stage makeup. “I tried to do exactly what the geisha were doing, but also make products that are a little bit easier to use,” Tsai said. “And they use our stuff now.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1404, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/t-magazine/13geisha-beddie/13geisha-beddie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bottled Secrets of the Geisha', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kyoto (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74405cf6-9cd9-5277-ad4a-e751bbadf62a', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74405cf6-9cd9-5277-ad4a-e751bbadf62a'}, {'abstract': 'Reporters at Bloomberg News were told to use the terminals to get an edge in the competitive world of financial journalism, more than half a dozen former employees said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/business/media/bloomberg-admits-terminal-snooping.html', 'snippet': 'Reporters at Bloomberg News were told to use the terminals to get an edge in the competitive world of financial journalism, more than half a dozen former employees said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporters at Bloomberg News were trained to use a function on the company’s financial data terminals that allowed them to view subscribers’ contact information and, in some cases, monitor login activity in order to advance news coverage, more than half a dozen former employees said.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/business/sub-jp-bloomberg/sub-jp-bloomberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/business/sub-jp-bloomberg/sub-jp-bloomberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/business/sub-jp-bloomberg/sub-jp-bloomberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy':