', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d922ce82-5723-5cc2-bfcf-6139a79358ec', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d922ce82-5723-5cc2-bfcf-6139a79358ec'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Ferguson is leaving Manchester, and Roberto Mancini may follow him out the door.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/all-the-comings-and-goings-in-manchester/', 'snippet': 'Alex Ferguson is leaving Manchester, and Roberto Mancini may follow him out the door.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a wild weekend for Manchester and its two biggest clubs, so maybe a quick recap is in order:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All the Comings and Goings in Manchester', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T04:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18bf3741-8897-5418-b29f-f6dfa9196a4a', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18bf3741-8897-5418-b29f-f6dfa9196a4a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10\xa0P.M. (13) THE INVISIBLE WAR (2012) The Department of Defense estimates that there were 22,800 sexual assaults in the United States military in 2011. Veterans Affairs studies have shown that one-third of women seeking assistance have been sexually assaulted, and that more men than women are assaulted while in service. This Academy Award nominee for best documentary feature, directed by Kirby Dick and produced by Amy Ziering, uses interviews with retired and active service members to investigate the epidemic of rape within the military. (A female soldier in a combat zone is more likely to be attacked by a fellow soldier than killed by enemy fire.) “Military service is often a family tradition, and the military itself, with its customs of loyalty, solidarity and shared sacrifice, can be a kind of family for its members,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “This means that the violations chronicled in ‘The Invisible War’ are compounded by a deep and terrible betrayal, which ripples outward from the various branches of the service into the society as a whole. This is not a movie that can be ignored.” (Above Kori Cioca, who served in the Coast Guard, and her husband, Rob.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T04:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c899e42-617b-5507-9976-a50b07d8f135', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c899e42-617b-5507-9976-a50b07d8f135'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/news-quiz-may-13-2013-2/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | May 13, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T05:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taylor Adams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bc41776-5ea5-544a-a721-dcd27e6041d8', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bc41776-5ea5-544a-a721-dcd27e6041d8'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: While a human cacophony rages outside the park, a paradise for insects lies inside as nature quietly thrives.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/a-bugs-life-in-central-park/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: While a human cacophony rages outside the park, a paradise for insects lies inside as nature quietly thrives.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/nyregion/13diary-illo-cityroom/13diary-illo-cityroom-articleLarge.png', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/nyregion/13diary-illo-cityroom/13diary-illo-cityroom-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/nyregion/13diary-illo-cityroom/13diary-illo-