ters-taunt-police/', 'snippet': 'A nighttime protest ride on bicycles confounds Moscow authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — I will take part in almost any activity that involves bicycling, so when I saw that someone was organizing a protest ride in Moscow, I knew I would go even though its purpose and logistics were not entirely clear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Russian Police for a Ride', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T10:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45ceb349-d3f5-5317-93a3-139c19d84825', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45ceb349-d3f5-5317-93a3-139c19d84825'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the attackers’ aim appeared not to be espionage but sabotage, and that the source of the attacks seemed to be in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/daily-report-new-wave-of-cyberattacks-against-u-s-corporations/', 'snippet': 'Officials said the attackers’ aim appeared not to be espionage but sabotage, and that the source of the attacks seemed to be in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new wave of cyberattacks is striking American corporations, prompting warnings from federal officials, including a vague one issued last week by the Department of Homeland Security. This time, officials say, the attackers’ aim is not espionage but sabotage, and the source seems to be somewhere in the Middle East, David E. Sanger and Nicole Perlroth report in The New York Times on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: New Wave of Cyberattacks Against U.S. Corporations', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T10:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89758bea-5f88-5d71-ab87-51fb247e59bf', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89758bea-5f88-5d71-ab87-51fb247e59bf'}, {'abstract': 'Elan, an Irish drug maker that is the target of a hostile takeover, agreed to pay $1 billion for a share of royalties on new drugs from Theravance of the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/elan-in-deal-on-drug-royalties/', 'snippet': 'Elan, an Irish drug maker that is the target of a hostile takeover, agreed to pay $1 billion for a share of royalties on new drugs from Theravance of the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Elan, an Irish drug maker that is the target of a hostile takeover, said on Monday that it had agreed to buy a share of royalties on new drugs from Theravance of the United States for $1 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elan in Deal on Drug Royalties', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T10:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualif