', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Soccer and Investing, Bias Is Toward Action', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T14:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df433e4f-d1d1-5283-b10d-66d06cf35987', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df433e4f-d1d1-5283-b10d-66d06cf35987'}, {'abstract': 'Shopping for groceries on an empty stomach does in fact influence food choices, a new study shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/really-never-go-grocery-shopping-on-an-empty-stomach/', 'snippet': 'Shopping for groceries on an empty stomach does in fact influence food choices, a new study shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Really? Never Go Grocery Shopping on an Empty Stomach', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T14:53:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1c024b1-c0dd-55f5-9e41-7fe4c8e6f893', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1c024b1-c0dd-55f5-9e41-7fe4c8e6f893'}, {'abstract': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/triple-play-baseball-quiz-week-6-results/', 'snippet': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three of the players in Question No. 1 greeted May with hot streaks, collecting hits in every game they played last week. Adam LaRoche was the correct answer, going 8 for 19 for a .421 average.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 6 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T14:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79947a39-a864-5a71-898d-84ae04348b25', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79947a39-a864-5a71-898d-84ae04348b25'}, {'abstract': 'A growing family of apartment houses sharing a common surname has sprouted up over the past 10 years, giving the sense of a mini, matchy architectural movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/nyregion/building-condos-in-brooklyn-by-the-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'A growing family of apartment houses sharing a common surname has sprouted up over the past 10 years, giving the sense of a mini, matchy architectural movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Belvedere LXX is a brand-new condominium on Eckford Street in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, built of burgundy brick. It is so new that its permits still hang in the window, the closets are bare of clothes, and the apartments have yet to hit the market.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/nyregion/14appraisal_cnd/14appraisal_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building Condos by the Numbers, Skipping Some Along the Way ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Condos by the Numbers, Skipping Some Along the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T14:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6397d3f1-1582-5a55-90dc-bfd0f86e19c9', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6397d3f1-1582-5a55-90dc-bfd0f86e19c9'}, {'abstract': 'Why hadn’t I yelled, or elbowed him? The truth is, I thought for a moment I might be crazy, that I was making it all up.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/i-was-groped-on-the-subway/', 'snippet': 'Why hadn’t I yelled, or elbowed him? The truth is, I thought for a moment I might be crazy, that I was making it all up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was late as usual, weaving through the 72nd Street subway station, rushing down the stairs to catch a departing train, and managed to squeeze into one of the packed cars just in time. It was Friday, a few weeks after my 29th birthday. I was on my way downtown to my job at my family’s taxi business, casually dressed in leggings and a striped orange dress. I pushed my still wet hair out of my face and found a sliver of space to stand. As the doors were closing, one more person shoved his way in and the car let out a collective groan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was Groped on the Subway', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kimberly Matus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kimberly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Matus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/100d7af1-fbdb-5a10-b4f9-617002c4dd1d', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/100d7af1-fbdb-5a10-b4f9-617002c4dd1d'}, {'abstract': '“We have trained our customers in a bad way,” said the owner, Beth Shaw.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/yogafit-tries-to-escape-the-discount-trap/', 'snippet': '“We have trained our customers in a bad way,” said the owner, Beth Shaw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the last She Owns It business group meeting, Beth Shaw, who owns YogaFit, started the discussion by sharing some painful lessons she has learned from discounting her company’s yoga teacher training.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'YogaFit Tries to Escape the D