ad been a famous battle flag since the fall of 1861. Its incorporation into the national flag confirmed the Southern Cross as the de facto symbol of Confederate nationalism. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Birth of the ‘Stainless Banner’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coski, John M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the Confederacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stars and Bars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T15:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Coski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/953fac91-0ff8-523b-bfc7-6575af0cde2b', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953fac91-0ff8-523b-bfc7-6575af0cde2b'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ photos from the week of May 6.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/13/fashion/streetstyleoveralls.html', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ photos from the week of May 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of readers’ photos from the week of May 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/fashion/streetstyleoveralls-slide-EWLA/streetstyleoveralls-slide-EWLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 