snippet': 'Can you get the burger without the cow? A clot in Andrew Revkin’s brain pushes him to learn about strokes — from his hospital bed. The (insect) buzz around Carl Zimmer’s new column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can you get the burger without the cow? A clot in Andrew Revkin’s brain pushes him to learn about strokes — from his hospital bed. The (insect) buzz around Carl Zimmer’s new column.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Tube Burger, A Lucky Stroke, Coming of the Cicadas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hamburgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cicadas (Insects)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T15:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/56fa02c2-238b-5770-87eb-5a850fb1e5b4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/56fa02c2-238b-5770-87eb-5a850fb1e5b4'}, {'abstract': 'Another set of weak economic data out of China showed that fixed-asset investment slowed, industrial production grew less than projected and retail sales growth was driven almost entirely by consumers taking advantage of the drop in gold prices.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/as-chinas-economy-stumbles-government-eyes-reform/', 'snippet': 'Another set of weak economic data out of China showed that fixed-asset investment slowed, industrial production grew less than projected and retail sales growth was driven almost entirely by consumers taking advantage of the drop in gold prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another week, another set of weak economic data out of China. Fixed-asset investment slowed and industrial production grew less than projected. And while retail sales growth met expectations, it was driven almost entirely by a 72.2 percent increase in jewelry purchases, apparently by consumers taking advantage of the drop in gold prices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As China’s Economy Stumbles, Government Eyes Reform', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T15:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f35c20-190c-59a5-8be7-381ef49076be', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f35c20-190c-59a5-8be7-381ef49076be'}, {'abstract': 'Randomly color a series of dots. Combine according to simple rules. Does order emerge?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/triangle-mysteries/', 'snippet': 'Randomly color a series of dots. Combine according to simple rules. Does order emerge?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s puzzle is based on a beautiful discovery by Steve Humble, who teaches primary and second school trainee teachers in the education department at Newcastle University in northeastern England. The conundrum is based on Mr. Humble’s research that appears in the current issue of The Mathematical Intelligencer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triangle Mysteries', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T16:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b169c30-a3c1-5c1f-9a56-18789bd3a1f6', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b169c30-a3c1-5c1f-9a56-18789bd3a1f6'}, {'abstract': 'The railroad is taking steps to modernize its fleet on the Northeast Corridor and in Pennsylvania, with 70 engines expected by the end of 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/us/amtrak-unveils-new-locomotives.html', 'snippet': 'The railroad is taking steps to modernize its fleet on the Northeast Corridor and in Pennsylvania, with 70 engines expected by the end of 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Amtrak rolled out three new locomotives on Monday, the first step in the railroad’s plan to modernize its aging fleet of trains.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/us/14amtrak/14amtrak