al', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89833817-1b1d-5435-8652-fa1847524e90', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89833817-1b1d-5435-8652-fa1847524e90'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers detected eggs of intestinal worms in stool samples with about 70 percent accuracy using an iPhone with an $8 lens attached.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/health/an-iphone-jury-rigged-as-a-microscope.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers detected eggs of intestinal worms in stool samples with about 70 percent accuracy using an iPhone with an $8 lens attached.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By sticking a little $8 lens to an iPhone with a piece of double-sided tape, a Canadian doctor has produced a microscope that works reasonably well at diagnosing intestinal worms in children.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An iPhone Jury-Rigged as a Microscope', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An iPhone Jury-Rigged as a Microscope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microscopes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parasites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Journal of Tropical Medicine and Hygiene', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T16:19:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person