ions in Bangladesh.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/big-retailers-quit-stalling-on-factory-safety/', 'snippet': 'After many excuses, H&M and other companies signed on to an agreement that should help improve conditions in Bangladesh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After much delay and many excuses, several western retailers and brands on Monday agreed to a plan that should help improve building safety in the garment factories of Bangladesh. The announcement, which came nearly three weeks after the collapse of the Rana Plaza factory building killed more than 1,100 people, is significant because it includes big companies such as H&M, which is the largest buyer of clothing from Bangladesh, and Inditex, the world’s largest fashion retailer whose brands include Zara and Massimo Dutti.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Retailers Quit Stalling on Factory Safety', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'H & M Hennes & Mauritz AB', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T20:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2142119b-57e2-58a7-810a-f3f0666d09fc', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2142119b-57e2-58a7-810a-f3f0666d09fc'}, {'abstract': 'Rangers Coach John Tortorella has demoted Brad Richards, who has the most Game 7 experience on the team, to the fourth line.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/richards-has-game-7-experience-but-has