 'nyt://article/66e40929-9af9-516b-82a9-5d8f0df6bb69', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66e40929-9af9-516b-82a9-5d8f0df6bb69'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Turkey, Bangladesh, Pakistan and Somalia.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/pictures-of-the-day-turkey-and-elsewhere-10/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Turkey, Bangladesh, Pakistan and Somalia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Turkey, Bangladesh, Pakistan and Somalia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Turkey and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T20:43:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edda8cbd-bb9a-5cee-ae72-df34cf96e846', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edda8cbd-bb9a-5cee-ae72-df34cf96e846'}, {'abstract': 'The writer, director and actress explains why she took her own family as her subject for her first documentary, “Stories We Tell.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/talking-talent-sarah-polley/', 'snippet': 'The writer, director and actress explains why she took her own family as her subject for her first documentary, “Stories We Tell.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For her latest film, the Canadian writer, director and actress Sarah Polley turned to her own life. “Stories We Tell,” her first documentary, examines her family’s secrets and mythology — including the question of Polley’s own true parentage — in the wake of her mother’s death from cancer when Polley, now 34, was 11. The documentary, which took her five years to complete, has already kindled Oscar talk for the director, who received an Adapted Screenplay nomination in 2008 for her first film, “Away From Her.” Poignant and moving, “Stories We Tell” confirms that Polley is as good behind the camera as she is on screen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | Sarah Polley', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polley, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stories We Tell (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T20:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff56f22e-3f57-5615-a590-747575dff30a', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff56f22e-3f57-5615-a590-747575dff30a'}, {'abstract': 'The audience members are all front-row, and many have a role in “Everyone Was Chanting Your Name.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/theater/reviews/everyone-was-chanting-your-name-at-abrons-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'The audience members are all front-row, and many have a role in “Everyone Was Chanting Your Name.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the words “audience participation” make you queasy, then “Everyone Was Chanting Your Name” probably isn’t for you. The lights are up at the Abrons Arts Center, and the rectangular seating arrangement is small enough to mean that everyone has a front-row seat: there’s nowhere to hide in this latest production by the rising young theater company 600 Highwaymen.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'