ent_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b30c8812-e087-5318-a9fe-20f5be713567', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b30c8812-e087-5318-a9fe-20f5be713567'}, {'abstract': 'Work on the facility that directs sewage was interrupted by Hurricane Sandy, and plans were modified to reflect lessons learned from the storm, but the project is still expected to be completed this year, officials announced.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/13/upgrades-on-schedule-for-cowanus-canal-pumping-station-despite-hurricane/', 'snippet': 'Work on the facility that directs sewage was interrupted by Hurricane Sandy, and plans were modified to reflect lessons learned from the storm, but the project is still expected to be completed this year, officials announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Hurricane Sandy swept across the Gowanus Canal last year, a pumping station that redirects sewage to a pollution-control plant was damaged and went offline for almost 33 hours, according to a report released by the city after the storm. About 13 million gallons of raw sewage flowed into the canal before the city installed a generator that restored power to the station. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upgrades on Schedule for Gowanus Canal Pumping Station Despite Hurricane', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gowanus Canal (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-13T20:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Hammill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hammill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f786f1d-7295-5ec1-86c6-45ab190bee96', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f786f1d-7295-5ec1-86c6-45ab190bee96'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes, who is accused of killing 12 people in a movie theater, changed his plea on Monday from not guilty to not guilty by reason of insanity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/us/james-holmes-aurora-shooting-suspect-enters-insanity-plea.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes, who is accused of killing 12 people in a movie theater, changed his plea on Monday from not guilty to not guilty by reason of insanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CENTENNIAL, Colo. — Mental health experts who evaluated the man accused of killing 12 people in a Colorado movie theater last year have offered a diagnosis that bolsters an insanity plea in the case, his lawyers said at a hearing here on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mental Evaluations Endorse Insanity Plea in Colorado Shootings, Defense Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Plea Of Insanity In Shooting In Colorado', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value'