litary, and his new tenure may depend on how he gets along with the generals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The last time that Nawaz Sharif had close dealings with the Pakistani Army, soldiers handcuffed him and imprisoned him in an ancient fort overlooking the Indus River, physically dragging him from office in a coup. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/JP-PAKISTAN-1/JP-PAKISTAN-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharif vs. Army, Round 3', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharif vs. Army, Round 3', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musharraf, Pervez', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T01:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/11ee1959-55ca-57e7-8638-270e66028dd6', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11ee1959-55ca-57e7-8638-270e66028dd6'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Kirsten Gillibrand is right in trying to persuade her colleagues not to cut food benefits to families who are living in poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/opinion/this-is-no-time-to-cut-food-stamps.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Kirsten Gillibrand is right in trying to persuade her colleagues not to cut food benefits to families who are living in poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Families who are living in poverty did not spend this nation into debt,” says Senator Kirsten Gillibrand, “and we should not be trying to balance the budget on their backs.” That humane principle will guide the New York Democrat as she seeks to persuade colleagues to resist a proposed $4.1 billion cut in food stamps in an omnibus farm bill heading toward Senate agriculture committee vote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Time to Cut Food Stamps', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Time to Cut Food Stamps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T01:13:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c4f8e08-aeff-5d8a-8ac9-9c99adcea085', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c4f8e08-aeff-5d8a-8ac9-9c99adcea085'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court was correct to rule that a farmer cannot reproduce patented seeds without permission of the patent-holder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/opinion/soybeans-and-the-spirit-of-invention.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court was correct to rule that a farmer cannot reproduce patented seeds without permission of the patent-holder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vernon Bowman, an Indiana farmer, bought a mix of soybean seeds from a grain elevator, planted them in a late-season crop and used seeds harvested from that crop to plant his late crop the following season. Included in that mix (intended mostly for animal feed) were Monsanto’s patented genetically altered seeds, which allow farmers to use herbicide, like Roundup, to kill weeds without damaging the soybean plants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soybeans and the Spirit of Invention', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soybeans and the Spirit of Invention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowman, Vernon Hugh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seeds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T01:13:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/117260c8-dd69-555c-88ec-9ce06238e96e', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/117260c8-dd69-555c-88ec-9ce06238e96e'}, {'abstract': 'Political one-upmanship has just hit a new low with the recent charges leveled against Victoria Nuland, the spokeswoman for the State Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/opinion/brooks-the-next-scapegoat.html', 'snippet': 'Political one-upmanship has just hit a new low with the recent charges leveled against Victoria Nuland, the spokeswoman for the State Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago, when she was a young Foreign Service officer in Moscow, Victoria Nuland gave me a dazzling briefing on the diverse factions inside the Russian parliament. Now she is a friend I typically see a couple times a year, at various functions, and I have watched her rise, working with ever