between that and all of the insanely interesting celebrities I’ve met while cultivating the Celebrity Guest Blogging feature, why, I —', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Status-Seeking Sort', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T02:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/009c221f-f7ca-574f-9be8-0d3538dd782d', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/009c221f-f7ca-574f-9be8-0d3538dd782d'}, {'abstract': 'An agency that is supposed to stay as far away from partisan politics as possible has been left in charge — almost by accident — of regulating a huge amount of election spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/us/politics/irs-ignored-complaints-on-political-spending-by-big-tax-exempt-groups-watchdog-groups-say.html', 'snippet': 'An agency that is supposed to stay as far away from partisan politics as possible has been left in charge — almost by accident — of regulating a huge amount of election spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last two years, government watchdog groups filed more than a dozen complaints with the Internal Revenue Service seeking inquiries into whether large nonprofit organizations like those founded by the Republican political operative Karl Rove and former Obama administration aides had violated their tax-exempt status by spending tens of millions of dollars on political advertising. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headli