yt://article/1ba23282-439d-57f3-9118-1fcd083f0e94'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, accompanied by Katherine Cherbas on cello, sings “Me and My Mother” from Sara Cooper and Zach Redler’s musical.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/in-performance-leslie-kritzer-of-the-memory-show/', 'snippet': 'The actress, accompanied by Katherine Cherbas on cello, sings “Me and My Mother” from Sara Cooper and Zach Redler’s musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the musical “The Memory Show,” Leslie Kritzer plays a woman, identified simply as Daughter, who has moved home to take care of her aging mother, who is in the early stages of Alzheimer’s disease. In the song “Me and My Mother,” Daughter has just witnessed her mother’s first major episode of dementia. The show, with a book and lyrics by Sara Cooper and music by Zach Redler, continues through Saturday at the Duke on 42nd Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Leslie Kritzer of ‘The Memory Show’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kritzer, Leslie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T12:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1305ea92-33df-5791-a85c-214324fd9621', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1305ea92-33df-5791-a85c-214324fd9621'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea said it was open to discussing bringing finished goods and raw materials from an industrial park  that had been jointly operated until North Korea withdrew all its workers an