ks', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Covering Up \r\nTracks on Amazon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20476625-8e0f-5866-902f-a1b76d0cece6', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20476625-8e0f-5866-902f-a1b76d0cece6'}, {'abstract': 'It would be a mistake for Sony to dismiss the hedge fund manager Daniel S. Loeb out of hand: His proposal values Sony’s entertainment businesses at more than half the company’s current market capitalization.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/loebs-bold-bet-on-sony/', 'snippet': 'It would be a mistake for Sony to dismiss the hedge fund manager Daniel S. Loeb out of hand: His proposal values Sony’s entertainment businesses at more than half the company’s current market capitalization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel S. Loeb is taking Japan’s economic renaissance at face value. The hedge fund manager wants Sony to spin off its entertainment arm. Though activists rarely prevail in Japan, Mr. Loeb’s idea may have merit, and Sony should take him seriously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loeb’s Bold Bet on Sony', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirai, Kazuo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Third Point LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Thal Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Thal', 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bca2d704-f31d-579c-a482-98c039407b7f', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bca2d704-f31d-579c-a482-98c039407b7f'}, {'abstract': 'Vermont is the first state to permit physician-assisted suicide by legislation, rather than referendum or court order.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/vermont-passes-aid-in-dying-measure/', 'snippet': 'Vermont is the first state to permit physician-assisted suicide by legislation, rather than referendum or court order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vermont will become the fourth state to make it legal for a physician to prescribe lethal medication to a terminally ill, mentally competent patient who wants to end his life. It has also become the first state to approve the practice through legislation, instead of via a public referendum (as in Oregon and Washington) or a court decision (in Montana).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vermont Passes ‘Aid in Dying’ Measure', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:18:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/442133f0-9fa7-552a-9f5b-55aaadb64540', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/442133f0-9fa7-552a-9f5b-55aaadb64540'}, {'abstract': 'A winter broadcast date for “Downton Abbey” dashes hopes of a simultaneous broadcast in Britain and the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/downton-abbey-to-return-in-january-after-british-broadcast/', 'snippet': 'A winter broadcast date for “Downton Abbey” dashes hopes of a simultaneous broadcast in Britain and the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fourth season of “Downton Abbey” will begin on Jan. 5, an executive producer said on Tuesday, dashing hopes that American and British viewers could watch the hit show at the same time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Downton Abbey’ to Return in January, After British Broadcast', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dac09930-f45b-5cce-89a8-9b09f95c8146', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dac09930-f45b-5cce-89a8-9b09f95c8146'}, {'abstract': 'The Bruins became the first team to overcome a three-goal deficit in the third period of a Game 7 in the N.H.L. playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/the-bruins-make-a-little-more-history.html', 'snippet': 'The Bruins became the first team to overcome a three-goal deficit in the third period of a Game 7 in the N.H.L. playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to hand it to the Boston Bruins. They have this Game 7 thing down to a science. Seriously. How do you top a 2011 Stanley Cup run that featured three Game 7 victories, including a first-round tightrope walk/grudge match in overtime against Montreal? How do you make fans forget last year’s Game 7 overtime loss at home in the first round against Washington? How do you wipe away the epic face plant of 2010, losing not only a 3-0 series lead to hated Philadelphia, but also a 3-0 lead in Game 7 at home?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruins Save Best for Last', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Maple Leafs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergeron, Patrice', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucic, Milan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessel, Phil', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db3b0d4-f862-5ba9-b005-b1bda9425eca', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db3b0d4-f862-5ba9-b005-b1bda9425eca'}, {'abstract': 'What he did was illegal. His crimes don’t really speak to the broader abortion debate.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/what-the-gosnell-case-doesnt-tell-us/', 'snippet': 'What he did was illegal. His crimes don’t really speak to the broader abortion debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A jury in Philadelphia on Monday convicted Kermit Gosnell, a doctor who clearly does not deserve that title before his name, of three counts of first-degree murder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Gosnell Case Doesn’t Mean', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosnell, Kermit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b13a8ba-f723-5a78-a298-9cff01e2fae2', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b13a8ba-f723-5a78-a298-9cff01e2fae2'}, {'abstract': 'Even when they stand right in front of thousands, few know grooms’ names or acknowledge them. Yet they know more about the horse at the end of their lead line than anyone else at the racetrack.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/at-goldencents-side-a-star-in-his-own-way/', 'snippet': 'Even when they stand right in front of thousands, few know grooms’ names or acknowledge them. Yet they know more about the horse at the end of their lead line than anyone else at the racetrack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — They are often the unknowns. Even when they stand right in front of thousands, few know grooms’ names or acknowledge them. Yet they know more about the horse at the end of their lead line than anyone else at the racetrack.\xa0 Often, by the time the horse is loaded into the starting gate, their groom has already spent more than nine hours by their side that day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Goldencents’ Side, a Star in His Own Way', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie June Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'June', 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80905634-5af2-5588-b512-43aad1174a59', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80905634-5af2-5588-b512-43aad1174a59'}, {'abstract': 'A political adviser to Shinzo Abe, Japan’s prime minister, arrived in the North Korean capital Tuesday, but officials in Tokyo would not confirm or comment about the trip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/world/asia/japanese-aide-visits-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'A political adviser to Shinzo Abe, Japan’s prime minister, arrived in the North Korean capital Tuesday, but officials in Tokyo would not confirm or comment about the trip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — A political aide to the prime minister of Japan made a sudden, rare visit to North Korea on Tuesday. Japanese officials refused to say what he was doing there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Aide Makes Rare Trip to North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japanese Aide Makes Rare Trip to North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iijima, Isao', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T14:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e1ed173-ee65-558b-9118-15edebd399f9', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e1ed173-ee65-558b-9118-15edebd399f9'}, {'abstract': 'Comparison shopping for rates won’t hurt your credit score, according to a consumer group.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/nuances-of-credit-scoring-still-elude-consumers/', 'snippet': 'Comparison shopping for rates won’t hurt your credit score, according to a consumer group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumers still have many misunderstandings about the details of credit scoring, like the impact of having several inquiries on their report around the same time, according to the Consumer Federation of America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuances of Credit Scoring Still Elude Consumers', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and D