', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Republicans, Incentives to Strike a Budget Deal With Obama', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Republicans, Incentives to Strike a Budget Deal With Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harwood, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/903404ab-5f2a-53cf-9c05-a1d94f795f41', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/903404ab-5f2a-53cf-9c05-a1d94f795f41'}, {'abstract': 'The Roman Catholic Church will host its first pavilion at the Venice Biennale.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/new-entrant-to-venice-biennale-the-vatican/', 'snippet': 'The Roman Catholic Church will host its first pavilion at the Venice Biennale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY —\xa0It commissioned the Sistine Chapel, countless portraits of popes and even Matisse’s chapel in Vence. Now the Roman Catholic Church will host its first pavilion at the Venice Biennale, featuring the Czech photographer Josef Koudelka, the Milan-based multimedia group Studio Azzurro and the artist Lawrence Carroll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Entrant to Venice Biennale: the Vatican', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Biennale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carroll, Lawrence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koudelka, Josef', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matisse, Henri', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrano, Andres', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eni SpA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vatican Museums', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b0fee76-f98d-52a3-b5cd-129ac9af6aeb', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b0fee76-f98d-52a3-b5cd-129ac9af6aeb'}, {'abstract': 'A publicist said the singer was ordered by her doctors to rest, but she plans to resume performing Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/beyonc-cancels-show-in-belgium/', 'snippet': 'A publicist said the singer was ordered by her doctors to rest, but she plans to resume performing Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyoncé has canceled a concert in Belgium that was scheduled for Tuesday night because she is dehydrated and exhausted, The Associated Press reported. The pop diva’s publicist told the wire service that she has been ordered by her doctors to rest. She had been slated to perform at the Sportpaleis in Antwerp. She has another show at the arena on Wednesday, and her publicist said “she is awaiting word from her doctors before making a decision” about that performance. Beyoncé, 31, started her Mrs. Carter Show World Tour last month in Belgrade, Serbia, and it will finish on Aug. 5 at the Barclays Center in Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 922}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1726, 'width': 1123, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/14artsbeat-beyonce/14artsbeat-beyonce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyoncé Cancels Show in Belgium', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40680ead-36a2-5bfb-a00b-20a76781728b', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40680ead-36a2-5bfb-a00b-20a76781728b'}, {'abstract': 'With the possible exception of Marlon Brando, no male star radiated more magnetism than Burt Lancaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/12/movies/lots-of-lancaster-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'With the possible exception of Marlon Brando, no male star radiated more magnetism than Burt Lancaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the possible exception of Marlon Brando, no male star of his era radiated more raw magnetism than Burt Lancaster, whose centennial is being celebrated by the Film Society of Lincoln Center this Friday through May 23. Nowadays, macho preening too often passes for the kind of feral grace radiated by Lancaster in films like “The Killers,” the 1946 noir classic adapted from a Ernest Hemingway short story and directed by Robert Siodmak. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lots of Lancaster at Lincoln Center', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lots of Lancaster At Lincoln Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:18:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54332d88-4aed-517c-b091-7e5f9cdbbfe6', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54332d88-4aed-517c-b091-7e5f9cdbbfe6'}, {'abstract': 'The National Transportation Safety Board is recommending that states reduce the allowable blood-alcohol content to 0.05 percent, instead of the current 0.08 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/us/legal-limit-drunken-driving-safety-board.html', 'snippet': 'The National Transportation Safety Board is recommending that states reduce the allowable blood-alcohol content to 0.05 percent, instead of the current 0.08 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Thousands of people are killed or injured every year by drivers who have not reached the legal standard for being drunk but who have a reduced ability to see, make decisions or operate a vehicle, the National Transportation Safety Board said on Tuesday, and it recommended that the states reduce the allowable blood-alcohol concentration by more than a third, to 0.05 percent from 0.08 percent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/us/15drunk/15drunk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'States Urged to Cut Limit on Alcohol for Drivers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'States Urged To Cut Limit On Alcohol For Drivers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Sobriety)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mothers Against Drunk Driving', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:27:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f646fcdf-4ccc-53c1-905e-d7d2383c0a9b', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f646fcdf-4ccc-53c1-905e-d7d2383c0a9b'}, {'abstract': 'Where to stay, eat and sleep in this remote market town.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/travel-essentials-taroudant-morocco/', 'snippet': 'Where to stay, eat and sleep in this remote market town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our Summer Travel issue, which hit newsstands on Sunday, Christopher Petkanas waxes poetic about Taroudant, an out-of-the-way, stylish haven from Morocco’s well-trodden tourist route. Here’s where to stay, eat and sleep in this remote market town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Essentials | Taroudant, Morocco', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac1311d6-829c-57db-ae09-89ddab76d8e5', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac1311d6-829c-57db-ae09-89ddab76d8e5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Crystal’s autobiographical one-man show about growing up on Long Island was a box-office hit and a Tony Award-winner when it was first presented on Broadway in 2004 and 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/billy-crystal-bringing-700-sundays-back-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Crystal’s autobiographical one-man show about growing up on Long Island was a box-office hit and a Tony Award-winner when it was first presented on Broadway in 2004 and 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Billy Crystal keeps this up, he eventually will have performed “700 Sundays” for, well, 700 Sundays. On Tuesday, Mr. Crystal, the comedian, actor and erstwhile Oscars host, said that he will bring “700 Sundays,” his Tony Award-winning one-man show about growing up on Long Island, back to Broadway in the fall for a nine-week run that is being described as the production’s final engagement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/crystal/crystal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 184, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/crystal/crystal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 184, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/crystal/crystal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/crystal/crystal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Billy Crystal Bringing  ‘700 Sundays’ Back to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crystal, Billy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value'