ce Agency officer.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/video-of-americans-arrest-in-moscow/', 'snippet': 'Russia’s Federal Security Service, the successor to the Soviet-era K.G.B., released photographs and video of Tuesday’s arrest of an American accused of being a Central Intelligence Agency officer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, Wednesday, 12:06 p.m. As my colleague Ellen Barry reports from Moscow, Russia’s Federal Security Service, the successor to the Soviet-era K.G.B., announced Tuesday that it had arrested a Central Intelligence Agency officer posing as an American diplomat as he tried to recruit a Russian agent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1465, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/world/europe/14lede_moscow/14lede_moscow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of American’s Arrest in Moscow', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFaul, Michael A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Security Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8717d424-6cc1-5778-adc3-cd4a47248ecb', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8717d424-6cc1-5778-adc3-cd4a47248ecb'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/the-gun-report-may-14-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, Brandon Holt, 6, was shot and killed by a 4-year-old boy in Toms River, N.J., kicking off a bloody month in which several toddlers accidentally shot other toddlers. The 4-year-old got a hold of his father’s .22 caliber rifle and brought it into the yard, where it went off, hitting Holt in the head. Yesterday it was announced that Anthony Senatore, 33, the father of the “gunman,” was arrested for having multiple unsecured weapons accessible to children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 14, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMARILLO (TEX)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Joplin (Mo)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toms River (NJ)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia and Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43c19fae-e714-5757-b69a-cf74caec94a8', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43c19fae-e714-5757-b69a-cf74caec94a8'}, {'abstract': 'The German bank will try to raise 2.5 billion euros ($3.2 billion), to protect against future shocks and to help repay a 2009 government bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/commerzbank-to-raise-3-2-billion-in-new-capital/', 'snippet': 'The German bank will try to raise 2.5 billion euros ($3.2 billion), to protect against future shocks and to help repay a 2009 government bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — European banks have gone on a capital-raising binge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulatory Pressure Drives Commerzbank to Seek Out New Capital', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerzbank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27443674-3f3a-539e-806d-6ee351d2e6a0', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27443674-3f3a-539e-806d-6ee351d2e6a0'}, {'abstract': 'Suzanne Davidson will replace Norma Hurlburt, who has held the post since 2000.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/a-new-executive-director-for-chamber-music-society-of-lincoln-center/', 'snippet': 'Suzanne Davidson will replace Norma Hurlburt, who has held the post since 2000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center has appointed Suzanne Davidson as its new executive director, starting on July 1. She succeeds Norma Hurlburt, the society’s director since 2000. Ms. Hurlburt is leaving to start her own consulting business for nonprofit organizations. The society also announced that its artistic directors, the cellist David Finckel and the pianist Wu Han, who are married, had renewed their contract for a third term, which will take them through the 2018-19 season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Executive Director for Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finckel, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurlburt, Norma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu Han', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Law School', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of American Ballet', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T15:47:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14662947-dbb0-5470-b6cb-2b16c14395bb', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14662947-dbb0-5470-b6cb-2b16c14395bb'}, {'abstract': 'A rickshaw ride in the Cardamom Hills of Kerala, in southwestern India, leads to instruction in a fragrant local dish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/dining/taking-a-curry-cooking-class-in-kerala.html', 'snippet': 'A rickshaw ride in the Cardamom Hills of Kerala, in southwestern India, leads to instruction in a fragrant local dish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kumily, India — One of the best parts of traveling, at least for me, is bringing back a food story, a new ingredient or a recipe. My family journeyed last year from the verdant tea plantations of Munnar down to the Cardamom Hills of Kerala, in southwestern India. Our driver, Janaki Raman, who had proved himself by dodging many a cow on the winding mountain roads, asked whether we might like to go to a local cooking class.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/dining/15CURRY_SPAN/15CURRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/dining/15CURRY_SPAN/15CURRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/dining/15CURRY_SPAN/15CURRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre