ame': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/125e6924-4064-567e-be11-d483019c5fa1', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/125e6924-4064-567e-be11-d483019c5fa1'}, {'abstract': 'In the midst of the premieres, the AIDS research nonprofit hosts a swanky benefit dedicated to the precious metal.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/objects-amfar-goes-for-the-gold-at-cannes/', 'snippet': 'In the midst of the premieres, the AIDS research nonprofit hosts a swanky benefit dedicated to the precious metal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midway through this year’s Cannes film festival, A-listers will take a break from the red carpets to attend amfAR’s annual Cinema Against AIDS benefit at the glamorous Hotel du Cap-Eden-Roc on the French Riviera. The highlight will be the Ultimate Gold Collection Fashion Show, an all-gold runway presentation curated by Carine Roitfeld. It will feature 40 models (including “It” girl Karlie Kloss and Daria Strokous, one of the faces of the current Christian Dior ad campaign) in one-of-a-kind gowns by the likes of Comme des Garcons, Alexander Wang, Giorgio Armani and Valentino, which will be auctioned after the show. They’ll be wearing bespoke jewelry made from the precious metal, commissioned by Roitfeld, including the cuffs seen above by the chic, celebrity-endorsed designers (from left) Kimberly McDonald, Hoorsenbuhs and Ana Khouri. The pieces will subsequently be made to order at LoveGold, an online community dedicated to gold jewelry. The site, in its first year as a presenting sponsor for the gala, will live stream exclusive footage of the catwalk on May 23.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Objects | amfAR Goes for the Gold at Cannes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Objects: At Cannes, Going for Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'amfAR, The Foundation for AIDS Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T17:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/407394b7-e985-5107-8e76-b4793fef4da4', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/407394b7-e985-5107-8e76-b4793fef4da4'}, {'abstract': 'Like the West, the East has one matchup of Original Six teams. But that is just one subplot as rivalries old and new are renewed.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/eastern-conference-semifinals-no-love-lost-between-foes/', 'snippet': 'Like the West, the East has one matchup of Original Six teams. But that is just one subplot as rivalries old and new are renewed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like the West, the East has one matchup of Original Six teams. But that is just one subplot as rivalries old and new are renewed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15karlsson/15karlsson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15karlsson/15karlsson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/sports/hockey/15karlsson/15karlsson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 68