d herself a recovering alcoholic, which is a less unusual distinction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Politician’s Disclosure Offers a Lesson in Eating Disorders', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharing a Battle Against an Eating Disorder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANOREXIA NERVOSA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bulimia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T17:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab42fefc-7ebe-5284-a4ee-78d252815481', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab42fefc-7ebe-5284-a4ee-78d252815481'}, {'abstract': 'Wal-Mart, rejecting a safety plan backed by more than a dozen European companies, said its monitors would “conduct in-depth safety inspections” at all factories it uses in Bangladesh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/business/six-retailers-join-bangladesh-factory-pact.html', 'snippet': 'Wal-Mart, rejecting a safety plan backed by more than a dozen European companies, said its monitors would “conduct in-depth safety inspections” at all factories it uses in Bangladesh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As American retailers face mounting pressure to join a landmark plan to improve factory safety in Bangladesh, newly found documents indicate that apparel had been produced for Wal-