ason/', 'snippet': 'The Miller Theater will celebrate the 60th birthday of John Zorn and will continue its two popular series, Composer Portraits and Pop-Up Concerts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The highlights of the 25th season of the Miller Theater at the Columbia University School of the Arts will include a festival celebrating the 60th birthday of John Zorn, the new music maverick; and an evening of 125 short compositions modeled after John Cage, whose centennial was last year. \xa0And back for the 2013-14 season is the Composer Portraits series, featuring the work of and discussions with Georg Friedrich Haas, Rand Steiger, Anna Thorvaldsdottir, Roger Reynolds, Unsuk Chin, Jean-Baptiste Barrière and Liza Lim.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miller Theater Announces New Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T20:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03bbaff9-ad09-53a9-a4be-860b3ff8ab70', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03bbaff9-ad09-53a9-a4be-860b3ff8ab70'}, {'abstract': 'A government adviser has suggested that manufacturers pay a 1 percent levy on the price of the devices to finance French movies, music and books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/business/global/france-urged-to-impose-tax-on-smartphones-and-tablets.html', 'snippet': 'A government adviser has suggested that manufacturers pay a 1 percent levy on the price of the devices to finance French movies, music and books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France’s “cultural exception” — the policy that creative works like books, music and movies deserve protection beyond what is accorded ordinary goods — is in line for a digital update. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Culture Moves Online, France Tries to Follow It With a Tax', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Plan\r\nWould Tax\r\nElectronics,\r\nFor Culture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T20:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b457e81c-119c-5242-993e-7281d56e22a7', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b457e81c-119c-5242-993e-7281d56e22a7'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities canceled a ceremony for the team, Paris Saint-Germain, after rampaging fans injured 32 people after the team’s victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/world/europe/paris-cancels-celebration-for-soccer-champions.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities canceled a ceremony for the team, Paris Saint-Germain, after rampaging fans injured 32 people after the team’s victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Officials canceled a city hall ceremony for the champions of France’s national soccer league on Tuesday after hundreds of rampaging fans attacked stores, cars and police officers in the capital during celebrations on Monday night. The violence, which left 32 people injured and 38 fans in police custody, erupted at an official celebration for Paris Saint-Germain, the winning team, near a neighborhood overlooking the Eiffel Tower.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Cancels Celebration for Soccer Champions', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Soccer Riots Scuttle Ceremony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris St-Germain FC (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T20:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be87f6e8-a9be-5015-92ba-4048be8c9d14', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be87f6e8-a9be-5015-92ba-4048be8c9d14'}, {'abstract': 'The unidentified substance was found in an envelope in the consulate in the southern city of Guangzhou, prompting the closing of some operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/world/asia/suspicious-substance-disrupts-us-consulate-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'The unidentified substance was found in an envelope in the consulate in the southern city of Guangzhou, prompting the closing of some operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Staff members at the United States Consulate in the southern Chinese city of Guangzhou discovered a suspicious substance in an envelope on Monday, prompting the closing of some operations. The substance, which was found in a part of the consulate not open to the public, has yet to be identified. No consulate workers have suffered any ill effects and no visitors are believed to have been exposed, said Nolan Barkhouse, a spokesman for the United States Embassy in Beijing. “The consulate has notified Chinese authorities and is maintaining close contact with them in case any assistance becomes necessary,” Mr. Barkhouse said. The consulate was closed for visa interviews on Tuesday and will remain closed Wednesday pending an investigation. The consulate handles 121,000 visa applications annually and processes all immigrant visas for Chinese children adopted by American citizens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspicious Substance Disrupts U.S. Consulate in China', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T20:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/be2ef552-ef4b-572a-aa9f-b7f8e29daedf', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be2ef552-ef4b-572a-aa9f-b7f8e29daedf'}, {'abstract': 'To justify Tesla’s high 2016 valuation multiple, revenue would need to keep growing at a fast clip, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/14/teslas-stock-is-trading-at-rich-multiples/', 'snippet': 'To justify Tesla’s high 2016 valuation multiple, revenue would need to keep growing at a fast clip, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tesla’s shareholders seem to be assuming that its chief executive, Elon Musk, is infallible. Tesla, the electric carmaker, is on a roll. Last week, it recorded its first quarterly profit and received the best score that Consumer Reports has bestowed on a car for six years. The company’s stock has since surged as much as 70 percent, leaving Tesla worth more than Fiat and Peugeot combined. Its stock is also trading at a whopping 27 times estimates for earnings in 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tesla’s Stock Is Trading at Rich Multiples', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-14T20:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17e2c794-ce20-59c7-8da7-5e0ad6135b65', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17e2c794-ce20-59c7-8da7-5e0ad6135b65'}, {'abstract': 'A time lapse of a video released by the Port Authority shows the spire being raised to the top 