: 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db1b1da-ab86-50a4-b12e-60e175f97817', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db1b1da-ab86-50a4-b12e-60e175f97817'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s indisputably defective death penalty system is made more horrifying by attempts to rush inmates to execution. Gov. Rick Scott should veto the Timely Justice Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/opinion/grotesque-speed-for-florida-capital-cases.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s indisputably defective death penalty system is made more horrifying by attempts to rush inmates to execution. Gov. Rick Scott should veto the Timely Justice Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Timely Justice Act, a grotesquely named bill passed by the Florida Legislature, could get to Gov. Rick Scott as soon as this week for him to sign into law. The measure would require a governor to sign a death warrant within 30 days of a review of a capital conviction by the State Supreme Court, and the state would be required to execute the defendant within 180 days of the warrant. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grotesque Speed for Florida Capital Cases', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grotesque Speed for Florida Capital Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aguirre-Jarquin, Clemente Javier', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T01:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial B