html', 'snippet': 'According to the Justice Department, Apple took a leadership role in a price-fixing conspiracy in the market for e-books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The e-mail, from Steve Jobs of Apple to James Murdoch of News Corporation, reads as if one old sport were trying to cajole another into joining a caper: “Throw in with Apple and see if we can all make a go of this to create a real mainstream e-books market at $12.99 and $14.99.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Now Paints Apple as ‘Ringmaster’ in Its Lawsuit on E-Book Price-Fixing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Now Paints Apple as ‘Ringmaster’ In Its Lawsuit on E-Book Price-Fixing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Macmillan Publishers', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Group', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon & Schuster Inc', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T02:33:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne