uri': 'nyt://article/e269ca43-909e-51c8-87c0-3b09bd367678'}, {'abstract': 'Kobo has produced what it said is the highest resolution e-ink reader, the $170 Aura HD. But how does it match up to other e-ink devices?', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/kobos-new-e-reader-is-sharp-but-maybe-not-sharp-enough/', 'snippet': 'Kobo has produced what it said is the highest resolution e-ink reader, the $170 Aura HD. But how does it match up to other e-ink devices?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kobo has produced what it said was the highest-resolution e-ink reader, the Aura HD, which means it should have the best-looking screen, right?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kobo’s New E-Reader Is Sharp, but Maybe Not Sharp Enough', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New E-Reader’s Display Allows for Customized Fonts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kobo Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T11:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc70e6b8-e388-5eb8-919e-6da66747af81', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc70e6b8-e388-5eb8-919e-6da66747af81'}, {'abstract': 'How the gypsy cuisine of China ended up in restaurants all over the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/hakka-dishes-that-helped-define-chinese-restaurant-cooking-in-america.html', 'snippet': 'How the gypsy cuisine of China ended up in restaurants all over the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When “The Hakka Cookbook” appeared last year, I immediately set up a cooking date with its author, Linda Lau Anusasananan, who lives in the exotic and far-flung city of San Mateo, south of San Francisco.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19eat1/19eat1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nomad’s Kitchen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "The Nomad's Kitchen", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Hakka Cookbook (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anusasananan, Linda Lau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30586108-3e79-5224-bb2a-812f21113355', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30586108-3e79-5224-bb2a-812f21113355'}, {'abstract': 'Medicine used to be obsessed with eradicating the tiny bugs that live within us. Now we’re beginning to understand all the ways they keep us healthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/say-hello-to-the-100-trillion-bacteria-that-make-up-your-microbiome.html', 'snippet': 'Medicine used to be obsessed with eradicating the tiny bugs that live within us. Now we’re beginning to understand all the ways they keep us healthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can tell you the exact date that I began to think of myself in the first-person plural — as a superorganism, that is, rather than a plain old individual human being. It happened on March 7. That’s when I opened my e-mail to find a huge, processor-choking file of charts and raw data from a laboratory located at the BioFrontiers Institute at the University of Colorado, Boulder. As part of a new citizen-science initiative called the American Gut project, the lab sequenced my microbiome — that is, the genes not of “me,” exactly, but of the several hundred microbial species with whom I share this body. These bacteria, which number around 100 trillion, are living (and dying) right now on the surface of my skin, on my tongue and deep in the coils of my intestines, where the largest contingent of them will be found, a pound or two of microbes together forming a vast, largely uncharted interior wilderness that scientists are just beginning to map.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/mag-19microbiome-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/mag-19microbiome-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 709}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/mag-19microbiome-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/mag-19microbiome-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 1124, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/19microbiome3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/19microbiome3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19microbiome3/19microbiome3-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some of My Best Friends Are Germs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some of My Best Friends Are Bacteria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollan, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intestinal Tract', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, Rob', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lozupone, Catherine A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dominguez-Bello, Maria Gloria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sonnenburg, Justin L', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T11:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52927b9c-e4fb-5a2b-9140-a834024e0c72', 'word_count': 7677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52927b9c-e4fb-5a2b-9140-a834024e0c72'}, {'abstract': 'Even before American skies are open to commercially operated drones, a drone start-up called Airware plans to announce Wednesday that it has rai