rom a consortium of investment firms that could have valued the company at more than $8 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Water Utility Rejects Takeover Offer', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T11:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/010fc7b8-2d4b-5633-9eb5-f7587f5a8202', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/010fc7b8-2d4b-5633-9eb5-f7587f5a8202'}, {'abstract': 'The French dance-music duo known for its synthetic dazzle has made its new album a flashback to the era of live musicianship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/arts/music/daft-punk-gets-human-with-a-new-album.html', 'snippet': 'The French dance-music duo known for its synthetic dazzle has made its new album a flashback to the era of live musicianship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Thomas Bangalter, half of the influential French dance-music act Daft Punk, has a house high in the Hollywood Hills here. He and his musical partner, Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo, divide their time between Los Angeles and Paris, where their families live. But for all their jet-setting, there’s little evidence of rock star flash to be seen (well, apart from the Porsche that Mr. de Homem-Christo has parked in the driveway). Built in the midcentury style called post and beam, the bungalow exudes a subtle retro feel, with white carpeting, a cross section of a tree trunk as a coffee table, and a gravel fireplace in the living room. The swimming pool, a small square of radiant Hockney blue, is visible through the glass walls. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 879, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 879}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1399, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19DAFT-PUNK/19DAFT-PUNK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daft Punk Gets Human With a New Album', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Almost Human', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daft Punk (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article',