oom', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pianos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Heights (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T12:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/853d5eca-f6a7-50b6-9add-5a4b8d07a2c1', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853d5eca-f6a7-50b6-9add-5a4b8d07a2c1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. LaBeouf, a star of “Transformers,” “Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull” and “The Company You Keep,” explains his film inspired by the Future Unlimited song “Haunted Love,” which came about while he worked on the Lars von Trier film “Nymphomaniac.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/for-his-latest-transformation-shia-labeouf-discusses-his-short-film-haunted-love/', 'snippet': 'Mr. LaBeouf, a star of “Transformers,” “Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull” and “The Company You Keep,” explains his film inspired by the Future Unlimited song “Haunted Love,” which came about while he worked on the Lars von Trier ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though there’s been no shortage of talk in recent weeks about work that Shia LaBeouf didn’t do, here’s a look at something that this unpredictable actor did do. Mr. LaBeouf, 26, is better known for his acting roles in movies like “Transformers,” “Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull” and “The Company You Keep,” but he has also dabbled in the occasional bit of film directing, including his short films “Maniac” (with the hip-hop star Kid Cudi) and “Born Villain” (with Marilyn Manson). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/shia/shia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 248, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/shia/shia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 248, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/shia/shia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/shia/shia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/arts/shia/shia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For His Latest Transformation, Shia LaBeouf Discusses His Short Film ‘Haunted Love’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaBeouf, Shia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Trier, Lars', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/010c09ef-7413-5504-95bd-254c91a682d3', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/010c09ef-7413-5504-95bd-254c91a682d3'}, {'abstract': 'Dual-time display, made popular by Pan Am pilots, has made a prominent return.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/market-report-the-g-m-t-watch-makes-a-comeback/', 'snippet': 'Dual-time display, made popular by Pan Am pilots, has made a prominent return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rolex debuted the first G.M.T. watch, which featured an additional hour hand to represent Greenwich Mean Time, in the 1950s. Pan Am pilots popularized the dual-time display, which allowed them to keep track of local time while flying across time zones, and inspired a slew of watchmakers to create their own G.M.T. products. Although they’ve been less popular in recent years, a recent wave of releases shows that these watches are coming back in a big way. Here are 12 of the best newcomers. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | The G.M.T. Watch Makes a Comeback', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Report: A World Traveler Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bda2208-8294-5bc2-9f52-d42dff10f2ab', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bda2208-8294-5bc2-9f52-d42dff10f2ab'}, {'abstract': 'As world leaders and commentators of every stripe have debated President Obama’s “red line,” there have been significant developments on the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/battlefield-update-the-fight-for-isolated-government-outposts-in-northern-syria/', 'snippet': 'As world leaders and commentators of every stripe have debated President Obama’s “red line,” there have been significant developments on the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent weeks considerable public attention has turned to questions of whether government forces in Syria have used chemical weapons. And all the while, conventional fighting with conventional weapons – the dominant form of violence and source of killing in this and most every war of our time – has continued to rage. As world leaders and commentators of every stripe have debated President Obama’s “red line,” there have been developments on the ground, which might herald tactical shifts and point to the verifiable, actual slog that is the Syrian civil war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battlefield Update: The Fight for Isolated Government Outposts in Northern Syria', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa51d604-bd12-58e4-8e10-438c0355c022', 'word_count': 1821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa51d604-bd12-58e4-8e10-438c0355c022'}, {'abstract': 'Maoist leadership is facing a crisis, mainly because most of the top rebel leaders have either been killed or arrested in the last few years.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/in-andhra-maoist-rebels-pin-hopes-on-memories-of-the-dead/', 'snippet': 'Maoist leadership is facing a crisis, mainly because most of the top rebel leaders have either been killed or arrested in the last few years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On April 16, Maoist rebels, operating in the dense forests of central and eastern India received a major blow when security forces killed one of their senior commanders, along with his wife and seven other rebels in Chhattisgarh, very close to the border of Andhra Pradesh. The slain commander, Marri Ravi, alias Sudhakar, was entrusted by the outlawed rebel group Communist Party of India (Maoist) to revive its movement in Andhra after the rebels were crushed seven years ago in their erstwhile bastion following a sustained military operation against them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/world/asia/13-notice-board-IndiaInk/13-notice-board-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/13/world/asia/13-notice-board-IndiaInk/13-notice-board-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 483}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/13/world/asia/13-notice-board-IndiaInk/13-notice-board-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u