bank-of-england-raises-outlook-for-economy.html', 'snippet': 'After years of warnings, the central bank governor, Mervyn A. King, said a recovery was “in sight.” Unemployment, however, rose in the first quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After five years of dire warnings about the state of the British economy, the governor of the Bank of England raised the outlook for growth on Wednesday and said a recovery was “in sight.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of England Raises Outlook for British Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank of England Raises Outlook for British Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Werdigier, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Mervyn A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:37:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79ceb8f0-d39a-5cb4-82e5-96c9505708d6', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79ceb8f0-d39a-5cb4-82e5-96c9505708d6'}, {'abstract': 'Sallie L. Krawcheck, a former executive of Bank of America and Citigroup, has agreed to buy 85 Broads, a global organization that supports women.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/krawcheck-to-buy-womens-network-85-broads/', 'snippet': 'Sallie L. Krawcheck, a former executive of Bank of America and Citigroup, has agreed to buy 85 Broads, a global organization that supports women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sallie L. Krawcheck, a former executive of Bank of America and Citigroup, has agreed to buy 85 Broads, a global organization that supports women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Krawcheck Agrees to Buy the Women’s Network 85 Broads', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:44:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ec024b4-379e-5828-bb55-5a7eb984cca2', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ec024b4-379e-5828-bb55-5a7eb984cca2'}, {'abstract': 'Why would dad-blogger conferences merit more respect from traditional news media than those attended primarily by moms?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/the-daddy-business-trip/', 'snippet': 'Why would dad-blogger conferences merit more respect from traditional news media than those attended primarily by moms?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was in a pile of men on the floor of a suite at the Ritz-Carlton in Laguna Niguel, Calif., a wineglass in one hand and a remote in the other. My pilemates brandished cocktails and bonbons. One of them had his head lodged in the open minibar. Two dozen fellow conference-goers surrounded us, their iPhone cameras flashing at the slovenly heap. Isn’t this what business trips are all about? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/style/motherlode-dad-blog-conference/motherlode-dad-blog-conference-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daddy Business Trip', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosman, Katherine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T13:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Hinds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hinds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/899bbed2-2113-5eaf-9f63-b9d0e1935a84', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/899bbed2-2113-5eaf-9f63-b9d0e1935a84'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/what-were-reading-for-wednesday/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guardian: Sometimes, Emma Sturgess argues, white bread is the right bread. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T14:02:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e35578d-df87-572b-b4e5-a80f422970f5', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e35578d-df87-572b-b4e5-a80f422970f5'}, {'abstract': 'A group called Blue Engine that places recent college graduates as full-time teaching assistants in a few public high schools is showing promising results.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/a-team-approach-to-get-students-college-ready/', 'snippet': 'A group called Blue Engine that places recent college graduates as full-time teaching assistants in a few public high schools is showing promising results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Parker Sheffy, a first-year teacher in the Bronx Leadership Academy II, a high school in the South Bronx, talks shop with friends who are also new teachers, he often hears about the problems they are facing: students not showing up to class on time, not understanding their work, not doing homework. “I’m thinking: I don’t have that problem… I don’t have that problem…” Sheffy recalled. In his ninth grade integrated algebra class, he estimates that 80 to 90 percent are on track to pass the Regents exam, more than double last year’s figure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Team Approach to Get Students College Ready', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T14:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f00e6802-2cd9-5e64-85da-f0a9dbd6ec66', 'word_count': 1877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f00e6802-2cd9-5e64-85da-f0a9dbd6ec66'}, {'abstract': 'Crews of smiling pets get to work in two new picture books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/books/construction-kitties-and-dig-dogs-dig.html', 'snippet': 'Crews of smiling pets get to work in two new picture books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the wildly successful “Goodnight, Goodnight, Construction Site” has shown, stories about trucks need not be tough. There can be warm, fuzzy elements amid the concrete and scrap metal. Even a teddy bear can find its way in. Perhaps there’s just something appealing about the juxtaposition of soft, fluffy animals and heavy-metal loaders, which feature in two new picture books this season. In both “Construction Kitties,” by Judy Sue Goodwin Sturges, with illustrations by Shari Halpern, and “Dig, Dogs, Dig,” by James Horvath, a crew of smiling pets get to work building — what else? — a playground.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/books/15childrens-2/15childrens-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/books/15childrens-2/15childrens-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/books/15childrens-2/15childrens-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/books/15childrens-2/15childrens-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/books/15childrens-2/15childrens-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im