e7f21-f65e-593b-9624-749be895965b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a4fe7f21-f65e-593b-9624-749be895965b'}, {'abstract': 'Does the improving deficit picture vindicate the White House’s policy approach?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/the-obama-synthesis-vindicated/', 'snippet': 'Does the improving deficit picture vindicate the White House’s policy approach?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having noted the ways in which the the recent scandals (and other developments) pose a challenge to this administration’s distinctive political/policy synthesis, I should also take note of the piece of recent news that makes that synthesis look better than it sometimes has. That news would be the latest deficit projections, as summarized by my colleague Annie Lowrey:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Obama Synthesis, Vindicated?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T16:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18614b14-97a1-50b5-8a70-2539a425c8c4', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18614b14-97a1-50b5-8a70-2539a425c8c4'}, {'abstract': 'A Broadway revival of “The Winslow Boy” will take the place of a planned production of “The Philadelphia Story.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/roundabout-theater-announces-changes-to-fall-season/', 'snippet': 'A Broadway revival of “The Winslow Boy” will take the place of a planned production of “The Philadelphia Story.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Broadway revival of Philip Barry’s classic comedy “The Philadelphia Story,” which the Tony Award nominee Alex Timbers (“Peter and the Starcatcher”) was to direct this fall, has been postponed, Roundabout Theater Company announced on Wednesday. Replacing that show will be a revival of Terence Rattigan’s 1946 drama, “The Winslow Boy,” starring Roger Rees (a Tony winner for “The Life and Adventures of Nicholas Nickleby”) and Mary Elizabeth Mastrantonio and directed by Lindsay Posner, who recently staged the play at the Old Vic in London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roundabout Theater Announces Changes to Fall Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T16:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdc40513-8575-54a2-ae76-9ff98cb87da0', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdc40513-8575-54a2-ae76-9ff98cb87da0'}, {'abstract': 'Starting this month, the travel company Airstream 2 Go will rent current-model Airstream trailers.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/for-rent-airstreams/', 'snippet': 'Starting this month, the travel company Airstream 2 Go will rent current-model Airstream trailers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If ever a recreational vehicle could be called iconic, it would be the Airstream. The sausage-shaped silvery aluminum trailer has been a fixture of American road trips since the company’s founding in 1931, but before this year it was available only for purchase. Starting this month, the travel company Airstream 2 Go will rent current-model Airstream trailers outfitted with flat-screen televisions, camping chairs, tables and barbecue grills, as well as GMC Yukons to pull them for journeys of at least five days. Initial rental locations include Las Vegas and Los Angeles, but there are plans to expand to other cities across the country.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Rent: Airstreams', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On The Road: For Rent: Airstreams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b832a68-42a3-57a6-b434-151505b4f605', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b832a68-42a3-57a6-b434-151505b4f605'}, {'abstract': 'Possible steering system failure prompts Subaru to recall thousands of 2013 Outback and Legacy models.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/subaru-to-recall-5400-vehicles-for-possible-steering-failure/', 'snippet': 'Possible steering system failure prompts Subaru to recall thousands of 2013 Outback and Legacy models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Subaru will recall nearly 5,400 2013 Outback and Legacy models because the steering may fail, the automaker has informed the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration. In a report posted on the agency’s Web site, Subaru said the inner and outer shafts of the steering column assembly could lose contact with one another, in which case “the driver would lose the ability to steer the vehicle.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subaru to Recall 5,400 Vehicles for Possible Steering Failure', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee6c76ea-47c7-5817-96c9-ab512cb971e5', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee6c76ea-47c7-5817-96c9-ab512cb971e5'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Loren Fishman, a rehabilitative medicine specialist, addresses reader questions about yoga, aging, osteoporosis,  shoulder pain and other issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/booming/advice-on-practicing-yoga-in-middle-age-part-2.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Loren Fishman, a rehabilitative medicine specialist, addresses reader questions about yoga, aging, osteoporosis,  shoulder pain and other issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the second set of answers to reader questions from Dr. Loren Fishman, a back-pain and rehabilitative medicine specialist who has long incorporated yoga into patient care. In 1972, before applying to medical school, he studied yoga with B.K.S. Iyengar for a year in Pune, India. Dr. Fishman is the medical director of Manhattan Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation in New York City, an assistant clinical professor at Columbia Medical School and an associate editor of the journal Topics in Geriatric Rehabilitation. He is also an author of eight books, including “Yoga for Osteoporosis: the Complete Guide.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 209, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 209, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/booming/01expertquery-booming-yoga1/01expertquery-booming-yoga1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice on Practicing Yoga in Middle Age, Part 2', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'nam