3/05/16/us/irs-says-counsel-didnt-tell-treasury-of-tea-party-scrutiny.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration stepped up pressure on the Internal Revenue Service and sought to insulate itself from the outcry over the agency’s special scrutiny of conservative groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama announced Wednesday night that the acting commissioner of the Internal Revenue Service had been ousted after disclosures that the agency gave special scrutiny to conservative groups. Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., meanwhile, warned top I.R.S. officials that a Justice Department inquiry would examine any false statements to see if they constituted a crime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/us/Obama/Obama-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S. Chief Out After Protest Over Scrutiny of Groups', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Outcry, Chief of I.R.S. Is Forced Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Steven T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkins, William J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lerner, Lois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92e5bc8a-966b-5bf2-951b-c2dbdcf1642c', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92e5bc8a-966b-5bf2-951b-c2dbdcf1642c'}, {'abstract': 'Brooks and Collins on the I.R.S.’s attack on the Tea Party and the Justice Department’s disdain for the First Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/the-taxman-cometh/', 'snippet': 'Brooks and Collins on the I.R.S.’s attack on the Tea Party and the Justice Department’s disdain for the First Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David, as you know, I’m from Cincinnati. Some people may think of it as just another city in Ohio, but there has been a lot of drama coming out of Cincinnati over the years. One of the stars of the savings and loan scandal of the ’80s, Charles Keating, used to lecture at the Catholic girls’ high school I went to. The lectures were not about finance but rather on the sinfulness of wearing shorts in the summertime. However, my point is that stuff happens in Cincinnati.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Taxman Cometh', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carper, Thomas R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:23:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e925f792-99f3-58a3-aed9-7b741ecc50a3', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e925f792-99f3-58a3-aed9-7b741ecc50a3'}, {'abstract': 'In her final post, Candice Childress, a high school senio