the-iraq-war/', 'snippet': 'In a new oral history of the Iraq war, Peter van Agtmael discusses what attracted him to photographing the American-led invasion — his roots, ambitions, experiences and reflections.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Photojournalists on War,” an oral history of the Iraq war by those who documented it from the front lines, was published this month by the University of Texas Press. The book consists of interviews conducted by Michael Kamber, who covered the war for eight years for The New York Times and is a co-founder of the Bronx Documentary Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photographer’s Unfiltered Account of the Iraq War', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berman, Nina (1960- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hetherington, Tim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hondros, Chris', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Eugene', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Joao', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f7bba44-f24d-52be-863f-24823361544e', 'word_count': 1876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f7bba44-f24d-52be-863f-24823361544e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Star Trek Into Darkness,” the U.S.S. Enterprise crew hunts for a terrorist in the latest film in the franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/movies/star-trek-into-darkness-directed-by-j-j-abrams.html', 'snippet': 'In “Star Trek Into Darkness,” the U.S.S. Enterprise crew hunts for a terrorist in the latest film in the franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is some intermittent complaining, in “Star Trek Into Darkness,” about the militarization of the Federation’s Starfleet. You may recall that the historic mission of the starship Enterprise was “to explore strange new worlds, to seek out new life and new civilizations.” While the crew on the first television series found its way into plenty of fights, the show itself always tried to stay true to the ideals of peaceful intergalactic ethnography.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kirk and Spock, in Their Roughhousing Days', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kirk and Spock, in Their Roughhousing Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMS, J J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Star Trek Into Darkness (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinto, Zachary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pine, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saldana, Zoe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pegg, Simon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orci, Roberto', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kurtzman, Alex', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weller, Peter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cho, John', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6430aa19-e652-5d9a-b446-4df86169b5a0', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6430aa19-e652-5d9a-b446-4df86169b5a0'}, {'abstract': 'The remarkable story of an unlikely cavalry campaign through Mississippi.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/the-music-teachers-raid/', 'snippet': 'The remarkable story of an unlikely cavalry campaign through Mississippi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of failed efforts to take Vicksburg by assaults from the north, by the early spring of 1863 Ulysses S. Grant had settled on a radically different approach. He would send a force over to the western bank of the Mississippi River; his troops would then march down through northern Louisiana, cross back over the river and establish a base of operations at Grand Gulf, Miss., about 30 miles south of Vicksburg, where there was less of a rebel presence. Grant could thus exploit advantageous terrain and weaker rebel defenses to move against the Confederate stronghold from the south. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Music Teacher’s Raid', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T17:50:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Bassett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bassett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a99669-d232-5505-984d-7a7d0524be78', 'word_count': 1574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a99669-d232-5505-984d-7a7d0524be78'}, {'abstract': 'Google is using its expertise in algorithms to offer users better social sharing tools through its Google Plus network. The company’s software will now select the best photos and fix their flaws, offer more links to topics mentioned in posts by members of a user’s social network and archive long-running chats.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/photos-take-the-spotlight-in-updates-to-googles-social-network/', 'snippet': 'Google is using its expertise in algorithms to offer users better social sharing tools through its Google Plus network. The company’s software will now select the best photos and fix their flaws, offer more links to topics mentioned in posts by me...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google may dominate Web search, but when it comes to social networks, the company’s Google Plus service is an underdog against Facebook and Twitter. As of December, Google Plus users were spending about 12 minutes a month on the service, according to the company, a smidgen of time compared with the hours that Facebook users spend on that site every month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-jumbo.png', 'height': 545, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 545, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/business/15google-v1/15google-v1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos Take the Spotlight in Updates to Google’s Social Network', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject