ticle/601f90f4-e154-53d8-a8e6-3157d8b18bc0', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601f90f4-e154-53d8-a8e6-3157d8b18bc0'}, {'abstract': 'A House hearing’s tensest exchange ended with the attorney general lashing back at a Republican congressman’s accusations about the Justice Department’s motives in not releasing some records on a nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/at-hearing-holder-calls-issas-accusations-shameful/', 'snippet': 'A House hearing’s tensest exchange ended with the attorney general lashing back at a Republican congressman’s accusations about the Justice Department’s motives in not releasing some records on a nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The possibility of contentious moments during the testimony of Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. at a House subcommittee hearing on Wednesday already seemed high, coming just days after the administration faced anger over seizures of journalists’ records. However, the tensest exchange of the hearing seemed to catch both Mr. Holder and members of the House Judiciary Committee’s oversight panel off guard, and ended with Mr. Holder calling a congressman’s behavior “shameful.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hearing, Holder Calls Issa’s Accusations ‘Shameful’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perez, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T19:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original'