': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1187, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/different/different-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s a Wilder Kingdom When a Marriage Expands', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s a Wilder Kingdom When a Marriage Expands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosebrock, Abby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ornstein, Bruce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T20:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3014b032-f365-5338-873d-d80c152e5df5', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3014b032-f365-5338-873d-d80c152e5df5'}, {'abstract': 'No, the slowdown in cost inflation hasn’t undercut the conservative position on health care reform.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/conservatives-and-health-care-costs/', 'snippet': 'No, the slowdown in cost inflation hasn’t undercut the conservative position on health care reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nested within the news about falling deficits\xa0is news about slowing health care cost inflation, which seems to be outlasting the recession and which is driving the long-term projections for Medicare spending downward. Since one of the big questions in the Great Obamacare Debate was whether the new health care law would accelerate cost growth (as expanded subsidies and regulations often tend to do) or reduce it (thanks to the various cost-containing experiments and pilot programs embedded within the bill), the news that costs are falling in advance of the bill’s implementation has some liberals crowing. Jonathan Chait, in particular, has taken to explaining why “the growing mass of evidence that the health-care-cost inflation problem is indeed solvable”\xa0cuts the legs out from under the entire right-of-center take on health care, deficits and entitlements, and puts the data squarely on the side of health care reform’s proponents. Here’s his elaboration on this theme:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservatives and Health Care Costs', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chait, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T20:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad577c66-81a2-5eb5-b108-124b152a50da', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad577c66-81a2-5eb5-b108-124b152a50da'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. said Zou Dejun and Qiu Jianping of Rino International used money from a stock offering to buy a California home.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/15/chinese-couple-settle-s-e-c-fraud-case/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. said Zou Dejun and Qiu Jianping of Rino International used money from a stock offering to buy a California home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A husband-and-wife team that ran a Chinese maker of pollution control equipment agreed on Wednesday to pay $3.75 million to settle accusations that they had defrauded American investors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Couple Settle Fraud Case Involving Chinese Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Couple Settle Fraud Case Involving Chinese Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rino International', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N