56-b227-beb8a216143c', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc571e57-d8c2-5956-b227-beb8a216143c'}, {'abstract': 'Hint: If it looks like you slept in those pajamas, then you better not wear them outside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/fashion/pjs-made-for-walking-out.html', 'snippet': 'Hint: If it looks like you slept in those pajamas, then you better not wear them outside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marc Jacobs in his new jammies uniform is the belle of the ball. Rihanna, Rita Ora and Elisa Sednaoui, in pajamas on the red carpet, obviously were invited. Why not you? ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1622, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/fashion/16PAJAMAS_SPAN-copy/16zPAJAMAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Snooze, You Lose', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Snooze, You Lose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pajamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T22:50:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Joy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a81153ed-58e0-50c7-a02b-eb2e6b90fae9', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a81153ed-58e0-50c7-a02b-eb2e6b90fae9'}, {'abstract': 'Imran Khan gave a three-day ultimatum to the national election commission on Wednesday to look into his political party’s claims of vote-rigging in last week’s election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/world/asia/pakistan-imran-khan-seeks-vote-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Imran Khan gave a three-day ultimatum to the national election commission on Wednesday to look into his political party’s claims of vote-rigging in last week’s election.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Imran Khan, the politician and former cricket star, gave a three-day ultimatum to the national election commission on Wednesday to look into his political party’s claims of vote-rigging in the contests for 25 parliamentary seats during last week’s general election. Mr. Khan warned that his party would start countrywide protests if the grievances were not addressed. Most of the accusations of voter fraud concern election districts in Lahore and Karachi. Election officials say repolling of 43 election stations in a wealthy Karachi district will take place on Sunday. According to the latest official tally, the party of Nawaz Sharif, the presumptive prime minister, leads with 124 seats in the 272-seat assembly. The Pakistan Peoples Party, the former governing party, won 31 seats, while Mr. Khan’s party won 27. The counts for 11 seats have yet to be officially verified. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Imran Khan Seeks Vote Inquiry', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Khan Seeks Vote Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Imran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Pakistan People's Party", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-15T22:54:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7afeaa80-11c0-5135-a158-9eb3ad6d6d5b', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7afeaa80-11c0-5135-a158-9eb3ad6d6d5b'}, {'abstract': 'Friends of the High Line held a benefit that honored Ethan Hawke and other supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/16/fashion/20130516-SCENE.html', 'snippet': 'Friend