1707'}, {'abstract': 'The head of the federal consumer protection agency was fired Wednesday, weeks after his daughter got inspectors to briefly shut down a restaurant that refused her the table she wanted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/world/americas/mexico-official-whose-daughter-forced-restaurant-closing-is-fired.html', 'snippet': 'The head of the federal consumer protection agency was fired Wednesday, weeks after his daughter got inspectors to briefly shut down a restaurant that refused her the table she wanted.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The head of the federal consumer protection agency was fired Wednesday, weeks after his daughter got inspectors to briefly shut down a restaurant that refused her the table she wanted. Four officials from the agency had been suspended after the episode became a Twitter sensation highlighting the deep sense of entitlement of the privileged in Mexico. The father, Humberto Benítez Treviño, had defied calls to resign, but President Enrique Peña Nieto, who had promised more accountability from his government, decided to fire him. A government statement said that while Mr. Benitez Treviño did not play a role in the inspection that led to the closing, the case had damaged the image and prestige of the agency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Official Whose Daughter Forced Restaurant Closing Is Fired', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Official Whose Daughter Forced Restaurant Closing Is Fired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benitez Trevino, Humberto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T00:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/76adeba8-208c-5709-91d2-1a02c56ccdc6', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76adeba8-208c-5709-91d2-1a02c56ccdc6'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets’ quarterback situation took another strange turn Wednesday, when the veteran David Garrard called it quits because of his left knee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/sports/football/jets-tear-up-quarterback-plan-as-david-garrard-retires.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets’ quarterback situation took another strange turn Wednesday, when the veteran David Garrard called it quits because of his left knee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jets had a plan. They would sign a veteran quarterback, which they did. They would draft a dynamic rookie, which they also did. And they would put both in an honest-to-goodness competition, challenging the incumbent for the right to start the season opener.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/yJETS/yJETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Know Bizarre: Balky Knee Forces Garrard to Retire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Know Bizarre: Balky Knee Forces Garrard to Retire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrard, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Idzik, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T00:28:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46fae62c-aabb-5a90-acef-ffe4476ea7b1', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46fae62c-aabb-5a90-acef-ffe4476ea7b1'}, {'abstract': 'The vote was 91 to 7 for Marilyn B. Tavenner, acting leader of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services since December 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/us/marilyn-tavenner-confirmed-as-medicaid-and-medicare-chief.html', 'snippet': 'The vote was 91 to 7 for Marilyn B. Tavenner, acting leader of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services since December 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate on Wednesday approved President Obama’s nominee to run Medicare and Medicaid, Marilyn B. Tavenner, providing the agency with its first confirmed chief in six and a half years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Acting Chief Wins Confirmation to Run Medicare and Medicaid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Acting Chief Wins Confirmation To Run Medicare and Medicaid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavenner, Marilyn B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T00:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56058428-8f8f-55d8-8317-9f9cc4d401f6', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56058428-8f8f-55d8-8317-9f9cc4d401f6'}, {'abstract': 'Abercrombie & Fitch became the second American company to agree to the legally enforceable plan to improve safety standards in Bangladesh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/business/global/abercrombie-fitch-agrees-to-bangladesh-factory-safety-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Abercrombie & Fitch became the second American company to agree to the legally enforceable plan to improve safety standards in Bangladesh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abercrombie & Fitch said on Wednesday that it had signed on to a landmark plan to improve factory safety in Bangladesh, becoming just the second American company to join an accord that more than two dozen European retailers and brands have embraced.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abercrombie & Fitch Signs Bangladesh Safety Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abercrombie & Fitch Signs Bangladesh Safety Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Abercrombie & Fitch Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T00:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstna