 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe8b06c-77ae-5f20-b57d-b77a5e0885e1', 'word_count': 2682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe8b06c-77ae-5f20-b57d-b77a5e0885e1'}, {'abstract': 'The White House now wants a law to protect journalists from government intrusion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/opinion/after-attacking-the-ap-a-peace-offering.html', 'snippet': 'The White House now wants a law to protect journalists from government intrusion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After coming under scorching bipartisan criticism for secretly going through the phone records of reporters at The Associated Press in a leak investigation, the Obama administration now says it supports a law that might have prevented this outrageous conduct. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Attacking The A.P., a Peace Offering', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Attacking The A.P., a Peace Offering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T01:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6000d4df-b756-52db-a79f-8306afd85924', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6000d4df-b756-52db-a79f-8306afd85924'}, {'abstract': 'New York State was right to order an investigation of firms that advertise payments as advances, not high-cost loans, to pensioners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/opinion/pension-predators-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'New York State was right to order an investigation of firms that advertise payments as advances, not high-cost loans, to pensioners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo has done retirees and military veterans a great service by ordering New York’s top banking regulator to investigate “pension advance” firms that persuade customers to sign over all or part of their monthly pensions in exchange for immediate cash payments. The payments, advertised as advances, are, in fact, cleverly disguised loans that can carry ruinously high interest rates and eventually strip older citizens of their meager assets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pension Predators', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pension Predators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T01:20:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d43c840-fbbf-502c-87df-ab92adeb8922', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d43c840-fbbf-502c-87df-ab92adeb8922'}, {'abstract': 'If social welfare groups had to disclose their political donors, the confusion and abuse would end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/opinion/take-politics-away-from-the-irs.html', 'snippet': 'If social welfare groups had to disclose their political donors, the confusion and abuse would end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s decision on Wednesday to dismiss the acting commissioner of the Internal Revenue Service was a largely symbolic demonstration of anger and authority. The official, Steven Miller, was not directly involved in the misguided decision to single out Tea Party groups for special scrutiny in granting tax exemptions. What is more important is Mr. Obama’s promise to clarify the extremely vague tax laws, which are the root cause of the problems in both the I.R.S. and the political system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Take Politics Away From the I.R.S.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take Politics Away From the I.R.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T01:20:36+0000', 'docum