teven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb26e5b4-bae0-5685-a75b-b5f17751a146', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb26e5b4-bae0-5685-a75b-b5f17751a146'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth Thompson, a candidate for Kings County District Attorney, is asking Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo for an independent investigation of dozens of prosecutions involving the work of a retired police detective, Louis Scarcella, that have recently come under scrutiny. <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/nyregion/a-conflict-is-seen-in-a-review-of-a-detectives-conduct.html">Related Article »</a>', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/16/nyregion/16scarcella-letter.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth Thompson, a candidate for Kings County District Attorney, is asking Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo for an independent investigation of dozens of prosecutions involving the work of a retired police detective, Louis Scarcella, that have recently come ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenneth Thompson, a candidate for Kings County District Attorney, is asking Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo for an independent investigation of dozens of prosecutions involving the work of a retired police detective, Louis Scarcella, that have recently come under scrutiny. <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/nyregion/a-conflict-is-seen-in-a-review-of-a-detectives-conduct.html">Related Article »</a>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Request for Investigation Into Prosecutions Involving Retired Detective Louis Scarcella', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scarcella, Louis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T03:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/eec9b7aa-cf4a-566e-82a4-8fa2f52c9641', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/eec9b7aa-cf4a-566e-82a4-8fa2f52c9641'}, {'abstract': 'The Harris County district attorney’s office said that it would investigate charges that a Houston doctor, Douglas Karpen, had delivered live babies during abortions and killed them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/us/texas-investigation-of-abortion-doctor.html', 'snippet': 'The Harris County district attorney’s office said that it would investigate charges that a Houston doctor, Douglas Karpen, had delivered live babies during abortions and killed them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Harris County district attorney’s office said Wednesday that it would investigate charges that a Houston doctor had delivered live babies during third-trimester abortions and killed them after they emerged, which federal and state laws forbid. The anti-abortion group Operation Rescue made the charges based on statements by three former employees of the abortion doctor, Douglas Karpen, which could not be independently verified. The organization said the doctor’s actions echoed the charges that led to the murder conviction of Dr. Kermit Gosnell in Philadelphia. Lt. Gov. David Dewhurst said he had read the allegations “with disgust,” and called for a full investigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Investigation of Abortion Doctor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Investigation of Abortion Doctor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Operation Rescue', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karpen, Douglas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T03:31:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ba3db57-6a9d-5632-b68f-c424675f14a9', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ba3db57-6a9d-5632-b68f-c424675f14a9'}, {'abstract': 'he Los Angeles Unified School District has voted to end the practice of suspending students who are defiant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/us/california-suspensions-end-for-defiant-students.html', 'snippet': 'he Los Angeles Unified School District has voted to end the practice of suspending students who are defiant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Unified School District has voted to end the practice of suspending students who are defiant. Concern has grown that “zero tolerance” disciplinary policies, which sometimes led to suspensions for acts like refusing to remove a hat in class, have disproportionately affected minority students, hindered academic achievement and lowered graduation rates. More than a third of all suspensions result from “willful defiance,” according district officials. Los Angeles Unified, with more than 600,000 students, is the first large school district in the country to curtail suspensions for defiance, officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Suspensions End for Defiant Students', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Suspensions End For Defiant Students', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T03:31:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/678bd034-1210-554a-9ed6-5005f1f39137', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678bd034-1210-554a-9ed6-5005f1f39137'}, {'abstract': 'A study of cancer patients in Washington State has found they were twice as likely to file for bankruptcy as people without cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/us/washington-cancer-patients-more-prone-to-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'A study of cancer patients in Washington State has found they were twice as likely to file for bankruptcy as people without cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study of cancer patients in Washington State has found they were twice as likely to file for bankruptcy as people without cancer. The study, led by researchers from the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle, linked bankruptcy court records and information from the regional cancer registry on about 200,000 cancer patients, and compared them with a similar group of people from the same area who did not have cancer. Young people with cancer experienced the highest bankruptcy rates, the study found, up to 10 times the rate of bankruptcy filings among older age groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington: Cancer Patients More Prone to Bankruptcy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Northwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Washington: Cancer Patients More Prone To Bankruptcy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hutchinson, Fred, Cancer Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T03:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/51154304-41b8-53e3-a004-c0268ba4cea6', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51154304-41b8-53e3-a004-c0268ba4cea6'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration controversies of recent days have reinforced fears of an overreaching government and called into question Mr. Obama’s ability to master his own presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/us/politics/new-controversies-may-undermine-obama.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration controversies of recent days have reinforced fears of an overreaching government and called into question Mr. Obama’s ability to master his own presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Thwarted on Capitol Hill, stymied in the Middle East and now beset by scandal, President Obama has reached a point just six months after a heady re-election where the second term he had hoped for has collided with the second term he actually has.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/politics/16obama-2/16obama-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Onset of Woes Casts Pall Over Obama’s Policy Aspirations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Onset of Woes Raises Questions on Obama Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T03:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70cfd4ad-9395-5ab8-8bb5-8a92861c2f06', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70cfd4ad-9395-5ab8-8bb5-8a92861c2f06'}, {'abstract': 'Another night of dismal hitting and pitching resulted in another loss for the Mets, an outcome Manager Terry Collins previously would have ranted about but has since learned to accept.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/sports/baseball/as-mets-struggle-collins-keeps-calm.html', 'snippet': 'Another night of dismal hitting and pitching resulted in another loss for the Mets, an outcome Manager Terry Collins previously would have ranted about but has since learned to accept.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Years ago, Terry Collins possessed a far more inflammable personality, one capable of channeling ire toward the players he managed. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/sub-METS/sub-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/sports/sub-METS/sub-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None