.com/2013/05/16/healing-in-the-aftermath-of-massacre/', 'snippet': 'After the massacre in Utoya, Norway, in July 2011, Andrea Gjestvang sought to photograph the victims’ process of recovery, both physical and emotional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a Friday afternoon in July 2011, Andrea Gjestvang was preparing to leave the offices of the Norwegian newspaper Verdens Gang, where she was working as a temporary photo editor, when an enormous explosion shook the building, blowing out windows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Healing in the Aftermath of a Massacre', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T09:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/becc617f-8e06-5633-84de-84143c37b6a3', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/becc617f-8e06-5633-84de-84143c37b6a3'}, {'abstract': 'The accident at the factory, which made sneakers for the Japanese manufacturer Asics, reinforced global worries about factory safety in poor countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/asia/cambodia-factory-ceiling-collapse.html', 'snippet': 'The accident at the factory, which made sneakers for the Japanese manufacturer Asics, reinforced global worries about factory safety in poor countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TREAM TBAL, Cambodia — Survivors