ht-on-the-assembled-parties.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Assembled Parties,” Jessica Hecht is playing a role the playwright Richard Greenberg wrote with her in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jessica Hecht was filming in Albuquerque last year, reprising her role as the lost love of Walter White’s youth on the concluding season of “Breaking Bad,” when she got a call from Lynne Meadow, the artistic director of Manhattan Theater Club, asking how soon she could be back in New York for a reading of a new play. Ms. Meadow withheld details of the project, “The Assembled Parties,” not disclosing that it was a Richard Greenberg play until Ms. Hecht had returned from New Mexico. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JESSICA1/19JESSICA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Comfortable Fit, Gracefully Worn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Comfortable Fit, Gracefully Worn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rooney, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hecht, Jessica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Assembled Parties (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a3e89ed-2a4f-5cce-88fc-4da4861fdf27', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a3e89ed-2a4f-5cce-88fc-4da4861fdf27'}, {'abstract': 'The main story at the Internal Revenue Service is one of incompetence, not conspiracy, when it comes to the review of applications from groups seeking tax-exempt status.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/a-dickensian-delay-at-the-i-r-s/', 'snippet': 'The main story at the Internal Revenue Service is one of incompetence, not conspiracy, when it comes to the review of applications from groups seeking tax-exempt status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plot device in Charles Dickens’s “Bleak House” follows the interminable case of Jarndyce v. Jarndyce through the English Court of Chancery. The litigation winds on for years until, finally, the costs of litigating the case have consumed the entire estate, leaving nothing for the heirs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dickensian Delay at the I.R.S.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Steven T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:12:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Fleischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d881e957-043a-5c2c-9057-04e0e0baf441', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d881e957-043a-5c2c-9057-04e0e0baf441'}, {'abstract': 'F.B.I. agents investigating the Boston Marathon bombing have repeatedly questioned a former separatist fighter who says he had a passing social relationship with a bombing suspect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/us/boston-bombing-developments.html', 'snippet': 'F.B.I. agents investigating the Boston Marathon bombing have repeatedly questioned a former separatist fighter who says he had a passing social relationship with a bombing suspect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — F.B.I. agents investigating the Boston Marathon bombing have repeatedly questioned Musa Khadzhimuratov, a Chechen refugee and former separatist fighter who says he had a passing social relationship with one of the two bombing suspects. They searched his family’s small apartment here on Tuesday, scouring his computers, subjecting him to a polygraph, and taking a DNA sample. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chechen Refugee Questioned in F.B.I.’s Inquiry of Bombing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chechen Refugee Questioned In F.B.I.’s Inquiry of Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, Katherine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:23:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane and Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e9cc46-5dce-5ac3-aed7-34da0112072d', 'word_count': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e9cc46-5dce-5ac3-aed7-34da0112072d'}, {'abstract': 'David Beckham, whose free kicks, good looks and savvy marketing made him one of the most recognizable athletes in the world, said Thursday that he would retire at season’s end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/sports/soccer/david-beckham-announces-retirement-from-soccer.html', 'snippet': 'David Beckham, whose free kicks, good looks and savvy marketing made him one of the most recognizable athletes in the world, said Thursday that he would retire at season’s end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Beckham broke a bone in his left foot before the 2002 World Cup, Tony Blair, then the British prime minister, interrupted a cabinet meeting to express his concern about England’s suddenly uncertain chances. Tabloid newspapers ran photos of Beckham’s injured foot on Page 1 and asked readers to lay their hands on the picture in an attempt at mass civic healing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 715}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 860, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/17beckhamweb1/17beckhamweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ