r scheme and a “wellness bar” looks to provide a friendly vibe to the neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | A Pharmacy for Lower East Siders', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Store: For Pills and an Ocean View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1765468d-7602-53d1-a751-831decccb96d', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1765468d-7602-53d1-a751-831decccb96d'}, {'abstract': 'Planners and residents of Lower Manhattan imagined a new World Trade Center that would be integrated in the neighborhood, but now they fear that security measures will keep it isolated as ever.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/world-trade-center-may-be-isolated-again-this-time-by-security-measures/', 'snippet': 'Planners and residents of Lower Manhattan imagined a new World Trade Center that would be integrated in the neighborhood, but now they fear that security measures will keep it isolated as ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wreckage had not been cleared from ground zero when planners and neighbors began imagining how the devastation of Sept. 11 could be redeemed, in some way, by a new World Trade Center, one that would be fully joined to the rest of Lower Manhattan rather than standing apart in chilling isolation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/17wtc1/17wtc1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Security, Trade Center Faces New Isolation', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Security, Trade Center Faces New Isolation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:36:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/199c6e48-db18-5430-9c53-aee1b6bbe0b8', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199c6e48-db18-5430-9c53-aee1b6bbe0b8'}, {'abstract': 'The Heat beat the Bulls to advance, but the Thunder, widely projected to make the N.B.A. finals, are done for the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/sports/after-round-2-one-nba-favorite-still-stands.html', 'snippet': 'The Heat beat the Bulls to advance, but the Thunder, widely projected to make the N.B.A. finals, are done for the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the first game of the playoffs, right before Russell Westbrook’s knee went pop and changed the Oklahoma City Thunder’s outlook to mostly cloudy with a chance of calamity, the Miami Heat and the Thunder could have penciled themselves in for a rematch of last year’s N.B.A. finals. Who was going to beat these two, loaded with star players and confidence? They played with that “What, us worry?” attitude, knowing there was always a switch somewhere they could flip and heroics would just happen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', '