aniacal focus of the Danish director Nicolas Winding Refn. Yet the 42-year-old filmmaker has never made a traditional action movie. Even his 2011 film, the harsh, neon-lit Los Angeles film “Drive,” starring Ryan Gosling as a Los Angeles getaway driver, was a chase film with hardly any car chases. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/gosling/gosling-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicolas Winding Refn on Being One With Ryan Gosling', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revenge, Served Without Regret', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Refn, Nicolas Winding', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Logan Hill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Logan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aba16e42-e416-5244-af41-b41240f57627', 'word_count': 1481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aba16e42-e416-5244-af41-b41240f57627'}, {'abstract': 'Three best play nominees — “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike,” “The Assembled Parties” and “Lucky Guy” — extended their runs.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/extended-runs-for-some-tony-nominees/', 'snippet': 'Three best play nominees — “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike,” “The Assembled Parties” and “Lucky Guy” — extended their runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway is often barren during summertime when it comes to plays, as their star actors return to Hollywood for film and television commitments (or go on vacation) after the Tony Awards are announced in June. But several plays have announced that they will not close as early as originally planned. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extended Runs for Some Tony Nominees', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be1bc31-8d85-5663-bc36-e960d8fa5c31', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be1bc31-8d85-5663-bc36-e960d8fa5c31'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/what-were-reading-694/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bloomberg Businessweek: KFC, once the fast-food emperor of China, is suddenly slumping because of competition and food-safety and avian-flu scares — while its once lagging United States business is perking up thanks to its boneless chicken (“I Ate the Bones”) promotion. … – Glenn Collins', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:40:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3b4266f-0dbd-5b35-adf0-69d4c4b20da1', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3b4266f-0dbd-5b35-adf0-69d4c4b20da1'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Vermes, one of the scrolls’ essential translators, wrote several books that placed Jesus in the tradition of Jewish teachers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/europe/geza-vermes-dead-sea-scrolls-scholar-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Vermes, one of the scrolls’ essential translators, wrote several books that placed Jesus in the tradition of Jewish teachers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Geza Vermes, a religious scholar who argued that Jesus as a historical figure could be understood only through the Jewish tradition from which he emerged, and who helped expand that understanding through his widely read English translations of the Dead Sea Scrolls, died on May 8 in Oxford, England. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 868}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1962, 'width': 1357, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/world/VERMES-obit/VERMES-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Geza Vermes, Scholar of ‘Historical Jesus,’ Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Geza Vermes, Scholar of ‘Historical Jesus,’ Dies at 88', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vermes, Geza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dead Sea Scrolls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jesus Christ', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T14:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ce86cef-58ff-5efd-9105-0398e01cde17', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ce86cef-58ff-5efd-9105-0398e01cde17'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Nelsons, 34, has been music director of the City of Birmingham Symphony Orchestra in Britain since 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/boston-symphony-orchestra-appoints-andris-nelsons-as-new-music-director/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Nelsons, 34, has been music director of the City of Birmingham Symphony Orchestra in Britain since 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andris Nelsons, a dynamic young Latvian conductor, has been named music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra, which has lingered without a leader for two years.', 'print_section'