ts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cc1753e-f08f-5518-bafd-03175543be03', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cc1753e-f08f-5518-bafd-03175543be03'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/the-gun-report-may-16-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, on the Senate floor, Richard Durbin, the Illinois Democrat, gave a nine-minute speech about the continuing gun violence in the months since Newtown, and the Senate’s inability to pass a universal background check bill. To illustrate the ongoing carnage—more than 4,000 Americans have been killed by a gun since Newtown, he pointed out—he read excerpts from last weekend’s Gun Report. You can watch his remarks here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 16, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prichard (Ala)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rochester (NY)', 'ra