 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/theater/far-from-heaven-the-musical-under-construction.html', 'snippet': 'The creative team behind the musical “Far From Heaven,” in previews at Playwrights Horizons, grappled with translating the source film’s cinematic style for the stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Frankel recalled sitting next to his grandmother at a movie theater in suburban Cleveland, visibly moved as she watched the 2002 Todd Haynes film “Far From Heaven,” a deconstruction of the Eisenhower-era melodramas of the director Douglas Sirk. He had first seen the film, set in 1957 Connecticut, a few months before in Chelsea with an audience of devoted cinephiles, who nodded approvingly at its evocation of the overripe cinematic style of Sirk and laughed knowingly at its commentary on the past. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19FAR1_SPAN/19Far1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19FAR1_SPAN/19Far1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19FAR1_SPAN/19Far1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19FAR1_SPAN/19Far1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19FAR1_SPAN/19Far1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail':