ducing-acela-like-wi-fi.html', 'snippet': 'The railroad said it had upgraded its cellular-based Wi-Fi offering using broadband technologies that will improve speed and reliability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After years of criticism of the wireless service on its trains, Amtrak announced on Thursday that it had upgraded its cellular-based Wi-Fi using broadband technologies that will improve the speed and reliability of the Internet in its passenger cars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/AMTRAK/AMTRAK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amtrak Upgrades Wi-Fi Service on Trains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amtrak Upgrades Wi-Fi Service on Trains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMTRAK', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T16:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7d992b1-6f7f-5207-8985-17c40e57a36a', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7d992b1-6f7f-5207-8985-17c40e57a36a'}, {'abstract': 'The United States upset the defending champion Russia, 8-3, in the quarterfinals at the International Ice Hockey Federation world championships. The Americans will play Switzerland in the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/u-s-routs-russia-to-reach-semifinals-at-world-championships/', 'snippet': 'The United States upset the defending champion Russia, 8-3, in the quarterfinals at the International Ice Hockey Federation world championships. The Americans will play Switzerland in the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HELSINKI, Finland — In stunning fashion, the United States beat defending champion Russia, 8-3, on Thursday in the quarterfinals at the International Ice Hockey Federation world championships. It was the most goals allowed by a Russian team in this tournament.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Routs Russia to Reach Semifinals at World Championships', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Eliminates Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryzgalov, Ilya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stastny, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varlamov, Semyon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Ice Hockey Federation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Hockey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T16:43:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Aykroyd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aykroyd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a1d9c9-b319-598e-96c3-c4438f382008', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a1d9c9-b319-598e-96c3-c4438f382008'}, {'abstract': 'Two-term presidents since World War II tended to be quite popular in their first terms, and significantly less so in their second terms. Is this proof of a second-term curse? In reality, there are some complications.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/is-there-really-a-second-term-curse/', 'snippet': 'Two-term presidents since World War II tended to be quite popular in their first terms, and significantly less so in their second terms. Is this proof of a second-term curse? In reality, there are some complications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is facing one of his roughest stretches in office after questions about the government’s response to the attacks in Benghazi, Libya, the admission by the Internal Revenue Service that it inappropriately targeted conservative groups which sought tax-exempt status, and the revelation that the Justice Department subpoenaed communications by The Associated Press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There Really a Second-Term Curse?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T16:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dcedcb0-e728-5f68-94e0-a24fe3bf0a71', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dcedcb0-e728-5f68-94e0-a24fe3bf0a71'}, {'abstract': 'The first time I talked to Phil Jackson, he spontaneously sketched a play on his placemat. I have to admit there was a not-tiny part of me that was squealing, internally.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/the-rembrandt-of-basketball/', 'snippet': 'The first time I talked to Phil Jackson, he spontaneously sketched a play on his placemat. I have to admit there was a not-tiny part of me that was squealing, internally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I talked to Phil Jackson, at a diner, he spontaneously sketched a play on his place mat. I try to keep things professional when I’m doing an interview, but I have to admit there was a not-tiny part of me that was squealing, internally: OMG the winningest N.B.A. coach of all time is literally drawing me a play right now, just like he drew Michael Jordan plays during time outs — OMG I’ve finally achieved my childhood dream of turning into Michael Jordan. (Phil Jackson, whom I wrote about in this weekend’s magazine, was leading Jordan to his first championships during the peak years of my adolescence, so the Jordan/Jackson mythology is still plugged into some pretty preprofessional emotional zones for me.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1028, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/15/magazine/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch/15-phil-jackson-mj-sketch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rembrandt of Basketball', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ''