 play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. – Knicks Coach Mike Woodson made a number of statements Thursday after what could be his team’s final shootaround of the 2012-13 season. With the Knicks on the brink of elimination in their Eastern Conference semifinals series against the Pacers, Woodson said he would demand his players be a tougher group in Game 5, which is Thursday night at Madison Square Garden. He also said all five players on the court would need to rebound in order to win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodson Turns to Copeland, but Won’t Desert Kidd', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Copeland, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodson, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T18:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b277d7c-a63d-5f07-bd48-419687c931a0', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b277d7c-a63d-5f07-bd48-419687c931a0'}, {'abstract': 'We must raise rates to avoid … something.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/the-sadomonetarists-of-basel/', 'snippet': 'We must raise rates to avoid … something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The WSJ highlights a speech by Jaime Caruana, general manager of the Bank for International Settlements, warning of the dangers of easy money and the need to raise rates now to avert … something or other. And his views matter, says the Journal:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sadomonetarists of Basel', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T18:44:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd2b453-f612-5548-bc38-3721251e96ee', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd2b453-f612-5548-bc38-3721251e96ee'}, {'abstract': 'In a new class in Brooklyn, dogs and their owners can work out and play together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/health/exercise-class-obedience-not-required.html', 'snippet': 'In a new class in Brooklyn, dogs and their owners can work out and play together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOGS may be our best friends, but that doesn’t necessarily make them the easiest exercise partners. The fitness trainer Angi Aramburu thinks otherwise, though, and this spring she started Go Fetch Run, an exercise class in which owners and their dogs can work out and play together. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17URBAN_SPAN/17URBAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17URBAN_SPAN/17URBAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'r