f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e081e9-1f0d-532f-918a-3eed07dc28e2', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e081e9-1f0d-532f-918a-3eed07dc28e2'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for Marc Bertoldi, owner of a luxury car business, argued that the Belgian authorities had not spelled out his precise role in the $50 million theft in February.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/europe/frenchman-staves-off-extradition-in-50-million-diamond-theft.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for Marc Bertoldi, owner of a luxury car business, argued that the Belgian authorities had not spelled out his precise role in the $50 million theft in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'METZ, France — The French owner of a luxury car business — accused of masterminding a $50 million million diamond theft at Brussels Airport — temporarily fended off extradition to Belgium on Thursday, arguing that the authorities there had not spelled out his precise role.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frenchman Staves Off Extradition in Diamond Theft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Diamond Theft Case Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bertoldi, Marc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T20:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/613ccff4-ed5e-57ad-beab-2cb518dfc80f', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/613ccff4-ed5e-57ad-beab-2cb518dfc80f'}, {'abstract': 'The latest assault on the fraying broadcast sports model came Thursday when ESPN announced it would pay $825 million over 11 years for complete control of the tennis tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/sports/tennis/ending-an-era-the-us-open-will-move-to-espn.html', 'snippet': 'The latest assault on the fraying broadcast sports model came Thursday when ESPN announced it would pay $825 million over 11 years for complete control of the tennis tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the United States Open tennis tournament was a mainstay of broadcast television, along with the Super Bowl, the World Series and the Masters. From Billie Jean King and Rod Laver to Roger Federer and the Williams sisters,\xa0viewers knew they could watch superstars, rising talents and upstarts play in the men’s and women’s finals and semifinals — and more — on CBS.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank