ent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Guard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T20:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew W. Lehren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Lehren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa34aef7-6c03-5992-a766-6c4d18dc8fe8', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa34aef7-6c03-5992-a766-6c4d18dc8fe8'}, {'abstract': 'Is tax law being widely flouted by political groups determined to avoid disclosure of their donors?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/business/a-fine-line-between-social-welfare-and-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Is tax law being widely flouted by political groups determined to avoid disclosure of their donors?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As everyone from Republican senators to President Obama denounces the Internal Revenue Service for singling out Tea Party organizations for extra scrutiny, it is worth asking how we got to the point that the I.R.S. is supposed to investigate political activities. It is also worth asking whether the tax law is being widely flouted by political groups determined to avoid disclosure of their donors — and whether successive administrations have failed to enforce the law.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fine Line Between Social and Political', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fine Line Between Social And Political', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T21:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2666a507-2e0e-5f0f-8def-15d2f1d3aca1', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2666a507-2e0e-5f0f-8def-15d2f1d3aca1'}, {'abstract': 'In Helene Wecker’s novel, two folkloric creatures emerge onto the streets of 1899 New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/books/review/the-golem-and-the-jinni-by-helene-wecker.html', 'snippet': 'In Helene Wecker’s novel, two folkloric creatures emerge onto the streets of 1899 New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Helene Wecker’s first novel, two more than usually disoriented foreigners emerge onto the streets of 1899 New York. One is a golem, a clay woman fashioned near Danzig, then shipped across the ocean as the wife of a man who inconveniently dies on the voyage. The other is a jinni from the Syrian desert, trapped inside a copper flask until a hapless tinsmith sets him free during a routine repair. “It was ludicrous,” thinks the surprised tinker. “Such things were only stories. But then, the only alternative was to conclude that he’d gone mad.” There is in fact plenty of madness in this clever story, but the magic of it often makes more sense than the ways of the humans with whom the golem and the jinni now live.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1797, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover/0519-bks-COKAL-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u