n': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/realestate/19mortgage-graphic/19mortgage-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/realestate/19mortgage-graphic/19mortgage-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/realestate/19mortgage-graphic/19mortgage-graphic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deduction Unevenly Used ', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deduction Unevenly Used', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prevost, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T21:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f08a32b-82fc-5616-8c96-192a283dd022', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f08a32b-82fc-5616-8c96-192a283dd022'}, {'abstract': 'Greta Gerwig is the co-writer and star of “Frances Ha,” a look at a vaguely artistic, post-collegiate New York cohort, directed by Noah Baumbach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/movies/frances-ha-with-greta-gerwig.html', 'snippet': 'Greta Gerwig is the co-writer and star of “Frances Ha,” a look at a vaguely artistic, post-collegiate New York cohort, directed by Noah Baumbach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day an unexpected tax refund arrives in the mail, and Frances, giddy over this windfall, decides to spend it treating a young man to dinner. (His name is Lev, he is played by Adam Driver, and this is the only time I will mention Lena Dunham or “Girls” in this review.) The restaurant rejects her credit card and won’t take a debit card, so Frances sets off through the black-and-white streets of New York in search of an A.T.M. Sprinting back to the table, she trips and sprawls headlong onto the sidewalk, the full calamity of her fall blocked from the camera’s view by a parked car. Then she gets up and keeps running.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If 27 Is Old, How Old Is Grown Up?', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If 27 Is Old, How Old Is Grown Up?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baumbach, Noah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerwig, Greta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sumner, Mickey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driver, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frances Ha (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T21:27:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/df8229f5-e4cf-5f4e-a4b1-b93ac11f37a1', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df8229f5-e4cf-5f4e-a4b1-b93ac11f37a1'}, {'abstract': 'Just west of Austin you’ll find the Hill Country, an area home to Comfort and Welfare, the echoes of Willie and Waylon and the tension between rural and refined.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/travel/36-hours-in-texas-hill-country.html', 'snippet': 'Just west of Austin you’ll find the Hill Country, an area home to Comfort and Welfare, the echoes of Willie and Waylon and the tension between rural and refined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two ways to think about the Texas Hill Country. Physically, it spreads across the undulating Edwards Plateau, with Austin to the east and San Antonio to the south. Near the center is Fredericksburg, which was once the main show in these parts, but no longer. To get a feeling for the Hill Country in the second sense — the state of mind where cool mingles with tradition, and industriousness and idleness are equally esteemed values (depending on the time of day) — head out among the limestone knolls full of live oak groves and cypress-lined creeks, and to the gritty pin-dot towns built largely of native stone. Here you’ll find a delicious tension between rural and refined. Inns and restaurants are bringing a clever touch to Lone Star hospitality and mythology, and with the vineyards and boutique farms (lavender, olives), some people make comparisons to Napa Valley or even Provence. But those assessments ignore something fundamental: the Hill Country — being Texas at its finest — is like nowhere else in the world.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 228, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 228}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN-sf/19HOURS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Texas Hill Country', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Texas Hill Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ralston, Jeannie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T21:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannie Ralston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ralston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 