vents, author discussions, street fairs and more in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/arts/spare-times-for-may-17-23.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, cultural events, author discussions, street fairs and more in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Internet Week New York (Monday through May 27) Like the Internet itself, this annual Web festival — the sixth — will offer something for everyone, with workshops, panel discussions, parties and performances. On Wednesday at 3 p.m., Randi Zuckerberg, bottom left, the chief executive of Zuckerberg Media and an older sister of Mark Zuckerberg, will talk about her business at a keynote address at festival headquarters, the Metropolitan Pavilion, 125 West 18th Street, Chelsea.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for May 17-23', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T22:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso and Lori Holcomb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb40e4a0-2deb-5c97-b445-d7a96f36da53', 'word_count': 3804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb40e4a0-2deb-5c97-b445-d7a96f36da53'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t do what I did and buy a movie for $12.99. There is another way.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/16/hollywoods-freebies/', 'snippet': 'Don’t do what I did and buy a movie for $12.99. There is another way.', 'lead_paragraph': ' How not to economize: rent Buster Keaton’s “The General” on iTunes for $3.99, as my husband and I did a couple Fridays ago, and then purchase it the next night for $12.99 when your kid begs to watch it again. Much better to visit Open Culture’s Web site instead, where you can find links to, among other things, 525 oldies in the public domain and other free films (be sure to scroll down to see the list, rather than using the search bar).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood’s Freebies', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-