 age. But a government survey released on Thursday found that juveniles did not report significantly more sexual victimization than adult inmates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Juvenile Inmates Found to Be at No Greater Risk for Prison Rape', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Juvenile Inmates Found to Be at No Greater Risk for Prison Rape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Justice Statistics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T23:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2cfb942-9ad8-5010-9bc4-4e8495a91f99', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2cfb942-9ad8-5010-9bc4-4e8495a91f99'}, {'abstract': 'In “Black Rock,” three young women decide to reconnect on an isolated island in Maine, only to find themselves running for their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/movies/black-rock-directed-by-katie-aselton.html', 'snippet': 'In “Black Rock,” three young women decide to reconnect on an isolated island in Maine, only to find themselves running for their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the funnier television comedies in recent years has been “The League,” a bawdy FX series about a fantasy football league. Fans of that show might expect a lot of laughs from “Black Rock,” since it was written by a “League” cast member, Mark Duplass, and stars another, Katie Aselton, who also directed it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BLACKROCK_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Us Girls, They Thought. Oops.', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Rock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aselton, Katie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosworth, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Black Rock (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T23:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1e781fa-1a98-5b0b-ab6c-ddd2936223b9', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1e781fa-1a98-5b0b-ab6c-ddd2936223b9'}, {'abstract': 'A scene from "Pieta," directed by Kim Ki-duk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002230112/clip-pieta.html', 'snippet': 'A scene from "Pieta," directed by Kim Ki-duk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A scene from "Pieta," directed by Kim Ki-duk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/video-pieta-clip/video-pieta-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/video-pieta-clip/video-pieta-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/video-pieta-clip/video-pieta-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/video-pieta-clip/video-pieta-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/16/arts/video-pieta-clip/video-pieta-clip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clip: ‘Pieta’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-16T23:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Drafthouse Films', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drafthouse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Films', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/887ad1f0-f2fe-5161-87c7-53e77674dd11', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/887ad1f0-f2fe-5161-87c7-53e77674dd11'}, {'abstract': '“Pieta,” a brutal drama by the South Korean director Kim Ki-duk, centers on a violent loan shark approached by a woman claiming to be his mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/movies/pieta-directed-by-kim-ki-duk.html', 'snippet': '“Pieta,” a brutal drama by the South Korean director Kim Ki-duk, centers on a violent loan shark approached by a woman claiming to be his mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morally cunning and with a tone as black as pitch, “Pieta,” the 18th film from the South Korean director Kim Ki-duk, is a deeply unnerving revenge movie in which redemption is dangled like a cat toy before a cougar. The beast in question is Kang-do (Lee Jung-jin), a merciless bag man for a powerful moneylender who cripples slum-dwelling debtors to collect on their insurance claims. As cold to himself as to his clients, he lives in a comfortless flat where the entrails from the previous night’s chicken dinner still decorate the bathroom floor. So when a strange woman (Cho Min-soo) begins to stalk him, claiming to be the mother who abandoned him long ago, Kang-do barely hesitates: he rapes her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_PIETA_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Vicious Sadist, the Faintest Glimmer of Soul', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pieta', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Ki-Duk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pieta (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T00:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35afd915-77e3-5383-bb1f-0d83df1731e6', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35afd915-77e3-5383-bb1f-0d83df1731e6'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Hadfield’s exploits in space may have cemented his reputation as the world’s best-known singing astronaut, not to mention Canada’s newest celebrity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/americas/performing-from-space-chris-hadfield-is-canadas-low-orbit-star.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Hadfield’s exploits in space may have cemented his reputation as the world’s best-known singing astronaut, not to mention Canada’s newest celebrity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — As far as YouTube hits go, Canada’s contribution has not yet approached the popularity of South Korea’s “Gangnam Style.” And perhaps because of the limitations of weightlessness, the music video lacked any dance moves at all.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/world/canada1/canada1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/world/canada1/canada1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/world/canada1/canada1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/world/canada1/canada1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1519, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_n