ontent_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Fracking Rules Proposed for U.S. Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, John M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T00:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c6a2ad1-ca41-5bae-9e24-6b0f1957adb8', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c6a2ad1-ca41-5bae-9e24-6b0f1957adb8'}, {'abstract': '“Cape Spin” examines the fierce struggle over a proposed wind farm off the Massachusetts coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/movies/cape-spin-a-documentary-about-cape-wind.html', 'snippet': '“Cape Spin” examines the fierce struggle over a proposed wind farm off the Massachusetts coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the initial proposal in 2001, the Cape Wind project — 130 turbines across a 24-square-mile stretch of Nantucket Sound — has stirred furious dissent. The installation would be the nation’s first offshore wind farm, reducing the fossil fuel emissions around coastal Massachusetts and helping to develop a clean-energy industry. But residents howl that the project would despoil a pristine seascape, damage fishing grounds, foul ferry and air traffic and even disrupt the religious practices of the Wampanoag tribe.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN/17RDP_CAPESPIN_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle of the Bullhorns as a Wind Project Beckons', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cape Spin:\r\nAn American Power Struggle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gemmel, Robbie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirby, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T00:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df35bd0-22e2-5444-bfb7-c49af4a48510', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df35bd0-22e2-5444-bfb7-c49af4a48510'}, {'abstract': 'Greek high school teachers on Thursday called off a strike after the government essentially banned it by enacting an emergency law that threatened strikers with arrest or dismissal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/europe/greece-teachers-abandon-strike-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Greek high school teachers on Thursday called off a strike after the government essentially banned it by enacting an emergency law that threatened strikers with arrest or dismissal.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Greek high school teachers on Thursday called off a planned strike after the government essentially banned it by enacting an emergency law that threatened strikers with arrest or dismissal. The teachers were unable to attract widespread political and public support for the planned Friday walkout, and after the government’s move a vote by the teachers failed to secure a majority. Only 23 percent voted in favor of joining the strike. The two main labor unions also refused to back the proposed strike, instead staging a four-hour walkout on Thursday that disrupted public services and flights. The teachers object to the government’s plans to increase their working hours, fearing the move will lead to job cutbacks. Amnesty International condemned the government’s “blanket prohibition on the teachers’ right to strike,” describing the use of an emergency law as “unnecessary and disproportionate” and a human rights violation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Teachers Abandon Strike Plan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Teachers Abandon Strike Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T00:37:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce13d254-e567-5723-9af4-441acf0b4e36', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce13d254-e567-5723-9af4-441acf0b4e36'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Bidder 70” focuses on Tim DeChristopher, who would serve time in prison for disrupting a federal auction of oil and gas drilling rights in Utah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/movies/bidder-70-a-documentary-about-tim-dechristopher.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Bidder 70” focuses on Tim DeChristopher, who would serve time in prison for disrupting a federal auction of oil and gas drilling rights in Utah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of 2008, Tim DeChristopher, a young economics student at the University of Utah, strolled into a federal auction of oil and gas drilling rights to prime Utah wilderness. Although he was opposed to the auction, which he considered “illegal and unethical,” he had no plans to disrupt it, but when he was mistakenly handed a paddle, he chose to use it, knowing that he had no way to pay for the parcels he would eventually win.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN/FILMROUNDUP2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/arts/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN/17RDP_BIDDER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75