e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c35315-a874-56b3-b960-704c4d9b2d7a', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c35315-a874-56b3-b960-704c4d9b2d7a'}, {'abstract': 'Antiship cruise missiles could make it more difficult for the United States and its allies to impose a naval embargo, establish a no-fly zone or carry out airstrikes in support of Syria’s rebels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/world/middleeast/russia-provides-syria-with-advanced-missiles.html', 'snippet': 'Antiship cruise missiles could make it more difficult for the United States and its allies to impose a naval embargo, establish a no-fly zone or carry out airstrikes in support of Syria’s rebels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Russia has sent advanced antiship cruise missiles to Syria, a move that illustrates the depth of its support for the Syrian government led by President Bashar al-Assad, American officials said Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Sends More Advanced Missiles to Aid Assad in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russians Send Better Missiles To Help Assad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59139a08-8cd5-571d-8cee-8a418820b2d0', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59139a08-8cd5-571d-8cee-8a418820b2d0'}, {'abstract': 'If ever a White House news conference fit the metaphorical moment, it was Thursday’s rainy-day affair in the Rose Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/us/politics/white-house-memo-obama-tries-to-regain-footing.html', 'snippet': 'If ever a White House news conference fit the metaphorical moment, it was Thursday’s rainy-day affair in the Rose Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama was in the middle of a careful answer to a question about whether anyone in the White House knew that the Internal Revenue Service was targeting conservative groups, when the rain started to fall. Intermittently, at first; then a steady patter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 532}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1815, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/MEMO/MEMO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A President Tries to Regain His Footing', 'kicker': 'White House Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A President Tries To Regain His Footing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95a69bdb-d6ce-5c17-96fd-5d6210f57bee', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95a69bdb-d6ce-5c17-96fd-5d6210f57bee'}, {'abstract': 'The removal of 17 Air Force officers from watching over nuclear-tipped missiles is part of a bigger underlying problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/opinion/cold-war-malaise-in-air-force-unit.html', 'snippet': 'The removal of 17 Air Force officers from watching over nuclear-tipped missiles is part of a bigger underlying problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounded like an alternative ending to “Dr. Strangelove,” subtitled: “How They Grew Careless Managing Nuclear Missiles.” Seventeen Air Force officers assigned to launch control for nuclear-tipped Minuteman missiles were removed from their posts last month for violating safety and code protection procedures and showing poor attitudes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold War Malaise at Launch Control', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cold War Malaise at Launch Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force Academy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8848232e-535c-5964-8e8b-74a41e93428f', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8848232e-535c-5964-8e8b-74a41e93428f'}, {'abstract': 'Behind their loud condemnations of President Obama, Republicans continue to damage the economy and society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/opinion/the-republicans-scandal-machine.html', 'snippet': 'Behind their loud condemnations of President Obama, Republicans continue to damage the economy and society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When politicians want to turn scandals into metaphors, actual details of wrongdoing or incompetence no longer matter. In fact, the details of the troubles swirling around the White House this week are bluntly contradicting Republicans who want to combine them into a seamless narrative of tyrannical government on the rampage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scandal Machine', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scandal Machine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5a2b8c-6d4f-584f-ac3a-1210a2859073', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5a2b8c-6d4f-584f-ac3a-1210a2859073'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers need a clearer picture of costs to make rational decisions about medical care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/opinion/the-murky-world-of-hospital-prices.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers need a clearer picture of costs to make rational decisions about medical care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, the federal government made public a vast trove of information on the list prices charged by hospitals for a large array of procedures commonly performed on hospitalized patients. It was a good start toward providing greater transparency in hospital billing, which has long been shrouded in secrecy. But it fell short of providing full information that patients need to make informed decisions about which hospitals to use and which insurance to buy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Murky World of Hospital Prices', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Murky World of Hospital Prices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe464a3-a36a-5191-8106-9146cd0831b9', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe464a3-a36a-5191-8106-9146cd0831b9'}, {'abstract': 'There is good reason to lower the blood-alcohol level to 0.05, while taking separate steps to get the hard-core drinkers off the roads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/opinion/a-lower-standard-for-drunken-driving.html', 'snippet': 'There is good reason to lower the blood-alcohol level to 0.05, while taking separate steps to get the hard-core drinkers off the roads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is surprising how few drinks can impair a driver’s judgment. A report from the National Transportation Safety Board estimates that alcohol-impaired driving contributes to thousands of deaths and tens of thousands of serious injuries each year. It is right to urge states to reduce that toll by lowering the allowable blood-alcohol concentration for drivers from 0.08 percent to 0.05 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lower Standard for Drunken Driving', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lower Standard for Drunken Driving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Sobriety)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T01:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e3c9295-7