ed by SILICON VALLEY, another debut, and the other two 13s include “DEATH IN VENICE,” another favorite of mine and POST-MODERNISM. We’re off to a good start on this Josh Knapp puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous When Leaked', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T02:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13dae046-3418-5048-a5eb-54c1abb14d1b', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13dae046-3418-5048-a5eb-54c1abb14d1b'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the defendants profited by buying the goods in low-tax states in the South and selling them illegally in New York, avoiding the state’s high taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/nyregion/16-accused-of-smuggling-cigarettes-worth-millions.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said the defendants profited by buying the goods in low-tax states in the South and selling them illegally in New York, avoiding the state’s high taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the men had once lived in the same Brooklyn building as the personal secretary of a senior Hamas member, the authorities said. Another was something of a father figure to the terrorist who fatally shot at a van full of yeshiva students on the Brooklyn Bridge. And a third is said to have once received an investment from Omar Abdel Rahman, the so-called blind sheik, who is now serving a life sentence for a terrorism plot. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime