aptop in 2010, and the case involving the 2-year-old is one of several civil suits against the priest and the diocese brought by the girls and their families. Father Ratigan pleaded guilty last year and is awaiting sentencing. His bishop, Robert W. Finn, was convicted on a misdemeanor charge of failing to report suspected child abuse to authorities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Diocese Settles Abuse Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Diocese Settles Abuse Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratigan, Shawn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robert William', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T02:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/05fd14b5-2ebb-5d08-a000-f687ea32abdb', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05fd14b5-2ebb-5d08-a000-f687ea32abdb'}, {'abstract': 'More than half of water samples from about 150 public swimming pools in Atlanta contained traces of fecal matter, researchers at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/health/fecal-matter-found-in-public-pools.html', 'snippet': 'More than half of water samples from about 150 public swimming pools in Atlanta contained traces of fecal matter, researchers at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than half of water samples from about 150 public swimming pools in Atlanta contained traces of fecal matter, a level of contamination that is most likely similar to levels across the country, researchers at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention found in a study.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fecal Matter Found in Public Pools', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fecal Matter Found In Public Pools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Feces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming Pools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T02:59:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7fc1542-1396-54ff-9ff0-77904d52de99', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7fc1542-1396-54ff-9ff0-77904d52de99'}, {'abstract': 'The New Orleans police charged two brothers with 20 counts of attempted murder in connection with a parade shooting spree on Sunday that wounded 20 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/us/louisiana-2-arrested-in-shootings-at-new-orleans-parade.html', 'snippet': 'The New Orleans police charged two brothers with 20 counts of attempted murder in connection with a parade shooting spree on Sunday that wounded 20 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police in New Orleans arrested two brothers and charged them both with 20 counts of attempted murder in connection with a shooting spree at a parade on Sunday that left 20 people wounded, 3 of them in critical condition. Akein Scott, 19, was arrested late Wednesday night and Shawn Scott, 24, was arrested on Thursday morning. The police also arrested and charged four others, ages 19 to 32, for providing “comfort and aid” to Akein Scott after investigators identified him as the likely gunman. The police said that the younger brother was a member of a gang, and several news outlets reported that he had been targeting a rival gang member from another neighborhood, who is recovering from bullet wounds. \xa0Akein Scott was already out on bail for gun and drug possession charges. His bail on the attempted murder charges was set at $10 million. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: 2 Arrested in Shootings at New Orleans Parade', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: 2 Arrested In Shootings at New Orleans Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Akein', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Shawn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T03:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2960eff-861d-5f01-8203-9d63561ff667', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2960eff-861d-5f01-8203-9d63561ff667'}, {'abstract': 'Republican lawmakers took to the floor to register their complaints about President Obama’s signature legislative achievement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/us/politics/house-votes-again-to-repeal-health-law.html', 'snippet': 'Republican lawmakers took to the floor to register their complaints about President Obama’s signature legislative achievement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One by one, they queued up in the aisles of the House of Representatives, eager for their one minute to unload on President Obama’s signature legislative achievement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/REPEAL/REPEAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/us/REPEAL/REPEAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/REPEAL/REPEAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/us/REPEAL/REPEAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop