, 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc8220c-e781-567a-92de-adc714e15dea'}, {'abstract': 'Members of a Congressional caucus want Google to explain how it will protect privacy with the introduction of Google Glass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/technology/lawmakers-pose-questions-on-google-glass.html', 'snippet': 'Members of a Congressional caucus want Google to explain how it will protect privacy with the introduction of Google Glass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eight members of Congress on Thursday formally demanded that Google address a range of privacy concerns about its new wearable technology device, Google Glass. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Show Concerns About Google’s New Glasses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers Show Concerns About Google’s New Glasses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Glass', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Vision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T04:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02205f3f-7df8-59f3-8d71-8f77d2040c78', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02205f3f-7df8-59f3-8d71-8f77d2040c78'}, {'abstract': 'Pacers point guard George Hill sustained a concussion in the first half of Game 4 after a collision with Knicks center Tyson Chandler.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/sports/basketball/pacers-george-hill-misses-game-5-with-concussion.html', 'snippet': 'Pacers point guard George Hill sustained a concussion in the first half of Game 4 after a collision with Knicks center Tyson Chandler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pacers point guard George Hill flew on the team plane to New York and participated in a shootaround on Thursday morning. But 90 minutes before Game 5, the team announced he was out with a concussion — a potentially pivotal turn of events in the Eastern Conference semifinal matchup with the Knicks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Concussion Sidelines Pacers’ Hill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concussion Sidelines Pacers’ Hill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T04:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5809e73a-d7c5-522a-b141-529841306cba', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5809e73a-d7c5-522a-b141-529841306cba'}, {'abstract': 'Laurene Powell Jobs has carefully entered the public sphere, pushing her agenda in education as well as global conservation, nutrition and immigration policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/business/steve-jobss-widow-sets-philanthropy-goals.html', 'snippet': 'Laurene Powell Jobs has carefully entered the public sphere, pushing her agenda in education as well as global conservation, nutrition and immigration policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marlene Castro knew the tall blonde woman only as Laurene, her mentor. They met every few weeks in a rough Silicon Valley neighborhood the year that Ms. Castro was applying to college, and they e-mailed often, bonding over conversations about Ms. Castro’s difficult childhood. Without Laurene’s help, Ms. Castro said, she might not have become the first person in her family to graduate from college.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/business/LAURENE/LAURENE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Jobs’s Widow Steps Onto Philanthropic Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modest Billionaire Makes Her Way Onto the Philanthropic Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lattman, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Claire Cain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Laurene Powell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T04:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e20c833f-f00e-5e4a-82bf-687575ad09bf', 'word_count': 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e20c833f-f00e-5e4a-82bf-687575ad09bf'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Marchand left the Bruins’ morning skate early, causing fans to worry that he might not play Thursday. But he played and hurt the Rangers in overtime with the winning goal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/bruins-brad-marchand-feels-pain-in-morning-and-inflicts-it-at-night-on-rangers.html', 'snippet': 'Brad Marchand left the Bruins’ morning skate early, causing fans to worry that he might not play Thursday. But he played and hurt the Rangers in overtime with the winning goal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — For a good hour Thursday, Bruins fans were seriously worried about Brad Marchand’s status for Game 1 of the team’s Eastern Conference semifinal series against the Rangers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/sports/hockey/17bruins1-img/17bruins1-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marchand Feels Pain in the Morning and Inflicts It at Night', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marchand Feels Pain in the Morning and Inflicts It at Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marchand, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergeron, Patrice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T04:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf33211-2cea-5271-8ace-fd8e946cccea', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf33211-2cea-5271-8ace-fd8e946cccea'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) RIGOLETTO Michael Mayer, who won a Tony Award for directing “Spring Awakening,” made his Metropolitan Opera debut with this Verdi work, in a new production known as “the Rat Pack ‘Rigoletto,’\xa0” which moved events from a decadent 16th-century Italian court to the Las Vegas strip around 1960. The Polish tenor Piotr Beczala is the Duke, here a Sinatra-like playboy whose entourage includes the world-weary comedian Rigoletto, sung by the Serbian baritone Zeljko Lucic. The German soprano Diana Damrau, above with Mr. Lucic, plays the innocent Gilda, Rigoletto’s daughter and the victim of the predatory Duke. The Italian Michele Mariotti leads the ensemble in what Anthony Tommasini, writing in The New York Times, called “an excellent outing for this rising conductor.” Mr. Tommasini also noted that Mr. Mayer “had modeled Rigoletto on aggressive comics like Don Rickles, who could crack up Sinatra.” But “the vagueness of the concept undermines Mr. Lucic’s otherwise affecting performance,” he added, writing “the production was a frustrating mix of inventive and half-baked thinking.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1644f17-e259-5652-8c1e-a2ef78c7eabe', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1644f17-e259-5652-8c1e-a2ef78c7eabe'}, {'abstract': 'Carmelo Anthony provided the offense, Tyson Chandler the muscle and Chris Copeland the 3-point shooting in the Knicks’ win over the Pacers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/16/sports/basketball/Knicks-Pacers-Gm5.html', 'snippet': 'Carmelo Anthony provided the off