the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | May 17, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T05:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taylor Adams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7054f89-3c19-592f-afb0-7a968160bb50', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7054f89-3c19-592f-afb0-7a968160bb50'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shah on the recent spot-fixing scandal, the state of Indian cricket and more.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/a-conversation-with-cricket-board-official-niranjan-r-shah/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shah on the recent spot-fixing scandal, the state of Indian cricket and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Niranjan Rasiklal Shah, 68, is one of the vice presidents of the Board of Control for Cricket in India, or B.C.C.I., which is among the world’s richest sporting bodies. He has been associated with the cricketing body for well over 30 years, serving as the board’s secretary for two terms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/asia/08-niranjan-shah-IndiaInk/08-niranjan-shah-IndiaInk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 441, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/08/world/asia/08-niranjan-shah-IndiaI