rial, Jonathan Weisman writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Rain', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46d685ac-4ae9-5bc1-a6c9-c95fdea74015', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46d685ac-4ae9-5bc1-a6c9-c95fdea74015'}, {'abstract': 'In the beginning, my dream of attending college in the United States with limited funds seemed to be just that: a dream. However, I am grateful to have had friends and family who were always supportive.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/envelope-please-sush-krishnamoorthy-11/', 'snippet': 'In the beginning, my dream of attending college in the United States with limited funds seemed to be just that: a dream. However, I am grateful to have had friends and family who were always supportive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Applying to college has been a long journey, one that I could not have made alone. In the beginning, my dream of attending college in the United States with limited funds seemed to be just that: a dream. However, I am grateful to have had friends and family who were always supportive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo'