e}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/61dd63af-c186-5074-90ec-7237d96b4f7d', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61dd63af-c186-5074-90ec-7237d96b4f7d'}, {'abstract': 'It also almost killed his literary career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/khaled-hosseini-on-how-the-iraq-war-hurt-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'It also almost killed his literary career.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In your new book, “And the Mountains Echoed,” one of the main characters is an Afghan-born physician in America, like you. He is embarrassed that he’s sweating the details of his new home theater while his countrymen are suffering. Do you have similar guilt?  Of course. I always have. The only reason I’m not where they are is just pure luck, it’s just a stupid genetic lottery. It’s an unmerited gift to have this life. My books became successful way beyond any reasonable expectation and were about those people on the streets. I felt that in some way I had profited from their wretchedness.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 1449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 425, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 605, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Khaled Hosseini on How the Iraq War Hurt Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "'You Could All But Hear The Collective Groan'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFGHAN-AMERICANS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hosseini, Khaled', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'And the Mountains Echoed (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ad2428-ecbf-5ccf-8762-06b856970674', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9ad2428-ecbf-5ccf-8762-06b856970674'}, {'abstract': 'And other reasons she has never been a good fit for Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/julie-delpy-dreams-of-being-joe-pesci.html', 'snippet': 'And other reasons she has never been a good fit for Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julie Delpy has many funny lines in the new film “Before Midnight,” but the funniest one — in which she mockingly runs through her boyfriend’s lackluster sexual routine, a line that starts with “Kissy, kissy” and ends with the sound of snoring and is otherwise far too graphic to repeat here — is delivered with such vigorous crudeness that I couldn’t resist asking her to recite it for me in person. Which she did, over and over, despite the fact that we were surrounded by fellow diners at the Chateau Marmont in Los Angeles.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19delpy1/mag-19Delpy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19delpy1/mag-19Delpy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 819}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19delpy1/mag-19Delpy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 751, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19delpy1/mag-19Delpy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1099, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19delpy1/mag-19Delpy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp