b_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/europeans-rate-their-neighbors/', 'snippet': 'How European Union nations stack up in trustworthiness, arrogance and compassion, according to fellow members — views probably reflecting both longstanding stereotypes and the recent debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pew Research Center released a report this week about decaying sentiment in the European Union, based on its polls showing disintegrating support for the mission of the union. Of all the tidbits in the report, though, this table is probably the most interesting:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europeans Rate Their Neighbors', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T11:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63eba56c-fae6-5a5b-a0af-e87cc3a979d6', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63eba56c-fae6-5a5b-a0af-e87cc3a979d6'}, {'abstract': 'The ride that spurred a redesign of presidential travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/who-made-that-motorcade.html', 'snippet': 'The ride that spurred a redesign of presidential travel.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Here is a fine new word,” wrote an Iowa sports columnist in 1911. Back then, the slang term “motorcade” — a riff on “cavalcade” — described any kind of derring-do by a team of drivers. Before there was a highway system, auto enthusiasts tore off on 1,000-mile safaris to prove the mettle of their horseless carriages. In 1912, representatives of Indiana car companies traveled the Midwest in a motorcade that drove into towns accompanied by a rain of confetti and a blast of organ music — pipes were hooked up to the fan shaft of one of the cars.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19wmt/mag-19WMT-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Motorcade?', 'kicker': 'Innovation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Motorcade)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Pagan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Theodore', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ac43536-4d3d-58f0-b986-8d71acf00fe4', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ac43536-4d3d-58f0-b986-8d71acf00fe4'}, {'abstract': 'Why the difference between a personal fortune of $100 million and $1 billion meant the world to the former McKinsey director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/magazine/rajat-guptas-lust-for-zeros.html', 'snippet': 'Why the difference between a personal fortune of $100 million and $1 billion meant the world to the former McKinsey director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late one Friday morning, Rajat Gupta was rushing through security at Philadelphia International Airport, carry-on in tow, when his cellphone rang. When Gupta heard from Goldman Sachs, on whose board he sat, it was often from its chief executive, Lloyd Blankfein. But on this morning, it was Gregory K. Palm, his old Harvard Business School classmate and the bank’s general counsel, on the line. Palm sounded unusually serious. So Gupta asked if he could call him back from the other side of security.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/magazine/19billionaires_337/19billionaires_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ra