par-content-is-on-the-move/', 'snippet': 'The articles on the On-Par blog are moving to the golf page at nytimes.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you for visiting On Par. This blog’s regular features, including live tournament analysis, news and notes from Bill Pennington, Karen Crouse and others, and other coverage, can now be found on the golf section front. This change in presentation will provide readers with a single destination for all important and timely golf news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The On-Par Content Is On the Move', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4b45d7e-e25d-52fd-be1c-5171111301d3', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4b45d7e-e25d-52fd-be1c-5171111301d3'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Holder tried to justify the government’s secret spying on reporters.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/did-the-a-p-leak-put-the-american-people-at-risk/', 'snippet': 'Eric Holder tried to justify the government’s secret spying on reporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric Holder tried the other day to justify the government’s secret spying on The Associated Press. He condemned an apparent leak to the A.P. regarding a foiled (remember that word, foiled) terrorist plot hatched in Yemen, which he said posed a dire threat to national security.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did the A.P. Leak ‘Put the American People at Risk’?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29da7bf1-3809-53e1-bc71-d73bf1a1df69', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29da7bf1-3809-53e1-bc71-d73bf1a1df69'}, {'abstract': 'The content on the Fifth Down blog is moving to the pro football page on nytimes.com.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-fifth-downs-content-is-on-the-move/', 'snippet': 'The content on the Fifth Down blog is moving to the pro football page on nytimes.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you for visiting The Fifth Down. This blog’s regular features, including live game analysis, news and notes from Judy Battista, Ben Shpigel and others, fantasy football analysis and other coverage, can now be found on the pro football section front. This change in presentation will provide readers with a single destination for all important and timely N.F.L. news and analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fifth Down’s Content Is On the Move', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:14:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f2acacb-5b46-5a9e-8cdd-ac362bfc3241', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f2acacb-5b46-5a9e-8cdd-ac362bfc3241'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/what-were-reading-695/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kitchn: Another widely misunderstood Southern staple: grits. The same as polenta? Not really. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f02a2c1e-e3e8-5cbe-9f6b-22f492b30006', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f02a2c1e-e3e8-5cbe-9f6b-22f492b30006'}, {'abstract': 'The content from the On the Run blog will not be found on the main sports page on nytimes.com.', 'web_url': 'https://marathon.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-on-the-run-blog-content-is-on-the-move/', 'snippet': 'The content from the On the Run blog will not be found on the main sports page on nytimes.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you for visiting the On the Run blog. This blog’s regular features, including news and notes about the New York City Marathon and live race analysis, can be found on our main sports section front. No changes have been made in the reporting, editing and other resources devoted to our marathon coverage. Thank you for reading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The On the Run Blog Content Is On the Move', 'kicker': 'On the Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec845ad7-a765-5fe7-82af-940bd5f3c797', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec845ad7-a765-5fe7-82af-940bd5f3c797'}, {'abstract': 'Would it work in your business? Would you do it?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/is-it-smart-pricing-to-create-the-appearance-of-a-discount/', 'snippet': 'Would it work in your business? Would you do it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article in The New York Times reports that — since the departure of Ronald B. Johnson, the former chief executive — J.C. Penney has gone back to some of its old pricing strategies, including this one: “Penney has already started to reverse Mr. Johnson’s overhaul by restoring a pricing system in which it artificially marks some items up and then down to give the appearance of a discount.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Smart Pricing to Create the ‘Appearance’ of a Discount?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JC Penney Company Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T14:24:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28b2f996-92d8-5716-bb43-10c0553ceb23', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28b2f996-92d8-5716-bb43-10c0553ceb23'}, {'abstract': 'The students in the New Jersey humanities classes with whom we collaborate for this feature start each day reading and writing about The Times. To date, they have written more than 120 essays each based on Times articles and have, their teachers say, shown “astounding gains.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/common-core-practice-pigs-cicadas-and-wrestling/', 'snippet': 'The students in the New Jersey humanities classes with whom we collaborate for this feature start each day reading and writing about The Times. To date, they have written more than 120 essays each based on Times articles and have, their teachers s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As you know if you’ve been reading these posts, Jonathan Olsen and Sarah Gross have made reading and writing with The Times a focus in their ninth-grade humanities classes since September.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/00cityroom-piggy1/00cityroom-piggy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/00cityroom-piggy1/00cityroom-piggy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/00cityroom-piggy1/00cityroom-piggy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/00cityroom-piggy1/00cityroom-piggy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/10/nyregion/00ci