s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/books/review/lets-explore-diabetes-with-owls-by-david-sedaris.html', 'snippet': 'Stuck in traffic with David Sedaris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interstate 95 between New York and Washington, D.C., is no one’s idea of a pleasant piece of real estate, and that went double for a recent Sunday afternoon. Fuming at the stop-and-go jam, I jabbed at the radio, looking for something, anything, to divert me from the conga line to nowhere.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-CARR-2/0519-bks-CARR-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Funny Talk', 'kicker': 'Audiobooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Funny Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sedaris, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T15:18:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ce00d95-97d5-5ce6-ae04-7a5afe03db80', 'word_count': 1393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ce00d95-97d5-5ce6-ae04-7a5afe03db80'}, {'abstract': 'A comprehensive collection of Ernest Hemingway’s novels, nonfiction and short stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/books/review/the-ernest-hemingway-audiobook-library.html', 'snippet': 'A comprehensive collection of Ernest Hemingway’s novels, nonfiction and short stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a foreshortened life that didn’t make 62, Ernest Hemingway got a lot down on paper. If, by his middle and later years, enough of it seemed self-\xadparodying and sometimes even mawkish, great swaths of it remain immortal — and not just the early work, as some critics would claim. Hemingway changed the look and sound of American speech on the printed page. But how did he get so much work done, the stories, the novels, the nonfiction (not to mention the thousands of letters he wrote), amid all that wasteful boozing and boasting, the depressions, the freakish accidents, the bouts of soaring blood pressure, the stark-awake and Seconal-stoked nights? ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/0519-bks-Hendrickson/0519-bks-Hendrickson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Audible Feast', 'kicker': 'Audiobooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Audible Feast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendrickson, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Ernest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T15:20:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Hendrickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hendrickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d50a134-9839-5188-809e-b220f47c1a91', 'word_count': 1439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d50a134-9839-5188-809e-b220f47c1a91'}, {'abstract': 'From the birth of the Republican Party to the Spanish-American War, John Hay was a seminal 19th-century figure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/books/review/all-the-great-prizes-by-john-taliaferro.html', 'snippet': 'From the birth of the Republican Party to the Spanish-American War, John Hay was a seminal 19th-century figure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To understand the career trajectory of John Hay (1838-1905), one should imagine Colin Powell, George W. Bush’s first secretary of state, as having somehow served John F. Kennedy, 40 years earlier, as a personal assistant. Between Hay’s time as Abraham Lincoln’s secretary and Theodore Roosevelt’s top diplomat, the United States changed even more than it did between Kennedy and Bush. Hay saw the country disintegrate during his first months with Lincoln, but in his last years with Roosevelt he was helping to construct a democratic-\xadimperial colossus, getting America ready for the American century.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 628}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 979, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1957, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/review/19MALLON/19MALLON-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Present at the Creations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Present at the Creations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mallon, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taliaferro, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hay, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'},