a-53d83e46f7a7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f0962954-e54d-559d-9e1a-53d83e46f7a7'}, {'abstract': 'Two new images of Queen Elizabeth II by Chris Levine, who has a show opening today in London.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-monarch-as-a-work-in-progress/', 'snippet': 'Two new images of Queen Elizabeth II by Chris Levine, who has a show opening today in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A solo exhibition devoted to the art of Chris Levine opened at the Fine Art Society Contemporary in London today. Levine,\xa0who created pictures of the Olympic Stadium and the Shard skyscraper for our London Issue last year, is perhaps best known for his holographic portrait of Queen Elizabeth II (above, but you have to see it in person to fully appreciate its 3-D-ness). The work was produced as part of an assignment a decade ago by the Jersey Heritage to commemorate the Isle of Jersey’s 800 years of allegiance to the British crown. A similar picture that was ultimately chosen to be the organization’s commission was printed on a 100-pound note for the queen’s diamond jubilee last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/magazine/14-chris-levine-2/14-chris-levine-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/14/magazine/14-chris-levine-2/14-chris-levine-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 724}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/magazine/14-chris-levine-2/14-chris-levine-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 849, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/14/magazine/14-chris-levine-2/14-chris-levine-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'he