34-83bc-7292f390276c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cfdab6ec-bafa-5934-83bc-7292f390276c'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Academy of Music presents a major new production of “The Mater Builder” starring John Turturro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/theater/perilous-fantasies-stoked-by-a-naif.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Academy of Music presents a major new production of “The Mater Builder” starring John Turturro.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Master Builder,” Ibsen’s mysterious 1893 drama of ambition and erotic obsession, is staged far more rarely than the familiar (and generally less mystic) dramas of his major realist period. The Brooklyn Academy of Music is remedying the lack this spring with a major new production starring John Turturro as the title character, Halvard Solness, the dream-drunk architect who seems to bring about good luck and ill fortune in equal measures. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perilous Fantasies Stoked by a Naïf', 'kicker': 'Week Ahead | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perilous Fantasies Stoked by a Naïf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:12:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/997d1e71-f470-5e42-be4b-501a56e5263f', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/997d1e71-f470-5e42-be4b-501a56e5263f'}, {'abstract': 'This season’s menswear collections revealed a trend toward shirts and trousers designed to be worn at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/objects-lets-stay-together/', 'snippet': 'This season’s menswear collections revealed a trend toward shirts and trousers designed to be worn at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the relief of men everywhere who struggle with pairing their shirts to their pants, this season designers proposed the idea of matching sets. Whether in the form of head-to-toe prints, like Calvin Klein’s digitized floral jacket, shirt and shorts, or the monochromatic uniforms put forth by Dior or Prada, these are tops and bottoms that make the biggest statement when worn together. One less decision to make in the mornings!', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Objects | Let’s Stay Together', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Objects: Keeping It Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24201e8b-f303-5907-a947-98728bc8c986', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24201e8b-f303-5907-a947-98728bc8c986'}, {'abstract': '“It’s kind of like, you know, going to the lion’s den,” Dallas Akins says before performing Trinculo’s monologue from Shakespeare’s “Tempest” for the actress Kathleen Turner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/arts/television/heeding-master-heart-in-mouth.html', 'snippet': '“It’s kind of like, you know, going to the lion’s den,” Dallas Akins says before performing Trinculo’s monologue from Shakespeare’s “Tempest” for the actress Kathleen Turner.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s kind of like, you know, going to the lion’s den,” Dallas Akins says before performing Trinculo’s monologue from Shakespeare’s “Tempest” for the actress Kathleen Turner. “She seems like someone you wouldn’t want to mess with.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heeding Master, Heart in Mouth', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heeding Master, Heart in Mouth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79c9cc68-0b1b-539c-bfe7-ae8a9dff136b', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79c9cc68-0b1b-539c-bfe7-ae8a9dff136b'}, {'abstract': 'XXL Freshmen Live 2013, at the Best Buy Theater, isn’t really the rookie show it purports to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/arts/music/hip-hop-freshmen-rule-the-roost.html', 'snippet': 'XXL Freshmen Live 2013, at the Best Buy Theater, isn’t really the rookie show it purports to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year since 2008, the hip-hop magazine XXL has anointed a group of up-and-coming rappers as part of its Freshman Class, giving over a month’s cover to a gaggle of relatively little-known faces. But as the Internet has become more vital in building hip-hop careers, these lists aren’t gambles so much as aggregates of established online wisdom. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hip-Hop Freshmen Rule the Roost', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hip-Hop Freshmen Rule the Roost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62f66aa4-11fe-5bb3-889a-cbff0c5420bb', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62f66aa4-11fe-5bb3-889a-cbff0c5420bb'}, {'abstract': 'Beginning Friday, IFC presents Mel Brooks’s groundbreaking satire of westerns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/movies/an-anarchic-genius-remapping-a-genre.html', 'snippet': 'Beginning Friday, IFC presents Mel Brooks’s groundbreaking satire of westerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a good time to be the former Melvin Kaminsky of Williamsburg, Brooklyn — known to the world as Mel Brooks. Now 86, this Oscar-, Tony- and Emmy-winning writer, director, performer, producer and indefatigable comic force of nature will receive the American Film Institute’s Lifetime Achievement Award on June 6 in Los Angeles. “Mel Brooks: Make a Noise,” an “American Masters” portrait, will be shown on Monday on PBS (check local listings), and “History of Mel Brooks Part I,” a film retrospective, runs through July 21 at the IFC Center. (The program also includes David Lynch’s “Elephant Man” (1980), made under the Brooksfilms banner.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Anarchic Genius, Remapping a Genre', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Anarchic Genius, Remapping a Genre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Mel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b96f221-d3ba-50cf-9cfa-a3b3a0a035db', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b96f221-d3ba-50cf-9cfa-a3b3a0a035db'}, {'abstract': 'One of the more sibilant names in American art belongs to the 19th-century landscape artist William Trost Richards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/arts/design/stroke-by-stroke-he-nailed-arcadia.html', 'snippet': 'One of the more sibilant names in American art belongs to the 19th-century landscape artist William Trost Richards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the more sibilant names in American art belongs to the 19th-century landscape artist William Trost Richards (1833-1905), the best-known of the all-but-forgotten Pre-Raphaelite offshoot that sprang up briefly in the United States during the 1860s. The group avoided the flamboyant narratives of their English counterparts and the Romanticism of the Hudson River School. Instead, they focused on meticulously realistic renderings of nature. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stroke by Stroke, He Nailed Arcadia', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stroke by Stroke, He Nailed Arcadia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e48d9c2-96e6-5102-ac05-afe4df2be567', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e48d9c2-96e6-5102-ac05-afe4df2be567'}, {'abstract': 'When discussing investment returns, Evercore Wealth Management factors in fees, taxes and inflation — and loses some potential clients in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/your-money/an-investment-firm-evercore-offers-clients-honest-returns.html', 'snippet': 'When discussing investment returns, Evercore Wealth Management factors in fees, taxes and inflation — and loses some potential clients in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a sales pitch you don’t often hear: Let us invest your money. You can count on a return of 3 percent, though there is a chance it will be less. But we can guarantee this return for 10 years. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/your-money/18wealth/18wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/your-money/18wealth/18wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/your-money/18wealth/18wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height