': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaaa9b55-82b8-5ec9-a712-7bd12d375671', 'word_count': 1458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaaa9b55-82b8-5ec9-a712-7bd12d375671'}, {'abstract': 'Opening on Tuesday is American Ballet Theater’s premiere of Frederick Ashton’s “A Month in the Country.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/arts/dance/family-boredom-upended-by-a-tutor.html', 'snippet': 'Opening on Tuesday is American Ballet Theater’s premiere of Frederick Ashton’s “A Month in the Country.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wedged between “Onegin” on Monday and “Don Quixote” on Friday is a gem, as American Ballet Theater continues its season at the Metropolitan Opera House. Opening on Tuesday is the company premiere of Frederick Ashton’s “A Month in the Country.” Choreographed in 1976, this ballet is a retelling of Turgenev’s play about a young tutor’s impact on a Russian household. Ashton set his work, in which the narrative unfolds as a series of exquisitely detailed moments, to Chopin as arranged by John Lanchbery. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Family Boredom, Upended by a Tutor', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Boredom, Upended by a Tutor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:34:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cee89099-f7cb-500a-9707-e01a16a95107', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cee89099-f7cb-500a-9707-e01a