blican of Michigan, and Senator Max Baucus, Democrat of Montana, who suddenly find themselves at the center of action in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/10-questions-for-the-tax-men-of-congress/', 'snippet': 'John Harwood sat down with the chairmen of the House and Senate tax-writing committees, Representative Dave Camp, Republican of Michigan, and Senator Max Baucus, Democrat of Montana, who suddenly find themselves at the center of action in Washingt...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chairmen of the House and Senate tax-writing committees, Representative Dave Camp, Republican of Michigan, and Senator Max Baucus, Democrat of Montana, suddenly find themselves at the center of action in Washington. They have joined forces to push for an overhaul of the nation’s tax code, which could pave the way to a budget deal between President Obama and Congress. And they have jumped to investigate the controversy surrounding the I.R.S.’s targeting of conservative groups that has dominated front pages for the last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 Questions for the Tax Men of Congress', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camp, David L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Ways and Means', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T16:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material