eat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/graphic-books-best-sellers-humans-and-mutants-working-together/', 'snippet': '“Uncanny Avengers” is No. 2 on the hardcover list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New to the graphic books hardcover best-seller list this week, at No. 2, is “Uncanny Avengers,” written by Rick Remender and illustrated by John Cassaday. The series is about a team of heroes composed of the recently feuding X-Men and Avengers, who are attempting to show the world that humans and mutants can peacefully coexist. For many years, the X-Men were the jewel in Marvel’s publishing crown, but the Avengers, under Brian Michael Bendis, soon became the top dog. Lately, both teams have been serviced by creators at the top of their game. (Mr. Bendis is writing an X-Men book and Mr. Remender, who had been writing an X-Men book, is now chronicling the adventures of this hybrid team.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/19graphicbooks/19graphicbooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 330, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/19graphicbooks/19graphicbooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 330, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/books/19graphicbooks/19graphicbooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/books/19graphicbooks/19graphicbooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Humans and Mutants Working Together', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T17:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd5615e-c707-5587-9894-49df5301c58d', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd5615e-c707-5587-9894-49df5301c58d'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/calendar-coming-events-in-brattleboro-vt-mass-logan-ohio/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Strolling of the Heifers, Brattleboro, Vt. This weekend parade and festival honors the region’s economic engine, its cows. On June 8, farmers will lead their prized heifer calves through the town’s center, with horses, mules and other animals following. The Slow Living Summit, which ends June 7, will feature food vendors and exhibits related to sustainable farming and eating. On June 9, cycling tours of 15 to 60 miles will visit some of the area’s farms and woodlands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Brattleboro, Vt.; Mass.; Logan, Ohio', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T17:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f842d73-3f04-5d66-8d30-b11d0ff938ac', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f842d73-3f04-5d66-8d30-b11d0ff938ac'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers tell us how much they know about the real returns they are getting on their investments.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-truth-about-investment-costs/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers tell us how much they know about the real returns they are getting on their investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan writes this week in his Wealth Matters column about the real cost of fees, taxes and inflation on investments. While most financial advisers already disclose their management fees, there are fees in the investments themselves. And, of course, taxes and inflation take their toll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Truth About Investment Costs', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T17:02:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a8ea67-2d36-5ac7-b8fc-b3823fb57cd9', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a8ea67-2d36-5ac7-b8fc-b3823fb57cd9'}, {'abstract': 'The story of one of the war’s most infamous fighting units, and the family that commanded it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-mississippi-marine-brigade/', 'snippet': 'The story of one of the war’s most infamous fighting units, and the family that commanded it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In America’s modern wars, Special Forces have played a key role in hunting down and destroying enemy guerrillas. During the Civil War, the Union employed a similar outfit: the Mississippi Marine Brigade. But officials quickly came to the conclusion that, unlike today’s units, the brigade was more trouble than it was worth. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mississippi Marine Brigade', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T17:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry L. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d777ccba-a6e0-540b-9760-49bc1c68833f', 'word_count': 2168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d777ccba-a6e0-540b-9760-49bc1c68833f'}, {'abstract': 'The debut album from Candice Glover, winner of “American Idol” on Thursday night, is set for a July release.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/album-from-american-idol-winner-is-on-the-way/', 'snippet': 'The debut album from Candice Glover, winner of “American Idol” on Thursday night, is set for a July release.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Interscope Records and the production company behind “American Idol” are wasting no time in bringing an album by this season’s winner, Candice Glover, to market. Billboard reported that the 23-year-old soul singer’s debut album, titled “Music Speaks,” will be out as soon as July 16. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Album From ‘American Idol’ Win