 riding a high-speed, downhill skid. Maybe it’s because she offered sexual favors to Ben Stiller, with whom she appeared in “The House of Blue Leaves” on Broadway. Or drunk-dialed Jesse Eisenberg, her boyfriend in “The Squid and the Whale,” one too many times. Or made it obvious to her doppelgänger, Mamie Gummer, that she hated her for being Meryl Streep’s daughter.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1274}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 483, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19SNAPSHOT/19SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Bracing Antidote, Self-Mocker