pet': 'What families can do if the V.A. rejects a veteran’s claim for caregiving benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve been rejected for the Department of Veterans Affairs Aid and Attendance (A&A) benefit, there are steps you can take to get your application reconsidered. But first, a warning: Do not do what the V.A. denial letter suggests you do, as that may only bring you years more of delays. And second, you’ll need to invoke the spirit of Winston Churchill in his 1941 speech to the Harrow School: “Never give in — never, never, never, never, in nothing great or small, large or petty, never give in.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Denial Letter Arrives', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T17:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Seliger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seliger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d82fa717-e268-577e-acb7-39a46fd373f5', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d82fa717-e268-577e-acb7-39a46fd373f5'}, {'abstract': 'Rolls-Royce has backed a supersonic car designed to go faster than 1,000 miles per hour while used Fisker Karmas plummet in value.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/wheelies-the-supersonic-bloodhound-edition/', 'snippet': 'Rolls-Royce has backed a supersonic car designed to go faster than 1,000 miles per hour while used Fisker Karmas plummet in value.', 'lead_paragraph'