organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4b74e46-d353-56e4-93f7-6d377b7a2a54', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4b74e46-d353-56e4-93f7-6d377b7a2a54'}, {'abstract': 'Discussing punk’s origins and its legacy, and answering the question: what did hippies ever do to punks to be so hated?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/popcast-punk-as-fashion-music-and-theory/', 'snippet': 'Discussing punk’s origins and its legacy, and answering the question: what did hippies ever do to punks to be so hated?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art’s current show “Punk: Chaos to Couture” tells a fractured story of mid-’70s origins — Vivienne Westwood and Malcolm McLaren’s Seditionaries shop in London, Richard Hell taking scissors to his hair and T-shirts in New York — and influences, leading to designers like Martin Margiela, Junya Watanabe and Gareth Pugh. But it doesn’t tell much about the concurrent development of punk’s music, nor about its basic impulses and ideals, whether utopian, social-realist or primal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Punk as Fashion, Music and Theory', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbcab609-8ba7-5f50-8537-76fc29aca9ca', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbcab609-8ba7-5f50-8537-76fc29aca9ca'}, {'abstract': 'As Rajat Gupta’s appeal is scheduled to be heard next week, a New York Times magazine article examines the circumstances that led to his partnership with Raj Rajaratnam, the billionaire head of the Galleon Group hedge fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/rajat-guptas-lust-for-zeros/', 'snippet': 'As Rajat Gupta’s appeal is scheduled to be heard next week, a New York Times magazine article examines the circumstances that led to his partnership with Raj Rajaratnam, the billionaire head of the Galleon Group hedge fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Rajat Gupta’s appeal is scheduled to be heard next week, Anita Raghavan, a DealBook contributor, has examined the circumstances that led to his partnership with Raj Rajaratnam, the billionaire head of the Galleon Group hedge fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rajat Gupta’s Lust for Zeros', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McKinsey & Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:14:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7571c0d-64c8-5282-9cc6-8e7cfbe23a4f', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7571c0d-64c8-5282-9cc6-8e7cfbe23a4f'}, {'abstract': 'The court’s action cleared the way for President François Hollande to sign the legislation into law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/world/europe/frances-same-sex-marriage-legislation-ruled-constitutional.html', 'snippet': 'The court’s action cleared the way for President François Hollande to sign the legislation into law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France’s constitutional high court on Friday rejected legal challenges to legislation that grants same-sex couples the right to marry and adopt children, clearing the legal text for passage into law by President François Hollande, who said he would do so on Saturday. The leftist majorities in both houses of Parliament passed the legislation last month amid mass demonstrations by opponents of same-sex marriage and an acrimonious political debate. Legislators from the right challenged the constitutionality of the law before the high court, the Constitutional Council, but it was widely expected that the legislation would be approved. In its ruling, the Constitutional Council found that the law would not create a “right to a child” for same-sex couples, a contention made by some opponents of the legislation. Those opponents say they fear the new law will open the way to medically assisted procreation for lesbian couples and the use of surrogate mothers, neither of which are legal practices in France.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France’s Same-Sex Marriage Legislation Ruled Constitutional', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Same-Sex Marriage Bill Cleared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Constitutional Council (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b718d1b-fa94-50d0-935d-8c6b79258d44', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b718d1b-fa94-50d0-935d-8c6b79258d44'}, {'abstract': 'The British designer J.W. Anderson, hired by Versace to create a capsule collection for Versus, has done such a good job distilling the flavor of Versus, you won’t feel you’ve missed a thing.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/a-sensation-that-youve-had-before/', 'snippet': 'The British designer J.W. Anderson, hired by Versace to create a capsule collection for Versus, has done such a good job distilling the flavor of Versus, you won’t feel you’ve missed a thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s all right if you’re not up to date on Versus, the Versace label first popular in the early 1990s, then revived a couple of years ago. The British designer J.W. Anderson, hired to create a capsule collection, has done such a good job distilling the flavor of Versus, you won’t feel you’ve missed a thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sensation That You’ve Had Before', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Versace, Donatella', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Versace, Gianni, SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b4caff4-3fd4-578f-96a6-d7a8e1ac487d', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b4caff4-3fd4-578f-96a6-d7a8e1ac487d'}, {'abstract': 'An overview of recent titles made available from Fox Cinema Archives shows releases of variable quality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/movies/homevideo/inconsistent-quality-from-fox-cinema-archives.html', 'snippet': 'An overview of recent titles made available from Fox Cinema Archives shows releases of variable quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been almost a year since 20th Century Fox Home Entertainment introduced the Fox Cinema Archives series, a line of manufactured-on-demand DVDs modeled on Warner Home Entertainment’s admirable Warner Archive Collection.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19KEHR_SPAN/19KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19KEHR_SPAN/19KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19KEHR_SPAN/19KEHR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19KEHR_SPAN/19KEHR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19