ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e84d02c5-f8d4-561f-9ecc-5309d46db905', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e84d02c5-f8d4-561f-9ecc-5309d46db905'}, {'abstract': 'With both sweet and exotic elements, a bowl of spiced cashews is the right match for a cocktail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/cocktail-nuts-with-a-spicy-twist.html', 'snippet': 'With both sweet and exotic elements, a bowl of spiced cashews is the right match for a cocktail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many years, one of my favorite places to meet someone for a cocktail was the King Cole Bar at the St. Regis Hotel. I loved the moodiness of the dark-paneled room, the whimsy of the Maxfield Parrish mural behind the bar.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cocktail Snacks With Verve ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cocktail Snacks With Verve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:38:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b87d90fd-9dd1-5ab3-8d04-fa3387c38016', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b87d90fd-9dd1-5ab3-8d04-fa3387c38016'}, {'abstract': 'The news that David Beckham is retiring from soccer somehow seems a prelude rather than an exit, the day we all knew would come for the British superstar — oops, sorry, global icon.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/hardly-into-the-sunset/', 'snippet': 'The news that David Beckham is retiring from soccer somehow seems a prelude rather than an exit, the day we all knew would come for the British superstar — oops, sorry, global icon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news that David Beckham is retiring from soccer somehow seems a prelude rather than an exit, the day we all knew would come for the British superstar — oops, sorry, global icon. Just saying those words sends a shiver of up the spine. Giorgio Armani was so on it when he got Becks to pose in his underwear. Seeing a billboard in Milan of his oil-rubbed body in his white GA’s could really take the edge off a lousy day of shows. Beckham in his briefs, like Marky Mark in his briefs, and a host of other hot dudes, was always going to be the treat that people wanted to see. The rest of fashion was just window dressing for the strip tease. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hardly Into the Sunset', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lingerie and Underwear', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:43:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cc5d2af-6dbe-5a34-8f55-de979ed37482', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cc5d2af-6dbe-5a34-8f55-de979ed37482'}, {'abstract': 'Michael White sets up Costata in the same location as Fiamma Osteria, where he started 11 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/starter-with-costata-chef-goes-back-to-the-future/', 'snippet': 'Michael White sets up Costata in the same location as Fiamma Osteria, where he started 11 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starter, an occasional column, takes a look at newly opened restaurants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starter: With Costata, Chef Goes Back to the Future', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:44:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0abf7938-98c2-5b44-8e59-b25f292b808a', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0abf7938-98c2-5b44-8e59-b25f292b808a'}, {'abstract': 'Small moves, it turns out, can make a significant difference.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/faced-with-overload-a-need-to-find-focus/', 'snippet': 'Small moves, it turns out, can make a significant difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are thrilled to introduce a new weekend column to DealBook called Life@Work by Tony Schwartz. Tony is one of the world’s top thought leaders on the workplace and getting the most out of people. He is a productivity maven and advises many of the Fortune 500 on how to build the right culture as the founder of the Energy Project. Earlier his year, he wrote a popular article for The New York Times’s Week in Review, “Relax! You’ll Be More Productive.” We’ve followed Tony for many years — using some of his tips and tricks ourselves — and we’re excited to be able share his insights regularly on DealBook. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Faced With Overload, a Need to Find Focus', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dbf6954-86ac-5184-a8c3-9ba2b707023f', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dbf6954-86ac-5184-a8c3-9ba2b707023f'}, {'abstract': 'Once too numerous to count, many juke joints have slipped away. So what remains? A pilgrimage through the South reveals the music and magic keeping this culture alive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/travel/driving-the-juke-joint-trail.html', 'snippet': 'Once too numerous to count, many juke joints have slipped away. So what remains? A pilgrimage through the South reveals the music and magic keeping this culture alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I expected my juke joint pilgrimage to feel like a peripatetic wake. Decades ago, blues luminaries like Charley Patton, Robert Johnson and Sonny Boy Williamson traveled across the South, guitar or harmonica in hand, from joint to joint for just enough money and food to get to the next one. In doing so they laid the foundation for nearly every form of popular American music that would follow.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-sf-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-sf-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19-juke-span-sf/19-juke-span-sf-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving the Juke Joint Trail', 'kicker': 'Cultured Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Car Stops for the Blues', 'name': None, 'seo'