': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e455b635-1d82-5706-96b4-7f3c5967ebaf', 'word_count': 1663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e455b635-1d82-5706-96b4-7f3c5967ebaf'}, {'abstract': 'The gateway to Kentucky’s bourbon country is ensuring it maintains a reputation as a prime player in the spirits world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/travel/in-louisville-a-school-for-spirits.html', 'snippet': 'The gateway to Kentucky’s bourbon country is ensuring it maintains a reputation as a prime player in the spirits world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a long time since scofflaw drinkers were forced to resort to bathtub gin. But after whipping up a batch of diluted grain alcohol flavored with juniper berry concentrate for about 40 curious students at a Moonshine University class in Louisville this winter, Colin Blake celebrated the end of Prohibition. “Happy Repeal Day, everybody!” he said.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/travel/19HEADSUP_SPAN/19HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Louisville, a School for Spirits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Learning to Distill Liquor in Small Batches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glusac, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisville (Ky)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1935f01b-1732-5b42-b438-63b634536d70', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1935f01b-1732-5b42-b438-63b634536d70'}, {'abstract': 'If the trailers are any indication, the shows the broadcast networks plan to introduce next season will present a fairly limited view of America.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-new-tv-season-one-stereotype-at-a-time/', 'snippet': 'If the trailers are any indication, the shows the broadcast networks plan to introduce next season will present a fairly limited view of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The America we live in and the America we (and the rest of the world) see on television: They’re different places, but may be more similar than we would like to admit. The broadcast upfronts, held in New York this week, offered a first look at 35 new prime-time shows due in the 2013-14 season. Based on the trailers released by ABC, CBS, CW, Fox and NBC, here are a few characteristics of made-for-TV America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New TV Season, One Stereotype at a Time', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T18:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/335c06ea-0dbf-5fd6-af25-979ae6eaacef', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/335c06ea-0dbf-5fd6-af25-979ae6eaacef'}, {'abstract': 'Miguel Blesa, the former executive chairman of Caja Madrid, is accused of leaving his bank saddled with huge losses because of the takeover of a bank based in Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/business/global/spanish-banker-goes-to-prison.html', 'snippet': 'Miguel Blesa, the former executive chairman of Caja Madrid, is accused of leaving his bank saddled with huge losses because of the takeover of a bank based in Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Miguel Blesa, the former executive chairman of Caja Madrid, has become the first prominent Spanish banker to go behind bars since the start of the financial crisis. He is accused of leaving the company saddled with huge losses because of an ill-advised takeover of a bank based in Miami in 2008. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1261, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/Spainbank/Spainbank-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 1