st-and-neat-female-bartenders-compete/', 'snippet': 'The national finals of Speed Rack, a competition for female bartenders, is in its second year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arguably the best — or at least the fastest — female bartenders in America were under one roof at a Lower East Side nightclub Thursday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast and Neat, Female Bartenders Compete', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T20:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80bc8051-6927-5457-a452-34df724c7dc0', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80bc8051-6927-5457-a452-34df724c7dc0'}, {'abstract': 'Some conservatives are alleging that the I.R.S. targeted not just conservative groups, but also individual conservative taxpayers. But a handful of anecdotal data points are not worth very much in a country of 300 million people.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/new-audit-allegations-show-flawed-statistical-thinking/', 'snippet': 'Some conservatives are alleging that the I.R.S. targeted not just conservative groups, but also individual conservative taxpayers. But a handful of anecdotal data points are not worth very much in a country of 300 million people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internal Revenue Service is under fire for inappropriately targeting conservative groups that sought tax-exempt status. As I wrote earlier this week, the revelation has the potential to motivate conservative turnout in the 2014 elections, perhaps costing Democrats as they seek to gain seats in the House and retain control of the Senate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Audit Allegations Show Flawed Statistical Thinking', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Claims on I.R.S. Are Challenged By Probability', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noonan, Peggy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T20:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe618df-4bb2-5b35-8843-3ed07331d1e7', 'word_count': 950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe618df-4bb2-5b35-8843-3ed07331d1e7'}, {'abstract': 'Some simple photo apps can turn ordinary photos into quirky works of art — converting images into colored bubbles or warping them like a funhouse mirror.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/apps-smart-extra-apps-for-editing-photos/', 'snippet': 'Some simple photo apps can turn ordinary photos into quirky works of art — converting images into colored bubbles or warping them like a funhouse mirror.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in my App Smart column, I wrote about some of the smartphone apps that have brought powerful photo manipulation techniques to your pocket. This is the kind of image trickery that used to be possible only on a desktop computer running Photoshop.', 's