dth': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/arts/18COMEDY/18COMEDY-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/arts/18COMEDY/18COMEDY-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/arts/18COMEDY/18COMEDY-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Less Politics, More Everyman: The Remade Rustics', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Less Politics, More Everyman: The Remade Rustics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foxworthy, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Engvall, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larry the Cable Guy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Collar Comedy Tour', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T20:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2533fd3a-5935-55ad-be56-ef843d569812', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2533fd3a-5935-55ad-be56-ef843d569812'}, {'abstract': 'A show at DDC will offer a retrospective of architectural-scale glass designs by resident artists at the Blenko Glass Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/garden/two-decades-of-blenko-glass.html', 'snippet': 'A show at DDC will offer a retrospective of architectural-scale glass designs by resident artists at the Blenko Glass Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most exhibitions taking place during the International Contemporary Furniture Fair in New York present the newest of the new, but “Big Color,” which opens at DDC on Friday, will offer a retrospective of architectural-scale glass designs created in the 1950s through the 1970s by resident artists at the Blenko Glass Company in West Virginia. Eight years in the making, the show is directed by Damon Crain, a 38-year-old former gallery owner and art consultant, who discovered art glass as a child in Ottawa and amassed a large collection of antique bottles by the age of 12. At DDC, he will show 120 pieces created by the Blenko designers Wayne Husted, Joel Philips Myers and John Nickerson. “Sometimes people aren’t sure how to live with the pieces,” he said, “but when they see them grouped together as a landscape, something clicks and it makes sense.” Prices range from $700 for a 22-inch cylindrical vase by Joel Myers to $5,500 for a 38-inch-tall decanter by Wayne Husted. DDC: 136 Madison Avenue (32nd Street), (212) 685-0800, cultureobject.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/garden/17SHOWS/17SHOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/17/garden/17SHOWS/17SHOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 808}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/garden/17SHOWS/17SHOWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr