8; a concert on Thursday night paid tribute to these titans of cabaret.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For every musical genre there is usually an event that more people claim to have attended than could possibly have been there. In rock, the Woodstock Music and Art Fair in 1969 leads a long list of touchstones. Many would cite Benny Goodman’s Jan. 16, 1938, Carnegie Hall concert as Woodstock’s swing equivalent. For cabaret, a prime date is May 19, 1968, when Mabel Mercer and Bobby Short, who are now regarded as the field’s patron saints, shared the stage at Town Hall in a concert recorded by Atlantic Records. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring the Woodstock of the Cabaret Universe', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honoring the Woodstock of the Cabaret Universe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Short, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mercer, Mabel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Town Hall (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T20:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17fe4b52-8c73-5597-b04b-db78fff8b203', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17fe4b52-8c73-5597-b04b-db78fff8b203'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/weekend-fare-142/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are still tickets left for the Taste of Tribeca taking place 11:30 a.m. to 3 p.m. Saturday on Duane Street, between Greenwich and Hudson Streets. Tastings from local restaurants will benefit arts and enrichment programs at local public schools P.S. 150 and P.S. 234.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T21:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f8a067d-85cb-5dbd-b91d-0c0461966be9', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f8a067d-85cb-5dbd-b91d-0c0461966be9'}, {'abstract': 'The International Contemporary Ensemble, joined by Third Coast Percussion, performed works by Julio Estrada at the Miller Theater on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/arts/music/julio-estrada-at-miller-theater-in-ice-composer-portraits.html', 'snippet': 'The International Contemporary Ensemble, joined by Third Coast Percussion, performed works by Julio Estrada at the Miller Theater on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The woman onstage appears to be struggling. The sounds that are coming out of her are wordless, labored and worrying. A wheezing inhalation. A whispered scream. Choking, gagging, strangled croaks. A high-pitched whine that remains trapped behind her closed lips and masklike face. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ritual Reaches: Playing the Backside of a Violin, Using a Guitar Like a Cello', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ritual Reaches: Playing the Backside of a Violin, Using a Guitar Like a Cello', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Contemporary Ensemble', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Estrada, Julio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-17T21:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e95b319a-d7cb-5b13-b96a-d0825098ec43', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e95b319a-d7cb-5b13-b96a-d0825098ec43'}, {'abstract': 'The days of CDs and liner notes are mostly gone, but for those wanting all of the information about the music they listen to, Rhapsody, for one, is now providing digital credits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/arts/music/rhapsodys-move-to-liner-notes-for-digital-tunes-may-set-trend.html', 'snippet': 'The days of CDs and liner notes are mostly gone, but for those wanting all of the information about the music they listen to, Rhapsody, for one, is now providing digital credits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For old-timers who still go to record stores, flip through bins, buy albums and dig into the liner notes, the experience of streaming songs on a service like Spotify or Rhapsody can be dismaying. Listen, say, to Michael Jackson’s “Off the Wall,” and you see only a track listing and a link to a cursory biography of the King of Pop.', 'print_secti