erson': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7509cb8-3b6c-5ef9-a2c6-adb0299f32a3', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7509cb8-3b6c-5ef9-a2c6-adb0299f32a3'}, {'abstract': 'Good writing may exceed the boundaries suggested, if not intended, by dictionary definitions.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/the-role-of-a-dictionary/', 'snippet': 'Good writing may exceed the boundaries suggested, if not intended, by dictionary definitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it happens I feel as if I have stepped into a Far Side cartoon. I am a magazine editor, and the galley of an article will come back from a proofreader with a low-frequency word circled and this comment in the margin: “Does this word even exist?” or “Is this a real word?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Role of a Dictionary', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Skinner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Skinner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/393a639d-05e0-5f37-b54e-2934bd3bd58b', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/393a639d-05e0-5f37-b54e-2934bd3bd58b'}, {'abstract': 'At Taiim Cellar, there are flights of wine and flights of fancy that come in the form of snacks, salads and sandwiches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/nyregion/a-review-of-taiim-cellar-in-scarsdale.html', 'snippet': 'At Taiim Cellar, there are flights of wine and flights of fancy that come in the form of snacks, salads and sandwiches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent spring night, the folks at Taiim Cellar — a new Middle Eastern wine bar tucked into a corner of the suburban souk that is downtown Scarsdale — had opened their door wide to let in a soft breeze. Petals floated from trees in the nearby public garden. Tidy place settings awaited guests. The scent of caramelized sugar hovered near the tiny kitchen, and jazz guitar drifted through speakers. Who could resist the spell? Zamir Iosepovici and his partners, Erion Hasko and Altin Sinai, have transformed a shoe repair shop using exotic veneers and furnishings: toffee-colored leatherette banquettes, plush chocolate-brown ottomans, brunet wood alcoves, jet-black bar stools and a stylish wine rack of latticed wood and copper. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/nyregion/19DINE-WE1_SPAN/19DINE-WE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/nyregion/19DINE-WE1_SPAN/19DINE-WE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/nyregion/19DINE-WE1_SPAN/19DINE-WE1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/nyregion/19DINE-WE1_SPAN/19DINE-WE1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1202, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail',