bstract': 'After a stellar regular season, Chicago goalie Corey Crawford is having his best postseason, earning his first series victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/sports/hockey/blackhawks-corey-crawford-hushes-critics-and-goal-horns.html', 'snippet': 'After a stellar regular season, Chicago goalie Corey Crawford is having his best postseason, earning his first series victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — For most of Wednesday’s game against the Detroit Red Wings, Chicago Blackhawks goaltender Corey Crawford stood in his crease, watching the action on the other end of the ice. He tapped his stick against his blocker, then against a goal post. He shifted his weight from leg to leg. He skated in circles and took sips from his water bottle. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/y-blackhawks/y-blackhawks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Blackhawk Hushes Doubters and Goal Horns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Blackhawk Hushes Doubters and Goal Horns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Corey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:20:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f31b767-b485-5bba-8a54-fe3111a008c3', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f31b767-b485-5bba-8a54-fe3111a008c3'}, {'abstract': 'A ban on abortion at the 12th week of pregnancy is likely to be declared unconstitutional, a federal district judge said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/us/abortion-law-in-arkansas-is-blocked-by-us-judge.html', 'snippet': 'A ban on abortion at the 12th week of pregnancy is likely to be declared unconstitutional, a federal district judge said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Friday temporarily blocked enforcement of one of the country’s most stringent abortion laws, an Arkansas ban on the procedure at the 12th week of pregnancy, saying the law was likely to be declared unconstitutional.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abortion Law in Arkansas Is Blocked by U.S. Judge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abortion Law In Arkansas Is Blocked By U.S. Judge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Susan Webber', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapert, Jason', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Reproductive Rights', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10918a15-9ca1-5c6d-8a7c-7915d6cb03cc', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10918a15-9ca1-5c6d-8a7c-7915d6cb03cc'}, {'abstract': 'Human Rights Watch said Friday that visits to two Syrian security centers contained proof of widespread, arbitrary detentions and torture by the government of President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/world/middleeast/rights-group-says-it-finds-proof-of-torture-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Human Rights Watch said Friday that visits to two Syrian security centers contained proof of widespread, arbitrary detentions and torture by the government of President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — An international human rights group said Friday that visits to two Syrian security centers recently captured by rebel fighters contained proof of widespread, arbitrary detentions and torture by the government of President Bashar al-Assad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rights Group Says It Finds Proof of Torture in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Group Says It Finds Proof of Torture in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solitary Confinement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:26:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d32c6a4-00b7-57f8-abbf-ebe715d782f6', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d32c6a4-00b7-57f8-abbf-ebe715d782f6'}, {'abstract': 'A new tradition at the Cannes Film Festival involves Harvey Weinstein previewing his slate for the year. Last year’s show included “Django Unchained,” “The Master” and “Silver Linings Playbook.” This year’s ranged from an auteur’s kung fu film to a biopic of Nelson Mandela.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/cannes-film-festival-the-harvey-weinstein-show/', 'snippet': 'A new tradition at the Cannes Film Festival involves Harvey Weinstein previewing his slate for the year. Last year’s show included “Django Unchained,” “The Master” and “Silver Linings Playbook.” This year’s ranged from an auteur’s kung fu film to ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — If there are lines separating art and commerce in the film world, they are obliterated annually at the Cannes Film Festival. The world’s most respected auteurs see their films have premieres in the Grand Palais, just above the Marché, the international film market in the basement, where distributors sell the rights to those same films as well as to B-movie action sequels like “Outpost III: Rise of the Spetsnaz” — whatever that is and wherever it’s rising from. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cannes Film Festival: The Harvey Weinstein Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weinstein Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Logan Hill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Logan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6abc47-19c7-532d-abdf-c14f62e520ae', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6abc47-19c7-532d-abdf-c14f62e520ae'}, {'abstract': 'The Cedar Tavern site is becoming a beauty salon. Good riddance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/opinion/bye-bye-bohemia.html', 'snippet': 'The Cedar Tavern site is becoming a beauty salon. Good riddance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE other evening I passed by 82 University Place in Greenwich Village, where a new European Wax Center was being constructed on the first floor, in a space once occupied by a fabled artists’ hangout, the Cedar Tavern. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerlow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerlow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 561}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerlow-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerlow-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerlow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/opinion/0518OPEDkerlow/0518OPEDkerl