2e3', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9abd6390-4d02-5013-befc-6115cde132e3'}, {'abstract': 'Stuck without a lyric in sight, pondering the intricacies of a little bird’s brain, I suddenly thought about crazy Mary Sweeney.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/17/what-the-woodpecker-told-me/', 'snippet': 'Stuck without a lyric in sight, pondering the intricacies of a little bird’s brain, I suddenly thought about crazy Mary Sweeney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last September, in one of those early red-gold days of autumn, I was awakened by a tap-tap-tapping out in the backyard. A woodpecker was hammering at the old Box Elder out past the prickly pears near the back alley. I lay in bed awhile letting my thoughts circle:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Woodpecker Told Me', 'kicker': 'Measure for Measure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rennie Sparks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rennie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sparks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4166d885-3913-5ba3-a659-d7cc390b9d33', 'word_count': 1517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4166d885-3913-5ba3-a659-d7cc390b9d33'}, {'abstract': 'Refining Canada’s petroleum-soaked oil sands produces petroleum coke, and the question of what to do with it has found at least one answer in Detroit, where a large coke pile covers an entire city block.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/business/energy-environment/mountain-of-petroleum-coke-from-oil-sands-rises-in-detroit.html', 'snippet': 'Refining Canada’s petroleum-soaked oil sands produces petroleum coke, and the question of what to do with it has found at least one answer in Detroit, where a large coke pile covers an entire city block.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WINDSOR, Ontario — Assumption Park gives residents of this city lovely views of the Ambassador Bridge and the Detroit skyline. Lately they’ve been treated to another sight: a three-story pile of petroleum coke covering an entire city block on the other side of the Detroit River.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/business/PILE/PILE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Black Mound of Canadian Oil Waste Is Rising Over Detroit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Canadian Oil, a Black Pile Rises in Detroit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch Carbon LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch Carbon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Charles G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marathon Petroleum Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T00:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df8fa0af-6da4-5c3e-8145-e0f06fea9ebb', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df8fa0af-6da4-5c3e-8145-e0f06fea9ebb'}, {'abstract': 'On the same day, a young Moroccan woman testified in a sex scandal involving former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi, and Italy’s new prime minister announced the suspension of a reviled tax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/world/europe/salacious-and-sober-collide-illustrating-hurdles-for-italys-government.html', 'snippet': 'On the same day, a young Moroccan woman