rnizer seem to be resonating with the Iranian public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — There was a time when Ali Akbar Hashemi Rafsanjani seemed to have it all. A founder of the Islamic Revolution, he headed a family empire that owned the second biggest Iranian airline, Mahan, had a near monopoly on the lucrative pistachio trade and controlled the country’s largest private university, Azad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/iran/iran-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying Unlikely Comeback, Ex-Iran President Strikes Chord With Public', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying Unlikely Comeback, Ex-Iran President Strikes Chord With Public', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rafsanjani, Ali Akbar Hashemi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian Council (Iran)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b66a1ee6-cc8f-554f-a5b4-44a7fa3b22e3', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b66a1ee6-cc8f-554f-a5b4-44a7fa3b22e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission was asked  to intervene after a main company that provides real-time tallies of shareholder votes stopped giving the information to proposal sponsors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/business/investor-group-wants-real-time-access-to-proxy-votes.html', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission was asked  to intervene after a main company that provides real-time tallies of shareholder votes stopped giving the information to proposal sponsors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Council of Institutional Investors asked the Securities and Exchange Commission to intervene after Broadridge, the main company that provides real-time tallies of shareholder votes, stopped giving the information to the groups that sponsor proposals. At the behest of the Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association, a group that lobbies for Wall Street, Broadridge stopped giving shareholder sponsors real-time updates. The move drew fire from some who say the ability to obtain real-time votes helps both sides devise their campaigns. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investor Group Wants Real-Time Access to Proxy Votes', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investor Group Wants Real-Time Access To Proxy Votes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver-Greenberg, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Industry and Financial Markets Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Institutional Investors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadridge Financial Solutions Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f273e2a6-02d5-504c-b879-7fe0919a76df', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f273e2a6-02d5-504c-b879-7fe0919a76df'}, {'abstract': 'Public awareness is raised, as are concerns about insurance coverage for preventive mastectomies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/opinion/angelina-jolies-disclosure.html', 'snippet': 'Public awareness is raised, as are concerns about insurance coverage for preventive mastectomies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angelina Jolie’s revelation on The Times’s Op-Ed page that she had a double mastectomy to reduce her risk of breast cancer greatly raises public awareness of the genetic testing she used, as well as concerns about insurance coverage for this kind of testing. Ms. Jolie had a family history of cancer and tested positive for genetic flaws in the BRCA1 gene, which indicates an elevated risk for breast and ovarian cancer. Her doctor estimated that she had an 87 percent chance of developing breast cancer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Angelina Jolie’s Disclosure', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Angelina Jolie’s Disclosure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mastectomy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5d5ade6-9c3b-5c51-a808-ed4ef53141c8', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5d5ade6-9c3b-5c51-a808-ed4ef53141c8'}, {'abstract': 'A video being shopped by two men with drug connections apparently shows Mayor Rob Ford of Toronto smoking a crack pipe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/world/americas/toronto-mayor-is-accused-of-using-crack-cocaine.html', 'snippet': 'A video being shopped by two men with drug connections apparently shows Mayor Rob Ford of Toronto smoking a crack pipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — Mayor Rob Ford of Toronto has long been dogged by controversy over his often boorish behavior and less than diligent attention to work. On Friday, Mr. Ford faced his greatest political test following two reports that he is seen in a video apparently using crack cocaine.The Toronto Star and the Web site Gawker reported on Thursday night that they were shown the video on a smartphone by two men who were trying to sell it. The Star, which said that two of its reporters had watched the recording, reported that it was made by a man who said he had sold crack to Mr. Ford. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/world/canada/canada-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Mayor Is Besieged by Questions of Crack Use', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toronto Mayor Is Besieged By Questions of Crack Use', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:26:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba6c519a-fbfb-548d-bdba-931e6fd2dd02', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba6c519a-fbfb-548d-bdba-931e6fd2dd02'}, {'abstract': 'Rationality and fairness are the fundamental issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/opinion/sales-taxes-and-the-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Rationality and fairness are the fundamental issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-one Republicans voted with 46 Democrats (and 2 Independents) recently to pass the Marketplace Fairness Act, a long-overdue bill allowing states to require online retailers to collect sales taxes and remit them to the state where the customer lives. Will the House be so rational? It’s a long shot. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales Taxes and the Internet', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sales Taxes and the Internet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/efa0fd82-3357-5d40-b2be-bc8d64f5ca79', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efa0fd82-3357-5d40-b2be-bc8d64f5ca79'}, {'abstract': 'The Assembly should expel Vito Lopez and remove Sheldon Silver from the leadership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/opinion/unforgivable-conduct-in-albany.html', 'snippet': 'The Assembly should expel Vito Lopez and remove Sheldon Silver from the leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sordid details of how a once-powerful Brooklyn politician pawed, groped and taunted young women on his staff are more than an indictment of one politician, Assemblyman Vito Lopez. They provide a galling picture of the way Sheldon Silver, the Assembly speaker and one of New York’s top legislative leaders, failed to provide an environment in which young women could work without fear of being sexually assaulted by a bully like Mr. Lopez. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unforgivable Conduct in Albany', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unforgivable Conduct in Albany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Commission on Public Ethics (NYS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/852b993b-9066-54de-bbe4-d46cb401c6ae', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852b993b-9066-54de-bbe4-d46cb401c6ae'}, {'abstract': 'A rich trove of archives and resources at the New York Public Library cross-references names and addresses with the long-awaited 1940 data, and the results are eye-opening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/opinion/the-new-york-public-library-cracks-the-1940-census.html', 'snippet': 'A rich trove of archives and resources at the New York Public Library cross-references names and addresses with the long-awaited 1940 data, and the results are eye-opening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All pack rats should be as creative as the New York Public Library, the obsessive collector of the most complete sets of bulky, outdated telephone directories in the world. Skeptics in the cellphone era might wonder why. But the library’s Milstein Division, a rich trove of national and local history archives and free genealogy resources, digitalized old New York phone directories to create a free Web site. It cross-references residents’ names and addresses with the long-awaited 1940 census data made public last year, which includes the person’s age, income, education, job and migration record.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracking the Brand-New 1940 Census', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cracking the Brand New 1940 Census', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T01:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3ed8b0f-5e32-584e-aa99-2fdf54c757ef', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3ed8b0f-5e32-584e-aa99-2fdf54c757ef'}, {'abstract': 'Olli Rehn, the European Union’s top economist and a focus of anger across Europe against harsh belt-tightening policies, says he is not a doctrinaire adherent to austerity measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim