ge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/18/sports/venturi-obit-1/venturi-obit-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ken Venturi, U.S. Open Golf Champion and Broadcaster, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ken Venturi Dies at 82; U.S. Open Golf Champion Became a Top Broadcaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Venturi, Ken', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Sports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T03:37:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/101e926b-8d7f-5d7c-af90-91e93a7520f2', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/101e926b-8d7f-5d7c-af90-91e93a7520f2'}, {'abstract': 'An Uzbek man, Fazliddin Kurbanov, pleaded not guilty to three federal terrorism charges that accuse him of providing support to a terrorist group in Uzbekistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/us/idaho-uzbek-man-pleads-not-guilty-to-charges-of-supporting-terrorism.html', 'snippet': 'An Uzbek man, Fazliddin Kurbanov, pleaded not guilty to three federal terrorism charges that accuse him of providing support to a terrorist group in Uzbekistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Uzbek man pleaded not guilty on Friday to three federal terrorism charges that accuse him of providing support to a terrorist group in Uzbekistan. Wearing slippers and yellow and white striped prison garb, the defendant, Fazliddin Kurbanov, entered the federal courtroom in Boise in shackles and spoke primarily through a Russian interpreter. Federal agents arrested Mr. Kurbanov, 30, a truck driver, on Thursday after an extensive investigation into his activities in Idaho and Utah over the last nine months. A federal grand jury has charged him with providing support to a terrorist group in Uzbekistan. He is scheduled to appear Tuesday for a detention hearing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Idaho: Uzbek Man Pleads Not Guilty to Charges of Supporting Terrorism', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Northwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Idaho: Uzbek Man Pleads Not Guilty To Charges of Supporting Terrorism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idaho', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kurbanov, Fazliddin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uzbekistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T03:40:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patti Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patti', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/893188a1-e1f0-5908-bb0a-becd9a486402', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/893188a1-e1f0-5908-bb0a-becd9a486402'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Darrell Issa issued a subpoena to Thomas R. Pickering, a retired diplomat, to force him to appear at a deposition to answer questions about his panel’s report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/us/subpoena-for-head-of-benghazi-panel.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Darrell Issa issued a subpoena to Thomas R. Pickering, a retired diplomat, to force him to appear at a deposition to answer questions about his panel’s report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chairman of the House Oversight and Government Reform Committee on Friday issued a subpoena to the chairman of the independent panel that investigated the attacks last year on the American diplomatic mission in Benghazi, Libya. The congressman, Darrell Issa of California, issued the subpoena to Thomas R. Pickering, a retired diplomat, to force him to appear at a deposition Thursday to answer questions about his panel’s report. Mr. Issa and other Republicans have criticized the report, saying it did not hold senior State Department officials accountable. Mr. Pickering and Adm. Mike Mullen, the retired chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, who also led the five-member panel, have agreed to testify at a public hearing, but they have balked at a private deposition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subpoena for Head of Benghazi Panel', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subpoena For Head of Benghazi Panel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subpoenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pickering, Thomas R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T03:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebbaa035-5963-5f22-ba94-660706119160', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebbaa035-5963-5f22-ba94-660706119160'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Saturday, May 18, 2013.', 'web_url': 