ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e83ad997-6539-5608-bf3e-174cae6f87d8', 'word_count': 1370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e83ad997-6539-5608-bf3e-174cae6f87d8'}, {'abstract': 'With summer looming, The Times looked at the condition of public beaches in the region battered by Hurricane Sandy, surveying three states and hundreds of miles of coastline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/19/nyregion/beach-guide.html', 'snippet': 'With summer looming, The Times looked at the condition of public beaches in the region battered by Hurricane Sandy, surveying three states and hundreds of miles of coastline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With summer looming, The Times looked at the condition of public beaches in the region battered by Hurricane Sandy, surveying three states and hundreds of miles of coastline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/beach-guide-190/beach-guide-190-jumbo.png', 'height': 158, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/beach-guide-190/beach-guide-190-superJumbo.png', 'height': 158, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/beach-guide-190/beach-guide-190-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/beach-guide-190/beach-guide-190-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/17/nyregion/beach-guide-190/beach-guide-190-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Survey of the Region’s Battered Beaches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T04:28:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3bb3d993-34cd-5a49-bf1a-f5830636e36a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3bb3d993-34cd-5a49-bf1a-f5830636e36a'}, {'abstract': 'The Rail’s contributors and a guest picker make their Preakness selections.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/no-politics-just-our-preakness-picks/', 'snippet': 'The Rail’s contributors and a guest picker make their Preakness selections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rail’s contributors welcome this year’s Preakness Stakes guest picker, Mayor Stephanie C. Rawlings-Blake, who became Baltimore’s 49th mayor in 2010 and in November 2011 was elected to her first full term, receiving 87 percent of the vote in the mayoral general election. There’s a similar level of consensus surrounding who will win on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Politics, Just Our Preakness Picks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rawlings-Blake, Stephanie C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T04:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d828a2-3016-5e06-b9ce-a1954ec1da7a', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d828a2-3016-5e06-b9ce-a1954ec1da7a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Starz) BRAVE (2012) Kelly Macdonald lends her voice to Pixar’s first female protagonist: Merida, above, a Scottish princess and ace archer crowned by a mass of wild and woolly persimmon-hued tendrils and riding a high-stepping Clydesdale, Angus. Her mother, Queen Elinor (Emma Thompson), wants her to behave more like a lady. The queen has also beckoned local clan leaders to bring their sons by the castle to compete for her daughter’s hand, causing a furious Merida to rebel. When her defiance doesn’t work, she seeks help from a witch (Julie Walters), who casts a spell that sidelines the queen — and eventually prompts Merida to embark on a mission to rescue her mother and, in the process, save her family. Entering “the big business of little girls,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times, “hasn’t been easy, to judge by the deep divide between the movie’s seductive pictorial splendor and its discouragingly uninspired script by Mark Andrews, Steve Purcell, Brenda Chapman and Irene Mecchi. (Ms. Chapman, the first woman hired to direct a Pixar feature, either left or was removed from “Brave” and now shares directing credit with Mr. Andrews.)” Still, “the animation, particularly in the outdoor scenes, can be transfixing with the photorealist details — every blade of grass and each hair in Angus’s mane looks perfectly individuated — blending seamlessly with the cartoon impressionism,” Ms. Dargis wrote, adding: “The association of Merida with the natural world accounts for some of the movie’s most beautifully animated sequences, and in other, smarter or maybe just braver, hands it might have also inspired new thinking about women, men, nature and culture.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b326432-72ac-5d2d-95cf-4282e198ba4d', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b326432-72ac-5d2d-95cf-4282e198ba4d'}, {'abstract': 'Long before he came to Nascar, Dick Trickle was a renowned driver in the Midwest. He died Thursday at age 71 from a self-inflicted gunshot wound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/sports/autoracing/racers-recall-life-of-dick-trickle.html', 'snippet': 'Long before he came to Nascar, Dick Trickle was a renowned driver in the Midwest. He died Thursday at age 71 from a self-inflicted gunshot wound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONCORD, N.C. — Dick Trickle had a name that was so easy to mock that anchors on ESPN’s “SportsCenter” made him famous by mentioning him regularly during the network’s auto racing reports in the 1990s. If that playful teasing ever overshadowed what he accomplished as a short-track racer in the Midwest and as a mentor to some of Nascar’s best, it never diminished Trickle’s impact on the sport.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multim