, 'word_count': 2516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa52c46-b236-50e3-a748-26bc2ec81a17'}, {'abstract': 'The tests broke the recent relative silence from the North, but the move was much less provocative than what had been feared earlier this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/world/asia/north-korea-missiles.html', 'snippet': 'The tests broke the recent relative silence from the North, but the move was much less provocative than what had been feared earlier this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — North Korea launched three short-range missiles into the sea off its east coast on Saturday, the South Korean Defense Ministry said. The tests broke the recent relative silence from the North, but the move was much less provocative than what had been feared in the tense weeks after the country’s nuclear test in February.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Reportedly Launches Short-Range Missiles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Reportedly Launches Short-Range Missiles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T08:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b99eb9c9-6ca4-5340-8e83-e5e9ec827200', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b99eb9c9-6ca4-5340-8e83-e5e9ec827200'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and a look at the weekly addresses.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/the-weekend-word-moving-on/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and a look at the weekly addresses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weekend Word: Moving On', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc054acf-d1b0-5c00-af69-1466fb105193', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc054acf-d1b0-5c00-af69-1466fb105193'}, {'abstract': 'Worthless cars get crushed for scrap all the time, but sometimes it’s hard to say goodbye.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/why-my-heart-aches-when-worthless-cars-go-to-the-crusher/', 'snippet': 'Worthless cars get crushed for scrap all the time, but sometimes it’s hard to say goodbye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Expanding upon my previous rumination about today’s worthless cars becoming tomorrow’s relatively pricey classics, I had another experience involving a car that isn’t worth a whole lot that was dumped, whole, into a line of cars to be crushed at a scrap yard on the outskirts of Denver.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why My Heart Aches When Worthless Cars Go to the Crusher', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c3bf423-290a-59ca-a3e2-994cff2a4f55', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c3bf423-290a-59ca-a3e2-994cff2a4f55'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/newswallah-bharat-edition-87/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir:\xa0\xa0Prime Minister Manmohan Singh has\xa0promised\xa0a package of 7 billion rupees, or $128 million, over a span of five years to promote sports in Jammu and Kashmir, according to a Press Trust of India report in The Business Standard. With the funding, the state proposes to build hockey and soccer grounds, as well as an indoor stadium in every town with a population of more than 50,000, the state’s sports minister said\xa0Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T11:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35aa2926-e767-5626-847b-f0126b338b4f', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35aa2926-e767-5626-847b-f0126b338b4f'}, {'abstract': 'It’s real — just ask Kinsley.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/the-liquidationist-urge/', 'snippet': 'It’s real — just ask Kinsley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m stayed out of the fracas over Mike Kinsley’s somewhat bizarre attack on my recent writings; Mark Thoma, Brad DeLong, and Dan Drezner have it covered. And I owe a debt to Kinsley, who hired me to write for Slate way back when, letting me establish a reputation as someone who could write short-form pieces about economics for a broad audience, which led down a path to, well, you know.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Liquidationist Urge', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T12:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c075e457-1970-51e7-b070-96d73777a0a5', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c075e457-1970-51e7-b070-96d73777a0a5'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Ken Jacobs, inspired by action painting and his years as a cinema professor, is seeing his work celebrated as he turns 80.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/movies/ken-jacobs-and-his-films-feted-in-80th-birthday-tributes.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Ken Jacobs, inspired by action painting and his years as a cinema professor, is seeing his work celebrated as he turns 80.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are artists who burn out at 30 and others who, accelerating as they mature, begin to seem like forces of nature. One such force is Ken Jacobs, who turns 80 next Saturday — an occasion marked by a recent tribute at the Museum of Modern Art, with another next weekend at Anthology Film Archives. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 202, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 202}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/arts/19JACOBS1_SPAN/19JACOBS1_SPAN-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Almost 80, He Continues the Ruckus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Almost 80, He Continues the Ruckus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank':