rge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19BAGS/19BAGS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Time to Bag the Plastic?', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It Time to Bag the Plastic?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Elisabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping Bags', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T14:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2774965-e834-5004-bd3a-d3d1a1b1238a', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2774965-e834-5004-bd3a-d3d1a1b1238a'}, {'abstract': 'Many Americans, left and right, feel ambivalence not just toward the I.R.S. but toward the federal government and the outsize part it plays in our daily lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/sunday-review/the-governments-worst-face.html', 'snippet': 'Many Americans, left and right, feel ambivalence not just toward the I.R.S. but toward the federal government and the outsize part it plays in our daily lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE reported targeting by the Internal Revenue Service of conservative organizations seeking tax-exempt status has led some to revisit the long history of presidents, or their administrations, using tax regulations to punish enemies. Some have drawn comparisons with the crimes of Watergate, when President Richard M. Nixon loosed the I.R.S. on an array of Democrats (including potential challengers to his re-election in 1972). Another example, parallel to the current episode, came in 1961, when President John F. Kennedy, alarmed by the growing strength of right-wing groups,\xa0“asked the director of audits at the I.R.S. to gather intelligence on organizations receiving tax exemptions,” as Rick Perlstein wrote in “Before the Storm,” his 2001 history of Barry M. Goldwater’s 1964 presidential campaign.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19TEAPARTY/19TEAPARTY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Government’s Worst Face', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Government’s Worst Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanenhaus, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, David Foster', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Pale King (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T14:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Tanenhaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanenhaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/57fd45da-d9d6-56f9-9c51-cc56744398f3', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57fd45da-d9d6-56f9-9c51-cc56744398f3'}, {'abstract': 'There is always that moment when you are alone with the prejudice: the joke, the leer, the disregard, the fact that the moment you walk through the door you are seen as lesser.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/opinion/sunday/how-to-be-a-woman-programmer.html', 'snippet': 'There is always that moment when you are alone with the prejudice: the joke, the leer, the disregard, the fact that the moment you walk through the door you are seen as lesser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS an ordinary computer programmer. I wrote code that ran at the levels between flashy human interfaces and the deep cores of operating systems, like the role of altos in a chorus, who provide the structure without your taking much notice of their melodic lines. I made realistic schedules and met my deadlines. Those were decent accomplishments. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sunday-review/19WOMEN/19WOMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarg