Ellen Ullman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ullman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dfa008f-cce7-5b1a-b4d0-cf0145671f0b', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dfa008f-cce7-5b1a-b4d0-cf0145671f0b'}, {'abstract': 'In an address to graduates at Bard College at Simon’s Rock, the Fed chairman says nothing about his day job, but he sketches a world in which competition to produce innovations yields ever-greater rewards.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/bernanke-says-better-days-lie-ahead/', 'snippet': 'In an address to graduates at Bard College at Simon’s Rock, the Fed chairman says nothing about his day job, but he sketches a world in which competition to produce innovations yields ever-greater rewards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben S. Bernanke is, of course, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, but he always seems most comfortable as an educator, a role he slips into for a commencement address on Saturday at Bard College at Simon’s Rock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bernanke Says Better Days Lie Ahead', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commencement Speeches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bard College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T15:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 't