 recognize one towering figure in cinema. This year, they are paying homage to Jerry Lewis with a special screening of “Max Rose,” the latest film for the 87-year-old American. In it, he plays an aging jazz pianist. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Le Grand Jerry Lewis', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Le Grand Jerry Lewis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poirier, Agnes C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T17:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnès C. Poirier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnès', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Poirier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff21b8f-d8cf-5c84-aee8-4302e96f272f', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff21b8f-d8cf-5c84-aee8-4302e96f272f'}, {'abstract': 'Is there a link between suicide and weakened social ties?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/opinion/sunday/douthat-loneliness-and-suicide.html', 'snippet': 'Is there a link between suicide and weakened social ties?', 'lead_paragraph': 'OVER the last decade, the United States has become a less violent country in every way save one. As Americans commit fewer and fewer crimes against other people’s lives and property, they have become more likely to inflict fatal violence on themselves.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All the Lonely People', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All the Lonely People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douthat, Ross G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dreher, Rod', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Little Way of Ruthie Leming (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T17:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3713844f-63fa-5982-95e9-b7ab66898afa', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3713844f-63fa-5982-95e9-b7ab66898afa'}, {'abstract': 'Shouldn’t news of our planet’s complete vulnerability come from a parent rather than a “friend”?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/opinion/sunday/we-need-to-talk-children-vs-asteroids.html', 'snippet': 'Shouldn’t news of our planet’s complete vulnerability come from a parent rather than a “friend”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Avoiding any frank talks with your children about the dangers lurking “out there” in the universe is completely natural. Pointing out a full moon or the Big Dipper is way easier than telling your little Johnny flat-out that a single meteorite the size of his school bus would wipe out everything in the region, including us, and so all his crying now isn’t going to change that.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Need to Talk', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Need To Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asteroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T17:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Franzen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Franzen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/414d39db-7494-5aa9-acf0-66f7e3041694', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414d39db-7494-5aa9-acf0-66f7e3041694'}, {'abstract': 'A change in the Topps company’s numbering system for its baseball cards has upset some fans and collectors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/sports/topps-changes-baseball-card-numbering-to-criticism.html', 'snippet': 'A change in the Topps company’s numbering system for its baseball cards has upset some fans and collectors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Cee Angi was young, a neighborhood bully forced her to trade her 1992 Topps Dave Winfield card for a David Segui. The bully did not know much about baseball, but he knew that the number Topps had assigned to the back of Winfield’s card, 5, made it more valuable than Segui’s, which was 477. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sports/dog-Topps/dog-Topps-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/19/sports/dog-Topps/dog-Topps-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sports/dog-Topps/dog-Topps-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/19/sports/dog-Topps/dog-Topps-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType'