k has reported about this and related studies.)', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corporate-Friendly Court', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Corporate-Friendly Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Symczyk, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genesis HealthCare Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Clarence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kagan, Elena', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T17:49:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4b95b0e-d054-5841-ba8b-21025954bc2c', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4b95b0e-d054-5841-ba8b-21025954bc2c'}, {'abstract': 'Do consumers have the power to change factory conditions abroad?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/opinion/sunday/before-you-buy-that-t-shirt.html', 'snippet': 'Do consumers have the power to change factory conditions abroad?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deaths and injuries of thousands of garment workers in Bangladesh raise the question of how American and Eu