uest of Orb, the race’s overwhelming favorite. Jockey Gary Stevens, who came out of retirement, won his third Preakness.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/live-analysis-the-138th-preakness-stakes-2/', 'snippet': 'Oxbow won the 138th Preakness Stakes, spoiling the Triple Crown quest of Orb, the race’s overwhelming favorite. Jockey Gary Stevens, who came out of retirement, won his third Preakness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Oxbow, one of three starters for the Hall of Fame trainer D. Wayne Lukas, held off Itsmyluckyday by a length and three-quarters to win the 138th running of the Preakness Stakes on Saturday at Pimlico Race Course. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights: Oxbow Derails Orb’s Crown Quest With Win in Preakness Stakes', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-18T21:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd676a8-a7b2-5d5f-9ea4-c53ff65bc316', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd676a8-a7b2-5d5f-9ea4-c53ff65bc316'}, {'abstract': 'A befitting debut by Jean O’Conor.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/18/befitting/', 'snippet': 'A befitting debut by Jean O’Conor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Jean O’Conor not only appears to be making a debut today, but she is also pulling the old switcheroo 