anists Beka Gochiashvili and Gadi Lehavi, say — aren’t the only ones being tutored. The relationship becomes public, through concerts and recordings and interviews and practice-room YouTube videos, much faster than it ever did before. Some of us enjoy seeing wisdom transferred; we’re willing to buy into that relationship, or even triangulate ourselves into it in some indirect way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1069, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/corea/corea-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching Musicians Evolve Onstage', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watching Musicians Evolve Onstage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corea, Chick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T21:34:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af11c670-4b02-561c-8302-7dbd95e16c66', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af11c670-4b02-561c-8302-7dbd95e16c66'}, {'abstract': 'The playwright Nicky Silver has adjusted Kurt Vonnegut’s 1993 play “Make Up Your Mind” so it can be staged in Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/theater/a-staging-for-vonneguts-make-up-your-mind.html', 'snippet': 'The playwright Nicky Silver has adjusted Kurt Vonnegut’s 1993 play “Make Up Your Mind” so it can be staged in Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Kurt Vonnegut’s 1993 play “Make Up Your Mind,” the character Roland Stackhouse invents a therapy for people who have trouble making decisions. Vonnegut was all too familiar with the syndrome. He wrote several drafts of the play but was unable to settle on a final script. One version was briefly staged in 1993 and then consigned to a drawer with 11 other variations. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/mind1/mind1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'article