Nelsons, 34, has been named music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra is the latest in what has felt like a youth trend in major American ensembles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/arts/music/andris-nelson-is-latest-of-orchestras-young-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'The news that the Latvian conductor Andris Nelsons, 34, has been named music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra is the latest in what has felt like a youth trend in major American ensembles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to classical music these days, the kids — relatively speaking, of course — are all right. The news that the Latvian conductor Andris Nelsons, 34, has been named music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra is the latest in what has felt like a youth trend in major American ensembles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/nelsons/nelsons-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young, Yes; Youthful, Sometimes', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young, Yes; Youthful, Sometimes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelsons, Andris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nezet-Seguin, Yannick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T21:50:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edeae242-ecc6-58ca-aab5-aad644a79f46', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edeae242-ecc6-58ca-aab5-aad644a79f46'}, {'abstract': '“Aurangzeb” weaves Bollywood tropes — twins separated as babies, parent-child reunions, crosses and double-crosses — with contemporary outrage at the rules of the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/movies/aurangzeb-directed-by-atul-sabharwal.html', 'snippet': '“Aurangzeb” weaves Bollywood tropes — twins separated as babies, parent-child reunions, crosses and double-crosses — with contemporary outrage at the rules of the game.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Aurangzeb,” Atul Sabharwal’s dark fable about corruption and family ties, begins with a quote from Horace: “Deep in the cavern of the infant’s breast, the father’s nature lurks, and lives anew.” And it borrows its name from the Mughal emperor who imprisoned his father (Shah Jahan of Taj Mahal fame) and killed his brothers and son. Mr. Sabharwal’s movie has echoes of both : Blood will tell — evil lurks in the evil man’s son, goodness in the good man’s. But also blood will flow — kinship, in certain ruthless precincts, is no guarantee of safety.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1130, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/aurangzed/aurangzed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blood Despite Kinship', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blood Despite Kinship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabharwal, Atul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T21:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d9c6d6-0368-518a-b32a-970b20581ba9', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d9c6d6-0368-518a-b32a-970b20581ba9'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway soprano Rebecca Luker performs selections from the Jerome Kern songbook in her cabaret show at 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/arts/music/rebecca-luker-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'The Broadway soprano Rebecca Luker performs selections from the Jerome Kern songbook in her cabaret show at 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comparison of a soprano with a nightingale goes back at least to the time of Jenny Lind, the 19th-century opera diva known as “the Swedish nightingale.” The term evokes a sweet, soaring voice in the night with an otherworldly aura. I thought of that on Friday evening as I listened to the glorious, richly hued timbre and fast vibrato of Rebecca Luker singing the Jerome Kern repertory at 54 Below.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source':