lr for about $1.1 billion in cash, people with knowledge of the agreement said on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yahoo’s board has agreed to buy the popular blogging service Tumblr for about $1.1 billion in cash, people with knowledge of the agreement said on Sunday, Nick Bilton and Michael J. de la Merced report in The New York Times. It is the biggest acquisition yet under Yahoo’s chief executive, Marissa Mayer. Read more » ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yahoo Is Said to Have Reached a Deal for Tumblr', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T22:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f925a5f9-bdb4-5701-9f97-d9373216fca4', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f925a5f9-bdb4-5701-9f97-d9373216fca4'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Croce implies that we need a doctor.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/crunchy-bit/', 'snippet': 'Tim Croce implies that we need a doctor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — I started in the southeast for this one, lured by the easy toehold of “Yes, MA’AM” and film star ANNA Paquin. At first, I thought that the theme might have to do with having As be the only vowel in the grid, but then I ran into the EMUS at 55 Down and was proven wrong. Desperately, fatally wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crunchy Bit', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat