lace “Need to Know” on Friday evenings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viewers can already wake up with Charlie Rose on “CBS This Morning,” and wind down their day with his late-night PBS newsmaker interview program. If that is not enough, Mr. Rose, who has been called “the hardest working man in television,” will soon be hosting a Friday night prime-time PBS show, as well. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlie Rose to Host a Show in Prime Time on PBS', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charlie Rose to Host a Show In Prime Time on PBS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Charlie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T22:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc3dcd1b-bc82-5863-a392-fe6cf21cc6ac', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc3dcd1b-bc82-5863-a392-fe6cf21cc6ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Pearl Theater Company, the Off Broadway troupe that mounts classic plays and new works dealing with classical themes, has announced its 2013-14 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/theater/pearl-theater-company-unveils-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'The Pearl Theater Company, the Off Broadway troupe that mounts classic plays and new works dealing with classical themes, has announced its 2013-14 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pearl Theater Company, the Off Broadway troupe that mounts classic plays and new works dealing with classical themes, has announced its 2013-14 season. The world premiere of “And Away We Go” by Terrence McNally (“Master Class,” “Ragtime”) — which was delayed earlier this year because of financial troubles for the company that have since been resolved — is scheduled for Nov. 12. The season will start on Sept. 3 with George Bernard Shaw’s “You Never Can Tell.” That is to be followed by “And Away We Go” (Nov. 12 to Dec. 15); Jean-Paul Sartre’s “No Exit” (Feb. 25 to March 30); and “The Rivals,” by Richard Brinsley Sheridan (April 22 to May 25).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pearl Theater Company Unveils Schedule', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pearl Theater Company Unveils Schedule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearl Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-19T22:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfacfa3-9cc2-5a7f-853a-528c14a1e657', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfacfa3-9cc2-5a7f-853a-528c14a1e657'}, {'abstract': 'With a game-tying drive, Juan Lagares provided a glimpse of the offense that the organization hopes will augment its vaunted young pitching staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/sports/baseball/daniel