1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T03:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c59e4a-e132-51f9-8962-ec0ef7780298', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c59e4a-e132-51f9-8962-ec0ef7780298'}, {'abstract': 'Before Sweden’s triumph over Switzerland, no host team had won the world championships since the Soviet Union in 1986.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/19/at-worlds-sweden-wins-gold-and-u-s-the-bronze/', 'snippet': 'Before Sweden’s triumph over Switzerland, no host team had won the world championships since the Soviet Union in 1986.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STOCKHOLM – Ending the so-called home ice curse, Sweden defeated Switzerland, 5-1, to win the gold medal at the International Ice Hockey Federation world championships on Sunday. Earlier, Alex Galchenyuk scored twice in the shootout to give the United States a 3-2 win over Finland in the bronze medal game.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Worlds, Sweden Wins Gold, and U.S. the Bronze', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweden Routs Switzerland in World Final', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T03:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Aykroyd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aykroyd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repor