': 'CANNES, France — When word broke that thieves had stolen $1 million worth of gaudy jewelry in Cannes, right after the premiere of Sofia Coppola’s “Bling Ring,” the news was so timely it practically seemed like creative guerrilla marketing. Ms. Coppola’s film is based on the true story of five Los Angeles kids who raid the homes of their most OMG-ed celebrities so they can dress, as all the ads and magazines implore, just like Paris Hilton, Lindsay Lohan, Audrina Patridge, Megan Fox and Miranda Kerr. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 901}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/katiechang/katiechang-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cannes Film Festival: A ‘Bling Ring’ Star’s Head-Spinning Trip', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Herself at Home at Paris Hilton’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, Katie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Logan Hill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Logan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01af84f4-779c-5cf6-bee2-a98e24333460', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01af84f4-779c-5cf6-bee2-a98e24333460'}, {'abstract': 'Winning the Dutch Cup capped a remarkable year for AZ, their American striker Jozy Altidore writes.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/altidore-teams-success-a-sweet-ending-to-season/', 'snippet': 'Winning the Dutch Cup capped a remarkable year for AZ, their American striker Jozy Altidore writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a professional soccer player, I’ve been called many names. Some have been good, while others I choose not to repeat since they would be clipped out by the Goal blog’s editors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Altidore: Team Success a Sweet Ending to Season', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altidore, Jozy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AZ Alkmaar (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jozy Altidore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jozy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altidore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f528c00-a93a-51e3-99b4-f94006d8474a', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f528c00-a93a-51e3-99b4-f94006d8474a'}, {'abstract': 'Each spring, a former professional cyclist leads riders on trips to sample the area’s main attractions: food and wine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/chianti-by-bike/', 'snippet': 'Each spring, a former professional cyclist leads riders on trips to sample the area’s main attractions: food and wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each spring, the ex-pro cyclist João Correia heads to Italy’s Chianti region to lead small groups of amateur riders on weeklong bike trips that feature arduous climbs, technical descents and plenty of time to sample the area’s main attractions: food and wine. Post-ride, Correia arranges lunch at a local bar and dinner at places like the winemaking complex of Castello di Ama, where works by such artists as Anish Kapoor can be enjoyed over a bottle of Chianti classico. The last trip of Correia’s season culminates with L’Eroica, a one-day festival of classic European véloisme, in which riders take on unpaved roads with pre-1987 gear, like steel frames and wool jerseys. “It’s a celebration of everything beautiful about cycling,” Correia says. Trips from $5,950; ingamba.pro.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chianti by Bike', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chianti (Wine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Vanderbilt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vanderbilt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7057dcfa-4a59-5347-933e-1fbe7ade0dbe', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7057dcfa-4a59-5347-933e-1fbe7ade0dbe'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls defeated visiting Los Angeles, 1-0, Sunday at Red Bull Arena.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/red-bulls-rewind-monster-in-the-middle/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls defeated visiting Los Angeles, 1-0, Sunday at Red Bull Arena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.J. — His play is not fancy and there is no need for flowery words.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sports/soccer/rbny/rbny-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sports/soccer/rbny/rbny-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sports/soccer/rbny/rbny-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/sports/soccer/rbny/rbny-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Rewind: Monster in the Middle', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Galaxy (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrison (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:10:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d950ba0-9d06-5715-827b-708f85665388', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d950ba0-9d06-5715-827b-708f85665388'}, {'abstract': 'The budget airline attributed its earnings to the strength of its “ultra-low-cost model” with air travelers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/business/global/ryanair-annual-profit-rises-13.html', 'snippet': 'The budget airline attributed its earnings to the strength of its “ultra-low-cost model” with air travelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The budget airline Ryanair reported a 13 percent increase in annual profit on Monday, as Europe’s protracted economic downturn continued to send air travelers in search of the lowest fares.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryanair Annual Profit Rises 13%', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryanair Annual Profit Rises 13%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ryanair Holdings PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83856d5c-9c36-52a0-941b-248fc519ffc9', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83856d5c-9c36-52a0-941b-248fc519ffc9'}, {'abstract': 'A fierce debate has erupted in Russia over whether Nazism and Communism are comparable.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/comparing-nazism-and-communism-online-in-russia-and-causing-a-storm/', 'snippet': 'A fierce debate has erupted in Russia over whether Nazism and Communism are comparable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Just saying that a Jew should have been made into a lampshade does not make you an anti-Semite, or so a prominent columnist asserted recently. And just because both Nazism and Soviet Communism were totalitarian regimes does not mean they are comparable. Such arguments, counterarguments and variations of them have dominated Russian blogs, social networks and some of the traditional media for the last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Totalitarianisms Like Snowflakes?', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T13:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd2535e9-2b90-5b0c-bb52-438319f244be', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd2535e9-2b90-5b0c-bb52-438319f244be'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said service interrupted by the train collision last week in Connecticut should be restored on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/nyregion/after-crash-metro-north-riders-face-morning-commute.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said service interrupted by the train collision last week in Connecticut should be restored on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said on Monday that it expected full commuter rail service to return by Wednesday morning, less than a week after a collision near Fairfield, Conn., involving two Metro-North Railroad trains injured more than 70 people and jammed a crucial transit corridor for much of the Northeast.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/Y-METRONORTH/Y-METRONORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/Y-METRONORTH/Y-METRONORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/ny