t-lobbying-group/', 'snippet': 'The Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association announced that Judd A. Gregg, a former Republican senator from New Hampshire, would become the group’s chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Wall Street’s lobbying outfit, a revolving door continues to spin. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Senator to Run Wall St. Lobby Group', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T15:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21874ff1-9e14-59e1-9250-9f13a3d55800', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21874ff1-9e14-59e1-9250-9f13a3d55800'}, {'abstract': 'Few are keen to crumple themselves and their belongings into a tiny apartment and call it home, yet the eagerness to explore these spaces seems to spread like a determined little wildfire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/nyregion/gulliver-seeks-rental-the-newfound-fascination-with-tiny-dwellings.html', 'snippet': 'Few are keen to crumple themselves and their belongings into a tiny apartment and call it home, yet the eagerness to explore these spaces seems to spread like a determined little wildfire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Luke Clark Tyler’s last New York City apartment, his shoes had some unusual companions in the closet. The shoes sat, in neat pairs, on a rack, directly below his dishes and right next to the microwave. A few inches away, a hip-high refrigerator lived beneath his desk. And the apartment was so narrow that Mr. Tyler could sit on a sofa pushed against one wall with his feet propped up on the opposite wall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 1670, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/nyregion/21appraisal3_cnd/21appraisal3_cnd-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gulliver Seeks Rental: The Newfound Fascination With Tiny Dwellings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gulliver Seeks Rental: The Newfound Fascination With Tiny Dwellings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Faircompanies Barcelona SL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T15:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af8fdce-6535-5667-b919-8079c9157b8f', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af8fdce-6535-5667-b919-8079c9157b8f'}, {'abstract': 'The Communist Party has referred the case for a criminal investigation as it continues a drive to combat corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/world/asia/former-bank-executive-in-china-faces-bribe-accusations.html', 'snippet': 'The Communist Party has referred the case for a criminal investigation as it continues a drive to combat corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — China’s top anticorruption agency said on Monday that a former state bank executive faced accusations of pocketing huge bribes, making him the latest senior official to face charges during the new leadership’s drive to show that it is attacking corruption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Bank Executive in China Faces Bribe Accusations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Bank Executive in China Faces Bribe Accusations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':