ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07d865a5-3208-5894-bfb4-16ecb52c93ef', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07d865a5-3208-5894-bfb4-16ecb52c93ef'}, {'abstract': 'A study pinpoints just four microbes as the most common causes of severe and fatal diarrhea among the world’s infants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/health/4-germs-cause-most-of-infants-severe-diarrhea.html', 'snippet': 'A study pinpoints just four microbes as the most common causes of severe and fatal diarrhea among the world’s infants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just four germs are responsible for most of the severe and fatal diarrhea among the world’s infants, according to a large new study.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Germs Cause Most of Infants’ Severe Diarrhea', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Germs Cause Most of Infants’ Severe Diarrhea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diarrhea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancet, The (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T16:49:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea72289-8832-5de7-b1aa-e2afe83fe802', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea72289-8832-5de7-b1aa-e2afe83fe802'}, {'abstract': 'With a strong nutritional profile, high-protein chia seeds are a great addition to fruity, nutty breakfast smoothies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/health/banana-muesli-smoothie-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'With a strong nutritional profile, high-protein chia seeds are a great addition to fruity, nutty breakfast smoothies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, before the term “super foods” was a part of our lexicon, I would always add a handful of chia seeds to my whole-grain bread dough. I knew the seeds were high in protein (chia, like quinoa, has all of the essential amino acids), and in those days vegetarians were obsessed with proving that we could get enough protein from plant sources. I didn’t use chia seeds in other recipes, and eventually I forgot about them, as did many others — except for the people who sprouted them in little terra cotta growers to create Chia Pets, a craze I happily missed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulking Up Smoothies With Chia Seeds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T16:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8804951-5045-5e02-99ef-1459a1014054', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8804951-5045-5e02-99ef-1459a1014054'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Turness, a British news executive, will face the same challenges as her counterparts at ABC and CBS as television viewers spend more time online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/business/media/deborah-turness-named-president-of-nbc-news.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Turness, a British news executive, will face the same challenges as her counterparts at ABC and CBS as television viewers spend more time online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deborah Turness was the first person interviewed for the prestigious job at the top of NBC News earlier this year. It was a telephone interview, because Ms. Turness was in London, where she oversaw ITV News. The person on the other end, Patricia Fili-Krushel, was so impressed that she flew Ms. Turness to New York for a follow-up. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC News Picks Leader to Steer Turnaround', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NBC News Picks Leader To Steer Turnaround', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turness, Deborah M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T16:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/169c5884-d1fb-58fd-860b-c65a00ed4e1c', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/169c5884-d1fb-58fd-860b-c65a00ed4e1c'}, {'abstract': 'A focus of fashion is the length of the leg, seen in tights or just bare.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/video-bill-cunninghams-on-the-street-full-bloom/', 'snippet': 'A focus of fashion is the length of the leg, seen in tights or just bare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A focus of fashion is the length of the leg, seen in tights or just bare. In the Brooklyn Botanic Garden, the Japanese wisteria is nature’s version: more than three feet long at the height of its blossoming. And while there, don’t forget the lilacs and azaleas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Bill Cunningham’s On the Street, Full Bloom', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Botanic Garden', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T16:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4185b01-90be-5fbb-85d8-1f6f7d74ac7e', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4185b01-90be-5fbb-85d8-1f6f7d74ac7e'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/dining-calendar-18/', 'snippet': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stag’s Leap Wine Cellars is teaming up with David Burke Kitchen, 23 Grand Street in SoHo, for a wine pairing dinner on Tuesday at 7 p.m. that will feature wines from Stag’s Napa Valley winery like the cabernet sauvignons that won the 1976 Paris Tasting. The four-course meal, at $150 per person, will feature several wines, hors d’oeuvres and dishes like sea scallops benedict. Steven Spadarotto, the vice president and general manager of Stag’s Leap, will be at the dinner to talk about the wine. Call (212) 201-9119 for reservations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dining Calendar', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T16:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447c98e3-a285-5455-828c-a83c73f481d5', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447c98e3-a285-5455-828c-a83c73f481d5'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of job seekers gathered in Queens, waiting until Local 3 of the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers would hand out applications for its training program.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/camping-out-for-five-days-in-hopes-of-a-union-job/', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of job seekers gathered in Queens, waiting until Local 3 of the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers would hand out applications for its training program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The men began arriving last Wednesday, first a trickle, then dozens. By Friday there were hundreds of them, along with a few women. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/nyregion/20cityroom-union/20cityroom-union-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/nyregion/20cityroom-union/20cityroom-union-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05