t': 'Before Grant laid his famous siege, he undertook two disastrous assaults on the bluff city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall of Vicksburg, Miss., to forces under Gen. Ulysses S. Grant is remembered for the long, intensive siege that led up to it. But before the Union Army put a stranglehold on Vicksburg, Grant made two disastrous assaults on the city, on May 19 and 22.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battles of Vicksburg', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vicksburg (Miss)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Violet Snow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Violet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Snow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/306aa886-d546-5448-af0e-82142ba56059', 'word_count': 1536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/306aa886-d546-5448-af0e-82142ba56059'}, {'abstract': 'The American Psychiatric Association’s official manual of mental disorders, newly revised, may not be ideal, but it offers clinicians a common language.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/health/the-dsm-5-as-a-guide-not-a-bible.html', 'snippet': 'The American Psychiatric Association’s official manual of mental disorders, newly revised, may not be ideal, but it offers clinicians a common language.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There won’t be many book parties when the latest version of the American Psychiatric Association’s official manual of mental disorders, known as the D.S.M.-5, rolls off the presses this week. Instead, the long-awaited guide has touched off a heated debate among psychiatrists about its scientific value and clinical usefulness.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Book Stops Here', 'kicker': 'Mind', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Book Stops Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN PSYCHIATRIC ASSN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Richard A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:11:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Friedman, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6b243a3-2ecb-5045-b99b-fd9559729997', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6b243a3-2ecb-5045-b99b-fd9559729997'}, {'abstract': 'The actor Jon Hamm is more than a Mad Man. He’s part of a new campaign for American Airlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/business/media/q-and-a-with-stuart-elliott.html', 'snippet': 'The actor Jon Hamm is more than a Mad Man. He’s part of a new campaign for American Airlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stuart Elliott, the advertising columnist, answers questions from readers each week. Questions can be sent to stuarte@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Stuart Elliott', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q. and A. With Stuart Elliott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/162a0744-3014-59d8-8895-302e3e5ccf1f', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162a0744-3014-59d8-8895-302e3e5ccf1f'}, {'abstract': 'The Association of Music Producers, New York, presented its first awards for music and sound. The Best of Show award was won by “Metamorphosis,” an animated short for Good Books, with music by Antfood, New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'The Association of Music Producers, New York, presented its first awards for music and sound. The Best of Show award was won by “Metamorphosis,” an animated short for Good Books, with music by Antfood, New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Association of Music Producers, New York, presented its first AMP Awards for Music and Sound. The Best of Show award was won by “Metamorphosis,” an animated short for Good Books, an online bookseller, with music by Antfood, New York. “Metamorphosis” also shared the award for best use of music/sound for Web or interactive branding with Yessian, for “Compilation,” for “Dream Bigger Dreams” by Nick Cave. The association also announced the inaugural inductions into the Association of Music Producers Hall of Fame, the Coca-Cola Company and the McDonald’s Corporation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8324bce6-7c63-52b4-a0b3-2b8551480b02', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8324bce6-7c63-52b4-a0b3-2b8551480b02'}, {'abstract': 'The company said there was no indication that the deaths, which occurred away from its factories, were work-related.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/business/global/3-foxconn-employees-are-said-to-have-committed-suicide.html', 'snippet': 'The company said there was no indication that the deaths, which occurred away from its factories, were work-related.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Three Chinese employees at Foxconn, one of the world’s biggest contract electronics manufacturers, died in what were believed to be suicides in recent weeks, which a group that monitors labor conditions in China says is the latest indication that the company continues to be plagued by labor problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Says Deaths Show Problems Remain at Foxconn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Says String of Deaths Shows Problems at Foxconn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foxconn Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd12f46-8ca1-50a1-bd38-24dd5aa2a153', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd12f46-8ca1-50a1-bd38-24dd5aa2a153'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate Finance Committee forwarded a six-page letter to Steven Miller, the acting I.R.S. commissioner who is resigning, with 41 pointed questions seeking information about who in the Obama administration knew what.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/senate-panel-asks-i-r-s-chief-to-detail-communications-with-white-house/', 'snippet': 'The Senate Finance Committee forwarded a six-page letter to Steven Miller, the acting I.R.S. commissioner who is resigning, with 41 pointed questions seeking information about who in the Obama administration knew what.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Internal Revenue Service and the Obama administration thought the Senate Finance Committee and its Democratic leaders would offer something of a respite from the battering they have been taking from Congressional Republicans, they learned otherwise on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Panel Asks I.R.S. Chief to Detail Communications With White House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service Political Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Steven T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Finance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T17:16:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ab028df-d4dd-5b9b-b463-8ccb1b4c4b24', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ab028df-d4dd-5b9b-b463-8ccb1b4c4b24'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department is racing to fulfill recommendations on diplomatic security, but some Republicans have questioned its ability to carry out the changes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/us/politics/after-benghazi-us-pressing-ahead-on-security-upgrades.html', 'snippet': 'The State Department is racing to fulfill recommendations on diplomatic security, but some Republicans have questioned its ability to carry out the changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — By late this summer, the State Department plans to send dozens of additional diplomatic security agents to high-threat embassies, install millions of dollars of advanced fire-survival gear and surveillance cameras in those diplomatic posts, and improve training for employees headed to the riskiest missions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/world/SECURITY/SECURITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/world/SECURITY/SECURITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/world/SECURITY/SECURITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/world/SECURITY/SECURITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/world/SECURITY/SECURITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wid