In | Escape to Provence', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Escape to Provence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Provence (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T18:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e156259-d9e5-5eed-abf4-ebc8d59bff52', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e156259-d9e5-5eed-abf4-ebc8d59bff52'}, {'abstract': 'Designers focused on improving lives for poor farmers have a solar-powered pumping plan.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/a-plan-to-bring-sun-powered-irrigation-to-poor-farmers/', 'snippet': 'Designers focused on improving lives for poor farmers have a solar-powered pumping plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the finest applications of solar photovoltaic panels is in powering drip irrigation systems for farmers in hot, sunny, poor parts of the world. You don’t even need to store the electricity. The pumping is mainly needed when the sun is shining.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/blogs/dotdrip/dotdrip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/blogs/dotdrip/dotdrip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 't