e': '2013-05-20T19:07:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f1a1bcb-69fe-52ee-ad6b-ba701b9c6d12', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f1a1bcb-69fe-52ee-ad6b-ba701b9c6d12'}, {'abstract': 'An unemployed former security guard shot and killed four people in a bank in the southern Israeli city of Beersheba on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/world/middleeast/gunman-kills-four-in-bank-in-southern-israel.html', 'snippet': 'An unemployed former security guard shot and killed four people in a bank in the southern Israeli city of Beersheba on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unemployed former security guard shot and killed four people in a bank in the southern Israeli city of Beersheba on Monday hours after the bank had refused his request for financial assistance, the police said. The gunman committed suicide after holing up in the bathroom of the bank with a female hostage for about an hour. The hostage escaped unharmed. The gunman, who lived nearby, had visited the bank in the morning and, according to the Israeli news media, found that his account had been blocked because of a debt. He returned later and killed the bank manager, his deputy and two clients. Random shootings of this kind are rare in Israel. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu described the event as “a terrible tragedy,” adding, “I cannot remember such an incident, certainly not in recent years.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gunman Kills Four in a Bank in Southern Israel', 'kicker': 'World Brief | Middle East ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Man Attacks Bank After His Account Is Blocked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T19:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a236754b-6cc4-5e9e-bee1-3d4d3e9db52f', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a236754b-6cc4-5e9e-bee1-3d4d3e9db52f'}, {'abstract': 'Usually light in body and moderate in alcohol, saisons are defined by their variety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/the-perfect-summer-beer-may-be-the-saison.html', 'snippet': 'Usually light in body and moderate in alcohol, saisons are defined by their variety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the American beer world has been in love with saisons: dry, fruity ales traditionally made by Belgian farmers in winter, then set aside for quenching thirst during hot summer days in the fields. But while most craft breweries have a saison beer in their rotation, and some even specialize in the style, it has yet to catch on with the general, I.P.A.-swilling public.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22BEER/22BEER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':