, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a59c548-1ad2-554a-948f-045bc45c1647', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a59c548-1ad2-554a-948f-045bc45c1647'}, {'abstract': 'Think of the scolds left behind.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/where-are-the-deficit-celebrations/', 'snippet': 'Think of the scolds left behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For three years and more Beltway politics has been all about the deficit. Urgent action was needed to avert crisis. A Grand Bargain absolutely had to be reached. Fix the Debt, now now now!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Are The Deficit Celebrations?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9016fe2-0b43-5ce2-bc8d-49145b62fa57', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9016fe2-0b43-5ce2-bc8d-49145b62fa57'}, {'abstract': 'A letter to the Editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/health/it-takes-a-community-1-letter.html', 'snippet': 'A letter to the Editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It Takes a Community (1 Letter)', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It Takes a Community', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:11:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/10dc41f4-209e-5f14-ba96-3236525e16d7', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10dc41f4-209e-5f14-ba96-3236525e16d7'}, {'abstract': 'A shot of espresso poured over ice cubes and simple syrup is as refreshing as it is flavorful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/new-yorks-cult-hit-is-an-italian-standard.html', 'snippet': 'A shot of espresso poured over ice cubes and simple syrup is as refreshing as it is flavorful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There isn’t much to the shakerato: a shot of espresso poured over ice cubes and simple syrup, then shaken. But when those three elements are rattled around in a cocktail shaker for what seems like an eternity (it actually clocks in at 15 seconds), they undergo an alchemical transformation: the dense espresso, now frothy, sweet and flecked with ice, is as refreshing as it is flavorful.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chilled Espresso, Shaken to a Froth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sips of Summer: Shakerato', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strand, Oliver', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e0825f1-0c9f-5bff-96ac-8774ece1b00c', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e0825f1-0c9f-5bff-96ac-8774ece1b00c'}, {'abstract': 'Crowned with fruit and ice, the sherry cobbler looks impressive and goes easy on you on a hot day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/the-king-of-sherry-cocktails.html', 'snippet': 'Crowned with fruit and ice, the sherry cobbler looks impressive and goes easy on you on a hot day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a renewed interest these days in sherry, not least among bartenders, who are creating cocktails at a breakneck pace using various expressions of the fortified wine. This has produced some liquid gems, particularly those drinks that capitalize on sherry’s reliable affinity with the agave spirits tequila and mezcal.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22SHERRY/22SHERRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The King of Sherry Cocktails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sips of Summer: Sherry Cobbler', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sherry (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonson, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c03986f5-ffa6-5000-b620-8b9e93abe9c1', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c03986f5-ffa6-5000-b620-8b9e93abe9c1'}, {'abstract': 'The whole point of drinking (and making) these peachy cocktails is that they’re easy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/say-yes-to-the-bellini.html', 'snippet': 'The whole point of drinking (and making) these peachy cocktails is that they’re easy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s say you’re hosting a summer fiesta. You want your guests to waltz into the backyard and find something more than chilled Sancerre and a tub full of beer bottles and ice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Say Yes to the Bellini', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sips of Summer: Bellini', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordinier, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d85bb4d-f15d-581b-b0bd-607c5602c6c3', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d85bb4d-f15d-581b-b0bd-607c5602c6c3'}, {'abstract': 'Drink a Paloma, made with muddled grapefruit and basil, instead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/give-the-margarita-a-rest.html', 'snippet': 'Drink a Paloma, made with muddled grapefruit and basil, instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, a friend returned from a trip to Mexico imploring anyone who would listen to give the margarita a rest and drink a Paloma instead. In its most elemental form, the Paloma is tequila and grapefruit soda (preferably Squirt), maybe with a splash of lime juice. That’s a good drink. But for all his evangelical zeal, my friend had a hard time finding Squirt in his Brooklyn neighborhood. He was willing to let go of authenticity, and let me make him a Paloma with fresh grapefruit juice, a little simple syrup and soda water instead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Give the Margarita a Rest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a0b2b61-569c-5fa4-be4d-74e8a652378c', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a0b2b61-569c-5fa4-be4d-74e8a652378c'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of investigating talking points, how about looking into the C.I.A.’s role in the Benghazi security failure?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/there-just-has-to-be-a-scandal-somewhere/', 'snippet': 'Instead of investigating talking points, how about looking into the C.I.A.’s role in the Benghazi security failure?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American public, Greg Sargent pointed out this morning, does not find a presidential scandal in either the Benghazi talking points or the Internal Revenue Service’s targeting of right-wing groups seeking a tax-exempt and disclosure-free status.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There Just Has to Be a Scandal – Somewhere', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pickering, Thomas R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:20:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93f1c11f-b73b-5a22-9721-82c1604f039f', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93f1c11f-b73b-5a22-9721-82c1604f039f'}, {'abstract': 'Some whiskeys are sufficiently light and refreshing to stand alongside gin or vodka in a summertime bar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/for-a-warm-day-a-young-whiskey.html', 'snippet': 'Some whiskeys are sufficiently light and refreshing to stand alongside gin or vodka in a summertime bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many people, whiskey and warm weather don’t mix: peat, sherry, smoke and caramel aren’t exactly thirst-quenching flavors. But not all whiskeys are created equal, and some are sufficiently light and refreshing to stand alongside gin or vodka in a summertime bar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22WHISKEY/22WHISKEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Warm Day, a Young Whiskey', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whiskey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clay Risen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Risen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f90f4a86-9236-54e1-a8fd-8c9f8f19ff0c', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f90f4a86-9236-54e1-a8fd-8c9f8f19ff0c'}, {'abstract': 'For summertime drinking, a pitcher of Americanos enjoyed on the back porch will not leave you down for the count.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/the-negronis-lighter-saner-progenitor.html', 'snippet': 'For summertime drinking, a pitcher of Americanos enjoyed on the back porch will not leave you down for the count.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Negroni is enjoying a moment now. For bartenders and barflies, this deliciously complex mix of Campari, gin and sweet vermouth has become an easy way to fly one’s flag as a knowing cocktail classicist. But the drink’s rising profile has cast a shadow over its once-popular progenitor, the Americano. Without this refreshing Italian-born highball — Campari, sweet vermouth and club soda — there would have been no blueprint for the gin-loving Count Camillo Negroni to experiment with a century ago. (The drink’s family line actually goes back even farther; the Americano grew out of a simpler aperitif that omitted the soda, called the Milano-Torino — Milano in honor of the birthplace of Campari, Torino for the vermouth.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Negroni’s Lighter, Saner Progenitor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sips of Summer: Americano', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonson, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:21:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c21842d1-0136-5dd8-9294-417957906dd1', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c21842d1-0136-5dd8-9294-417957906dd1'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers are reporting that early ancestors of humans had inner ear bones very similar to those of modern men and women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/science/ear-bones-of-ancestors-are-like-those-of-modern-humans.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers are reporting that early ancestors of humans had inner ear bones very similar to those of modern men and women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our very early ancestors possessed bones in the middle ear very similar to those of modern humans, researchers are reporting. The finding suggests that hearing sensitivity is one of the oldest features of human evolution.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Link to Ears of Early Humans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evolution: A Link to Ears of Early Humans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ears and Hearing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution (Biology)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:22:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e17d7af7-c4ed-5537-a9cc-502aa32b2931', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e17d7af7-c4ed-5537-a9cc-502aa32b2931'}, {'abstract': 'The kalimotxo is wonderfully refreshing, and doesn’t require all that fruit-chopping and waiting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/wine-and-cola-it-works.html', 'snippet': 'The kalimotxo is wonderfully refreshing, and doesn’t require all that fruit-chopping and waiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some might consider the kalimotxo (pronounced cal-ee-MO-cho) a guilty pleasure; I’ve received more than a few skeptical glances when I’ve ordered it at bars in New York. But I don’t feel an iota of contrition when I drink this Basque-country classic. It couldn’t be easier: equal parts red wine (some say the cheaper the better, but that’s up to you) and cola. I like a squeeze of lemon juice for a little brightness, and maybe a slice of lemon or orange to dress it up. But purists might consider even those modest additions a little fussy. The overall effect is surprisingly sangria-esque, minus all that fruit-chopping and waiting, and wonderfully refreshing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wine and Cola? It Works', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a859e22-6ade-5d59-88c8-83c000eb728d', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a859e22-6ade-5d59-88c8-83c000eb728d'}, {'abstract': 'Cold soups take nicely to the addition of a little alcohol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/waiter-theres-a-cocktail-in-my-soup.html', 'snippet': 'Cold soups take nicely to the addition of a little alcohol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A while ago, struck by how similar a tomato-based gazpacho was to a Bloody Mary mix, I added vodka to the soup. Voilà: a chilled cocktail and summery first course in one. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22soup/22soup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiter, There’s a Cocktail in My Soup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soup? Cocktail? Both', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3641bad-448c-59ed-9a7e-8afa53bf4337', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3641bad-448c-59ed-9a7e-8afa53bf4337'}, {'abstract': 'Made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda, the Americano is a light summertime drink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/100000002235480/americano-an-italian-born-highball.html', 'snippet': 'Made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda, the Americano is a light summertime drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda, the Americano is a light summertime drink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/dining/video-summer-drinks-americano/video-summer-drinks-americano-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americano: An Italian-Born Highball', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'Jenny Woodward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woodward', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/06f8a735-2fd1-5655-9ca0-414f7201d36c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/06f8a735-2fd1-5655-9ca0-414f7201d36c'}, {'abstract': 'A consumer group has prepared an “anti-phishing” tip sheet.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/tips-on-avoiding-phishing-frauds/', 'snippet': 'A consumer group has prepared an “anti-phishing” tip sheet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I consider myself fairly cautious about Internet security, but I was still nearly caught off guard by a phishing effort aimed at me a couple of years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips on Avoiding Phishing Frauds', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Phishing (Computer Fraud)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Federation of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/211f3c18-320d-56e3-8b26-eb7975025acc', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/211f3c18-320d-56e3-8b26-eb7975025acc'}, {'abstract': 'A less geographically mobile America is not necessarily a more communitarian America.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/when-place-is-not-enough/', 'snippet': 'A less geographically mobile America is not necessarily a more communitarian America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column\xa0invoked Rod Dreher’s new book, “The Little Way of Ruthie Leming,” while trying to tease out some issues surrounding loneliness and community in America, and particularly the possible link between Americans’ weakening social ties and our slowly rising suicide rate. Readers interested in these questions should also check out\xa0Damon Linker’s recent column on “Little Way”, which puts Dreher’s book in the context of a broader intellectual tendency on the post-Bush, post-Great Recession right:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Place Is Not Enough', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:42:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb9cb4e-cc9c-500c-ae0b-f1e706c9a78f', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb9cb4e-cc9c-500c-ae0b-f1e706c9a78f'}, {'abstract': '“Look and Listen,” a festival of new music performed in art galleries, kicked off its 12th season with a concert at the Pratt Manhattan Gallery on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/music/look-and-listen-at-the-pratt-manhattan-gallery.html', 'snippet': '“Look and Listen,” a festival of new music performed in art galleries, kicked off its 12th season with a concert at the Pratt Manhattan Gallery on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Look and Listen is the title of a festival of new music performed in art galleries that kicked off its 12th season with a concert at the Pratt Manhattan Gallery on Friday evening. But during a performance of Lewis Nielson’s piece “Le Journal du Corps” by the intrepid JACK quartet, I found myself compulsively engaged in a third activity: labeling. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing a Couple of Senses Into Sync', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing A Couple Of Senses Into Sync', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 