/', 'snippet': 'Coming soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theory of interstellar trade is a well-understood topic, with an extensive literature consisting of one paper (pdf) I wrote in 1978. Interstellar finance, however, is less well covered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Theory of Interstellar Finance', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T20:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1a215c9-f1db-5112-9af8-8b95815eaded', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1a215c9-f1db-5112-9af8-8b95815eaded'}, {'abstract': 'Tertulia, a concert series meant to broaden the appeal of chamber music, combines dinner with a performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/music/that-corner-spot-its-perfect-for-a-concert.html', 'snippet': 'Tertulia, a concert series meant to broaden the appeal of chamber music, combines dinner with a performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harding’s, a cozy Flatiron district restaurant handsomely appointed in Americana and offering an inventive menu to match, was abuzz on Sunday evening, its dining room filled with the lively sound of customers mingling over glasses of wine. At 20 minutes after 8, a hostess tapped a glass for attention as a pianist, a violinist and a cellist settled into a corner niche to perform.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/21TERTULIA/21TERTULIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height':