_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aee2e1d-5712-54e9-be65-0e0833892ba8', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aee2e1d-5712-54e9-be65-0e0833892ba8'}, {'abstract': 'A Congressional inquiry’s findings were remarkable both for the tens of billions of dollars involved and for Apple’s audacity in saying some of its subsidiaries were stateless and beyond any tax authority’s reach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/business/apple-avoided-billions-in-taxes-congressional-panel-says.html', 'snippet': 'A Congressional inquiry’s findings were remarkable both for the tens of billions of dollars involved and for Apple’s audacity in saying some of its subsidiaries were stateless and beyond any tax authority’s reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Even as Apple became the nation’s most profitable technology company, it avoided billions in taxes in the United States and around the world through a web of subsidiaries so complex it spanned continents and went beyond anything most experts had ever seen, Congressional investigators disclosed on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Web of Tax Shelters Saved It Billions, Panel Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Billions In Taxes Avoided By Apple, U.S. Inquiry Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duhigg, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Timothy D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Shelters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz and Charles Duhigg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70d02eb9-4c88-5035-b998-864054f26bb2', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70d02eb9-4c88-5035-b998-864054f26bb2'}, {'abstract': 'With pimples emerging well before the teenage years, and a rise in the number of preadolescent patients, doctors have put together guidelines on treatment for children as young as 7.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/younger-children-seek-an-acne-cure/', 'snippet': 'With pimples emerging well before the teenage years, and a rise in the number of preadolescent patients, doctors have put together guidelines on treatment for children as young as 7.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If your 10-year-old has acne, rest assured he or she is not alone. According to treatment guidelines published this month in the journal Pediatrics, acne is common in children ages 7 to 12.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21ACNE/21ACNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21ACNE/21ACNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21ACNE/