tname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f31d9b04-f758-5dd0-a5c3-e8aaf804aebc', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f31d9b04-f758-5dd0-a5c3-e8aaf804aebc'}, {'abstract': 'There are so many meant-to-shock moments in Tommy Smith’s “White Hot” that tedium soon replaces repulsion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/theater/reviews/white-hot-by-tommy-smith-at-the-flea-theater.html', 'snippet': 'There are so many meant-to-shock moments in Tommy Smith’s “White Hot” that tedium soon replaces repulsion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are so many meant-to-shock moments in “White Hot” — a pregnant woman punching herself in the face, repeatedly, and a description of agonizing, bloody sex are just two — that tedium soon replaces repulsion. That’s probably what the playwright, Tommy Smith, was after. But some of that energy would certainly have been better used to create an absorbing scene or the semblance of a plot. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/whitehot/whitehot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/whitehot/whitehot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/whitehot/whitehot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/whitehot/whitehot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran