com/2013/05/21/science/kepler-telescopes-troubles-a-maya-pyramid-in-ruins-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Recent developments in health and science news. This week: A Maya pyramid in Belize ruined by a construction crew, and evidence of scientific consensus on climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kepler Space Telescope is 40 million miles from Earth, which makes sending a repairman difficult. Unlike the Hubble telescope, which was designed to be serviced by astronauts, Kepler was meant to live far from Earth, well beyond a wrench’s reach. And its Pauline-like peril and uncertain future lent some drama to this week’s scientific doings. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/science/21WEEK1/21WEEK1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kepler Telescope’s Troubles, a Maya Pyramid in Ruins and More', 'kicker': 'The Week', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kepler Space Telescope', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kingson, Jennifer A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Measles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belize', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer A. Kingson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Kingson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Summary', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6615bd5-8110-5396-a400-7e3953e5f4cb', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6615bd5-8110-5396-a400-7e3953e5f4cb'}, {'abstract': 'Former Secretary of State Colin Powell is expected to attend a ceremony welcoming the Reserve Officer Training Corps back to the City University of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/r-o-t-c-returns-to-new-yorks-city-college-more-than-four-decades-after-removal/', 'snippet': 'Former Secretary of State Colin Powell is expected to attend a ceremony welcoming the Reserve Officer Training Corps back to the City University of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I attended City College a few years ago and spoke with college officials about bringing back the Reserve Officer Training Corps, or R.O.T.C., they dismissed the idea as impossible. The wounds from those wild days during the Vietnam War were still too raw. But in an afternoon ceremony on Tuesday that Colin Powell — the former secretary of state and retired four-star general who happens to be a City College graduate — is expected to attend, Army R.O.T.C. will be welcomed back to the City University of New York, with its headquarters at City College. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'R.O.T.C. Returns to New York’s City College More Than Four Decades After Removal', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Colin L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City College of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Don Gomez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Don', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gomez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]