e rigors of a rocket launching and then spin for a long time to keep a spacecraft properly oriented — in Kepler’s case, to keep its telescope precisely pointed at the same field of stars — is difficult.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flywheel', 'kicker': 'After The Fact', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flywheel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kepler Space Telescope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c75d941e-f5a3-5cb6-8860-ca278ea30ad2', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c75d941e-f5a3-5cb6-8860-ca278ea30ad2'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports, including the final of the Swiss Cup, the World Table Tennis Championships and major league baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/20/sports/20130520photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports, including the final of the Swiss Cup, the World Table Tennis Championships and major league baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports, including the final of the Swiss Cup, the World Table Tennis Championships and major league baseball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/sports/20130520photoreplay-sli