ial': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/93223235-c60e-52a4-a1cd-6adad73c2f8e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/93223235-c60e-52a4-a1cd-6adad73c2f8e'}, {'abstract': 'The remaining dancers of the Metropolitan Opera Ballet have accepted buyout packages and left the company, which dates back to the opera’s founding in 1883.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/dance/metropolitan-opera-disbands-its-ballet-corps.html', 'snippet': 'The remaining dancers of the Metropolitan Opera Ballet have accepted buyout packages and left the company, which dates back to the opera’s founding in 1883.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera has decided to disband its resident ballet company, whose roots date back to the opera’s founding in 1883. The 8 remaining dancers of the Metropolitan Opera Ballet, down from 16 in 2011, have accepted buyout packages and left the company, their union confirmed on Monday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/MET/MET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Opera Dismantles Its Ballet in Buyouts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Opera Dismantles Its Ballet In Buyouts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kozinn, Allan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/842d9b70-e9d9-5b83-9876-47d9020b71a2', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/842d9b70-e9d9-5b83-9876-47d9020b71a2'}, {'abstract': 'Mathematicians have long believed that there are an infinite number of twin primes. A new paper gets closer to an answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/science/solving-a-riddle-of-primes.html', 'snippet': 'Mathematicians have long believed that there are an infinite number of twin primes. A new paper gets closer to an answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three and five are prime numbers — that is, they are divisible only by 1 and by themselves. So are 5 and 7. And 11 and 13. And for each of these pairs of prime numbers, the difference is 2.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Solving a Riddle of Primes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Solving A Riddle Of Primes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T21:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a52d5a66-1ec3-5dde-ae2e-df8ca8dcd1fb', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a52d5a66-1ec3-5dde-ae2e-df8ca8dcd1fb'}, {'abstract': 'The National, Mike Pride and Hush Point have new albums out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/music/the-national-mike-pride-and-hush-point-release-albums.html', 'snippet': 'The National, Mike Pride and Hush Point have new albums out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serenity isn’t all that serene for the National on the band’s sixth album, “Trouble Will Find Me” (4AD). It’s the plushest, most burnished album from a New York City band that has increasingly leaned toward the measured and stately. This time, the National utterly refuses to buttonhole listeners; the music calmly awaits attention, but amply repays it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/jpnewmusic4-1369075982798/jpnewmusic4-1369075982798-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/jpnewmusic4-1369075982798/jpnewmusic4-1369075982798-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}