ano to Adam Guettel’s “Migratory V,” a song from her new album, “Go Back Home.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/in-performance-at-home-with-audra-mcdonald/', 'snippet': 'The singer accompanies herself on piano to Adam Guettel’s “Migratory V,” a song from her new album, “Go Back Home.”', 'lead_paragraph': '5:59 p.m. | Updated  It’s a busy month for Audra McDonald. On May 9 she performed at Avery Fisher Hall for Lincoln Center’s spring gala. On Tuesday her first solo album in seven years — “Go Back Home,” with songs by John Kander and Fred Ebb, Stephen Sondheim, Adam Gwon and other composers — is being released. On Friday she hosts “Audra McDonald in Concert: Go Back Home,” a broadcast of her Avery Fisher performance, for “Live From Lincoln Center.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: At Home With Audra McDonald', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guettel, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Audra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb3c0e0-8df1-52ec-8b5b-69f41030a747', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb3c0e0-8df1-52ec-8b5b-69f41030a747'}, {'abstract': "The Web site of Real Bronx Tours no longer refers to “a ride through a real New York City ‘GHETTO'” after a newspaper publicized the feature, but fallout has continued.", 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/20/tour-company-drops-pitch-for-visitors-to-see-a-real-ghetto/', 'snippet': "The Web site of Real Bronx Tours no longer refers to “a ride through a real New York City ‘GHETTO'” after a newspaper publicized the feature, but fallout has continued.", 'lead_paragraph': 'A company called Real Bronx Tours is no longer offering adventurous visitors to New York “a ride through a real New York City ‘GHETTO’” – at least on its Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bronx Tour Company Drops Pitch to See a Real Ghetto', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Ruben Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T22:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ce0cbb-4181-5e00-b1f7-6259aab33dbd', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ce0cbb-4181-5e00-b1f7-6259aab33dbd'}, {'abstract': 'Rennie Harris RHAW presents nine dance works that blend hip-hop styles with salsa, tap and other forms at the New Victory Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/dance/rennie-harris-rhaw-at-the-new-victory-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Rennie Harris RHAW presents nine dance works that blend hip-hop styles with salsa, tap and other forms at the New Victory Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They could almost be dancing for one another, these kids, on the street, in a club. Except that their circle is open at the front and they face outward, performing for spectators. Each gets a turn in the middle, and at first what they do isn’t that impressive. But it builds, and soon enough the dancers are balancing on their heads with legs like angular sculptures, swinging their arms like nunchucks, creating strobe-light effects without strobe lights — inspiring awe.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Powerful, It Stands in for Sound and Light', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Powerful, It Stands In For Sound And Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Rennie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-20T22:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17bafe04-dd50-5024-a4c4-66691bdf4034', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17bafe04-dd50-5024-a4c4-66691bdf4034'}, {'abstract': 'Carol Margolis considers herself an experienced traveler, but even she was not prepared for what happened on a recent trip from Norway to Colorado.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/business/seeking-serenity-on-business-trip-gone-awry.html', 'snippet': 'Carol Margolis considers herself an experienced traveler, but even she was not prepared for what happened on a recent trip from Norway to Colorado.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I HAVE really good travel karma,” Carol Margolis said. “Well, almost all the time.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times'