that he has resigned from the Assembly after accusations that he sexually harassed young women on his staff, Mr. Lopez is threatening to run for City Council. New Yorkers deserve better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vito Lopez, formally accused last week of groping and abusing young women on his staff, resigned from his Assembly seat early Monday morning. That is a relief. But Mr. Lopez is still threatening to run for City Council in Brooklyn and has raised almost $40,000 in contributions to begin a campaign. Brooklyn’s residents and the city’s taxpayers deserve far better and should demand his immediate withdrawal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Public Office for Vito Lopez', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Public Office for Vito Lopez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, City Councils', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T01:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/79714793-48c4-548c-967f-e529df3cb7d5', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79714793-48c4-548c-967f-e529df3cb7d5'}, {'abstract': 'New services are moving beyond the Facebook approach, with tools to create new content instead of just sharing it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/technology/social-media-is-moving-into-creativity-like-tumblr.html', 'snippet': 'New services are moving beyond the Facebook approach, with tools to create new content instead of just sharing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yahoo’s $1.1 billion proposed acquisition of Tumblr is a huge coup for the young founder of the even younger start-up and a splashy move by Marissa Mayer to shake up her company.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Flashy Bet for Yahoo on a Shift in Social Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flashy Bet for Yahoo On a Shift in Social Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Marissa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T01:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58f3d2ae-bb0d-5847-8dac-8cc52b010f61', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58f3d2ae-bb0d-5847-8dac-8cc52b010f61'}, {'abstract': 'David Karp, 26, whose mother responded to his high school boredom with a suggestion that he try home-schooling, played a role in several start-ups before founding Tumblr.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/technology/david-karp-quit-school-to-get-serious-about-start-ups.html', 'snippet': 'David Karp, 26, whose mother responded to his high school boredom with a suggestion that he try home-schooling, played a role in several start-ups before founding Tumblr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Karp was 14, he was clearly a bright teenager. Quiet, somewhat reclusive, bored with his classes at the Bronx High School of Science. He spent most of his free time in his bedroom, glued to his computer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1300, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/business/Karp/Karp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Tumblr, Founder Made Mom Proud. He Quit School.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before Tumblr, Founder Made Mom Proud. He Quit School.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T01:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham and Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b63f2d1-4643-5cc3-8d9b-1e08cc736cdd', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b63f2d1-4643-5cc3-8d9b-1e08cc736cdd'}, {'abstract': 'Doubts are growing about whether a promised peace conference will even come off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/opinion/why-is-russia-still-arming-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Doubts are growing about whether a promised peace conference will even come off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The slim hope generated two weeks ago when the United States and Russia announced plans for an international conference aimed at ending Syria’s increasingly virulent civil war is fast fading — and Russia is a big reason. Instead of using its leverage as Syria’s enabler and defender to move President Bashar al-Assad toward a negotiated solution, Russia recently sent him advanced antiship cruise missiles, and there is fresh talk now of advanced A-300 air defense weapons. The Russians have also augmented their naval presence in the region.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is Russia Still Arming Syria?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Is Russia Still Arming Syria?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T01:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddad87b2-cd26-5624-8bb4-2a44dab2dc9e', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddad87b2-cd26-5624-8bb4-2a44dab2dc9e'}, {'abstract': 'Cincinnati center fielder Shin-Soo Choo, who is expected to be one of the top free agents on the market this winter, might make a great addition for the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/sports/baseball/reds-shin-soo-choo-could-be-good-addition-for-mets.html', 'snippet': 'Cincinnati center fielder Shin-Soo Choo, who is expected to be one of the top free agents on the market this winter, might make a great addition for the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets spent much of last winter insisting, in the words of General Manager Sandy Alderson, that they were not punting on the 2013 season. He had to say it, because admitting the obvious would have been demoralizing for fans and players. But actions told the truth.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/sports/KEPNER-1/KEPNER-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Mets Can Start Rebuilding ', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Mets Can Start Rebuilding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Choo, Shin-Soo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Reds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T01:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4442a0-2f20-5fde-973e-004243398a08', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4442a0-2f20-5fde-973e-004243398a08'}, {'abstract': 'The bipartisan group of eight senators who drafted an immigration overhaul see Senator Orrin G. Hatch of Utah as a potentially influential partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/us/politics/senator-hatch-emerges-as-key-player-on-immigration-reform.html', 'snippet': 'The bipartisan group of eight senators who drafted an immigration overhaul see Senator Orrin G. Hatch of Utah as a potentially influential partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As proponents of a new immigration overhaul cast about for a Republican ally to help give their bill an extra boost, they have focused on a 79-year-old lawmaker with new hipster glasses (from Costco), black Nike sneakers (for his bad arches) and, perhaps most important, a deep and complicated relationship with immigration policy: Senator Orrin G. Hatch of Utah.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'