013-05-21T04:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/995eac52-ba13-51ba-8767-95f18af9c18b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/995eac52-ba13-51ba-8767-95f18af9c18b'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters of antigay violence held a march in Greenwich Village that ended at the site where Mark Carson was fatally shot.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/killing-of-gay-man-spurs-rally/', 'snippet': 'Protesters of antigay violence held a march in Greenwich Village that ended at the site where Mark Carson was fatally shot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protesters of antigay violence held a march in Greenwich Village on Monday that ended at the site where Mark Carson, 32, was fatally shot early Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Killing of Gay Man Spurs Rally', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, Mark (d 2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morales, Elliot (May 18, 2013 Murder)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T04:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maira Garcia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maira', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garcia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c9cae0-4d39-5ee5-a82f-86ef9500a5b4', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c9cae0-4d39-5ee5-a82f-86ef9500a5b4'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (HBO) MOONRISE KINGDOM (2012) In this storybook tale from Wes Anderson, the 12-year-old Suzy (Kara Hayward) and her soul mate, Sam (Jared Gilman), fall in love and run off, while still on an island, sending the adults in charge — Suzy’s parents (the Bishops, played by Bill Murray and Frances McDormand); Scout Master Ward (Edward Norton, above center); and Captain Sharp (Bruce Willis) — into a panic as a violent storm approaches. “Written by Mr. Anderson and Roman Coppola (they worked together several times before), ‘Moonrise Kingdom’ breezes along with a beautifully coordinated admixture of droll humor, deadpan and slapstick,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. But, she added, as in all of Mr. Anderson’s films, “there’s a deep, pervasive melancholia here too, a sense of regret evident in Mr. Bishop’s slouch (with his plaid pants, he is a walking John Cheever tragedy) and in the way Captain Sharp and Mrs. Bishop look, and don’t look, at each other. Adulthood can seem so desperately painful, so maybe Sam and Suzy shouldn’t be quite as eager to grow up.” Still, Ms. Dargis said: “Sam and Suzy, while their story has the charms of a fairy tale and some of its terrors, aren’t playing at love. They are in love, and that is the most real thing in the world.” Mr. Anderson and Mr. Coppola earned an Oscar nomination for best original screenplay.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf82868-f0eb-5c5a-a78a-e723216c4e9b', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf82868-f0eb-5c5a-a78a-e723216c4e9b'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/news-quiz-may-21-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | May 21, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T05:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1472743-bbef-5656-82a3-1d9574757794', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1472743-bbef-5656-82a3-1d9574757794'}, {'abstract': 'Concern among international students and their parents about safety on American campuses long predates the Boston Marathon bombings.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/does-u-s-violen