theater critic for The Village Voice, kept drawing applause that rivaled the Obie winners and presenters (including Ms. Streep).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obies Ceremony Celebrates Departing Village Voice Theater Critic', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cannavale, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feingold, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lois', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Voice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T14:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f83e2e6-e5f6-548f-9a04-d6bcd98714dc', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f83e2e6-e5f6-548f-9a04-d6bcd98714dc'}, {'abstract': 'Carol Burnett, who starred for 11 years on her CBS variety series “The Carol Burnett Show,” will receive the Kennedy Center’s Mark Twain Prize for American Humor, an award that has previously gone to Ellen DeGeneres, Will Ferrell and Tina Fey.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/carol-burnett-to-receive-mark-twain-prize-for-humor/', 'snippet': 'Carol Burnett, who starred for 11 years on her CBS variety series “The Carol Burnett Show,” will receive the Kennedy Center’s Mark Twain Prize for American Humor, an award that has previously gone to Ellen DeGeneres, Will Ferrell and Tina Fey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carol Burnett, it’s time to pull your best dress from the closet (and preferably not one that has been made from the curtains of your stately mansion) because you’ll be needing it at a celebratory gala. On Tuesday the John F. Kennedy Center said that Ms. Burnett, the actress and star of “The Carol Burnett Show,” had been named the winner of the Mark Twain Prize for American Humor, its annual award for “people who have had an impact on American society in ways similar” to the prize’s namesake. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/burnett/burnett-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 156, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/burnett/burnett-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 156, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/burnett/burnett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/arts/burnett/burnett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carol Burnett to Receive Mark Twain Prize for Humor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Carol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'm