f-b160-ca9eaf8e5a23'}, {'abstract': 'If the voice in your head wants something different, why not a dry riesling or pinot blanc from Alsace?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/the-richness-of-soft-shell-crabs-calls-for-chardonnay/', 'snippet': 'If the voice in your head wants something different, why not a dry riesling or pinot blanc from Alsace?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to be analytical when you’re salivating with anticipation. Luckily, these soft-shell crabs don’t require much thinking. The richness of the crab, combined with the butter, lemon and the nuts (mmmm), screams out for chardonnay, the kind with body, richness, lively acidity and minimal oak. More and more California chardonnays from Santa Barbara and the Sonoma Coast are expressing this sort of energy. A Meursault or a good premier cru Chablis would be lovely.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Richness of Soft-Shell Crabs Calls for Chardonnay', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And To Drink...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chardonnay (Wine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T15:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20eabc96-24a0-57f2-8e5e-d0a2127a74a0', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20eabc96-24a0-57f2-8e5e-d0a2127a74a0'}, {'abstract': 'The story of Anna Dickinson, a pro-war Quaker turned master of the political stump speech.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/the-civil-wars-oratorical-wunderkind/', 'snippet': 'The story of Anna Dickinson, a pro-war Quaker turned master of the political stump speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in 1863, faced with a series of state elections that threatened to undermine support for the war, Republican party leaders unleashed an unexpected political weapon: a 20-year-old Quaker named Anna Dickinson. For eight weeks, Dickinson barnstormed across New England, speaking nearly every night on behalf of Republican candidates. The young woman who couldn’t legally cast a ballot anywhere in the United States quickly proved herself adept at swaying elections. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civil War’s Oratorical Wunderkind', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T15:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lois Leveen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lois', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leveen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0807d0-1a0d-57f6-9782-22cf893c5163', 'word_count': 1521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0807d0-1a0d-57f6-9782-22cf893c5163'}, {'abstract': 'Some parents have been worried about giving their children pain relievers like ibuprofen and acetaminophen, based on reports that children who are given the drugs are more likely to develop asthma. But a new study suggests that the relationship may be little more than a statistical oversight.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/pain-relievers-do-not-cause-asthma-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'Some parents have been worried about giving their children pain relievers like ibuprofen and acetaminophen, based on reports that children who are given the drugs are more likely to develop asthma. But a new study suggests that the relationship ma...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some parents have been worried about giving their children pain relievers like ibuprofen and acetaminophen, based on reports that children who take the drugs are more likely to develop asthma. Researchers have even speculated that the rising prevalence of asthma was a result of wider use of acetaminophen, sold under the brand name Tylenol, in treating childhood fevers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/health/21well_asthma/21well_asthma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/health/21well_asthma/21well_asthma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1148}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/health/21well_asthma/21well_asthma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 536, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/health/21well_asthma/21well_asthma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1071, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/health/21well_asthma/21well_asthma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb