s that Damrosch Park is being improperly used for commercial purposes, limiting public access.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawsuit has been filed against New York City and Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts accusing them of limiting public access to Damrosch Park by using it for commercial purposes, including Fashion Week, for as many as 10 months of the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawsuit Accuses New York and Lincoln Center of Limiting Access to Damrosch Park', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T16:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44dde803-2a5b-54cb-8283-fe0de69094b1', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44dde803-2a5b-54cb-8283-fe0de69094b1'}, {'abstract': 'Glafira Rosales sold most of the disputed works through the New York gallery Knoedler & Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/arts/design/dealer-at-center-of-art-scandal-arrested-on-tax-charges.html', 'snippet': 'Glafira Rosales sold most of the disputed works through the New York gallery Knoedler & Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a case of alleged forgeries that roiled the New York art market and led to a host of civil lawsuits, federal authorities on Tuesday declared a series of works sold as Modernist masterpieces to be fake and charged a little-known Long Island dealer at the center of the scandal with tax fraud.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image