off', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ec7825-c904-55a4-bd62-2db08a46b710', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ec7825-c904-55a4-bd62-2db08a46b710'}, {'abstract': 'Questionable financial tactics are one reason for the enormous backlog of applications for a caregiving benefit, officials claim.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/v-a-warns-aging-veterans-against-pension-poachers/', 'snippet': 'Questionable financial tactics are one reason for the enormous backlog of applications for a caregiving benefit, officials claim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve applied for the Aid and Attendance benefit from Department of Veterans Affairs — which can provide as much as $2,019 monthly for a veteran and spouse for caregiving expenses — then you are all too familiar with some of the reasons for the typical 8-to-18-month delays in getting an answer from the V.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'V.A. Warns Aging Veterans Against ‘Pension Poachers’', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T16:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Seliger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seliger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}