 None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/theater/21borle/21borle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1997, 'width': 1712, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/theater/21borle/21borle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/theater/21borle/21borle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/theater/21borle/21borle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christian Borle and Shuler Hensley in New Encores! Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Encores! Great American Musicals in Concert (Series)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borle, Christian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doyle, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hensley, Shuler', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicholaw, Casey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rando, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T17:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6825215-ac96-5e42-93b7-b958841c6a8a', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6825215-ac96-5e42-93b7-b958841c6a8a'}, {'abstract': 'The Billboard Music Awards don’t have the following of the Grammys but as Sunday night’s show demonstrated, they certainly hold their own in terms of drama. And people on Twitter weighed in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/fashion/music-awards-worthy-of-a-tony.html', 'snippet': 'The Billboard Music Awards don’t have the following of the Grammys but as Sunday night’s show demonstrated, they certainly hold their own in terms of drama. And people on Twitter weighed in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Billboard Music Awards don’t have the following of the Grammys or even the American Music Awards, but as Sunday night’s show demonstrated, they certainly hold their own in terms of drama. The actual performances were easily upstaged by a seemingly well-lubricated Kid Rock complaining about lip-syncing (an obvious dig at Selena Gomez’s enthusiastically danced but suspiciously perfect rendition of “Come and Get It”); Ms. Gomez giving her on-and-off boyfriend Justin Bieber the evil eye as he collected one of his two awards, then gleefully embracing her BFF Taylor Swift when Ms. Swift beat him out for Top Artist, and then Mr. Bieber apparently near tears when he approached the stage to accept the fan-voted Milestone Award as a good portion of the room loudly booed him. The last even prompted a bewildered Tweet from a famous ex-football player.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/fashion/23HASHTAGSPAN/23HASHTAGSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/fashion/23HASHTAGSPAN/23HASHTAGSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',