PN is such a robust part of the Walt Disney Company. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ESPN, Despite Growth, Is Cutting 300 to 400 Jobs ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ESPN Cuts Up to 400 Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, James Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T19:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Andrew Miller and Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/504e72ef-bcc9-5ba3-ac3f-de3269d7ae0e', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/504e72ef-bcc9-5ba3-ac3f-de3269d7ae0e'}, {'abstract': 'Prime minister Bidzina Ivanishvili has called for prosecutions following the violence, but the case is expected to upset his relations with the church.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/world/europe/4-held-in-attack-on-georgia-gay-rights-advocates.html', 'snippet': 'Prime minister Bidzina Ivanishvili has called for prosecutions following the violence, but the case is expected to upset his relations with the church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Georgian police have arrested four men who took part in a mob attack on a gay rights demonstration in Tbilisi that injured dozens, the Georgian Interior ministry announced Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Arrested in Attack on Georgia Gay Rights Demonstration', 'kicker': 'World Brief | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivanishvili, Bidzina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T20:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/76bc99cb-3b39-55cc-ae85-3822403b36d9', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76bc99cb-3b39-55cc-ae85-3822403b36d9'}, {'abstract': 'For his latest exhibit, the fashion photographer devised a new technology that allows viewers to experience the same moment from multiple viewpoints.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/21/on-view-steven-sebrings-fourth-dimensional-perspective/', 'snippet': 'For his latest exhibit, the fashion photographer devised a new technology that allows viewers to experience the same moment from multiple viewpoints.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s dope, isn’t it?” asked Steven Sebring in his Lower Manhattan studio. He was gazing at what he calls the Rig, a 10.5-by-15-foot igloo-like silver contraption (or “geodome”) designed to capture the form and movement of the subject standing inside from every imaginable angle. Sebring, a fashion photographer and award-winning filmmaker, used the device to create “Revolution,” a three-year effort on display for three days at the 69th Regiment Armory. The multimedia exhibition pays simultaneous tribute to the 19th-century English photographer Eadweard Muybridge and to Marcel Duchamp, whose abstract classic “Nude Descending a Staircase, No. 2″ drew inspiration from Muybridge’s pioneering stop-motion imagery. The device contains 100 synchronized cameras that shoot in predetermined sequences, allowing Sebring to capture form and movement from numerous perspectives simultaneously — for example, his muse, Coco Rocha, spinning and dancing (as seen in “Discovery,” the first clip above). He can then present the results in numerous forms, including film, photographs and sculpture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steven Sebring’s Fourth-Dimensional Perspective', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duchamp, Marcel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muybridge, Eadweard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T20:08:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Podolsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Podolsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8addfa3b-dc82-5108-8c2e-dcc0cc7cfa0e', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8addfa3b-dc82-5108-8c2e-dcc0cc7cfa0e'}, {'abstract': 'Inside the West Village restaurant where the thing to 