63d345-299f-5054-ba13-2d4aa8130319'}, {'abstract': 'Everything about the young British singer Laura Mvula’s show at the Bowery Ballroom on Monday night was a group effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/arts/music/laura-mvula-at-the-bowery-ballroom.html', 'snippet': 'Everything about the young British singer Laura Mvula’s show at the Bowery Ballroom on Monday night was a group effort.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Green Garden,” the young British singer Laura Mvula’s most popular song, is a fleet track, built by adding one percussion part at a time underneath Ms. Mvula’s smooth, emphatic, optimistic vocals, which are quickly complemented by dense, intricate harmonies that sometimes come out straight, and sometimes through a digital filter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/MVULA/MVULA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/MVULA/MVULA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/MVULA/MVULA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/MVULA/MVULA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/MVULA/MVULA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dense and Organic, a Sum of Many Parts', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dense and Organic, a Sum of Many Parts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mvula, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T21:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/76e15158-4a25-5e92-b3ea-2c8fd36b4d60', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76e15158-4a25-5e92-b3ea-2c8fd36b4d60'}, {'abstract': 'The book, and any attendant publicity, would allow Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, to get her personal story in front of potential voters at a critical moment in the election cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/nyregion/promotion-of-quinn-memoir-is-called-political-spending-by-rival.html', 'snippet': 'The book, and any attendant publicity, would allow Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, to get her personal story in front of potential voters at a critical moment in the election cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker and currently the front-running candidate for mayor, signed a deal to write a memoir that would be published in the lead-up to the primary election this year, it seemed like a fairly ingenious move. The book, and any attendant publicity, would allow her to get her personal story, including the way she coped with her mother’s death when Ms. Quinn was 16 and her later struggle to come to terms with her homosexuality, in front of potential voters at a critical moment in the election cycle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rival Says Promotion of Quinn Memoir Is Political Spending', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rival Says Promotion of Quinn Memoir Is Political Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T21:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f34a8fa6-11a2-5583-970d-ac26a61ab44f', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f34a8fa6-11a2-5583-970d-ac26a61ab44f'}, {'abstract': 'The actress and singer Laura Benanti, performing cabaret at 54 Below, emerges as a vibrant free spirit able to leap from one genre to another with ease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/arts/music/laura-benanti-sings-cabaret-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'The actress and singer Laura Benanti, performing cabaret at 54 Below, emerges as a vibrant free spirit able to leap from one genre to another with ease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Funny how the substitution of a single pronoun — “I” for “you” — can transform a Broadway standard into a whimsical joke. That trick was effected by Laura Benanti on Monday evening at 54 Below, where her revised version of “On the Street Where You Live” became a comic ode to West 54th Street, where she grew up, not far from the club in which she was performing. Being a Broadway baby, even in Manhattan, she recalled, she felt estranged from her peers in matters of musical taste. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheekily Hopscotching Across Genres', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cheekily Hopscotching Across Genres', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benanti, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T21:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/282ea9cf-7ebe-5377-a4a5-fa4d70721208', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/282ea9cf-7ebe-5377-a4a5-fa4d70721208'}, {'abstract': 'Zakary Pelaccio, a partner in the various Fatty restaurants, has moved upstate to open Fish & Game; and more restaurant openings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dining/off-the-menu-zakary-pelaccio-opening-fish-game-and-more-restaurant-openings.html', 'snippet': 'Zakary Pelaccio, a partner in the various Fatty restaurants, has moved upstate to open Fish & Game; and more restaurant openings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Headliner', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/dining/22OFF1_SPAN/22OFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarg