'Latest in His Hyphenate? Manager', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Quincy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-21T21:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6daf532e-96f0-5138-99a4-c5d730f5db14', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6daf532e-96f0-5138-99a4-c5d730f5db14'}, {'abstract': 'Giorgio Moroder, who worked with Donna Summer and other acts, and made his own albums, forged a link between music’s past and its future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/arts/music/giorgio-moroder-in-red-bull-music-academy-series.html', 'snippet': 'Giorgio Moroder, who worked with Donna Summer and other acts, and made his own albums, forged a link between music’s past and its future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A packed dance floor was the appropriate greeting for the pioneering producer Giorgio Moroder, 73, on Monday night at the Brooklyn club Output. Billed as Mr. Moroder’s first live disc-jockey set, it was part of the monthlong Red Bull Music Academy series, which is drawing connections between the past and present of dance music, hip-hop, electronic music and experimental rock. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/21OUTPUT/21OUTPUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/arts/21OUTPUT/21OUTPUT-articleLarge.jpg',