'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T00:44:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a8ff7d-096b-54de-90ff-83c23b1b88e1', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a8ff7d-096b-54de-90ff-83c23b1b88e1'}, {'abstract': 'The officer, Brig. Gen. Bryan T. Roberts, was suspended from duty Tuesday and is facing allegations of misconduct that include adultery and a physical altercation, Army officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/us/south-carolina-general-faces-adultery-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'The officer, Brig. Gen. Bryan T. Roberts, was suspended from duty Tuesday and is facing allegations of misconduct that include adultery and a physical altercation, Army officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The commander of the Army’s training center at Fort Jackson, S.C., was suspended from duty Tuesday while he is investigated for adultery, Army officials announced. The officer, Brig. Gen. Bryan T. Roberts, is facing allegations of misconduct that include adultery and a physical altercation, Army officials said. They cited privacy restrictions and the requirements of the inquiry in declining to identify the woman or to describe the altercation. According to an Army biography, General Roberts was commissioned in 1983 and has served in Iraq and in Germany, at the Pentagon and in the White House Military Office. The inquiry comes as a number of senior officers have come under scrutiny for misbehavior and as the military struggles with its record on reducing sexual harassment and sexual assault. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: General Faces Adultery Investigation', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina: General Faces Adultery Investigation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Bryan T', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Jackson (SC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T00:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/456f7d4e-7908-59fa-a036-5278b842c837', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/456f7d4e-7908-59fa-a036-5278b842c837'}, {'abstract': 'Putting a stadium, concrete access, traffic jams and another set of users into Flushing Meadows-Corona Park in Queens could be Major League Soccer’s first unredeemable act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/sports/soccer/soccer-stadium-in-queens-is-no-walk-in-the-park.html', 'snippet': 'Putting a stadium, concrete access, traffic jams and another set of users into Flushing Meadows-Corona Park in Queens could be Major League Soccer’s first unredeemable act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inserting a soccer stadium into the green lungs of Quee