ontent_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona Law On Abortions Struck Down As Restrictive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T00:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adb09d58-f104-5d6a-b09e-abc376fdf190', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adb09d58-f104-5d6a-b09e-abc376fdf190'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appellate court panel struck down on Tuesday Arizona’s restrictive abortion law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/21/us/abortion-9th-circuit-opinion.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appellate court panel struck down on Tuesday Arizona’s restrictive abortion law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appellate court panel struck down on Tuesday Arizona’s restrictive abortion law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion From 9th Circuit Court of Appeals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T00:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/edf2b487-977b-5fd8-9085-5dc80354a544', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/edf2b487-977b-5fd8-9085-5dc80354a544'}, {'abstract': 'In the convoluted world of corporate tax accounting, corporate money that is technically overseas is often held in American banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/business/for-us-companies-money-offshore-means-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'In the convoluted world of corporate tax accounting, corporate money that is technically overseas is often held in American banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like some of the nation’s prominent chief executives, Apple’s Timothy D. Cook has a simple proposal to help spur the economy and encourage corporate tax compliance: give American companies a tax break to bring to the United States untaxed profits parked overseas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/business/SUB-22-JP-HOME/SUB-22-JP-HOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/business/SUB-22-JP-HOME/SUB-22-JP-HOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/business/SUB-22-JP-HOME/SUB-22-JP-HOME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/business/SUB-22-JP-HOME/SUB-22-JP-HOME-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For U.S. Companies, Money ‘Offshore’ Means Manhattan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple Hits Tax Tension Head-On: For U.S. Companies, Money ‘Offshore’ Means Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kocieniewski, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Shelters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T01:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kocieniewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kocieniewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef71c0bf-036a-5d25-a788-96cf66c28b4c', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef71c0bf-036a-5d25-a788-96cf66c28b4c'}, {'abstract': 'In China, the rich can pay a fine and have a second child. The poor face menstrual monitoring and state-mandated abortions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/opinion/chinas-brutal-one-child-policy.html', 'snippet': 'In China, the rich can pay a fine and have a second child. The poor face menstrual monitoring and state-mandated abortions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — ZHANG YIMOU, the celebrated film director and arranger of the 2008 Summer Olympics’ opening ceremony in Beijing, was accused last week of being the latest high-profile violator of China’s one-child policy. The People’s Daily, the Communist Party mouthpiece, alleged that Mr. Zhang had fathered seven children with four different women.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/opinion/0522OPED/0522OPED-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Brutal One-Child Policy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Brutal One-Child Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma Jian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T01:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ma Jian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e69488dd-8dac-50a0-86f5-98e2e2be228f', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e69488dd-8dac-50a0-86f5-98e2e2be228f'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a certain excitement to tornado season, until a storm like this touches down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/opinion/the-view-from-an-oklahoma-basement.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a certain excitement to tornado season, until a storm like this touches down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDMOND, Okla. — IT seems I am one of the few lucky people in the Oklahoma City area to have a basement. Before the tornadoes rolled through on Sunday and Monday, I spread an old rug on the basement floor, ringed it with pillows and blankets, and deposited my 5-year-old daughter in the middle wearing a helmet, shoes and socks, long pants and long sleeves and a pair of SpongeBob shades. We brought down batteries, a radio, flashlights, a kerosene lamp and matches, bottled water, bags of almonds, dried mango, potato chips, my laptop, my phone, my Kindle. And a dozen plastic dinosaurs. My daughter is really into dinosaurs. My husband spent the two days dashing up and down the stairs, unwilling to turn off the live coverage on the big screen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The View From an Oklahoma Basement', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The View From an Oklahoma Basement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basements and Cellars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T01:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Squires', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Squires', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d36be7a7-fa79-5602-a268-eeb2f1989312', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d36be7a7-fa79-5602-a268-eeb2f1989312'}, {'abstract': 'A trip to Yemen, Syria and Turkey is illuminating, but also raises many questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/opinion/friedman-tell-me-how-this-ends.html', 'snippet': 'A trip to Yemen, Syria and Turkey is illuminating, but also raises many questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANLIURFA, Turkey — \xa0I’ve been traveling to Yemen, Syria and Turkey to film a documentary on how environmental stresses contributed to the Arab awakening. As I looked back on the trip, it occurred to me that three of our main characters — the leaders of the two Yemeni villages that have been fighting over a single water well and the leader of the Free Syrian Army in Raqqa Province, whose cotton farm was wiped out by drought — have 36 children among them: 10, 10 and 16. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thom