'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T01:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e098851-27e4-5fd3-bd77-a7a1293f5658', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e098851-27e4-5fd3-bd77-a7a1293f5658'}, {'abstract': 'Closing arguments in the case helped bring to light numerous problems with the New York Police Department’s controversial program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/opinion/stop-and-frisk-on-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Closing arguments in the case helped bring to light numerous problems with the New York Police Department’s controversial program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judge Shira Scheindlin, of Federal District Court in Manhattan, got to the heart of the problem with the New York Police Department’s stop-and-frisk program on Monday, after hearing testimony for two months in the civil rights case, Floyd v. City of New York. The plaintiffs charge the department with illegally detaining hundreds of thousands of people on the streets each year not because of suspicious behavior but because of their race. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop-and-Frisk on Trial', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stop-and-Frisk on Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrano, Pedro', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T01:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b3533d3-c1e6-543e-bbb1-c1a03448aa03', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b3533d3-c1e6-543e-bbb1-c1a03448aa03'}, {'abstract': 'A Fox News reporter accused of conspiring with a leaker was just doing his job. His case is an example of how the Obama administration lacks respect for a free press.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/opinion/another-chilling-leak-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'A Fox News reporter accused of conspiring with a leaker was just doing his job. His case is an example of how the Obama administration lacks respect for a free press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the decision to label a Fox News television reporter a possible “co-conspirator” in a criminal investigation of a news leak, the Obama administration has moved beyond protecting government secrets to threatening fundamental freedoms of the press to gather news. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Chilling Leak Investigation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Chilling Leak Investigation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, James', 'rank': 3,