mbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 21, 2013', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T03:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea2f8141-0601-5a9b-9d99-ae258a059eb1', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea2f8141-0601-5a9b-9d99-ae258a059eb1'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Rohrer helped invent the scanning tunneling microscope, which made it possible to see individual atoms and move them around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/science/heinrich-rohrer-physicist-who-won-nobel-dies-at-79.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Rohrer helped invent the scanning tunneling microscope, which made it possible to see individual atoms and move them around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heinrich Rohrer, who shared the 1986 Nobel Prize in Physics for inventing a microscope that made it possible to see individual atoms and move them around, an achievement that led to vastly faster computing and greatly advanced molecular biology, died on Thursday night or early Friday morning in Wollerau, Switzerland. He was 79.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/us/ROHRER-obit/ROHRER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390,