f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6c68965-4a71-5d28-993d-e7259c59960b', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6c68965-4a71-5d28-993d-e7259c59960b'}, {'abstract': 'The annual percentage rate on a merchant-cash-advance loan can be as high as 60 or even 100 percent — enough to make most rational business people shake in their boots.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/why-alternative-lenders-should-set-some-standards/', 'snippet': 'The annual percentage rate on a merchant-cash-advance loan can be as high as 60 or even 100 percent — enough to make most rational business people shake in their boots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my loan brokerage, the phone often rings with small-business owners who want cash quickly for a wide variety of reasons. They may be in a desperate situation, or they may be so fed up with the local banks that they don’t even want to try that route. Or perhaps they’ve been told by friends how frustrating it can be to apply for a Small Business Administration loan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Alternative Lenders Should Set Some Standards', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T11:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material