nyt://video/23e177c2-a832-5545-8841-5c57cd503ec0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/23e177c2-a832-5545-8841-5c57cd503ec0'}, {'abstract': 'The Pacers’ Paul George put up a determined defense against the Knicks’ Carmelo Anthony in the playoffs. As a reward for his efforts, George was asked to defend LeBron James.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/sports/basketball/nba-playoffs-pacers-paul-george-goes-from-anthony-to-james.html', 'snippet': 'The Pacers’ Paul George put up a determined defense against the Knicks’ Carmelo Anthony in the playoffs. As a reward for his efforts, George was asked to defend LeBron James.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For six games over the last two weeks, Paul George of the Indiana Pacers had one of the tougher assignments in the N.B.A. playoffs. His job was to guard the Knicks’ Carmelo Anthony one on one, to keep the offensive damage that Anthony can inflict to a minimum, to do whatever he had to do, within the rules, to wear down one of the league’s top scorers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/sports/PACERS-floater/PACERS-floater-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Anthony to James, George’s Life Doesn’t Get Easier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Anthony to James, George&#8217;s Life Doesn&#8217;t Get Easier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T12:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/023e7a7f-c466-5853-b45b-742a39604d3c', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/023e7a7f-c466-5853-b45b-742a39604d3c'}, {'abstract': 'Bridge International Academies in Kenya offers a fast-growing model for providing affordable education to poor children on a grand scale.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/a-by-the-e-book-education-for-5-a-month/', 'snippet': 'Bridge International Academies in Kenya offers a fast-growing model for providing affordable education to poor children on a grand scale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis Abudho and his family of five children live in a one-bedroom house without electricity in Bandani, an informal settlement in Kisumu, Kenya. Abudho is active in the PTA at Bridge International Academy in Bandani, where his four oldest children (three boys and a girl) are in baby level, first, third and fifth grade. You might not expect someone like Abudho — who said he is a casual laborer, operating a bread machine at a local mill and bakery — to have four children in private school. But he can afford it — the cost of school for each child at Bridge, including books and materials, is the equivalent of $5.16 a month. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A By-the-E-Book Education, for $5 a Month', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BRAC (Bangladesh)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bridge International Academies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Omega SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ghana', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T12:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name'