cations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T12:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cbb926-4bcd-5474-bcbe-9ff6a189253f', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cbb926-4bcd-5474-bcbe-9ff6a189253f'}, {'abstract': 'Three museums gear up to celebrate the Italian provocateur Francesco Vezzoli in all his decadent glory.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/idol-worship/', 'snippet': 'Three museums gear up to celebrate the Italian provocateur Francesco Vezzoli in all his decadent glory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The satirical artist Francesco Vezzoli has always seemed more enchanted by movie stars and velvet ropes than by ivory towers. Still, curators can’t get enough of him. This month the Italian-born bon vivant embarks on an artistic tour that he is calling “The Trinity.” The event kicks off at the MAXXI national art museum in Rome, where his bedazzled portraits of pop stars like Lady Gaga will be on display alongside his needlepoints of various saints. Then, this fall, he will dismantle a deconsecrated 19th-century Italian church and rebuild it at MoMA PS1 in Queens. Vezzoli finishes up at the Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art, with a show focusing fittingly on his obsession with all things cinematic. Asked if, at 41, a global retrospective might be premature, Vezzoli says, “I see this project more like a parody of a Cher farewell tour, a silly movie launch or a Fitzcarraldo experience — something extravagant and certainly not celebratory, at least in my intentions.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Idol Worship', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vezzoli, Francesco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T13:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c37f1d-6068-5560-81c1-8de88b60fc09', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c37f1d-6068-5560-81c1-8de88b60fc09'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers voiced their opinions on Anthony D. Weiner’s candidacy for mayor, weighing in on his past and potential as a candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/22/nyregion/new-yorkers-react-to-weiner-mayor-candidacy.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers voiced their opinions on Anthony D. Weiner’s candidacy for mayor, weighing in on his past and potential as a candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Yorkers voiced their opinions on Anthony D. Weiner’s candidacy for mayor, weighing in on his past and potential as a candidate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Yorkers Respond to Weiner’s Candidacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T13:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/bd7bb32f-5ad8-5c8e-a584-be652dd36242', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/bd7bb32f-5ad8-5c8e-a584-be652dd36242'}, {'abstract': 'In Greece, the perils of a drawn-out debt crisis are imprinted on its younger population — whose unemployment numbers are soaring — who turn to selling their bodies for money and to a dangerous, cheap new street drug for escape.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/societal-ills-spike-in-crisis-stricken-greece/', 'snippet': 'In Greece, the perils of a drawn-out debt crisis are imprinted on its younger population — whose unemployment numbers are soaring — who turn to selling their bodies for money and to a dangerous, cheap new street drug for escape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — “Five euros only, just 5 euros,” whispered Maria, a young prostitute with sunken cheeks and bedraggled hair, as she pitched herself forward from the shadows of a graffiti-riddled alley in central Athens on a recent weeknight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Societal Ills Spike in Crisis-Stricken Greece', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T13:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b83476b5-0d19-5d95-9c4f-0a8ceb8478b2', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b83476b5-0d19-5d95-9c4f-0a8ceb8478b2'}, {'abstract': 'When I called my 5-month-old a chubby bunny, an acquaintance assured me she would “grow out of it.”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/not-worried-about-a-little-baby-fat/', 'snippet': 'When I called my 5-month-old a chubby bunny, an acquaintance assured me she would “grow out of it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was showing my favorite photograph of the baby to an acquaintance. She commented on the girl’s sweet thighs sticking out of her flowered onesie and her kissable cheeks, and I said, with maternal pride, “She’s such a chubby bunny.” The other woman seemed mildly horrified that I would call my daughter chubby, even in an admiring way. “Don’t worry,” she said. “She’ll grow out of it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Worried About a Little Baby Fat', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T13:34:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d394b1f2-c984-50b1-b464-7db2d5e103bb', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d394b1f2-c984-50b1-b464-7db2d5e103bb'}, {'abstract': 'Polls show State Senator Barbara Buono losing to Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey by a wide margin, but her campaign says it can shrink that gap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/nyregion/challenging-christie-barbara-buono-begins-tv-ad-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Polls show State Senator Barbara Buono losing to Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey by a wide margin, but her campaign says it can shrink that gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey has raised more than three times as much money as his challenger in his bid for re-election this year, has already run two television advertisements and, according to the latest polls, has approval ratings in the 70 percent range. He would seem well on his way to his goal of winning the election in November by a historic margin, big enough to propel him to the front of the Republican primary for president in 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing Uphill Battle, Christie Challenger Will Begin TV Ad Campaign', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Uphill Battle, Challenger to Christie Begins TV Ad Campaign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buono, Barbara', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T13:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1