ell from a loss to Pittsburgh in their playoff series.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/senators-resilience-starts-with-anderson/', 'snippet': 'Not much has come easy for Ottawa goalie Craig Anderson in his career, so his team fully expected he would bounce back well from a loss to Pittsburgh in their playoff series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — Senators goaltender Craig Anderson has had his share of ups and downs in his career, which is why Ottawa Coach Paul MacLean was confident he would bounce back despite being pulled after giving up three early goals in Game 2 of their playoff series against Pittsburgh. Anderson responded in Game 3 with 49 saves in a 2-1 double-overtime victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senators’ Resilience Starts with Anderson', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, CRAIG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacLean, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ottawa Senators', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T14:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dhiren Mahiban', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dhiren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahiban', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/798201ff-eb80-54ea-af79-ff4bfc508098', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/798201ff-eb80-54ea-af79-ff4bfc508098'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s Peter Baker on the fiscal arguments beginning to burn through Congress, touched off by President Obama’s promise to help victims in Oklahoma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim