ven the elections held on May 11 — fiercely contested, marred by violence — are being discussed in culinary metaphors. The contest in Karachi has been called a clash between the “burgers” and the “bun kebabs,” between the Westernized youth and middle-class locals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burgers and Bun Kebabs', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T14:35:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bac417a-3bad-59cb-a702-33d356073cb9', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bac417a-3bad-59cb-a702-33d356073cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Under a new deal, the network will continue what has already become a 35-year tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/business/media/cbs-to-keep-airing-tony-awards-through-2018.html', 'snippet': 'Under a new deal, the network will continue what has already become a 35-year tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBS announced Wednesday morning that it would continue what has become a 35-year tradition for the network, by agreeing to a deal with The Broadway League and the American Theater Wing that will extend its rights to broadcast the annual Tony Awards show through 2018.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '