: 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e1d3c5f-f370-5b3d-888f-be2e376ee20f', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e1d3c5f-f370-5b3d-888f-be2e376ee20f'}, {'abstract': 'Lois Lerner, the official who disclosed that the Internal Revenue Service had targeted conservative groups, denied that she had misled Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/us/politics/irs-official-denies-misleading-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Lois Lerner, the official who disclosed that the Internal Revenue Service had targeted conservative groups, denied that she had misled Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Internal Revenue Service official who first disclosed that the agency had targeted conservative groups for special scrutiny, and in doing so ignited a controversy that has ensnared the White House, denied on Wednesday that she had ever provided false information to Congress. She then invoked her Fifth Amendment right against self-incrimination and declined to testify at a House hearing on the agency’s actions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/us/23irs/23irs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/us/23irs/23irs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/us/23irs/23irs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/us/23irs/23irs-superJumb