u can make in your own kitchen, tweaked for home cooks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calliope’s Chocolate Hazelnut Ice Cream', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calliope (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T15:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c128ce00-bb13-591c-b3d3-7018aec7c4b7', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c128ce00-bb13-591c-b3d3-7018aec7c4b7'}, {'abstract': 'A lot has changed since the 4-foot-by-8-foot carts with wagon wheels debuted 40 years ago. Most notably, they contribute to an estimated $8 billion in annual mall sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/business/smallbusiness/hidden-in-plain-sight-tiny-mall-kiosks-make-a-surprisingly-big-impact.html', 'snippet': 'A lot has changed since the 4-foot-by-8-foot carts with wagon wheels debuted 40 years ago. Most notably, they contribute to an estimated $8 billion in annual mall sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Typically bound by short-term leases, displaying products made by others, and run by first-time entrepreneurs with limited capital, shopping mall carts and kiosks have long been considered an unsophisticated small-business underclass. More recently, however, these small-footprint retailers have come to be seen as possessing surprising potential. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/business/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Mall Kiosks Make a Surprisingly Big Impact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Just a ‘Temporary Leasing Space,’ Mall Kiosks Make a Big Impact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping Centers and Malls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T15:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Grossmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grossmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6198a114-27bf-5a78-8039-26b95a4a2d1e', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6198a114-27bf-5a78-8039-26b95a4a2d1e'}, {'abstract': 'A small experiment finds that family members are more comfortable with the phrase “allow a natural death.”', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/dnr-by-another-name/', 'snippet': 'A small experiment finds that family members are more comfortable with the phrase “allow a natural death.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’d like to bring you up to speed on what’s going on,” the doctor said. He had a red goatee and was wearing a white coat. He said that my father had pneumonia and needed a “breathing machine,” and that he also had sepsis and acute lung injury. “The statistics are not too good,” he said solemnly. “Around 40 percent of people who are just like him will die from this.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DNR by Another Name', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T15:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middle