standard view is that teaching imparts knowledge, either knowing how (skills) or knowing that (information).\xa0 Tests seem important because they measure the knowledge students have gained from a course.\xa0 But how well would most of us do on the tests we aced even just a few years ago?\xa0 Discuss the causes of the Thirty Years War.\xa0 Mary is 20 years old, which is twice the age Ann was when Mary was the age Ann is now: how old is Ann?\xa0 How do Shakespeare’s early comedies differ from his late romances?\xa0 Give a quick summary of Mendel’s Laws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do I Teach?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T15:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7192ab09-3bc0-5e04-929d-a7b309aaba52', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7192ab09-3bc0-5e04-929d-a7b309aaba52'}, {'abstract': 'The Leveraged Finance Fights Melanoma benefit at Rockefeller Plaza’s garden on Tuesday night attracted a star-studded Wall Street crowd that raised more than $1.2 million to help fight skin cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/wall-streets-a-list-turns-out-to-fight-skin-cancer/', 'snippet': 'The Leveraged Finance Fights Melanoma benefit at Rockefeller Plaza’s garden on Tu