obby would have seemed an outlandish place to present an opera. But opera on unusual stages has become an agreeably prominent trend, with recent productions offered at quirky spaces, like a nightclub on the Lower East Side.  ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1195, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/rodrigo/rodrigo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Emotional Crew Staying at This Hotel', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Emotional Crew Staying At This Hotel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'operamission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:40:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac46c162-fee9-5f6b-8d0d-66d5648dfba6', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac46c162-fee9-5f6b-8d0d-66d5648dfba6'}, {'abstract': 'Moments after a man was hacked to death on a street in London on Wednesday, one of two suspects in the attack approached a witness who was recording the scene on video and asked to make a statement.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/london-attack-suspect-recorded-statement-after-killing-video-shows/', 'snippet': 'Moments after a man was hacked to death on a street in London on Wednesday, one of two suspects in the attack approached a witness who was recording the scene on video and asked to make a statement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 6:27 p.m. Moments after a man was hacked to death on a street in London on Wednesday, one of two suspects in the attack, carrying a meat cleaver and a knife in his blood-drenched hands, approached a witness who was recording the scene on video and asked to make a statement. ITV News obtained the graphic, distressing video, in which the suspect described the killing of a man wearing a British military charity T-shirt as retaliation for the actions of British troops in Muslim countries. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Attack Suspect Recorded Statement After Killing, Video Shows', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c75d6fbb-ee92-53c8-8b76-652cc283b6d1', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c75d6fbb-ee92-53c8-8b76-652cc283b6d1'}, {'abstract': 'The change puts a spotlight back on Morgan Stanley’s fixed-income division, which has been shrinking since the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/morgan-stanley-shakes-up-fixed-income/', 'snippet': 'The change puts a spotlight back on Morgan Stanley’s fixed-income division, which has been shrinking since the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:45 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley’s Head of Fixed Income to Retire', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Morgan Stanley’s Head Of Fixed Income to Retire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelleher, Colm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:42:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36b0fa09-3f55-5bc6-ad47-308a9484fb94', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36b0fa09-3f55-5bc6-ad47-308a9484fb94'}, {'abstract': 'City Ballet’s Tuesday night program offered the beautiful visual design of Balanchine’s “Serenade,” followed by the bland aggression of Ulysses Dove’s “Red Angels.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/arts/dance/city-ballets-serenade-and-red-angels-at-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'City Ballet’s Tuesday night program offered the beautiful visual design of Balanchine’s “Serenade,” followed by the bland aggression of Ulysses Dove’s “Red Angels.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To see New York City Ballet perform “Serenade” is to give a gift to yourself. The first ballet George Balanchine created for American dancers, the work, which officially premiered in 1935, is set to Tchaikovsky and reveals all of the hallmarks of his choreography — fast footwork, voluminous attack within classical positions, and the fusing of music and movement in such a profound way that you can’t always distinguish between what you’re watching and what you’re hearing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/subserenade/subserenade-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/subserenade/subserenade-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/subserenade/subserenade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_na