eb_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/arts/music/noah-preminger-at-the-jazz-standard.html', 'snippet': 'Songs from the saxophonist Noah Preminger’s new album, “Haymaker,” highlighted his show in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah Preminger played a cadenza on tenor saxophone near the end of his first set at the Jazz Standard on Tuesday night, and within its tight dimensions there were traces of almost everything that makes him special. Starting out in a gallant midregister before fluttering around his foghorn depths and ethereal upper reaches, he conveyed patience and composure, along with fluency, prudence and control. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urgency and Range, but Always in Control', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Urgency And Range, But Always In Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preminger, Noah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz Standard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/06f7c681-b472-58a2-b144-17a2609eeb52', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06f7c681-b472-58a2-b144-17a2609eeb52'}, {'abstract': 'The British Library receives handwritten lyrics to “Strawberry Fields Forever,” “She Said She Said” and “In My Life.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/beatles-biographer-donates-song-manuscripts-to-british-library/', 'snippet': 'The British Library receives handwritten lyrics to “Strawberry Fields Forever,” “She Said She Said” and “In My Life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hunter Davies, the prolific British writer whose 1968 biography of the Beatles – “The Beatles: The Authorized Biography” – offered a close-up and detailed, if somewhat sanitized, portrait of the group while it was still together and at the height of its power, has donated a handful of Beatles song manuscripts and John Lennon letters to the British Library.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beatles’ Biographer Donates Song Manuscripts to British Library', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manuscripts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davies, Hunter (1936- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Library', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:45:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66a0e31f-a55f-57c5-81e6-bdadd41ecd54', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66a0e31f-a55f-57c5-81e6-bdadd41ecd54'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Bartlett, a former adviser to President George W. Bush, will succeed Leslie Dach, a former Clinton White House staff member, as executive vice president for corporate affairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/business/wal-mart-hires-a-new-chief-image-maker.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Bartlett, a former adviser to President George W. Bush, will succeed Leslie Dach, a former Clinton White House staff member, as executive vice president for corporate affairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To continue burnishing its image, Wal-Mart has replaced a former Clinton White House aide with a former Bush White House staff member.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wal-Mart Hires Former Bush Aide as Chief Image Maker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wal-Mart Hires Former Bush Aide as Chief Image Maker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartlett, Dan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dach, Leslie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T20:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/727e6563-1b08-53e9-808f-c32f3266a061', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727e6563-1b08-53e9-808f-c32f3266a061'}, {'abstract': 'In the new NBC comedy “Save Me,” a suburban housewife has a near-death experience and gains the power to receive direct input from God and the power to know people’s secrets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/arts/television/save-me-nbcs-new-comedy-stars-anne-heche.html', 'snippet': 'In the new NBC comedy “Save Me,” a suburban housewife has a near-death experience and gains the power to receive direct input from God and the power to know people’s secrets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is floundering NBC crying out to a higher power with the titles of its new shows? A recently announced drama is to be called “Believe.” And on Thursday night, introduced with back-to-back episodes, comes the comedy “Save Me.” “Save Me” will not, in all probability, save NBC. It might not even be around long enough to develop a consistent tone or viewpoint, both of which are lacking in the pilot. But it has a pretty good actress, Anne Heche (“Hung”), at the head of the cast, and it at least tries to add a touch of levity to what has always been a ponderously serious genre.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/saveme/saveme-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/saveme/saveme-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/saveme/saveme-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/arts/saveme/saveme-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 20