Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a77ccbc-d906-5138-98f5-21e66aa000f3', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a77ccbc-d906-5138-98f5-21e66aa000f3'}, {'abstract': 'A show featuring the work of Koloman Moser opens Thursday at the Neue Galerie in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/garden/koloman-moser-designing-modern-vienna-1897-1907-opens-at-the-neue-galerie.html', 'snippet': 'A show featuring the work of Koloman Moser opens Thursday at the Neue Galerie in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Koloman Moser: Designing Modern Vienna 1897-1907,” which opens Thursday at the Neue Galerie in New York, is the first American museum retrospective devoted to the artist and designer, who was a founding member of the Vienna Secession and, later, the Wiener Werkstätte. Moser was trained as a painter but went on to design wardrobes, cigar cabinets and chandeliers for wealthy Austrians. His pieces incorporated patterns that reveal “an exciting ambiguous solution,” said Christian Witt-Dörring, the curator of decorative arts at the museum who organized the show. “You look at a gold and silver stenciled wall,” he said, “and the pattern is curvilinear, but also square.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 863}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1783, 'width': 1239, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_SHOWS/23CURR4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Designer Who Redid Vienna', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Designer Who Redid Vienna', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neue Galerie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moser, Koloman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T22:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f75af6e-aadf-5e96-85fc-0ab80a1946c4', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f75af6e-aadf-5e96-85fc-0ab80a1946c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Shabby Chic Dollhouse recreates a Victorian-style cottage in the Catskills that lacks heat and running water but was dripping with charm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/garden/the-shabby-chic-dollhouse-recreates-a-victorian-style-cottage-in-the-catskills.html', 'snippet': 'The Shabby Chic Dollhouse recreates a Victorian-style cottage in the Catskills that lacks heat and running water but was dripping with charm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June 2010, this section wrote about a Victorian-style cottage in the Catskills that served as a retreat and a creative canvas for its owner, Sandra Foster. The tiny pink-and-white house lacked heat and running water but was dripping with charm. And when Caroline Dupuis, a dollhouse builder in McKinney, Tex., was sent a link to the article by a friend, she was moved to recreate the cottage in miniature.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_GOODSSPAN/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_GOODSSPAN/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_GOODSSPAN/23CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_GOODSSPAN/23CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1227, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption