', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Our home has a precarious staircase with no handrail. Is it worth the trouble to add one before trying to sell?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Ready', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Ready', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T22:37:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6973349-cf9f-5382-b45d-ac878489ed89', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6973349-cf9f-5382-b45d-ac878489ed89'}, {'abstract': 'Doris Leslie Blau, the New York-based vintage rug company, will have a new home on the sixth floor of ABC Carpet & Home in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/garden/doris-leslie-blau-opens-at-abc-carpet-home.html', 'snippet': 'Doris Leslie Blau, the New York-based vintage rug company, will have a new home on the sixth floor of ABC Carpet & Home in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 4, the vintage rug company founded in 1965 as Doris Leslie Blau, and now known as DLB, will have a new home in a 1,600-square-foot shop on the sixth floor of ABC Carpet & Home in Manhattan. Formerly sold only to the trade, the rugs will now be within easy grasp of downtown designers and consumers. The first collection will include about 40 vintage and reproduction Swedish rugs from the 1930s to the 1950s, a genre that was a veritable secret to the trade when Nader Bolour, a third-generation antique rug dealer who is DLB’s owner and president, began buying examples three years ago. Now they are bringing up to $50,000 at auction. And what does Mr. Bolour’s crystal ball reveal about the next hot carpet? “Antique silk,” he pronounced.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/garden/23CURR_OPENSPAN/23CURR7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DLB Comes to ABC', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DLB Comes to ABC', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC Carpet & Home', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DLB Doris Leslie Blau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T22:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a58b15dd-4f62-5eb2-ab74-8d53962de56d', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a58b15dd-4f62-5eb2-ab74-8d53962de56d'}, {'abstract': 'Honestly, mostly.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/the-joy-of-term-papers/', 'snippet': 'Honestly, mostly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No, really (and mostly) — they’re the source of limited posting recently. While I wouldn’t mind having a bit, um, fewer papers to read, it’s a real joy when you get papers from young people that provide fresh thinking and tell you things you really didn’t know. And I had a bunch of those this semester.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joy of Term Papers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-22T22:40:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be386dc4-c3d2