-a-knack-for-picking-winners/', 'snippet': 'If you are a betting person, you might want to keep an eye out for Uniqlo’s now familiar red square logo appearing on athletes in the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The week before Adam Scott won the Masters in April, Uniqlo announced that it had signed the golfer to a multiyear endorsement contract. A year earlier, Novak Djokovic also became a brand ambassador for Uniqlo and reclaimed his spot as the world’s No. 1 men’s tennis player. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Endorsements, Uniqlo Has a Knack for Picking Winners', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Luck Logo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nishikori, Kei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Adam (1980- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uniqlo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T03:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79afb67d-3ca1-5f79-9f64-34fd8e08e87b', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79afb67d-3ca1-5f79-9f64-34fd8e08e87b'}, {'abstract': 'The ordeal of Pedro Portugal, 52, a businessman, ended when officers posing as building inspectors raided a warehouse where he was kept for 32 days, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/nyregion/suspects-are-arrested-in-kidnapping-and-torture-of-queens-man.html', 'snippet': 'The ordeal of Pedro Portugal, 52, a businessman, ended when officers posing as building inspectors raided a warehouse where he was kept for 32 days, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pedro Portugal was walking to his car in Queens last month when he was grabbed by a group of men, bundled into a sport utility vehicle and taken to a warehouse nearby. There, the authorities said, masked men burned him with acid, threatened to cut off fingers and knocked out several teeth — all in an effort to get $3 million in ransom. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Man Is Rescued After Being Held for Ransom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queens Man Is Rescued After Being Held for Ransom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moncayo, Eduardo', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acuna, Christian', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portugal, Pedro', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T03:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4588c699-b4de-588d-a829-3e1b4aa923da', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4588c699-b4de-588d-a829-3e1b4aa923da'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, May 23, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-thursday-may-23-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, May 23, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I know this country better than my own country, and I still feel like an outsider. That’s the thing that bothers me.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, May 23, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T03:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f03dfa5-eef0-5d00-8b58-d1da4dc49308', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f03dfa5-eef0-5d00-8b58-d1da4dc49308'}, {'abstract': 'Club América and Cruz Azul face off in a two-game series for the Mexican league Clausura title in an all-capital city series beginning on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/22/in-mexico-finals-are-a-capital-affair/', 'snippet': 'Club América and Cruz Azul face off in a two-game series for the Mexican league Clausura title in an all-capital city series beginning on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The finals of this season’s Mexican Clausura provide a rare but appetizing matchup, with an all-capital city series, the first since 2002. It will be the third meeting between Cruz Azul and Club América for the title. The last champions, Xolos of Tijuana, did not make the playoffs (but are facing Brazilian powerhouse Atlético Mineiro in the Copa Libertadores quarterfinals).', 'sou