5bc3-5f5c-ae0f-3f9dbca3e40c', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c874590-5bc3-5f5c-ae0f-3f9dbca3e40c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (AMC) SHOWVILLE This new competition series touches down each week in a small American town and puts together a talent show in four days. On Day 1, the actor and director Alec Mapa and the choreographer Lisette Bustamante hold open auditions and select four acts. On Days 2 and 3, they prepare the finalists for the show as they juggle jobs, home lives and nerves. And on Day 4, the contestants perform before their friends, families and neighbors, who will determine the winner of $10,000 and a loving cup signifying the town’s favorite act. First stop: Holland, Mich., where Randy and Darlene Schaap, above, were among the contestants.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/31ea6288-29b5-5997-9d5e-6a9d777149d4', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31ea6288-29b5-5997-9d5e-6a9d777149d4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Marsh was a longtime chief executive of the beverage company, now part of the Dr Pepper Snapple Group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/business/leonard-marsh-80-dies-a-founder-of-snapple.html', 's