 clubs will play a host of league fixtures without their star players, who’ll be away on international duty. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Time May Be Running Out for Brazil’s State Championships', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T11:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Young', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Young', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff4cda1-c988-5259-87ef-4001dcb9fd64', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff4cda1-c988-5259-87ef-4001dcb9fd64'}, {'abstract': 'Most important, when giving feedback: be direct.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/how-we-train-employees-to-analyze-the-business/', 'snippet': 'Most important, when giving feedback: be direct.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Be direct.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Train Employees to Analyze the Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Loyalty Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T11:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burkhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burkhart', 'qualif