8) was an Austrian artist and designer — of everything from interiors and exhibitions to textiles and glass — and a co-founder (with Josef Hoffman and Fritz Waerndorfer) of the influential, secessionist production cooperative Wiener Werkstätte. Often overshadowed by Hoffmann, Moser is finally getting his first American museum exhibition: “Koloman Moser: Designing Modern Vienna 1897-1907,” which opens today at the Neue Galerie New York and runs through Sept. 2. The show, which was organized in collaboration with the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston (where it will be on view later this year), presents more than 200 examples of Moser’s prodigious output in an installation designed by the Chicago architect John Vinci to evoke the notion of the Gesamtkunstwerk, or total work of art, an ideal of the Vienna Secession. For those who can’t resist the temptation to take home a souvenir, the Neue Galerie’s shop is selling objects like the tea service shown here (priced à la carte from $50 to $225), a reproduction of a 1901-2 design by Moser, with circle-pattern decoration by Jutta Sika, one of his students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Koloman Moser’s Viennese Vision', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neue Galerie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vienna (Austria)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T13:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5307e2b6-bb0e-5bbd-abd2-d51294cda40a', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5307e2b6-bb0e-5bbd-abd2-d51294cda40a'}, {'abstract': 'When the man who invented the GIF, the widely used Web graphic, said that people were pronouncing the term wrong, it started an unexpected debate.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/battle-over-gif-pronunciation-erupts/', 'snippet': 'When the man who invented the GIF, the widely used Web graphic, said that people were pronouncing the term wrong, it started an unexpected debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been called “The Great Schism of the 21st Century” and “The Most Absurd Religious War in Geek History.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/22/technology/22gif/22gif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, '