undation report shows a sharp increase in enrollment of lower-income, nonwhite students at community colleges, institutions that will do much to shape the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Students at community colleges increasingly come from low-income families, as I mention in an article for Thursday’s newspaper about a new report. The trends, in their simplest terms:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Changing Face of Community Colleges', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Community Colleges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Century Foundation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T14:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da5aabf-ef64-5e8c-a665-ebc072adcadf', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da5aabf-ef64-5e8c-a665-ebc072adcadf'}, {'abstract': 'An online conversation with a young energy activist turned solar entrepreneur.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/dot-chat-from-energy-campaigner-to-solar-finance-entrepreneur/', 'snippet': 'An online conversation with a young energy activist turned solar entrepreneur.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:15 p.m. | Updated |I spent 45 minutes earlier today in an invigorating online discussion of new models for financing small solar-energy installations. The participants were Billy Parish, who at 31 is a founder of Mosaic, a company through which small investors can earn interest financing the installation of solar panels, and Andreas Karelas, the executive director, of RE-volv, a nonprofit revolving fund also financing solar projects. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dot Chat: From Energy Campaigners to Solar Finance Entrepreneurs', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bornstein, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google+', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T14:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36da74a9-be85-5883-89b2-53a3049678f4', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36da74a9-be85-5883-89b2-53a3049678f4'}, {'abstract': 'The city added more people since 2011 than all the other cities in the metropolitan area combined, according to a new analysis of census results.', 'web_url': 