day night, and Brad Richards will not be in the lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/rangers-bench-brad-richards-for-game-4/', 'snippet': 'The Rangers, down by 3-0 to the Boston Bruins, face elimination at Madison Square Garden on Thursday night, and Brad Richards will not be in the lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad Richards will not be in the lineup Thursday night when the Rangers play an elimination game against the Boston Bruins in their N.H.L. Eastern Conference semifinals series at Madison Square Garden. The Bruins lead the series, three games to none.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 560}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 955, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1910, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/hockey/24richards/24richards-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers Bench Brad Richards for Game 4', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamrlik, Roman', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stralman, Anton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:08:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naila-Jean Meyers and Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naila-jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8b16240-24c5-554f-8e63-8983cf493a61', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8b16240-24c5-554f-8e63-8983cf493a61'}, {'abstract': '“Before Midnight” follows the continuing romance of characters played by Julie Delpy and Ethan Hawke in the third film in a series directed by Richard Linklater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/movies/before-midnight-with-julie-delpy-and-ethan-hawke.html', 'snippet': '“Before Midnight” follows the continuing romance of characters played by Julie Delpy and Ethan Hawke in the third film in a series directed by Richard Linklater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where did the time go? Has it really been nine years since we last saw Celine and Jesse, in Paris, rekindling the romance that first sparked nine years before that, in Vienna? Luckily (for us and for them) they are still together, having hatched a pair of sweet blond twin girls and glided, or maybe stumbled, into their 40s. And, of course, because they are played by Julie Delpy and Ethan Hawke, Celine and Jesse are still better looking than most of the rest of us, and still have quite a lot to say about themselves, each other and the world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Years Later, Once More', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Years Later, Once More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delpy, Julie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawke, Ethan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linklater, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Before Midnight (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d65b715c-75be-503d-a5fc-ea54e83bbf3a', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d65b715c-75be-503d-a5fc-ea54e83bbf3a'}, {'abstract': 'The Spurs’ defense isn’t always remarkable, but it has been good enough to stop Zach Randolph and the Grizzlies.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/for-randolph-the-challenge-is-offense/', 'snippet': 'The Spurs’ defense isn’t always remarkable, but it has been good enough to stop Zach Randolph and the Grizzlies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The overtime period of San Antonio’s 93-89 win over the Memphis Grizzlies in Game 2 of the Western Conference finals Tuesday night amounted to an ugly microcosm of the preceding 48 minutes: a mess of disjointed, almost reluctant offense punctuated by rare glimmers of grace. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/sports/basketball/24randolph/24randolph-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Randolph, the Challenge Is Offense', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Popovich, Gregg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Zach', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Grizzlies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:18:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Cavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4968535d-8e7e-52e2-b195-9a26dc021dc3', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4968535d-8e7e-52e2-b195-9a26dc021dc3'}, {'abstract': 'Newsweek takes on the upward trend in suicide rates.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/the-trajectory-of-suicide/', 'snippet': 'Newsweek takes on the upward trend in suicide rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since I’ve been writing about the recent uptick in suicide rates, I should link to Newsweek’s big new piece on the same trend, which offers a good survey of how self-slaughter has become one of the world’s leading causes of death. The piece’s author, Tony Dokoupil, actually\xa0goes a little bit further than I would: Given how much of suicide’s new statistical prominence is explained by the (happy) decline in other ways of death, and given that suicide rates were dipping in the U.S. up until the turn of millenium, I’m not sure that the language of “epidemic” quite makes sense at this point; I think the Center for Disease Control’s formulation,\xa0“an increasing public health concern,” is a more appropriate way of putting it. The big question, as my column tried to suggest, is where the current trend is going, and whether the upward movement is likely to persist. And here the Newsweek essay has a good distillation of the case for pessimism:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trajectory of Suicide', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newsweek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03621957-c9c6-51b5-a7b6-73ea13989a3e', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03621957-c9c6-51b5-a7b6-73ea13989a3e'}, {'abstract': 'Children of mothers with cancer must learn this painful lesson early: the vulnerability of the figure on whom they have grounded their existence. With varying degrees of fearful awareness, such children intuit that the mother who comforts by murmuring “I am here” will not always be there.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/mothers-with-cancer/', 'snippet': 'Children of mothers with cancer must learn this painful lesson early: the vulnerability of the figure on whom they have grounded their existence. With varying degrees of fearful awareness, such children intuit that the mother who comforts by murmu...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ensconced in Babyland, I attend the relentless rhythms of soothing my visiting 3-month-old grandson, who cannot seem to sleep more than 40 minutes at a stretch. I have determined to jettison all other obligations with two exceptions: providing meals for my nursing daughter and reading a memoir lent to me by a friend who must have known how it would move me. In “The Kitchen Congregation,” Nora Seton mourns the death of her mother, a novelist, from cancer at age 56. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mothers With Cancer', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c211e2-096b-5c9d-8467-cba8a4b624ee', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c211e2-096b-5c9d-8467-cba8a4b624ee'}, {'abstract': 'The annual Deutsche Bank shareholders meeting began with applause for Anshu Jain, the bank’s co-chief executive, but attention quickly turned to the myriad problems that the bank has been trying to shake.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/warm-welcome-at-deutsche-bank-meeting-followed-by-rancor/', 'snippet': 'The annual Deutsche Bank shareholders meeting began with applause for Anshu Jain, the bank’s co-chief executive, but attention quickly turned to the myriad problems that the bank has been trying to shake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Anshu Jain, co-chief executive of Deutsche Bank, had barely spoken two sentences to shareholders Thursday when he was interrupted by applause. It wasn’t what he said that pleased the audience so much as the language he used: German.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warm Welcome at Deutsche Bank Meeting, Followed by Rancor', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitschen, Jurgen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jain, Anshu', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:40:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bf209b8-e7a0-5a47-bbe8-6e64c08824d0', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bf209b8-e7a0-5a47-bbe8-6e64c08824d0'}, {'abstract': 'The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board said the firm found a fraud risk in nine audits in 2009 but did not sufficiently follow up on the risk.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/regulator-cites-flaws-in-ernst-young-procedures/', 'snippet': 'The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board said the firm found a fraud risk in nine audits in 2009 but did not sufficiently follow up on the risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States regulator of accounting firms said on Thursday that a Big Four firm, Ernst & Young, had been too willing to trust figures supplied by corporate executives instead of evaluating them independently and had failed to improve its procedures even after being told to do so.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulator Cites Flaws in Ernst & Young’s Audit Procedures', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ernst & Young’s Audit Procedures Faulted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ERNST & YOUNG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Company Accounting Oversight Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/378fcf53-d1e7-55fd-9136-19b572d09bfc', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/378fcf53-d1e7-55fd-9136-19b572d09bfc'}, {'abstract': 'Being polite can help get some airline fees waived.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/getting-change-fees-waived-for-a-canceled-flight/', 'snippet': 'Being polite can help get some airline fees waived.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Airlines take a lot of heat for indifferent customer service — and it’s often justified. But I recently had a pleasantly reasonable experience with American Airlines, although it did take a little time to resolve.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Change Fees Waived for a Canceled Flight', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Success Story On Airline Fee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T16:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce0053d7-afdb-5321-84cf-cb461ce13ea0', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce0053d7-afdb-5321-84cf-cb461ce13ea0'}, {'abstract': 'Bertram Lyons, an archivist at the American Folklife Center, is answering questions on how to manage your analog and digital material from old videotapes to pictures on your blog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/booming/advice-on-how-to-preserve-your-photos-records-videos-and-online-media.html', 'snippet': 'Bertram Lyons, an archivist at the American Folklife Center, is answering questions on how to manage your analog and digital material from old videotapes to pictures on your blog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bertram Lyons will answer questions relating to archiving and preserving family history and stories: analog and digital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist-span/23expert-booming-archivist-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist-span/23expert-booming-archivist-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist-span/23expert-booming-archivist-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist-span/23expert-booming-archivist-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048,