rd Rock Hotel Chicago recently introduced the Nursing Mothers Amenity Program, providing guests with hospital-grade breast pumps, mini-refrigerators and bra pads.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/help-with-breast-feeding/', 'snippet': 'The Hard Rock Hotel Chicago recently introduced the Nursing Mothers Amenity Program, providing guests with hospital-grade breast pumps, mini-refrigerators and bra pads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nursing mothers, traveling light is an oxymoron. But one hotelier is at least reducing the load a bit. The Hard Rock Hotel Chicago, in partnership with Medela, a manufacturer of breast pumps and breast-feeding accessories, recently introduced the Nursing Mothers Amenity Program. For $30 per stay, guests are provided with hospital-grade breast pumps, mini-refrigerators, microwaves, cooler bags, ice packs and bra pads. The hotel’s concierge staff is trained to handle nursing-specific requests, like how to safely send expressed milk.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Help With Breast-Feeding', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hotels: Help With Breast-Feeding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4d59993-9448-5311-8e81-f51cccc4dc21', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4d59993-9448-5311-8e81-f51cccc4dc21'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph H. Boardman has led the government-owned railroad corporation to record growth in ridership and revenue since taking over in November 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/business/amtrak-extends-contract-of-its-president.html', 'snippet': 'Joseph H. Boardman has led the government-owned railroad corporation to record growth in ridership and revenue since taking over in November 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Amtrak’s board of directors on Thursday extended the contract of the company’s president, Joseph H. Boardman, who has led the government-owned railroad corporation to record growth in ridership and revenue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amtrak Extends Contract of Its President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amtrak Extends Contract of Its President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMTRAK', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boardman, Joseph H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T17:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a95654bc-2d76-53d6-b741-895cf5199824', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a95654bc-2d76-53d6-b741-895cf5199824'}, {'abstract': 'Institutional Shareholder Services agreed to settle civil charges that it failed to prevent an employee from improperly selling confidential investor vote data.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/i-s-s-settles-investigation-into-leaks-of-shareholder-vote-data/', 'snippet': 'Institutional Shareholder Services agreed to settle civil charges that it failed to prevent an employee from improperly selling confidential investor vote data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Institutional Shareholder Services, the biggest independent adviser to shareholders on corporate elections, agreed to pay a fine on Thursday to settle civil charges that it failed to stop an employee from improperly selling confidential vote data.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fine Settles an Inquiry Into Selling of I.S.S. Vote Data', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fine Settles An Inquiry Into Selling Of Vote Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Shareholder Services Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSCI', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T17:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/571e23e6-4df5-5701-90d6-0ffa707cc6c5', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/571e23e6-4df5-5701-90d6-0ffa707cc6c5'}, {'ab