ds': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a0fded5-f1c4-53fe-b461-0880bd768541', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a0fded5-f1c4-53fe-b461-0880bd768541'}, {'abstract': 'Reflections on the 971 poems submitted for our Fourth Annual Found Poetry Contest. Winners will be announced starting May 28.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/reflections-on-our-most-popular-found-poetry-contest-yet/', 'snippet': 'Reflections on the 971 poems submitted for our Fourth Annual Found Poetry Contest. Winners will be announced starting May 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in March, we invited you to enter our Fourth Annual Found Poetry Student Contest, and 971 of you did, sending in verse that was so interesting and intricate that it’s taken us more than a month to read, reread, discuss and winnow it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 303}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1033, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/learning/PoetryContest13LN/PoetryContest13LN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reflections on Our Most Popular Found Poetry Contest Yet', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86712f92-90b4-57ae-8d7c-91765c06523b', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86712f92-90b4-57ae-8d7c-91765c06523b'}, {'abstract': 'At today’s annual meeting, the national council will decide whether to allow gay scouts. The ban on gay leaders will remain in place.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/boy-scouts-vote-on-gay-youth-members/', 'snippet': 'At today’s annual meeting, the national council will decide whether to allow gay scouts. The ban on gay leaders will remain in place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an op-ed this week for USA Today, Wayne Perry, president of the Boy Scouts of America, mused that “somehow, Scouting has become one of the focal points in the debate on homosexuality.” The reasons behind that “somehow” are not too obscure. Mr. Perry asserted in the same op-ed that the B.S.A. is “part of the fabric of this nation” and delivers “the nation’s foremost youth program of character development and values-based leadership training.” How is it surprising that such a large, vital organization would attract criticism for its longstanding policy of excluding gay members and leaders?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boy Scouts Vote on Gay Youth Members', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4f5d42b-eab5-517c-aea3-9406eda05aca', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4f5d42b-eab5-517c-aea3-9406eda05aca'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent interview with Amanda Knox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/books/review/against-amanda.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent interview with Amanda Knox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Against Amanda', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Against Amanda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c44838d-2a34-5d2f-b53f-85bee4d8d329', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c44838d-2a34-5d2f-b53f-85bee4d8d329'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent review of “The Sleepwalkers” and “July 1914.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/books/review/on-the-brink.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent review of “The Sleepwalkers” and “July 1914.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘On the Brink’', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘On The Brink’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9784c02-bd55-54dd-ac78-db7d6a957573', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9784c02-bd55-54dd-ac78-db7d6a957573'}, {'abstract': 'An exploration of how, or if, interfaith marriages work in a nation of many religions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/books/review/til-faith-do-us-part-by-naomi-schaefer-riley.html', 'snippet': 'An exploration of how, or if, interfaith marriages work in a nation of many religions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have always been a religiously diverse people, even as the definition of what counts as diversity has changed. In 1774, members of the Continental Congress protested the idea of bringing in a chaplain to lead prayers: “We were so divided in religious sentiment,” one of them explained, “that we could not join in the same act of worship.” Overwhelmingly Protestant, they nonetheless recognized the significant differences of theology and practice that divided Anglicans from Presbyterians, Baptists from Quakers.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 681}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 903, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1714, 'width': 1511, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/Niebuhr-SUB/Niebuhr-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Church and the State of Matrimony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Church and the State of Matrimony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riley, Naomi Schaefer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T18:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gustav Niebuhr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gustav', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Niebuhr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe53046-706a-5522-8ef9-34bfb7a1a316', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe53046-706a-5522-8ef9-34bfb7a1a316'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Weiner made his first public appearances on Thursday after announcing his mayoral bid on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000002242063/anthony-d-weiner-on-the-campaign-trail.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Weiner made his first public appearances on Thursday after announcing his mayoral bid on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Weiner made his first public appearances on Thursday after announcing his mayoral bid on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/nyregion/24weiner-videostill/24weiner-videostill-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/nyregion/24weiner-videostill/24weiner-videostill-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'