'_id': 'nyt://article/7ff0120e-ae0c-5f8a-83bd-38ed817c37b1', 'word_count': 5078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff0120e-ae0c-5f8a-83bd-38ed817c37b1'}, {'abstract': 'Our attraction to the mythical unicorn is explored in a new exhibition at the Cloisters, using Metropolitan Museum holdings and items from other collections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/arts/design/search-for-the-unicorn-at-the-cloisters.html', 'snippet': 'Our attraction to the mythical unicorn is explored in a new exhibition at the Cloisters, using Metropolitan Museum holdings and items from other collections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum is an excellent place to hunt for mythical beasts. Look in almost any gallery of art made before 1900 and you’ll find dragons, sphinxes, centaurs, hydras, phoenixes and griffins. The Cloisters, the Met’s medieval branch at the northern tip of Manhattan, offers multiple sightings of a particularly elusive creature: the unicorn, star of the celebrated Unicorn Tapestries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24UNICORN1_SPAN/24UNICORN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24UNICORN1_SPAN/24UNICORN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24UNICORN1_SPAN/24UNICORN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24UNICORN1_SPAN/24UNICORN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu