c53caca2ec', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/1666a3d8-f045-5508-9fff-4cc53caca2ec'}, {'abstract': 'In “The English Teacher,” Julianne Moore plays a high school teacher leading a solitary life who suddenly takes a chance on a former star pupil with artistic ambitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/movies/the-english-teacher-starring-julianne-moore.html', 'snippet': 'In “The English Teacher,” Julianne Moore plays a high school teacher leading a solitary life who suddenly takes a chance on a former star pupil with artistic ambitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you eliminated its obtrusively perky soundtrack and revised its dishonest feel-good ending, “The English Teacher” would be a very different — and much better — movie. Instead, this would-be comedy, directed by Craig Zisk from a screenplay by the married writers Dan and Stacy Chariton, is perversely determined to make you laugh. You’re more likely to squirm, though, at what seems as incongruous as a Chekhov play staged in clown costume. At least it is not dull. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24ENGLISH1_SPAN/ENGLISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24ENGLISH1_SPAN/ENGLISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24ENGLISH1_SPAN/ENGLISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24ENGLISH1_SPAN/ENGLISH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}