 that Mr. Atkinson, a former Washington Post editor and reporter, will be writing a trilogy covering the years 1775-1781.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having conquered the best-seller lists with his trilogy about World War II, the Pulitzer Prize-winning author Rick Atkinson will be taking three-book aim at another conflict: the American Revolution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Atkinson to Write Trilogy about the American Revolution', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T23:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ee758cc-d320-5f09-9594-ed78856e2d50', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ee758cc-d320-5f09-9594-ed78856e2d50'}, {'abstract': 'Addressing issues over leaving a mentor, obese seat mates, separate moviegoing and wedding-gift slackers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/fashion/a-circle-of-life-exit.html', 'snippet': 'Addressing issues over leaving a mentor, obese seat mates, separate moviegoing and wedding-gift slackers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve worked closely with my boss for four years. He has been a really generous mentor, but I’ve gone about as far as I can at our company. Recently, I was offered an amazing position by a competitor, and I took it. I expected a difficult conversation with my boss, but nothing like what I got. He practically said, “You are dead to me.” What should I do? I feel terrible and unsure of myself.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': N