: 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1949dee6-1344-5e00-808e-d54413208264', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1949dee6-1344-5e00-808e-d54413208264'}, {'abstract': 'Stephanie Vogt is trying to qualify for the French Open and put her tiny home country on the tennis map.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/liechtenstein-rising/', 'snippet': 'Stephanie Vogt is trying to qualify for the French Open and put her tiny home country on the tennis map.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the 24 players in the final round of women’s singles qualifying at the 2013 French Open, there are a lot of the usual suspects. Three Americans. Three Russians. Three Czechs. But on the uppermost line of the draw, the letters “LIE” signal a new arrival: Stephanie Vogt, of tiny, landlocked Liechtenstein (population 36,000).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liechtenstein Rising', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T23:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffd41cc-287c-569c-a57c-a64298a8192e', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffd41cc-287c-569c-a57c-a64298a8192e'}, {'abstract': 'The Belmont Stakes is a little over two weeks away, and the big question is whether Orb, the impressive Kentucky Derby winner who faltered in the Preakness, will compete.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/orb-looking-good-but-belmont-still-in-question/', 'snippet': 'The Belmont Stakes is a little over two weeks away, and the big question is whether Orb, the impressive Kentucky Derby winner who faltered in the Preakness, will compete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Belmont Stakes is a little over two weeks away, and the big question is whether Orb, the impressive Kentucky Derby winner who faltered in the Preakness, will compete. If he does, the race will be cast as a showdown between the Derby winner and the Preakness winner, Oxbow, and will help the race gain some needed buzz.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orb Looking Good, but Belmont Status Still in Question', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGaughey, Shug', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T23:12:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ebba0a-fc56-5058-a4b6-4a2cdf9bcd32', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ebba0a-fc56-5058-a4b6-4a2cdf9bcd32'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from the new European galleries at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/24/arts/design/met-european-paintings-photos.html', 'snippet': 'Photos from the new European galleries at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from the new European galleries at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Home for Familiar Paintings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-23T23:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1eac2ce3-1003-52cc-a9d8-3470781cf3d2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1eac2ce3-1003-52cc-a9d8-3470781cf3d2'}, {'abstract': '“A Green Story,” inspired by real events, is about a Greek immigrant who succeeds because of all-American hard work and an early belief in the green movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/movies/a-green-story-directed-by-nika-agiashvili.html', 'snippet': '“A Green Story,” inspired by real events, is about a Greek immigrant who succeeds because of all-American hard work and an early belief in the green movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inspired by true events, “A Green Story” is like the tribute reel at a retirement dinner. Or a lengthy advertisement for Earth Friendly Products, whose retired founder’s achievement it celebrates. But however you might describe it, “A Green Story” cannot be applauded for its moral complexity. This stately film lays out the good, the bad, the sad and the proud in stark patterns, to mostly soporific effect.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/movies/green-span/green-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/movies/green-span/green-span-articleLarge.jpg', '