ourtyard with a temporary infla...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Koshalek, the director of the Smithsonian Institution’s Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden in Washington, said on Thursday that he was resigning after the board of trustees failed to reach a consensus on the future of a long-planned project to cover the museum’s interior courtyard with a temporary inflatable bubble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Director of Hirshhorn Museum Resigns Over Stalled ‘Bubble’ Project', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koshalek, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T00:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1575ee4-f366-5a6b-8310-aa1fe437fa94', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1575ee4-f366-5a6b-8310-aa1fe437fa94'}, {'abstract': 'It was not clear whether President Obama’s aim of shuttering the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, would be achieved soon, but he began a renewed push to winnow down its population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/us/politics/obama-lifts-moratorium-on-transfer-of-some-detainees.html', 'snippet': 'It was not clear whether President Obama’s aim of shuttering the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, would be achieved soon, but he began a renewed push to winnow down its population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Thursday lifted a moratorium on repatriating low-level inmates from the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, to Yemen and, in a surprise move, announced the creation of a new Pentagon position to spearhead the transfer of detainees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Lifts Moratorium on Transfer of Detainees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Lifts Moratorium On Transfer Of Detainees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T00:44:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3def28-d65b-5122-bf0c-a0b1ddea925c', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3def28-d65b-5122-bf0c-a0b1ddea925c'}, {'abstract': 'The four executives were ordered to testify before a grand jury investigating actions at the hedge fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/23/4-sac-executives-subpoenaed-in-insider-trading-inquiry/', 'snippet': 'The four executives were ordered to testify before a grand jury investigating actions at the hedge fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four senior executives of the hedge fund SAC Capital Advisors have received subpoenas to testify before a grand jury as part of the government’s intensifying investigation into insider trading at the firm, according to people briefed on the case.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 SAC Executives Subpoenaed in Insider Trading Inquiry', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 SAC Executives Subpoenaed in Insider Trading Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T00:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e92daa61-7186-5668-95df-50ec878ad5d7', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e92daa61-7186-5668-95df-50ec878ad5d7'}, {'abstract': 'In 2010, the off-duty detective, Leopold McLean, 48, fired several shots at Lepaul Gammons, then 39, including one that hit him in the buttocks, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/nyregion/detective-convicted-of-attempted-murder-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'In 2010, the off-duty detective, Leopold McLean, 48, fired several shots at Lepaul Gammons, then 39, including one that hit him in the buttocks, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A veteran New York City police detective once assigned to the mayor’s security team was convicted of attempted murder and reckless endangerment on Thursday for shooting a man while off duty, the Queens district attorney said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'pr