d.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Well, here’s the deal: I’m all for innovation and for pushing the envelope to see where the future of puzzles might be, but to put it nicely, I’m not convinced that this is it. Sorry, Joe Krozel. I think you’ve jumped the cruciverbal shark on this one. I may be in the minority here, but I’ll explain my position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Perhaps Having One Too Many', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T02:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ea389d0-c4e3-5083-8e98-f0995024ff33', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ea389d0-c4e3-5083-8e98-f0995024ff33'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 24, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/pageoneplus/corrections-may-24-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 24, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 24, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T02:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e78c0cd-02e2-52f2-8420-c2295c1df4df', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e78c0cd-02e2-52f2-8420-c2295c1df4df'}, {'abstract': 'Mando Alvarado’s new drama, “Basilica,” is bounded by home, church and bar in San Juan, Tex.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/theater/reviews/basilica-by-mando-alvarado-at-the-cherry-lane-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Mando Alvarado’s new drama, “Basilica,” is bounded by home, church and bar in San Juan, Tex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s this funny thing that can occur when you’re watching a play, a development in that hazy somewhere between suspension of, and stymieing of, disbelief. It happens when enough of a world has been created onstage so that you care about it and the people who inhabit it — and then something goes awry, stops short or simply parts ways with your own sensibilities, so that you feel that an injustice has been done to that world by the same people who made you care about it in the first place. Excitement withers, followed by creeping frustration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24BASILICA_SPAN/24BASILICA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24BASILICA_SPAN/24BASILICA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24BASILICA_SPAN/24BASILICA_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/arts/24BASILICA_SPAN/24BASILICA_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url