led in Iraq, began to notice the mementos left by friends and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, James Estrin interviewed Luke Sharrett, a freelance photographer for The New York Times and other publications, about the gravestones at Arlington National Cemetery in Virginia. Mr. Sharrett’s answers have been edited into a narrative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sacrifices Set in Adorned Stone', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tombs and Tombstones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arlington National Cemetery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Sharrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6f1f908-bf4a-5dff-b281-9cab5e70f551', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6f1f908-bf4a-5dff-b281-9cab5e70f551'}, {'abstract': 'Why do you plan to save these belongings? Do you hope they will be more valuable in the future, or do you keep them for sentimental reasons?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/do-you-plan-on-saving-any-of-your-belongings-for-the-future/', 'snippet': 'Why do you plan to save these belongings? Do you hope they will be more valuable in the future, or do you keep them for sentimental reasons?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you collect autographed baseballs, ticket stubs, funky earrings, classic video games or anything else? Sometimes we decide to hold on to a few objects because we think they will be valuable someday, or because we just can’t bear to part with them for sentimental reasons. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24apple-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24apple-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24apple-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24apple-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24tech-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24tech-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/technology/24apple-LN/24tech-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Plan on Saving Any of Your Belongings for the Future?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '20