icle', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf0730c5-02f5-5f73-ac16-99613a38004e', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf0730c5-02f5-5f73-ac16-99613a38004e'}, {'abstract': 'The attackers set off a large explosion followed by numerous smaller blasts, sending United Nations and international agency workers into bomb shelters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/world/asia/insurgents-attack-near-un-mission-in-kabul.html', 'snippet': 'The attackers set off a large explosion followed by numerous smaller blasts, sending United Nations and international agency workers into bomb shelters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — In what appeared to be a concerted effort to test the capabilities of Afghan security forces in the capital, Taliban insurgents sought to penetrate the heavily fortified heart of Kabul on Friday, blasting their way into a residential compound of the International Organization for Migration, an agency that has worked with the United Nations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/world/asia/25afghanistan/25afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/world/asia/25afghanistan/25afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/world/asia/25afghanistan/25afghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType':