middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sater', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Kriston', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindsay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mabry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3a2893ef-9a49-5194-b69b-c349f0ea2cb1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3a2893ef-9a49-5194-b69b-c349f0ea2cb1'}, {'abstract': 'In bringing back its lovely, probing solo show “Sontag: Reborn,” Builders reintroduces us to one of its most meditative works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/theater/watching-sontag-make-up-her-mind.html', 'snippet': 'In bringing back its lovely, probing solo show “Sontag: Reborn,” Builders reintroduces us to one of its most meditative works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning the personal journals of a writer and intellectual into compelling theater is the kind of difficult challenge that the Builders Association delights in. The company has long hid its literary sensibilities under a high-tech veneer, and in bringing back its lovely, probing solo show “Sontag: Reborn,” Builders reintroduces us to one of its most meditative works. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching Sontag Make Up Her Mind', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watching Sontag Make Up Her Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T14:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/334801cd-d808-540b-8b60-9f2ae073f4fe', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/334801cd-d808-540b-8b60-9f2ae073f4fe'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters will not be totally surprised if the Boston Bruins allow their playoff series with the Rangers to become complicated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/sports/hockey/the-bruins-chaos-theory.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters will not be totally surprised if the Boston Bruins allow their playoff series with the Rangers to become complicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some teams, a little chaos is in their DNA. The Boston Bruins, for instance, do not seem comfortable unless their playoff series go to seven games. It is even better if they are down a few goals in the third period, so failing to sweep the Rangers Thursday night in Game 4 came as a surprise to almost no one. The series may have only just begun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/25leading1/25leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bruins’ Chaos Theory', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rask, Tuukka', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreider, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krzyzewski, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toews, Jonathan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chara, Zdeno', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roy, Patrick', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Jimmy (1984- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francona, Terry', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kane, Patrick (1988- )', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T14:48:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a0f41ca-ca34-5f4f-9541-62fe13518788', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a0f41ca-ca34-5f4f-9541-62fe13518788'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE LOWER RIVER,  by Paul Theroux (Mariner/Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $14.95.) Longing for the purposefulness of his Peace Corps days, the American protagonist of Theroux’s riveting novel returns to an African village after an absence of 40 years. But nostalgia soon turns into despair: the school he built is in ruins, the church and clinic are gone, and the villagers’ overtures toward him are tinged with menace.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T14:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5710177-a340-58b8-bc8e-fcddf9e4daa4', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5710177-a340-58b8-bc8e-fcddf9e4daa4'}, {'abstract': 'The “Sphere,” a sculpture by Fritz Koenig, was to have been moved from Battery Park in the late spring of 2012, but it appears there are no plans to relocate it.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/a-sphere-that-has-taken-a-year-to-roll-nowhere/', 'snippet': 'The “Sphere,” a sculpture by Fritz Koenig, was to have been moved from Battery Park in the late spring of 2012, but it appears there are no plans to relocate it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last word on the fate of Fritz Koenig’s “Sphere” for the World Trade Center, installed in 2002 at Battery Park as the city’s interim 9/11 memorial, came a year ago from Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg. “I think it’s beautiful where it is,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/21/blogs/20130521Sphere1/20130521Sphere1-thumbStandard.jpg'