 would be a lot better off with a 4 percent inflation target rather than the 2 percent that is now central bank orthodoxy. Intellectually, this position is hardly outlandish; indeed, Ball’s case is very similar to the case Olivier Blanchard made three years ago, just stated more forcefully and with more evidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Four Percent Solution', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T15:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2315290-303d-5f4d-81b2-7261dc4c92b8', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2315290-303d-5f4d-81b2-7261dc4c92b8'}, {'abstract': 'Amid entanglements between Russia and young Americans, a first novel explores the sense of betrayal in the loss of family and friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/books/review/you-are-one-of-them-by-elliott-holt.html', 'snippet': 'Amid entanglements between Russia and young Americans, a first novel explores the sense of betrayal in the loss of family and friends.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The first defector was my sister.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/0526-bks-Shipstead/0526-bks-Shipstead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/books/review/0526-bks-Shipstead/0526-bks-Shipstead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarg