k, Elliott Holt discusses her novel “You Are One of Them”; Rick Atkinson discusses his “The Guns at Last Light”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/05/24/books/review/26books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Elliott Holt discusses her novel “You Are One of Them”; Rick Atkinson discusses his “The Guns at Last Light”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Elliott Holt discusses her novel “You Are One of Them”; Rick Atkinson discusses his “The Guns at Last Light”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the New York Times Book Review: ‘You Are One of Them’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T15:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/de84b2b1-2112-56d0-803c-e35db7bb39f2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/de84b2b1-2112-56d0-803c-e35db7bb39f2'}, {'abstract': 'The French Open draw was not friendly to the French competitors, giving tough draws to players like Jo-Wilfried Tsonga and Gael Monfils.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/draw-punctures-french-hopes-for-a-home-country-celebration/', 'snippet': 'The French Open draw was not friendly to the French competitors, giving tough draws to players like Jo-Wilfried Tsonga and Gael Monfils.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – After the live jazz trio gave way to the French Open draw ceremony here – complete with Champagne for refreshments – a theme quickly emerged. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Draw Punctures French Hopes for a Home Country Celebration', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JUDY BATTISTA', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BATTISTA', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/320e4691-b63f-5996-9d44-624f8cb16b9d', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/320e4691-b63f-5996-9d44-624f8cb16b9d'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend is the year’s biggest for auto racing. Here’s where to find the action.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/coming-up-is-auto-racings-biggest-weekend-of-the-year/', 'snippet': 'This weekend is the year’s biggest for auto racing. Here’s where to find the action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend is auto racing’s biggest of the year. No major championship will be decided, but the weekend will see three classic events run in the United States and Europe. The action kicked off Thursday morning with practice in Monaco, which on Sunday will be the site of the sixth event of the year counting toward the Formula One World Drivers Championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Up Is Auto Racing’s Biggest Weekend of the Year', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '