: None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c618b4-09eb-5017-bad1-c5db107bb1f8', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c618b4-09eb-5017-bad1-c5db107bb1f8'}, {'abstract': 'Elliott Holt discusses her novel “You Are One of Them”; Rick Atkinson discusses his “The Guns at Last Light”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/book-review-podcast-lamenting-defectors-soviet-and-otherwise/', 'snippet': 'Elliott Holt discusses her novel “You Are One of Them”; Rick Atkinson discusses his “The Guns at Last Light”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in The New York Times Book Review, Maggie Shipstead reviews Elliott Holt’s new novel, “You Are One of Them,” which was inspired by the story of Samantha Smith, the American schoolgirl who wrote to the Soviet premier Yuri Andropov in 1982 and asked if he intended to start a nuclear war. Ms. Shipstead writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: Lamenting Defectors, Soviet and Otherwise', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:19:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f290be57-6ebf-5d63-bb36-835135910f22', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f290be57-6ebf-5d63-bb36-835135910f22'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Dern and Will Forte talk about starring in “Nebraska” for Alexander Payne.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/cannes-film-festival-bruce-dern-and-will-forte-on-nebraska/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Dern and Will Forte talk about starring in “Nebraska” for Alexander Payne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — In Alexander Payne’s “About Schmidt” (2002), Jack Nicholson returned to form and earned an Oscar nomination for playing an older father on a journey with his daughter. At this year’s Cannes Film Festival, Mr. Payne’s new film “Nebraska” stars Mr. Nicholson’s old pal Bruce Dern as an older father who goes on a journey with his son, played by Will Forte. Mr. Dern is Woody, an alcoholic who is nearing senility and becomes convinced that a sweepstakes pamphlet is an actual guarantee of a million-dollar prize. Mr. Forte, in his first dramatic role, is David, who takes pity on his dad and drives him to Nebraska to claim it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/dernforte/dernforte-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cannes Film Festival: Bruce Dern and Will Forte on ‘Nebraska’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forte, Will', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicholson, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:19:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Logan Hill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Logan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c60ddee0-140c-555c-8db5-840892746669', 'word_count': 1557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c60ddee0-140c-555c-8db5-840892746669'}, {'abstract': 'Being depressed is known to increase the risk for stroke. Now a new study suggests that the association is even stronger in younger women.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/depression-raises-stroke-risk-in-younger-women/', 'snippet': 'Being depressed is known to increase the risk for stroke. Now a new study suggests that the association is even stronger in younger women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being depressed is known to increase the risk for stroke. Now a new study suggests that the association is even stronger in younger women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 216, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 216, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Depression Raises Stroke Risk in Younger Women', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43abea7e-57af-56ff-bd83-0bdc850814ba', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43abea7e-57af-56ff-bd83-0bdc850814ba'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama wants to end the “global war on terror.” Republicans desperately want to keep it going.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/the-g-o-p-s-cold-war-posture/', 'snippet': 'President Obama wants to end the “global war on terror.” Republicans desperately want to keep it going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most striking thing about President Obama’s speech on counter-terrorism yesterday was his eagerness to end the “global war on terror” and redefine it as a series of smaller-scale skirmishes. And the most striking thing about the reaction of Republicans was their stated refusal to end it, their longing to keep it going as the pinnacle of national priorities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The G.O.P.’s Cold-War Posture', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8dea0b2-6462-5e80-acb3-3f6fd6c8534e', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8dea0b2-6462-5e80-acb3-3f6fd6c8534e'}, {'abstract': 'The singer owes millions in taxes from the years 2009 to 2011, according to reports.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/mary-j-blige-hit-with-3-4-million-tax-lien/', 'snippet': 'The singer owes millions in taxes from the years 2009 to 2011, according to reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget about the Tea Party. The Internal Revenue Service seems to be out for blood when it comes to R&B singers residing in New Jersey. First Lauryn Hill was sentenced to jail for failing to pay income taxes over three years. Now the I.R.S. has hit Mary J. Blige and her husband, who live in Cresskill, with a $3.4 million tax lien, according to The Associated Press. Court documents assert that Ms. Blige owes more than $574,000 for the 2009 tax year, more than $2.2 million for 2010 and $647,000 for 2011. A representative for Ms. Blige told The A.P. that she was working to resolve the dispute as quickly as possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary J. Blige Hit With $3.4 Million Tax Lien', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blige, Mary J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b51955-3367-5fb1-a6e8-0d40e2bb6457', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b51955-3367-5fb1-a6e8-0d40e2bb6457'}, {'abstract': 'The 11-room co-op apartment, at 97th Street, features a wraparound terrace with views of Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/26/realestate/20130526-EXCLUSIVE.html', 'snippet': 'The 11-room co-op apartment, at 97th Street, features a wraparound terrace with views of Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 11-room co-op apartment, at 97th Street, features a wraparound terrace with views of Central Park