that Japanese ownership of the American cellphone operator is a risk to national security is half-baked and shows boss Charlie Ergen’s desperation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Security Sideshow in the Fight Over Sprint', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dish Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SOFTBANK Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:40:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f54aa81-cc03-552c-8623-9f80002814a2', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f54aa81-cc03-552c-8623-9f80002814a2'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/weekend-calendar/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn Flea expands its empire with the debut on Friday of SmorgasBar, located on Front Street near Fulton Street at the South Street Seaport, to help the area’s recovery from Hurricane Sandy. Through October, various vendors will set up shop next to a bar — which serves beer, wines and spirits — located inside a shipping container. The hours are 11 a.m. to 11 p.m. Friday and Saturdays, and 11 a.m. to 10 p.m. the rest of the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Flea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T16:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a03abb42-08a3-5409-b962-fb93eacb3530', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a03abb42-08a3-5409-b962-fb93eacb3530'}, {'abstract': 'Disagreements come and go, but for Tracy and Grant MacSwain never with the thought of “I can’t stand this anymore.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/booming/for-42-years-agreeing-on-the-big-stuff-if-not-the-little-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Disagreements come and go, but for Tracy and Grant MacSwain never with the thought of “I can’t stand this anymore.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Booming’s “Making It Last” column profiles baby boomer couples who have been together 25 years or more. Send us your story and photos through our submission form. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/booming/24last-booming-macswain-span/24last-booming-macswain-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/24/booming/24last-booming-macswain-span/24last-booming-macswain-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlarg