ippet': 'Six Americans — Vania King, Grace Min, Steve Johnson, Jack Sock, Denis Kudla and Rhyne Williams — advanced through qualifying and into the French Open main draw on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Shrugging off raindrops and unseasonal cold temperatures, four American men and two American women advanced out of qualifying into the main draws of the French Open singles championships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Emerge from French Open Qualifying', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T17:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d06390ed-11f5-53e7-81ba-dadb91d820c3', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d06390ed-11f5-53e7-81ba-dadb91d820c3'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/the-gun-report-may-24-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We received a sad email this morning—a producer at the PBS Newshour wanted us to know that a young employee, Julian Dawkins, 22, a shuttle driver for the Newshour, was shot to death early Wednesday morning. As it happens, we had already found the news of his death and were planning to include it in today’s report. (It’s the 11th item today.) People at the Newshour are still trying to piece together the circumstances of his death, which are murky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 24, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEXANDRIA (VA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Arlington County (Va)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Birmingham (Ala)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cedar Rapids (Iowa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East New York (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lexington (Ky)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Little Rock (Ark)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Memphis (Tenn)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia Beach (Va)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T17:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d944f70-4ded-55fb-b690-02cee9c4a598', 'word_count': 1356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d944f70-4ded-55fb-b690-02cee9c4a598'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events across the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/calendar-coming-events-in-isle-of-wight-sydney-waukesha-wis/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events across the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walking With Dinosaurs Trail, Isle of Wight The Isle of Wight, home to about a dozen species of dinosaurs millions of years ago, is starting a Walking With Dinosaurs Trail on June 21, in advance of the release this year of “Walking With Dinosaurs: The 3D Movie.” The island, off the southeast coast of England, was recently named the “Dinosaur Capital of Great Britain” (exhibit, above). Would-be dinosaur explorers can join experts on beach fossil hunts, use the Dinosaur Island App to see themselves alongside digital reconstructions of the reptiles and learn about ones portrayed in the movie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Isle of Wight; Sydney; Waukesha, Wis.', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T17:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afac5304-3030-5c44-8389-ce71bede090d', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afac5304-3030-5c44-8389-ce71bede090d'}, {'abstract': 'No problems have been reported on customer vehicles, but Cadillac said it found some vehicles in its fleet with loose lug nuts.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/cadillac-to-recall-19000-srx-models-for-wheel-problem-triumph-and-nissan-issue-recalls/', 'snippet': 'No problems have been reported on customer vehicles, but Cadillac said it found some vehicles in its fleet with loose lug nuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors will recall almost 19,000 2013 Cadillac SRX models because the lug nuts on its 18-inch wheels may loosen, the automaker told the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cadillac to Recall SRX Models for Wheel Problem; Triumph and Nissan Issue Recalls', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Triumph Motor Cars', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T17:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dd61a96-02db-532e-ac2a-669df45ccfa9', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dd61a96-02db-532e-ac2a-669df45ccfa9'}, {'abstract': 'Wind, rain, pounding surf and dazzling views on a five-day, less-than-waterproof, head-clearing trek on the Welsh coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/travel/slow-travel-walking-in-wales.html', 'snippet': 'Wind, rain, pounding surf and dazzling views on a five-day, less-than-waterproof, head-clearing trek on the Welsh coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My idea of heaven is a long walk. Aimless hours pass, thoughts drift. I was never ambitious about how many miles I covered — until I read a biography of Johann Sebastian Bach. He loved to walk, too, and thought nothing of walking to a town hundreds of miles away to try a new organ, or to look for a new job. He walked for weeks — months, even — humming to himself, I hope. I wondered why I always traveled by car, or train, or plane, always in a rush. I wanted to walk from one town to another, too. I began to yearn for slow travel.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/travel/26-wales-combo-new-sf/26-wales-combo-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/travel/26-wales-combo-new-sf/26-wales-combo-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 532}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/travel/26-wales-combo-new-sf/26-wales-combo-new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/travel/26-wales-combo-new-sf/26-wales-combo-new-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1815, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/travel/26-wales-combo-new-sf/26-wales-combo-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name