': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '21st Century Fox', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T19:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d2353c5-4769-50da-9374-b571fabd7377', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d2353c5-4769-50da-9374-b571fabd7377'}, {'abstract': 'Opponents warned, despite scientific evidence, that fluoride would unnecessarily, even dangerously pollute good water.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/portland-rejects-fluoridationagain/', 'snippet': 'Opponents warned, despite scientific evidence, that fluoride would unnecessarily, even dangerously pollute good water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Portland, Oregon, has once again voted against adding fluoride to the city water supply — not, it seems, out of any love of cavities, but in response to a perceived threat to the city’s anti-establishment culture. At least that’s the view of one of those handy political science professors inevitably called upon to explain the inexplicable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portland Rejects Fluoridation—Again', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fluorides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T19:14:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e865cde8-676c-56c7-bfc3-78eb22dfe6fb', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e865cde8-676c-56c7-bfc3-78eb22dfe6fb'}, {'abstract': 'This year, the makeup theme among the guests at the annual amfAR Cinema Against AIDS gala was a soft, barely there face so naked you know it could only be pulled off with a proper pre-Cannes facial and body cleanse.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/classic-beauty-at-cannes-amfar/', 'snippet': 'This year, the makeup theme among the guests at the annual amfAR Cinema Against AIDS gala was a soft, barely there face so naked you know it could only be pulled off with a proper pre-Cannes facial and body cleanse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cannes is one of those film festivals where the glamor is as important as the films. Beside the carousel of screenings and red carpets, the big event is the annual amfAR Cinema Against AIDS gala. The attendees include a cross section of actors, artists, designers, models and socialites who offer a range of spring style and beauty inspirations. This year, the makeup theme among the guests was a soft, barely there face, so naked you know it could only be pulled off with a proper pre-Cannes facial and body cleanse. The only variation was a red lip. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping it Classic in Cannes', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'amfAR, The Foundation for AIDS Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T19:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/497e8dbf-1c8c-5933-a7a7-f316c7c6afcf', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/497e8dbf-1c8c-5933-a7a7-f316c7c6afcf'}, {'abstract': 'A five-bedroom Greenwich Colonial on just over an acre, and a four-bedroom in Westchester with lots of large windows and decks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/26/realestate/20130526-OTMREG.html', 'snippet': 'A five-bedroom Greenwich Colonial on just over an acre, and a four-bedroom in Westchester with lots of large windows and decks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A five-bedroom Greenwich Colonial on just over an acre, and a four-bedroom in Westchester with lots of large windows and decks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/realestate/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/realestate/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/realestate/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G/20130526-OTMREG-slide-PU4G-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'wi