ft on the Forbes list of the 30 most influential people under 30.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So What Will He Do When 20?', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So What Will He Do When 20?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tao, Conrad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17cabfac-16f7-5bc0-91b6-2a2b265c5b6a', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17cabfac-16f7-5bc0-91b6-2a2b265c5b6a'}, {'abstract': 'The king and queen of Belgium visit a festival in the port city of Ostend.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/maritime-treats-in-belgium/', 'snippet': 'The king and queen of Belgium visit a festival in the port city of Ostend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'King Albert II of Belgium samples smoked herring, as Queen Paola looks on, at a maritime festival in the port city of Ostend. The festival features exhibits of about 170 ships and various performances and food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maritime Treats in Belgium', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e8c322a-b7c5-52bc-83ec-476ac65430ce', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e8c322a-b7c5-52bc-83ec-476ac65430ce'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s first-ever store is opening in a two-story space on Avenue of the Americas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/garden/knoll-international-opening-a-retail-store.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s first-ever store is opening in a two-story space on Avenue of the Americas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an effort to become more accessible, Knoll International has opened its first retail store in its 75-year history. The shop, on the ground floor of the furniture company’s new corporate headquarters in New York, is a two-story space on Avenue of the Americas, around the corner from the Museum of Modern Art. It was designed by ARO, an architectural firm whose credits include the newly renovated Donald Judd Home and Studio. The architects used end-grain oak flooring and bright colors and fabrics to make the shop feel more like a living room. Illuminated lacquer shelving lines the back wall, taking advantage of the double-height space to display rows of chairs, including classics by Mies van der Rohe, Marcel Breuer and Eero Saarinen. For the official opening on June 13, Richard Schultz’s outdoor furniture will take center stage, and Mr. Schultz will be in the store from 4 to 7 p.m.to sign his Petal tables. Knoll will sell new designs as well, including Jonathan Olivares’s stackable, outdoor-friendly aluminum chairs. Fabrics from Knoll Textile’s Luxe line designed by Rodarte, Proenza Schouler and the company’s design director, Dorothy Cosonas, will be part of the mix, as will lush wool felt rugs by Filzfelt. The store is at 1330 Avenue of the Americas (54th Street); Information: (212) 343-4190 or knoll.com. ', 'sour