', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HENRI/0525HENRI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HENRI/0525HENRI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HENRI/0525HENRI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long Day’s Journey Toward Infinite Night', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Long Day’s Journey Toward Infinite Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ea7bac4-01dd-552e-b930-185e0cbab213', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ea7bac4-01dd-552e-b930-185e0cbab213'}, {'abstract': 'Jane Monheit is singing at Birdland, and her best performances on Tuesday evening were of familiar songs that she turned into heartfelt reflections on motherhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/arts/music/jane-monheit-at-birdland.html', 'snippet': 'Jane Monheit is singing at Birdland, and her best performances on Tuesday evening were of familiar songs that she turned into heartfelt reflections on motherhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well over a decade has passed since the sultry pop-jazz singer Jane Monheit, then in her early 20s, was greeted with the ecstatic hyperbole often accorded to vocal wunderkinder. My memories of Ms. Monheit in the early 2000s are of a phenomenally well-equipped singer wielding an instrument that made a wonderful sound but that left much to be desired when it came to interpreting lyrics. The beauty of her voice and her facility at decorative improvisation spoke for themselves. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reshaping Familiar Pop With a Maternal Caress', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reshaping Familiar Pop With a Maternal Caress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monheit, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4019cf1a-95d0-5b39-a613-fe2b277f6f56', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4019cf1a-95d0-5b39-a613-fe2b277f6f56'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural highlights from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/the-week-in-culture-pictures-may-25-2/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural highlights from this week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More photographs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/artsspecial/0525BEST-slide-GJZM/0525BEST-slide-GJZ