d977f245f9a', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab3490bb-dfb3-5d8d-bae5-1d977f245f9a'}, {'abstract': 'An introduction to the first guest columnist in the Meh List’s summer tour of The New York Times newsroom.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/brian-stelter-says-whats-meh/', 'snippet': 'An introduction to the first guest columnist in the Meh List’s summer tour of The New York Times newsroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past few months, we’ve been encouraging readers to submit suggestions to the Meh List, either on Twitter, via #mehlist, or by e-mailing me directly. I haven’t done an empirical analysis, but I’m pretty sure that the No. 1 suggestion is “The Meh List.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/meh-list-logo/meh-list-logo-jumbo.png', 'height': 133, 'width': 368, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/meh-list-logo/meh-list-logo-superJumbo.png', 'height': 133, 'width': 368, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/meh-list-logo/meh-list-logo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/meh-list-logo/meh-list-logo-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brian Stelter Says What’s Meh', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Henig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b77f812-61e7-529b-bc72-5c8fa6208881', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b77f812-61e7-529b-bc72-5c8fa6208881'}, {'abstract': 'The Porsche 911 may be turning 50, but it still carries its distinctive profile, and the engine remains an opposed 6-cylinder placed at the rear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/automobiles/collectibles/timeless-but-not-frozen-in-time.html', 'snippet': 'The Porsche 911 may be turning 50, but it still carries its distinctive profile, and the engine remains an opposed 6-cylinder placed at the rear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Admirers of the Porsche 911 would insist that no other model in the auto industry has stayed so true to its original formula, a production life span that is closing in on 50 years. Yes, the Chevrolet Corvette celebrates its 60th anniversary this year, but the muscle-bound 2013 version is hardly cut from the same cloth as Harley Earl’s tepid roadster of 1953.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/automobiles/Porsche3/Porsche3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/automobiles/Porsche3/Porsche3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/automobiles/Porsche3/Porsche3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/automobiles/Porsch