 Won’t Start New Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Horace Mann School', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f05aebc7-7640-5cdf-9a44-f3bdc308a001', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f05aebc7-7640-5cdf-9a44-f3bdc308a001'}, {'abstract': 'Lea Salonga sings standards at the Café Carlyle in a show that is partly a tribute to Barbra Streisand and Ella Fitzgerald.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/arts/music/lea-salonga-at-the-cafe-carlyle.html', 'snippet': 'Lea Salonga sings standards at the Café Carlyle in a show that is partly a tribute to Barbra Streisand and Ella Fitzgerald.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midway through her show on Wednesday night at the Café Carlyle, the Filipina singer Lea Salonga recalled being told not to bother auditioning for the role of Eliza Doolittle in a revival of “My Fair Lady” because she “wasn’t white.” Although her tone was one of calm indignation, you could feel an undertone of feistiness throughout the evening. Ms. Salonga is a performer whose formidable talent is matched by her unstoppable drive and keen intelligence. As Broadway divas go, she is a cut above most. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Serenely Indomitable, Whatever the Challenge', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Serenely Indomitable, Whatever the Challenge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salonga, Lea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/182810ed-be30-5e77-9f26-c057f1e5961c', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/182810ed-be30-5e77-9f26-c057f1e5961c'}, {'abstract': 'A reader reacts to an article on practicing yoga in middle age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/booming/twists-for-students-with-osteoporosis.html', 'snippet': 'A reader reacts to an article on practicing yoga in middle age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twists for Students With Osteoporosis', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T20:56:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materia