yes only),” the full version of a work presented in excerpt last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Darrell Jones’s “Hoo-Ha (for your eyes only),” three men wear headpieces with long ponytails that whirl like helicopter blades as heads roll. They wear jeans and sneakers and silver bangles that rattle as they toss their wrists about in voguing moves. They scatter rose petals. They simulate sex.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525HOOHA/0525HOOHA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voguing Moves, Rose Petals, Slap Fights and a Moaning Crescendo', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voguing Moves, Rose Petals, Slap Fights and a Moaning Crescendo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Darrell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danspace Project', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T21:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8684f495-4c99-5a35-b5f9-330e2be05701', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8684f495-4c99-5a35-b5f9-330e2be05701'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Maxwell Davies’s “Eight Songs for a Mad King” was a featured work at a show by Cantata Profana at Roulette on Wednesday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/arts/music/cantata-profana-at-roulette.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Maxwell Davies’s “Eight Songs for a Mad King” was a featured work at a show by Cantata Profana at Roulette on Wednesday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a common situation for any inquisitive musician: too much curiosity about disparate pieces and few opportunities to play them all within a single ensemble. Cantata Profana, formed this year by students from the Yale University School of Music and its Institute of Sacred Music, addresses that problem head-on. The group, which performed at Roulette in Brooklyn on Wednesday evening, cast its net impressively wide for its New York City debut, presenting both vocal and instrumental works, early music and modern fare.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/arts/0525PROFANA/0525PROFANA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mad King Stalks the Stage, Ready to Shock', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mad King Stalks the Stage, Ready to Shock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davies, Peter Maxwell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T21:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name