oon but to declare a mistrial in the penalty phase of the trial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistrial Set in Penalty for a Killer in Arizona', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mistrial Set In Penalty For a Killer In Arizona', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arias, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb3fdf4-0ccf-5f0c-a4ea-dbe667a4099f', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb3fdf4-0ccf-5f0c-a4ea-dbe667a4099f'}, {'abstract': 'The first of 350 additional Marine guards at high-risk embassies and consulates around the world later this year will cost about $1.6 million each.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/world/additional-embassy-guards-will-come-at-steep-price-each.html', 'snippet': 'The first of 350 additional Marine guards at high-risk embassies and consulates around the world later this year will cost about $1.6 million each.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When the State Department fields the first of 350 additional Marine security guards at high-risk embassies and consulates around the world later this year, the price tag will be steep: about $1.6 million per Marine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Additional Embassy Guards Will Come With a Steep Price', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Additional Embassy Guards Will Come With a Steep Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:23:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ffa8756-0723-5f86-8779-0fd52e17f1d8', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ffa8756-0723-5f86-8779-0fd52e17f1d8'}, {'abstract': 'No one can pinpoint exactly when and how the Love-15-30-40 scoring system came into play, though there are several theories, some ranked higher than others.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/quirks-of-the-game-how-tennis-got-its-scoring-system/', 'snippet': 'No one can pinpoint exactly when and how the Love-15-30-40 scoring system came into play, though there are several theories, some ranked higher than others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Billie Jean King was first learning about tennis, she said, her coach explained that the point system went, “15, then 30” at which point the eager and exuberant student proclaimed, “and then 45, right?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quirks of the Game: How Tennis Got Its Scoring System', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By STUART MILLER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MILLER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d26ce9a1-0177-5d74-84b8-1e6f0dd1c9f0', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d26ce9a1-0177-5d74-84b8-1e6f0dd1c9f0'}, {'abstract': 'Brokerage firms say that options, traditionally used by professional traders, can be profitable for ordinary investors, but this does not square with many investors’ experiences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/business/growth-in-options-trading-helps-brokers-but-not-small-investors.html', 'snippet': 'Brokerage firms say that options, traditionally used by professional traders, can be profitable for ordinary investors, but this does not square with many investors’ experiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the brokerage firms that helped pique American’s interest in stocks are now luring them into something much riskier: stock options. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/business/Options/Options-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/business/Options/Options-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/business/Options/Options-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/business/Options/Options-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1575, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Growth in Options Trading Helps Brokers but Not Small Investors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trading Options, but Not Keeping Up With the Pros', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Popper, Nathaniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charles Schwab Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E TRADE Financial Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TD Ameritrade Holding Corp.', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:36:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': No