rvivors.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Phillip Wise of the Bethany Police Department followed the tornado so he could pull survivors from the wreckage in Oklahoma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOORE, Okla. — Phillip Wise on Monday chased one of the most ferocious tornadoes to touch down in Oklahoma in years. Through his windshield from a half-mile out, the Category 5 twister was not so much a funnel but a shapeless, swirling wall of mud, pieces of homes, and airborne cars and horses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/us/MOORE/MOORE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Rescue Survivors, He Pursued the Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Rescue Survivors, He Pursued the Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moore (Okla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ef746ec-0c66-5e03-8ac1-8f6cafde0b59', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ef746ec-0c66-5e03-8ac1-8f6cafde0b59'}, {'abstract': 'The Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index has more than doubled since Barack Obama took office, an accomplishment achieved by only four other presidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/business/economy/sp-has-more-than-doubled-under-obama.html', 'snippet': 'The Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index has more than doubled since Barack Obama took office, an accomplishment achieved by only four other presidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the 84 years that the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index has been calculated, it doubled during the terms of only four presidents before Barack Obama’s election in 2008. This month that number rose to five as the index climbed to more than twice what it was when he took office. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Measured by S.&P. Returns, Obama Is on a Short List', 'kicker': 'Off The Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Measured by S.&P. Returns, Obama Is on a Short List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-24T23:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229864eb-b993-5b8b-9b3b-40e464d4c39a', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229864eb-b993-5b8b-9b3b-40e464d4c39a'}, {'abstract': 'Why did Confederates spend weeks salvaging a sunken Union ironclad in Charleston harbor?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/raiding-the-keokuk/', 'snippet': 'Why did Confederates spend weeks salvaging a sunken Union ironclad in Charleston harbor?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late on an April night in 1863 a flotilla of small boats circled a partially sunken ship off the coast of Morris Island, S.C., not far from Fort Sumter in Charleston Harbor. Soon two iron towers studded with bolts rose like islands from the dark waters. Onboard the ship, a Union ironclad called the Keokuk – sunk a few days before in the failed Union attempt to bombard Fort Sumter into submission – stood several men, silently waiting, their eyes on Adolphus W. LaCoste, the civilian in charge of the Confederate salvage operation. His hand raised, they held their breath as a Union picket boat rowed past, towards the lights of the blockading fleet. As the voices of the rowers faded, LaCoste gave the signal to resume. In water up to their waists, with hands and wrenches tugging and turning, they strained at the armored decks over the guns of the sunken ironclad. They had one thing in mind: the guns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raiding the Keokuk', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salvage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Sumter (SC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T00:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devin Poore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf77f6a4-c51e-5000-a10a-77cd305d4ff1', 'word_count': 1699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf77f6a4-c51e-5000-a10a-77cd305d4ff1'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/nyregion/events-in-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to ctcal@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Events in Connecticut', 'kicker': 'Calendar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli