in “Clybourne Park” for 50 years. And there it is, on Long Wharf Theater’s Mainstage — not at its best, because the owners are leaving and the living room is strewn with moving boxes. But look at all that space and the handsome wooden staircase and the door that leads to a real backyard. No wonder Lena Younger, the heroine of Lorraine Hansberry’s seminal 1959 drama “A Raisin in the Sun,” was so proud to be able to move her five-member family there, after living in a cramped two-bedroom apartment on the South Side of Chicago. To hell with the fact that everybody else in the neighborhood was white.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSCT1_SPAN/26ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 's