dge Finds Violations of Rights by Sheriff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Finds Violations Of Rights By Sheriff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARPAIO, JOSEPH M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maricopa County (Ariz)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd99390-7bf1-5b1a-8042-043fbf379a91', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd99390-7bf1-5b1a-8042-043fbf379a91'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans are trying to restrict vital information with bills that would curtail and ban surveys by the Census Bureau.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/opinion/strategic-ignorance-and-the-census.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans are trying to restrict vital information with bills that would curtail and ban surveys by the Census Bureau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an age when knowledge is power, restricting knowledge is a power grab, creating the conditions of ignorance that allow bias, ideology and propaganda to flourish, unchallenged and unchecked. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strategic Ignorance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strategic Ignorance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poe, Ted', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Jeffrey D', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/087940b5-54ed-55e0-8c86-15ea60eaaef4', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087940b5-54ed-55e0-8c86-15ea60eaaef4'}, {'abstract': 'New York City rightly prohibits the use of public schools for regular religious services. The City Council wants to change that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/opinion/get-churches-out-of-public-schools.html', 'snippet': 'New York City rightly prohibits the use of public schools for regular religious services. The City Council wants to change that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City prohibits the use of public school facilities for regular religious services. That policy makes sense for buildings that are used and maintained by taxpayers. But the City Council wants to eliminate that policy through a new state law. It voted 38 to 11 on Wednesday to pass a resolution asking the Legislature and Gov. Andrew Cuomo to approve legislation to permit religious services on public school properties when they are not in use.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Churches Out of Public Schools', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Churches Out of Public Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ede592c-44f3-543b-8450-cbd2a11ef874', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ede592c-44f3-543b-8450-cbd2a11ef874'}, {'abstract': 'Many senators who opposed better scrutiny for weapons buyers try to pretend the opposite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/opinion/deception-on-gun-background-checks.html', 'snippet': 'Many senators who opposed better scrutiny for weapons buyers try to pretend the opposite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A strange thing happened after 45 senators killed a bill to expand background checks for gun buyers five weeks ago: many of those same senators suddenly discovered a profound affection for background checks. They had been for them all along, it turns out, and wanted nothing more than to keep guns out of the hands of felons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deception on Gun Background Checks', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deception on Gun Background Checks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Dean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayotte, Kelly A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mayors Against Illegal Guns', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flake, Jeffrey L', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/805b8b9d-6422-54b0-a216-af128d2b1353', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/805b8b9d-6422-54b0-a216-af128d2b1353'}, {'abstract': 'Physical activity should be a core educational concern, not a dispensable option.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/opinion/exercise-and-academic-performance.html', 'snippet': 'Physical activity should be a core educational concern, not a dispensable option.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As schools everywhere strive to improve the academic performance of their students, many have cut physical education and recess periods to leave more time for sedentary classroom instruction. A sensible new report from the Institute of Medicine, a unit of the National Academy of Sciences, shows how shortsighted this trend can be. It found that exercise can significantly improve children’s cognitive abilities and their academic performance, as well as their health. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exercise and Academic Performance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exercise and Academic Performance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physical Education and Training', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:26:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3fc5e3-f3f2-5c53-bb7b-bab89a16ff8e', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3fc5e3-f3f2-5c53-bb7b-bab89a16ff8e'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan McDonagh, an emerging offensive threat, led the Rangers’ skaters in ice time in Game 4 and had a larger role on the power play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/sports/hockey/ryan-mcdonagh-does-it-all-for-rangers.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan McDonagh, an emerging offensive threat, led the Rangers’ skaters in ice time in Game 4 and had a larger role on the power play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — A potential solution to the Rangers’ power-play woes surfaced in Game 4 against the Boston Bruins, and Coach John Tortorella only wished he had thought of it earlier. After all, it seemed so obvious.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/sports/y-RANGERS/y-RANGERS-thumbLarge.