ercrowded Syrian refugee camp in Jordan for the United Nations, is a ruddy-faced German who thrives in international disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZAATARI, Jordan — Kilian Kleinschmidt had a problem. The afternoon before Kuwait’s ambassador to Jordan was scheduled to visit the overcrowded Syrian refugee camp here, children vandalized mobile homes that Kuwait had donated, stealing windows, doors and floor mats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calm Boss Overseeing a Syrian Refugee Camp’s Chaos', 'kicker': 'The Saturday Profile', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calm Boss Overseeing a Syrian Refugee Camp’s Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kleinschmidt, Kilian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T01:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Biography', '_id': 'nyt://article/89ac6f28-d5e0-59ca-9e17-a768a6a88000', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89ac6f28-d5e0-59ca-9e17-a768a6a88000'}, {'abstract': 'A replica of a Shinnecock village at the Shinnecock Nation Cultural Center and Museum is intended to give visitors the sense that they are stepping inside an indigenous community of centuries ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/nyregion/building-a-traditional-village-at-shinnecock-nation-cultural-center-and-museum.html', 'snippet': 'A replica of a Shinnecock village at the Shinnecock Nation Cultural Center and Museum is intended to give visitors the sense that they are stepping inside an indigenous community of centuries ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent afternoon, Jason Johnson, clad in buckskin leggings, a breechcloth and a headdress of turkey feathers, was tending a fire and stripping the bark from tupelo logs in a wooded, two-acre plot behind the Shinnecock Nation Cultural Center and Museum in Southampton.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSLI1/26ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSLI1/26ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSLI1/26ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSLI1/26ARTSLI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ARTSLI1/26ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/