y You” involves a face-off with New York characters flaunting unappealing values and a sense of entitlement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/theater/reviews/i-wanna-destroy-you-at-the-beckett-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Joshua Conkel’s comedy “I Wanna Destroy You” involves a face-off with New York characters flaunting unappealing values and a sense of entitlement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mick is sick of the city. He misses lightning bugs and children on lawns and driving. And the New Yorkers in Joshua Conkel’s comedy “I Wanna Destroy You” are so hideous that you almost have to agree with him.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They’re Tan and Toned, but They’re Not Very Nice', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’re Tan And Toned, But They’re Not Very Nice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Anita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'At Hand Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conkel, Joshua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T02:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2818f45a-6a75-5fc3-b6ce-5f282b6b616a', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2818f45a-6a75-5fc3-b6ce-5f282b6b616a'}, {'abstract': 'David Steinberg truly makes this puzzle his own.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/24/irreverent-sermonettes/', 'snippet': 'David Steinberg truly makes this puzzle his own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — I don’t believe I’ve had an easier and more fun entry into a Saturday puzzle in, well, ever. PURPLE HAZE is “all in my brain,” and even if you were never a fan of Jimi Hendrix, I’m sure you know this classic rock song. It was enough to get me rocking and laughing at one of my favorite clue/entry pairings in a long time: a “labor leader’s cry” might be “PUSH!” and if you’re like me, the response is likely to be to grab the labor leader by the collar and shriek “Shut up!  More ice chips!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irreverent Sermonettes', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T02:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/483edb4f-804c-5015-ad12-804e78ae7eff', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/483edb4f-804c-5015-ad12-804e78ae7eff'}, {'abstract': 'A vote by Senator Frank R. Lautenberg for a failed control gun bill gained him allies for the first credible bill in years to revamp the nation’s outmoded chemical safety law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/us/politics/lautenbergs-chemical-safety-bill-gains-momentum.html', 'snippet': 'A vote by Senator Frank R. Lautenberg for a failed control gun bill gained him allies for the first credible bill in years to revamp the nation’s outmoded chemical safety law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The first credible effort in years to revamp the nation’s outmoded chemical safety law grew in part from the Sen