ount': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc1312e-c5f3-5fb3-9f02-9c20978e4d12'}, {'abstract': 'If true, Mokhtar Belmokhtar’s claim would put one of the Sahel’s most hardened militants, whom Chad’s military said it had killed, back at the center of jihad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/world/africa/militant-says-he-is-behind-fatal-niger-attack.html', 'snippet': 'If true, Mokhtar Belmokhtar’s claim would put one of the Sahel’s most hardened militants, whom Chad’s military said it had killed, back at the center of jihad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — Mokhtar Belmokhtar, the mastermind of the January seizure of an Algerian gas plant that left dozens of foreign hostages dead, has claimed responsibility for another terrorist attack: the suicide bombings on Thursday in Niger that killed about 30 people, including 24 soldiers and at least six jihadists. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Militant Says He Is Behind Attack in Niger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militant Says He Is Behind Attack in Niger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belmokhtar, Mokhtar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chad', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sahara Desert', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T03:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/181b726a-ac22-5b1f-b404-764b52c59b94', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/181b726a-ac22-5b1f-b404-764b52c59b94'}, {'abstract': 'Marianna Scandole takes care of passengers on the Hampton Jitney and the Hampton Ambassador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/nyregion/marianna-scandole-is-a-host-on-the-hampton-jitney.html', 'snippet': 'Marianna Scandole takes care of passengers on the Hampton Jitney and the Hampton Ambassador.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people go to great lengths to avoid getting stuck in Long Island beach traffic. Marianna Scandole does it for a living. Ms. Scandole, 26, is a host on the Hampton Jitney and the Hampton Ambassador, which carry lower- and higher-paying passengers through some of the region’s most illustrious clogged arteries. For Ms. Scandole, who previously worked as a nanny, the job is something of a career trial balloon. “I want to become a flight attendant, so I thought that would be an excellent way to get some practice in,” she said. She lives with her mother and younger sister in Hampton Bays.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE3/26ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE3/26ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/nyregion/26