otation-of-the-day-for-saturday-may-25-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Saturday, May 25, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We like to believe in Brazil that we live in a peaceful, happy place, when the truth of our existence is far more complicated. It’s like we’re Narcissus gazing into a pool of sewage.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, May 25, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T03:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/def44b54-6cb4-5b2a-9a06-600a19b5eb1f', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def44b54-6cb4-5b2a-9a06-600a19b5eb1f'}, {'abstract': 'An affidavit details what information the United States government gathered from conversations between Stephen Jin-Woo Kim, a government employee, and an unnamed journalist believed to be James Rosen, the chief Washington correspondent for Fox News.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/25/us/politics/james-rosen-affidavit.html', 'snippet': 'An affidavit details what information the United States government gathered from conversations between Stephen Jin-Woo Kim, a government employee, and an unnamed journalist believed to be James Rosen, the chief Washington correspondent for Fox New...', 'lead_paragraph': 'An affidavit details what information the United States government gathered from conversations between Stephen Jin-Woo Kim, a government employee, and an unnamed journalist believed to be James Rosen, the chief Washington correspondent for Fox News.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Application and Affidavit for Rosen Search Warr