p into a tournament can be much tougher to spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is easy to spot the players coming into a Grand Slam tournament with a head of steam, arriving in Paris with an impressive roster of victories that make them ones to watch at the tournament. For this year’s French Open, players like Benoit Paire, Grigor Dimitrov, Simona Halep and Bethanie Mattek-Sands would easily fit into that category, among others.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Players Not to Watch at Roland Garros', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Names Do Not Always Equal Big Plays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartoli, Marion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benneteau, Julien', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paszek, Tamira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radwanska, Agnieszka', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tipsarevic, Janko', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wozniacki, Caroline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe63ab8d-eb99-58d7-828e-9635bd7dd281', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe63ab8d-eb99-58d7-828e-9635bd7dd281'}, {'abstract': 'An Apple-1 computer, made in 1976 and originally priced at $666, sold for a record $671,400 at an auction in Germany. The sale shows the run-up in prices for t