rge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vintage Apple-1 Sells for Record $671,400', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c5560b5-4562-59a6-aef4-8c548d9b95cf', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c5560b5-4562-59a6-aef4-8c548d9b95cf'}, {'abstract': 'Austerity isn’t the only problem — but so what?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/europes-keynesian-problem/', 'snippet': 'Austerity isn’t the only problem — but so what?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong tries to find nice things to say about Ken Rogoff’s latest. But he tries too hard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Keynesian Problem', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9174a4f1-07df-5f26-9e98-b7f4186581eb', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9174a4f1-07df-5f26-9e98-b7f4186581eb'}, {'abstract': 'A band of House Republicans ignores good news on energy use and sticks to scare tactics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/the-oil-extremists.html', 'snippet': 'A band of House Republicans ignores good news on energy use and sticks to scare tactics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal Energy Information Administration reported in March that at some point this year — maybe in the fall, maybe next month, maybe tomorrow — United States crude oil production will surpass imports for the first time since 1995. This is an important milestone. It does not mean that America has reached energy independence, not by a long shot. That is and will remain an elusive dream for a country that uses one-fifth of the world’s oil while possessing little more than one-fiftieth of its reserves.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Oil Extremists', 'kicker': 'Editiorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Oil Extremists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastings, Doc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Natural Resources Committee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'National Petroleum Reserve (Alaska)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert B. Semple Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ff257cd-e77b-5994-bc39-7c5924032f48', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ff257cd-e77b-5994-bc39-7c5924032f48'}, {'abstract': 'A new federal study shows that too many prisons and jails tolerate sexual abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/rape-behind-bars.html', 'snippet': 'A new federal study shows that too many prisons and jails tolerate sexual abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new federal report shows that the nation’s prisons and jails have a long way to go before they comply with the Prison Rape Elimination Act. That 2003 law requires institutions receiving federal money to adopt a zero-tolerance policy on rape and to embrace rigorous prevention measures like those outlined last year by the Justice Department. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rape Behind Bars', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rape Behind Bars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Justice Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/22b6ddf6-ccb4-5382-b815-5531c739fe34', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22b6ddf6-ccb4-5382-b815-5531c739fe34'}, {'abstract': 'Apple is the latest example of how American multinationals avoid taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/a-is-for-avoidance.html', 'snippet': 'Apple is the latest example of how American multinationals avoid taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before last week’s Senate hearing on Apple, it was clear that the aggressive use of tax havens and other tax avoidance tactics had become standard operating procedure for global American companies. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘A’ Is for Avoidance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘A’ Is for Avoidance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Shelters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6e99bb-fdfb-5e32-b615-93d7ac98bda4', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6e99bb-fdfb-5e32-b615-93d7ac98bda4'}, {'abstract': 'Before adopting punitive measures to fight against hackers, the two nations need to try working together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/preventing-a-us-china-cyberwar.html', 'snippet': 'Before adopting punitive measures to fight against hackers, the two nations need to try working together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President Obama and President Xi Jinping of China have their first meeting next month in California, addressing the issue of China’s cyberattacks on American institutions will be an important priority. Both nations need to take steps to avoid drifting into an all-out cyberwar. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preventing a U.S.-China Cyberwar', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preventing a U.S.-China Cyberwar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T14:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf144c99-00a1-5326-9f0d-b672de7439b3', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf144c99-00a1-5326-9f0d-b672de7439b3'}, {'abstract': 'A hunting trophy follows a family everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/the-deer-on-the-wall.html', 'snippet': 'A hunting trophy follows a family everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little more than 60 years ago, when he was still a young man, my dad shot a mule deer while hunting in northwestern Colorado. Like so may things in his early life