d_paragraph': 'Kevin Towers was scouting for the Yankees in 2010 when a trade got his attention. The Arizona Diamondbacks, spiraling toward a last-place finish in the National League West, dealt pitcher Dan Haren, a three-time All-Star, to the Los Angeles Angels for a package that included two promising left-handers in Class A.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sports/dog-bases/dog-bases-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Late Start in the Sport, Brilliant Start to a Career', 'kicker': 'Extra Bases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Late Start in the Sport, Brilliant Start to a Career', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbin, Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T15:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb8aae7c-b074-59ee-90ba-0f0319af946c', 'word_count': 1604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb8aae7c-b074-59ee-90ba-0f0319af946c'}, {'abstract': 'Dario Franchitti, the defending champion at the Indianapolis 500, would get a record-tying fourth career victory if he wins Sunday’s race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/sports/autoracing/dario-franchitti-aims-for-history-at-indy-500.html', 'snippet': 'Dario Franchitti, the defending champion at the Indianapolis 500, would get a record-tying fourth career victory if he wins Sunday’s race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — The lights from a photo shoot had dimmed, but the gleam in Dario Franchitti’s eyes remained. The five-foot sterling silver Borg-Warner trophy stood before him, the history of the Indianapolis 500 told through the miniature busts of each year’s winner carved into its side. Franchitti, a Scot, traced the years with his fingers and found his countryman Jim Clark, the 1965 winner. He scanned for Ray Harroun, the 1911 winner. Then, near the bottom of the trophy, he settled on his own face — or, rather, the three of them. ', 'print_s