modesty, has raised morale, observers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — He has criticized the “cult of money” and greed he sees driving the world financial system, reflecting his affinity for liberation theology. He has left Vatican officials struggling to keep up with his off-the-cuff remarks and impromptu forays into the crowds of tens of thousands that fill St. Peter’s Square during his audiences. He has delighted souvenir vendors near the Vatican by increasing tourist traffic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Francis’ Humility and Emphasis on the Poor Strike a New Tone at the Vatican', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Francis’ Humility and Emphasis on the Poor Strike a New Tone at the Vatican', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T18:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc256635-d6f8-5d6f-9efa-efdeb38fc0c7', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc256635-d6f8-5d6f-9efa-efdeb38fc0c7'}, {'abstract': 'Environmentalists are worried that a wind-energy project near the Mojave Desert could affect the fragile condor population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/us/turbine-plans-unnerve-fans-of-condors-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'Environmentalists are worried that a wind-energy project near the Mojave Desert could affect the fragile condor population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The California condor’s slow 20-year climb back from the brink of extinction has long been a fragile not-quite-success story in the conservation world. So when the news came on Friday that developers of a wind-energy project near the Mojave Desert would not face criminal charges if the blades killed a single condor, environmental groups expressed grave concern.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turbine Plans Unnerve Fans of Condors in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turbine Plans Unnerve Fans of Condors in California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barringer, Felicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T18:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7d2dfe8-fe9b-58a0-a675-65b8ce6617c8', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7d2dfe8-fe9b-58a0-a675-65b8ce6617c8'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge excoriated Joe Arpaio for illegally using race as a factor in neighborhood sweeps and traffic stops.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/arizonas-illegal-sheriff/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge excoriated Joe Arpaio for illegally using race as a factor in neighborhood sweeps and traffic stops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do we know that Joe Arpaio, sheriff of Maricopa County, Ariz., is a racial profiler, an abuser of power who has subjected Latinos for years to unconstitutional arrests, detention and harassment?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona’s Illegal Sheriff', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T19:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c210506e-9530-56c4-8832-bbda4b852504', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c210506e-9530-56c4-8832-bbda4b852504'}, {'abstract': 'Community gardens for immigrant groups can provide familiar foods that are hard to find in the grocery store. They can also be a balm for alienation and depression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/us/in-california-gardening-for-mental-health.html', 'snippet': 'Community gardens for immigrant groups can provide familiar foods that are hard to find in the grocery store. They can also be a balm for alienation and depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRESNO, Calif. — Like Scotch broom and dandelions, despair can be invasive. This is why, every Monday, Lee Lee, a Hmong refugee, puts on her sun hat and flip-flops, grabs the hoe handmade by her father and brother in Laos and heads to the Hmong Village Community Garden here, where she tends rows of purple lemon grass, bitter melon and medicinal herbs along with other Hmong women.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Serenity in a Patch of California Land', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking Serenity in a Patch of Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Patricia Leigh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'