c85d-d005-5e1f-9768-b9db2612508f'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of focusing on what is said to be their central challenge — how to share this land with another nation — Israelis are largely ignoring it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/sunday-review/what-mideast-crisis-israelis-have-moved-on.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of focusing on what is said to be their central challenge — how to share this land with another nation — Israelis are largely ignoring it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR years, conventional wisdom has held that as long as Israel faces the external challenge of Arab — especially Palestinian — hostility it will never come to terms with its internal divisions. The left has sometimes used it as an argument: we must make peace with the Palestinians so that we can set our house in order — write a constitution, figure out the public role of religion. Others have viewed the threat as almost a silver lining keeping the place together: differences among Israeli Jews (religious or secular, Ashkenazic or Sephardic) are so profound, the argument goes, that if the society ever manages to turn its attention inward, it might tear itself apart.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1505, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/sunday-review/26ISRAEL/26ISRAEL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Mideast Crisis? Israelis Have Moved On', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Mideast Crisis? Israelis Have Moved On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronner, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapid, Yair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yesh Atid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T19:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ac37a69-91fe-5262-a76e-f3a67d521ce7', 'word_count': 1270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ac37a69-91fe-5262-a76e-f3a67d521ce7'}, {'abstract': 'The two men have been portrayed by prosecutors as the masterminds behind the covert operations during the 1990s wars in Bosnia and Croatia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/world/europe/verdicts-expected-for-heads-of-milosevics-secret-police.html', 'snippet': 'The two men have been portrayed by prosecutors as the masterminds behind the covert operations during the 1990s wars in Bosnia and Croatia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — He was the president’s man for all seasons, prosecutors said, ready to organize hit squads, permit the killing of prisoners, sign off on covert weapon shipments or mediate the release of peacekeepers. Jovica Stanisic, the onetime chief of the secret police, was widely thought to be the second most powerful man in Serbia during Slobodan Milosevic’s presidency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1466, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Verdicts Expected Soon for 2 Milosevic Agents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Verdicts Expected Soon For 2 Milosevic Agents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yugoslavia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milosevic, Slobodan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simatovic, Franko', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanisic, Jovica', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T20:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a113e8a-02fb-5408-b787-0b0db92aaa89', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a113e8a-02fb-5408-b787-0b0db92aaa89'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s speech on national security and the recovery from last week’s tornado in Oklahoma are the focus of the Sunday shows.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/sunday-breakfast-menu-may-26/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s speech on national security and the recovery from last week’s tornado in Oklahoma are the focus of the Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still echoing through Washington, President Obama’s speech Thursday on shifting the nation’s approach to counterterrorism will be up for debate on the Sunday shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, May 26', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T20:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44dfdcf8-802c-5c08-964c-ee967bff8011', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44dfdcf8-802c-5c08-964c-ee967bff8011'}, {'abstract': 'Mata Amritanandamayi, known as Amma, is a globe-trotting guru who embraces the masses — and a get-it-done management style for her charities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/business/ammas-multifaceted-empire-built-on-hugs.html', 'snippet': 'Mata Amritanandamayi, known as Amma, is a globe-trotting guru who embraces the masses — and a get-it-done management style for her charities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are entourages — and then there is the retinue of Mata Amritanandamayi, a 59-year-old Indian guru known simply as Amma, or “mother.” On Friday, she began a two-month North American tour during which she will be accompanied by 275 volunteers. They plan to ride in four buses across the continent from Bellevue, Wash., to Marlborough, Mass., visiting 11 cities, including New York. And at each stop along the way, Amma will sit on stage for 15 hours at a stretch, greeting her thousands of devotees. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/business/26-AMMA/26-AMMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amma’s Multifaceted Empire, Built on Hugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Empire Built on Hugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amritanandamayi, Mata', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halpern, Jake', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kerala (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amrita University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MA Center', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T20:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Halpern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halpern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c549fa6-af32-53ae-8e97-7b84216d1421', 'word_count': 4088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c549fa6-af32-53ae-8e97-7b84216d1421'}, {'abstract': 'Much of our produce is relatively low in phytonutrients — compounds that may reduce the risk of many diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/opinion/sunday/breeding-the-nutrition-out-of-our-food.html', 'snippet': 'Much of our produce is relatively low in phytonutrients — compounds that may reduce the risk of many diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE like the idea that food can be the answer to our ills, that if we eat nutritious foods we won’t need medicine or supplements. We have valued this notion for a long, long time. The Greek physician Hippocrates proclaimed nearly 2,500 years ago: “Let food be thy medicine and medicine be thy food.” Today, medical experts concur. If we heap our plates with fresh fruits and vegetables, they tell us, we will come closer to optimum health.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'su