perJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/opinion/corn-img/corn-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 466, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/opinion/corn-img/corn-img-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/25/opinion/corn-img/corn-img-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/25/opinion/corn-img/corn-img-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nutritional Weaklings in the Supermarket', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lettuce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blueberries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carrots', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T21:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e5b35c37-308e-5bd8-86d1-5e7dea9c18f5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e5b35c37-308e-5bd8-86d1-5e7dea9c18f5'}, {'abstract': 'Joon Pahk and Jeremy Horwitz produce some large grid, small screen entertainment for us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/25/made-for-tv-movies/', 'snippet': 'Joon Pahk and Jeremy Horwitz produce some large grid, small screen entertainment for us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — There was a time after I had my kids when I thought I would never get out to the theaters to see a movie again, at least not one that didn’t involve Pokemon. The Boy was not big on sitting for long periods of time, even with his small lap loaded with candy, so very often The Girl was left to watch a large portion of the movie by herself while I chased The Boy up the aisle and out into the lobby. Now that they’re older, of course, things are different and they are much more likely to chase me up the aisle as I stomp out (“What?! Bruce Willis was dead all along?? What the heck is that?! I want my money back!”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Made-for-TV Movies', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-25T22:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/125f17c7-eb6a-5c45-a55a-b3002c88f962', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/125f17c7-eb6a-5c45-a55a-b3002c88f962'}, {'abstract': 'In India, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh’s reticence was once considered a sign of integrity; now it is being seen as a weakness as corruption scandals shake his party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/26/world/asia/india-grows-impatient-with-prime-minister-singh.html', 'snippet': 'In India, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh’s reticence was once considered a sign of integrity; now it is being seen as a weakness as corruption scandals shake his party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — He speaks so softly that even his public comments are sometimes nearly inaudible. He has not held a formal news conference in India since 2011. And a pack of reporters were driven to hold a protest recently when he refused to participate in the routine political act of being photographed while filing for re-election in Assam State.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/26/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub