e}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/feee43d8-c32f-5000-8d90-0cf0e8ed27f4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/feee43d8-c32f-5000-8d90-0cf0e8ed27f4'}, {'abstract': 'In the new Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, hoarding is now defined as a distinct disorder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/health/understanding-hoarding.html', 'snippet': 'In the new Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, hoarding is now defined as a distinct disorder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hoarding was once considered a type of obsessive compulsive disorder, but studies have shown that only 20 percent of people who hoard also have O.C.D. Some 50 percent of hoarders, however, suffer from major depression. In the new Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, hoarding is now defined as distinct disorder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Understanding Hoarding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Understanding Hoarding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoarding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T01:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9ea5804-e848-5c12-8253-d00714ab1fef', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9ea5804-e848-5c12-8253-d00714ab1fef'}, {'abstract': 'With 3 to 5 percent of Americans suffering from hoarding, local officials are trying to address the multidimensional aspects of the behavior and reduce its threat to others.', 'web_url': 'https