sts show up to protest, some are beaten by gay-bashers, and the next year they show up again – just to prove that they will keep showing up.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/moscows-gay-bashing-ritual/', 'snippet': 'L.G.B.T. activists show up to protest, some are beaten by gay-bashers, and the next year they show up again – just to prove that they will keep showing up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — I arrived at the edge of Gorky Park as one arrives on a red carpet: A score of photographers surrounded me and started clicking away. I was the first person to show up for an L.G.B.T. rally scheduled for 5 p.m. Saturday, one of three pride events held in the city that day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moscow’s Gay-Bashing Ritual', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T11:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56b4fee3-655b-59dc-9b13-ee0e9895f0d9', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56b4fee3-655b-59dc-9b13-ee0e9895f0d9'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor of Osaka’s statement about wartime brothels is either ignorant, naive or deliberately misleading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/opinion/global/japans-wartime-brothels.html', 'snippet': 'The mayor of Osaka’s statement about wartime brothels is either ignorant, naive or deliberately misleading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The statement earlier this month by Toru Hashimoto, mayor of Osaka, that brothels established by the Japanese Army in occupied territories during World War II were necessary to relieve war-crazed soldiers is either ignorant, naive or deliberately misleading. It is a fact that across Asia, Japan’s soldiers and officers “relieved themselves” by systematic rape of the civilian population.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s wartime brothels', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T12:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a152f723-9cde-5104-8fc5-ef55702a1cce', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a152f723-9cde-5104-8fc5-ef55702a1cce'}, {'abstract': 'A glimpse of how people across India are trying to beat the heat.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/braving-the-indian-heat/', 'snippet': 'A glimpse of how people across India are trying to beat the heat.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Braving the Indian Heat', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': 