ltimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blake Is Reflective After First-Round Loss', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blake, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Troicki, Viktor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T15:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f386be6-72d3-5ba2-bc5e-6831c8ea1b35', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f386be6-72d3-5ba2-bc5e-6831c8ea1b35'}, {'abstract': 'When I look at the images after a national tragedy, I see the children’s faces — terrified, shocked, changed. I know what that feels like.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/remembering-a-childs-grief/', 'snippet': 'When I look at the images after a national tragedy, I see the children’s faces — terrified, shocked, changed. I know what that feels like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each time I catch a glimpse of chilling footage from the recent tragedies in this country (the Newtown shootings, the Boston bombings and, now, the Oklahoma tornado), I find myself looking at the children in the images — terrified, shocked, changed. I see their faces when I close my eyes to sleep at night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering a Child’s Grief', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'