'_id': 'nyt://article/4e20995e-bcc8-51f7-8724-ae4b28ae2d25', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e20995e-bcc8-51f7-8724-ae4b28ae2d25'}, {'abstract': '“Many in my generation resent the inconveniences of aging, injury and illness and regard them as if they are optional,” writes the author. “This is delusional, but there you go.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/booming/for-a-boomer-sunblocks-came-late-and-cancer-too-soon.html', 'snippet': '“Many in my generation resent the inconveniences of aging, injury and illness and regard them as if they are optional,” writes the author. “This is delusional, but there you go.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In retrospect, I should have taken a last look at the nose I was born with. This was on the first Wednesday of November in 2011, the day of a scheduled appointment with a dermatological surgeon for Mohs micrographic surgery, the purpose of which was to carefully remove some previously discovered skin cancer from the lower left side of my nose. But it was also the fourth day after a surprise autumn snowstorm that had left our home in north central Connecticut without heat or electricity and the surrounding landscape devastated by thousands of fallen trees. On the morning of my procedure I washed my hair and sponged my body with a few quarts of water heated in a stockpot on a gas barbecue grill outside the house, threw on some clothes and rushed out the door. The entire exercise felt like an inconvenience. Looking back, taking proper care of my freckled, reddish skin, descended from somewhere on the moors of Ireland, had always felt like an inconvenience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/27/booming/27mystory-booming-cancer-span/27mystory-booming-cancer-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Boomer,  Sunscreens Came Late and Cancer Too Soon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T20:41:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Layden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Layden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff8d3e5-86d3-5ef8-8aca-9d672357ee0f', 'word_count': 2390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff8d3e5-86d3-5ef8-8aca-9d672357ee0f'}, {'abstract': 'The Royal Ballet in London commissioned a fairy tale as the basis of “Raven Girl,” a new work by Wayne McGregor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/arts/dance/raven-girl-a-wayne-mcgregor-ballet-premiere-in-london.html', 'snippet': 'The Royal Ballet in London commissioned a fairy tale as the basis of “Raven Girl,” a new work by Wayne McGregor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Fairy tales and myth are central to ballet. A woman turned into a swan by an evil magician; a sylph who falls in love with a human and finds the consequence is death; a girl who dies of a broken heart but is transformed into a ghostly spirit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/MCGREGOR/MCGREGOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/MCGREGOR/MCGREGOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 877}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/MCGREGOR/MCGREGOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 701, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/MCGREGOR/MCGREGOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 