raph': '“I will not be a victim of romance,” Laura Marling declares near the start of her magnificent new album, “Once I Was an Eagle” (Ribbon Music). That doesn’t stop her from plunging into it. In her new songs, love is combative, tempting, cruel, inscrutable, predatory and yet, occasionally, a comfort, with music to match every change of heart and mind. “Once I Was an Eagle” is the fourth album by this 23-year-old British songwriter, and her ambitions continue to grow.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/arts/jpnewmusic1/jpnewmusic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su