ject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ilaria, Giuseppe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedetto, Massimiliano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T23:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cafc7a0e-a628-5811-933a-19410ba2285d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cafc7a0e-a628-5811-933a-19410ba2285d'}, {'abstract': 'Fewer resources, lack of interest and the Internet have led to fewer high school newspapers in the city’s public schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/nyregion/at-school-papers-the-ink-is-drying-up.html', 'snippet': 'Fewer resources, lack of interest and the Internet have led to fewer high school newspapers in the city’s public schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Clinton News used to be the source for everything that mattered to its readers in the northwest Bronx. It published 10,000 copies every other week in the 1930s and even circulated overseas among Bronx residents fighting in World War II.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/nyregion/PAPERS1/PAPERS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At School Papers, the Ink Is Drying Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At School Papers, the Ink Is Drying Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu, Winnie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dewitt Clinton High School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T23:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/158336db-9dcc-59c6-9ae2-0fa9b4d75db5', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/158336db-9dcc-59c6-9ae2-0fa9b4d75db5'}, {'abstract': 'Grigor Dimitrov, a 21-year-old Bulgarian, defeated Novak Djokovic in Madrid and took Rafael Nadal to three sets in Monte Carlo.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/improving-dimitrov-knows-expectations-are-higher-at-french-open/', 'snippet': 'Grigor Dimitrov, a 21-year-old Bulgarian, defeated Novak Djokovic in Madrid and took Rafael Nadal to three sets in Monte Carlo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Grigor Dimitrov whistles as he recalls a particularly tough session of training last December. Having spent his teenage years at the Mouratoglou Academy in Paris, Dimitrov, a stylish Bulgarian, made the decision to break out of his comfort zone at the end of 2012, uprooting to the rather more chilly environment of Bromma, a suburb in western Stockholm. His goal? To join forces with the former world No. 2 Magnus Norman, the man he felt could help him make the transition from promising youngster to genuine world beater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Improving Dimitrov Knows Expectations Are Higher at French Open', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimitrov, Grigor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Magnus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T23:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3390f35-46c4-586e-85e4-42c87f9428eb', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3390f35-46c4-586e-85e4-42c87f9428eb'}, {'abstract': 'The businesspeople who gave the $27 million, 136-foot yacht to King Juan Carlos of Spain 13 years ago want him to return it rather than give it to the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/world/europe/king-of-spain-gives-up-yacht-but-donors-want-it-back.html', 'snippet': 'The businesspeople who gave the $27 million, 136-foot yacht to King Juan Carlos of Spain 13 years ago want him to return it rather than give it to the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — In hard times like these, everyone has to make sacrifices. And King Juan Carlos of Spain wanted it known that he was doing his part, too. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'King Gives Up Royal Yacht, but Donors Want It Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King Gives Up Royal Yacht, But Donors Want It Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juan Carlos I, King of Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Majorca (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-27T23:36:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a91e9171-f92c-5e19-b70f-025a17ed719c', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a91e9171-f92c-5e19-b70f-025a17ed719c'}, {'abstract': 'The Heat scored 70 points in the first half — including 18 by LeBron James while he played in the post — in easily winning Game 3 Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/sports/basketball/pacers-defense-looks-to-reassert-itself-in-game-4.html', 'snippet': 'The Heat scored 70 points in the first half — including 18 by LeBron James while he played in the post — in easily winning Game 3 Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — The Pacers like to call themselves a defensive-minded team, and the numbers bear them out. The Pacers led the N.B.A. during the regular season in opponents’ field-goal percentage (.420) and 3-point field-goal percentage (.327), and were second to Memphis in points allowed (90.7). ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 681}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1804, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/28/sports/28EAST-1/28EAST-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 