 primary schedule and not bring back the old lever-based machines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/opinion/clunker-voting-machines-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The Board of Elections needs to come up with some other solution to handle the tight primary schedule and not bring back the old lever-based machines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City’s Board of Elections has complained for weeks that the electronic voting machines first used in 2010 cannot handle the city’s tight primary elections schedule. But one solution, endorsed by the board and under consideration in Albany, seems absurd. The board and the State Legislature are talking about scrapping the new machines and replacing them with the old metal clunkers, with their creaky levers, that went out of production more than 30 years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep the Clunkers Away From the Polls', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keep the Clunkers Away From the Polls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Machines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:15:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e65a383-67b0-5bb5-9610-e8be4bf084bc', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e65a383-67b0-5bb5-9610-e8be4bf084bc'}, {'abstract': 'States should have some flexibility as they move to the new and more demanding curriculum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/opinion/caution-and-the-common-core-state-education-standards.html', 'snippet': 'States should have some flexibility as they move to the new and more demanding curriculum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rigorous Common Core learning standards that have been adopted by 45 states represent a once-in-a-generation opportunity for the United States to improve public schools nationally, bringing math, science and literacy education up to levels achieved by high-performing nations abroad. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caution and the Common Core', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caution and the Common Core', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1008e456-1bf3-5ffd-b54c-cc27d42a97dc', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1008e456-1bf3-5ffd-b54c-cc27d42a97dc'}, {'abstract': 'The immigration system cannot abandon fairness in the rush to prosecute and punish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/opinion/immigration-and-border-injustice.html', 'snippet': 'The immigration system cannot abandon fairness in the rush to prosecute and punish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who view fixing immigration as simply a matter of getting tougher on lawbreakers tend to overlook how tough the system already is, an ever-growing web of agents, cops, courts and prisons whose cruelty and deficiencies are appalling. Much attention has focused on the excesses of local law enforcement, exemplified by self-appointed immigration enforcers like Sheriff Joe Arpaio of Maricopa County, Ariz., whose department was found guilty in federal court on Friday of violating the constitutional rights of Latinos for years through racially biased crime sweeps, arrests, detention and harassment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Border Injustice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Border Injustice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARPAIO, JOSEPH M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:17:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e1c198-d29a-5abe-92b9-3a9a9dd65adb', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e1c198-d29a-5abe-92b9-3a9a9dd65adb'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s decision to rewrite the playbook on counterterrorism policy dates to his re-election concerns, and it represents an effort to shape his legacy and to set the rules for his successors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/us/politics/in-terror-shift-obama-took-a-long-path.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s decision to rewrite the playbook on counterterrorism policy dates to his re-election concerns, and it represents an effort to shape his legacy and to set the rules for his successors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The pivot in counterterrorism policy that President Obama announced last week was nearly two years in the making, but perhaps the most critical moment came last spring during a White House meeting as he talked about the future of the nation’s long-running terrorism war. Underlying the discussion was a simple fact: It was an election year. And Mr. Obama might lose.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/world/JP-OBAMA-1/JP-OBAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/world/JP-OBAMA-1/JP-OBAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/world/JP-OBAMA-1/JP-OBAMA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/world/JP-OBAMA-1/JP-OBAMA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/world/JP-OBAMA-1/JP-OBAMA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy'