 the umpire in a first-round loss at the French Open Monday, so he took his case to Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When 101st-ranked Sergiy Stakhovsky’s racquet proved insufficent to gain an edge on the No. 7 seed Richard Gasquet through the first two games on Court Suzanne Lenglen Monday, Stakhovsky found a more modern piece of equipment to try to swing the match his way: his iPhone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upset at a Call, Stakhovsky Goes the Social Media Route', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasquet, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:43:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e939651-76cf-5c4f-9fc8-f9af70805635', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e939651-76cf-5c4f-9fc8-f9af70805635'}, {'abstract': 'Central Park and the High Line have donors who can drop millions in a moment; other parks, frequently those outside Manhattan that don’t draw tourists, are getting desperate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/nyregion/reducing-some-city-parks-to-the-status-of-beggars.html', 'snippet': 'Central Park and the High Line have donors who can drop millions in a moment; other parks, frequently those outside Manhattan that don’t draw tourists, are getting desperate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Hindy, the Brooklyn Brewery baron and a fellow whose love of this city is manifest, serves as board member of the Prospect Park Alliance. He noticed the city was steadily edging away from its financial commitment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reducing Some City Parks to the Status of Beggars', 'kicker': 'Gotham', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reducing Some City Parks to the Status of Beggars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prospect Park Alliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:51:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b478cd03-f341-5e76-8468-526809ed7963', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b478cd03-f341-5e76-8468-526809ed7963'}, {'abstract': 'The 23-year-old American qualifier Steve Johnson battled Albert Montanes of Spain Monday at the French Open, but he fell in five sets.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/27/johnson-falls-to-montanes-in-see-saw-battle/', 'snippet': 'The 23-year-old American qualifier Steve Johnson battled Albert Montanes of Spain Monday at the French Open, but he fell in five sets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Steve Johnson of the United States stroked 56 shots beyond the reach of Albert Montanes of Spain, but he came up short in a three-and-a-half hour duel that see-sawed to a 6-4, 4-6, 6-3, 3-6, 6-1 victory for Montanes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnson Falls to Montanes in See-Saw Battle', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMATEUR ATHLETICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montanes, Albert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30a4ac9e-9db2-58ce-8436-e175155d1e21', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30a4ac9e-9db2-58ce-8436-e175155d1e21'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway experience does not typically include audience participation, but something unusual happens when Cicely Tyson performs “Blessed Assurance” in “The Trip to Bountiful.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/theater/cicely-tyson-and-blessed-assurance.html', 'snippet': 'The Broadway experience does not typically include audience participation, but something unusual happens when Cicely Tyson performs “Blessed Assurance” in “The Trip to Bountiful.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long after the curtain rises on the second act of “The Trip to Bountiful,” the Broadway revival of the Horton Foote play at the Stephen Sondheim Theater, something unusual happens. Cicely Tyson, as Mrs. Carrie Watts, sits on a bus station bench in a small Texas town. She is on the run from her abusive daughter-in-law and henpecked son in Houston, desperate to see the family farm in Bountiful once more before she dies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/theater/BOUNTIFUL/BOUNTIFUL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Something Happened on the Way to Bountiful: Everyone Sang Along', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Something Happened on Way to Bountiful: Everyone Sang Along', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Trip to Bountiful (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyson, Cicely', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foote, Horton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T01:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76ec27da-0b5b-53cb-bcb1-747cbe15758d', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76ec27da-0b5b-53cb-bcb1-747cbe15758d'}, {'abstract': 'Ellis and Liberty Islands are set to have new security checkpoints, but Senator Charles E. Schumer says that checking tourists after they have arrived leaves the statue vulnerable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/nyregion/schumer-opposes-new-security-plan-for-statue-of-liberty.html', 'snippet': 'Ellis and Liberty Islands are set to have new security checkpoints, but Senator Charles E. Schumer says that checking tourists after they have arrived leaves the statue vulnerable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Charles E. Schumer called on the National Park Service on Monday to scrap what he called a dangerous new security plan for the Statue of Liberty, saying that it could leave visitors to the tourist attraction vulnerable to a terrorist attack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citing Danger, Schumer Calls