y marks his third time out. Kick back and solve this one with a nice, cold BREWSKI.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fit to Be Tied', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T02:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbff4ccd-08d5-5263-8ffc-e799db60fadd', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbff4ccd-08d5-5263-8ffc-e799db60fadd'}, {'abstract': 'The nomination of the judges to a key federal court all at once is certain to unleash fierce Republican opposition and could rekindle a broader partisan struggle over Senate rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/us/politics/obama-plans-to-nominate-3-judges-for-key-court.html', 'snippet': 'The nomination of the judges to a key federal court all at once is certain to unleash fierce Republican opposition and could rekindle a broader partisan struggle over Senate rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama will soon accelerate his efforts to put a lasting imprint on the country’s judiciary by simultaneously nominating three judges to an important federal court, a move that is certain to unleash fierce Republican opposition and could rekindle a broader partisan struggle over Senate rules.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/us/jp-JUDGES-1/jp-JUDGES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 60