 Bausch & Lomb Is Sold for $8.7 Billion | Club Med’s Future', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world leader in uranium enrichment, Urenco, is plumply profitable and has at least 10 years of steady work lined up. So why is it up for sale?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking an Exit From Uranium', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T14:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3da311d0-0f58-567c-866d-46e575bbabe1', 'word_count': 1829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3da311d0-0f58-567c-866d-46e575bbabe1'}, {'abstract': 'Re-elected yet freshly embattled, President Obama made his first visit to the Jersey Shore since Hurricane Sandy, and Gov. Chris Christie received him with unrestrained gratitude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/us/obama-and-christie-to-view-recovery-on-jersey-shore.html', 'snippet': 'Re-elected yet freshly embattled, President Obama made his first visit to the Jersey Shore since Hurricane Sandy, and Gov. Chris Christie received him with unrestrained gratitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POINT PLEASANT BEACH, N.J. — Politics makes strange beachfellows. President Obama and Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey affirmed this notion, and enjoyed its benefits, on Tuesday in a drizzly reunion on the Jersey Shore, seven months after Hurricane Sandy punished the famous coastline and united them in an unlikely politica