festival near Genoa, Italy, is intended to bring modern dance to a region known more for its cuisine and scenery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOGLIASCO, Italy — The Ligurian region of Italy is better known for its magnificent coastline and its delicious cuisine (the birthplace of pesto!) than for dance. But Danza Contempo Ligure, a small festival based in Genoa, suggests that there is no shortage of choreographic activity. The final day of the new weeklong festival took place in Bogliasco, a small coastal village just beyond the Genoa city limits. The location was the Villa dei Pini, the grand house that belongs to the Bogliasco Foundation, an organization that provides residencies to artists and humanities scholars, and the participating choreographers made fine use of the villa’s beautiful gardens and coastal location despite unseasonally chilly weather.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/global-home/iht-rdv-dance-28May/iht-rdv-dance-28May-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance in the Birthplace of Pesto', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Genoa (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T14:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9260b3f7-c93e-550b-8c22-ad4974a7033f', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9260b3f7-c93e-550b-8c22-ad4974a7033f'}, {'abstract': 'The author of this week’s cover article answers questions about what scientists now know about women’s sexuality — and how they’re trying to manipulate it.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/behind-the-cover-story-daniel-bergner-on-the-female-viagra/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover article answers questions about what scientists now know about women’s sexuality — and how they’re trying to manipulate it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Bergner, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story about the development of a pill to stimulate female desire. His new book, “What Do Women Want?: Adventures in the Science of Female Desire” comes out next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/24-daniel-bergner/24-daniel-bergner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 220, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/24-daniel-bergner/24-daniel-bergner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 220, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/24-daniel-bergner/24-daniel-bergner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/24-daniel-bergner/24-daniel-bergner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/24/magazine/24-daniel-bergner/24-daniel-bergner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Daniel Bergner on the Female ‘Viagra’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergner, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T14:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a499d245-16c6-5cd9-8509-cff01cbfa619', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a499d245-16c6-5cd9-8509-cff01cbfa619'}, {'abstract': 'Portraying SAC Capital Advisors as a den of thieves could send a message about how the Justice Department is policing Wall Street, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/sac-could-give-the-justice-dept-a-high-value-target/', 'snippet': 'Portraying SAC Capital Advisors as a den of thieves could send a message about how the Justice Department is policing Wall Street, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subpoenas issued to executives at SAC Capital Advisors to testify before a grand jury provide a powerful indication that prosecutors have made the firm the focus of their latest effort to crack down on insider trading. Unfortunately for SAC, it may also be a case of being in the wrong place at the wrong time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAC Could Give the Justice Dept. a High-Value Target', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2