ins, who was shot and killed on March 11 while sitting in her father’s lap in a minivan in Chicago? Authorities said Monday that the man accused in the shooting, which also wounded her father, was seeking revenge for the theft of a video game console. Koman Willis, a documented gang member with 38 previous arrests, was charged with first-degree murder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: Memorial Day Edition', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T15:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera and Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98080140-8b71-5c3e-a2c5-20de255b8bc2', 'word_count': 3822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98080140-8b71-5c3e-a2c5-20de255b8bc2'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court said a one-year filing deadline for prisoners seeking federal review of their state court convictions under a 1996 law may be relaxed if they present compelling evidence of their innocence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/us/justices-make-it-easier-for-inmates-to-challenge-convictions.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court said a one-year filing deadline for prisoners seeking federal review of their state court convictions under a 1996 law may be relaxed if they present compelling evidence of their innocence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a pair of 5-to-4 decisions that divided along ideological lines, the Supreme Court on Tuesday made it easier for inmates to challenge their convictions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Divided Court, in 2 Rulings, Makes It Easier to Challenge Criminal Convictions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Divided Court, in 2 Rulings, Makes It Easier to Challenge Criminal Convictions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-28T15:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd18a94-ef59-5dfe-8e18-db9c3d1e3819', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd18a94-ef59-5dfe-8e18-db9c3d1e3819'}, {'abstract': 'A shelter in Uttar Pradesh that rescues cows from cow-lifter gangs is funded by Indian-Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/28/indian-cows-find-patrons-in-u-s/', 'snippet': 'A shelter in Uttar Pradesh that rescues cows from cow-lifter gangs is funded by Indian-Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARSANA, Uttar Pradesh — The cow’s status as a sacred being in Hinduism is increasingly being threatened as more wealthy Indians, even Hindus, are turning carnivorous, as Gardiner Harris of The New York Times recently reported. Meanwhile, the increasing demand for beef is driving gangs to steal cows that are wandering around Delhi so that the animals can be sold to slaughterhouses.Still, cows have plenty of protectors in India, and even beyond its borders. Thousands of miles away, Indian citizens living in the United States regularly send money to cow shelters in India like Mataji Gaushala, located in Barsana, near Mathura in Uttar Pradesh. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/28/world/asia/28-Abhi