e imperfect, conforms to the State Constitution. The ruling by the Colorado Supreme Court, which overturned a lower court’s decision, handed a stinging defeat to parents and school districts that argued that the financing formula was fundamentally unfair and unbalanced, and widened the gaps between “have” and “have-not” school districts. Many state officials welcomed the court’s ruling. They said it would remove the heated educational battle from the courts and return it to the hands of elected lawmakers, who have already taken steps to try to improve how Colorado finances its schools. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado: Court Upholds System for Financing Schools', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colorado: Court Upholds System For Financing Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T00:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2977c370-9bc0-5c39-9cbc-2fef6ef80a81', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2977c370-9bc0-5c39-9cbc-2fef6ef80a81'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of Lance Armstrong’s admission that he used performance-enhancing drugs, Nike announced that it will stop manufacturing Livestrong-brand shoes and apparel at the end of this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/sports/cycling/nike-to-cut-ties-with-livestrong.html', 'snippet': 'In the wake of Lance Armstrong’s admission that he used performance-enhancing drugs, Nike announced that it will stop manufacturing Livestrong-brand shoes and apparel at the end of this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nike stuck by Tiger Woods in the wake of his infidelity and gave Michael Vick an endorsement deal after Vick had served time in prison for his role in a dogfighting ring, which included killing dogs that underperformed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/29/sports/yARMSTRONG/yARMSTRONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':