09, when rallies in support of opposition candidates set the stage for the mass protests that followed the vote, but one of the candidates injected some passion into the race on Monday when he showed a flash of anger during an interview on state television.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Candidate for Iran’s Presidency Defends Record as Nuclear Negotiator', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Republic of Iran Broadcaster', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T01:18:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b91f427-6333-5c9d-a543-c55ee2b24bce', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b91f427-6333-5c9d-a543-c55ee2b24bce'}, {'abstract': 'Baseball’s ceremonial first pitch, a pregame ritual once reserved for presidents, war heroes and mayors, has become little more than a marketing opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/sports/baseball/baseballs-first-pitch-loses-its-exclusivity.html', 'snippet': 'Baseball’s ceremonial first pitch, a pregame ritual once reserved for presidents, war heroes and mayors, has become little more than a marketing opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly before a recent game at Citi Field, four dancers in skin-tight, metallic green body suits slunk toward the pitcher’s mound, where a man wearing a red tuxedo and top hat