ate': '2013-05-29T14:23:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Almudena Toral', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Almudena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toral', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e14ec031-ab8a-5d2b-be3a-376ae1d5015a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e14ec031-ab8a-5d2b-be3a-376ae1d5015a'}, {'abstract': 'A video about the artist Sarah Sze’s installation in the United States Pavilion at the Venice Biennale.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/sarah-sze-the-stones-of-venice/', 'snippet': 'A video about the artist Sarah Sze’s installation in the United States Pavilion at the Venice Biennale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — Everyone is anxiously waiting to get into the Biennale, which opens to the art world here on Wednesday and to the public on Saturday. But those who have already arrived can take an early peek at the work of one artist. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarah Sze: The Stones of Venice', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sze, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T14:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fc8a63a-9779-5e9a-b0d6-77c6f28c18be', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fc8a63a-9779-5e9a-b0d6-77c6f28c18be'}, {'abstract': 'The harrowing medical journey of a Civil War amputee.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/napoleon-perkins-loses-his-leg/', 'snippet': 'The harrowing medical journey of a Civil War amputee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Napoleon Perkins dragged himself toward the plank road behind the Chancellor house, shot and shells plowing up the ground all around him and apple blossoms drifting into his hair. Moments before, during some of the fiercest fighting at the Battle of Chancellorsville in Virginia, Perkins had been unhitching one of his horses from a Fifth Maine artillery caisson when a rebel shell struck him in the right leg just above the knee. At first he did not realize how badly he had been wounded; but when he tried to walk to the rear, his leg buckled and nearly severed in two. Perkins managed to reach the road and began to crawl across it, but could go no farther. Dizzy but still conscious, he watched the Chancellor house and the nearby woods catch fire and burn, killing many of his comrades who had been similarly wounded in the fight, but could not flee the flames.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Napoleon Perkins Loses His Leg', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMPUTATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T14:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By megan kate nelson', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe47fada-ae8b-519c-ba77-3ceeac579845', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe47fada-ae8b-519c-ba77-3ceeac579845'}, {'abstract': 'Britain is preparing to privatize Royal Mail, the country’s postal service, whose origins date to 1516 and the carrying of post for Henry VIII and the Tudor court.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/britain-plans-i-p-o-for-postal-service/', 'snippet': 'Britain is preparing to privatize Royal Mail, the country’s postal service, whose origins date to 1516 and the carrying of post for Henry VIII and the Tudor court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Britain is preparing to privatize Royal Mail, the country’s postal service, whose origins date to 1516 and the carrying of post for Henry VIII and the Tudor court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Plans I.P.O. for Postal Service', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T14:33:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0a700e8-e072-5a0f-ab18-5b933a754266', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0a700e8-e072-5a0f-ab18-5b933a754266'}, {'abstract': 'LeBron James’s relegation to the bench for the closing seconds of Game 4 was as surprising as the Pacers bouncing back from being routed in Game 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/sports/basketball/nba-playoffs-heat-falter-in-game-4-after-lebron-james-fouls-out.html', 'snippet': 'LeBron James’s relegation to the bench for the closing seconds of Game 4 was