type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/640c6316-7a13-5ffc-a4d9-5b913fe4b17b', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/640c6316-7a13-5ffc-a4d9-5b913fe4b17b'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters were as puzzled by the performances of the Miami Heat’s best players in Game 4 as they were by the referees’ calls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/sports/basketball/heats-big-three-are-missing-in-crucial-moments-of-game-4-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters were as puzzled by the performances of the Miami Heat’s best players in Game 4 as they were by the referees’ calls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the Miami Heat become bored with themselves, the whole dominating-the-N.B.A. thing being a bit on the dull side. Their losses are a bit like the times when your older brother plays you in the driveway and shoots with only his left hand. Maybe the Heat players are just trying to challenge themselves: “O.K., we’re up by 3 with just over five minutes to go. What if LeBron fouls out, we let Indiana score a bunch in a row, Dwyane gets called for something like traveling in the final minute and then we see what happens? Got it? Let’s go!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/30leading/30leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/30leading/30leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 991}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/30leading/30leading-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 620, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/30leading/30leading-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1240