erve Jamie Dimon’s dual role as C.E.O. and chairman suggests that shareholders may be part of the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shareholders can’t be counted on.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flawed System Suits the Shareholders Just Fine', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flawed System That Suits the Shareholders Just Fine ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayo, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Henry M Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stout, Lynn A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Eisinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8f57099-7ab7-590c-a68b-93282a72f83d', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8f57099-7ab7-590c-a68b-93282a72f83d'}, {'abstract': 'Bertram Lyons, an archivist at the American Folklife Center of the Library of Congress in Washington, answers questions about preserving audio materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/booming/tips-on-archiving-family-history-part-1.html', 'snippet': 'Bertram Lyons, an archivist at the American Folklife Center of the Library of Congress in Washington, answers questions about preserving audio materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers sent dozens of questions about archiving and preserving family history and stories to Bertram Lyons, an archivist at the American Folklife Center of the Library of Congress in Washington. He manages digital archives relating to folklife, including StoryCorps, which records and collects oral histories. In addition to academic workshops, he participates in public outreach, answering questions from people interested in preserving audio and visual material in analog and digital media, as well as related documents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/23/booming/23expert-booming-archivist/23expert-booming-archivist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips on Archiving Family History, Part 1', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9c53c4-a870-52f9-9c83-0ac2819ae65f', 'word_count': 2916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9c53c4-a870-52f9-9c83-0ac2819ae65f'}, {'abstract': 'Jack Grubman, the former Citigroup telecommunications analyst and now an industry consultant, argues against a proposed Dish Network-Sprint deal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/grubman-dishsprint-numbers-dont-add-up-to-shareholder-value/', 'snippet': 'Jack Grubman, the former Citigroup telecommunications analyst and now an industry consultant, argues against a proposed Dish Network-Sprint deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Grubman is a consultant to the telecommunications industry through his firm Magee Group. He was a top-ranked telecommunications research analyst on Wall Street in the 1980s and 1990s. In 2003, he settled a lawsuit with the Securities and Exchange Commission over accusations that his work for investment banking clients led him to publish misleading research reports on companies that his employer, Citigroup, advised. As part of the settlement, in which Mr. Grubman did not admit or deny the allegations, he was barred from the securities industry. Mr. Grubman has no role either as an adviser or an investor in any of the companies discussed in this essay. This is his first public commentary since his settlement a decade ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grubman: Dish/Sprint Numbers Don’t Add Up to Shareholder Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grubman, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Softbank Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Grubman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grubman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4106f3da-5cd3-52c7-93d8-f5352ccdfef1', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4106f3da-5cd3-52c7-93d8-f5352ccdfef1'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Rashbass, chief executive of The Economist Group, will become C.E.O of Reuters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/business/media/reuters-names-new-head-of-news-operation.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Rashbass, chief executive of The Economist Group, will become C.E.O of Reuters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomson Reuters has hired Andrew Rashbass, chief executive of The Economist Group, to take on a newly created role overseeing the sprawling Reuters news operation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reuters Names New Head of News Operation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thomson Reuters Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Media', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41cd7145-9299-5a6d-9a09-56a886b0ed16', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41cd7145-9299-5a6d-9a09-56a886b0ed16'}, {'abstract': 'A tasting tour across the epicenter of California’s artisanal cheese movement offers far more than just exceptional bites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/travel/5-stops-on-a-california-cheese-trail.html', 'snippet': 'A tasting tour across the epicenter of California’s artisanal cheese movement offers far more than just exceptional bites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marcia Barinaga was showing me and seven other visitors around her ridge-top sheep ranch overlooking the long, slender finger of Tomales Bay and the hills of Point Reyes National Seashore in Marin County, north of San Francisco. As she told us about her flock of 100 East Friesians in a pasture where some of the less timid sheep had gathered around, she bussed the pinkish, wet nose of a ewe. It was an offhand gesture but a telling one, revealing a deep affection for the animals that provide the milk she transforms into cheese in the style of her Basque ancestors.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PURSUITS4/02PURSUITS4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 Stops on a California Cheese Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Cheese Lovers, Going to the Source', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marin County (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sonoma County (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Hall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8439dac1-a672-5af8-b3d7-d2df44f625df', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8439dac1-a672-5af8-b3d7-d2df44f625df'}, {'abstract': 'Looking for some not-so-obvious places where you can soak up New York City flavor? The amateur historian and “Bowery Boy” Greg Young recommends a few options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/travel/discovering-new-york-beyond-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'Looking for some not-so-obvious places where you can soak up New York City flavor? The amateur historian and “Bowery Boy” Greg Young recommends a few options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Greg Young became one-half of “The Bowery Boys,” the podcast about New York City history he started with his friend Tom Meyers in 2007, visitors to the Big Apple have sought out his tourism recommendations. Forgoing Manhattan, Mr. Young, an amateur historian and Missouri native, sends them to the outer boroughs, to sites that are “offbeat but still truly unique to New York City and not overrun with crowds.” And they are outdoors, a plus for the summer ahead.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/0602QNA01-sf/0602QNA01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Discovering New York, Beyond Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You take Manhattan. Greg Young on city history in other boroughs.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Roosevelt Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T16:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3120b86-3e51-5fde-bdb4-50ab37089321', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3120b86-3e51-5fde-bdb4-50ab37089321'}, {'abstract': 'The seminal hardcore band had its glory days in the late 1970s and early ’80s. Now, former members have put together two versions of the group, and feathers are being ruffled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/arts/music/black-flag-returns-in-two-permutations.html', 'snippet': 'The seminal hardcore band had its glory days in the late 1970s and early ’80s. Now, former members have put together two versions of the group, and feathers are being ruffled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Two singers, two gigs, two cities and stages, the same opening song. “It’s not my imagination,” it begins, drawled. Pause, and then a yell: “I’ve got a gun at my back!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New Yo