n who was shot to death in Greenwich Village this month, had a favorite phrase he used when people heckled him on the street. “He’d say, ‘Pay it and pump,’ which means don’t pay it any attention, keep moving,” said Alonzo, 33, an online radio host who said Mr. Carson had been his best friend since they were teenagers on Webster Avenue in the Bronx.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/nyregion/carson/carson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Killed in the Village Is Remembered as Outgoing and Private', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Killed in the Village Is Remembered as Outgoing and Private', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, Mark (d 2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T17:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5dcd605-2e5e-5fcd-b0e9-337e75aeb633', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5dcd605-2e5e-5fcd-b0e9-337e75aeb633'}, {'abstract': 'Coach John Tortorella was fired after the Rangers were eliminated by the Bruins in the second round of the playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/rangers-fire-john-tortorella-as-coach.html', 'snippet': 'Coach John Tortorella was fired after the Rangers were eliminated by the Bruins in the second round of the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Rangers coach, John Tortorella was a creature of certitude — opinionated, volatile and confident to the point of arrogance. He drove his players to throw themselves in front of shots, occasionally criticized them in public and often insulted members of the news media. On Monday, as the Rangers packed up their locker room at the end of another season without a Stanley Cup, Tortorella spoke like a man certain he would be around to fix the team. He even said he was looking forward to training camp in the fall. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/hockey/30tortorella-1/30tortorella-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Much to His Surprise, Fiery Tortorella Is Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Much to His Surprise, Fiery Tortorella Is Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T17:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4203ff2b-dc3a-5ac1-a7c8-549897aefdf5', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4203ff2b-dc3a-5ac1-a7c8-549897aefdf5'}, {'abstract': 'Zal Batmanglij, the director of “The East,” narrates a scene from the film.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/anatomy-of-a-scene-the-east/', 'snippet': 'Zal Batmanglij, the director of “The East,” narrates a scene from the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director Zal Batmanglij, who was profiled in a recent Arts & Leisure article, has made his second film, a thriller titled “The East” (May 31) that he wrote with Brit Marling. In this video, he narrates a scene featuring Ms. Marling and Shiloh Fernandez and discusses his interest in a “spy thriller made using a smart phone and some paper clips and aluminum cans.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: ‘The East’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batmanglij, Zal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marling, Brit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T17:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a386c9-f6e3-5281-a408-8abf9d08f0ec', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a386c9-f6e3-5281-a408-8abf9d08f0ec'}, {'abstract': 'Pacers center Roy Hibbert’s impact as a shot blocker is well documented, but he is also averaging 22.8 points and 6.5 offensive rebounds a game against Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/sports/basketball/roy-hibbert-gives-pacers-more-possessions-and-a-better-chance.html', 'snippet': 'Pacers center Roy Hibbert’s impact as a shot blocker is well documented, but he is also averaging 22.8 points and 6.5 offensive rebounds a game against Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first two months of the season, Roy Hibbert looked like a terrible investment. The Pacers had given Hibbert, a 7-foot-2 center, a four-year, $58.4 million contract, the maximum he could be paid under N.B.A. rules, and he seemed to be regressing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/BECKLEY/BECKLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/BECKLEY/BECKLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 842}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/sports/