ons and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:23:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/042c3cc7-5165-5b8e-82c2-63e2ec87321e', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042c3cc7-5165-5b8e-82c2-63e2ec87321e'}, {'abstract': 'A lack of fine dining has always been St.-Tropez’s Achilles heel, but that’s changing with an influx of smart new restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/food-matters-st-tropezs-sophisticated-new-palate/', 'snippet': 'A lack of fine dining has always been St.-Tropez’s Achilles heel, but that’s changing with an influx of smart new restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one saw it coming. This summer in St.-Tropez, people aren’t just talking the usual fame and fashion, they’re talking food. Food? In St.-Tropez? Mais, oui! In fact, the only new Michelin three-star restaurant in France this year is La Vague d’Or in St.-Tropez, and Bruno Doucet, the hottest bistro chef in Paris, opened a branch of his famously epicurean La Regalade at the sleek Benkirai Hotel last summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Matters | St.-Tropez’s Sophisticated New Palate', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St-Tropez (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61182561-1cc0-5cf8-94e6-25cd3c3fab89', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61182561-1cc0-5cf8-94e6-25cd3c3fab89'}, {'abstract': 'James Gorman, Morgan Stanley’s chief executive and proud father, sent an e-mail on Wednesday promoting his daughter’s music career.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/meet-james-gorman-c-e-o-and-music-agent/', 'snippet': 'James Gorman, Morgan Stanley’s chief executive and proud father, sent an e-mail on Wednesday promoting his daughter’s music career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wall Street, it’s not uncommon for children to follow their parents into finance. However, Caroline Gorman, the daughter of Morgan Stanley’s chief executive, James Gorman, appears headed down a much different path. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet James Gorman, C.E.O. and Music Agent', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c3565f0-e0ae-500d-92ca-27763f9ab446', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c3565f0-e0ae-500d-92ca-27763f9ab446'}, {'abstract': 'If debt investors are to shoulder the risk of suffering a loss, they will need more confidence about what lurks in banks’ balance sheets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/how-to-make-bank-bail-ins-work/', 'snippet': 'If debt investors are to shoulder the risk of suffering a loss, they will need more confidence about what lurks in banks’ balance sheets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regulators want banks to be able to go bust like ordinary companies. That means bondholders taking the pain if a bank fails. But if debt investors are to shoulder the risk of suffering a loss, they will need more confidence about what lurks in banks’ balance sheets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Bank Bail-Ins Work', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:32:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Unmack and Peter Thal Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Unmack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Thal', 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/643c2523-16bc-5ef3-8457-4fd9ee9c67f3', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/643c2523-16bc-5ef3-8457-4fd9ee9c67f3'}, {'abstract': 'After years of falling short, Flickr was reborn last week. And every free account holder gets one terabyte of storage, a vast amount of space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/technology/personaltech/the-new-flickr-space-and-more-space-free.html', 'snippet': 'After years of falling short, Flickr was reborn last week. And every free account holder gets one terabyte