olice Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Stabbings Given as Cause of Soldier’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rigby, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adebolajo, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adebowale, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07c422be-d0df-5e92-9e71-2c538724a3a6', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07c422be-d0df-5e92-9e71-2c538724a3a6'}, {'abstract': 'New makeup products are eliminating the current scourge of American diets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/fashion/going-without-gluten-beauty-spots.html', 'snippet': 'New makeup products are eliminating the current scourge of American diets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was probably inevitable that gluten, the current scourge of American diets, be eliminated from makeup as well. Even trace amounts, absorbed through lips or eyes, can impact those with celiac disease. The benefits to the rest of the population are less clear, but nonetheless a number of beauty brands, like the ones below, are capitalizing on the current mass aversion to the grain-derived protein.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/fashion/30SPOTS_SPAN/30SPOTS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Without Gluten', 'kicker': 'Beauty Spots', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gluten', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:50:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce7e8cc7-0b34-5737-8912-ea32f223f8fa', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce7e8cc7-0b34-5737-8912-ea32f223f8fa'}, {'abstract': 'Aside from looking beautiful, your dinner can be wrapped in a green leaf for a number of reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/cooking-with-leaves/', 'snippet': 'Aside from looking beautiful, your dinner can be wrapped in a green leaf for a number of reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aside from looking beautiful, your dinner can be wrapped in a green leaf for a number of reasons. This culinary technique protects food in a secure, impermeable package. Said leaf-wrapped food — meat or fish or savory mixture — may then be grilled, steamed or roasted. In the process, the leaves add a unique flavor and perfume to the dish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking With Leaves', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/089a0e94-579f-547a-aa73-a430842a1de8', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/089a0e94-579f-547a-aa73-a430842a1de8'}, {'abstract': 'The endorsement solidifies John C. Liu’s credentials as perhaps the most pro-union and liberal of the Democratic candidates for mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/citys-largest-public-employees-union-endorses-liu/', 'snippet': 'The endorsement solidifies John C. Liu’s credentials as perhaps the most pro-union and liberal of the Democratic candidates for mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a boost to his embattled mayoral campaign, John C. Liu, the city comptroller, received the support on Wednesday of the city’s largest public employees union, District Council 37.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City’s Largest Public Employees Union Endorses Liu', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Lillian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T18:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b568ec6f-15df-55cb-ae75-28292f102985', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b568ec6f-15df-55cb-ae75-28292f102985'}, {'abstract': 'From new-music premieres to art museum collaborations, the New York Philharmonic announced plans for an eclectic 11-day series next spring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-offers-details-on-2014-biennial.html', 'snippet': 'From new-music premieres to art museum collaborations, the New York Philharmonic announced plans for an eclectic 11-day series next spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the New York Philharmonic announced its 2013-14 season in January, it sketched out a major new initiative, the NY Phil Biennial, in broad terms and a sprinkling of intriguing details. On Wednesday, the orchestra filled in more of the blanks, making clear that it is expanding its contemporary-music activities well beyond the composer residencies, the new-music series Contact! and the special events that it has embraced since Alan Gilbert took over as the Philharmonic’s music director four years ago.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philharmonic Maps Out a Kaleidoscopic Biennial ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philharmonic Maps Out a Kaleidoscopic Biennial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d16e31-edcc-5269-8b26-5231f1921a46', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d16e31-edcc-5269-8b26-5231f1