ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da4979f8-8315-5765-a05b-2454725fd992', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da4979f8-8315-5765-a05b-2454725fd992'}, {'abstract': 'A violin and a viola owned and played by Mozart will be used in performances in the United States in June.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/mozart-never-made-it-to-america-but-his-violin-and-viola-are-on-the-way/', 'snippet': 'A violin and a viola owned and played by Mozart will be used in performances in the United States in June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though he made his way all around Europe in his brief lifetime, Mozart never found his way to the United States. But a violin and viola that he owned and played will be making their first American appearances early next month, in concerts in Boston and New York. Both instruments will be heard at Jordan Hall during the Boston Early Music Festival, when the violinist Amandine Beyer and the violist Milos Valent offer a chamber music program with the pianist Kristian Bezuidenhout and the clarinetist Erich Hoeprich (June 10). The instruments will also be on display at the festival’s exhibition on June 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mozart Never Made It to America, but His Violin and Viola Are On the Way', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Austrian Cultural Forum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T19:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn',