}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T20:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31f2327c-104d-5b8c-9fb1-01116b29932a', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31f2327c-104d-5b8c-9fb1-01116b29932a'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of photographs by Ringo Starr will be published next month as an e-book, and in December as a physical (and expensive) one.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/an-inside-look-at-the-beatles-ringos-photos/', 'snippet': 'A collection of photographs by Ringo Starr will be published next month as an e-book, and in December as a physical (and expensive) one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his lengthy solo turn in “A Hard Day’s Night,” Ringo Starr takes a walk around London with a camera, snapping pictures and getting into trouble. Perhaps because of that image, Mr. Starr came to be thought of as the biggest shutterbug among the Beatles, and until he lost much of his collection in a fire in Los Angeles in 1979 he was believed to be the group’s unofficial archivist and memorabilia collector.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Inside Look at the Beatles: Ringo’s Photos', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starr, Ringo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organization