Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T21:29:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7449a681-049c-5f51-b31a-4f10ca17c70d', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7449a681-049c-5f51-b31a-4f10ca17c70d'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Afghanistan, Colombia, Spain and Vatican City.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/pictures-of-the-day-afghanistan-and-elsewhere-46/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Afghanistan, Colombia, Spain and Vatican City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Afghanistan, Colombia, Spain and Vatican City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Afghanistan and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T21:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f0a6a8-74ef-53d2-8038-329744e96a09', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f0a6a8-74ef-53d2-8038-329744e96a09'}, {'abstract': 'A Q& A with Andy Cohen on his first time going to the C.F.D.A. awards and his dream casting for a reality show.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/andy-cohen-playing-to-a-tough-room/', 'snippet': 'A Q& A with Andy Cohen on his first time going to the C.F.D.A. awards and his dream casting for a reality show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few industries are as ripe for parody as fashion, and yet few comedians have managed to get so much as a snicker out of a roomful of designers when they all come together for their annual awards night each June. Many have tried. Tracey Ullman spoofed the recession in 2009. Last year, Seth Meyers reprised Marc Jacobs in drag, which is a tough act to follow.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Cohen, Playing to a Tough Room', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playing to a Tough Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Fashion Designers of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T21:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d0415eb-a27d-5954-9f4b-7dfe51560ba2', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d0415eb-a27d-5954-9f4b-7dfe51560ba2'}, {'abstract': 'Here are some of the more interesting (and sometimes edible) farm-to-table spas and treatments around.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/some-grub-with-your-rub/', 'snippet': 'Here are some of the more interesting (and sometimes edible) farm-to-table spas and treatments around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The farm-to-table trend that has sprouted up in dining rooms across the country is now finding its place in spa rooms from Laguna Beach, Calif., to Cambridge, Mass, with natural ingredients being grown on sprawling produce farms and in hotel rooftop gardens for the sole purpose of being picked, blended and then slathered on clients’ skin. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Grub With Your Rub?', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T21:37:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ayren Jackson-Cannady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ayren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jackson-Cannady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bc09811-1a66-5466-9dd2-4d4d2065a22f', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bc09811-1a66-5466-9dd2-4d4d2065a22f'}, {'abstract': 'Eliane Elias, the Brazilian pianist and singer, highlighted her new album, a tribute to Chet Baker, at Birdland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/arts/music/eliane-elias-at-birdland.html', 'snippet': 'Eliane Elias, the Brazilian pianist and singer, highlighted her new album, a tribute to Chet Baker, at Birdland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does the Brazilian jazz pianist and singer Eliane Elias have in common with Chet Baker? Not much, I would venture. But Ms. Elias’s new album, “I Thought About You (a Tribute to Chet Baker),” is her take on songs associated with the cool jazz trumpeter and singer whose music evokes a faraway gaze into a cloudy sky. Its release coincided with Ms. Elias’s Tuesday evening opening at Birdland, where she led a group that included Marc Johnson on bass, Steve Cardenas on guitar and Mauricio Zottarelli on drums.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/arts/ELIAS/ELIAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Piano, but Lauding a Trumpeter', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Piano, But Lauding A Trumpeter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elias, Eliane', 'rank': 