on': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae011850-ddde-5dd9-819b-a23f6b85c38d', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae011850-ddde-5dd9-819b-a23f6b85c38d'}, {'abstract': 'Jewel-like glass mosaic lamps from Istanbul fill an East Village shop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/garden/jewel-like-glass-mosaic-lamps-from-istanbul-fill-an-east-village-shop.html', 'snippet': 'Jewel-like glass mosaic lamps from Istanbul fill an East Village shop.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A customer walked in and said, ‘I expected you to be an 85-year-old fortune teller,’\xa0” said Melissa Benovic of Mosaic Lamps, in the East Village. Earlier this year, Ms. Benovic, who is in fact 35, opened the 300-square-foot boutique with her fiancé, Ilker Arslan, 36, a native of Turkey. They were inspired by a visit they had made three years ago to the Grand Bazaar in Istanbul, where they saw shop after shop selling glass-mosaic lamps tinted emerald, ruby and cobalt. The fixtures, which have brass fittings and are lighted with LEDs, are not for reading, or for threading a needle. “They are mood-setting,” Ms. Benovic said. “They’re warm, and calming.” Prices range from $55 for a 10-inch-high lamp to $2,500 for a 43-inch-long chandelier. 208 East Sixth Street (Cooper Square). Information: (212) 228-1964 or mosaiclampsnyc.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 638, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30OPEN_SPAN/30OPEN_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Otherworldly Glow', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Otherworldly Glow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T22:54:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc2e743-ac91-5d5e-bb54-d324ac44536f', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc2e743-ac91-5d5e-bb54-d324ac44536f'}, {'abstract': 'Luis Pons’s new furniture collection is constructed from an assortment of frames.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/garden/luis-pons-furniture-made-from-frames.html', 'snippet': 'Luis Pons’s new furniture collection is constructed from an assortment of frames.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, at the Wanted Design show in New York, the Miami-based designer Luis Pons presented five furniture groups that incorporate picture frames. In the collection called Frame, for example, classical picture-frame moldings are applied to minimal 1950s-style credenzas, dressers and nightstands, concealing drawers, as shown here. Mr. Pons created his first Frame prototype in 2005, and has made custom versions since. But standard sizes and finishes are now available for the first time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 1276, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30FURNITURE_SPAN/30CURR3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty of Frames, but Not a Picture in Sight', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plenty of Frames, But Not a Picture in Sight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pons, Luis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-29T22:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Milioti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Milioti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f4cff53-f4fc-5c7f-95e3-3a5112db77cb', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f4cff53-f4fc-5c7f-95e3-3a5112db77cb'}, {'abstract': 'Michele Quan’s handpainted ceramic houses are designed for small birds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/garden/high-end-ceramic-birdhouses.html', 'snippet': 'Michele Quan’s handpainted ceramic houses are designed for small birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michele Quan, originally a jewelry designer who made her name as a founder of the company Me&Ro, became a ceramist almost a decade ago and now works in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Many of her handmade stoneware and porcelain objects, including garlands and bells, are meant to dangle from trees. This is also the case with her latest: stoneware birdhouses. “I imagined these becoming part of the landscape, and how beautiful they could be, moving with the wind, with the ever-changing background,” she said. The tubular birdhouses are punctuated by a central hole sized for chickadees, bluebirds, wrens, sparrows and warblers. Other openings are for ventilation and drainage. Each piece is hand-painted, in motifs including stripes, flowers, stylized leaf clusters, a sun and moon, and Sanskrit calligraphy reading “Om mani padme hum,” the mantra of the bodhisattva of compassion. A hemp cord is attached for hanging. Prices range from $250 to $475. Information: mquan.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 861}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1944, 'width': 1355, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/garden/30GOODS/30CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't