.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/firm-last-words/', 'snippet': 'Julian Lim runs with his Thursday theme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — As I’ve mentioned, there is no need to feel like you are going crazy when you solve a puzzle like today’s grid by Julian Lim, because I am here to do that for you. We here at the Wordplay offices realize that you have a choice of crossword blogs to read, so we like to thank you by offering frequent tests of my sanity as a public service. You’re welcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Firm Last Words', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T02:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f84a9e-1d42-5014-ac58-70c704c22192', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f84a9e-1d42-5014-ac58-70c704c22192'}, {'abstract': 'Economists disagree about what would happen to global economic innovation if the United States adopted the social welfare policies of Scandinavian countries.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/29/why-cant-america-be-sweden/', 'snippet': 'Economists disagree about what would happen to global economic innovation if the United States adopted the social welfare policies of Scandinavian countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daron Acemoglu, an eminent economist at M.I.T., has ignited a firestorm by arguing that contemporary forces of globalization bar the United States from adopting the liberal social welfare policies of Scandinavian countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Can’t America Be Sweden?', 'kicker': 'Thomas B. Edsall', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acemoglu, Daron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, James A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodrik, Dani', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scandinavia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T02:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e731db-c378-5f63-ac0b-2144800793f0', 'word_count': 1941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e731db-c378-5f63-ac0b-2144800793f0'}, {'abstract': 'An Italian scholar said Wednesday that he had discovered the oldest known complete Torah scroll, dating from the 12th  to the 13th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/world/europe/italy-oldest-known-torah-scroll-found-scholar-says.html', 'snippet': 'An Italian scholar said Wednesday that he had discovered the oldest known complete Torah scroll, dating from the 12th  to the 13th century.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Italian scholar said Wednesday that he had discovered the oldest known complete Torah scroll, dating from the 12th \xa0to the 13th century. The roll, which contains the Pentateuch, or five books of Moses, was stored in the library of the University of Bologna\xa0and mistakenly catalogued as a document from the 17th\xa0century.\xa0Mauro Perani, a professor of Hebrew, said that the scroll was written and its segments of sheepskin sewed together between 1155 and 1225. He said that it was not the oldest known biblical text, but it was the oldest scroll of the Pentateuch found so far. Two independent studies corroborated the scroll’s age through carbon-dating tests, the university said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Oldest Known Torah Scroll Found, Scholar Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Scholar Says Oldest Known Torah Scroll Found', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bologna (Italy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Bologna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perani, Mauro', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T02:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab19f35-5b1e-5962-8a54-42f7331a4c2d', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab19f35-5b1e-5962-8a54-42f7331a4c2d'}, {'abstract': 'Schools that work with low-income students have struggled to bring readers