r health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/business/new-rules-give-employers-leeway-on-use-of-health-incentives.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration issued a rule that employers could reward or penalize employees who meet specific standards related to their health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration issued a final rule on Wednesday that gives employers greater leeway to use employee wellness programs, with financial rewards and penalties for workers worth up to 50 percent of the premium as an incentive to exercise, quit smoking, lose weight, eat more healthful food and lower cholesterol and blood pressure. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Employers Get Leeway on Health Incentives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Employers Get Leeway On Health Incentives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Partnership for Women and Families', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T02:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'n