'_id': 'nyt://article/d7f11fa0-079a-535b-b718-e2c8af559d06', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7f11fa0-079a-535b-b718-e2c8af559d06'}, {'abstract': 'Farmers in the small township north of Pondicherry are adopting dynamic farming techniques to fight the uncertain monsoon.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/for-farmers-fearing-drought-auroville-offers-some-lessons/', 'snippet': 'Farmers in the small township north of Pondicherry are adopting dynamic farming techniques to fight the uncertain monsoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUROVILLE, Tamil Nadu— Now that June is right around the corner, farmers and economists in India are anxiously awaiting the arrival of monsoon season, which will bring up to 80 percent of the country’s annual rainfall. They have good reason to worry: with the agriculture sector contributing nearly 15 percent to India’s gross domestic product last fiscal year, a lackluster monsoon could be disastrous for farmers and, in turn, the wider economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/world/asia/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/world/asia/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/world/asia/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/world/asia/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk/30-Aurovile-BitterG-indiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 172