ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba0d7cc-7192-5e38-b07d-d3f90cdb494f', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba0d7cc-7192-5e38-b07d-d3f90cdb494f'}, {'abstract': 'When you’re cooking for the restaurant’s “family” — the cooks, the waiters, the busboys — you had better come up with a crowd-pleaser.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/magazine/team-taco.html', 'snippet': 'When you’re cooking for the restaurant’s “family” — the cooks, the waiters, the busboys — you had better come up with a crowd-pleaser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Family is where you find it. For restaurant people, family is often the people at work: Method-actor captains and decent-sculptor waiters; tattooed chefs de partie, willowy hostesses, bookish sommeliers and the four cousins from Puebla who keep the whole enterprise afloat. They gather once a day in the dining room, well before your dinner, to eat their own.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1052, 'width': 1580, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02eat1/mag-02Eat-t-000_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Team Taco', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Team Taco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sifton, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tacos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T11:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c8b703-619f-5e38-9454-de2b3009aa62', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c8b703-619f-5e38-9454-de2b3009aa62'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Larsen confronts the daily challenges of running a family business in the hope that it will be there for the fifth generation.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/the-small-picture-thinking-about-succession/', 'snippet': 'Sam Larsen confronts the daily challenges of running a family business in the hope that it will be there for the fifth generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We recently asked small-business owners to send us photographs that captured the soul of their businesses in a single shot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Small Picture: Thinking About Succession', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T11:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cafef7f7-77e5-57bc-980d-dd9e2eb36cc7', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cafef7f7-77e5-57bc-980d-dd9e2eb36cc7'}, {'abstract': 'Four years after the publication of “Let the Great World Spin,” Colum McCann’s magnificent, cathartic 9/11 novel continues to help people cope with tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/magazine/colum-mccanns-radical-empathy.html', 'snippet': 'Four years after the publication of “Let the Great World Spin,” Colum McCann’s magnificent, cathartic 9/11 novel continues to help people cope with tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Colum McCann’s apartment, on the ninth floor of an elegant building just off Central Park, there’s a room where he writes that looks as if it were airlifted in from the woods. It’s all rough-hewed floorboards and shelves made of unvarnished pine and two-by-fours and a long, thick cedar slab for a desk. At one end of that desk there’s a space that used to be a closet, but at McCann’s request, the friend who built the office took off the door and put a platform in there, and this is where McCann writes, “in the cupboard,” as he put it. “It concentrates my vision. No windows, two very tight walls.” He sits on a couple of cushions with his computer on his lap. On the wall beside him are dozens of messages scrawled by friends and kids and fellow writers and some by McCann himself: “What is the source of our first suffering? It lies in the fact that we hesitated to speak. It was born in the moment when we accumulated silent things within us.” “Keep yourself away from answers, but alive in the middle of the question.” “Stay rotten.” “Hi, Dad, I love you.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02mccann1/mag-02McCann-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02mccann1/mag-02McCann-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02mccann1/mag-02McCann-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02mccann1/mag-02McCann-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/magazine/02mccann1/mag-02McCann-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width':