m/2013/05/30/toru-hashimotos-self-destruction/', 'snippet': 'How the media-savvy mayor of Osaka, Japan, tripped over “comfort women.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Two weeks ago, Toru Hashimoto, the popular, media-savvy mayor of Osaka, was a depreciating asset in Japanese politics. The co-leader of the Japan Restoration Association, he was watching his four-year old experiment in political theater slide into irrelevance. Support for his political party, which finished a strong second in the House of Representatives election only five months ago, was now down below 5 percent and falling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rising Star’s Self-Destruction', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hashimoto, Toru', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T12:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cucek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cucek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4272dea7-a3ba-57f5-bf40-b3b286185dfc', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4272dea7-a3ba-57f5-bf40-b3b286185dfc'}, {'abstract': 'OS X includes Font Book, a program for viewing, deleting and managing the fonts on the Mac.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/qa-pruning-the-macs-font-collection/', 'snippet': 'OS X includes Font Book, a program for viewing, deleting and managing the fonts on the Mac.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Pruning the Mac’s Font Collection', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72535e45-7d90-5436-b292-8821c1da837c', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72535e45-7d90-5436-b292-8821c1da837c'}, {'abstract': 'The Kickstarter co-founder Perry Chen understands how communities can fuel creativity. The artist Theaster Gates knows how creativity can invigorate a community. What happens when they put their heads together?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/in-conversation-perry-chen-and-theaster-gates-on-community-driven-creativity/', 'snippet': 'The Kickstarter co-founder Perry Chen understands how communities can fuel creativity. The artist Theaster Gates knows how creativity can invigorate a community. What happens when they put their heads together?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kickstarter co-founder Perry Chen understands how communities can fuel creativity. The artist Theaster Gates knows how creativity can invigorate a community. What happens when they put their heads together?At first glance, an Internet entrepreneur and an artist seem to operate in different creative spheres. Yet Perry Chen, the co-founder and C.E.O. of the crowd-funding Web site Kickstarter, and Theaster Gates, a Chicago art star-cum-urban planner, actually think they have a lot in common. Kickstarter began in 2009, and since then the site has raised more than $500 million for 40,000 projects — from Iraq war documentaries to Brooklyn restaurants — revolutionizing the way creative ideas are financed in the digital age. Theaster Gates’s artistic practice, which encompasses everything from sculpture to a roving choir, is in its way just as groundbreaking. On his own block on the South Side of Chicago, Gates has engineered a miniature urban utopia, turning the once-blighted buildings that surround him into artist residencies, a library and even a cinema house that shows works by aspiring filmmakers from the neighborhood. Both Gates’s and Chen’s work may inspire social change, but it’s the power of creativity, not of compassion, that spurs them from one genre-defying innovation to the next.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Chen and Theaster Gates on Community-Driven Creativity', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecting the Dots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T13:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b38af51b-6ffc-56d5-ba9f-5b2f07950b40', 'word_count': 1567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b38af51b-6ffc-56d5-ba9f-5b2f07950b40'}, {'abstract': 'With a new version of its Windows operating system due later this year, Microsoft is reviving some hallmarks of previous versions, including the Start menu, but it is keeping the touch-friendly, tile-based look of Windows 8 that has turned off many computer shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/with-windows-8-1-a-new-start-that-looks-familiar/', 'snippet': 'With a new version of its Windows operating system due later this year, Microsoft is reviving some hallmarks of previous versions, including the Start menu, but it is keeping the touch-friendly, tile-based look of Windows 8 that has turned off man...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, Microsoft is bringing back some comforting hallmarks of its Windows operating system, including the Start menu. No, it is not chucking out the modern, touch-friendly, tile-based look of Windows 8, the new version of the software that has sent much of the PC industry, many pundits and some computer shoppers into a tizzy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/business/30bits-windows/30bits-windows-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Windows 8.1, a New Start That Looks Familiar', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Windows 8 Changes Not ‘a U-Turn at All’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows (Operating System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T13:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/331c2042-eab0-5435-93b4-dda35c62649d', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/331c2042-eab0-5435-93b4-dda35c62649d'}, {'abstract': 'A mother of two teenage daughters, who was victimized more than a year ago, found little support from the government or the legal system.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/for-kolkata-rape-victim-a-lonely-wait-for-justice/', 'snippet': 'A mother of two teenage daughters, who was victimized more than a year ago, found little support from the government or the legal system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOLKATA, West Bengal —In February 2012, a woman was gang-raped in a moving car after she was offered a lift from outside a nightclub on Kolkata’s Park Street. Unlike the majority of rape victims in India, she decided to report the crime, not only to 