ps://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/the-g-o-p-s-court-shrinking-plan/', 'snippet': 'Republicans don’t want new appointments to the D.C. Circuit, so that conservative-appointed judges can remain in the majority there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid has vowed to crack down on Republican filibusters several times with no effect, so it’s hard not to feel dubious about his latest threat to change Senate rules if Republicans continue to block President Obama’s nominations. He claims he is considering eliminating the 60-vote threshold to approve judicial and executive nominees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The G.O.P.’s Court-Shrinking Plan', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T14:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b42d250c-4652-59de-ace2-98ea30db7402', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b42d250c-4652-59de-ace2-98ea30db7402'}, {'abstract': 'Instagram photos from life at The New York Times Magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1.html', 'snippet': 'Instagram photos from life at The New York Times Magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Instagram photos from life at The New York Times Magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8/kathy-ryan-instagram1-slide-ZVN8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Office Romance, Part 1', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T14:05:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c2fab7ae-01ca-5193-b3b2-c6a2a75a9dc8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c2fab7ae-01ca-5193-b3b2-c6a2a75a9dc8'}, {'abstract': 'Theaters in London and Paris marked the centennial of a revolutionary, game-changing moment in modern music and dance.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/homage-paid-to-rite-of-spring-with-stravinsky-and-without/', 'snippet': 'Theaters in London and Paris marked the centennial of a revolutionary, game-changing moment in modern music and dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Wednesday was the 100th anniversary, to the day, of the first performance of “The Rite of Spring,” the Stravinsky-Nijinsky collaboration at the Théâtre des Champs-Élysées in Paris that marked a revolutionary, game-changing moment in modern music and dance. There were celebratory performances all over the world of various versions of “Rite” — at the Théâtre des Champs-Élysées, the Maryinsky Ballet performed Millicent Hodson and Kenneth Archer’s reconstructed version of Nijinsky’s ballet alongside a new version by the German choreographer Sasha Waltz.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/blogs/30rdv-spring-art2/30rdv-spring-art2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/30/blogs/30rdv-spring-art2/30rdv-spring-art2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/blogs/30rdv-spring-art2/30rdv-spring-art2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'