'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0317e414-c011-598c-a779-38206fa298d6', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0317e414-c011-598c-a779-38206fa298d6'}, {'abstract': 'Sheldon is the new Rhoda.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/the-big-bang-theory-and-the-mary-tyler-moore-show-a-comparison/', 'snippet': 'Sheldon is the new Rhoda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past weekend’s Riff essay\xa0looked at “The Big Bang Theory” —\xa0a hit network sitcom that I was late to accept but quick to love. The show’s strong ensemble cast also brought to mind an unlikely comparison: “The Mary Tyler Moore Show,” a more critically lauded success that featured, arguably, the best sitcom ensemble cast of all time. Here, an unscientific analysis of the main characters on “Mary Tyler Moore” with their surprising “Big Bang Theory” doubles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/30/magazine/30-big-bang-and-mary-tyler/30-big-bang-a