l': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/9db564b3-51f0-5d0f-af17-054715e6d667', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9db564b3-51f0-5d0f-af17-054715e6d667'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Sze, a sculptor who is representing the United States at the Venice Biennale, used found objects to create “Triple Point,” a series of intricate, disorienting environments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/arts/design/at-venice-biennale-sarah-szes-triple-point.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Sze, a sculptor who is representing the United States at the Venice Biennale, used found objects to create “Triple Point,” a series of intricate, disorienting environments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — The Biennale doesn’t open to the public until Saturday, but the art world arrived early for a peek. Artists, curators and creators responsible for this vast assemblage of exhibitions here have been on hand to meet, greet and explain their work.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Venice Biennale, Sarah Sze’s ‘Triple Point’', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Venice Biennale, Objects Found and Installed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogel, Carol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Biennale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sze, Sarah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koolhaas, Rem', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T19:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c03d5716-40ae-55b2-88f4-01256ccbee12', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c03d5716-40ae-55b2-88f4-01256ccbee12'}, {'abstract': 'The directors Jen and Sylvia Soska talk about “American Mary,” which centers on a world where people have their bodies surgically modified as a form of self-expression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/movies/jen-and-sylvia-soskas-american-mary.html', 'snippet': 'The directors Jen and Sylvia Soska talk about “American Mary,” which centers on a world where people have their bodies surgically modified as a form of self-expression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of siblings make movies. The brothers Coen (“No Country for Old Men”) are Oscar winners. Andy and Lana Wachowski (“Cloud Atlas”) are a prominent brother-sister team (although Lana was once Larry). But sister directors? And not just sisters, but identical twins?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02HORROR7_SPAN/02HORROR7_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Directors, and Twins, Who Distrust the Normal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Directors, and Twins, Who Distrust the Normal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piepenburg, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Mary (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soska, Sylvia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soska, Jen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T19:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/f918b859-4443-5001-87d9-2e7b776f7a43', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f918b859-4443-5001-87d9-2e7b776f7a43'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some horror movie physicians whose malpractice insurance must be abnormally high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/movies/their-bedside-manners-need-work.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some horror movie physicians whose malpractice insurance must be abnormally high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Dr. Giggles ever took the Hippocratic Oath, his eyes must have glazed at the “abstain from doing harm” part. Otoscopes are meant to examine noses and ears, not be plunged into brains. But often in horror movies, doctors don’t heal, scalpels aren’t for surgery and “medicine” only makes life worse. Fans know that syringes crave eyeballs, not upper arms.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/movies/02mary-span/02mary-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Their Bedside Manners Need Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Their Bedside Manners Need Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piepenburg, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Mary (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T19:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92cee1a8-d7a2-5c89-9e1d-96e2c81007fe', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92cee1a8-d7a2-5c89-9e1d-96e2c81007fe'}, {'abstract': 'The musician-run club ShapeShifter Lab, celebrating its one-year anniversary, has become a home for improvised music in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/arts/music/improvised-music-at-a-purposeful-home.html', 'snippet': 'The musician-run club ShapeShifter Lab, celebrating its one-year anniversary, has become a home for improvised music in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SKYE STEELE had just raced through an intricate tune called “Man-Made Nemesis” last week at ShapeShifter Lab when he tucked his violin under one arm, issuing an invitation in the form of an order. All the musicians in the audience — he called out half a dozen by name — were implored to join his band, the Railroad Rodia, for a chantlike finale. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05