ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58db7eb6-cf10-5c64-9673-afbb74e91515', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58db7eb6-cf10-5c64-9673-afbb74e91515'}, {'abstract': 'Politics, secret agents and strained family relations are part of “Shadow Dancer,” a thriller set in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/movies/shadow-dancer-starring-clive-owen.html', 'snippet': 'Politics, secret agents and strained family relations are part of “Shadow Dancer,” a thriller set in Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the prologue of James Marsh’s taut, somber conspiracy thriller “Shadow Dancer,” the 12-year-old Collette McVeigh (Maria Laird), idly stringing beads into a necklace, ignores her father’s request to go out and buy cigarettes. It is 1973 in Belfast, and the city is a powder keg. Her younger brother goes instead, and is shot to death outside the house in cross-fire between British and Irish Republican Army forces. As the McVeigh home erupts in anguished chaos, the father casts a recriminatory glare at Collette, who is guilt-stricken. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31SUBSHADOW_SPAN/SUBSHADOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31SUBSHADOW_SPAN/SUBSHADOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31SUBSHADOW_SPAN/SUBSHADOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31SUBSHADOW_SPAN/SUBSHADOW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1644, 'subType': 'sup