d-a5854df61bee', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a77fbf0-a011-59c7-b03d-a5854df61bee'}, {'abstract': '“Now You See Me,” directed by Louis Leterrier, follows the exploits of a criminal group of magicians as they are pursued by a dogged F.B.I. agent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/movies/now-you-see-me-directed-by-louis-leterrier.html', 'snippet': '“Now You See Me,” directed by Louis Leterrier, follows the exploits of a criminal group of magicians as they are pursued by a dogged F.B.I. agent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s one thing to watch a magician pull a rabbit out of a hat. It’s quite another to watch a movie of the same thing. Movies are themselves a kind of magic, dependent on technological wizardry. That’s why, when watching a film of a humble magic trick, you feel no sense of wonder, for the stunt has already been accomplished in a medium that’s all about illusion. So what, you shrug. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31NOWYOU1_SPAN/NOWYOU1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31NOWYOU1_SPAN/NOWYOU1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31NOWYOU1_SPAN/NOWYOU1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31NOWYOU1_SPAN/NOWYOU1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/31NOWY