ed', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4222a1-7747-5dc0-acd5-6dc38184f851', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4222a1-7747-5dc0-acd5-6dc38184f851'}, {'abstract': '“The Kings of Summer,” directed by Jordan Vogt-Roberts, centers on three teenage boys who run away from home — but not very far — and live out a comic wilderness fantasy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/movies/the-kings-of-summer-directed-by-jordan-vogt-roberts.html', 'snippet': '“The Kings of Summer,” directed by Jordan Vogt-Roberts, centers on three teenage boys who run away from home — but not very far — and live out a comic wilderness fantasy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the strife between parents and their teenage children can be so bitter that even the tiniest set-to is charged with hostility that threatens to erupt into violence. The most amusing — and darkest — moments in Jordan Vogt-Roberts’s flighty comedy “The Kings of Summer,” set in suburban Ohio, pit Joe (Nick Robinson), a smart, hormonally overcharged 15-year-old, against his loving but cruelly sarcastic widowed father, Frank (Nick Offerman of “Parks and Recreation”). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Into the Hormonal Wild', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Into the Hormonal Wild', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Kings of Summer (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Offerman, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogt-Roberts, Jordan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullally, Megan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T21:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50b33159-14a6-51d1-976e-d787bac4022b', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50b33159-14a6-51d1-976e-d787bac4022b'}, {'abstract': 'There is a little more than a week to go before the Belmont Stakes, and many of the contenders completed workouts this week. In all, 16 horses are under consideration for the race, which is the maximum field size.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/workouts-continue-as-belmont-field-swells/', 'snippet': 'There is a little more than a week to go before the Belmont Stakes, and many of the contenders completed workouts this week. In all, 16 horses are under consideration for the race, which is the maximum field size.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a little more than a week to go before the Belmont Stakes, and many of the contenders completed workouts this week. Some of those will complete a final workout over the weekend or early next week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Workouts Continue as Belmont Field Swells', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukas, D Wayne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pletcher, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-30T21:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'report