eluctance to join an earlier alliance, Wal-Mart, Gap and others are joining another plan for Bangladesh led by a nonprofit group in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Feeling pressure from consumer and labor groups for not doing more to ensure factory safety in Bangladesh, Wal-Mart, Gap and numerous other retailers along with the nation’s main retail federations are seeking to forge a new plan to promote safety in that country’s apparel industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Retailers Announce New Factory Safety Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Retailers Announce New Factory Safety Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gap Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T00:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d62dac0-900e-579d-ad88-54cb2779435f', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d62dac0-900e-579d-ad88-54cb2779435f'}, {'abstract': 'A 22-year-old woman who was denied an abortion by El Salvador’s Supreme Court can terminate her pregnancy at the first sign of danger, the health minister said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/world/americas/el-salvador-doctors-can-induce-birth-to-save-woman-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'A 22-year-old woman who was denied an abortion by El Salvador’s Supreme Court can terminate her pregnancy at the first sign of danger, the health minister said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A 22-year-old woman who was denied an abortion by El Salvador’s Supreme Court can terminate her pregnancy at the first sign of danger, the health minister, María Isabel Rodríguez, said Thursday. “At this point, the interruption of the pregnancy is no longer an abortion,” Ms. Rodríguez said, “it is an induced birth.” Doctors say that the woman, known only as Beatriz, is carrying a fetus with a severe birth defect and almost no chance of surviving, and that she faces serious health risks if her pregnancy continues because she has lupus and related complications. After the Supreme Court’s ruling, the Inter-American Court of Human Rights called on the government to \xa0“immediately adopt the necessary measures to protect the life, personal integrity and health” of Beatriz. Ms. Rodríguez said the woman could be induced to have either an abdominal or vaginal birth “because the important thing is saving Beatriz’s life.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'El Salvador: Doctors Can Induce Birth to Save Woman, Official Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'El Salvador: Official Says Doctors Can Induce Birth to Save Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Salvador', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lupus Erythematosus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Defects', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T00:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5741e0a-6fe2-5c73-8ae1-fe9f362f9c25', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5741e0a-6fe2-5c73-8ae1-fe9f362f9c25'}, {'abstract': 'Cans of Coors Light made to commemorate the 2013 Puerto Rican Day parade were criticized and the beer’s parent company said the cans would no longer be produced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/nyregion/beer-can-timed-to-parade-has-shortened-shelf-life.html', 'snippet': 'Cans of Coors Light made to commemorate the 2013 Puerto Rican Day parade were criticized and the beer’s parent company said the cans would no longer be produced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The special cans of Coors Light beer started popping up in New York City in recent weeks ahead of the coming parade. The vitriol followed soon after with elected officials and others saying that the cans were tasteless and sent the wrong message.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/nyregion/coors-1/coors-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600,