'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2dc3ef5-ed2a-5710-be94-751159e97207', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2dc3ef5-ed2a-5710-be94-751159e97207'}, {'abstract': 'Entergy, the company that owns the Indian Point nuclear power plant, has spent millions of dollars on lobbying to make its case across the state: Keep it open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/nyregion/going-all-out-in-support-of-indian-point.html', 'snippet': 'Entergy, the company that owns the Indian Point nuclear power plant, has spent millions of dollars on lobbying to make its case across the state: Keep it open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a break in the testimony, a few cordial people took seats near me and introduced themselves. Among them was Norris McDonald, who came to the legislative hearing in Lower Manhattan to testify about the future of the Indian Point nuclear power plant. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Owner Makes All-Out Push for Indian Point', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Owner Makes All-Out Push For Indian Pt.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Entergy Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T01:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6f6c7a3-eded-58b7-865b-00176a02791a', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6f6c7a3-eded-58b7-865b-00176a02791a'}, {'abstract': 'The ugly and destructive war on food stamps, which do good for both families and the economy, doesn’t make sense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/opinion/from-the-mouths-of-babes.html', 'snippet': 'The ugly and destructive war on food stamps, which do good for both families and the economy, doesn’t make sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many observers, I usually read reports about political goings-on with a sort of weary cynicism. Every once in a while, however, politicians do something so wrong, substantively and morally, that cynicism just won’t cut it; it’s time to get really angry instead. So it is with the ugly, destructive war against food stamps.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Mouths of Babes', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From The Mouths Of Babes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, Stephen L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T01:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op