Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9842e848-b689-560e-a319-bf65ea653189', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9842e848-b689-560e-a319-bf65ea653189'}, {'abstract': 'After flaws in the case of Marines accused in a 2005 Iraq massacre prompted a review, a Defense Department panel proposed that American troops should not be investigated by the branches in which they serve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/us/us-combat-commanders-should-handle-war-zone-investigations-panel-says.html', 'snippet': 'After flaws in the case of Marines accused in a 2005 Iraq massacre prompted a review, a Defense Department panel proposed that American troops should not be investigated by the branches in which they serve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Concerned about possible flaws in criminal proceedings against American troops accused of killing or abusing civilians in a war zone, a Defense Department panel has proposed that investigations and prosecutions of crimes be carried out by a senior commander in the theater of combat and not the branch of the armed services in which the accused serves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Combat Commanders Should Handle War Zone Investigations, Panel Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commanders, Not Service Branches, Should Handle War Cases, Panel Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11