eral regulators cut the catch for Gulf of Maine cod by 77 percent, saying the limit is the only way to rebuild stocks that scientists say are heavily depleted', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Martha Coakley filed a lawsuit on Thursday against the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration in an effort to block federal rules that severely limit the amount of cod New England fishermen are allowed to catch annually. Effective May 1, federal regulators cut the catch for Gulf of Maine cod by 77 percent, saying the limit is the only way to rebuild stocks that scientists say are heavily depleted. Ms. Coakley’s complaint says regulators violated federal law by not giving due consideration to the economic impact of the cuts on fishermen and by failing to use the best available science. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: State Sues Over Cod Limits', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: State Sues Over Cod Limits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cod (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coakley, Martha M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad72f2fa-9e49-5a86-866b-f8c8c0617348', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad72f2fa-9e49-5a86-866b-f8c8c0617348'}, {'abstract': 'Although the Nikkei 225-share index fell more than 13 percent from its peak last week,  economists pointed to  data showing  that the economy is catching up to expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/business/global/in-wake-of-market-dip-japanese-investors-find-comfort-in-higher-factory-output.html', 'snippet': 'Although the Nikkei 225-share index fell more than 13 percent from its peak last week,  economists pointed to  data showing  that the economy is catching up to expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan inched closer to the end of deflation and factory output picked up, government data showed Friday, offering proof that the real economy is slowly catching up to the high expectations set by its recent bold economic policies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/business/Nikkei/Nikkei-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/business/Nikkei/Nikkei-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/business/Nikkei/Nikkei-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/business/Nikkei/Nikkei-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Wake of Japanese Market Dip, Investors Find Comfort in Higher Factory Output', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Wake of Japanese Market Dip, Investors Find Comfort in Higher Factory Output', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e309729-ae1b-5c33-b5fd-6440f9cb1ad1', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e309729-ae1b-5c33-b5fd-6440f9cb1ad1'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ Mark Teixeira was expected to return from the disabled list Friday and reclaim his position at first from Lyle Overbay, who has racked up 29 runs batted in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/returning-teixeira-will-displace-overbay-on-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ Mark Teixeira was expected to return from the disabled list Friday and reclaim his position at first from Lyle Overbay, who has racked up 29 runs batted in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, Lyle Overbay was standing at first base at Yankee Stadium chatting with Mark Teixeira, as opposing baseball players often do between pitches. Both men are in the fraternity of first baseman, but at that moment Overbay was a base runner for the Toronto Blue Jays, and Teixeira, the fielder, had only recently joined the Yankees. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/31pins1/31pins1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Returning Teixeira Will Displace Valuable Contributor for Yankees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Returning Teixeira Will Displace Valuable Contributor for Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Overbay, Lyle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:18:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37edd4f-c816-5ce6-8803-3cd7e187079b', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37edd4f-c816-5ce6-8803-3cd7e187079b'}, {'abstract': 'Undergraduates receiving Pell grants, 2010-11, at selected elite universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/31/education/varied-enrollment-of-disadvantaged-students.html', 'snippet': 'Undergraduates receiving Pell grants, 2010-11, at selected elite universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Undergraduates receiving Pell grants, 2010-11, at selected elite universities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Varied Enrollment of Disadvantaged Students', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:26:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Education', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/195e69bb-5376-5adc-b101-00511ba948bd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/195e69bb-5376-5adc-b101-00511ba948bd'}, {'abstract': 'Because of the high cost, some colleges do a lot more than others to find and enroll low-income students, which critics of race-based affirmative action see as a way to encourage diversity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/education/college-slots-for-poorer-students-still-limited.html', 'snippet': 'Because of the high cost, some colleges do a lot more than others to find and enroll low-income students, which critics of race-based affirmative action see as a way to encourage diversity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opponents of race-based affirmative action in college admissions urge that colleges use a different tool to encourage diversity: giving a leg up to poor students. But many educators see real limits to how eager colleges are to enroll more poor students, no matter how qualified — and the reason is money.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/us/AFFIRM-2/AFFIRM-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Income-Based Diversity Lags at Some Universities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colleges Show Uneven Effort To Enroll Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:26:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61f59e23-f1c3-524c-8c86-63bcb2ba9313', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61f59e23-f1c3-524c-8c86-63bcb2ba9313'}, {'abstract': 'Six third-round matches worth viewing during Thursday’s action at Roland Garros.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/30/what-to-watch-on-day-6-at-the-french-open/', 'snippet': 'Six third-round matches worth viewing during Thursday’s action at Roland Garros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, 14 second-round singles matches were unable to be completed, including two of the recommended matches (Schiavone-Flipkens and \xa0Haas-Sock). Those two remain worthy picks, as do the following six third-round matches. Seeded players cannot play each another until the third round, and as it happens all six selected Friday matches feature two seeds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Watch on Day 6 at the French Open', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T02:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e46799-6976-5f92-a8b4-7cfad2a8d367', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e46799-6976-5f92-a8b4-7cfad2a8d367'}, {'abstract': 'In 16 previous years of interleague play, no Mets team had swept a season series from the Yankees. Yet one of the most ill-equipped Mets teams finally did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/sports/baseball/anonymous-mets-succeed-where-celebrated-predecessors-couldnt.html', 'snippet': 'In 16 previous years of interleague play, no Mets team had swept a season series from the Yankees. Yet one of the most ill-equipped Mets teams finally did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bobby Valentine’s 1997 Mets were a plucky group of overachievers who won their first Subway Series game against the Yankees, the defending World Series champions, but they did not sweep the series. The 1998 and ’99 Mets were brash contenders, but they could not do it, either. Nor could the 2000 Mets, who won the National League pennant, or the 2006 team that went deep into the playoffs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 473}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1614, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/sports/YANKEES1/YANKEES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where No Mets Have Gone Before', 'kicker': 'Mets 3