 'The police identified a suspect on Thursday in the killing of a 14-year-old Queens girl who was shot in the head as she rode a city bus home from a friend’s birthday party on May 18.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/nyregion/31busslay-nyregion/31busslay-nyregion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 180, 'width': 144, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/nyregion/31busslay-nyregion/31busslay-nyregion-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 180, 'width': 144, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/nyregion/31busslay-nyregion/31busslay-nyregion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/31/nyregion/31busslay-nyregion/31busslay-nyregion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Sought in Fatal Shooting of Queens Girl on Bus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect Sought in Fatal Shooting of Queens Girl on Bus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Robinson, D'aja", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClinton, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T04:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89369649-4111-5a94-b75e-aba8211666f5', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89369649-4111-5a94-b75e-aba8211666f5'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, New Yorkers in Brooklyn rallied to the challenge of the area’s first hot day of the season. Eli Belizaire, in Park Slope, tackled an ice cream cone. John Loftin sold cold water at the intersection of Kings Highway and Remson Avenue in East Flatbush. And the driver of a red convertible, with a towel on his head to cool off, decided he might as well go shirtless.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/fending-off-the-heat-of-the-dog-days-of-spring/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, New Yorkers in Brooklyn rallied to the challenge of the area’s first hot day of the season. Eli Belizaire, in Park Slope, tackled an ice cream cone. John Loftin sold cold water at the intersection of Kings Highway and Remson Avenue in...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, New Yorkers in Brooklyn rallied to the challenge of the area’s first hot day of the season. Eli Belizaire, in Park Slope, tackled an ice cream cone. John Loftin sold cold water at the intersection of Kings Highway and Remson Avenue in East Flatbush. And the driver of a red convertible, with a towel on his head to cool off, decided he might as well go shirtless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fending Off the Heat of the Dog Days of Spring', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T04:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b2f8d20-6b0a-5662-97e6-a0122b6d32bb', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b2f8d20-6b0a-5662-97e6-a0122b6d32bb'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Rex Ryan said the Jets were not surprised when David Garrard, signed to compete for the starting quarterback job, abruptly chose to retire two weeks ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/sports/football/ryan-says-garrard-didnt-shock-jets.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Rex Ryan said the Jets were not surprised when David Garrard, signed to compete for the starting quarterback job, abruptly chose to retire two weeks ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coach Rex Ryan said Thursday that the Jets were not surprised when David Garrard, signed to compete for the starting quarterback job, abruptly chose to retire two weeks ago. Garrard’s decision, spurred by the condition of his left knee, narrowed the competition to Mark Sanchez and Geno Smith. Garrard was placed on the reserve/retired list Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Says Garrard Didn’t Shock Jets', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Shock for Jets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrard, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T04:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/147f753b-01e9-5cc8-aaab-b7017cf5a204', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/147f753b-01e9-5cc8-aaab-b7017cf5a204'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (WE) BRIDEZILLAS This reality series kicks off its 10th and final season with the promise that these will be the worst-behaved brides ever. The temper tantrums begin as one woman feuds with her wedding planner, who just happens to be her future mother-in-law, and another (Ariel, above, with her husband, Brook) makes it clear to her entourage that she’s the boss. In “Marriage Boot Camp: Bridezillas,” a new series at 9, five former bridezillas and their husbands share a house as they try to save their marriages with help from counselors, including Jim and Elizabeth Carroll, a married team. And in “Pregnant & Dating,” a new series at 10, five women with a fondness for highlighting their baby bumps with various permutations of spandex search for Mr. Right as their pregnancies progress.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7006b674-33bb-54eb-84dc-e28c5d45f352', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7006b674-33bb-54eb-84dc-e28c5d45f352'}, {'abstract': 'Sergei M. Guriev, now teaching at an elite Paris university, said investigators demanded that he surrender five years’ worth of e-mails and submit to searches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/world/europe/economist-sergei-guriev-doesnt-plan-return-to-russia-soon.html', 'snippet': 'Sergei M. Guriev, now teaching at an elite Paris university, said investigators demanded that he surrender five years’ worth of e-mails and submit to searches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Hours after the economist Sergei M. Guriev said that he had fled Russia because he feared he would be prosecuted in a politically tinged case, Russia’s largest bank announced that its shareholders had overwhelmingly re-elected him to its board of directors, a show of support that points to rifts within Russia’s ruling class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/01russia_inline/01russia_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 886, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/world/01russia_inline/01russia_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 886}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/01russia_inline/01russia_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/01russia_inline/01russia_inline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1387, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima