'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | May 31, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T05:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e31aeee-8252-5297-9ab1-c776c67a43c2', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e31aeee-8252-5297-9ab1-c776c67a43c2'}, {'abstract': 'As China’s middle and upper classes grow, they are traveling abroad in fast-growing numbers and encountering other cultures, often for the first time. Comments by China’s ambassador to Thailand on the theme inspired some lively discussion of the issue.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/speak-more-chinese-ambassador-tells-thais/', 'snippet': 'As China’s middle and upper classes grow, they are traveling abroad in fast-growing numbers and encountering other cultures, often for the first time. Comments by China’s ambassador to Thailand on the theme inspired some lively discussion of the i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Some Thai police are corrupt and the justice system is slow, but perhaps more importantly, not enough Thais speak Chinese — that’s the gist of “a long list” of complaints by China’s Ambassador to Thailand, Guan Mu, delivered at a meeting with Thai officials Wednesday on the popular vacation island of Phuket, the Phuket News reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/world/asia/31PhuketRDV/31PhuketRDV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cr