, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8590e9ba-c765-5696-a822-9a72b66c3a60', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8590e9ba-c765-5696-a822-9a72b66c3a60'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bald on his recent book “Bengali Harlem and the Lost Histories of South Asian America” and his plans to turn it into a documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/a-conversation-with-author-and-filmmaker-vivek-bald/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bald on his recent book “Bengali Harlem and the Lost Histories of South Asian America” and his plans to turn it into a documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker and author Vivek Bald’s book “Bengali Harlem and the Lost Histories of South Asian America” created a buzz within the South Asian-American community when it was released in November. Mr. Bald documents the histories of seldom-acknowledged groups of early South Asian migrants to the United States, like Muslim silk and cotton traders from West Bengal in the 1880s and Indian sailors who deserted British steamships in the early 20th century. They settled in New Orleans, Harlem in New York and New Jersey and formed strong community bonds with African-American and Hispanic communities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/world/asia/31-bengal-harlem-IndiaInk/31-bengal-harlem-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 432, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/world/asia/31-bengal-harlem-IndiaInk/31-bengal-harlem-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 432, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/w