es of manners and etiquette, I hope we’re back to the substance. And there are really three points that have been established; I’m not sure that everyone understands that any one of those points is enough to refute most of the debt/deficit discussion of the past three years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt and Growth: The State of the Debate', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T13:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5011283e-d681-5552-8afe-36a37268cf41', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5011283e-d681-5552-8afe-36a37268cf41'}, {'abstract': 'Dell begins its official campaign to support a proposed $24.4 billion sale. | Lloyds Banking to a sell $5 billion in real estate-backed securities. | Would-be masters of the universe learn spreadsheet modeling at ‘boot camps.’', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/dell-fights-back/', 'snippet': 'Dell begins its official campaign to support a proposed $24.4 billion sale. | Lloyds Banking to a sell $5 billion in real estate-backed securities. | Would-be masters of the universe learn spreadsheet modeling at ‘boot camps.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'DELL FIGHTS BACK \xa0|\xa0 The fight over Dell Inc. has climbed to a new level.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dell Fights Back', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T13:22:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_n