and a relentless “take the ball on the rise” style to win a record 109 singles titles, including eight Grand Slam championships, five of them at the United States Open.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02connors/02connors-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tennis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tennis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lattman, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connors, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T14:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a6921ed-e6db-5724-befa-bf0f344c7772', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a6921ed-e6db-5724-befa-bf0f344c7772'}, {'abstract': 'Patricia Volk recalls her tumultuous relationship with her mother, and with the work of the fashion designer Elsa Schiaparelli.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/books/review/shocked-by-patricia-volk.html', 'snippet': 'Patricia Volk recalls her tumultuous relationship with her mother, and with the work of the fashion designer Elsa Schiaparelli.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven years ago, a drunken woman made a dramatic emphatic gesture in a Manhattan cab that sent one of my vintage faux gold-and-turquoise Schiaparelli clip-on earrings flying somewhere into the back seat’s nether regions. This is not one of those taxi stories with a happy ending (the sole copy of the manuscript recovered; the priceless Strad delivered in time for the big concert). The driver spent several minutes kindly helping me search. Numbers were exchanged. Forms filed. All in vain.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02SUBJACOBS/02SUBJACOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'arti