utionize the game and won eight national titles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/books/review/sum-it-up-by-pat-summitt-with-sally-jenkins.html', 'snippet': 'A memoir by Pat Summitt, the University of Tennessee women’s basketball coach who helped revolutionize the game and won eight national titles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College coaches have to construct teams — complex organisms — from players who are often just figuring out who they are, as athletes and as adults. They’re supposed to remember that the pieces they are fitting together, on the court or the field, are also students. And they have to rebuild again and again, with every graduation. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1503, 'width': 1494, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02BAZELON/02BAZELON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lady Vol', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lady Vol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summitt, Pat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Sally', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Tennessee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T14:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e491c7e-afc9-5d35-9e14-717c4860082f', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e491c7e-afc9-5d35-9e14-717c4860082f'}, {'abstract': 'In “Eleven Rings,” Phil Jackson ruminates on the philosophy and the players that made him the most successful coach in NBA history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/books/review/eleven-rings-by-phil-jackson-and-hugh-delehanty.html', 'snippet': 'In “Eleven Rings,” Phil Jackson ruminates on the philosophy and the players that made him the most successful coach in NBA history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late March, apparently in order to help promote “Eleven Rings,” Phil Jackson joined Twitter with a splash. His first tweet received attention on various sports Web sites, including USA Today’s and ESPN.com, because its text read, in full, “11 champ;ipnsikp[ ringhs.” (An ad made the joke clear: he had tried to type while wearing all 11 rings.) Jackson’s fingers soon found the correct keys, and he was off and tweeting. One might have expected profound insights from Jackson, whose 11 N.B.A. rings came while leading the Chicago Bulls in the 1990s and the Los Angeles Lakers in the 2000s and 2010s. The news media had long cast him as the “Zen master,” an intellectual with an interest in Eastern thought who used Buddhism to manage the titanic egos of Michael Jordan, Shaquille O’Neal and Kobe Bryant. For the wizened sage mumbling his koans, isn’t a medium limited to 140 characters ideal?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '47', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02TRACEY/02TRACEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02TRACEY/02TRACEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 748}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02TRACEY/02TRACEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 821, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02TRACEY/02TRACEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1642, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02TRACEY/02TRACEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width'