31/appeals-court-revives-financiers-suit-against-citigroup/', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court vacated a 2011 jury verdict clearing Citigroup of any wrongdoing over its role in the sale of EMI to Guy Hands’s private equity firm, Terra Firma Capital Partners, ruling that the trial court judge, Jed S. Rakoff, gave impr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British financier Guy Hands will have another chance to try to prove his claim that he was defrauded by his longtime bankers at Citigroup.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Revives Financier’s Fraud Suit Against Citigroup Over the Sale of EMI', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Revives Financier’s Fraud Suit Against Citigroup Over the Sale of EMI', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boies, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hands, Guy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boies Schiller & Flexner', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Terra Firma Capital Partners Ltd', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed52815-2ead-5851-afad-047b3e825a26', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed52815-2ead-5851-afad-047b3e825a26'}, {'abstract': 'A formal description of Luigi Dallapiccola’s one-act “Il Prigioniero,” a bleak 12-tone opera about a despairing prisoner during the Spanish Inquisition, might not sound like a crowd pleaser.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/arts/music/breaking-out-a-prisoners-tale.html', 'snippet': 'A formal description of Luigi Dallapiccola’s one-act “Il Prigioniero,” a bleak 12-tone opera about a despairing prisoner during the Spanish Inquisition, might not sound like a crowd pleaser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A formal description of Luigi Dallapiccola’s one-act “Il Prigioniero,” a bleak 12-tone opera about a despairing prisoner during the Spanish Inquisition, might not sound like a crowd pleaser. Still, the conductor Alan Gilbert is giving New York Philharmonic audiences a rare chance to experience this sensual and mysterious 1950 work as part of Gilbert’s Playlist, a series devoted to his favorites. I share his enthusiasm for “Il Prigioniero,” which I first saw in a wrenching production at the Paris National Opera in 2008.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Out A Prisoner’s Tale', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaking Out A Prisoner’s Tale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0b9454b-bde5-566e-ac0b-78b8df54c73a', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0b9454b-bde5-566e-ac0b-78b8df54c73a'}, {'abstract': 'This week, guests discuss reviews in the annual Summer Reading issue. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/05/31/books/review/02books_pod_blog.html', 'snippet': 'This week, guests discuss reviews in the annual Summer Reading issue. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, guests discuss reviews in the annual Summer Reading issue. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the New York Times Book Review: Summer Reading', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/c97096c3-8d4f-52e1-881e-6047a3259cea', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/c97096c3-8d4f-52e1-881e-6047a3259cea'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday night, ABC Family bids farewell to the trials and tribulations of adolescent pregnancy with the finale of “The Secret Life of the American Teenager.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/arts/television/two-mothers-many-problems.html', 'snippet': 'On Monday night, ABC Family bids farewell to the trials and tribulations of adolescent pregnancy with the finale of “The Secret Life of the American Teenager.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday night, ABC Family bids farewell to the trials and tribulations of adolescent pregnancy with the finale of “The Secret Life of the American Teenager,” at 8, and introduces a different kind of motherhood in its latest original drama, “The Fosters,” at 9. Created by Bradley Bredeweg (“Fly Girls”) and Peter Paige (“Queer as Folk”), with the pop star Jennifer Lopez leading the executive producers, “The Fosters” charts the twists and turns in the lives of Stef Foster (Teri Polo), a police officer, and her romantic partner, Lena Adams (Sherri Saum), a school vice principal. Together they’re mothers to Brandon (David Lambert), Stef’s biological son from a previous marriage, and the adopted twins Mariana (Cierra Ramirez) and Jesus (Jake T. Austin). ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Mothers, Many Problems', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Mothers, Many Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/670abed1-a325-55e5-9e88-d06e875c1032', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670abed1-a325-55e5-9e88-d06e875c1032'}, {'abstract': 'Children born to mothers who get more vitamins from their diets develop stronger bones even years later, a new study shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/mothers-diet-can-build-strong-bones-in-children/', 'snippet': 'Children born to mothers who get more vitamins from their diets develop stronger bones even years later, a new study shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children born to mothers who get more vitamins from their diets develop stronger bones even years later, a new study shows. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Bones Start in the Womb', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:07:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ee0c03-1bc5-5118-9200-288635e80b7c', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ee0c03-1bc5-5118-9200-288635e80b7c'}, {'abstract': '“Cornelius” is getting its first London revival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/theater/1935-play-becomes-a-forget-me-not.html', 'snippet': '“Cornelius” is getting its first London revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody paid much attention when “Cornelius” opened in London in 1935, though the play was written by the popular novelist and dramatist J. B. Priestley and starred no less an actor than Ralph Richardson. But this portrait of capitalism, as one character calls it, a “game of snakes and ladders — without the ladders,” was perhaps too tough-minded for escapist Depression audiences and survived for a mere seven weeks before fading into the twilight of forgotten flops.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1935 Play Becomes A Forget-Me-Not', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1935 Play Becomes A Forget-Me-Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8baf9b9-8ad7-5852-9d4c-f98c46f6a515', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8baf9b9-8ad7-5852-9d4c-f98c46f6a515'}, {'abstract': 'Each of us has a finite reservoir of energy in any given day. But there are techniques to avoid feeling exhausted.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/keep-calm-and-carry-on/', 'snippet': 'Each of us has a finite reservoir of energy in any given day. But there are techniques to avoid feeling exhausted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had just finished facilitating a daylong workshop for a team of leaders at Walmart when I received a voicemail telling me my flight from Bentonville, Ark., that evening had been canceled and I would not be able to get home until sometime the next day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep Calm and Carry On', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Adam M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93373e8f-611f-59b8-bfee-04a739a79560', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93373e8f-611f-59b8-bfee-04a739a79560'}, {'abstract': 'It was Secretary of State John Kerry’s most pointed criticism so far of Russia’s supply of weaponry to the Syrian government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/world/middleeast/kerry-castigates-russia-over-syria-bound-missiles.html', 'snippet': 'It was Secretary of State John Kerry’s most pointed criticism so far of Russia’s supply of weaponry to the Syrian government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Secretary of State John Kerry on Friday strongly criticized Russia’s pledge to sell advanced antiaircraft weapons to Syria, suggesting that along with the growing involvement of Iran and Hezbollah in the fighting, the sale threatened to disrupt efforts to negotiate a political settlement and could destabilize the region.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/world/diplo/diplo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Castigates Russia Over Syria-Bound Missiles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Rebukes Russia for Its Sale of Antiaircraft Missiles to Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95a76ab1-384e-56d6-aa53-7cf5ef68dd5d', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95a76ab1-384e-56d6-aa53-7cf5ef68dd5d'}, {'abstract': 'The words “military industrial complex” are not the first ones that spring to mind when you think about Leonardo da Vinci.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/arts/design/shes-rearming-leonardos-ideas.html', 'snippet': 'The words “military industrial complex” are not the first ones that spring to mind when you think about Leonardo da Vinci.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The words “military industrial complex” are not the first ones that spring to mind when you think about Leonardo da Vinci, but his designs for outlandish weaponry for the powerful Duke of Milan, Ludovico Sforza, his patron, are among his most reproduced drawings.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s Rearming Leonardo’s Ideas', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s Rearming Leonardo’s Ideas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c22282d7-cd91-5686-91e0-7c7d26d576ef', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c22282d7-cd91-5686-91e0-7c7d26d576ef'}, {'abstract': 'In duets choreographed by Christopher Wheeldon, there are no same-sex couples, and the women can seem subservient to men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/arts/dance/christopher-wheeldons-pas-de-deux.html', 'snippet': 'In duets choreographed by Christopher Wheeldon, there are no same-sex couples, and the women can seem subservient to men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a sign of Christopher Wheeldon’s eminence that his choreography, more than anyone else’s today, raises central issues about the nature of ballet. Is it an art of escapism or one that reflects vital features of the world we know? If it’s an art of ideals, what are they?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02WHEELDON1_SPAN/02SUBWHEELDON4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l