w-podcast-annual-summer-reading-issue/', 'snippet': 'Peter Lattman on Jimmy Connors, Anthony Gottlieb on Jewish humor, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week New York Times Book Review presents its annual Summer Reading issue, which includes looks at new books about Jewish humor, Superman, Prince, Mary Tyler Moore, Mickey Mantle and Willie Mays, Greenwich Village and much more. Peter Lattman reviews the new memoir by the tennis star Jimmy Connors, “The Outsider.” Mr. Lattman writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02cover-shadow/02cover-shadow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02cover-shadow/02cover-shadow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02cover-shadow/02cover-shadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02cover-shadow/02cover-shadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/books/review/02cover-shadow/02cover-shadow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: Annual Summer Reading Issue', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosman, Julie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connors, Jimmy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowles, Gregory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gottlieb, Anthony', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Alexandra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lattman, Peter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Pamela', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volk, Patricia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wisse, Ruth R', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:19:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db66a353-5ad5-5738-9f5e-b060e18038fc', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db66a353-5ad5-5738-9f5e-b060e18038fc'}, {'abstract': 'A 4,207-square-foot floor-through unit with four bedrooms and views of the park and surrounding historic neighborhood was the most expensive sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/big-ticket-treetop-park-views-for-16575000/', 'snippet': 'A 4,207-square-foot floor-through unit with four bedrooms and views of the park and surrounding historic neighborhood was the most expensive sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it was the lure of a free key to exclusive Gramercy Park, but the as-yet-unfinished gut renovation of a historic Salvation Army rooming house at 18 Gramercy Park South by Zeckendorf Development and Robert A. M. Stern, the premier team that produced the premium price precedents set by 15 Central Park West, has recorded its first closing. A floor-through unit on the ninth floor sold for its full asking price of $16,575,000, an amount that escalated to $16,877,493.75 once the transfer taxes kicked in, and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records.The 4,207-square-foot residence has four bedrooms and five and a half baths, and provides treetop views of the park and surrounding historic neighborhood with the addition of 35 large windows. The anticipated monthly carrying costs are $11,200. According to the developer, 8 of the available 16 residences, including a $42 million duplex penthouse with four terraces and two pools that was snapped up by Leslie Alexander, the owner of the Houston Rockets, went swiftly to contract for the full listing price despite being bought off the offering plan.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/realestate/02BIGTICKET/02BIGTICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/realestate/02BIGTICKET/02BIGTICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 623}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/realestate/02BIGTICKET/02BIGTICKET-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 987, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/realestate/02BIGTICKET/02BIGTICKET-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1974, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/realestate/02BIGTICKET/Ticket-thumbStandard.jp