None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:21:33+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/75bd80ad-7e3e-5c0d-b073-cc482c737eb8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/75bd80ad-7e3e-5c0d-b073-cc482c737eb8'}, {'abstract': 'Bethanie Mattek-Sands scored the biggest win of her career Thursday, beating the 2011 French Open champion Li Na in three sets at the French Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/mattek-sands-aggressive-game-plan-succeeds-against-li/', 'snippet': 'Bethanie Mattek-Sands scored the biggest win of her career Thursday, beating the 2011 French Open champion Li Na in three sets at the French Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a lost year spent rehabbing various injuries and learning that she had several food allergies, Bethanie Mattek-Sands scored the biggest win of her career Thursday, beating the 2011 French Open champion Li Na in three sets. The match was played in cold and drizzly conditions, but Mattek-Sands followed her game plan to perfection and finished the match with a steely calm as she swung out aggressively and never let up on Li. Mattek-Sands broke Li’s serve three times in the third set, hitting out on her return of serve and beating Li at her own game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mattek-Sands’s Aggressiveness Succeeds Against Li', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ra