_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/be29680e-7113-5614-aeea-fd19b3f5666c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/be29680e-7113-5614-aeea-fd19b3f5666c'}, {'abstract': 'A Minnesota hotelier who lost a close race against Representative Michele Bachmann last year and was gearing up for a rematch in 2014 has said that he will not run after all, now that Mrs. Bachmann, a Tea Party favorite, has announced that she will not seek re-election.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/bachmann-opponent-says-he-will-not-run/', 'snippet': 'A Minnesota hotelier who lost a close race against Representative Michele Bachmann last year and was gearing up for a rematch in 2014 has said that he will not run after all, now that Mrs. Bachmann, a Tea Party favorite, has announced that she wil...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Minnesota hotelier who lost a close race against Representative Michele Bachmann last year and was gearing up for a rematch in 2014 has said that he will not run after all — just two days after Mrs. Bachmann, a fiery Tea Party Republican, said she would not seek re-election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Opponent Says He Will Not Run', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:40:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33f74aa7-372d-5bf7-8db2-349fa6c0dc65', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33f74aa7-372d-5bf7-8db2-349fa6c0dc65'}, {'abstract': 'When disasters strike, people are moved to send money. Sometimes reports surface saying that the funds aren’t being disbursed properly. What does a donor do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/your-money/contemplating-effective-relief-actions-when-tragedies-occur.html', 'snippet': 'When disasters strike, people are moved to send money. Sometimes reports surface saying that the funds aren’t being disbursed properly. What does a donor do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNFORTUNATELY, it has become a sad tradition. An unthinkable tragedy occurs — the shootings at a movie theater in Aurora, Colo., or the bombings at the Boston Marathon. We are stunned, and then — to help the victims, to start the healing, to just feel like we are doing something — we give money.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr