20-f6212831288b'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the men who made the “Forlorn Hope” attack at Port Hudson, Miss.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/redemption-at-port-hudson/', 'snippet': 'Behind the men who made the “Forlorn Hope” attack at Port Hudson, Miss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Maj. Gen. Christopher C. Augur, his May 21, 1863 victory over Confederate forces at a crossroads near the hamlet of Plains Store, outside Baton Rouge, La., was particularly sweet. Possession of the roads by Augur’s division closed the last escape route for the Confederate garrison of Port Hudson, located about 25 miles north and one of the last rebel bastions on the Mississippi River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redemption at Port Hudson', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/222df404-6317-50a5-969a-729591329e55', 'word_count': 2164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/222df404-6317-50a5-969a-729591329e55'}, {'abstract': 'Icona Pop, a Swedish duo whose “I Love It” has given a hedonistic beat to TV shows, will perform at Randalls Island on Saturday in the Governors Ball music festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/arts/music/icona-pop-discusses-its-tour-including-governors-ball.html', 'snippet': 'Icona Pop, a Swedish duo whose “I Love It” has given a hedonistic beat to TV shows, will perform at Randalls Island on Saturday in the Governors Ball music festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe it was the placement on a coke-fueled episode of “Girls,” or as the theme song to the MTV reality show “Snooki & Jwoww,” but the music of Icona Pop has always seemed fit for a neon-tinged night out. Since they broke onto the charts last year with the soundtrack-ready single “I Love It” (co-written by and featuring the British singer Charli XCX) the Swedish duo has made its name on synthy dance pop with hedonistic lyrics and imagery. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/arts/02PLAYLIST3_SPAN/02PLAYLIST3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vocal Sessions in the Car and News From Outer Space', 'kicker': 'Playlist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vocal Sessions in the Car and News From Outer Space', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Icona Pop (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T16:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b721c77-a570-5aaf-b048-6f523a377755', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b721c77-a570-5aaf-b048-6f523a377755'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/calendar-coming-events-in-paris-sodankyla-finland-england/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris Jazz Festival, Paris Every weekend from June 9 to July 29, jazz musicians from across the globe will perform in the beautifully lush Parc Floral in the Bois des Vincennes at Paris’s eastern edge. Troy Andrews, above, known as Trombone Shorty, who hails from New Orleans and has appeared in the HBO series “Treme,” will perform alongside his band, Orleans Avenue, on July 14, and the Cuban jazz pianist Roberto Fonseca will play on July 7. Local, though by no means lesser, acts include the Manu Katché Quartet on June 30.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Paris; Sodankyla, Finland; England', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T17:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30217f58-6f4a-59e5-ab58-db200b772f66', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30217f58-6f4a-59e5-ab58-db200b772f66'}, {'abstract': 'T asked a group of authorities on subjects ranging from music to design to literature to profile the most game-changing men and women under 30 in their fields.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/05/30/t-magazine/02-twentysomething.html', 'snippet': 'T asked a group of authorities on subjects ranging from music to design to literature to profile the most game-changing men and women under 30 in their fields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T asked a group of authorities on subjects ranging from music to design to literature to profile the most game-changing men and women under 30 in their fields.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids These Days', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T17:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5aa27846-13c8-59bd-a4a9-efa6b9390017', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5aa27846-13c8-59bd-a4a9-efa6b9390017'}, {'abstract': 'A fast-growing Christian movement in the United States has revived debate about ethical practices in intercountry adoptions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/us/moved-to-adopt-evangelicals-find-children-and-pitfalls-abroad.html', 'snippet': 'A fast-growing Christian movement in the United States has revived debate about ethical practices in intercountry adoptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOZEMAN, Mont. — As a girl, Danna Hopkins dreamed of having 20 children. Today, she and her husband, Brian, the pastor of an evangelical church here, are building a large family, but not in the way she had imagined.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/01/us/EVANGELICALS/EVANGELICALS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75