 was as if Roger Federer revealed he detested grass or Victoria Azarenka disclosed a previous aversion to hardcourts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stosur’s Penchant for Clay Developed Over Time', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T17:17:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVID COX', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'COX', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8194159-8a8b-5f94-96c6-2a1aacb62b0c', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8194159-8a8b-5f94-96c6-2a1aacb62b0c'}, {'abstract': 'If he cooperates with prosecutors, Mathew Martoma, an ex-portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors, may be in a position to implicate the firm’s owner, Steven A. Cohen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/business/sac-case-tests-a-classic-dilemma.html', 'snippet': 'If he cooperates with prosecutors, Mathew Martoma, an ex-portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors, may be in a position to implicate the firm’s owner, Steven A. Cohen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine the pressure on Mathew Martoma, the 38-year-old former portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors charged with insider trading who may — or may not — be in a position to implicate Steven A. Cohen, the hedge fund’s billionaire founder and owner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images