 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b853d79-b840-5fa0-9f83-a7cbeb9c5360', 'word_count': 1827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b853d79-b840-5fa0-9f83-a7cbeb9c5360'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/weekend-fare-144/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fletcher’s Brooklyn Barbecue, a barbecue joint at Third Avenue in Gowanus, has just opened a Manhattan location for the summer, running daily from 11 a.m. to 7 p.m. at Pier 57, near West 15th Street and 11th Avenue. The menu includes barbecue sandwiches, wood-smoked chicken and a rotating selection of specials like barbecue hot link sandwiches with peppers and onions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bell House (Brooklyn, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eataly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Fletcher's Brooklyn Barbecue (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T17:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c613133b-bea7-50da-96d2-337a829caf2e', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c613133b-bea7-50da-96d2-337a829caf2e'}, {'abstract': 'The price index favored by the Federal Reserve, focusing on so-called “core inflation,” shows its lowest year-over-year rise since the government started keeping track more than five decades ago.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/little-cause-for-inflation-worries/', 'snippet': 'The price index favored by the Federal Reserve, focusing on so-called “core inflation,” shows its lowest year-over-year rise since the government started keeping track more than five decades ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Periodically I am asked whether we should worry about inflation, given how much money the Federal Reserve has pumped into the economy. Based on the Bureau of Economic Analysis data released Friday morning, this answer is still emphatically no.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Cause for Inflation Worries', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T17:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c4a582e-6f05-5159-84ce-f71883dca657', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c4a582e-6f05-5159-84ce-f71883dca657'}, {'abstract': 'After free performances in Central Park for 39 summers, the opera canceled its