ype': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02PILGRIM-slide-YKCK/02PILGRIM-slide-YKCK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Into India’s Himalayas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Himalayas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T18:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6e12a358-d7f8-5c09-a928-e748e7c73fba', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6e12a358-d7f8-5c09-a928-e748e7c73fba'}, {'abstract': 'Rolling countryside, stark valleys and recurring scenes of churches straight ahead on a drive through southeastern Sicily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/travel/on-a-road-trip-in-sicily-churches-everywhere.html', 'snippet': 'Rolling countryside, stark valleys and recurring scenes of churches straight ahead on a drive through southeastern Sicily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It happened each time we drove into one of southeastern Sicily’s hill towns. It could be a village or a big town, run-down or fixed-up, but as we drove uphill toward the historic center, the vision ahead was always roughly the same: a stunning Baroque church, honey-colored or pale white, decorated with columns or curves, angels or Cupids, shells or leaves, urns or shields, sometimes all of the above. A bell tower might be missing or there might be grass growing between the paving stones, but each of those churches exemplified what unfolds all across this corner of Sicily: an exuberant style that played itself out on facades of churches and palazzi in the wake of a devastating earthquake in 1693.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02-cultured-span/02-cultured-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Road Trip in Sicily, Churches Everywhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Nature With Exuberant Design', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bohlen, Celestine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sicily (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T18:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celestine Bohlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celestine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bohlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaeb3d63-fd77-55c8-bcaf-959bab9d897f', 'word_count': 1924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaeb3d63-fd77-55c8-bcaf-959bab9d897f'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last decade, the city’s Namal port has been transformed into a leisure destination, with a boardwalk, restaurants and a farmers’ market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/travel/in-tel-aviv-a-port-is-reborn.html', 'snippet': 'Over the last decade, the city’s Namal port has been transformed into a leisure destination, with a boardwalk, restaurants and a farmers’ market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tel Aviv, a seaside city, has no shortage of waterfront space. It has so much that when its port, Namal, began to fall into disuse four decades ago, overshadowed by a port to the south that became Israel’s main nexus of sea trade, it was shuttered. No one thought to rehabilitate it. There were plenty of other places to take advantage of the sea.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/travel/02HEADSUP1_SPAN-sf/02HEADSUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images