document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e7d5c75b-a508-5263-9267-4c6cfb9935d3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e7d5c75b-a508-5263-9267-4c6cfb9935d3'}, {'abstract': 'Workplace protections for L.G.B.T. people amount to a patchwork of state and local laws and judicial decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/your-money/protections-for-gays-in-workplace-are-piecemeal.html', 'snippet': 'Workplace protections for L.G.B.T. people amount to a patchwork of state and local laws and judicial decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jake, a 43-year-old worker at an auto parts warehouse in Ohio, often spends his lunch break in his car. By eating alone, he doesn’t have to talk with co-workers about his weekend plans or worry about using the wrong pronoun that could reveal that his life partner of 12 years is another man. Since many of his colleagues drop gay slurs on a daily basis, it’s a topic he would rather avoid.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 843, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1685, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/your-money/01money/01money-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fired for Being Gay? Protections Are Piecemeal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fired for Being Gay? Protections Are Piecemeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernard, Tara Siegel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T18:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3854ba15-de89-5eac-a83e-5345b73c3026', 'word_count': 1545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3854ba15-de89-5eac-a83e-5345b73c3026'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s lawmakers are doing their jobs! Which is more than you can say about Congress, which couldn’t even pass a background check bill.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/new-jersey-pushes-gun-control/', 'snippet': 'The state’s lawmakers are doing their jobs! Which is more than you can say about Congress, which couldn’t even pass a background check bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two surprising things going on in New Jersey: one, the state legislature, which is famous for either doing nothing or doing the wrong thing, has passed a series of tough gun control measures; and two, it’s plausible that Gov. Chris Christie will sign some of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Pushes Gun Control', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T19:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/702ba6f5-78d6-5da3-b27c-f954e71465b5', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/702ba6f5-78d6-5da3-b27c-f954e71465b5'}, {'abstract': '', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/05/31/opinion/bird-glued-struggle.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sections A, B, C and D, Glued Struggle', 