nail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1-SPAN/02VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1-SPAN/02VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1-SPAN/02VOWS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Age Gap Bridged by a Love of Animals', 'kicker': 'Renee Dutcher and Teo Alfero', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Age Gap Bridged by a Love of Animals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T19:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Diamond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Diamond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50bae130-52a1-53a4-bfa9-5f1981a77662', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50bae130-52a1-53a4-bfa9-5f1981a77662'}, {'abstract': 'Beware brave personal essay writer, because you are in for a world of brutal, self righteous, angry commentary.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/how-to-write-a-personal-essay-that-you-know-will-be-torn-apart-in-the-comments-section/', 'snippet': 'Beware brave personal essay writer, because you are in for a world of brutal, self righteous, angry commentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirteen years ago I wrote a Lives column about retaking the SATs as an adult. I was 28 and felt it was high time I redeemed myself for my original scores, a set of numbers that had stalked me for a decade. In the essay, “Evening the Score,” I expressed the fear that my abysmal performance would land me in community college, not thinking for a second that I might offend anyone. Yet, I did. While unabashedly Yahooing myself a while later, I discovered I had been granted the (THE!) 2001 Shame Award by the Two Year College Association. It took a minute for the full weight of it to hit me. Ever so slowly, the smile spread across my face. I won! Not only was it one of the only awards I’d ever received, it proved that someone actually read my piece. My only regret was that I had been given the award in absentia (talk about shameful, I wasn’t even invited to that year’s T.W.C.A. convention, where the honor was announced) and therefore had no plaque or certificate to hang next to my four-year college diploma (which I did in fact earn, despite my standardized-test deficiencies).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Write a Personal Essay That You Know Will Be Torn Apart in the Comments Section', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T19:33:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d977dea-37ee-5f0d-a86c-59f32147eb5b', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d977dea-37ee-5f0d-a86c-59f32147eb5b'}, {'abstract': 'While Apple and Google agree that the future of computers will be wearable, they disagree about which kind of computers people will actually want to wear.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/is-wearable-computing-ready-for-mainstream-consumers/', 'snippet': 'While Apple and Google agree that the future of computers will be wearable, they disagree about which kind of computers people will actually want to wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple and Google seem to agree on one thing: the future of computers will be wearable. Where they disagree is which kind of computers people will actually want to wear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/31/technology/bits-wearable/bits-wearable-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'c