ur and are firm enough for salads.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/the-other-white-beans/', 'snippet': 'Fresh shell beans such as cranberry and cannellini cook in under an hour and are firm enough for salads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s column, I write about using white beans in a hearty asparagus salad. In this video I show you how to trim the asparagus, but here’s more on what beans to use in the salad. I tested several white bean varieties, canned and dried, and the best were dried controne beans, an heirloom variety imported from Italy. They cooked up creamy and velvety, yet remained intact. They are available online and at specialty markets, but they are expensive. The bag I purchased cost $12 for 10 ounces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other White Beans', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T20:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27f03205-019d-5edd-a45f-e517f5dc4831', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27f03205-019d-5edd-a45f-e517f5dc4831'}, {'abstract': 'A teenage wizard and his science-geek friend find themselves doing battle with invaders from outer space in this British import.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/arts/television/wizards-vs-aliens-on-hub-network.html', 'snippet': 'A teenage wizard and his science-geek friend find themselves doing battle with invaders from outer space in this British import.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Make a television series about a teenage wizard, and you are bound to be accused of trying to ride the coattails of Harry Potter. And since you have no chance of matching the enduring appeal of J. K. Rowling’s Potter books and the movies based on them, the smart move would be to do everything possible to distance yourself from that universe and define your TV show as something completely different.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1222, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01WIZARDS/01WIZARDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So How Good Is Magic Against Extraterrestrials?', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So How Good Is Magic Against Extraterrestrials?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T20:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/69e1efc4-9b4e-5d8c-8e3e-a9317803516d', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69e1efc4-9b4e-5d8c-8e3e-a9317803516d'}, {'abstract': 'The health care law is expected to produce a sharp increase in self-employment next year because of access to insurance on the individual market, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/affordable-care-act-could-be-good-for-entrepreneurship/', 'snippet': 'The health care law is expected to produce a sharp increase in self-employment next year because of access to insurance on the individual market, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Affordable Care Act is expected to produce a sharp increase in entrepreneurship next year, according to a new report from the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation, the Urban Institute and Georgetown University’s Health Policy Institute. The number of self-employed people is expected to rise by 1.5 million — a relative increase of more than 11 percent — as a direct result of the health care overhaul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Affordable Care Act Could Be Good for Entrepreneurship', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson, Robert Wood, Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Urban Institute', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T21:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb2b1eb-853f-5e04-9133-b8a7bf256293', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb2b1eb-853f-5e04-9133-b8a7bf256293'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural highlights from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/the-week-in-culture-pictures-may-31/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural highlights from this week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More photographs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/artsspecial/20130601BEST-slide-OKBI/20130601BEST-slide-OKBI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/31/arts/artsspecial/20130601BEST-slide-OKBI/20130601BEST-slide-OKBI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xl