Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/281cb550-7757-5fb7-a607-c29f42118443', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/281cb550-7757-5fb7-a607-c29f42118443'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of the United Nations Committee Against Torture said legal proceedings had begun against two groups because of reports they sent to the panel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/world/europe/un-panel-criticizes-russia-for-prosecuting-rights-groups.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of the United Nations Committee Against Torture said legal proceedings had begun against two groups because of reports they sent to the panel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations Committee Against Torture criticized Russia on Friday for prosecuting two human rights groups because of reports they submitted to the committee.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel Criticizes Prosecutions in Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Criticizes Prosecutions In Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Committee Against Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Verdict Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADC Memorial', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T21:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb20f2b3-6988-5e32-bcf9-7f9268bbb0db', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb20f2b3-6988-5e32-bcf9-7f9268bbb0db'}, {'abstract': 'Audience participation and expert advice make new operas stronger, according to the American Lyric Theater, which uses the InsightALT festival as a developmental tool.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/arts/music/insightalt-a-festival-of-operas-in-progress.html', 'snippet': 'Audience participation and expert advice make new operas stronger, according to the American Lyric Theater, which uses the InsightALT festival as a developmental tool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The creation of a new opera is a chancy proposition. So the American Lyric Theater has come up with a way to bolster budding librettists and composers: invite a crowd of opinionated New Yorkers to a concert reading of a fledgling work and ask them to criticize it. Bring in a living opera legend and let her have a go at it, too. Whatever is left standing, the reasoning goes, has a fighting chance to make it into production. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01LYRIC/01LYRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01LYRIC/01LYRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01LYRIC/01LYRIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '