rside Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T22:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eb8cce4-eeaf-56f0-bd76-64b4ccce03e3', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eb8cce4-eeaf-56f0-bd76-64b4ccce03e3'}, {'abstract': 'Relatives of victims of man-made disasters have an idea for improving the distribution of donations.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/05/31/taking-the-downside-out-of-donations-to-disaster-victims/', 'snippet': 'Relatives of victims of man-made disasters have an idea for improving the distribution of donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s become a American habit built on compassion: after human-caused disasters, as with natural ones, people reach deep into their pockets to help the victims or their survivors. The Connecticut school shootings and the Boston Marathon bombing are among the recent examples.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Downside Out of Donations to Disaster Victims', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-05-31T22:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f228651-b36c-59a2-ba9c-ac266e452ff3', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f228651-b36c-59a2-ba9c-ac266e452ff3'}, {'abstract': 'Female and male perspectives contrasted in Kelly Rowland and The-Dream’s concert Thursday night at the Best Buy Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/01/arts/music/kelly-rowland-and-the-dream-at-the-best-buy-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Female and male perspectives contrasted in Kelly Rowland and The-Dream’s concert Thursday night at the Best Buy Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The joys of the slow bump and grind were something Kelly Rowland and The-Dream could agree on when their shared tour came to the Best Buy Theater on Thursday night. But from there, female and male perspectives diverged. When Ms. Rowland wasn’t promising delights or giving bedroom instructions, she was singing about relationships under stress from divided loyalties, jealousy, broken promises and outright abuse. By contrast, when The-Dream wasn’t exulting in carnal delights, he was usually waiting impatiently for the next opportunity. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01KELLY_SPAN/01KELLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01KELLY_SPAN/01KELLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01KELLY_SPAN/01KELLY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/01/arts/01KELLY_SPAN/01KELLY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/0