: 'By Ed Viesturs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viesturs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6ba6b02-abfb-5f15-8056-a7bc63b11a06', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6ba6b02-abfb-5f15-8056-a7bc63b11a06'}, {'abstract': 'Contemporary works are placed outdoors throughout the historic districts of Ossining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/02/nyregion/ossining-in-3d-bicentennial-sculpture-exhibit-on-view-in-ossining.html', 'snippet': 'Contemporary works are placed outdoors throughout the historic districts of Ossining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tree made entirely of nails graces a 19th-century churchyard. A woman molded in bronze lounges by the library, legs outstretched, face turned toward the sky. Along the shore, a shard of crimson glass atop a towering column of rose-colored granite catches reflections from the Hudson River beyond.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/nyregion/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/02/nyregion/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 565}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/nyregion/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/02/nyregion/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN/02ARTSWE_ALTSPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name'